</section>
<div id="p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="p1.1" class="ltx_p ltx_align_center"><span id="p1.1.1" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:207%;">Supplementary Material</span></p>
</div>
<div id="p2" class="ltx_para">
<p id="p2.1" class="ltx_p">This Supplementary Material contains the remaining proofs and technical details.
The proof that supports the general framework is collected in Section <a href="#A1" title="Appendix A Proof for the General Framework ‣ Optimal Detection for Language Watermarks with Pseudorandom Collision" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">A</span></a>.
The proofs about the Gumbel-max watermark are presented in Section <a href="#A2" title="Appendix B Proof for Gumbel-max Watermarks in Section ‣ Optimal Detection for Language Watermarks with Pseudorandom Collision" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">B</span></a>.
Section <a href="#A3" title="Appendix C Proof for Inverse Transform Watermarks in Section ‣ Optimal Detection for Language Watermarks with Pseudorandom Collision" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">C</span></a> includes the proofs of results for the inverse transform watermark.
Sections <a href="#A4" title="Appendix D Details of Simulation Study ‣ Optimal Detection for Language Watermarks with Pseudorandom Collision" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">D</span></a> and <a href="#A5" title="Appendix E Details for Real-World Examples ‣ Optimal Detection for Language Watermarks with Pseudorandom Collision" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">E</span></a> contain experiment details for simulation and real-world examples, respectively.</p>
</div>
<section id="A1" class="ltx_appendix">
<h2 class="ltx_title ltx_title_appendix"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_appendix">Appendix A </span>Proof for the General Framework</h2>

<section id="A1.SS1" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection">A.1 </span>Proof of Theorem <a href="#S3.Thmthm1" title="Theorem 3.1 (Explicit lower bound for detection efficiency). ‣ 3.3 Detection Efficiency and Optimal Scores ‣ 3 A Statistical Framework under Pseudorandomness Collision ‣ Optimal Detection for Language Watermarks with Pseudorandom Collision" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">3.1</span></a></h3>

<div id="A1.SS1.2" class="ltx_proof">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_font_italic ltx_title_proof">Proof of Theorem <a href="#S3.Thmthm1" title="Theorem 3.1 (Explicit lower bound for detection efficiency). ‣ 3.3 Detection Efficiency and Optimal Scores ‣ 3 A Statistical Framework under Pseudorandomness Collision ‣ Optimal Detection for Language Watermarks with Pseudorandom Collision" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">3.1</span></a>.</h6>
<div id="A1.SS1.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A1.SS1.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A1.SS1.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text">By Markov’s inequality, it follows that for any <math id="A1.SS1.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\theta\geq 0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>θ</mi><mo>≥</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\theta\geq 0</annotation></semantics></math>,</span></p>
<table id="A1.Ex24" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A1.Ex24.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="{\mathbb{P}}_{1}(S_{n}&lt;\gamma_{n,\alpha})={\mathbb{P}}_{1}(e^{-\theta S_{n}}&gt;e^{-\theta\gamma_{n,\alpha}})\leq e^{\theta\gamma_{n,\alpha}}\,\EB_{1}[{\mathrm{e}}^{-\theta S_{n}}]." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>ℙ</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>S</mi><mi>n</mi></msub><mo>&lt;</mo><msub><mi>γ</mi><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>α</mi></mrow></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><msub><mi>ℙ</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msup><mi>e</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>θ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>S</mi><mi>n</mi></msub></mrow></mrow></msup><mo>&gt;</mo><msup><mi>e</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>θ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>γ</mi><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>α</mi></mrow></msub></mrow></mrow></msup></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>≤</mo><mrow><msup><mi>e</mi><mrow><mi>θ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>γ</mi><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>α</mi></mrow></msub></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>𝔼</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><msup><mi>e</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>θ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>S</mi><mi>n</mi></msub></mrow></mrow></msup><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\mathbb{P}}_{1}(S_{n}&lt;\gamma_{n,\alpha})={\mathbb{P}}_{1}(e^{-\theta S_{n}}&gt;e^{-\theta\gamma_{n,\alpha}})\leq e^{\theta\gamma_{n,\alpha}}\,\EB_{1}[{\mathrm{e}}^{-\theta S_{n}}].</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A1.SS1.p1.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="A1.SS1.p1.2.1" class="ltx_text">Recall that <math id="A1.SS1.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="S_{n}=\sum_{{\mathcal{V}}\in\Pi}h_{{\mathcal{V}}}(Y_{{\mathcal{V}}})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>S</mi><mi>n</mi></msub><mo rspace="0.111em">=</mo><mrow><msub><mo>∑</mo><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒱</mi><mo>∈</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">Π</mi></mrow></msub><mrow><msub><mi>h</mi><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒱</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>Y</mi><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒱</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">S_{n}=\sum_{{\mathcal{V}}\in\Pi}h_{{\mathcal{V}}}(Y_{{\mathcal{V}}})</annotation></semantics></math> and scores for each minimal unit <math id="A1.SS1.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="h_{{\mathcal{V}}}(Y_{{\mathcal{V}}})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>h</mi><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒱</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>Y</mi><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒱</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">h_{{\mathcal{V}}}(Y_{{\mathcal{V}}})</annotation></semantics></math> are independent.
It then follows that</span></p>
<table id="A1.Ex25" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A1.Ex25.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\EB_{1}[{\mathrm{e}}^{-\theta S_{n}}]=\prod_{{\mathcal{V}}\in\Pi}\phi_{\bm{P}_{{\mathcal{V}}},h_{{\mathcal{V}}}}(\theta)." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>𝔼</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><msup><mi>e</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>θ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>S</mi><mi>n</mi></msub></mrow></mrow></msup><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.111em">=</mo><mrow><munder><mo movablelimits="false">∏</mo><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒱</mi><mo>∈</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">Π</mi></mrow></munder><mrow><msub><mi>ϕ</mi><mrow><msub><mi>𝐏</mi><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒱</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>h</mi><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒱</mi></msub></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>θ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\EB_{1}[{\mathrm{e}}^{-\theta S_{n}}]=\prod_{{\mathcal{V}}\in\Pi}\phi_{\bm{P}_{{\mathcal{V}}},h_{{\mathcal{V}}}}(\theta).</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A1.SS1.p1.3" class="ltx_p"><span id="A1.SS1.p1.3.1" class="ltx_text">Taking logarithms yields</span></p>
<table id="A1.Ex26" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A1.Ex26.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\log\EB_{1}[{\mathrm{e}}^{-\theta S_{n}}]=\sum_{{\mathcal{V}}\in\Pi}\log\phi_{\bm{P}_{{\mathcal{V}}},h_{{\mathcal{V}}}}(\theta)." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><msub><mi>𝔼</mi><mn>1</mn></msub></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><msup><mi>e</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>θ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>S</mi><mi>n</mi></msub></mrow></mrow></msup><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.111em">=</mo><mrow><munder><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒱</mi><mo>∈</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">Π</mi></mrow></munder><mrow><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><msub><mi>ϕ</mi><mrow><msub><mi>𝐏</mi><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒱</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>h</mi><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒱</mi></msub></mrow></msub></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>θ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\log\EB_{1}[{\mathrm{e}}^{-\theta S_{n}}]=\sum_{{\mathcal{V}}\in\Pi}\log\phi_{\bm{P}_{{\mathcal{V}}},h_{{\mathcal{V}}}}(\theta).</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A1.SS1.p1.4" class="ltx_p"><span id="A1.SS1.p1.4.1" class="ltx_text">Thus, the Type II error satisfies</span></p>
<table id="A1.Ex27" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A1.Ex27.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="1-\EB_{1}[T_{n}]\leq\exp\!\left(\theta\gamma_{n,\alpha}+\sum_{{\mathcal{V}}\in\Pi}\log\phi_{\bm{P}_{{\mathcal{V}}},h_{{\mathcal{V}}}}(\theta)\right)." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mrow><msub><mi>𝔼</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><msub><mi>T</mi><mi>n</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>≤</mo><mrow><mpadded style="width:1.370em;" width="1.370em"><mi>exp</mi></mpadded><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>θ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>γ</mi><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>α</mi></mrow></msub></mrow><mo rspace="0.055em">+</mo><mrow><munder><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒱</mi><mo>∈</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">Π</mi></mrow></munder><mrow><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><msub><mi>ϕ</mi><mrow><msub><mi>𝐏</mi><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒱</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>h</mi><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒱</mi></msub></mrow></msub></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>θ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">1-\EB_{1}[T_{n}]\leq\exp\!\left(\theta\gamma_{n,\alpha}+\sum_{{\mathcal{V}}\in\Pi}\log\phi_{\bm{P}_{{\mathcal{V}}},h_{{\mathcal{V}}}}(\theta)\right).</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A1.SS1.p1.5" class="ltx_p"><span id="A1.SS1.p1.5.1" class="ltx_text">Dividing by <math id="A1.SS1.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="N_{n}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>N</mi><mi>n</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">N_{n}</annotation></semantics></math> (the total number of minimal units <math id="A1.SS1.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="|\Pi|" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">Π</mi><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">|\Pi|</annotation></semantics></math>), we have for any <math id="A1.SS1.p1.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\theta\geq 0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>θ</mi><mo>≥</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\theta\geq 0</annotation></semantics></math>,</span></p>
<table id="A1.EGx17" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A1.Ex28"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.Ex28.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\left(1-\EB_{1}[T_{n}]\right)^{1/N_{n}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mrow><msub><mi>𝔼</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><msub><mi>T</mi><mi>n</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>/</mo><msub><mi>N</mi><mi>n</mi></msub></mrow></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\left(1-\EB_{1}[T_{n}]\right)^{1/N_{n}}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.Ex28.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\leq\exp\!\left(\frac{\theta\gamma_{n,\alpha}}{N_{n}}+\frac{1}{N_{n}}\sum_{{\mathcal{V}}\in\Pi}\log\phi_{\bm{P}_{{\mathcal{V}}},h_{{\mathcal{V}}}}(\theta)\right)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>≤</mo><mrow><mpadded style="width:1.370em;" width="1.370em"><mi>exp</mi></mpadded><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><mi>θ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>γ</mi><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>α</mi></mrow></msub></mrow><msub><mi>N</mi><mi>n</mi></msub></mfrac></mstyle><mo>+</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mn>1</mn><msub><mi>N</mi><mi>n</mi></msub></mfrac></mstyle><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munder><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒱</mi><mo>∈</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">Π</mi></mrow></munder></mstyle><mrow><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><msub><mi>ϕ</mi><mrow><msub><mi>𝑷</mi><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒱</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>h</mi><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒱</mi></msub></mrow></msub></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>θ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\leq\exp\!\left(\frac{\theta\gamma_{n,\alpha}}{N_{n}}+\frac{1}{N_{n}}\sum_{{\mathcal{V}}\in\Pi}\log\phi_{\bm{P}_{{\mathcal{V}}},h_{{\mathcal{V}}}}(\theta)\right)</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A1.E31"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.E31.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\leq\exp\!\left(\frac{\theta\gamma_{n,\alpha}}{N_{n}}+\frac{1}{N_{n}}\sum_{{\mathcal{V}}\in\Pi}\sup_{\bm{P}_{{\mathcal{V}}}\subseteq{\mathcal{P}}_{{\mathcal{V}}}}\log\phi_{\bm{P}_{{\mathcal{V}}},h_{{\mathcal{V}}}}(\theta)\right)." display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>≤</mo><mrow><mpadded style="width:1.370em;" width="1.370em"><mi>exp</mi></mpadded><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><mi>θ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>γ</mi><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>α</mi></mrow></msub></mrow><msub><mi>N</mi><mi>n</mi></msub></mfrac></mstyle><mo>+</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mn>1</mn><msub><mi>N</mi><mi>n</mi></msub></mfrac></mstyle><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munder><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒱</mi><mo>∈</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">Π</mi></mrow></munder></mstyle><mrow><munder><mo lspace="0.167em" movablelimits="false" rspace="0.167em">sup</mo><mrow><msub><mi>𝑷</mi><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒱</mi></msub><mo>⊆</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒫</mi><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒱</mi></msub></mrow></munder><mrow><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><msub><mi>ϕ</mi><mrow><msub><mi>𝑷</mi><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒱</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>h</mi><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒱</mi></msub></mrow></msub></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>θ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\leq\exp\!\left(\frac{\theta\gamma_{n,\alpha}}{N_{n}}+\frac{1}{N_{n}}\sum_{{\mathcal{V}}\in\Pi}\sup_{\bm{P}_{{\mathcal{V}}}\subseteq{\mathcal{P}}_{{\mathcal{V}}}}\log\phi_{\bm{P}_{{\mathcal{V}}},h_{{\mathcal{V}}}}(\theta)\right).</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(31)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
<div id="A1.SS1.p2" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A1.SS1.p2.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A1.SS1.p2.1.1" class="ltx_text">To proceed with the proof, we introduce a new quantity, denoted by <math id="A1.SS1.p2.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="D_{n,\mathscr{P}}({\bm{h}})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>D</mi><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>,</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathscript">𝒫</mi></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝒉</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">D_{n,\mathscr{P}}({\bm{h}})</annotation></semantics></math>:</span></p>
<table id="A1.EGx18" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A1.E32"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.E32.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\displaystyle D_{n,\mathscr{P}}({\bm{h}}):=-\inf_{\theta\geq 0}\left\{\theta\cdot\frac{\gamma_{n,\alpha}}{N_{n}}+\frac{1}{N_{n}}\sum_{{\mathcal{V}}\in\Pi}\sup_{\bm{P}_{{\mathcal{V}}}\subseteq{\mathcal{P}}_{{\mathcal{V}}}}\log\phi_{\bm{P}_{{\mathcal{V}}},h_{{\mathcal{V}}}}(\theta)\right\}." display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>D</mi><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>,</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathscript">𝒫</mi></mrow></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝒉</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo rspace="0em">:=</mo><mo lspace="0em">−</mo><munder><mo lspace="0em" movablelimits="false" rspace="0em">inf</mo><mrow><mi>θ</mi><mo>≥</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow></munder><mrow><mo>{</mo><mi>θ</mi><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><msub><mi>γ</mi><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>α</mi></mrow></msub><msub><mi>N</mi><mi>n</mi></msub></mfrac></mstyle><mo>+</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mn>1</mn><msub><mi>N</mi><mi>n</mi></msub></mfrac></mstyle><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munder><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒱</mi><mo>∈</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">Π</mi></mrow></munder></mstyle><munder><mo lspace="0.167em" movablelimits="false" rspace="0.167em">sup</mo><mrow><msub><mi>𝑷</mi><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒱</mi></msub><mo>⊆</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒫</mi><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒱</mi></msub></mrow></munder><mi>log</mi><msub><mi>ϕ</mi><mrow><msub><mi>𝑷</mi><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒱</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>h</mi><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒱</mi></msub></mrow></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>θ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>}</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle D_{n,\mathscr{P}}({\bm{h}}):=-\inf_{\theta\geq 0}\left\{\theta\cdot\frac{\gamma_{n,\alpha}}{N_{n}}+\frac{1}{N_{n}}\sum_{{\mathcal{V}}\in\Pi}\sup_{\bm{P}_{{\mathcal{V}}}\subseteq{\mathcal{P}}_{{\mathcal{V}}}}\log\phi_{\bm{P}_{{\mathcal{V}}},h_{{\mathcal{V}}}}(\theta)\right\}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(32)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A1.SS1.p2.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="A1.SS1.p2.2.1" class="ltx_text">Therefore, by taking the minimum with respect to <math id="A1.SS1.p2.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\theta\geq 0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>θ</mi><mo>≥</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\theta\geq 0</annotation></semantics></math> in (<a href="#A1.Ex28" title="In Proof of Theorem . ‣ A.1 Proof of Theorem ‣ Appendix A Proof for the General Framework ‣ Optimal Detection for Language Watermarks with Pseudorandom Collision" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">31</span></a>), we have that</span></p>
<table id="A1.EGx19" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A1.Ex29"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.Ex29.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\exp(-R_{n,\mathscr{P}}({\bm{h}}))=\sup_{\bm{P}_{{\mathcal{V}}}\subseteq{\mathcal{P}}_{{\mathcal{V}}},\forall{\mathcal{V}}}\left(1-\EB_{1}[T_{n}]\right)^{1/N_{n}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>exp</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><msub><mi>R</mi><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>,</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathscript">𝒫</mi></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝒉</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.1389em">=</mo><mrow><munder><mo lspace="0.1389em" movablelimits="false" rspace="0em">sup</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>𝑷</mi><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒱</mi></msub><mo>⊆</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒫</mi><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒱</mi></msub></mrow><mo>,</mo><mrow><mo rspace="0.167em">∀</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒱</mi></mrow></mrow></munder><msup><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mrow><msub><mi>𝔼</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><msub><mi>T</mi><mi>n</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>/</mo><msub><mi>N</mi><mi>n</mi></msub></mrow></msup></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\exp(-R_{n,\mathscr{P}}({\bm{h}}))=\sup_{\bm{P}_{{\mathcal{V}}}\subseteq{\mathcal{P}}_{{\mathcal{V}}},\forall{\mathcal{V}}}\left(1-\EB_{1}[T_{n}]\right)^{1/N_{n}}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A1.Ex30"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.Ex30.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\quad\leq\exp\!\left(\inf_{\theta\geq 0}\left\{\theta\cdot\frac{\gamma_{n,\alpha}}{N_{n}}+\frac{1}{N_{n}}\sum_{{\mathcal{V}}\in\Pi}\sup_{\bm{P}_{{\mathcal{V}}}\subseteq{\mathcal{P}}_{{\mathcal{V}}}}\log\phi_{\bm{P}_{{\mathcal{V}}},h_{{\mathcal{V}}}}(\theta)\right\}\right)=\exp(-D_{n,\mathscr{P}}({\bm{h}}))," display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo lspace="1.278em">≤</mo><mrow><mpadded style="width:1.370em;" width="1.370em"><mi>exp</mi></mpadded><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><munder><mo lspace="0em" movablelimits="false" rspace="0em">inf</mo><mrow><mi>θ</mi><mo>≥</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow></munder><mrow><mo>{</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>θ</mi><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><msub><mi>γ</mi><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>α</mi></mrow></msub><msub><mi>N</mi><mi>n</mi></msub></mfrac></mstyle></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mn>1</mn><msub><mi>N</mi><mi>n</mi></msub></mfrac></mstyle><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munder><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒱</mi><mo>∈</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">Π</mi></mrow></munder></mstyle><mrow><munder><mo lspace="0.167em" movablelimits="false" rspace="0.167em">sup</mo><mrow><msub><mi>𝑷</mi><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒱</mi></msub><mo>⊆</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒫</mi><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒱</mi></msub></mrow></munder><mrow><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><msub><mi>ϕ</mi><mrow><msub><mi>𝑷</mi><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒱</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>h</mi><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒱</mi></msub></mrow></msub></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>θ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>}</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>exp</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><msub><mi>D</mi><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>,</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathscript">𝒫</mi></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝒉</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\quad\leq\exp\!\left(\inf_{\theta\geq 0}\left\{\theta\cdot\frac{\gamma_{n,\alpha}}{N_{n}}+\frac{1}{N_{n}}\sum_{{\mathcal{V}}\in\Pi}\sup_{\bm{P}_{{\mathcal{V}}}\subseteq{\mathcal{P}}_{{\mathcal{V}}}}\log\phi_{\bm{P}_{{\mathcal{V}}},h_{{\mathcal{V}}}}(\theta)\right\}\right)=\exp(-D_{n,\mathscr{P}}({\bm{h}})),</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A1.SS1.p2.3" class="ltx_p"><span id="A1.SS1.p2.3.1" class="ltx_text">which implies that we have <math id="A1.SS1.p2.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="R_{n,\mathscr{P}}({\bm{h}})\geq D_{n,\mathscr{P}}({\bm{h}})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>R</mi><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>,</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathscript">𝒫</mi></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝒉</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>≥</mo><mrow><msub><mi>D</mi><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>,</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathscript">𝒫</mi></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝒉</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">R_{n,\mathscr{P}}({\bm{h}})\geq D_{n,\mathscr{P}}({\bm{h}})</annotation></semantics></math> for any scores <math id="A1.SS1.p2.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="{\bm{h}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>𝒉</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\bm{h}}</annotation></semantics></math>.</span></p>
</div>
<div id="A1.Thmlem1" class="ltx_theorem ltx_theorem_lem">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_title_theorem"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_theorem"><span id="A1.Thmlem1.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Lemma A.1</span></span><span id="A1.Thmlem1.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">.</span></h6>
<div id="A1.Thmlem1.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A1.Thmlem1.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A1.Thmlem1.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">Let Assumptions <a href="#S3.Thmasmp3" title="Assumption 3.3. ‣ 3.3 Detection Efficiency and Optimal Scores ‣ 3 A Statistical Framework under Pseudorandomness Collision ‣ Optimal Detection for Language Watermarks with Pseudorandom Collision" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">3.3</span></a> <a href="#S3.I3.i1" title="item (i) ‣ Assumption 3.3. ‣ 3.3 Detection Efficiency and Optimal Scores ‣ 3 A Statistical Framework under Pseudorandomness Collision ‣ Optimal Detection for Language Watermarks with Pseudorandom Collision" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">(i)</span></a> and <a href="#S3.I3.i2" title="item (ii) ‣ Assumption 3.3. ‣ 3.3 Detection Efficiency and Optimal Scores ‣ 3 A Statistical Framework under Pseudorandomness Collision ‣ Optimal Detection for Language Watermarks with Pseudorandom Collision" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">(ii)</span></a> hold with <math id="A1.Thmlem1.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="0&lt;C_{\mathrm{var}}&lt;\infty" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mn>0</mn><mo>&lt;</mo><msub><mi>C</mi><mi>var</mi></msub><mo>&lt;</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">∞</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">0&lt;C_{\mathrm{var}}&lt;\infty</annotation></semantics></math> the uniform variance bound for each <math id="A1.Thmlem1.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="h_{{\mathcal{V}}}(Y_{\mathcal{V}})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>h</mi><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒱</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>Y</mi><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒱</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">h_{{\mathcal{V}}}(Y_{\mathcal{V}})</annotation></semantics></math>, that is, <math id="A1.Thmlem1.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathrm{Var}_{0}(h_{{\mathcal{V}}}(Y_{\mathcal{V}}))\leq C_{\mathrm{var}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>Var</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>h</mi><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒱</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>Y</mi><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒱</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>≤</mo><msub><mi>C</mi><mi>var</mi></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathrm{Var}_{0}(h_{{\mathcal{V}}}(Y_{\mathcal{V}}))\leq C_{\mathrm{var}}</annotation></semantics></math> for any minimal unit <math id="A1.Thmlem1.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="{\mathcal{V}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒱</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\mathcal{V}}</annotation></semantics></math>.
It follows that for any <math id="A1.Thmlem1.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\alpha\in(0,1)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>α</mi><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>1</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\alpha\in(0,1)</annotation></semantics></math>,</span></p>
<table id="A1.EGx20" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A1.E33"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.E33.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\left|\frac{\gamma_{n,\alpha}}{N_{n}}-\mu_{n}\right|\leq\varepsilon_{0}=\sqrt{\frac{C_{\mathrm{var}}}{N_{n}\cdot\min(\alpha,1-\alpha)}}\quad\text{where}\quad\mu_{n}=\frac{1}{N_{n}}\sum_{{\mathcal{V}}\in\Pi}\EB_{0}[h_{{\mathcal{V}}}]." display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mrow><mo>|</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><msub><mi>γ</mi><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>α</mi></mrow></msub><msub><mi>N</mi><mi>n</mi></msub></mfrac></mstyle><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>μ</mi><mi>n</mi></msub></mrow><mo>|</mo></mrow><mo>≤</mo><msub><mi>ε</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo>=</mo><msqrt><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><msub><mi>C</mi><mi>var</mi></msub><mrow><msub><mi>N</mi><mi>n</mi></msub><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><mrow><mi>min</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>α</mi><mo>,</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mi>α</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mfrac></mstyle></msqrt></mrow><mspace style="width:1em;" width="1em"></mspace><mtext class="ltx_mathvariant_italic">where</mtext><mspace style="width:1em;" width="1em"></mspace><mrow><msub><mi>μ</mi><mi>n</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mn>1</mn><msub><mi>N</mi><mi>n</mi></msub></mfrac></mstyle><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munder><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒱</mi><mo>∈</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">Π</mi></mrow></munder></mstyle><mrow><msub><mi>𝔼</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><msub><mi>h</mi><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒱</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\left|\frac{\gamma_{n,\alpha}}{N_{n}}-\mu_{n}\right|\leq\varepsilon_{0}=\sqrt{\frac{C_{\mathrm{var}}}{N_{n}\cdot\min(\alpha,1-\alpha)}}\quad\text{where}\quad\mu_{n}=\frac{1}{N_{n}}\sum_{{\mathcal{V}}\in\Pi}\EB_{0}[h_{{\mathcal{V}}}].</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(33)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
</div>
<div id="A1.Thmlem2" class="ltx_theorem ltx_theorem_lem">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_title_theorem"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_theorem"><span id="A1.Thmlem2.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Lemma A.2</span></span><span id="A1.Thmlem2.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">.</span></h6>
<div id="A1.Thmlem2.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A1.Thmlem2.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A1.Thmlem2.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">Under Assumption <a href="#S3.Thmasmp3" title="Assumption 3.3. ‣ 3.3 Detection Efficiency and Optimal Scores ‣ 3 A Statistical Framework under Pseudorandomness Collision ‣ Optimal Detection for Language Watermarks with Pseudorandom Collision" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">3.3</span></a>, there exists a universal constant <math id="A1.Thmlem2.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\overline{M}&gt;0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mover accent="true"><mi>M</mi><mo stretchy="true">¯</mo></mover><mo>&gt;</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\overline{M}&gt;0</annotation></semantics></math>, independent of <math id="A1.Thmlem2.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="n" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>n</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">n</annotation></semantics></math> and the partition <math id="A1.Thmlem2.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\Pi" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi mathvariant="normal">Π</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Pi</annotation></semantics></math>, such that for any family of belief classes <math id="A1.Thmlem2.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathscr{P}=\{{\mathcal{P}}_{{\mathcal{V}}}\}_{{\mathcal{V}}\in\Pi}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathscript">𝒫</mi><mo>=</mo><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒫</mi><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒱</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒱</mi><mo>∈</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">Π</mi></mrow></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathscr{P}=\{{\mathcal{P}}_{{\mathcal{V}}}\}_{{\mathcal{V}}\in\Pi}</annotation></semantics></math>, the optimal value of <math id="A1.Thmlem2.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\theta" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>θ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\theta</annotation></semantics></math> in the definitions of both <math id="A1.Thmlem2.p1.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="D_{n,\mathscr{P}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>D</mi><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>,</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathscript">𝒫</mi></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">D_{n,\mathscr{P}}</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="A1.Thmlem2.p1.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="B_{n,\mathscr{P}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>B</mi><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>,</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathscript">𝒫</mi></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">B_{n,\mathscr{P}}</annotation></semantics></math> lies within the interval <math id="A1.Thmlem2.p1.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="[0,\overline{M}]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>M</mi><mo stretchy="true">¯</mo></mover><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">[0,\overline{M}]</annotation></semantics></math>.</span></p>
</div>
</div>
<div id="A1.SS1.p3" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A1.SS1.p3.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A1.SS1.p3.1.1" class="ltx_text">Recall that</span></p>
<table id="A1.Ex31" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A1.Ex31.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="B_{n,\mathscr{P}}({\bm{h}}):=-\inf_{\theta\geq 0}\frac{1}{N_{n}}\sum_{{\mathcal{V}}\in\Pi}\left\{\theta\,\EB_{0}[h_{{\mathcal{V}}}]\,+\,\sup_{\bm{P}_{{\mathcal{V}}}\subseteq{\mathcal{P}}_{{\mathcal{V}}}}\log\phi_{\bm{P}_{{\mathcal{V}}},h_{{\mathcal{V}}}}(\theta)\right\}." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>B</mi><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>,</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathscript">𝒫</mi></mrow></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝒉</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo rspace="0em">:=</mo><mo lspace="0em">−</mo><munder><mo lspace="0em" movablelimits="false" rspace="0.167em">inf</mo><mrow><mi>θ</mi><mo>≥</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow></munder><mfrac><mn>1</mn><msub><mi>N</mi><mi>n</mi></msub></mfrac><munder><mo movablelimits="false" rspace="0em">∑</mo><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒱</mi><mo>∈</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">Π</mi></mrow></munder><mrow><mo>{</mo><mi>θ</mi><msub><mi>𝔼</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><msub><mi>h</mi><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒱</mi></msub><mo rspace="0.170em" stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow><mo rspace="0.114em">+</mo><munder><mo movablelimits="false" rspace="0.167em">sup</mo><mrow><msub><mi>𝐏</mi><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒱</mi></msub><mo>⊆</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒫</mi><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒱</mi></msub></mrow></munder><mi>log</mi><msub><mi>ϕ</mi><mrow><msub><mi>𝐏</mi><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒱</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>h</mi><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒱</mi></msub></mrow></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>θ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>}</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">B_{n,\mathscr{P}}({\bm{h}}):=-\inf_{\theta\geq 0}\frac{1}{N_{n}}\sum_{{\mathcal{V}}\in\Pi}\left\{\theta\,\EB_{0}[h_{{\mathcal{V}}}]\,+\,\sup_{\bm{P}_{{\mathcal{V}}}\subseteq{\mathcal{P}}_{{\mathcal{V}}}}\log\phi_{\bm{P}_{{\mathcal{V}}},h_{{\mathcal{V}}}}(\theta)\right\}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A1.SS1.p3.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="A1.SS1.p3.2.1" class="ltx_text">By Lemma <a href="#A1.Thmlem2" title="Lemma A.2. ‣ Proof of Theorem . ‣ A.1 Proof of Theorem ‣ Appendix A Proof for the General Framework ‣ Optimal Detection for Language Watermarks with Pseudorandom Collision" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">A.2</span></a>, there exists a universal constant <math id="A1.SS1.p3.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\overline{M}&gt;0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mover accent="true"><mi>M</mi><mo stretchy="true">¯</mo></mover><mo>&gt;</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\overline{M}&gt;0</annotation></semantics></math> that doesn’t depend on <math id="A1.SS1.p3.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="n" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>n</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">n</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="A1.SS1.p3.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\Pi" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi mathvariant="normal">Π</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Pi</annotation></semantics></math> such that the optimal <math id="A1.SS1.p3.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\theta" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>θ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\theta</annotation></semantics></math> in the definition of both <math id="A1.SS1.p3.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="D_{n,\mathscr{P}}({\bm{h}})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>D</mi><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>,</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathscript">𝒫</mi></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝒉</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">D_{n,\mathscr{P}}({\bm{h}})</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="A1.SS1.p3.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="B_{n,\mathscr{P}}({\bm{h}})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>B</mi><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>,</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathscript">𝒫</mi></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝒉</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">B_{n,\mathscr{P}}({\bm{h}})</annotation></semantics></math> are uniformly bounded above by <math id="A1.SS1.p3.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\overline{M}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mover accent="true"><mi>M</mi><mo stretchy="true">¯</mo></mover><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\overline{M}</annotation></semantics></math>.
Combining this with Lemma <a href="#A1.Thmlem1" title="Lemma A.1. ‣ Proof of Theorem . ‣ A.1 Proof of Theorem ‣ Appendix A Proof for the General Framework ‣ Optimal Detection for Language Watermarks with Pseudorandom Collision" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">A.1</span></a>, we obtain the approximation bound</span></p>
<table id="A1.E34" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A1.E34.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\bigl|B_{n,\mathscr{P}}({\bm{h}})-D_{n,\mathscr{P}}({\bm{h}})\bigr|\,\leq\,{\varepsilon}_{0}\cdot\overline{M}\,=\,\Theta\!\left(\frac{1}{\sqrt{N_{n}}}\right)," display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em" stretchy="true">|</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>B</mi><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>,</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathscript">𝒫</mi></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝒉</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><msub><mi>D</mi><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>,</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathscript">𝒫</mi></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝒉</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em" rspace="0.170em" stretchy="true">|</mo></mrow><mo rspace="0.448em">≤</mo><mrow><msub><mi>ε</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>M</mi><mo stretchy="true">¯</mo></mover></mrow><mo rspace="0.448em">=</mo><mrow><mpadded style="width:0.621em;" width="0.621em"><mi mathvariant="normal">Θ</mi></mpadded><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mfrac><mn>1</mn><msqrt><msub><mi>N</mi><mi>n</mi></msub></msqrt></mfrac><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\bigl|B_{n,\mathscr{P}}({\bm{h}})-D_{n,\mathscr{P}}({\bm{h}})\bigr|\,\leq\,{\varepsilon}_{0}\cdot\overline{M}\,=\,\Theta\!\left(\frac{1}{\sqrt{N_{n}}}\right),</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(34)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A1.SS1.p3.3" class="ltx_p"><span id="A1.SS1.p3.3.1" class="ltx_text">where <math id="A1.SS1.p3.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="{\varepsilon}_{0}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>ε</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\varepsilon}_{0}</annotation></semantics></math> is the approximation error from Lemma <a href="#A1.Thmlem1" title="Lemma A.1. ‣ Proof of Theorem . ‣ A.1 Proof of Theorem ‣ Appendix A Proof for the General Framework ‣ Optimal Detection for Language Watermarks with Pseudorandom Collision" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">A.1</span></a>,
and <math id="A1.SS1.p3.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\overline{M}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mover accent="true"><mi>M</mi><mo stretchy="true">¯</mo></mover><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\overline{M}</annotation></semantics></math> is the bound from Lemma <a href="#A1.Thmlem2" title="Lemma A.2. ‣ Proof of Theorem . ‣ A.1 Proof of Theorem ‣ Appendix A Proof for the General Framework ‣ Optimal Detection for Language Watermarks with Pseudorandom Collision" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">A.2</span></a>.</span></p>
</div>
<div id="A1.SS1.p4" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A1.SS1.p4.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A1.SS1.p4.1.1" class="ltx_text">∎</span></p>
</div>
</div>
<div id="A1.SS1.p5" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A1.SS1.p5.1" class="ltx_p">Finally, we provide the proofs of Lemma <a href="#A1.Thmlem1" title="Lemma A.1. ‣ Proof of Theorem . ‣ A.1 Proof of Theorem ‣ Appendix A Proof for the General Framework ‣ Optimal Detection for Language Watermarks with Pseudorandom Collision" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">A.1</span></a> and Lemma <a href="#A1.Thmlem2" title="Lemma A.2. ‣ Proof of Theorem . ‣ A.1 Proof of Theorem ‣ Appendix A Proof for the General Framework ‣ Optimal Detection for Language Watermarks with Pseudorandom Collision" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">A.2</span></a>.</p>
</div>
<div id="A1.SS1.3" class="ltx_proof">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_font_italic ltx_title_proof">Proof of Lemma <a href="#A1.Thmlem1" title="Lemma A.1. ‣ Proof of Theorem . ‣ A.1 Proof of Theorem ‣ Appendix A Proof for the General Framework ‣ Optimal Detection for Language Watermarks with Pseudorandom Collision" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">A.1</span></a>.</h6>
<div id="A1.SS1.p6" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A1.SS1.p6.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A1.SS1.p6.1.1" class="ltx_text">Let <math id="A1.SS1.p6.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mu_{n}=\EB_{0}[S_{n}/N_{n}]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>μ</mi><mi>n</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mrow><msub><mi>𝔼</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><msub><mi>S</mi><mi>n</mi></msub><mo>/</mo><msub><mi>N</mi><mi>n</mi></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mu_{n}=\EB_{0}[S_{n}/N_{n}]</annotation></semantics></math> denote the expectation of the score <math id="A1.SS1.p6.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="S_{n}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>S</mi><mi>n</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">S_{n}</annotation></semantics></math> under the null. By the definition of <math id="A1.SS1.p6.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="S_{n}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>S</mi><mi>n</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">S_{n}</annotation></semantics></math>, we have</span></p>
<table id="A1.Ex32" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A1.Ex32.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mu_{n}=\EB_{0}\left[\frac{1}{N_{n}}\sum_{{\mathcal{V}}\in\Pi}h_{{\mathcal{V}}}(Y_{{\mathcal{V}}})\right]=\frac{1}{N_{n}}\sum_{{\mathcal{V}}\in\Pi}\EB_{0}[h_{{\mathcal{V}}}(Y_{{\mathcal{V}}})]." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>μ</mi><mi>n</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mrow><msub><mi>𝔼</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>[</mo><mrow><mfrac><mn>1</mn><msub><mi>N</mi><mi>n</mi></msub></mfrac><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><munder><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒱</mi><mo>∈</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">Π</mi></mrow></munder><mrow><msub><mi>h</mi><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒱</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>Y</mi><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒱</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>]</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mfrac><mn>1</mn><msub><mi>N</mi><mi>n</mi></msub></mfrac><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><munder><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒱</mi><mo>∈</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">Π</mi></mrow></munder><mrow><msub><mi>𝔼</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><msub><mi>h</mi><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒱</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>Y</mi><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒱</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mu_{n}=\EB_{0}\left[\frac{1}{N_{n}}\sum_{{\mathcal{V}}\in\Pi}h_{{\mathcal{V}}}(Y_{{\mathcal{V}}})\right]=\frac{1}{N_{n}}\sum_{{\mathcal{V}}\in\Pi}\EB_{0}[h_{{\mathcal{V}}}(Y_{{\mathcal{V}}})].</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A1.SS1.p6.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="A1.SS1.p6.2.1" class="ltx_text">Since the minimal units are independent under <math id="A1.SS1.p6.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="H_{0}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>H</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">H_{0}</annotation></semantics></math>, the variance of <math id="A1.SS1.p6.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="S_{n}/N_{n}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>S</mi><mi>n</mi></msub><mo>/</mo><msub><mi>N</mi><mi>n</mi></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">S_{n}/N_{n}</annotation></semantics></math> can be bounded as</span></p>
<table id="A1.Ex33" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A1.Ex33.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathrm{Var}_{0}\left(\frac{S_{n}}{N_{n}}\right)=\frac{1}{N_{n}^{2}}\mathrm{Var}_{0}(S_{n})=\frac{1}{N_{n}^{2}}\sum_{{\mathcal{V}}\in\Pi}\mathrm{Var}_{0}(h_{{\mathcal{V}}}(Y_{{\mathcal{V}}}))." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>Var</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mfrac><msub><mi>S</mi><mi>n</mi></msub><msub><mi>N</mi><mi>n</mi></msub></mfrac><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mfrac><mn>1</mn><msubsup><mi>N</mi><mi>n</mi><mn>2</mn></msubsup></mfrac><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>Var</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>S</mi><mi>n</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mfrac><mn>1</mn><msubsup><mi>N</mi><mi>n</mi><mn>2</mn></msubsup></mfrac><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><munder><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒱</mi><mo>∈</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">Π</mi></mrow></munder><mrow><msub><mi>Var</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>h</mi><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒱</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>Y</mi><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒱</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathrm{Var}_{0}\left(\frac{S_{n}}{N_{n}}\right)=\frac{1}{N_{n}^{2}}\mathrm{Var}_{0}(S_{n})=\frac{1}{N_{n}^{2}}\sum_{{\mathcal{V}}\in\Pi}\mathrm{Var}_{0}(h_{{\mathcal{V}}}(Y_{{\mathcal{V}}})).</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A1.SS1.p6.3" class="ltx_p"><span id="A1.SS1.p6.3.1" class="ltx_text">Using the uniform variance bound <math id="A1.SS1.p6.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathrm{Var}_{0}(h_{{\mathcal{V}}}(Y_{{\mathcal{V}}}))\leq C_{\mathrm{var}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>Var</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>h</mi><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒱</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>Y</mi><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒱</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>≤</mo><msub><mi>C</mi><mi>var</mi></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathrm{Var}_{0}(h_{{\mathcal{V}}}(Y_{{\mathcal{V}}}))\leq C_{\mathrm{var}}</annotation></semantics></math>, we have <math id="A1.SS1.p6.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathrm{Var}_{0}\left(\frac{S_{n}}{N_{n}}\right)\leq\frac{1}{N_{n}^{2}}\sum_{{\mathcal{V}}\in\Pi}C_{\mathrm{var}}=\frac{C_{\mathrm{var}}}{N_{n}}." display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>Var</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mfrac><msub><mi>S</mi><mi>n</mi></msub><msub><mi>N</mi><mi>n</mi></msub></mfrac><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>≤</mo><mrow><mfrac><mn>1</mn><msubsup><mi>N</mi><mi>n</mi><mn>2</mn></msubsup></mfrac><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><msub><mo>∑</mo><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒱</mi><mo>∈</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">Π</mi></mrow></msub><msub><mi>C</mi><mi>var</mi></msub></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mfrac><msub><mi>C</mi><mi>var</mi></msub><msub><mi>N</mi><mi>n</mi></msub></mfrac></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathrm{Var}_{0}\left(\frac{S_{n}}{N_{n}}\right)\leq\frac{1}{N_{n}^{2}}\sum_{{\mathcal{V}}\in\Pi}C_{\mathrm{var}}=\frac{C_{\mathrm{var}}}{N_{n}}.</annotation></semantics></math>
Hence, by Chebyshev’s inequality, it follows that for any <math id="A1.SS1.p6.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\varepsilon&gt;0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>ε</mi><mo>&gt;</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\varepsilon&gt;0</annotation></semantics></math></span></p>
<table id="A1.Ex34" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A1.Ex34.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="{\mathbb{P}}_{0}\left(\left|\frac{S_{n}}{N_{n}}-\mu_{n}\right|\geq\varepsilon\right)\leq\frac{\mathrm{Var}_{0}(S_{n}/N_{n})}{\varepsilon^{2}}\leq\frac{C_{\mathrm{var}}}{N_{n}\varepsilon^{2}}." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>ℙ</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mrow><mo>|</mo><mrow><mfrac><msub><mi>S</mi><mi>n</mi></msub><msub><mi>N</mi><mi>n</mi></msub></mfrac><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>μ</mi><mi>n</mi></msub></mrow><mo>|</mo></mrow><mo>≥</mo><mi>ε</mi></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>≤</mo><mfrac><mrow><msub><mi>Var</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>S</mi><mi>n</mi></msub><mo>/</mo><msub><mi>N</mi><mi>n</mi></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><msup><mi>ε</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></mfrac><mo>≤</mo><mfrac><msub><mi>C</mi><mi>var</mi></msub><mrow><msub><mi>N</mi><mi>n</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>ε</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow></mfrac></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\mathbb{P}}_{0}\left(\left|\frac{S_{n}}{N_{n}}-\mu_{n}\right|\geq\varepsilon\right)\leq\frac{\mathrm{Var}_{0}(S_{n}/N_{n})}{\varepsilon^{2}}\leq\frac{C_{\mathrm{var}}}{N_{n}\varepsilon^{2}}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A1.SS1.p6.4" class="ltx_p"><span id="A1.SS1.p6.4.1" class="ltx_text">When we set</span></p>
<table id="A1.Ex35" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A1.Ex35.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\varepsilon=\sqrt{\frac{C_{\mathrm{var}}}{N_{n}\cdot\min(\alpha,1-\alpha)}}." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>ε</mi><mo>=</mo><msqrt><mfrac><msub><mi>C</mi><mi>var</mi></msub><mrow><msub><mi>N</mi><mi>n</mi></msub><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><mrow><mi>min</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>α</mi><mo>,</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mi>α</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mfrac></msqrt></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\varepsilon=\sqrt{\frac{C_{\mathrm{var}}}{N_{n}\cdot\min(\alpha,1-\alpha)}}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A1.SS1.p6.5" class="ltx_p"><span id="A1.SS1.p6.5.1" class="ltx_text">This choice implies that <math id="A1.SS1.p6.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\frac{C_{\mathrm{var}}}{N_{n}\varepsilon_{0}^{2}}=\min(\alpha,1-\alpha)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mfrac><msub><mi>C</mi><mi>var</mi></msub><mrow><msub><mi>N</mi><mi>n</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>ε</mi><mn>0</mn><mn>2</mn></msubsup></mrow></mfrac><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>min</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>α</mi><mo>,</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mi>α</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\frac{C_{\mathrm{var}}}{N_{n}\varepsilon_{0}^{2}}=\min(\alpha,1-\alpha)</annotation></semantics></math>. Therefore, we have:</span></p>
<ul id="A1.I1" class="ltx_itemize">
<li id="A1.I1.i1" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">•</span> 
<div id="A1.I1.i1.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A1.I1.i1.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><math id="A1.I1.i1.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="{\mathbb{P}}_{0}(S_{n}/N_{n}\geq\mu_{n}+\varepsilon_{0})\leq{\mathbb{P}}_{0}(|S_{n}/N_{n}-\mu_{n}|\geq\varepsilon_{0})\leq\min(\alpha,1-\alpha)\leq\alpha" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>ℙ</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>S</mi><mi>n</mi></msub><mo>/</mo><msub><mi>N</mi><mi>n</mi></msub></mrow><mo>≥</mo><mrow><msub><mi>μ</mi><mi>n</mi></msub><mo>+</mo><msub><mi>ε</mi><mn>0</mn></msub></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>≤</mo><mrow><msub><mi>ℙ</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>S</mi><mi>n</mi></msub><mo>/</mo><msub><mi>N</mi><mi>n</mi></msub></mrow><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>μ</mi><mi>n</mi></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow><mo>≥</mo><msub><mi>ε</mi><mn>0</mn></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>≤</mo><mrow><mi>min</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>α</mi><mo>,</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mi>α</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>≤</mo><mi>α</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\mathbb{P}}_{0}(S_{n}/N_{n}\geq\mu_{n}+\varepsilon_{0})\leq{\mathbb{P}}_{0}(|S_{n}/N_{n}-\mu_{n}|\geq\varepsilon_{0})\leq\min(\alpha,1-\alpha)\leq\alpha</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>
</div></li>
<li id="A1.I1.i2" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">•</span> 
<div id="A1.I1.i2.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A1.I1.i2.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><math id="A1.I1.i2.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="{\mathbb{P}}_{0}(S_{n}/N_{n}\leq\mu_{n}-\varepsilon_{0})\leq{\mathbb{P}}_{0}(|S_{n}/N_{n}-\mu_{n}|\geq\varepsilon_{0})\leq\min(\alpha,1-\alpha)\leq 1-\alpha" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>ℙ</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>S</mi><mi>n</mi></msub><mo>/</mo><msub><mi>N</mi><mi>n</mi></msub></mrow><mo>≤</mo><mrow><msub><mi>μ</mi><mi>n</mi></msub><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>ε</mi><mn>0</mn></msub></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>≤</mo><mrow><msub><mi>ℙ</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>S</mi><mi>n</mi></msub><mo>/</mo><msub><mi>N</mi><mi>n</mi></msub></mrow><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>μ</mi><mi>n</mi></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow><mo>≥</mo><msub><mi>ε</mi><mn>0</mn></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>≤</mo><mrow><mi>min</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>α</mi><mo>,</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mi>α</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>≤</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mi>α</mi></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\mathbb{P}}_{0}(S_{n}/N_{n}\leq\mu_{n}-\varepsilon_{0})\leq{\mathbb{P}}_{0}(|S_{n}/N_{n}-\mu_{n}|\geq\varepsilon_{0})\leq\min(\alpha,1-\alpha)\leq 1-\alpha</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>
</div></li>
</ul>
<p id="A1.SS1.p6.6" class="ltx_p"><span id="A1.SS1.p6.6.1" class="ltx_text">We now use these bounds to constrain <math id="A1.SS1.p6.m10" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\gamma_{n,\alpha}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>γ</mi><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>α</mi></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\gamma_{n,\alpha}</annotation></semantics></math>. By definition, <math id="A1.SS1.p6.m11" class="ltx_Math" alttext="{\mathbb{P}}_{0}(S_{n}\geq\gamma_{n,\alpha})=\alpha" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>ℙ</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>S</mi><mi>n</mi></msub><mo>≥</mo><msub><mi>γ</mi><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>α</mi></mrow></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mi>α</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\mathbb{P}}_{0}(S_{n}\geq\gamma_{n,\alpha})=\alpha</annotation></semantics></math>.
For the upper bound, since <math id="A1.SS1.p6.m12" class="ltx_Math" alttext="{\mathbb{P}}_{0}(S_{n}\geq(\mu_{n}+\varepsilon_{0})N_{n})&lt;\alpha" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>ℙ</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>S</mi><mi>n</mi></msub><mo>≥</mo><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>μ</mi><mi>n</mi></msub><mo>+</mo><msub><mi>ε</mi><mn>0</mn></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>N</mi><mi>n</mi></msub></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>&lt;</mo><mi>α</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\mathbb{P}}_{0}(S_{n}\geq(\mu_{n}+\varepsilon_{0})N_{n})&lt;\alpha</annotation></semantics></math>, it must be that the threshold <math id="A1.SS1.p6.m13" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\gamma_{n,\alpha}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>γ</mi><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>α</mi></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\gamma_{n,\alpha}</annotation></semantics></math> is smaller than <math id="A1.SS1.p6.m14" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(\mu_{n}+\varepsilon_{0})N_{n}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>μ</mi><mi>n</mi></msub><mo>+</mo><msub><mi>ε</mi><mn>0</mn></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>N</mi><mi>n</mi></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(\mu_{n}+\varepsilon_{0})N_{n}</annotation></semantics></math>. Thus,</span></p>
<table id="A1.Ex36" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A1.Ex36.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\gamma_{n,\alpha}\leq(\mu_{n}+\varepsilon_{0})N_{n}\implies\frac{\gamma_{n,\alpha}}{N_{n}}\leq\mu_{n}+\varepsilon_{0}." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>γ</mi><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>α</mi></mrow></msub><mo>≤</mo><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>μ</mi><mi>n</mi></msub><mo>+</mo><msub><mi>ε</mi><mn>0</mn></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>N</mi><mi>n</mi></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">⟹</mo><mfrac><msub><mi>γ</mi><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>α</mi></mrow></msub><msub><mi>N</mi><mi>n</mi></msub></mfrac><mo>≤</mo><mrow><msub><mi>μ</mi><mi>n</mi></msub><mo>+</mo><msub><mi>ε</mi><mn>0</mn></msub></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\gamma_{n,\alpha}\leq(\mu_{n}+\varepsilon_{0})N_{n}\implies\frac{\gamma_{n,\alpha}}{N_{n}}\leq\mu_{n}+\varepsilon_{0}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A1.SS1.p6.7" class="ltx_p"><span id="A1.SS1.p6.7.1" class="ltx_text">For the lower bound, by definition <math id="A1.SS1.p6.m15" class="ltx_Math" alttext="{\mathbb{P}}_{0}(S_{n}&lt;\gamma_{n,\alpha})=1-\alpha" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>ℙ</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>S</mi><mi>n</mi></msub><mo>&lt;</mo><msub><mi>γ</mi><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>α</mi></mrow></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mi>α</mi></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\mathbb{P}}_{0}(S_{n}&lt;\gamma_{n,\alpha})=1-\alpha</annotation></semantics></math>.
Since <math id="A1.SS1.p6.m16" class="ltx_Math" alttext="{\mathbb{P}}_{0}(S_{n}&lt;(\mu_{n}-\varepsilon_{0})N_{n})&lt;1-\alpha" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>ℙ</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>S</mi><mi>n</mi></msub><mo>&lt;</mo><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>μ</mi><mi>n</mi></msub><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>ε</mi><mn>0</mn></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>N</mi><mi>n</mi></msub></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>&lt;</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mi>α</mi></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\mathbb{P}}_{0}(S_{n}&lt;(\mu_{n}-\varepsilon_{0})N_{n})&lt;1-\alpha</annotation></semantics></math>, it must be that the threshold <math id="A1.SS1.p6.m17" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\gamma_{n,\alpha}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>γ</mi><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>α</mi></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\gamma_{n,\alpha}</annotation></semantics></math> is larger than <math id="A1.SS1.p6.m18" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(\mu_{n}-\varepsilon_{0})N_{n}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>μ</mi><mi>n</mi></msub><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>ε</mi><mn>0</mn></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>N</mi><mi>n</mi></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(\mu_{n}-\varepsilon_{0})N_{n}</annotation></semantics></math>. Thus,</span></p>
<table id="A1.Ex37" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A1.Ex37.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\gamma_{n,\alpha}\geq(\mu_{n}-\varepsilon_{0})N_{n}\implies\frac{\gamma_{n,\alpha}}{N_{n}}\geq\mu_{n}-\varepsilon_{0}." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>γ</mi><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>α</mi></mrow></msub><mo>≥</mo><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>μ</mi><mi>n</mi></msub><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>ε</mi><mn>0</mn></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>N</mi><mi>n</mi></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">⟹</mo><mfrac><msub><mi>γ</mi><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>α</mi></mrow></msub><msub><mi>N</mi><mi>n</mi></msub></mfrac><mo>≥</mo><mrow><msub><mi>μ</mi><mi>n</mi></msub><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>ε</mi><mn>0</mn></msub></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\gamma_{n,\alpha}\geq(\mu_{n}-\varepsilon_{0})N_{n}\implies\frac{\gamma_{n,\alpha}}{N_{n}}\geq\mu_{n}-\varepsilon_{0}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A1.SS1.p6.8" class="ltx_p"><span id="A1.SS1.p6.8.1" class="ltx_text">Combining the upper and lower bounds, we have:</span></p>
<table id="A1.Ex38" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A1.Ex38.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mu_{n}-\varepsilon_{0}\leq\frac{\gamma_{n,\alpha}}{N_{n}}\leq\mu_{n}+\varepsilon_{0}," display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>μ</mi><mi>n</mi></msub><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>ε</mi><mn>0</mn></msub></mrow><mo>≤</mo><mfrac><msub><mi>γ</mi><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>α</mi></mrow></msub><msub><mi>N</mi><mi>n</mi></msub></mfrac><mo>≤</mo><mrow><msub><mi>μ</mi><mi>n</mi></msub><mo>+</mo><msub><mi>ε</mi><mn>0</mn></msub></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mu_{n}-\varepsilon_{0}\leq\frac{\gamma_{n,\alpha}}{N_{n}}\leq\mu_{n}+\varepsilon_{0},</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A1.SS1.p6.9" class="ltx_p"><span id="A1.SS1.p6.9.1" class="ltx_text">which is equivalent to:</span></p>
<table id="A1.Ex39" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A1.Ex39.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\left|\frac{\gamma_{n,\alpha}}{N_{n}}-\mu_{n}\right|\leq\varepsilon_{0}=\sqrt{\frac{C_{\mathrm{var}}}{N_{n}\cdot\min(\alpha,1-\alpha)}}." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mo>|</mo><mrow><mfrac><msub><mi>γ</mi><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>α</mi></mrow></msub><msub><mi>N</mi><mi>n</mi></msub></mfrac><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>μ</mi><mi>n</mi></msub></mrow><mo>|</mo></mrow><mo>≤</mo><msub><mi>ε</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo>=</mo><msqrt><mfrac><msub><mi>C</mi><mi>var</mi></msub><mrow><msub><mi>N</mi><mi>n</mi></msub><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><mrow><mi>min</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>α</mi><mo>,</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mi>α</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mfrac></msqrt></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\left|\frac{\gamma_{n,\alpha}}{N_{n}}-\mu_{n}\right|\leq\varepsilon_{0}=\sqrt{\frac{C_{\mathrm{var}}}{N_{n}\cdot\min(\alpha,1-\alpha)}}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A1.SS1.p6.10" class="ltx_p"><span id="A1.SS1.p6.10.1" class="ltx_text">This completes the proof. The second part can be proved similarly.
∎</span></p>
</div>
</div>
<div id="A1.SS1.4" class="ltx_proof">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_font_italic ltx_title_proof">Proof of Lemma <a href="#A1.Thmlem2" title="Lemma A.2. ‣ Proof of Theorem . ‣ A.1 Proof of Theorem ‣ Appendix A Proof for the General Framework ‣ Optimal Detection for Language Watermarks with Pseudorandom Collision" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">A.2</span></a>.</h6>
<div id="A1.SS1.p7" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A1.SS1.p7.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A1.SS1.p7.1.1" class="ltx_text">The claim for <math id="A1.SS1.p7.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="B_{n,\mathscr{P}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>B</mi><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>,</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathscript">𝒫</mi></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">B_{n,\mathscr{P}}</annotation></semantics></math> follows directly from Assumption <a href="#S3.Thmasmp3" title="Assumption 3.3. ‣ 3.3 Detection Efficiency and Optimal Scores ‣ 3 A Statistical Framework under Pseudorandomness Collision ‣ Optimal Detection for Language Watermarks with Pseudorandom Collision" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">3.3</span></a> <a href="#S3.I3.i3" title="item (iii) ‣ Assumption 3.3. ‣ 3.3 Detection Efficiency and Optimal Scores ‣ 3 A Statistical Framework under Pseudorandomness Collision ‣ Optimal Detection for Language Watermarks with Pseudorandom Collision" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">(iii)</span></a>. We now prove the result for <math id="A1.SS1.p7.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="D_{n,\mathscr{P}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>D</mi><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>,</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathscript">𝒫</mi></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">D_{n,\mathscr{P}}</annotation></semantics></math>.
Let <math id="A1.SS1.p7.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\theta_{B}^{\star}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msubsup><mi>θ</mi><mi>B</mi><mo>⋆</mo></msubsup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\theta_{B}^{\star}</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="A1.SS1.p7.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\theta_{D}^{\star}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msubsup><mi>θ</mi><mi>D</mi><mo>⋆</mo></msubsup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\theta_{D}^{\star}</annotation></semantics></math> denote the optimal values of <math id="A1.SS1.p7.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\theta" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>θ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\theta</annotation></semantics></math> for <math id="A1.SS1.p7.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="B_{n,\mathscr{P}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>B</mi><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>,</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathscript">𝒫</mi></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">B_{n,\mathscr{P}}</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="A1.SS1.p7.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="D_{n,\mathscr{P}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>D</mi><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>,</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathscript">𝒫</mi></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">D_{n,\mathscr{P}}</annotation></semantics></math>, respectively.
For any fixed <math id="A1.SS1.p7.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\theta\geq 0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>θ</mi><mo>≥</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\theta\geq 0</annotation></semantics></math>, define</span></p>
<table id="A1.EGx21" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A1.E35"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.E35.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle b_{n,\mathscr{P},{\bm{h}}}(\theta)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>b</mi><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>,</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathscript">𝒫</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>𝒉</mi></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>θ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle b_{n,\mathscr{P},{\bm{h}}}(\theta)</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.E35.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle:=\theta\,\EB_{0}[h_{{\mathcal{V}}}]+\frac{1}{N_{n}}\sum_{{\mathcal{V}}\in\Pi}\sup_{\bm{P}_{{\mathcal{V}}}\subseteq{\mathcal{P}}_{{\mathcal{V}}}}\log\phi_{\bm{P}_{{\mathcal{V}}},h_{{\mathcal{V}}}}(\theta)," display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>θ</mi><mo lspace="0.337em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>𝔼</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><msub><mi>h</mi><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒱</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mn>1</mn><msub><mi>N</mi><mi>n</mi></msub></mfrac></mstyle><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munder><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒱</mi><mo>∈</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">Π</mi></mrow></munder></mstyle><mrow><munder><mo lspace="0.167em" movablelimits="false" rspace="0.167em">sup</mo><mrow><msub><mi>𝐏</mi><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒱</mi></msub><mo>⊆</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒫</mi><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒱</mi></msub></mrow></munder><mrow><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><msub><mi>ϕ</mi><mrow><msub><mi>𝐏</mi><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒱</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>h</mi><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒱</mi></msub></mrow></msub></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>θ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle:=\theta\,\EB_{0}[h_{{\mathcal{V}}}]+\frac{1}{N_{n}}\sum_{{\mathcal{V}}\in\Pi}\sup_{\bm{P}_{{\mathcal{V}}}\subseteq{\mathcal{P}}_{{\mathcal{V}}}}\log\phi_{\bm{P}_{{\mathcal{V}}},h_{{\mathcal{V}}}}(\theta),</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(35)</span></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A1.E36"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.E36.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle d_{n,\mathscr{P},{\bm{h}}}(\theta)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>d</mi><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>,</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathscript">𝒫</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>𝒉</mi></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>θ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle d_{n,\mathscr{P},{\bm{h}}}(\theta)</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.E36.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle:=\frac{\theta\gamma_{n,\alpha}}{N_{n}}+\frac{1}{N_{n}}\sum_{{\mathcal{V}}\in\Pi}\sup_{\bm{P}_{{\mathcal{V}}}\subseteq{\mathcal{P}}_{{\mathcal{V}}}}\log\phi_{\bm{P}_{{\mathcal{V}}},h_{{\mathcal{V}}}}(\theta)." display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><mi>θ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>γ</mi><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>α</mi></mrow></msub></mrow><msub><mi>N</mi><mi>n</mi></msub></mfrac></mstyle><mo>+</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mn>1</mn><msub><mi>N</mi><mi>n</mi></msub></mfrac></mstyle><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munder><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒱</mi><mo>∈</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">Π</mi></mrow></munder></mstyle><mrow><munder><mo lspace="0.167em" movablelimits="false" rspace="0.167em">sup</mo><mrow><msub><mi>𝑷</mi><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒱</mi></msub><mo>⊆</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒫</mi><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒱</mi></msub></mrow></munder><mrow><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><msub><mi>ϕ</mi><mrow><msub><mi>𝑷</mi><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒱</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>h</mi><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒱</mi></msub></mrow></msub></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>θ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle:=\frac{\theta\gamma_{n,\alpha}}{N_{n}}+\frac{1}{N_{n}}\sum_{{\mathcal{V}}\in\Pi}\sup_{\bm{P}_{{\mathcal{V}}}\subseteq{\mathcal{P}}_{{\mathcal{V}}}}\log\phi_{\bm{P}_{{\mathcal{V}}},h_{{\mathcal{V}}}}(\theta).</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(36)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A1.SS1.p7.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="A1.SS1.p7.2.1" class="ltx_text">Both functions are convex in <math id="A1.SS1.p7.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\theta" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>θ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\theta</annotation></semantics></math> and we have <math id="A1.SS1.p7.m10" class="ltx_Math" alttext="b^{\prime}_{n,\mathscr{P},{\bm{h}}}(\theta_{B}^{\star})=0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msubsup><mi>b</mi><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>,</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathscript">𝒫</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>𝒉</mi></mrow><mo>′</mo></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msubsup><mi>θ</mi><mi>B</mi><mo>⋆</mo></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">b^{\prime}_{n,\mathscr{P},{\bm{h}}}(\theta_{B}^{\star})=0</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="A1.SS1.p7.m11" class="ltx_Math" alttext="d^{\prime}_{n,\mathscr{P},{\bm{h}}}(\theta_{D}^{\star})=0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msubsup><mi>d</mi><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>,</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathscript">𝒫</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>𝒉</mi></mrow><mo>′</mo></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msubsup><mi>θ</mi><mi>D</mi><mo>⋆</mo></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">d^{\prime}_{n,\mathscr{P},{\bm{h}}}(\theta_{D}^{\star})=0</annotation></semantics></math>.
By Assumption <a href="#S3.Thmasmp3" title="Assumption 3.3. ‣ 3.3 Detection Efficiency and Optimal Scores ‣ 3 A Statistical Framework under Pseudorandomness Collision ‣ Optimal Detection for Language Watermarks with Pseudorandom Collision" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">3.3</span></a> <a href="#S3.I3.i3" title="item (iii) ‣ Assumption 3.3. ‣ 3.3 Detection Efficiency and Optimal Scores ‣ 3 A Statistical Framework under Pseudorandomness Collision ‣ Optimal Detection for Language Watermarks with Pseudorandom Collision" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">(iii)</span></a>, there exists a universal constant <math id="A1.SS1.p7.m12" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\overline{M}&gt;0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mover accent="true"><mi>M</mi><mo stretchy="true">¯</mo></mover><mo>&gt;</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\overline{M}&gt;0</annotation></semantics></math>, independent of <math id="A1.SS1.p7.m13" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\Pi" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi mathvariant="normal">Π</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Pi</annotation></semantics></math>, such that <math id="A1.SS1.p7.m14" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\theta_{B}^{\star}&lt;\overline{M}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msubsup><mi>θ</mi><mi>B</mi><mo>⋆</mo></msubsup><mo>&lt;</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>M</mi><mo stretchy="true">¯</mo></mover></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\theta_{B}^{\star}&lt;\overline{M}</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="A1.SS1.p7.m15" class="ltx_Math" alttext="b^{\prime}_{n,\mathscr{P},{\bm{h}}}(\overline{M})&gt;c&gt;0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msubsup><mi>b</mi><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>,</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathscript">𝒫</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>𝒉</mi></mrow><mo>′</mo></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>M</mi><mo stretchy="true">¯</mo></mover><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>&gt;</mo><mi>c</mi><mo>&gt;</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">b^{\prime}_{n,\mathscr{P},{\bm{h}}}(\overline{M})&gt;c&gt;0</annotation></semantics></math> for some constant <math id="A1.SS1.p7.m16" class="ltx_Math" alttext="c" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>c</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">c</annotation></semantics></math>. Moreover, Lemma <a href="#A1.Thmlem1" title="Lemma A.1. ‣ Proof of Theorem . ‣ A.1 Proof of Theorem ‣ Appendix A Proof for the General Framework ‣ Optimal Detection for Language Watermarks with Pseudorandom Collision" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">A.1</span></a> implies that when <math id="A1.SS1.p7.m17" class="ltx_Math" alttext="N_{n}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>N</mi><mi>n</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">N_{n}</annotation></semantics></math> is sufficiently large, we also have <math id="A1.SS1.p7.m18" class="ltx_Math" alttext="d^{\prime}_{n,\mathscr{P},{\bm{h}}}(\overline{M})&gt;c/2&gt;0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msubsup><mi>d</mi><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>,</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathscript">𝒫</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>𝒉</mi></mrow><mo>′</mo></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>M</mi><mo stretchy="true">¯</mo></mover><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>&gt;</mo><mrow><mi>c</mi><mo>/</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow><mo>&gt;</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">d^{\prime}_{n,\mathscr{P},{\bm{h}}}(\overline{M})&gt;c/2&gt;0</annotation></semantics></math>.
Therefore, for large enough <math id="A1.SS1.p7.m19" class="ltx_Math" alttext="N_{n}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>N</mi><mi>n</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">N_{n}</annotation></semantics></math>, the minimizer <math id="A1.SS1.p7.m20" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\theta_{D}^{\star}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msubsup><mi>θ</mi><mi>D</mi><mo>⋆</mo></msubsup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\theta_{D}^{\star}</annotation></semantics></math> must also satisfy <math id="A1.SS1.p7.m21" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\theta_{D}^{\star}&lt;\overline{M}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msubsup><mi>θ</mi><mi>D</mi><mo>⋆</mo></msubsup><mo>&lt;</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>M</mi><mo stretchy="true">¯</mo></mover></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\theta_{D}^{\star}&lt;\overline{M}</annotation></semantics></math>, completing the proof.
∎</span></p>
</div>
</div>
</section>
<section id="A1.SS2" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection">A.2 </span>Asymptotic Tightness</h3>

<div id="A1.SS2.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A1.SS2.p1.1" class="ltx_p">In this subsection, we show that the lower bound in Theorem <a href="#S3.Thmthm1" title="Theorem 3.1 (Explicit lower bound for detection efficiency). ‣ 3.3 Detection Efficiency and Optimal Scores ‣ 3 A Statistical Framework under Pseudorandomness Collision ‣ Optimal Detection for Language Watermarks with Pseudorandom Collision" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">3.1</span></a> is asymptotically tight under a set of standard regularity conditions. We first introduce the assumptions required for this result. The interpretation and justification of Assumption <a href="#A1.Thmasmp1" title="Assumption A.1 (Regularity conditions for lower bound tightness). ‣ A.2 Asymptotic Tightness ‣ Appendix A Proof for the General Framework ‣ Optimal Detection for Language Watermarks with Pseudorandom Collision" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">A.1</span></a> are in Section <a href="#A1.SS8" title="A.8 Verification of Regularity Conditions for Considered Watermarks ‣ Appendix A Proof for the General Framework ‣ Optimal Detection for Language Watermarks with Pseudorandom Collision" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">A.8</span></a>.</p>
</div>
<div id="A1.Thmasmp1" class="ltx_theorem ltx_theorem_asmp">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_title_theorem"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_theorem"><span id="A1.Thmasmp1.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Assumption A.1</span></span><span id="A1.Thmasmp1.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold"> </span>(Regularity conditions for lower bound tightness)<span id="A1.Thmasmp1.4" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">.</span></h6>
<div id="A1.Thmasmp1.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A1.Thmasmp1.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A1.Thmasmp1.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">We assume that</span></p>
<ol id="A1.I2" class="ltx_enumerate">
<li id="A1.I2.i1" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">1.</span> 
<div id="A1.I2.i1.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A1.I2.i1.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A1.I2.i1.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold ltx_font_italic">(Finite maximizers)</span><span id="A1.I2.i1.p1.1.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic"> For each minimal unit </span><math id="A1.I2.i1.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="{\mathcal{V}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒱</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\mathcal{V}}</annotation></semantics></math><span id="A1.I2.i1.p1.1.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic"> and all </span><math id="A1.I2.i1.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\theta\geq 0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>θ</mi><mo>≥</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\theta\geq 0</annotation></semantics></math><span id="A1.I2.i1.p1.1.4" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">, the supremum of the MGF over the belief class </span><math id="A1.I2.i1.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="{\mathcal{P}}_{{\mathcal{V}}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒫</mi><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒱</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\mathcal{P}}_{{\mathcal{V}}}</annotation></semantics></math><span id="A1.I2.i1.p1.1.5" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic"> is achieved on a finite subset </span><math id="A1.I2.i1.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="{\mathcal{P}}_{{\mathcal{V}}}^{\star}\subseteq{\mathcal{P}}_{{\mathcal{V}}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msubsup><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒫</mi><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒱</mi><mo>⋆</mo></msubsup><mo>⊆</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒫</mi><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒱</mi></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\mathcal{P}}_{{\mathcal{V}}}^{\star}\subseteq{\mathcal{P}}_{{\mathcal{V}}}</annotation></semantics></math><span id="A1.I2.i1.p1.1.6" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">:</span></p>
<table id="A1.Ex40" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A1.Ex40.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\sup_{\bm{P}_{{\mathcal{V}}}\subseteq{\mathcal{P}}_{{\mathcal{V}}}}\phi_{\bm{P}_{{\mathcal{V}}},h_{{\mathcal{V}}}}(\theta)=\sup_{\bm{P}_{{\mathcal{V}}}\subseteq{\mathcal{P}}_{{\mathcal{V}}}^{\star}}\phi_{\bm{P}_{{\mathcal{V}}},h_{{\mathcal{V}}}}(\theta)." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><munder><mo movablelimits="false">sup</mo><mrow><msub><mi>𝑷</mi><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒱</mi></msub><mo>⊆</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒫</mi><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒱</mi></msub></mrow></munder><mrow><msub><mi>ϕ</mi><mrow><msub><mi>𝑷</mi><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒱</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>h</mi><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒱</mi></msub></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>θ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.1389em">=</mo><mrow><munder><mo lspace="0.1389em" movablelimits="false" rspace="0.167em">sup</mo><mrow><msub><mi>𝑷</mi><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒱</mi></msub><mo>⊆</mo><msubsup><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒫</mi><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒱</mi><mo>⋆</mo></msubsup></mrow></munder><mrow><msub><mi>ϕ</mi><mrow><msub><mi>𝑷</mi><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒱</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>h</mi><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒱</mi></msub></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>θ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\sup_{\bm{P}_{{\mathcal{V}}}\subseteq{\mathcal{P}}_{{\mathcal{V}}}}\phi_{\bm{P}_{{\mathcal{V}}},h_{{\mathcal{V}}}}(\theta)=\sup_{\bm{P}_{{\mathcal{V}}}\subseteq{\mathcal{P}}_{{\mathcal{V}}}^{\star}}\phi_{\bm{P}_{{\mathcal{V}}},h_{{\mathcal{V}}}}(\theta).</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div></li>
<li id="A1.I2.i2" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">2.</span> 
<div id="A1.I2.i2.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A1.I2.i2.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A1.I2.i2.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold ltx_font_italic">(Informative scores)</span><span id="A1.I2.i2.p1.1.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic"> The score functions </span><math id="A1.I2.i2.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="{\bm{h}}=\{h_{{\mathcal{V}}}\}_{{\mathcal{V}}\in\Pi}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>𝒉</mi><mo>=</mo><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><msub><mi>h</mi><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒱</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒱</mi><mo>∈</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">Π</mi></mrow></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\bm{h}}=\{h_{{\mathcal{V}}}\}_{{\mathcal{V}}\in\Pi}</annotation></semantics></math><span id="A1.I2.i2.p1.1.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic"> are informative in the sense that, for every minimal unit </span><math id="A1.I2.i2.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="{\mathcal{V}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒱</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\mathcal{V}}</annotation></semantics></math><span id="A1.I2.i2.p1.1.4" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">, </span><math id="A1.I2.i2.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\EB_{0}[h_{{\mathcal{V}}}(Y_{{\mathcal{V}}})]&lt;\EB_{1,\bm{P}_{{\mathcal{V}}}}[h_{{\mathcal{V}}}(Y_{{\mathcal{V}}})]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>𝔼</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><msub><mi>h</mi><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒱</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>Y</mi><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒱</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>&lt;</mo><mrow><msub><mi>𝔼</mi><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>𝐏</mi><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒱</mi></msub></mrow></msub><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><msub><mi>h</mi><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒱</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>Y</mi><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒱</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\EB_{0}[h_{{\mathcal{V}}}(Y_{{\mathcal{V}}})]&lt;\EB_{1,\bm{P}_{{\mathcal{V}}}}[h_{{\mathcal{V}}}(Y_{{\mathcal{V}}})]</annotation></semantics></math><span id="A1.I2.i2.p1.1.5" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic"> for all </span><math id="A1.I2.i2.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\bm{P}_{{\mathcal{V}}}\subseteq{\mathcal{P}}_{{\mathcal{V}}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>𝑷</mi><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒱</mi></msub><mo>⊆</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒫</mi><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒱</mi></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\bm{P}_{{\mathcal{V}}}\subseteq{\mathcal{P}}_{{\mathcal{V}}}</annotation></semantics></math><span id="A1.I2.i2.p1.1.6" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">.</span></p>
</div></li>
<li id="A1.I2.i3" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">3.</span> 
<div id="A1.I2.i3.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A1.I2.i3.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A1.I2.i3.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold ltx_font_italic">(CGF regularity)</span><span id="A1.I2.i3.p1.1.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic"> For all </span><math id="A1.I2.i3.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\bm{P}_{{\mathcal{V}}}\subseteq{\mathcal{P}}_{{\mathcal{V}}}^{\star}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>𝑷</mi><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒱</mi></msub><mo>⊆</mo><msubsup><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒫</mi><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒱</mi><mo>⋆</mo></msubsup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\bm{P}_{{\mathcal{V}}}\subseteq{\mathcal{P}}_{{\mathcal{V}}}^{\star}</annotation></semantics></math><span id="A1.I2.i3.p1.1.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">, the cumulant generating function </span><math id="A1.I2.i3.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\log\phi_{\bm{P}_{{\mathcal{V}}},h_{{\mathcal{V}}}}(\theta)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><msub><mi>ϕ</mi><mrow><msub><mi>𝑷</mi><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒱</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>h</mi><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒱</mi></msub></mrow></msub></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>θ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\log\phi_{\bm{P}_{{\mathcal{V}}},h_{{\mathcal{V}}}}(\theta)</annotation></semantics></math><span id="A1.I2.i3.p1.1.4" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic"> is well-defined and smooth on its domain. Moreover, for any compact set </span><math id="A1.I2.i3.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="K" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>K</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">K</annotation></semantics></math><span id="A1.I2.i3.p1.1.5" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic"> inside its domain, there exist constants </span><math id="A1.I2.i3.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="0&lt;\sigma^{2}_{\min}(K),C_{k}(K)&lt;\infty" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mn>0</mn><mo>&lt;</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>σ</mi><mi>min</mi><mn>2</mn></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>K</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>C</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>K</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>&lt;</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">∞</mi></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">0&lt;\sigma^{2}_{\min}(K),C_{k}(K)&lt;\infty</annotation></semantics></math><span id="A1.I2.i3.p1.1.6" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic"> such that for all </span><math id="A1.I2.i3.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\theta\in K" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>θ</mi><mo>∈</mo><mi>K</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\theta\in K</annotation></semantics></math><span id="A1.I2.i3.p1.1.7" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">:</span></p>
<ul id="A1.I2.i3.I1" class="ltx_itemize">
<li id="A1.I2.i3.I1.ix1" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">(i)</span> 
<div id="A1.I2.i3.I1.ix1.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A1.I2.i3.I1.ix1.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><math id="A1.I2.i3.I1.ix1.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\sigma^{2}_{\min}(K)\leq\displaystyle\frac{{\mathrm{d}}^{2}}{{\mathrm{d}}\theta^{2}}\log\phi_{\bm{P}_{{\mathcal{V}}},h_{{\mathcal{V}}}}(\theta)\leq C_{2}(K)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msubsup><mi>σ</mi><mi>min</mi><mn>2</mn></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>K</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>≤</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><msup><mi>d</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>θ</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow></mfrac></mstyle><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><msub><mi>ϕ</mi><mrow><msub><mi>𝑷</mi><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒱</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>h</mi><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒱</mi></msub></mrow></msub></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>θ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>≤</mo><mrow><msub><mi>C</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>K</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\sigma^{2}_{\min}(K)\leq\displaystyle\frac{{\mathrm{d}}^{2}}{{\mathrm{d}}\theta^{2}}\log\phi_{\bm{P}_{{\mathcal{V}}},h_{{\mathcal{V}}}}(\theta)\leq C_{2}(K)</annotation></semantics></math><span id="A1.I2.i3.I1.ix1.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">.</span></p>
</div></li>
<li id="A1.I2.i3.I1.ix2" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">(ii)</span> 
<div id="A1.I2.i3.I1.ix2.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A1.I2.i3.I1.ix2.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><math id="A1.I2.i3.I1.ix2.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\left|\frac{{\mathrm{d}}^{k}}{{\mathrm{d}}\theta^{k}}\log\phi_{\bm{P}_{{\mathcal{V}}},h_{{\mathcal{V}}}}(\theta)\right|\leq C_{k}(K)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mo>|</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><msup><mi>d</mi><mi>k</mi></msup><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>θ</mi><mi>k</mi></msup></mrow></mfrac></mstyle><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><msub><mi>ϕ</mi><mrow><msub><mi>𝑷</mi><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒱</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>h</mi><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒱</mi></msub></mrow></msub></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>θ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>|</mo></mrow><mo>≤</mo><mrow><msub><mi>C</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>K</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\left|\frac{{\mathrm{d}}^{k}}{{\mathrm{d}}\theta^{k}}\log\phi_{\bm{P}_{{\mathcal{V}}},h_{{\mathcal{V}}}}(\theta)\right|\leq C_{k}(K)</annotation></semantics></math><span id="A1.I2.i3.I1.ix2.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic"> for </span><math id="A1.I2.i3.I1.ix2.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="k=3,4" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>3</mn></mrow><mo>,</mo><mn>4</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">k=3,4</annotation></semantics></math><span id="A1.I2.i3.I1.ix2.p1.1.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">.</span></p>
</div></li>
</ul>
</div></li>
<li id="A1.I2.i4" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">4.</span> 
<div id="A1.I2.i4.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A1.I2.i4.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A1.I2.i4.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold ltx_font_italic">(Score density regularity)</span><span id="A1.I2.i4.p1.1.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">
The set of size-one minimal units is </span><math id="A1.I2.i4.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\Pi_{1}:=\{{\mathcal{V}}\in\Pi:|{\mathcal{V}}|=1\}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Π</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>:=</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒱</mi><mo>∈</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">Π</mi></mrow><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒱</mi><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Pi_{1}:=\{{\mathcal{V}}\in\Pi:|{\mathcal{V}}|=1\}</annotation></semantics></math><span id="A1.I2.i4.p1.1.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">, representing all non-repetitive tokens. We assume that these units are sufficiently large and regular. In particular, there exist universal constants </span><math id="A1.I2.i4.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="c,\lambda&gt;0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>c</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>λ</mi></mrow><mo>&gt;</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">c,\lambda&gt;0</annotation></semantics></math><span id="A1.I2.i4.p1.1.4" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic"> and </span><math id="A1.I2.i4.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="C_{BV}&lt;\infty" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>C</mi><mrow><mi>B</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>V</mi></mrow></msub><mo>&lt;</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">∞</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">C_{BV}&lt;\infty</annotation></semantics></math><span id="A1.I2.i4.p1.1.5" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic"> such that, for all </span><math id="A1.I2.i4.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="N_{n}&gt;0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>N</mi><mi>n</mi></msub><mo>&gt;</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">N_{n}&gt;0</annotation></semantics></math><span id="A1.I2.i4.p1.1.6" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">, the size of </span><math id="A1.I2.i4.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\Pi_{1}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Π</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Pi_{1}</annotation></semantics></math><span id="A1.I2.i4.p1.1.7" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic"> satisfies </span><math id="A1.I2.i4.p1.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="|\Pi_{1}|\geq cN_{n}^{\lambda}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Π</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow><mo>≥</mo><mrow><mi>c</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>N</mi><mi>n</mi><mi>λ</mi></msubsup></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">|\Pi_{1}|\geq cN_{n}^{\lambda}</annotation></semantics></math><span id="A1.I2.i4.p1.1.8" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">. Furthermore, for any </span><math id="A1.I2.i4.p1.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="{\mathcal{V}}\in\Pi_{1}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒱</mi><mo>∈</mo><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Π</mi><mn>1</mn></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\mathcal{V}}\in\Pi_{1}</annotation></semantics></math><span id="A1.I2.i4.p1.1.9" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">, the score density has uniformly bounded total variation:</span></p>
<table id="A1.Ex41" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A1.Ex41.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\sup_{\bm{P}_{{\mathcal{V}}}\subseteq{\mathcal{P}}_{{\mathcal{V}}}^{\star}}\mathrm{TV}(\rho_{\bm{P}_{{\mathcal{V}}}})\leq C_{BV}," display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><munder><mo movablelimits="false">sup</mo><mrow><msub><mi>𝑷</mi><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒱</mi></msub><mo>⊆</mo><msubsup><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒫</mi><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒱</mi><mo>⋆</mo></msubsup></mrow></munder><mrow><mi>TV</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>ρ</mi><msub><mi>𝑷</mi><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒱</mi></msub></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>≤</mo><msub><mi>C</mi><mrow><mi>B</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>V</mi></mrow></msub></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\sup_{\bm{P}_{{\mathcal{V}}}\subseteq{\mathcal{P}}_{{\mathcal{V}}}^{\star}}\mathrm{TV}(\rho_{\bm{P}_{{\mathcal{V}}}})\leq C_{BV},</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A1.I2.i4.p1.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="A1.I2.i4.p1.2.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">where </span><math id="A1.I2.i4.p1.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\rho_{\bm{P}_{{\mathcal{V}}}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>ρ</mi><msub><mi>𝑷</mi><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒱</mi></msub></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\rho_{\bm{P}_{{\mathcal{V}}}}</annotation></semantics></math><span id="A1.I2.i4.p1.2.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic"> denotes the alternative PDF of </span><math id="A1.I2.i4.p1.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="h_{{\mathcal{V}}}(Y_{{\mathcal{V}}})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>h</mi><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒱</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>Y</mi><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒱</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">h_{{\mathcal{V}}}(Y_{{\mathcal{V}}})</annotation></semantics></math><span id="A1.I2.i4.p1.2.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic"> under NTP distributions </span><math id="A1.I2.i4.p1.m10" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\bm{P}_{{\mathcal{V}}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>𝑷</mi><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒱</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\bm{P}_{{\mathcal{V}}}</annotation></semantics></math><span id="A1.I2.i4.p1.2.4" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">, and </span><math id="A1.I2.i4.p1.m11" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathrm{TV}(\rho):=\int_{-\infty}^{\infty}|\rho^{\prime}(x)|,{\mathrm{d}}x" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>TV</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>ρ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.111em">:=</mo><mrow><msubsup><mo rspace="0em">∫</mo><mrow><mo>−</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">∞</mi></mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">∞</mi></msubsup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><mrow><msup><mi>ρ</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo><mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">𝑑</mo><mi>x</mi></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathrm{TV}(\rho):=\int_{-\infty}^{\infty}|\rho^{\prime}(x)|,{\mathrm{d}}x</annotation></semantics></math><span id="A1.I2.i4.p1.2.5" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic"> is the total variation of </span><math id="A1.I2.i4.p1.m12" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\rho" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>ρ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\rho</annotation></semantics></math><span id="A1.I2.i4.p1.2.6" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">.</span></p>
</div></li>
</ol>
</div>
</div>
<div id="A1.SS2.p2" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A1.SS2.p2.1" class="ltx_p">The assumptions in Assumption <a href="#A1.Thmasmp1" title="Assumption A.1 (Regularity conditions for lower bound tightness). ‣ A.2 Asymptotic Tightness ‣ Appendix A Proof for the General Framework ‣ Optimal Detection for Language Watermarks with Pseudorandom Collision" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">A.1</span></a> are mild and largely standard in statistical analysis. The finite maximizer condition simply restricts attention to a finite representative subset of distributions without narrowing the generality of the belief class. The informativeness requirement ensures that the scores meaningfully distinguish between null and alternative distributions, which is fundamental for any detection framework. The regularity of the cumulant generating function (CGF) is a standard smoothness condition, guaranteeing that variance and higher-order moments remain controlled on compact sets. Finally, the score density regularity condition leverages the abundance of non-repetitive tokens in typical texts, making the growth and bounded-variation requirements natural and broadly satisfied in practice. Together, these conditions provide technical tractability while remaining weak enough to encompass a wide range of realistic scenarios. The verification of those assumptions in our case is in Section <a href="#A1.SS8" title="A.8 Verification of Regularity Conditions for Considered Watermarks ‣ Appendix A Proof for the General Framework ‣ Optimal Detection for Language Watermarks with Pseudorandom Collision" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">A.8</span></a>.</p>
</div>
<div id="A1.Thmthm1" class="ltx_theorem ltx_theorem_thm">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_title_theorem"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_theorem"><span id="A1.Thmthm1.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Theorem A.1</span></span><span id="A1.Thmthm1.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold"> </span>(Formal version of Remark <a href="#S3.Thmrem3" title="Remark 3.3 (Asymptotic tightness). ‣ 3.3 Detection Efficiency and Optimal Scores ‣ 3 A Statistical Framework under Pseudorandomness Collision ‣ Optimal Detection for Language Watermarks with Pseudorandom Collision" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">3.3</span></a>)<span id="A1.Thmthm1.4" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">.</span></h6>
<div id="A1.Thmthm1.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A1.Thmthm1.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A1.Thmthm1.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">Suppose Assumptions <a href="#S3.Thmasmp3" title="Assumption 3.3. ‣ 3.3 Detection Efficiency and Optimal Scores ‣ 3 A Statistical Framework under Pseudorandomness Collision ‣ Optimal Detection for Language Watermarks with Pseudorandom Collision" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">3.3</span></a> and <a href="#A1.Thmasmp1" title="Assumption A.1 (Regularity conditions for lower bound tightness). ‣ A.2 Asymptotic Tightness ‣ Appendix A Proof for the General Framework ‣ Optimal Detection for Language Watermarks with Pseudorandom Collision" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">A.1</span></a> hold. Then, the lower bound <math id="A1.Thmthm1.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="B_{n,\mathscr{P}}({\bm{h}})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>B</mi><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>,</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathscript">𝒫</mi></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝐡</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">B_{n,\mathscr{P}}({\bm{h}})</annotation></semantics></math>, defined in (<a href="#S3.E9" title="In Theorem 3.1 (Explicit lower bound for detection efficiency). ‣ 3.3 Detection Efficiency and Optimal Scores ‣ 3 A Statistical Framework under Pseudorandomness Collision ‣ Optimal Detection for Language Watermarks with Pseudorandom Collision" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">9</span></a>), is asymptotically tight, in the sense that</span></p>
<table id="A1.Ex42" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A1.Ex42.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\left|R_{n,{\mathcal{P}}}({\bm{h}})-B_{n,\mathscr{P}}({\bm{h}})\right|\leq\omega_{N_{n}}," display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mo>|</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>R</mi><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>,</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒫</mi></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝒉</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><msub><mi>B</mi><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>,</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathscript">𝒫</mi></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝒉</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>|</mo></mrow><mo>≤</mo><msub><mi>ω</mi><msub><mi>N</mi><mi>n</mi></msub></msub></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\left|R_{n,{\mathcal{P}}}({\bm{h}})-B_{n,\mathscr{P}}({\bm{h}})\right|\leq\omega_{N_{n}},</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A1.Thmthm1.p1.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="A1.Thmthm1.p1.2.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">where <math id="A1.Thmthm1.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\omega_{N_{n}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>ω</mi><msub><mi>N</mi><mi>n</mi></msub></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\omega_{N_{n}}</annotation></semantics></math> is a deterministic function of <math id="A1.Thmthm1.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="N_{n}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>N</mi><mi>n</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">N_{n}</annotation></semantics></math> satisfying <math id="A1.Thmthm1.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\omega_{N_{n}}\to 0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>ω</mi><msub><mi>N</mi><mi>n</mi></msub></msub><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\omega_{N_{n}}\to 0</annotation></semantics></math> as <math id="A1.Thmthm1.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="N_{n}\to\infty" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>N</mi><mi>n</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">∞</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">N_{n}\to\infty</annotation></semantics></math>.</span></p>
</div>
</div>
<div id="A1.SS2.2" class="ltx_proof">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_font_italic ltx_title_proof">Proof of Theorem <a href="#A1.Thmthm1" title="Theorem A.1 (Formal version of Remark ). ‣ A.2 Asymptotic Tightness ‣ Appendix A Proof for the General Framework ‣ Optimal Detection for Language Watermarks with Pseudorandom Collision" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">A.1</span></a>.</h6>
<div id="A1.SS2.p3" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A1.SS2.p3.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A1.SS2.p3.1.1" class="ltx_text">Under Assumption <a href="#S3.Thmasmp3" title="Assumption 3.3. ‣ 3.3 Detection Efficiency and Optimal Scores ‣ 3 A Statistical Framework under Pseudorandomness Collision ‣ Optimal Detection for Language Watermarks with Pseudorandom Collision" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">3.3</span></a>, Theorem <a href="#S3.Thmthm1" title="Theorem 3.1 (Explicit lower bound for detection efficiency). ‣ 3.3 Detection Efficiency and Optimal Scores ‣ 3 A Statistical Framework under Pseudorandomness Collision ‣ Optimal Detection for Language Watermarks with Pseudorandom Collision" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">3.1</span></a> guarantees that</span></p>
<table id="A1.Ex43" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A1.Ex43.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="R_{n,{\mathcal{P}}}({\bm{h}})\geq B_{n,\mathscr{P}}({\bm{h}})-\omega_{N_{n}}." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>R</mi><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>,</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒫</mi></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝒉</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>≥</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>B</mi><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>,</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathscript">𝒫</mi></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝒉</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>ω</mi><msub><mi>N</mi><mi>n</mi></msub></msub></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">R_{n,{\mathcal{P}}}({\bm{h}})\geq B_{n,\mathscr{P}}({\bm{h}})-\omega_{N_{n}}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A1.SS2.p3.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="A1.SS2.p3.2.1" class="ltx_text">To establish asymptotic tightness, it remains to prove the upper bound:</span></p>
<table id="A1.Ex44" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A1.Ex44.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="R_{n,{\mathcal{P}}}({\bm{h}})\leq B_{n,\mathscr{P}}({\bm{h}})+\omega_{N_{n}}," display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>R</mi><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>,</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒫</mi></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝒉</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>≤</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>B</mi><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>,</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathscript">𝒫</mi></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝒉</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><msub><mi>ω</mi><msub><mi>N</mi><mi>n</mi></msub></msub></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">R_{n,{\mathcal{P}}}({\bm{h}})\leq B_{n,\mathscr{P}}({\bm{h}})+\omega_{N_{n}},</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A1.SS2.p3.3" class="ltx_p"><span id="A1.SS2.p3.3.1" class="ltx_text">under the additional Assumption <a href="#A1.Thmasmp1" title="Assumption A.1 (Regularity conditions for lower bound tightness). ‣ A.2 Asymptotic Tightness ‣ Appendix A Proof for the General Framework ‣ Optimal Detection for Language Watermarks with Pseudorandom Collision" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">A.1</span></a>.
To this end, it suffices to show that</span></p>
<table id="A1.E37" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A1.E37.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="R_{n,{\mathcal{P}}}({\bm{h}})\leq D_{n,\mathscr{P}}({\bm{h}})+\omega_{N_{n}}," display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>R</mi><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>,</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒫</mi></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝒉</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>≤</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>D</mi><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>,</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathscript">𝒫</mi></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝒉</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><msub><mi>ω</mi><msub><mi>N</mi><mi>n</mi></msub></msub></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">R_{n,{\mathcal{P}}}({\bm{h}})\leq D_{n,\mathscr{P}}({\bm{h}})+\omega_{N_{n}},</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(37)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A1.SS2.p3.4" class="ltx_p"><span id="A1.SS2.p3.4.1" class="ltx_text">where <math id="A1.SS2.p3.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="D_{n,\mathscr{P}}({\bm{h}})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>D</mi><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>,</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathscript">𝒫</mi></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝒉</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">D_{n,\mathscr{P}}({\bm{h}})</annotation></semantics></math> is the intermediate quantity defined in (<a href="#A1.E32" title="In Proof of Theorem . ‣ A.1 Proof of Theorem ‣ Appendix A Proof for the General Framework ‣ Optimal Detection for Language Watermarks with Pseudorandom Collision" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">32</span></a>). Once this is shown, the result follows from the bound</span></p>
<table id="A1.Ex45" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A1.Ex45.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="|D_{n,\mathscr{P}}({\bm{h}})-B_{n,\mathscr{P}}({\bm{h}})|=\Theta\left(\frac{1}{\sqrt{N_{n}}}\right)" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>D</mi><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>,</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathscript">𝒫</mi></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝒉</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><msub><mi>B</mi><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>,</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathscript">𝒫</mi></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝒉</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Θ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mfrac><mn>1</mn><msqrt><msub><mi>N</mi><mi>n</mi></msub></msqrt></mfrac><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">|D_{n,\mathscr{P}}({\bm{h}})-B_{n,\mathscr{P}}({\bm{h}})|=\Theta\left(\frac{1}{\sqrt{N_{n}}}\right)</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A1.SS2.p3.5" class="ltx_p"><span id="A1.SS2.p3.5.1" class="ltx_text">established in (<a href="#A1.E34" title="In Proof of Theorem . ‣ A.1 Proof of Theorem ‣ Appendix A Proof for the General Framework ‣ Optimal Detection for Language Watermarks with Pseudorandom Collision" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">34</span></a>), completing the proof.</span></p>
</div>
<div id="A1.SS2.p4" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A1.SS2.p4.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A1.SS2.p4.1.1" class="ltx_text">To proceed with the proof, we then introduce some notations.
For each minimal unit <math id="A1.SS2.p4.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="{\mathcal{V}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒱</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\mathcal{V}}</annotation></semantics></math>, the number of possible assignments <math id="A1.SS2.p4.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\bm{P}_{{\mathcal{V}}}\subseteq{\mathcal{P}}_{{\mathcal{V}}}^{\star}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>𝑷</mi><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒱</mi></msub><mo>⊆</mo><msubsup><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒫</mi><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒱</mi><mo>⋆</mo></msubsup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\bm{P}_{{\mathcal{V}}}\subseteq{\mathcal{P}}_{{\mathcal{V}}}^{\star}</annotation></semantics></math> is finite, given that <math id="A1.SS2.p4.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="|{\mathcal{P}}_{{\mathcal{V}}}^{\star}|" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><msubsup><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒫</mi><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒱</mi><mo>⋆</mo></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">|{\mathcal{P}}_{{\mathcal{V}}}^{\star}|</annotation></semantics></math> is finite.
We denote this finite collection of structured assignments by <math id="A1.SS2.p4.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="{\mathcal{Q}}^{\star}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒬</mi><mo>⋆</mo></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\mathcal{Q}}^{\star}</annotation></semantics></math>, defined as</span></p>
<table id="A1.Ex46" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A1.Ex46.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="{\mathcal{Q}}^{\star}=\left\{\{\bm{P}_{{\mathcal{V}}}\}_{{\mathcal{V}}\in\Pi}:\bm{P}_{{\mathcal{V}}}\subseteq{\mathcal{P}}_{{\mathcal{V}}}^{\star}\right\}." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msup><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒬</mi><mo>⋆</mo></msup><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo>{</mo><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><msub><mi>𝑷</mi><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒱</mi></msub><mo rspace="0.278em" stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒱</mi><mo>∈</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">Π</mi></mrow></msub><mo rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mrow><msub><mi>𝑷</mi><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒱</mi></msub><mo>⊆</mo><msubsup><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒫</mi><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒱</mi><mo>⋆</mo></msubsup></mrow><mo>}</mo></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\mathcal{Q}}^{\star}=\left\{\{\bm{P}_{{\mathcal{V}}}\}_{{\mathcal{V}}\in\Pi}:\bm{P}_{{\mathcal{V}}}\subseteq{\mathcal{P}}_{{\mathcal{V}}}^{\star}\right\}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A1.SS2.p4.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="A1.SS2.p4.2.1" class="ltx_text">Let <math id="A1.SS2.p4.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="{\mathcal{Q}}^{\star}=\{{\mathcal{Q}}_{1}^{\star},\dots,{\mathcal{Q}}_{K}^{\star}\}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msup><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒬</mi><mo>⋆</mo></msup><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><msubsup><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒬</mi><mn>1</mn><mo>⋆</mo></msubsup><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi><mo>,</mo><msubsup><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒬</mi><mi>K</mi><mo>⋆</mo></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\mathcal{Q}}^{\star}=\{{\mathcal{Q}}_{1}^{\star},\dots,{\mathcal{Q}}_{K}^{\star}\}</annotation></semantics></math> be an enumeration of all such combinations, and define the probability simplex over <math id="A1.SS2.p4.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\{1,2,\dots,K\}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>2</mn><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>K</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\{1,2,\dots,K\}</annotation></semantics></math> by</span></p>
<table id="A1.Ex47" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A1.Ex47.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\Lambda:=\left\{\lambda=(\lambda_{1},\dots,\lambda_{K})\in\mathbb{R}^{K}:\lambda_{i}\geq 0,\ \sum_{i=1}^{K}\lambda_{i}=1\right\}." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Λ</mi><mo>:=</mo><mrow><mo>{</mo><mi>λ</mi><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>λ</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>λ</mi><mi>K</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>∈</mo><msup><mi>ℝ</mi><mi>K</mi></msup><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><msub><mi>λ</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>≥</mo><mn>0</mn><mo rspace="0.500em">,</mo><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>K</mi></munderover><msub><mi>λ</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>}</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Lambda:=\left\{\lambda=(\lambda_{1},\dots,\lambda_{K})\in\mathbb{R}^{K}:\lambda_{i}\geq 0,\ \sum_{i=1}^{K}\lambda_{i}=1\right\}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A1.SS2.p4.3" class="ltx_p"><span id="A1.SS2.p4.3.1" class="ltx_text">Each element <math id="A1.SS2.p4.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="{\mathcal{Q}}_{i}^{\star}\in{\mathcal{Q}}^{\star}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msubsup><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒬</mi><mi>i</mi><mo>⋆</mo></msubsup><mo>∈</mo><msup><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒬</mi><mo>⋆</mo></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\mathcal{Q}}_{i}^{\star}\in{\mathcal{Q}}^{\star}</annotation></semantics></math> corresponds to a particular assignment of NTP distributions that potentially attains the supremum in <math id="A1.SS2.p4.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\sup_{\bm{P}_{{\mathcal{V}}}\subseteq{\mathcal{P}}_{{\mathcal{V}}}}\phi_{\bm{P}_{{\mathcal{V}}},h_{{\mathcal{V}}}}(\theta)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mo>sup</mo><mrow><msub><mi>𝑷</mi><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒱</mi></msub><mo>⊆</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒫</mi><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒱</mi></msub></mrow></msub><mrow><msub><mi>ϕ</mi><mrow><msub><mi>𝑷</mi><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒱</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>h</mi><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒱</mi></msub></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>θ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\sup_{\bm{P}_{{\mathcal{V}}}\subseteq{\mathcal{P}}_{{\mathcal{V}}}}\phi_{\bm{P}_{{\mathcal{V}}},h_{{\mathcal{V}}}}(\theta)</annotation></semantics></math>. Specifically, we write <math id="A1.SS2.p4.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="{\mathcal{Q}}_{i}^{\star}=(\bm{Q}_{i,{\mathcal{V}}})_{{\mathcal{V}}\in\Pi}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msubsup><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒬</mi><mi>i</mi><mo>⋆</mo></msubsup><mo>=</mo><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>𝑸</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>,</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒱</mi></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒱</mi><mo>∈</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">Π</mi></mrow></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\mathcal{Q}}_{i}^{\star}=(\bm{Q}_{i,{\mathcal{V}}})_{{\mathcal{V}}\in\Pi}</annotation></semantics></math>, where each minimal unit <math id="A1.SS2.p4.m10" class="ltx_Math" alttext="{\mathcal{V}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒱</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\mathcal{V}}</annotation></semantics></math> is assigned the distributions <math id="A1.SS2.p4.m11" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\bm{Q}_{i,{\mathcal{V}}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>𝑸</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>,</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒱</mi></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\bm{Q}_{i,{\mathcal{V}}}</annotation></semantics></math>. Thus, the index <math id="A1.SS2.p4.m12" class="ltx_Math" alttext="i\in[K]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mi>K</mi><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">i\in[K]</annotation></semantics></math> indexes <math id="A1.SS2.p4.m13" class="ltx_Math" alttext="K" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>K</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">K</annotation></semantics></math> distinct type-wise configurations of NTP distributions across the entire partition <math id="A1.SS2.p4.m14" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\Pi" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi mathvariant="normal">Π</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Pi</annotation></semantics></math>.</span></p>
</div>
<div id="A1.SS2.p5" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A1.SS2.p5.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A1.SS2.p5.1.1" class="ltx_text">Now, we are ready to prove this upper bound (<a href="#A1.E37" title="In Proof of Theorem . ‣ A.2 Asymptotic Tightness ‣ Appendix A Proof for the General Framework ‣ Optimal Detection for Language Watermarks with Pseudorandom Collision" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">37</span></a>). It follows that</span></p>
<table id="A1.EGx22" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A1.Ex48"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.Ex48.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle-R_{n,\mathscr{P}}({\bm{h}})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><msub><mi>R</mi><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>,</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathscript">𝒫</mi></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝒉</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle-R_{n,\mathscr{P}}({\bm{h}})</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.Ex48.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=\frac{1}{N_{n}}\sup_{\bm{P}_{{\mathcal{V}}}\subseteq{\mathcal{P}}_{{\mathcal{V}}},\forall{\mathcal{V}}}\log\EB_{1}(1-\EB_{1}[T_{n}|\{\bm{P}_{{\mathcal{V}}}\}_{{\mathcal{V}}}])," display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mn>1</mn><msub><mi>N</mi><mi>n</mi></msub></mfrac></mstyle><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><munder><mo movablelimits="false" rspace="0.167em">sup</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>𝑷</mi><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒱</mi></msub><mo>⊆</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒫</mi><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒱</mi></msub></mrow><mo>,</mo><mrow><mo rspace="0.167em">∀</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒱</mi></mrow></mrow></munder><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><mrow><msub><mi>𝔼</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mrow><msub><mi>𝔼</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><msub><mi>T</mi><mi>n</mi></msub><mo fence="false" rspace="0.167em" stretchy="false">|</mo><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><msub><mi>𝐏</mi><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒱</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒱</mi></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=\frac{1}{N_{n}}\sup_{\bm{P}_{{\mathcal{V}}}\subseteq{\mathcal{P}}_{{\mathcal{V}}},\forall{\mathcal{V}}}\log\EB_{1}(1-\EB_{1}[T_{n}|\{\bm{P}_{{\mathcal{V}}}\}_{{\mathcal{V}}}]),</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A1.E38"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.E38.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\overset{(a)}{\geq}\max_{\lambda\in\Lambda}\frac{1}{N_{n}}\sum_{i=1}^{K}\lambda_{i}\log\left(1-\EB_{1}[T_{n}\mid\{\bm{P}_{{\mathcal{V}}}\}_{{\mathcal{V}}}={\mathcal{Q}}^{\star}_{i}]\right)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mover accent="true"><mo>≥</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="0.700em" minsize="0.700em">(</mo><mi mathsize="0.700em">a</mi><mo maxsize="0.700em" minsize="0.700em">)</mo></mrow></mover><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><munder><mi>max</mi><mrow><mi>λ</mi><mo>∈</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">Λ</mi></mrow></munder><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mn>1</mn><msub><mi>N</mi><mi>n</mi></msub></mfrac></mstyle><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>K</mi></munderover></mstyle><mrow><msub><mi>λ</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mrow><msub><mi>𝔼</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><msub><mi>T</mi><mi>n</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.167em">∣</mo><mrow><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><msub><mi>𝐏</mi><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒱</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒱</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><msubsup><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒬</mi><mi>i</mi><mo>⋆</mo></msubsup></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\overset{(a)}{\geq}\max_{\lambda\in\Lambda}\frac{1}{N_{n}}\sum_{i=1}^{K}\lambda_{i}\log\left(1-\EB_{1}[T_{n}\mid\{\bm{P}_{{\mathcal{V}}}\}_{{\mathcal{V}}}={\mathcal{Q}}^{\star}_{i}]\right)</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(38)</span></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A1.E39"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.E39.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\overset{(b)}{\geq}\max_{\lambda\in\Lambda}\frac{1}{N_{n}}\sum_{i=1}^{K}\lambda_{i}\left[\min_{\theta\geq 0}\left(\theta\cdot\frac{\gamma_{n,\alpha}}{N_{n}}+\frac{1}{N_{n}}\sum_{{\mathcal{V}}\in\Pi}\log\phi_{\bm{Q}_{i,{\mathcal{V}}},h_{{\mathcal{V}}}}(\theta)\right)-\alpha_{N_{n}}\right]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mover accent="true"><mo>≥</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="0.700em" minsize="0.700em">(</mo><mi mathsize="0.700em">b</mi><mo maxsize="0.700em" minsize="0.700em">)</mo></mrow></mover><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><munder><mi>max</mi><mrow><mi>λ</mi><mo>∈</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">Λ</mi></mrow></munder><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mn>1</mn><msub><mi>N</mi><mi>n</mi></msub></mfrac></mstyle><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>K</mi></munderover></mstyle><mrow><msub><mi>λ</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>[</mo><mrow><mrow><munder><mi>min</mi><mrow><mi>θ</mi><mo>≥</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow></munder><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>θ</mi><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><msub><mi>γ</mi><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>α</mi></mrow></msub><msub><mi>N</mi><mi>n</mi></msub></mfrac></mstyle></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mn>1</mn><msub><mi>N</mi><mi>n</mi></msub></mfrac></mstyle><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munder><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒱</mi><mo>∈</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">Π</mi></mrow></munder></mstyle><mrow><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><msub><mi>ϕ</mi><mrow><msub><mi>𝑸</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>,</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒱</mi></mrow></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>h</mi><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒱</mi></msub></mrow></msub></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>θ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>α</mi><msub><mi>N</mi><mi>n</mi></msub></msub></mrow><mo>]</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\overset{(b)}{\geq}\max_{\lambda\in\Lambda}\frac{1}{N_{n}}\sum_{i=1}^{K}\lambda_{i}\left[\min_{\theta\geq 0}\left(\theta\cdot\frac{\gamma_{n,\alpha}}{N_{n}}+\frac{1}{N_{n}}\sum_{{\mathcal{V}}\in\Pi}\log\phi_{\bm{Q}_{i,{\mathcal{V}}},h_{{\mathcal{V}}}}(\theta)\right)-\alpha_{N_{n}}\right]</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(39)</span></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A1.E40"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.E40.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=\max_{\lambda\in\Lambda}\min_{\theta_{i}\geq 0,\forall i}\frac{1}{N_{n}}\sum_{i=1}^{K}\lambda_{i}\left[\left(\theta_{i}\cdot\frac{\gamma_{n,\alpha}}{N_{n}}+\frac{1}{N_{n}}\sum_{{\mathcal{V}}\in\Pi}\log\phi_{\bm{Q}_{i,{\mathcal{V}}},h_{{\mathcal{V}}}}(\theta_{i})\right)-\alpha_{N_{n}}\right]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><munder><mi>max</mi><mrow><mi>λ</mi><mo>∈</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">Λ</mi></mrow></munder><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><munder><mi>min</mi><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>θ</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>≥</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><mo>,</mo><mrow><mo rspace="0.167em">∀</mo><mi>i</mi></mrow></mrow></munder></mrow><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mn>1</mn><msub><mi>N</mi><mi>n</mi></msub></mfrac></mstyle><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>K</mi></munderover></mstyle><mrow><msub><mi>λ</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>[</mo><mrow><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>θ</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><msub><mi>γ</mi><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>α</mi></mrow></msub><msub><mi>N</mi><mi>n</mi></msub></mfrac></mstyle></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mn>1</mn><msub><mi>N</mi><mi>n</mi></msub></mfrac></mstyle><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munder><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒱</mi><mo>∈</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">Π</mi></mrow></munder></mstyle><mrow><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><msub><mi>ϕ</mi><mrow><msub><mi>𝑸</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>,</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒱</mi></mrow></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>h</mi><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒱</mi></msub></mrow></msub></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>θ</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>α</mi><msub><mi>N</mi><mi>n</mi></msub></msub></mrow><mo>]</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=\max_{\lambda\in\Lambda}\min_{\theta_{i}\geq 0,\forall i}\frac{1}{N_{n}}\sum_{i=1}^{K}\lambda_{i}\left[\left(\theta_{i}\cdot\frac{\gamma_{n,\alpha}}{N_{n}}+\frac{1}{N_{n}}\sum_{{\mathcal{V}}\in\Pi}\log\phi_{\bm{Q}_{i,{\mathcal{V}}},h_{{\mathcal{V}}}}(\theta_{i})\right)-\alpha_{N_{n}}\right]</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(40)</span></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A1.E41"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.E41.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\overset{(c)}{=}\min_{\theta_{i}\geq 0,\forall i}\max_{\lambda\in\Lambda}\frac{1}{N_{n}}\sum_{i=1}^{K}\lambda_{i}\left[\left(\theta_{i}\cdot\frac{\gamma_{n,\alpha}}{N_{n}}+\frac{1}{N_{n}}\sum_{{\mathcal{V}}\in\Pi}\log\phi_{\bm{Q}_{i,{\mathcal{V}}},h_{{\mathcal{V}}}}(\theta_{i})\right)-\alpha_{N_{n}}\right]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mover accent="true"><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="0.700em" minsize="0.700em">(</mo><mi mathsize="0.700em">c</mi><mo maxsize="0.700em" minsize="0.700em">)</mo></mrow></mover><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><munder><mi>min</mi><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>θ</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>≥</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><mo>,</mo><mrow><mo rspace="0.167em">∀</mo><mi>i</mi></mrow></mrow></munder><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><munder><mi>max</mi><mrow><mi>λ</mi><mo>∈</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">Λ</mi></mrow></munder><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mn>1</mn><msub><mi>N</mi><mi>n</mi></msub></mfrac></mstyle><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>K</mi></munderover></mstyle><mrow><msub><mi>λ</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>[</mo><mrow><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>θ</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><msub><mi>γ</mi><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>α</mi></mrow></msub><msub><mi>N</mi><mi>n</mi></msub></mfrac></mstyle></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mn>1</mn><msub><mi>N</mi><mi>n</mi></msub></mfrac></mstyle><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munder><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒱</mi><mo>∈</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">Π</mi></mrow></munder></mstyle><mrow><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><msub><mi>ϕ</mi><mrow><msub><mi>𝑸</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>,</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒱</mi></mrow></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>h</mi><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒱</mi></msub></mrow></msub></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>θ</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>α</mi><msub><mi>N</mi><mi>n</mi></msub></msub></mrow><mo>]</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\overset{(c)}{=}\min_{\theta_{i}\geq 0,\forall i}\max_{\lambda\in\Lambda}\frac{1}{N_{n}}\sum_{i=1}^{K}\lambda_{i}\left[\left(\theta_{i}\cdot\frac{\gamma_{n,\alpha}}{N_{n}}+\frac{1}{N_{n}}\sum_{{\mathcal{V}}\in\Pi}\log\phi_{\bm{Q}_{i,{\mathcal{V}}},h_{{\mathcal{V}}}}(\theta_{i})\right)-\alpha_{N_{n}}\right]</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(41)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A1.SS2.p5.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="A1.SS2.p5.2.1" class="ltx_text">Here, (a) follows from the fact that <math id="A1.SS2.p5.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="{\mathcal{P}}_{{\mathcal{V}}}^{\star}\subseteq{\mathcal{P}}_{{\mathcal{V}}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msubsup><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒫</mi><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒱</mi><mo>⋆</mo></msubsup><mo>⊆</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒫</mi><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒱</mi></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\mathcal{P}}_{{\mathcal{V}}}^{\star}\subseteq{\mathcal{P}}_{{\mathcal{V}}}</annotation></semantics></math> and each <math id="A1.SS2.p5.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="{\mathcal{Q}}_{i}^{\star}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msubsup><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒬</mi><mi>i</mi><mo>⋆</mo></msubsup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\mathcal{Q}}_{i}^{\star}</annotation></semantics></math> specifies a valid instance of <math id="A1.SS2.p5.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\{\bm{P}_{{\mathcal{V}}}\}_{{\mathcal{V}}\in\Pi}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><msub><mi>𝑷</mi><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒱</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒱</mi><mo>∈</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">Π</mi></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\{\bm{P}_{{\mathcal{V}}}\}_{{\mathcal{V}}\in\Pi}</annotation></semantics></math>; (b) applies Lemma <a href="#A1.Thmlem3" title="Lemma A.3 (Non-i.i.d. large deviation lower bound). ‣ Proof of Theorem . ‣ A.2 Asymptotic Tightness ‣ Appendix A Proof for the General Framework ‣ Optimal Detection for Language Watermarks with Pseudorandom Collision" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">A.3</span></a>, which provides a non-asymptotic large deviation bound for independent but non-identically distributed random variables; and (c) uses the minimax theorem in Lemma <a href="#A1.Thmlem4" title="Lemma A.4 (Minimax theorem). ‣ Proof of Theorem . ‣ A.2 Asymptotic Tightness ‣ Appendix A Proof for the General Framework ‣ Optimal Detection for Language Watermarks with Pseudorandom Collision" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">A.4</span></a> to exchange the order of the maximum and the infimum (where we view <math id="A1.SS2.p5.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(\theta_{1},\ldots,\theta_{K})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>θ</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>θ</mi><mi>K</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(\theta_{1},\ldots,\theta_{K})</annotation></semantics></math> as a new <math id="A1.SS2.p5.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\theta" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>θ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\theta</annotation></semantics></math> to apply this lemma). The term <math id="A1.SS2.p5.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\alpha_{N_{n}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>α</mi><msub><mi>N</mi><mi>n</mi></msub></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\alpha_{N_{n}}</annotation></semantics></math> denotes a positive deterministic function of <math id="A1.SS2.p5.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="N_{n}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>N</mi><mi>n</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">N_{n}</annotation></semantics></math> that converges to zero as <math id="A1.SS2.p5.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="N_{n}\to\infty" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>N</mi><mi>n</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">∞</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">N_{n}\to\infty</annotation></semantics></math>.</span></p>
</div>
<div id="A1.SS2.p6" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A1.SS2.p6.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A1.SS2.p6.1.1" class="ltx_text">Consequently, we have</span></p>
<table id="A1.EGx23" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A1.Ex49"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.Ex49.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle-R_{n,\mathscr{P}}({\bm{h}})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><msub><mi>R</mi><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>,</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathscript">𝒫</mi></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝒉</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle-R_{n,\mathscr{P}}({\bm{h}})</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.Ex49.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\overset{(a)}{\geq}\min_{\theta\geq 0}\left\{\theta\cdot\frac{\gamma_{n,\alpha}}{N_{n}}+\frac{1}{N_{n}}\sum_{{\mathcal{V}}\in\Pi}\sup_{\bm{P}_{{\mathcal{V}}}^{\star}\subseteq{\mathcal{P}}^{\star}}\log\phi_{\bm{P}_{{\mathcal{V}}}^{\star},h_{{\mathcal{V}}}}(\theta)\right\}-\alpha_{N_{n}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mover accent="true"><mo>≥</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="0.700em" minsize="0.700em">(</mo><mi mathsize="0.700em">a</mi><mo maxsize="0.700em" minsize="0.700em">)</mo></mrow></mover><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><munder><mi>min</mi><mrow><mi>θ</mi><mo>≥</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow></munder><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>{</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>θ</mi><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><msub><mi>γ</mi><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>α</mi></mrow></msub><msub><mi>N</mi><mi>n</mi></msub></mfrac></mstyle></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mn>1</mn><msub><mi>N</mi><mi>n</mi></msub></mfrac></mstyle><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munder><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒱</mi><mo>∈</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">Π</mi></mrow></munder></mstyle><mrow><munder><mo lspace="0.167em" movablelimits="false" rspace="0.167em">sup</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>𝑷</mi><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒱</mi><mo>⋆</mo></msubsup><mo>⊆</mo><msup><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒫</mi><mo>⋆</mo></msup></mrow></munder><mrow><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><msub><mi>ϕ</mi><mrow><msubsup><mi>𝑷</mi><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒱</mi><mo>⋆</mo></msubsup><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>h</mi><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒱</mi></msub></mrow></msub></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>θ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>}</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>α</mi><msub><mi>N</mi><mi>n</mi></msub></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\overset{(a)}{\geq}\min_{\theta\geq 0}\left\{\theta\cdot\frac{\gamma_{n,\alpha}}{N_{n}}+\frac{1}{N_{n}}\sum_{{\mathcal{V}}\in\Pi}\sup_{\bm{P}_{{\mathcal{V}}}^{\star}\subseteq{\mathcal{P}}^{\star}}\log\phi_{\bm{P}_{{\mathcal{V}}}^{\star},h_{{\mathcal{V}}}}(\theta)\right\}-\alpha_{N_{n}}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A1.Ex50"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.Ex50.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\overset{(b)}{=}\min_{\theta\geq 0}\left\{\theta\cdot\frac{\gamma_{n,\alpha}}{N_{n}}+\frac{1}{N_{n}}\sum_{{\mathcal{V}}\in\Pi}\sup_{\bm{P}_{{\mathcal{V}}}\subseteq{\mathcal{P}}_{{\mathcal{V}}}}\log\phi_{\bm{P}_{{\mathcal{V}}},h_{{\mathcal{V}}}}(\theta)\right\}-\alpha_{N_{n}}." display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mover accent="true"><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="0.700em" minsize="0.700em">(</mo><mi mathsize="0.700em">b</mi><mo maxsize="0.700em" minsize="0.700em">)</mo></mrow></mover><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><munder><mi>min</mi><mrow><mi>θ</mi><mo>≥</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow></munder><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>{</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>θ</mi><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><msub><mi>γ</mi><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>α</mi></mrow></msub><msub><mi>N</mi><mi>n</mi></msub></mfrac></mstyle></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mn>1</mn><msub><mi>N</mi><mi>n</mi></msub></mfrac></mstyle><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munder><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒱</mi><mo>∈</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">Π</mi></mrow></munder></mstyle><mrow><munder><mo lspace="0.167em" movablelimits="false" rspace="0.167em">sup</mo><mrow><msub><mi>𝑷</mi><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒱</mi></msub><mo>⊆</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒫</mi><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒱</mi></msub></mrow></munder><mrow><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><msub><mi>ϕ</mi><mrow><msub><mi>𝑷</mi><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒱</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>h</mi><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒱</mi></msub></mrow></msub></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>θ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>}</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>α</mi><msub><mi>N</mi><mi>n</mi></msub></msub></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\overset{(b)}{=}\min_{\theta\geq 0}\left\{\theta\cdot\frac{\gamma_{n,\alpha}}{N_{n}}+\frac{1}{N_{n}}\sum_{{\mathcal{V}}\in\Pi}\sup_{\bm{P}_{{\mathcal{V}}}\subseteq{\mathcal{P}}_{{\mathcal{V}}}}\log\phi_{\bm{P}_{{\mathcal{V}}},h_{{\mathcal{V}}}}(\theta)\right\}-\alpha_{N_{n}}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A1.SS2.p6.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="A1.SS2.p6.2.1" class="ltx_text">where (a) follows from the fact that the maximum over the simplex is attained at an extreme point, that is, there exists some <math id="A1.SS2.p6.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="i\in[K]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mi>K</mi><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">i\in[K]</annotation></semantics></math> such that each <math id="A1.SS2.p6.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\bm{Q}_{i,{\mathcal{V}}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>𝑸</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>,</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒱</mi></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\bm{Q}_{i,{\mathcal{V}}}</annotation></semantics></math> in <math id="A1.SS2.p6.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="{\mathcal{Q}}_{i}^{\star}=(\bm{Q}_{i,{\mathcal{V}}})_{{\mathcal{V}}\in\Pi}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msubsup><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒬</mi><mi>i</mi><mo>⋆</mo></msubsup><mo>=</mo><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>𝑸</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>,</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒱</mi></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒱</mi><mo>∈</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">Π</mi></mrow></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\mathcal{Q}}_{i}^{\star}=(\bm{Q}_{i,{\mathcal{V}}})_{{\mathcal{V}}\in\Pi}</annotation></semantics></math> achieves the supremum <math id="A1.SS2.p6.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\sup_{\bm{P}_{{\mathcal{V}}}\subseteq{\mathcal{P}}^{\star}}\log\phi_{\bm{P}_{{\mathcal{V}}},h_{{\mathcal{V}}}}(\theta)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mo>sup</mo><mrow><msub><mi>𝑷</mi><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒱</mi></msub><mo>⊆</mo><msup><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒫</mi><mo>⋆</mo></msup></mrow></msub><mrow><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><msub><mi>ϕ</mi><mrow><msub><mi>𝑷</mi><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒱</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>h</mi><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒱</mi></msub></mrow></msub></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>θ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\sup_{\bm{P}_{{\mathcal{V}}}\subseteq{\mathcal{P}}^{\star}}\log\phi_{\bm{P}_{{\mathcal{V}}},h_{{\mathcal{V}}}}(\theta)</annotation></semantics></math>; and (b) uses the condition that <math id="A1.SS2.p6.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\sup_{\bm{P}_{{\mathcal{V}}}\subseteq{\mathcal{P}}_{{\mathcal{V}}}}\phi_{\bm{P}_{{\mathcal{V}}},h_{{\mathcal{V}}}}(\theta)=\sup_{\bm{P}_{{\mathcal{V}}}\subseteq{\mathcal{P}}^{\star}}\phi_{\bm{P}_{{\mathcal{V}}},h_{{\mathcal{V}}}}(\theta)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mo>sup</mo><mrow><msub><mi>𝑷</mi><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒱</mi></msub><mo>⊆</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒫</mi><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒱</mi></msub></mrow></msub><mrow><msub><mi>ϕ</mi><mrow><msub><mi>𝑷</mi><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒱</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>h</mi><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒱</mi></msub></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>θ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.1389em">=</mo><mrow><msub><mo lspace="0.1389em" rspace="0.167em">sup</mo><mrow><msub><mi>𝑷</mi><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒱</mi></msub><mo>⊆</mo><msup><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒫</mi><mo>⋆</mo></msup></mrow></msub><mrow><msub><mi>ϕ</mi><mrow><msub><mi>𝑷</mi><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒱</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>h</mi><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒱</mi></msub></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>θ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\sup_{\bm{P}_{{\mathcal{V}}}\subseteq{\mathcal{P}}_{{\mathcal{V}}}}\phi_{\bm{P}_{{\mathcal{V}}},h_{{\mathcal{V}}}}(\theta)=\sup_{\bm{P}_{{\mathcal{V}}}\subseteq{\mathcal{P}}^{\star}}\phi_{\bm{P}_{{\mathcal{V}}},h_{{\mathcal{V}}}}(\theta)</annotation></semantics></math> for all <math id="A1.SS2.p6.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\theta\geq 0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>θ</mi><mo>≥</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\theta\geq 0</annotation></semantics></math>.</span></p>
</div>
<div id="A1.SS2.p7" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A1.SS2.p7.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A1.SS2.p7.1.1" class="ltx_text">As a result, we obtain the bound</span></p>
<table id="A1.EGx24" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A1.E42"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.E42.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle-R_{n,\mathscr{P}}({\bm{h}})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><msub><mi>R</mi><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>,</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathscript">𝒫</mi></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝒉</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle-R_{n,\mathscr{P}}({\bm{h}})</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.E42.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\geq\min_{\theta\geq 0}\left\{\theta\cdot\frac{\gamma_{n,\alpha}}{N_{n}}+\frac{1}{N_{n}}\sum_{{\mathcal{V}}\in\Pi}\sup_{\bm{P}_{{\mathcal{V}}}\subseteq{\mathcal{P}}_{{\mathcal{V}}}}\log\phi_{\bm{P}_{{\mathcal{V}}},h_{{\mathcal{V}}}}(\theta)\right\}-\alpha_{N_{n}}," display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>≥</mo><mrow><mrow><munder><mi>min</mi><mrow><mi>θ</mi><mo>≥</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow></munder><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>{</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>θ</mi><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><msub><mi>γ</mi><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>α</mi></mrow></msub><msub><mi>N</mi><mi>n</mi></msub></mfrac></mstyle></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mn>1</mn><msub><mi>N</mi><mi>n</mi></msub></mfrac></mstyle><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munder><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒱</mi><mo>∈</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">Π</mi></mrow></munder></mstyle><mrow><munder><mo lspace="0.167em" movablelimits="false" rspace="0.167em">sup</mo><mrow><msub><mi>𝑷</mi><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒱</mi></msub><mo>⊆</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒫</mi><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒱</mi></msub></mrow></munder><mrow><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><msub><mi>ϕ</mi><mrow><msub><mi>𝑷</mi><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒱</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>h</mi><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒱</mi></msub></mrow></msub></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>θ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>}</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>α</mi><msub><mi>N</mi><mi>n</mi></msub></msub></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\geq\min_{\theta\geq 0}\left\{\theta\cdot\frac{\gamma_{n,\alpha}}{N_{n}}+\frac{1}{N_{n}}\sum_{{\mathcal{V}}\in\Pi}\sup_{\bm{P}_{{\mathcal{V}}}\subseteq{\mathcal{P}}_{{\mathcal{V}}}}\log\phi_{\bm{P}_{{\mathcal{V}}},h_{{\mathcal{V}}}}(\theta)\right\}-\alpha_{N_{n}},</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(42)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A1.SS2.p7.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="A1.SS2.p7.2.1" class="ltx_text">which implies the upper bound</span></p>
<table id="A1.Ex51" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A1.Ex51.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="R_{n,{\mathcal{P}}}({\bm{h}})\leq D_{n,\mathscr{P}}({\bm{h}})+\alpha_{N_{n}}." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>R</mi><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>,</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒫</mi></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝒉</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>≤</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>D</mi><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>,</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathscript">𝒫</mi></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝒉</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><msub><mi>α</mi><msub><mi>N</mi><mi>n</mi></msub></msub></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">R_{n,{\mathcal{P}}}({\bm{h}})\leq D_{n,\mathscr{P}}({\bm{h}})+\alpha_{N_{n}}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A1.SS2.p7.3" class="ltx_p"><span id="A1.SS2.p7.3.1" class="ltx_text">This completes the proof.</span></p>
</div>
<div id="A1.Thmlem3" class="ltx_theorem ltx_theorem_lem">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_title_theorem"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_theorem"><span id="A1.Thmlem3.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Lemma A.3</span></span><span id="A1.Thmlem3.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold"> </span>(Non-i.i.d. large deviation lower bound)<span id="A1.Thmlem3.4" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">.</span></h6>
<div id="A1.Thmlem3.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A1.Thmlem3.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A1.Thmlem3.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">Let Assumptions <a href="#S3.Thmasmp3" title="Assumption 3.3. ‣ 3.3 Detection Efficiency and Optimal Scores ‣ 3 A Statistical Framework under Pseudorandomness Collision ‣ Optimal Detection for Language Watermarks with Pseudorandom Collision" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">3.3</span></a> and <a href="#A1.Thmasmp1" title="Assumption A.1 (Regularity conditions for lower bound tightness). ‣ A.2 Asymptotic Tightness ‣ Appendix A Proof for the General Framework ‣ Optimal Detection for Language Watermarks with Pseudorandom Collision" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">A.1</span></a> hold, and let <math id="A1.Thmlem3.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="{\mathcal{Q}}_{i}^{*}=\{\bm{Q}_{i,{\mathcal{V}}}\}_{{\mathcal{V}}\in\Pi}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msubsup><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒬</mi><mi>i</mi><mo>∗</mo></msubsup><mo>=</mo><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><msub><mi>𝐐</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>,</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒱</mi></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒱</mi><mo>∈</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">Π</mi></mrow></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\mathcal{Q}}_{i}^{*}=\{\bm{Q}_{i,{\mathcal{V}}}\}_{{\mathcal{V}}\in\Pi}</annotation></semantics></math> denote a given assignment of NTP distributions. Then, we have</span></p>
<table id="A1.Ex52" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A1.Ex52.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\frac{1}{N_{n}}\log\left(1-\EB_{1}\left[T_{n}~|~\{\bm{P}_{{\mathcal{V}}}\}_{{\mathcal{V}}}={\mathcal{Q}}_{i}^{\star}\right]\right)\geq\min_{\theta\geq 0}\left\{\theta\cdot\frac{\gamma_{n,\alpha}}{N_{n}}+\sum_{{\mathcal{V}}\in\Pi}\frac{1}{N_{n}}\log\phi_{\bm{Q}_{i,{\mathcal{V}}},h_{{\mathcal{V}}}}(\theta)\right\}-\alpha_{N_{n}}," display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mfrac><mn>1</mn><msub><mi>N</mi><mi>n</mi></msub></mfrac><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mrow><msub><mi>𝔼</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>[</mo><mrow><msub><mi>T</mi><mi>n</mi></msub><mo fence="false" rspace="0.497em" stretchy="false">|</mo><mrow><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><msub><mi>𝐏</mi><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒱</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒱</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><msubsup><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒬</mi><mi>i</mi><mo>⋆</mo></msubsup></mrow></mrow><mo>]</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>≥</mo><mrow><mrow><munder><mi>min</mi><mrow><mi>θ</mi><mo>≥</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow></munder><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>{</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>θ</mi><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><mfrac><msub><mi>γ</mi><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>α</mi></mrow></msub><msub><mi>N</mi><mi>n</mi></msub></mfrac></mrow><mo rspace="0.055em">+</mo><mrow><munder><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒱</mi><mo>∈</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">Π</mi></mrow></munder><mrow><mfrac><mn>1</mn><msub><mi>N</mi><mi>n</mi></msub></mfrac><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><msub><mi>ϕ</mi><mrow><msub><mi>𝑸</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>,</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒱</mi></mrow></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>h</mi><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒱</mi></msub></mrow></msub></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>θ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>}</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>α</mi><msub><mi>N</mi><mi>n</mi></msub></msub></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\frac{1}{N_{n}}\log\left(1-\EB_{1}\left[T_{n}~|~\{\bm{P}_{{\mathcal{V}}}\}_{{\mathcal{V}}}={\mathcal{Q}}_{i}^{\star}\right]\right)\geq\min_{\theta\geq 0}\left\{\theta\cdot\frac{\gamma_{n,\alpha}}{N_{n}}+\sum_{{\mathcal{V}}\in\Pi}\frac{1}{N_{n}}\log\phi_{\bm{Q}_{i,{\mathcal{V}}},h_{{\mathcal{V}}}}(\theta)\right\}-\alpha_{N_{n}},</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A1.Thmlem3.p1.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="A1.Thmlem3.p1.2.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">where <math id="A1.Thmlem3.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\alpha_{N_{n}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>α</mi><msub><mi>N</mi><mi>n</mi></msub></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\alpha_{N_{n}}</annotation></semantics></math> is a non-negative function of <math id="A1.Thmlem3.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="N_{n}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>N</mi><mi>n</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">N_{n}</annotation></semantics></math> that converges to zero as <math id="A1.Thmlem3.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="N_{n}\to\infty" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>N</mi><mi>n</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">∞</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">N_{n}\to\infty</annotation></semantics></math>, and is independent of the choice of <math id="A1.Thmlem3.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="{\mathcal{Q}}_{i}^{\star}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msubsup><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒬</mi><mi>i</mi><mo>⋆</mo></msubsup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\mathcal{Q}}_{i}^{\star}</annotation></semantics></math>.</span></p>
</div>
</div>
<div id="A1.Thmlem4" class="ltx_theorem ltx_theorem_lem">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_title_theorem"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_theorem"><span id="A1.Thmlem4.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Lemma A.4</span></span><span id="A1.Thmlem4.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold"> </span>(Minimax theorem)<span id="A1.Thmlem4.4" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">.</span></h6>
<div id="A1.Thmlem4.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A1.Thmlem4.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A1.Thmlem4.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">Let <math id="A1.Thmlem4.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="{\mathcal{P}}^{\star}=\{\bm{P}_{1}^{\star},\dots,\bm{P}_{K}^{\star}\}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msup><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒫</mi><mo>⋆</mo></msup><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><msubsup><mi>𝐏</mi><mn>1</mn><mo>⋆</mo></msubsup><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi><mo>,</mo><msubsup><mi>𝐏</mi><mi>K</mi><mo>⋆</mo></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\mathcal{P}}^{\star}=\{\bm{P}_{1}^{\star},\dots,\bm{P}_{K}^{\star}\}</annotation></semantics></math> be a finite set, and let <math id="A1.Thmlem4.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="L(\bm{P}^{\star},\theta)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>L</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>𝐏</mi><mo>⋆</mo></msup><mo>,</mo><mi>θ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">L(\bm{P}^{\star},\theta)</annotation></semantics></math> be a function defined on <math id="A1.Thmlem4.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="{\mathcal{P}}^{\star}\times\Theta" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msup><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒫</mi><mo>⋆</mo></msup><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">×</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">Θ</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\mathcal{P}}^{\star}\times\Theta</annotation></semantics></math>, where <math id="A1.Thmlem4.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\Theta\subset\mathbb{R}^{d}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Θ</mi><mo>⊂</mo><msup><mi>ℝ</mi><mi>d</mi></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Theta\subset\mathbb{R}^{d}</annotation></semantics></math> is a convex set. Assume that for each fixed <math id="A1.Thmlem4.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\bm{P}^{\star}\in{\mathcal{P}}^{\star}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msup><mi>𝐏</mi><mo>⋆</mo></msup><mo>∈</mo><msup><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒫</mi><mo>⋆</mo></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\bm{P}^{\star}\in{\mathcal{P}}^{\star}</annotation></semantics></math>, the function <math id="A1.Thmlem4.p1.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="L(\bm{P}^{\star},\cdot)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>L</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>𝐏</mi><mo>⋆</mo></msup><mo rspace="0em">,</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">⋅</mo><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">L(\bm{P}^{\star},\cdot)</annotation></semantics></math> is continuous and convex in <math id="A1.Thmlem4.p1.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\theta" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>θ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\theta</annotation></semantics></math>.
Let <math id="A1.Thmlem4.p1.m8" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\Lambda:=\left\{\lambda\in\mathbb{R}^{K}:\lambda_{i}\geq 0,\ \sum_{i=1}^{K}\lambda_{i}=1\right\}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Λ</mi><mo>:=</mo><mrow><mo>{</mo><mi>λ</mi><mo>∈</mo><msup><mi>ℝ</mi><mi>K</mi></msup><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><msub><mi>λ</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>≥</mo><mn>0</mn><mo rspace="0.500em">,</mo><msubsup><mo>∑</mo><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>K</mi></msubsup><msub><mi>λ</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>}</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Lambda:=\left\{\lambda\in\mathbb{R}^{K}:\lambda_{i}\geq 0,\ \sum_{i=1}^{K}\lambda_{i}=1\right\}</annotation></semantics></math> denote the probability simplex over <math id="A1.Thmlem4.p1.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="{\mathcal{P}}^{\star}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒫</mi><mo>⋆</mo></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\mathcal{P}}^{\star}</annotation></semantics></math>, and define</span></p>
<table id="A1.Ex53" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A1.Ex53.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="F(\lambda,\theta):=\sum_{i=1}^{K}\lambda_{i}L(\bm{P}_{i}^{\star},\theta)." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>F</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>λ</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>θ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.111em">:=</mo><mrow><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>K</mi></munderover><mrow><msub><mi>λ</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>L</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msubsup><mi>𝑷</mi><mi>i</mi><mo>⋆</mo></msubsup><mo>,</mo><mi>θ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">F(\lambda,\theta):=\sum_{i=1}^{K}\lambda_{i}L(\bm{P}_{i}^{\star},\theta).</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A1.Thmlem4.p1.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="A1.Thmlem4.p1.2.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">Then,</span></p>
<table id="A1.Ex54" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A1.Ex54.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\max_{\lambda\in\Lambda}\min_{\theta\in\Theta}F(\lambda,\theta)=\min_{\theta\in\Theta}\max_{\lambda\in\Lambda}F(\lambda,\theta)=\min_{\theta\in\Theta}\sup_{\bm{P}^{\star}\in{\mathcal{P}}^{\star}}L(\bm{P}^{\star},\theta)." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><munder><mi>max</mi><mrow><mi>λ</mi><mo>∈</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">Λ</mi></mrow></munder><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><mrow><munder><mi>min</mi><mrow><mi>θ</mi><mo>∈</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">Θ</mi></mrow></munder><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><mrow><mi>F</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>λ</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>θ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><munder><mi>min</mi><mrow><mi>θ</mi><mo>∈</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">Θ</mi></mrow></munder><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><mrow><munder><mi>max</mi><mrow><mi>λ</mi><mo>∈</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">Λ</mi></mrow></munder><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><mrow><mi>F</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>λ</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>θ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>min</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><mrow><mmultiscripts><munder><mo movablelimits="false">sup</mo><mrow><msup><mi>𝑷</mi><mo>⋆</mo></msup><mo>∈</mo><msup><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒫</mi><mo>⋆</mo></msup></mrow></munder><mprescripts></mprescripts><mrow><mi>θ</mi><mo>∈</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">Θ</mi></mrow><mrow></mrow></mmultiscripts><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><mrow><mi>L</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>𝑷</mi><mo>⋆</mo></msup><mo>,</mo><mi>θ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\max_{\lambda\in\Lambda}\min_{\theta\in\Theta}F(\lambda,\theta)=\min_{\theta\in\Theta}\max_{\lambda\in\Lambda}F(\lambda,\theta)=\min_{\theta\in\Theta}\sup_{\bm{P}^{\star}\in{\mathcal{P}}^{\star}}L(\bm{P}^{\star},\theta).</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
</div>
<div id="A1.SS2.p8" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A1.SS2.p8.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A1.SS2.p8.1.1" class="ltx_text">∎</span></p>
</div>
</div>
<div id="A1.SS2.p9" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A1.SS2.p9.1" class="ltx_p">We provide the proof of Lemma <a href="#A1.Thmlem4" title="Lemma A.4 (Minimax theorem). ‣ Proof of Theorem . ‣ A.2 Asymptotic Tightness ‣ Appendix A Proof for the General Framework ‣ Optimal Detection for Language Watermarks with Pseudorandom Collision" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">A.4</span></a> below. The proof of Lemma <a href="#A1.Thmlem3" title="Lemma A.3 (Non-i.i.d. large deviation lower bound). ‣ Proof of Theorem . ‣ A.2 Asymptotic Tightness ‣ Appendix A Proof for the General Framework ‣ Optimal Detection for Language Watermarks with Pseudorandom Collision" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">A.3</span></a> is deferred to Section <a href="#A1.SS3" title="A.3 Proof of Lemma ‣ Appendix A Proof for the General Framework ‣ Optimal Detection for Language Watermarks with Pseudorandom Collision" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">A.3</span></a>, as it is more technical and lengthy.</p>
</div>
<div id="A1.SS2.3" class="ltx_proof">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_font_italic ltx_title_proof">Proof of Lemma <a href="#A1.Thmlem4" title="Lemma A.4 (Minimax theorem). ‣ Proof of Theorem . ‣ A.2 Asymptotic Tightness ‣ Appendix A Proof for the General Framework ‣ Optimal Detection for Language Watermarks with Pseudorandom Collision" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">A.4</span></a>.</h6>
<div id="A1.SS2.p10" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A1.SS2.p10.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A1.SS2.p10.1.1" class="ltx_text">Note that the function <math id="A1.SS2.p10.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="F(\lambda,\theta)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>F</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>λ</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>θ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">F(\lambda,\theta)</annotation></semantics></math> is convex in <math id="A1.SS2.p10.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\theta" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>θ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\theta</annotation></semantics></math> for each fixed <math id="A1.SS2.p10.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\lambda" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>λ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\lambda</annotation></semantics></math>, and linear (hence concave) in <math id="A1.SS2.p10.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\lambda" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>λ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\lambda</annotation></semantics></math> for each fixed <math id="A1.SS2.p10.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\theta" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>θ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\theta</annotation></semantics></math>.
By assumption, <math id="A1.SS2.p10.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="L(\bm{P}_{i}^{\star},\cdot)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>L</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msubsup><mi>𝑷</mi><mi>i</mi><mo>⋆</mo></msubsup><mo rspace="0em">,</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">⋅</mo><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">L(\bm{P}_{i}^{\star},\cdot)</annotation></semantics></math> is continuous and convex on the convex domain <math id="A1.SS2.p10.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\Theta" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi mathvariant="normal">Θ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Theta</annotation></semantics></math>, so <math id="A1.SS2.p10.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="F" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>F</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">F</annotation></semantics></math> is concave-convex and jointly continuous on the product space <math id="A1.SS2.p10.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\Lambda\times\Theta" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Λ</mi><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">×</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">Θ</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Lambda\times\Theta</annotation></semantics></math>. Since <math id="A1.SS2.p10.m10" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\Delta" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Delta</annotation></semantics></math> is convex and compact, and <math id="A1.SS2.p10.m11" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\Theta" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi mathvariant="normal">Θ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Theta</annotation></semantics></math> is convex, we may apply Sion’s minimax theorem to exchange the order of <math id="A1.SS2.p10.m12" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\min" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>min</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\min</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="A1.SS2.p10.m13" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\max" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>max</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\max</annotation></semantics></math>:</span></p>
<table id="A1.Ex55" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A1.Ex55.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\min_{\theta\in\Theta}\max_{\lambda\in\Lambda}F(\lambda,\theta)=\max_{\lambda\in\Lambda}\min_{\theta\in\Theta}F(\lambda,\theta)." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><munder><mi>min</mi><mrow><mi>θ</mi><mo>∈</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">Θ</mi></mrow></munder><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><mrow><munder><mi>max</mi><mrow><mi>λ</mi><mo>∈</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">Λ</mi></mrow></munder><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><mrow><mi>F</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>λ</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>θ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><munder><mi>max</mi><mrow><mi>λ</mi><mo>∈</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">Λ</mi></mrow></munder><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><mrow><munder><mi>min</mi><mrow><mi>θ</mi><mo>∈</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">Θ</mi></mrow></munder><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><mrow><mi>F</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>λ</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>θ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\min_{\theta\in\Theta}\max_{\lambda\in\Lambda}F(\lambda,\theta)=\max_{\lambda\in\Lambda}\min_{\theta\in\Theta}F(\lambda,\theta).</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A1.SS2.p10.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="A1.SS2.p10.2.1" class="ltx_text">Because the maximum over <math id="A1.SS2.p10.m14" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\lambda\in\Lambda" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>λ</mi><mo>∈</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">Λ</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\lambda\in\Lambda</annotation></semantics></math> of a convex combination <math id="A1.SS2.p10.m15" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\sum_{i}\lambda_{i}L(\bm{P}_{i}^{\star},\theta)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mo>∑</mo><mi>i</mi></msub><mrow><msub><mi>λ</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>L</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msubsup><mi>𝑷</mi><mi>i</mi><mo>⋆</mo></msubsup><mo>,</mo><mi>θ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\sum_{i}\lambda_{i}L(\bm{P}_{i}^{\star},\theta)</annotation></semantics></math> is achieved at a vertex of the simplex, we observe:</span></p>
<table id="A1.EGx25" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_gather ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A1.Ex56"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A1.Ex56.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\min_{\theta\in\Theta}\max_{\lambda\in\Lambda}F(\lambda,\theta)=\min_{\theta\in\Theta}\max_{\bm{P}^{\star}\in{\mathcal{P}}^{\star}}L(\bm{P}^{\star},\theta)." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><munder><mi>min</mi><mrow><mi>θ</mi><mo>∈</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">Θ</mi></mrow></munder><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><mrow><munder><mi>max</mi><mrow><mi>λ</mi><mo>∈</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">Λ</mi></mrow></munder><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><mrow><mi>F</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>λ</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>θ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><munder><mi>min</mi><mrow><mi>θ</mi><mo>∈</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">Θ</mi></mrow></munder><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><mrow><munder><mi>max</mi><mrow><msup><mi>𝑷</mi><mo>⋆</mo></msup><mo>∈</mo><msup><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒫</mi><mo>⋆</mo></msup></mrow></munder><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><mrow><mi>L</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>𝑷</mi><mo>⋆</mo></msup><mo>,</mo><mi>θ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\min_{\theta\in\Theta}\max_{\lambda\in\Lambda}F(\lambda,\theta)=\min_{\theta\in\Theta}\max_{\bm{P}^{\star}\in{\mathcal{P}}^{\star}}L(\bm{P}^{\star},\theta).</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A1.SS2.p10.3" class="ltx_p"><span id="A1.SS2.p10.3.1" class="ltx_text">∎</span></p>
</div>
</div>
</section>
<section id="A1.SS3" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection">A.3 </span>Proof of Lemma <a href="#A1.Thmlem3" title="Lemma A.3 (Non-i.i.d. large deviation lower bound). ‣ Proof of Theorem . ‣ A.2 Asymptotic Tightness ‣ Appendix A Proof for the General Framework ‣ Optimal Detection for Language Watermarks with Pseudorandom Collision" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">A.3</span></a></h3>

<div id="A1.SS3.2" class="ltx_proof">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_font_italic ltx_title_proof">Proof of Lemma <a href="#A1.Thmlem3" title="Lemma A.3 (Non-i.i.d. large deviation lower bound). ‣ Proof of Theorem . ‣ A.2 Asymptotic Tightness ‣ Appendix A Proof for the General Framework ‣ Optimal Detection for Language Watermarks with Pseudorandom Collision" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">A.3</span></a>.</h6>
<div id="A1.SS3.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A1.SS3.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A1.SS3.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text">At a high level, we analyze the quantity</span></p>
<table id="A1.Ex57" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A1.Ex57.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="1-\EB_{1}\left[T_{n}~|~\{\bm{P}_{{\mathcal{V}}}\}_{{\mathcal{V}}}={\mathcal{Q}}_{i}^{\star}\right]={\mathbb{P}}_{1}(S_{n}\leq\gamma_{n,\alpha})" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mrow><msub><mi>𝔼</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>[</mo><mrow><msub><mi>T</mi><mi>n</mi></msub><mo fence="false" rspace="0.497em" stretchy="false">|</mo><mrow><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><msub><mi>𝐏</mi><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒱</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒱</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><msubsup><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒬</mi><mi>i</mi><mo>⋆</mo></msubsup></mrow></mrow><mo>]</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><msub><mi>ℙ</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>S</mi><mi>n</mi></msub><mo>≤</mo><msub><mi>γ</mi><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>α</mi></mrow></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">1-\EB_{1}\left[T_{n}~|~\{\bm{P}_{{\mathcal{V}}}\}_{{\mathcal{V}}}={\mathcal{Q}}_{i}^{\star}\right]={\mathbb{P}}_{1}(S_{n}\leq\gamma_{n,\alpha})</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A1.SS3.p1.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="A1.SS3.p1.2.1" class="ltx_text">by isolating its dominant term and deriving the lower bound stated in the lemma.
Since all NTP distributions are fixed by the assignment <math id="A1.SS3.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="{\mathcal{Q}}_{i}^{\star}=\{\bm{Q}_{i,{\mathcal{V}}}\}_{{\mathcal{V}}\in\Pi}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msubsup><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒬</mi><mi>i</mi><mo>⋆</mo></msubsup><mo>=</mo><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><msub><mi>𝑸</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>,</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒱</mi></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒱</mi><mo>∈</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">Π</mi></mrow></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\mathcal{Q}}_{i}^{\star}=\{\bm{Q}_{i,{\mathcal{V}}}\}_{{\mathcal{V}}\in\Pi}</annotation></semantics></math>, we omit this dependence from the notation for clarity.</span></p>
</div>
</div>
<section id="A1.SS3.SSS0.Px1" class="ltx_paragraph">
<h5 class="ltx_title ltx_title_paragraph">Step 1: Define tilted random variables.</h5>

<div id="A1.SS3.SSS0.Px1.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A1.SS3.SSS0.Px1.p1.1" class="ltx_p">We begin by defining the random variables:</p>
<table id="A1.Ex58" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A1.Ex58.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="X_{{\mathcal{V}}}:=-h_{{\mathcal{V}}}(Y_{{\mathcal{V}}})." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>X</mi><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒱</mi></msub><mo>:=</mo><mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><msub><mi>h</mi><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒱</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>Y</mi><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒱</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">X_{{\mathcal{V}}}:=-h_{{\mathcal{V}}}(Y_{{\mathcal{V}}}).</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A1.SS3.SSS0.Px1.p1.2" class="ltx_p">for each minimal unit <math id="A1.SS3.SSS0.Px1.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="{\mathcal{V}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒱</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\mathcal{V}}</annotation></semantics></math>. Let <math id="A1.SS3.SSS0.Px1.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="F_{{\mathcal{V}}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>F</mi><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒱</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">F_{{\mathcal{V}}}</annotation></semantics></math> denote the alternative CDF of <math id="A1.SS3.SSS0.Px1.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="X_{{\mathcal{V}}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>X</mi><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒱</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">X_{{\mathcal{V}}}</annotation></semantics></math>.
Next, for any <math id="A1.SS3.SSS0.Px1.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\theta\geq 0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>θ</mi><mo>≥</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\theta\geq 0</annotation></semantics></math>, we define the tilted random variable <math id="A1.SS3.SSS0.Px1.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\bar{X}_{{\mathcal{V}}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>X</mi><mo>¯</mo></mover><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒱</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\bar{X}_{{\mathcal{V}}}</annotation></semantics></math> with its CDF given by</p>
<table id="A1.Ex59" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A1.Ex59.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\bar{F}_{{\mathcal{V}}}(x):=\frac{1}{\phi_{\bm{Q}_{i,{\mathcal{V}}},h_{{\mathcal{V}}}}(\theta)}\int_{-\infty}^{x}{\mathrm{e}}^{\theta y}{\mathrm{d}}F_{{\mathcal{V}}}(y)," display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>F</mi><mo>¯</mo></mover><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒱</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>:=</mo><mrow><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mrow><msub><mi>ϕ</mi><mrow><msub><mi>𝑸</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>,</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒱</mi></mrow></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>h</mi><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒱</mi></msub></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>θ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mfrac><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><msubsup><mo>∫</mo><mrow><mo>−</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">∞</mi></mrow><mi>x</mi></msubsup><mrow><msup><mi>e</mi><mrow><mi>θ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>y</mi></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>d</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>F</mi><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒱</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>y</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\bar{F}_{{\mathcal{V}}}(x):=\frac{1}{\phi_{\bm{Q}_{i,{\mathcal{V}}},h_{{\mathcal{V}}}}(\theta)}\int_{-\infty}^{x}{\mathrm{e}}^{\theta y}{\mathrm{d}}F_{{\mathcal{V}}}(y),</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A1.SS3.SSS0.Px1.p1.3" class="ltx_p">where the normalizing constant</p>
<table id="A1.Ex60" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A1.Ex60.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\phi_{\bm{Q}_{i,{\mathcal{V}}},h_{{\mathcal{V}}}}(\theta):=\EB_{1,\bm{Q}_{i,{\mathcal{V}}}}[{\mathrm{e}}^{-\theta h_{{\mathcal{V}}}(Y_{{\mathcal{V}}})}]=\int_{-\infty}^{\infty}{\mathrm{e}}^{\theta y}{\mathrm{d}}F_{{\mathcal{V}}}(y)" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>ϕ</mi><mrow><msub><mi>𝑸</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>,</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒱</mi></mrow></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>h</mi><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒱</mi></msub></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>θ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>:=</mo><mrow><msub><mi>𝔼</mi><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>𝐐</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>,</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒱</mi></mrow></msub></mrow></msub><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><msup><mi>e</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>θ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>h</mi><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒱</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>Y</mi><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒱</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></msup><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.111em">=</mo><mrow><msubsup><mo>∫</mo><mrow><mo>−</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">∞</mi></mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">∞</mi></msubsup><mrow><msup><mi>e</mi><mrow><mi>θ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>y</mi></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>dF</mi><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒱</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>y</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\phi_{\bm{Q}_{i,{\mathcal{V}}},h_{{\mathcal{V}}}}(\theta):=\EB_{1,\bm{Q}_{i,{\mathcal{V}}}}[{\mathrm{e}}^{-\theta h_{{\mathcal{V}}}(Y_{{\mathcal{V}}})}]=\int_{-\infty}^{\infty}{\mathrm{e}}^{\theta y}{\mathrm{d}}F_{{\mathcal{V}}}(y)</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A1.SS3.SSS0.Px1.p1.4" class="ltx_p">is the MGF of <math id="A1.SS3.SSS0.Px1.p1.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="X_{{\mathcal{V}}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>X</mi><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒱</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">X_{{\mathcal{V}}}</annotation></semantics></math>.
The mean and variance of the tilted random variable <math id="A1.SS3.SSS0.Px1.p1.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\bar{X}_{{\mathcal{V}}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>X</mi><mo>¯</mo></mover><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒱</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\bar{X}_{{\mathcal{V}}}</annotation></semantics></math> are given by:</p>
<table id="A1.EGx26" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A1.E43"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td colspan="2" class="ltx_td ltx_align_center ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.E43.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\begin{split}\EB_{1}[\bar{X}_{{\mathcal{V}}}]&amp;=\frac{1}{\phi_{\bm{Q}_{i,{\mathcal{V}}},h_{{\mathcal{V}}}}(\theta)}\int_{-\infty}^{\infty}y\,{\mathrm{e}}^{\theta y}{\mathrm{d}}F_{{\mathcal{V}}}(y)=\frac{{\mathrm{d}}}{{\mathrm{d}}\theta}\log\phi_{\bm{Q}_{i,{\mathcal{V}}},h_{{\mathcal{V}}}}(\theta)=:m_{{\mathcal{V}}}(\theta),\\
\mathrm{Var}_{1}(\bar{X}_{{\mathcal{V}}})&amp;=\frac{1}{\phi_{\bm{Q}_{i,{\mathcal{V}}},h_{{\mathcal{V}}}}(\theta)}\int_{-\infty}^{\infty}(y-\EB_{1}[\bar{X}_{{\mathcal{V}}}])^{2}{\mathrm{e}}^{\theta y}{\mathrm{d}}F_{{\mathcal{V}}}(y)=\frac{{\mathrm{d}}^{2}}{{\mathrm{d}}\theta^{2}}\log\phi_{\bm{Q}_{i,{\mathcal{V}}},h_{{\mathcal{V}}}}(\theta)=:\sigma^{2}_{{\mathcal{V}}}(\theta).\end{split}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mtable columnspacing="0pt" rowspacing="0pt"><mtr><mtd class="ltx_align_right" columnalign="right"><mrow><msub><mi>𝔼</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>X</mi><mo>¯</mo></mover><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒱</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow></mtd><mtd class="ltx_align_left" columnalign="left"><mrow><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mrow><msub><mi>ϕ</mi><mrow><msub><mi>𝑸</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>,</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒱</mi></mrow></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>h</mi><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒱</mi></msub></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>θ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mfrac></mstyle><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><msubsup><mo>∫</mo><mrow><mo>−</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">∞</mi></mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">∞</mi></msubsup></mstyle><mrow><mi>y</mi><mo lspace="0.340em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>e</mi><mrow><mi>θ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>y</mi></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>d</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>F</mi><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒱</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>y</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mi>d</mi><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>θ</mi></mrow></mfrac></mstyle><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><msub><mi>ϕ</mi><mrow><msub><mi>𝑸</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>,</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒱</mi></mrow></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>h</mi><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒱</mi></msub></mrow></msub></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>θ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mphantom></mphantom><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mrow><msub><mi>m</mi><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒱</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>θ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow></mtd></mtr><mtr><mtd class="ltx_align_right" columnalign="right"><mrow><msub><mi>Var</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>X</mi><mo>¯</mo></mover><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒱</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mtd><mtd class="ltx_align_left" columnalign="left"><mrow><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mrow><msub><mi>ϕ</mi><mrow><msub><mi>𝑸</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>,</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒱</mi></mrow></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>h</mi><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒱</mi></msub></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>θ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mfrac></mstyle><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><msubsup><mo>∫</mo><mrow><mo>−</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">∞</mi></mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">∞</mi></msubsup></mstyle><mrow><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>y</mi><mo>−</mo><mrow><msub><mi>𝔼</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>X</mi><mo>¯</mo></mover><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒱</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>e</mi><mrow><mi>θ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>y</mi></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>dF</mi><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒱</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>y</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><msup><mi>d</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>θ</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow></mfrac></mstyle><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><msub><mi>ϕ</mi><mrow><msub><mi>𝐐</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>,</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒱</mi></mrow></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>h</mi><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒱</mi></msub></mrow></msub></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>θ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mphantom></mphantom><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>σ</mi><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒱</mi><mn>2</mn></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>θ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow></mtd></mtr></mtable><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\begin{split}\EB_{1}[\bar{X}_{{\mathcal{V}}}]&amp;=\frac{1}{\phi_{\bm{Q}_{i,{\mathcal{V}}},h_{{\mathcal{V}}}}(\theta)}\int_{-\infty}^{\infty}y\,{\mathrm{e}}^{\theta y}{\mathrm{d}}F_{{\mathcal{V}}}(y)=\frac{{\mathrm{d}}}{{\mathrm{d}}\theta}\log\phi_{\bm{Q}_{i,{\mathcal{V}}},h_{{\mathcal{V}}}}(\theta)=:m_{{\mathcal{V}}}(\theta),\\
\mathrm{Var}_{1}(\bar{X}_{{\mathcal{V}}})&amp;=\frac{1}{\phi_{\bm{Q}_{i,{\mathcal{V}}},h_{{\mathcal{V}}}}(\theta)}\int_{-\infty}^{\infty}(y-\EB_{1}[\bar{X}_{{\mathcal{V}}}])^{2}{\mathrm{e}}^{\theta y}{\mathrm{d}}F_{{\mathcal{V}}}(y)=\frac{{\mathrm{d}}^{2}}{{\mathrm{d}}\theta^{2}}\log\phi_{\bm{Q}_{i,{\mathcal{V}}},h_{{\mathcal{V}}}}(\theta)=:\sigma^{2}_{{\mathcal{V}}}(\theta).\end{split}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(43)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
</section>
<section id="A1.SS3.SSS0.Px2" class="ltx_paragraph">
<h5 class="ltx_title ltx_title_paragraph">Step 2: Reformulate the tail probability.</h5>

<div id="A1.SS3.SSS0.Px2.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A1.SS3.SSS0.Px2.p1.1" class="ltx_p">Recall the test statistic <math id="A1.SS3.SSS0.Px2.p1.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="S_{n}=\sum_{{\mathcal{V}}\in\Pi}h_{{\mathcal{V}}}(Y_{{\mathcal{V}}})=-\sum_{{\mathcal{V}}\in\Pi}X_{{\mathcal{V}}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>S</mi><mi>n</mi></msub><mo rspace="0.111em">=</mo><msub><mo>∑</mo><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒱</mi><mo>∈</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">Π</mi></mrow></msub><msub><mi>h</mi><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒱</mi></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>Y</mi><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒱</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo rspace="0em">=</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.055em">−</mo><msub><mo>∑</mo><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒱</mi><mo>∈</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">Π</mi></mrow></msub><msub><mi>X</mi><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒱</mi></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">S_{n}=\sum_{{\mathcal{V}}\in\Pi}h_{{\mathcal{V}}}(Y_{{\mathcal{V}}})=-\sum_{{\mathcal{V}}\in\Pi}X_{{\mathcal{V}}}</annotation></semantics></math>. Thus, for any <math id="A1.SS3.SSS0.Px2.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="x\in{\mathbb{R}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo>∈</mo><mi>ℝ</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">x\in{\mathbb{R}}</annotation></semantics></math>, we can write <math id="A1.SS3.SSS0.Px2.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="{\mathbb{P}}_{1}(S_{n}\leq-N_{n}x)={\mathbb{P}}_{1}\left(\sum_{{\mathcal{V}}\in\Pi}X_{{\mathcal{V}}}\geq N_{n}x\right)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>ℙ</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>S</mi><mi>n</mi></msub><mo>≤</mo><mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><msub><mi>N</mi><mi>n</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>x</mi></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><msub><mi>ℙ</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mo lspace="0em">∑</mo><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒱</mi><mo>∈</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">Π</mi></mrow></msub><msub><mi>X</mi><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒱</mi></msub></mrow><mo>≥</mo><mrow><msub><mi>N</mi><mi>n</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>x</mi></mrow></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\mathbb{P}}_{1}(S_{n}\leq-N_{n}x)={\mathbb{P}}_{1}\left(\sum_{{\mathcal{V}}\in\Pi}X_{{\mathcal{V}}}\geq N_{n}x\right)</annotation></semantics></math>. We then express the tail probability <math id="A1.SS3.SSS0.Px2.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="{\mathbb{P}}_{1}\left(\sum_{{\mathcal{V}}\in\Pi}X_{{\mathcal{V}}}\geq N_{n}x\right)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>ℙ</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mo lspace="0em">∑</mo><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒱</mi><mo>∈</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">Π</mi></mrow></msub><msub><mi>X</mi><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒱</mi></msub></mrow><mo>≥</mo><mrow><msub><mi>N</mi><mi>n</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>x</mi></mrow></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\mathbb{P}}_{1}\left(\sum_{{\mathcal{V}}\in\Pi}X_{{\mathcal{V}}}\geq N_{n}x\right)</annotation></semantics></math> in terms of the CDF of tilted random variables, as stated in the following lemma, whose proof can be found in Section <a href="#A1.SS4" title="A.4 Proof of Lemma ‣ Appendix A Proof for the General Framework ‣ Optimal Detection for Language Watermarks with Pseudorandom Collision" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">A.4</span></a>.</p>
</div>
<div id="A1.Thmlem5" class="ltx_theorem ltx_theorem_lem">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_title_theorem"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_theorem"><span id="A1.Thmlem5.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Lemma A.5</span></span><span id="A1.Thmlem5.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">.</span></h6>
<div id="A1.Thmlem5.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A1.Thmlem5.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A1.Thmlem5.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">Let <math id="A1.Thmlem5.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\bar{H}(t)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mover accent="true"><mi>H</mi><mo>¯</mo></mover><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\bar{H}(t)</annotation></semantics></math> be the CDF of the standardized sum <math id="A1.Thmlem5.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\frac{\sum_{{\mathcal{V}}\in\Pi}\bar{X}_{{\mathcal{V}}}-N_{n}m(\theta)}{\sqrt{N_{n}\sigma^{2}(\theta)}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mfrac><mrow><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="false"><msub><mo maxsize="0.700em" minsize="0.700em" stretchy="true">∑</mo><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒱</mi><mo>∈</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">Π</mi></mrow></msub></mstyle><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>X</mi><mo>¯</mo></mover><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒱</mi></msub></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><msub><mi>N</mi><mi>n</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>m</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>θ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><msqrt><mrow><msub><mi>N</mi><mi>n</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>σ</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>θ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></msqrt></mfrac><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\frac{\sum_{{\mathcal{V}}\in\Pi}\bar{X}_{{\mathcal{V}}}-N_{n}m(\theta)}{\sqrt{N_{n}\sigma^{2}(\theta)}}</annotation></semantics></math>. Then we have</span></p>
<table id="A1.Ex61" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A1.Ex61.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="{\mathbb{P}}_{1}\left(\sum_{{\mathcal{V}}\in\Pi}X_{{\mathcal{V}}}\geq N_{n}x\right)=\prod_{{\mathcal{V}}\in\Pi}\phi_{\bm{Q}_{i,{\mathcal{V}}},h_{{\mathcal{V}}}}(\theta){\mathrm{e}}^{-\theta N_{n}m(\theta)}\int_{\frac{N_{n}x-N_{n}m(\theta)}{\sqrt{N_{n}\sigma^{2}(\theta)}}}^{\infty}{\mathrm{e}}^{-\theta\sqrt{N_{n}\sigma^{2}(\theta)}t}{\mathrm{d}}\bar{H}_{n}(t)," display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>ℙ</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mrow><munder><mo lspace="0em" movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒱</mi><mo>∈</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">Π</mi></mrow></munder><msub><mi>X</mi><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒱</mi></msub></mrow><mo>≥</mo><mrow><msub><mi>N</mi><mi>n</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>x</mi></mrow></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.111em">=</mo><mrow><munder><mo movablelimits="false">∏</mo><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒱</mi><mo>∈</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">Π</mi></mrow></munder><mrow><msub><mi>ϕ</mi><mrow><msub><mi>𝑸</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>,</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒱</mi></mrow></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>h</mi><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒱</mi></msub></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>θ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>e</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>θ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>N</mi><mi>n</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>m</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>θ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><msubsup><mo>∫</mo><mfrac><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>N</mi><mi>n</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>x</mi></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><msub><mi>N</mi><mi>n</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>m</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>θ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><msqrt><mrow><msub><mi>N</mi><mi>n</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>σ</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>θ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></msqrt></mfrac><mi mathvariant="normal">∞</mi></msubsup><mrow><msup><mi>e</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>θ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msqrt><mrow><msub><mi>N</mi><mi>n</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>σ</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>θ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></msqrt><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>d</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>H</mi><mo>¯</mo></mover><mi>n</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\mathbb{P}}_{1}\left(\sum_{{\mathcal{V}}\in\Pi}X_{{\mathcal{V}}}\geq N_{n}x\right)=\prod_{{\mathcal{V}}\in\Pi}\phi_{\bm{Q}_{i,{\mathcal{V}}},h_{{\mathcal{V}}}}(\theta){\mathrm{e}}^{-\theta N_{n}m(\theta)}\int_{\frac{N_{n}x-N_{n}m(\theta)}{\sqrt{N_{n}\sigma^{2}(\theta)}}}^{\infty}{\mathrm{e}}^{-\theta\sqrt{N_{n}\sigma^{2}(\theta)}t}{\mathrm{d}}\bar{H}_{n}(t),</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A1.Thmlem5.p1.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="A1.Thmlem5.p1.2.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">where the mixture mean and variance are defined as</span></p>
<table id="A1.Ex62" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A1.Ex62.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="m(\theta):=\frac{1}{N_{n}}\sum_{{\mathcal{V}}\in\Pi}m_{{\mathcal{V}}}(\theta),\qquad\sigma^{2}(\theta):=\frac{1}{N_{n}}\sum_{{\mathcal{V}}\in\Pi}\sigma^{2}_{{\mathcal{V}}}(\theta)." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>m</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>θ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>:=</mo><mrow><mfrac><mn>1</mn><msub><mi>N</mi><mi>n</mi></msub></mfrac><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><munder><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒱</mi><mo>∈</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">Π</mi></mrow></munder><mrow><msub><mi>m</mi><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒱</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>θ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="2.167em">,</mo><mrow><mrow><msup><mi>σ</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>θ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>:=</mo><mrow><mfrac><mn>1</mn><msub><mi>N</mi><mi>n</mi></msub></mfrac><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><munder><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒱</mi><mo>∈</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">Π</mi></mrow></munder><mrow><msubsup><mi>σ</mi><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒱</mi><mn>2</mn></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>θ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">m(\theta):=\frac{1}{N_{n}}\sum_{{\mathcal{V}}\in\Pi}m_{{\mathcal{V}}}(\theta),\qquad\sigma^{2}(\theta):=\frac{1}{N_{n}}\sum_{{\mathcal{V}}\in\Pi}\sigma^{2}_{{\mathcal{V}}}(\theta).</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A1.Thmlem5.p1.3" class="ltx_p"><span id="A1.Thmlem5.p1.3.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">with each <math id="A1.Thmlem5.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="m_{{\mathcal{V}}}(\theta)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>m</mi><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒱</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>θ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">m_{{\mathcal{V}}}(\theta)</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="A1.Thmlem5.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\sigma^{2}_{{\mathcal{V}}}(\theta)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msubsup><mi>σ</mi><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒱</mi><mn>2</mn></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>θ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\sigma^{2}_{{\mathcal{V}}}(\theta)</annotation></semantics></math> given in (<a href="#A1.E43" title="In Step 1: Define tilted random variables. ‣ A.3 Proof of Lemma ‣ Appendix A Proof for the General Framework ‣ Optimal Detection for Language Watermarks with Pseudorandom Collision" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">43</span></a>).</span></p>
</div>
</div>
</section>
<section id="A1.SS3.SSS0.Px3" class="ltx_paragraph">
<h5 class="ltx_title ltx_title_paragraph">Step 3: Decompose the tail integral via Edgeworth expansion.</h5>

<div id="A1.SS3.SSS0.Px3.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A1.SS3.SSS0.Px3.p1.1" class="ltx_p">We next apply Edgeworth expansion to approximate the PDF of <math id="A1.SS3.SSS0.Px3.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\bar{H}_{n}(t)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>H</mi><mo>¯</mo></mover><mi>n</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\bar{H}_{n}(t)</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>
</div>
<div id="A1.Thmlem6" class="ltx_theorem ltx_theorem_lem">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_title_theorem"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_theorem"><span id="A1.Thmlem6.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Lemma A.6</span></span><span id="A1.Thmlem6.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">.</span></h6>
<div id="A1.Thmlem6.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A1.Thmlem6.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A1.Thmlem6.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">Let <math id="A1.Thmlem6.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\varphi" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>φ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\varphi</annotation></semantics></math> denote the PDF of the standard normal distribution <math id="A1.Thmlem6.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="{\mathcal{N}}(0,1)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒩</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>1</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\mathcal{N}}(0,1)</annotation></semantics></math>. Under Assumptions <a href="#S3.Thmasmp3" title="Assumption 3.3. ‣ 3.3 Detection Efficiency and Optimal Scores ‣ 3 A Statistical Framework under Pseudorandomness Collision ‣ Optimal Detection for Language Watermarks with Pseudorandom Collision" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">3.3</span></a> and <a href="#A1.Thmasmp1" title="Assumption A.1 (Regularity conditions for lower bound tightness). ‣ A.2 Asymptotic Tightness ‣ Appendix A Proof for the General Framework ‣ Optimal Detection for Language Watermarks with Pseudorandom Collision" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">A.1</span></a>, for any <math id="A1.Thmlem6.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="x\in{\mathbb{R}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo>∈</mo><mi>ℝ</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">x\in{\mathbb{R}}</annotation></semantics></math>, we have:</span></p>
<table id="A1.Ex63" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A1.Ex63.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\frac{{\mathrm{d}}\bar{H}_{n}(x)}{{\mathrm{d}}x}=\varphi(x)+\frac{\lambda_{3,N_{n}}}{6\sqrt{N_{n}}}(x^{3}-3x)\varphi(x)+R_{N_{n}}(x)," display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mfrac><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>H</mi><mo>¯</mo></mover><mi>n</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>x</mi></mrow></mfrac><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>φ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mfrac><msub><mi>λ</mi><mrow><mn>3</mn><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>N</mi><mi>n</mi></msub></mrow></msub><mrow><mn>6</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msqrt><msub><mi>N</mi><mi>n</mi></msub></msqrt></mrow></mfrac><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msup><mi>x</mi><mn>3</mn></msup><mo>−</mo><mrow><mn>3</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>x</mi></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>φ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><msub><mi>R</mi><msub><mi>N</mi><mi>n</mi></msub></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\frac{{\mathrm{d}}\bar{H}_{n}(x)}{{\mathrm{d}}x}=\varphi(x)+\frac{\lambda_{3,N_{n}}}{6\sqrt{N_{n}}}(x^{3}-3x)\varphi(x)+R_{N_{n}}(x),</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A1.Thmlem6.p1.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="A1.Thmlem6.p1.2.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">where <math id="A1.Thmlem6.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="R_{N_{n}}(x)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>R</mi><msub><mi>N</mi><mi>n</mi></msub></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">R_{N_{n}}(x)</annotation></semantics></math> is a residual term satisfying <math id="A1.Thmlem6.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\sup_{x\in{\mathbb{R}}}|R_{N_{n}}(x)|=o(1/\sqrt{N_{n}})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mo>sup</mo><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo>∈</mo><mi>ℝ</mi></mrow></msub><mrow><mo lspace="0em" stretchy="false">|</mo><mrow><msub><mi>R</mi><msub><mi>N</mi><mi>n</mi></msub></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>o</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>/</mo><msqrt><msub><mi>N</mi><mi>n</mi></msub></msqrt></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\sup_{x\in{\mathbb{R}}}|R_{N_{n}}(x)|=o(1/\sqrt{N_{n}})</annotation></semantics></math>, and</span></p>
<table id="A1.Ex64" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A1.Ex64.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\lambda_{3,N_{n}}=\frac{1}{N_{n}}\sum_{{\mathcal{V}}\in\Pi}\frac{\EB[|X_{\mathcal{V}}-\EB_{1,\bm{Q}_{{\mathcal{V}}_{\tau}}}[X_{\mathcal{V}}]|^{3}]}{\sigma^{3}(\theta)}." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>λ</mi><mrow><mn>3</mn><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>N</mi><mi>n</mi></msub></mrow></msub><mo>=</mo><mrow><mfrac><mn>1</mn><msub><mi>N</mi><mi>n</mi></msub></mfrac><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><munder><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒱</mi><mo>∈</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">Π</mi></mrow></munder><mfrac><mrow><mi>𝔼</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><mrow><msub><mi>X</mi><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒱</mi></msub><mo>−</mo><mrow><msub><mi>𝔼</mi><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>𝐐</mi><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒱</mi><mi>τ</mi></msub></msub></mrow></msub><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><msub><mi>X</mi><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒱</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow><mn>3</mn></msup><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><mrow><msup><mi>σ</mi><mn>3</mn></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>θ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mfrac></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\lambda_{3,N_{n}}=\frac{1}{N_{n}}\sum_{{\mathcal{V}}\in\Pi}\frac{\EB[|X_{\mathcal{V}}-\EB_{1,\bm{Q}_{{\mathcal{V}}_{\tau}}}[X_{\mathcal{V}}]|^{3}]}{\sigma^{3}(\theta)}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
</div>
<div id="A1.SS3.SSS0.Px3.p2" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A1.SS3.SSS0.Px3.p2.1" class="ltx_p">The proof of Lemma <a href="#A1.Thmlem6" title="Lemma A.6. ‣ Step 3: Decompose the tail integral via Edgeworth expansion. ‣ A.3 Proof of Lemma ‣ Appendix A Proof for the General Framework ‣ Optimal Detection for Language Watermarks with Pseudorandom Collision" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">A.6</span></a> can be found in Section <a href="#A1.SS5" title="A.5 Proof of Lemma ‣ Appendix A Proof for the General Framework ‣ Optimal Detection for Language Watermarks with Pseudorandom Collision" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">A.5</span></a>.
Using the above expansion, we evaluate the integral in the tail expression whose proof can be found in Section <a href="#A1.SS6" title="A.6 Proof of Lemma ‣ Appendix A Proof for the General Framework ‣ Optimal Detection for Language Watermarks with Pseudorandom Collision" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">A.6</span></a></p>
</div>
<div id="A1.Thmlem7" class="ltx_theorem ltx_theorem_lem">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_title_theorem"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_theorem"><span id="A1.Thmlem7.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Lemma A.7</span></span><span id="A1.Thmlem7.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">.</span></h6>
<div id="A1.Thmlem7.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A1.Thmlem7.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A1.Thmlem7.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">Under Assumption <a href="#A1.Thmasmp1" title="Assumption A.1 (Regularity conditions for lower bound tightness). ‣ A.2 Asymptotic Tightness ‣ Appendix A Proof for the General Framework ‣ Optimal Detection for Language Watermarks with Pseudorandom Collision" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">A.1</span></a>, for any <math id="A1.Thmlem7.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\theta" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>θ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\theta</annotation></semantics></math> in the fixed interval (e.g., from Lemma <a href="#A1.Thmlem8" title="Lemma A.8 (Stability of roots for mixture equations). ‣ Step 4: Putting the pieces together. ‣ A.3 Proof of Lemma ‣ Appendix A Proof for the General Framework ‣ Optimal Detection for Language Watermarks with Pseudorandom Collision" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">A.8</span></a>), then</span></p>
<table id="A1.Ex65" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A1.Ex65.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\int_{0}^{\infty}{\mathrm{e}}^{-\theta\sqrt{N_{n}\sigma^{2}(\theta)}t}{\mathrm{d}}\bar{H}_{n}(t)=\Theta\left(\frac{1}{\sqrt{N_{n}}}\right)." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><msubsup><mo>∫</mo><mn>0</mn><mi mathvariant="normal">∞</mi></msubsup><mrow><msup><mi>e</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>θ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msqrt><mrow><msub><mi>N</mi><mi>n</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>σ</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>θ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></msqrt><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>d</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>H</mi><mo>¯</mo></mover><mi>n</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Θ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mfrac><mn>1</mn><msqrt><msub><mi>N</mi><mi>n</mi></msub></msqrt></mfrac><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\int_{0}^{\infty}{\mathrm{e}}^{-\theta\sqrt{N_{n}\sigma^{2}(\theta)}t}{\mathrm{d}}\bar{H}_{n}(t)=\Theta\left(\frac{1}{\sqrt{N_{n}}}\right).</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A1.Thmlem7.p1.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="A1.Thmlem7.p1.2.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">where <math id="A1.Thmlem7.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\Theta(\cdot)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Θ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">⋅</mo><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Theta(\cdot)</annotation></semantics></math> denote asymptotic equivalence up to constant factors.<span id="footnote7" class="ltx_note ltx_role_footnote"><sup class="ltx_note_mark">7</sup><span class="ltx_note_outer"><span class="ltx_note_content"><sup class="ltx_note_mark">7</sup>
                    <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_note"><span id="footnote7.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_upright">7</span></span>
                    
                    
                    
                  <span id="footnote7.6" class="ltx_text ltx_font_upright">That is, for two positive sequences </span><math id="footnote7.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="a_{n}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>a</mi><mi>n</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">a_{n}</annotation></semantics></math><span id="footnote7.7" class="ltx_text ltx_font_upright"> and </span><math id="footnote7.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="b_{n}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>b</mi><mi>n</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">b_{n}</annotation></semantics></math><span id="footnote7.8" class="ltx_text ltx_font_upright">, we write </span><math id="footnote7.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="a_{n}=\Theta(b_{n})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>a</mi><mi>n</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Θ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>b</mi><mi>n</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">a_{n}=\Theta(b_{n})</annotation></semantics></math><span id="footnote7.9" class="ltx_text ltx_font_upright"> if there exist constants </span><math id="footnote7.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="0&lt;c&lt;C&lt;\infty" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mn>0</mn><mo>&lt;</mo><mi>c</mi><mo>&lt;</mo><mi>C</mi><mo>&lt;</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">∞</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">0&lt;c&lt;C&lt;\infty</annotation></semantics></math><span id="footnote7.10" class="ltx_text ltx_font_upright"> such that </span><math id="footnote7.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="c\cdot b_{n}\leq a_{n}\leq C\cdot b_{n}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>c</mi><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><msub><mi>b</mi><mi>n</mi></msub></mrow><mo>≤</mo><msub><mi>a</mi><mi>n</mi></msub><mo>≤</mo><mrow><mi>C</mi><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><msub><mi>b</mi><mi>n</mi></msub></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">c\cdot b_{n}\leq a_{n}\leq C\cdot b_{n}</annotation></semantics></math><span id="footnote7.11" class="ltx_text ltx_font_upright"> for all sufficiently large </span><math id="footnote7.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="n" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>n</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">n</annotation></semantics></math><span id="footnote7.12" class="ltx_text ltx_font_upright">.</span></span></span></span></span></p>
</div>
</div>
</section>
<section id="A1.SS3.SSS0.Px4" class="ltx_paragraph">
<h5 class="ltx_title ltx_title_paragraph">Step 4: Putting the pieces together.</h5>

<div id="A1.SS3.SSS0.Px4.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A1.SS3.SSS0.Px4.p1.1" class="ltx_p">Combining Lemmas <a href="#A1.Thmlem5" title="Lemma A.5. ‣ Step 2: Reformulate the tail probability. ‣ A.3 Proof of Lemma ‣ Appendix A Proof for the General Framework ‣ Optimal Detection for Language Watermarks with Pseudorandom Collision" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">A.5</span></a>, <a href="#A1.Thmlem6" title="Lemma A.6. ‣ Step 3: Decompose the tail integral via Edgeworth expansion. ‣ A.3 Proof of Lemma ‣ Appendix A Proof for the General Framework ‣ Optimal Detection for Language Watermarks with Pseudorandom Collision" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">A.6</span></a>, and <a href="#A1.Thmlem7" title="Lemma A.7. ‣ Step 3: Decompose the tail integral via Edgeworth expansion. ‣ A.3 Proof of Lemma ‣ Appendix A Proof for the General Framework ‣ Optimal Detection for Language Watermarks with Pseudorandom Collision" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">A.7</span></a>, and setting <math id="A1.SS3.SSS0.Px4.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="x=m(\theta)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>m</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>θ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">x=m(\theta)</annotation></semantics></math>, we obtain that</p>
<table id="A1.EGx27" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A1.E44"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.E44.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle{\mathbb{P}}_{1}(S_{n}\leq-N_{n}x)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>ℙ</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>S</mi><mi>n</mi></msub><mo>≤</mo><mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><msub><mi>N</mi><mi>n</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>x</mi></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle{\mathbb{P}}_{1}(S_{n}\leq-N_{n}x)</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.E44.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=\prod_{{\mathcal{V}}\in\Pi}\phi_{\bm{Q}_{i,{\mathcal{V}}},h_{{\mathcal{V}}}}(\theta){\mathrm{e}}^{-\theta N_{n}m(\theta)}\cdot\Theta\left(\frac{1}{\sqrt{N_{n}}}\right)." display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munder><mo movablelimits="false">∏</mo><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒱</mi><mo>∈</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">Π</mi></mrow></munder></mstyle><mrow><msub><mi>ϕ</mi><mrow><msub><mi>𝑸</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>,</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒱</mi></mrow></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>h</mi><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒱</mi></msub></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>θ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>e</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>θ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>N</mi><mi>n</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>m</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>θ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></msup></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Θ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mn>1</mn><msqrt><msub><mi>N</mi><mi>n</mi></msub></msqrt></mfrac></mstyle><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=\prod_{{\mathcal{V}}\in\Pi}\phi_{\bm{Q}_{i,{\mathcal{V}}},h_{{\mathcal{V}}}}(\theta){\mathrm{e}}^{-\theta N_{n}m(\theta)}\cdot\Theta\left(\frac{1}{\sqrt{N_{n}}}\right).</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(44)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A1.SS3.SSS0.Px4.p1.2" class="ltx_p">Taking logarithms and normalizing, we complete the proof by noting that</p>
<table id="A1.EGx28" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A1.E45"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.E45.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\frac{1}{N_{n}}\log{\mathbb{P}}_{1}(S_{n}\leq-N_{n}x)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mn>1</mn><msub><mi>N</mi><mi>n</mi></msub></mfrac></mstyle><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><msub><mi>ℙ</mi><mn>1</mn></msub></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>S</mi><mi>n</mi></msub><mo>≤</mo><mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><msub><mi>N</mi><mi>n</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>x</mi></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\frac{1}{N_{n}}\log{\mathbb{P}}_{1}(S_{n}\leq-N_{n}x)</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.E45.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=\frac{1}{N_{n}}\log\prod_{{\mathcal{V}}\in\Pi}\left(\phi_{\bm{Q}_{i,{\mathcal{V}}},h_{{\mathcal{V}}}}(\theta){\mathrm{e}}^{-\theta N_{n}m(\theta)}\cdot\Theta\left(\frac{1}{\sqrt{N_{n}}}\right)\right)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mn>1</mn><msub><mi>N</mi><mi>n</mi></msub></mfrac></mstyle><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>log</mi><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munder><mo movablelimits="false">∏</mo><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒱</mi><mo>∈</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">Π</mi></mrow></munder></mstyle><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>ϕ</mi><mrow><msub><mi>𝑸</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>,</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒱</mi></mrow></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>h</mi><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒱</mi></msub></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>θ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>e</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>θ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>N</mi><mi>n</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>m</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>θ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></msup></mrow><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Θ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mn>1</mn><msqrt><msub><mi>N</mi><mi>n</mi></msub></msqrt></mfrac></mstyle><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=\frac{1}{N_{n}}\log\prod_{{\mathcal{V}}\in\Pi}\left(\phi_{\bm{Q}_{i,{\mathcal{V}}},h_{{\mathcal{V}}}}(\theta){\mathrm{e}}^{-\theta N_{n}m(\theta)}\cdot\Theta\left(\frac{1}{\sqrt{N_{n}}}\right)\right)</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(45)</span></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A1.E46"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.E46.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=-\theta x+\frac{1}{N_{n}}\sum_{{\mathcal{V}}\in\Pi}\log\left(\phi_{\bm{Q}_{i,{\mathcal{V}}},h_{{\mathcal{V}}}}(\theta)\right)-\Theta\left(\frac{\log N_{n}}{N_{n}}\right)," display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>θ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>x</mi></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mn>1</mn><msub><mi>N</mi><mi>n</mi></msub></mfrac></mstyle><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munder><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒱</mi><mo>∈</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">Π</mi></mrow></munder></mstyle><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>ϕ</mi><mrow><msub><mi>𝑸</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>,</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒱</mi></mrow></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>h</mi><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒱</mi></msub></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>θ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Θ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><msub><mi>N</mi><mi>n</mi></msub></mrow><msub><mi>N</mi><mi>n</mi></msub></mfrac></mstyle><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=-\theta x+\frac{1}{N_{n}}\sum_{{\mathcal{V}}\in\Pi}\log\left(\phi_{\bm{Q}_{i,{\mathcal{V}}},h_{{\mathcal{V}}}}(\theta)\right)-\Theta\left(\frac{\log N_{n}}{N_{n}}\right),</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(46)</span></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A1.E47"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.E47.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\overset{(a)}{=}\theta\frac{\gamma_{n,\alpha}}{N_{n}}+\frac{1}{N_{n}}\sum_{{\mathcal{V}}\in\Pi}1\log\left(\phi_{\bm{Q}_{i,{\mathcal{V}}},h_{{\mathcal{V}}}}(\theta)\right)-\Theta\left(\frac{\log N_{n}}{N_{n}}\right)," display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mrow><mover accent="true"><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="0.700em" minsize="0.700em">(</mo><mi mathsize="0.700em">a</mi><mo maxsize="0.700em" minsize="0.700em">)</mo></mrow></mover><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>θ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><msub><mi>γ</mi><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>α</mi></mrow></msub><msub><mi>N</mi><mi>n</mi></msub></mfrac></mstyle></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mn>1</mn><msub><mi>N</mi><mi>n</mi></msub></mfrac></mstyle><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munder><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒱</mi><mo>∈</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">Π</mi></mrow></munder></mstyle><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>ϕ</mi><mrow><msub><mi>𝑸</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>,</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒱</mi></mrow></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>h</mi><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒱</mi></msub></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>θ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Θ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><msub><mi>N</mi><mi>n</mi></msub></mrow><msub><mi>N</mi><mi>n</mi></msub></mfrac></mstyle><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\overset{(a)}{=}\theta\frac{\gamma_{n,\alpha}}{N_{n}}+\frac{1}{N_{n}}\sum_{{\mathcal{V}}\in\Pi}1\log\left(\phi_{\bm{Q}_{i,{\mathcal{V}}},h_{{\mathcal{V}}}}(\theta)\right)-\Theta\left(\frac{\log N_{n}}{N_{n}}\right),</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(47)</span></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A1.E48"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.E48.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\displaystyle\overset{(b)}{\geq}\inf_{\theta\geq 0}\left\{\theta\frac{\gamma_{n,\alpha}}{N_{n}}+\frac{1}{N_{n}}\sum_{{\mathcal{V}}\in\Pi}\log\left(\phi_{\bm{Q}_{i,{\mathcal{V}}},h_{{\mathcal{V}}}}(\theta)\right))\right\}-\Theta\left(\frac{\log N_{n}}{{N_{n}}}\right)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mover accent="true"><mo>≥</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="0.700em" minsize="0.700em">(</mo><mi mathsize="0.700em">b</mi><mo maxsize="0.700em" minsize="0.700em">)</mo></mrow></mover><munder><mo lspace="0.278em" movablelimits="false" rspace="0em">inf</mo><mrow><mi>θ</mi><mo>≥</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow></munder><mrow><mo>{</mo><mi>θ</mi><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><msub><mi>γ</mi><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>α</mi></mrow></msub><msub><mi>N</mi><mi>n</mi></msub></mfrac></mstyle><mo>+</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mn>1</mn><msub><mi>N</mi><mi>n</mi></msub></mfrac></mstyle><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munder><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒱</mi><mo>∈</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">Π</mi></mrow></munder></mstyle><mi>log</mi><mrow><mo>(</mo><msub><mi>ϕ</mi><mrow><msub><mi>𝑸</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>,</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒱</mi></mrow></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>h</mi><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒱</mi></msub></mrow></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>θ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>}</mo><mo>−</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">Θ</mi><mo>(</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><msub><mi>N</mi><mi>n</mi></msub></mrow><msub><mi>N</mi><mi>n</mi></msub></mfrac></mstyle><mo>)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\overset{(b)}{\geq}\inf_{\theta\geq 0}\left\{\theta\frac{\gamma_{n,\alpha}}{N_{n}}+\frac{1}{N_{n}}\sum_{{\mathcal{V}}\in\Pi}\log\left(\phi_{\bm{Q}_{i,{\mathcal{V}}},h_{{\mathcal{V}}}}(\theta)\right))\right\}-\Theta\left(\frac{\log N_{n}}{{N_{n}}}\right)</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(48)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A1.SS3.SSS0.Px4.p1.3" class="ltx_p">where (a) follows by setting <math id="A1.SS3.SSS0.Px4.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="x=-\frac{\gamma_{n,\alpha}}{N_{n}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo>−</mo><mfrac><msub><mi>γ</mi><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>α</mi></mrow></msub><msub><mi>N</mi><mi>n</mi></msub></mfrac></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">x=-\frac{\gamma_{n,\alpha}}{N_{n}}</annotation></semantics></math>, and (b) uses the conclusion that the solution to <math id="A1.SS3.SSS0.Px4.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="m(\theta)=-\frac{\gamma_{n,\alpha}}{N_{n}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>m</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>θ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo>−</mo><mfrac><msub><mi>γ</mi><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>α</mi></mrow></msub><msub><mi>N</mi><mi>n</mi></msub></mfrac></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">m(\theta)=-\frac{\gamma_{n,\alpha}}{N_{n}}</annotation></semantics></math> satisfies <math id="A1.SS3.SSS0.Px4.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\theta\geq 0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>θ</mi><mo>≥</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\theta\geq 0</annotation></semantics></math> from Lemma <a href="#A1.Thmlem8" title="Lemma A.8 (Stability of roots for mixture equations). ‣ Step 4: Putting the pieces together. ‣ A.3 Proof of Lemma ‣ Appendix A Proof for the General Framework ‣ Optimal Detection for Language Watermarks with Pseudorandom Collision" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">A.8</span></a>. The proof of Lemma <a href="#A1.Thmlem8" title="Lemma A.8 (Stability of roots for mixture equations). ‣ Step 4: Putting the pieces together. ‣ A.3 Proof of Lemma ‣ Appendix A Proof for the General Framework ‣ Optimal Detection for Language Watermarks with Pseudorandom Collision" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">A.8</span></a> is in Section <a href="#A1.SS7" title="A.7 Proof of Lemma ‣ Appendix A Proof for the General Framework ‣ Optimal Detection for Language Watermarks with Pseudorandom Collision" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">A.7</span></a>.</p>
</div>
<div id="A1.Thmlem8" class="ltx_theorem ltx_theorem_lem">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_title_theorem"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_theorem"><span id="A1.Thmlem8.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Lemma A.8</span></span><span id="A1.Thmlem8.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold"> </span>(Stability of roots for mixture equations)<span id="A1.Thmlem8.4" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">.</span></h6>
<div id="A1.Thmlem8.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A1.Thmlem8.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A1.Thmlem8.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">Let Assumptions <a href="#S3.Thmasmp3" title="Assumption 3.3. ‣ 3.3 Detection Efficiency and Optimal Scores ‣ 3 A Statistical Framework under Pseudorandomness Collision ‣ Optimal Detection for Language Watermarks with Pseudorandom Collision" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">3.3</span></a> and <a href="#A1.Thmasmp1" title="Assumption A.1 (Regularity conditions for lower bound tightness). ‣ A.2 Asymptotic Tightness ‣ Appendix A Proof for the General Framework ‣ Optimal Detection for Language Watermarks with Pseudorandom Collision" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">A.1</span></a> hold. Consider the equation <math id="A1.Thmlem8.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="m(\theta)=-\frac{\gamma_{n,\alpha}}{N_{n}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>m</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>θ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo>−</mo><mfrac><msub><mi>γ</mi><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>α</mi></mrow></msub><msub><mi>N</mi><mi>n</mi></msub></mfrac></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">m(\theta)=-\frac{\gamma_{n,\alpha}}{N_{n}}</annotation></semantics></math>, where <math id="A1.Thmlem8.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="m(\theta)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>m</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>θ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">m(\theta)</annotation></semantics></math> is given in Lemma <a href="#A1.Thmlem5" title="Lemma A.5. ‣ Step 2: Reformulate the tail probability. ‣ A.3 Proof of Lemma ‣ Appendix A Proof for the General Framework ‣ Optimal Detection for Language Watermarks with Pseudorandom Collision" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">A.5</span></a>.
Then the root of this equation is well-defined and lies within a fixed interval <math id="A1.Thmlem8.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="[\underline{M},\overline{M}]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><munder accentunder="true"><mi>M</mi><mo stretchy="true">¯</mo></munder><mo>,</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>M</mi><mo stretchy="true">¯</mo></mover><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">[\underline{M},\overline{M}]</annotation></semantics></math>, where the constants <math id="A1.Thmlem8.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\underline{M},\overline{M}&gt;0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><munder accentunder="true"><mi>M</mi><mo stretchy="true">¯</mo></munder><mo>,</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>M</mi><mo stretchy="true">¯</mo></mover></mrow><mo>&gt;</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\underline{M},\overline{M}&gt;0</annotation></semantics></math> are independent of <math id="A1.Thmlem8.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="N_{n}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>N</mi><mi>n</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">N_{n}</annotation></semantics></math> and the specific choice of NTP assignment <math id="A1.Thmlem8.p1.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="{\mathcal{Q}}_{i}^{\star}=(\bm{Q}_{i,{\mathcal{V}}})_{{\mathcal{V}}\in\Pi}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msubsup><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒬</mi><mi>i</mi><mo>⋆</mo></msubsup><mo>=</mo><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>𝐐</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>,</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒱</mi></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒱</mi><mo>∈</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">Π</mi></mrow></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\mathcal{Q}}_{i}^{\star}=(\bm{Q}_{i,{\mathcal{V}}})_{{\mathcal{V}}\in\Pi}</annotation></semantics></math>.</span></p>
</div>
</div>
<div id="A1.SS3.SSS0.Px4.p2" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A1.SS3.SSS0.Px4.p2.1" class="ltx_p">∎</p>
</div>
</section>
</section>
<section id="A1.SS4" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection">A.4 </span>Proof of Lemma <a href="#A1.Thmlem5" title="Lemma A.5. ‣ Step 2: Reformulate the tail probability. ‣ A.3 Proof of Lemma ‣ Appendix A Proof for the General Framework ‣ Optimal Detection for Language Watermarks with Pseudorandom Collision" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">A.5</span></a></h3>

<div id="A1.SS4.2" class="ltx_proof">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_font_italic ltx_title_proof">Proof of Lemma <a href="#A1.Thmlem5" title="Lemma A.5. ‣ Step 2: Reformulate the tail probability. ‣ A.3 Proof of Lemma ‣ Appendix A Proof for the General Framework ‣ Optimal Detection for Language Watermarks with Pseudorandom Collision" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">A.5</span></a>.</h6>
<div id="A1.SS4.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A1.SS4.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A1.SS4.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text">Let <math id="A1.SS4.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="W_{n}(x)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>W</mi><mi>n</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">W_{n}(x)</annotation></semantics></math>, <math id="A1.SS4.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\bar{W}_{n}(x)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>W</mi><mo>¯</mo></mover><mi>n</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\bar{W}_{n}(x)</annotation></semantics></math>, and <math id="A1.SS4.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\bar{H}_{n}(x)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>H</mi><mo>¯</mo></mover><mi>n</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\bar{H}_{n}(x)</annotation></semantics></math> denote the CDFs of the random variables <math id="A1.SS4.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\sum_{{\mathcal{V}}\in\Pi}X_{{\mathcal{V}}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mo>∑</mo><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒱</mi><mo>∈</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">Π</mi></mrow></msub><msub><mi>X</mi><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒱</mi></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\sum_{{\mathcal{V}}\in\Pi}X_{{\mathcal{V}}}</annotation></semantics></math>, <math id="A1.SS4.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\sum_{{\mathcal{V}}\in\Pi}\bar{X}_{{\mathcal{V}}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mo>∑</mo><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒱</mi><mo>∈</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">Π</mi></mrow></msub><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>X</mi><mo>¯</mo></mover><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒱</mi></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\sum_{{\mathcal{V}}\in\Pi}\bar{X}_{{\mathcal{V}}}</annotation></semantics></math>, and the standardized sum <math id="A1.SS4.p1.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\frac{\sum_{{\mathcal{V}}\in\Pi}\bar{X}_{{\mathcal{V}}}-N_{n}m(\theta)}{\sqrt{N_{n}\sigma^{2}(\theta)}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mfrac><mrow><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="false"><msub><mo maxsize="0.700em" minsize="0.700em" stretchy="true">∑</mo><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒱</mi><mo>∈</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">Π</mi></mrow></msub></mstyle><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>X</mi><mo>¯</mo></mover><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒱</mi></msub></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><msub><mi>N</mi><mi>n</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>m</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>θ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><msqrt><mrow><msub><mi>N</mi><mi>n</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>σ</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>θ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></msqrt></mfrac><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\frac{\sum_{{\mathcal{V}}\in\Pi}\bar{X}_{{\mathcal{V}}}-N_{n}m(\theta)}{\sqrt{N_{n}\sigma^{2}(\theta)}}</annotation></semantics></math>, respectively.
By definition, it follows that</span></p>
<table id="A1.EGx29" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A1.E49"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.E49.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\bar{H}_{n}(x)=\bar{W}_{n}\left(\sqrt{N_{n}\sigma^{2}(\theta)}x+N_{n}m(\theta)\right)." display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>H</mi><mo>¯</mo></mover><mi>n</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>W</mi><mo>¯</mo></mover><mi>n</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mrow><msqrt><mrow><msub><mi>N</mi><mi>n</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>σ</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>θ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></msqrt><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>x</mi></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><msub><mi>N</mi><mi>n</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>m</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>θ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\bar{H}_{n}(x)=\bar{W}_{n}\left(\sqrt{N_{n}\sigma^{2}(\theta)}x+N_{n}m(\theta)\right).</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(49)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A1.SS4.p1.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="A1.SS4.p1.2.1" class="ltx_text">Let <span id="A1.SS4.p1.2.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_markedasmath">i</span> denote the imaginary unit. The characteristic function of <math id="A1.SS4.p1.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="W_{n}(x)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>W</mi><mi>n</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">W_{n}(x)</annotation></semantics></math> is given by</span></p>
<table id="A1.EGx30" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A1.E50"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.E50.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle w_{n}(z):=\EB_{1,{\mathcal{Q}}_{i}^{\star}}[{\mathrm{e}}^{{\textnormal{i}}z\sum_{{\mathcal{V}}\in\Pi}X_{{\mathcal{V}}}}]=\prod_{{\mathcal{V}}\in\Pi}\phi_{\bm{Q}_{i,{\mathcal{V}}},h_{{\mathcal{V}}}}({\textnormal{i}}z)." display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>w</mi><mi>n</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>z</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>:=</mo><mrow><msub><mi>𝔼</mi><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>,</mo><msubsup><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒬</mi><mi>i</mi><mo>⋆</mo></msubsup></mrow></msub><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><msup><mi>e</mi><mrow><mtext>i</mtext><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>z</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="false"><msub><mo maxsize="0.700em" minsize="0.700em" stretchy="true">∑</mo><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒱</mi><mo>∈</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">Π</mi></mrow></msub></mstyle><msub><mi>X</mi><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒱</mi></msub></mrow></mrow></msup><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munder><mo movablelimits="false">∏</mo><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒱</mi><mo>∈</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">Π</mi></mrow></munder></mstyle><mrow><msub><mi>ϕ</mi><mrow><msub><mi>𝐐</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>,</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒱</mi></mrow></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>h</mi><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒱</mi></msub></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mtext>i</mtext><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>z</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle w_{n}(z):=\EB_{1,{\mathcal{Q}}_{i}^{\star}}[{\mathrm{e}}^{{\textnormal{i}}z\sum_{{\mathcal{V}}\in\Pi}X_{{\mathcal{V}}}}]=\prod_{{\mathcal{V}}\in\Pi}\phi_{\bm{Q}_{i,{\mathcal{V}}},h_{{\mathcal{V}}}}({\textnormal{i}}z).</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(50)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A1.SS4.p1.3" class="ltx_p"><span id="A1.SS4.p1.3.1" class="ltx_text">Similarly, the characteristic function of <math id="A1.SS4.p1.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\bar{W}_{n}(x)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>W</mi><mo>¯</mo></mover><mi>n</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\bar{W}_{n}(x)</annotation></semantics></math> is</span></p>
<table id="A1.EGx31" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A1.E51"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.E51.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\bar{w}_{n}(z):=\EB_{1,{\mathcal{Q}}_{i}^{\star}}[{\mathrm{e}}^{{\textnormal{i}}z\sum_{{\mathcal{V}}\in\Pi}\bar{X}_{{\mathcal{V}}}}]=\prod_{{\mathcal{V}}\in\Pi}\bar{\phi}_{\bm{Q}_{i,{\mathcal{V}}},h_{{\mathcal{V}}}}({\textnormal{i}}z)," display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>w</mi><mo>¯</mo></mover><mi>n</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>z</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>:=</mo><mrow><msub><mi>𝔼</mi><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>,</mo><msubsup><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒬</mi><mi>i</mi><mo>⋆</mo></msubsup></mrow></msub><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><msup><mi>e</mi><mrow><mtext>i</mtext><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>z</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="false"><msub><mo maxsize="0.700em" minsize="0.700em" stretchy="true">∑</mo><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒱</mi><mo>∈</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">Π</mi></mrow></msub></mstyle><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>X</mi><mo>¯</mo></mover><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒱</mi></msub></mrow></mrow></msup><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munder><mo movablelimits="false">∏</mo><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒱</mi><mo>∈</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">Π</mi></mrow></munder></mstyle><mrow><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>ϕ</mi><mo>¯</mo></mover><mrow><msub><mi>𝐐</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>,</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒱</mi></mrow></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>h</mi><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒱</mi></msub></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mtext>i</mtext><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>z</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\bar{w}_{n}(z):=\EB_{1,{\mathcal{Q}}_{i}^{\star}}[{\mathrm{e}}^{{\textnormal{i}}z\sum_{{\mathcal{V}}\in\Pi}\bar{X}_{{\mathcal{V}}}}]=\prod_{{\mathcal{V}}\in\Pi}\bar{\phi}_{\bm{Q}_{i,{\mathcal{V}}},h_{{\mathcal{V}}}}({\textnormal{i}}z),</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(51)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A1.SS4.p1.4" class="ltx_p"><span id="A1.SS4.p1.4.1" class="ltx_text">where by definition, we have</span></p>
<table id="A1.Ex66" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A1.Ex66.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\bar{\phi}_{\bm{Q}_{i,{\mathcal{V}}},h_{{\mathcal{V}}}}({\textnormal{i}}z)=\phi_{\bm{Q}_{i,{\mathcal{V}}},h_{{\mathcal{V}}}}({\textnormal{i}}(z-{\textnormal{i}}\theta))/\phi_{\bm{Q}_{i,{\mathcal{V}}},h_{{\mathcal{V}}}}(\theta)" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>ϕ</mi><mo>¯</mo></mover><mrow><msub><mi>𝑸</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>,</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒱</mi></mrow></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>h</mi><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒱</mi></msub></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mtext>i</mtext><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>z</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>ϕ</mi><mrow><msub><mi>𝑸</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>,</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒱</mi></mrow></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>h</mi><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒱</mi></msub></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mtext>i</mtext><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>z</mi><mo>−</mo><mrow><mtext>i</mtext><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>θ</mi></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>/</mo><msub><mi>ϕ</mi><mrow><msub><mi>𝑸</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>,</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒱</mi></mrow></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>h</mi><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒱</mi></msub></mrow></msub></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>θ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\bar{\phi}_{\bm{Q}_{i,{\mathcal{V}}},h_{{\mathcal{V}}}}({\textnormal{i}}z)=\phi_{\bm{Q}_{i,{\mathcal{V}}},h_{{\mathcal{V}}}}({\textnormal{i}}(z-{\textnormal{i}}\theta))/\phi_{\bm{Q}_{i,{\mathcal{V}}},h_{{\mathcal{V}}}}(\theta)</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A1.SS4.p1.5" class="ltx_p"><span id="A1.SS4.p1.5.1" class="ltx_text">is the MGF of the centered variable <math id="A1.SS4.p1.m10" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\bar{X}_{{\mathcal{V}}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>X</mi><mo>¯</mo></mover><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒱</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\bar{X}_{{\mathcal{V}}}</annotation></semantics></math> under the NTP distribution <math id="A1.SS4.p1.m11" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\bm{Q}_{i,{\mathcal{V}}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>𝑸</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>,</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒱</mi></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\bm{Q}_{i,{\mathcal{V}}}</annotation></semantics></math>. Using this relation, we obtain the identity:</span></p>
<table id="A1.EGx32" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A1.E52"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.E52.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle w_{n}(z)=\bar{w}_{n}(z+{\textnormal{i}}\theta)\cdot\prod_{{\mathcal{V}}\in\Pi}\phi_{\bm{Q}_{i,{\mathcal{V}}},h_{{\mathcal{V}}}}(\theta)." display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>w</mi><mi>n</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>z</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>w</mi><mo>¯</mo></mover><mi>n</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>z</mi><mo>+</mo><mrow><mtext>i</mtext><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>θ</mi></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.055em" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munder><mo movablelimits="false">∏</mo><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒱</mi><mo>∈</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">Π</mi></mrow></munder></mstyle><mrow><msub><mi>ϕ</mi><mrow><msub><mi>𝑸</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>,</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒱</mi></mrow></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>h</mi><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒱</mi></msub></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>θ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle w_{n}(z)=\bar{w}_{n}(z+{\textnormal{i}}\theta)\cdot\prod_{{\mathcal{V}}\in\Pi}\phi_{\bm{Q}_{i,{\mathcal{V}}},h_{{\mathcal{V}}}}(\theta).</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(52)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A1.SS4.p1.6" class="ltx_p"><span id="A1.SS4.p1.6.1" class="ltx_text">If the imaginary part of <math id="A1.SS4.p1.m12" class="ltx_Math" alttext="z" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>z</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">z</annotation></semantics></math> is zero, the left side of the last equation is the characteristic function of <math id="A1.SS4.p1.m13" class="ltx_Math" alttext="W_{n}(x)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>W</mi><mi>n</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">W_{n}(x)</annotation></semantics></math>, while the right side is the characteristic function of</span></p>
<table id="A1.Ex67" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A1.Ex67.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\prod_{{\mathcal{V}}\in\Pi}\phi_{\bm{Q}_{i,{\mathcal{V}}},h_{{\mathcal{V}}}}(\theta)\int_{-\infty}^{x}{\mathrm{e}}^{-\theta y}{\mathrm{d}}\bar{W}_{n}(y)." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><munder><mo movablelimits="false">∏</mo><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒱</mi><mo>∈</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">Π</mi></mrow></munder><mrow><msub><mi>ϕ</mi><mrow><msub><mi>𝑸</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>,</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒱</mi></mrow></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>h</mi><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒱</mi></msub></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>θ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><msubsup><mo>∫</mo><mrow><mo>−</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">∞</mi></mrow><mi>x</mi></msubsup><mrow><msup><mi>e</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>θ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>y</mi></mrow></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>d</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>W</mi><mo>¯</mo></mover><mi>n</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>y</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\prod_{{\mathcal{V}}\in\Pi}\phi_{\bm{Q}_{i,{\mathcal{V}}},h_{{\mathcal{V}}}}(\theta)\int_{-\infty}^{x}{\mathrm{e}}^{-\theta y}{\mathrm{d}}\bar{W}_{n}(y).</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A1.SS4.p1.7" class="ltx_p"><span id="A1.SS4.p1.7.1" class="ltx_text">Thus, for all <math id="A1.SS4.p1.m14" class="ltx_Math" alttext="x\in\mathbb{R}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo>∈</mo><mi>ℝ</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">x\in\mathbb{R}</annotation></semantics></math>, we have</span></p>
<table id="A1.EGx33" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A1.E53"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.E53.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle W_{n}(x)=\prod_{{\mathcal{V}}\in\Pi}\phi_{\bm{Q}_{i,{\mathcal{V}}},h_{{\mathcal{V}}}}(\theta)\int_{-\infty}^{x}{\mathrm{e}}^{-\theta y}{\mathrm{d}}\bar{W}_{n}(y)." display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>W</mi><mi>n</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munder><mo movablelimits="false">∏</mo><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒱</mi><mo>∈</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">Π</mi></mrow></munder></mstyle><mrow><msub><mi>ϕ</mi><mrow><msub><mi>𝑸</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>,</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒱</mi></mrow></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>h</mi><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒱</mi></msub></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>θ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><msubsup><mo>∫</mo><mrow><mo>−</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">∞</mi></mrow><mi>x</mi></msubsup></mstyle><mrow><msup><mi>e</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>θ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>y</mi></mrow></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>d</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>W</mi><mo>¯</mo></mover><mi>n</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>y</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle W_{n}(x)=\prod_{{\mathcal{V}}\in\Pi}\phi_{\bm{Q}_{i,{\mathcal{V}}},h_{{\mathcal{V}}}}(\theta)\int_{-\infty}^{x}{\mathrm{e}}^{-\theta y}{\mathrm{d}}\bar{W}_{n}(y).</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(53)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
<div id="A1.SS4.p2" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A1.SS4.p2.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A1.SS4.p2.1.1" class="ltx_text">Now, make the change of variables <math id="A1.SS4.p2.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="y=N_{n}m(\theta)+\sqrt{N_{n}\sigma^{2}(\theta)}t" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>y</mi><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>N</mi><mi>n</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>m</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>θ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><msqrt><mrow><msub><mi>N</mi><mi>n</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>σ</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>θ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></msqrt><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">y=N_{n}m(\theta)+\sqrt{N_{n}\sigma^{2}(\theta)}t</annotation></semantics></math>, which yields</span></p>
<table id="A1.EGx34" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A1.E54"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.E54.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle W_{n}\left(x\right)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>W</mi><mi>n</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle W_{n}\left(x\right)</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.E54.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=\prod_{{\mathcal{V}}\in\Pi}\phi_{\bm{Q}_{i,{\mathcal{V}}},h_{{\mathcal{V}}}}(\theta)\int_{-\infty}^{\frac{x-N_{n}m(\theta)}{\sqrt{N_{n}\sigma^{2}(\theta)}}}{\mathrm{e}}^{-\theta(N_{n}m(\theta)+\sqrt{N_{n}\sigma^{2}(\theta)}t)}{\mathrm{d}}\bar{H}_{n}(t)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munder><mo movablelimits="false">∏</mo><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒱</mi><mo>∈</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">Π</mi></mrow></munder></mstyle><mrow><msub><mi>ϕ</mi><mrow><msub><mi>𝑸</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>,</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒱</mi></mrow></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>h</mi><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒱</mi></msub></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>θ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><msubsup><mo>∫</mo><mrow><mo>−</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">∞</mi></mrow><mfrac><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo>−</mo><mrow><msub><mi>N</mi><mi>n</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>m</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>θ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><msqrt><mrow><msub><mi>N</mi><mi>n</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>σ</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>θ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></msqrt></mfrac></msubsup></mstyle><mrow><msup><mi>e</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>θ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>N</mi><mi>n</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>m</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>θ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><msqrt><mrow><msub><mi>N</mi><mi>n</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>σ</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>θ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></msqrt><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>d</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>H</mi><mo>¯</mo></mover><mi>n</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=\prod_{{\mathcal{V}}\in\Pi}\phi_{\bm{Q}_{i,{\mathcal{V}}},h_{{\mathcal{V}}}}(\theta)\int_{-\infty}^{\frac{x-N_{n}m(\theta)}{\sqrt{N_{n}\sigma^{2}(\theta)}}}{\mathrm{e}}^{-\theta(N_{n}m(\theta)+\sqrt{N_{n}\sigma^{2}(\theta)}t)}{\mathrm{d}}\bar{H}_{n}(t)</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(54)</span></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A1.E55"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.E55.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=\prod_{{\mathcal{V}}\in\Pi}\phi_{\bm{Q}_{i,{\mathcal{V}}},h_{{\mathcal{V}}}}(\theta){\mathrm{e}}^{-\theta N_{n}m(\theta)}\int_{-\infty}^{\frac{x-N_{n}m(\theta)}{\sqrt{N_{n}\sigma^{2}(\theta)}}}{\mathrm{e}}^{-\theta\sqrt{N_{n}\sigma^{2}(\theta)}t}{\mathrm{d}}\bar{H}_{n}(t)." display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munder><mo movablelimits="false">∏</mo><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒱</mi><mo>∈</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">Π</mi></mrow></munder></mstyle><mrow><msub><mi>ϕ</mi><mrow><msub><mi>𝑸</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>,</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒱</mi></mrow></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>h</mi><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒱</mi></msub></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>θ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>e</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>θ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>N</mi><mi>n</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>m</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>θ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><msubsup><mo>∫</mo><mrow><mo>−</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">∞</mi></mrow><mfrac><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo>−</mo><mrow><msub><mi>N</mi><mi>n</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>m</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>θ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><msqrt><mrow><msub><mi>N</mi><mi>n</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>σ</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>θ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></msqrt></mfrac></msubsup></mstyle><mrow><msup><mi>e</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>θ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msqrt><mrow><msub><mi>N</mi><mi>n</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>σ</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>θ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></msqrt><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>d</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>H</mi><mo>¯</mo></mover><mi>n</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=\prod_{{\mathcal{V}}\in\Pi}\phi_{\bm{Q}_{i,{\mathcal{V}}},h_{{\mathcal{V}}}}(\theta){\mathrm{e}}^{-\theta N_{n}m(\theta)}\int_{-\infty}^{\frac{x-N_{n}m(\theta)}{\sqrt{N_{n}\sigma^{2}(\theta)}}}{\mathrm{e}}^{-\theta\sqrt{N_{n}\sigma^{2}(\theta)}t}{\mathrm{d}}\bar{H}_{n}(t).</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(55)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A1.SS4.p2.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="A1.SS4.p2.2.1" class="ltx_text">Therefore, by substituting <math id="A1.SS4.p2.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="x\leftarrow N_{n}x" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">←</mo><mrow><msub><mi>N</mi><mi>n</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>x</mi></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">x\leftarrow N_{n}x</annotation></semantics></math>, we obtain</span></p>
<table id="A1.Ex68" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A1.Ex68.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="1-W_{n}(N_{n}x)=\prod_{{\mathcal{V}}\in\Pi}\phi_{\bm{Q}_{i,{\mathcal{V}}},h_{{\mathcal{V}}}}(\theta){\mathrm{e}}^{-\theta N_{n}m(\theta)}\int_{\frac{N_{n}x-N_{n}m(\theta)}{\sqrt{N_{n}\sigma^{2}(\theta)}}}^{\infty}{\mathrm{e}}^{-\theta\sqrt{N_{n}\sigma^{2}(\theta)}t}{\mathrm{d}}\bar{H}_{n}(t)," display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mrow><msub><mi>W</mi><mi>n</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>N</mi><mi>n</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>x</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.111em">=</mo><mrow><munder><mo movablelimits="false">∏</mo><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒱</mi><mo>∈</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">Π</mi></mrow></munder><mrow><msub><mi>ϕ</mi><mrow><msub><mi>𝑸</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>,</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒱</mi></mrow></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>h</mi><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒱</mi></msub></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>θ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>e</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>θ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>N</mi><mi>n</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>m</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>θ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><msubsup><mo>∫</mo><mfrac><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>N</mi><mi>n</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>x</mi></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><msub><mi>N</mi><mi>n</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>m</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>θ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><msqrt><mrow><msub><mi>N</mi><mi>n</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>σ</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>θ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></msqrt></mfrac><mi mathvariant="normal">∞</mi></msubsup><mrow><msup><mi>e</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>θ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msqrt><mrow><msub><mi>N</mi><mi>n</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>σ</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>θ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></msqrt><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>d</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>H</mi><mo>¯</mo></mover><mi>n</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">1-W_{n}(N_{n}x)=\prod_{{\mathcal{V}}\in\Pi}\phi_{\bm{Q}_{i,{\mathcal{V}}},h_{{\mathcal{V}}}}(\theta){\mathrm{e}}^{-\theta N_{n}m(\theta)}\int_{\frac{N_{n}x-N_{n}m(\theta)}{\sqrt{N_{n}\sigma^{2}(\theta)}}}^{\infty}{\mathrm{e}}^{-\theta\sqrt{N_{n}\sigma^{2}(\theta)}t}{\mathrm{d}}\bar{H}_{n}(t),</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A1.SS4.p2.3" class="ltx_p"><span id="A1.SS4.p2.3.1" class="ltx_text">which concludes the proof.
∎</span></p>
</div>
</div>
</section>
<section id="A1.SS5" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection">A.5 </span>Proof of Lemma <a href="#A1.Thmlem6" title="Lemma A.6. ‣ Step 3: Decompose the tail integral via Edgeworth expansion. ‣ A.3 Proof of Lemma ‣ Appendix A Proof for the General Framework ‣ Optimal Detection for Language Watermarks with Pseudorandom Collision" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">A.6</span></a></h3>

<div id="A1.SS5.2" class="ltx_proof">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_font_italic ltx_title_proof">Proof of Lemma <a href="#A1.Thmlem6" title="Lemma A.6. ‣ Step 3: Decompose the tail integral via Edgeworth expansion. ‣ A.3 Proof of Lemma ‣ Appendix A Proof for the General Framework ‣ Optimal Detection for Language Watermarks with Pseudorandom Collision" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">A.6</span></a>.</h6>
<div id="A1.SS5.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A1.SS5.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A1.SS5.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text">At a high level, we apply the Edgeworth expansion to approximate the PDF of <math id="A1.SS5.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\bar{H}_{n}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>H</mi><mo>¯</mo></mover><mi>n</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\bar{H}_{n}</annotation></semantics></math> using functionals of the standard Gaussian distribution. We will make use of the following lemma and verify that its conditions are satisfied in our setting.</span></p>
</div>
<div id="A1.Thmlem9" class="ltx_theorem ltx_theorem_lem">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_title_theorem"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_theorem"><span id="A1.Thmlem9.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Lemma A.9</span></span><span id="A1.Thmlem9.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold"> </span>(Classical Edgeworth expansion)<span id="A1.Thmlem9.4" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">.</span></h6>
<div id="A1.Thmlem9.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A1.Thmlem9.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A1.Thmlem9.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">Let <math id="A1.Thmlem9.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="X_{1},\dots,X_{n}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>X</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>X</mi><mi>n</mi></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">X_{1},\dots,X_{n}</annotation></semantics></math> be independent, zero-mean real-valued random variables with variances <math id="A1.Thmlem9.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\sigma_{i}^{2}=\mathrm{Var}(X_{i})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msubsup><mi>σ</mi><mi>i</mi><mn>2</mn></msubsup><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>Var</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>X</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\sigma_{i}^{2}=\mathrm{Var}(X_{i})</annotation></semantics></math> and finite third moments. Define</span></p>
<table id="A1.Ex69" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A1.Ex69.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="S_{n}:=\sum_{i=1}^{n}X_{i},\quad B_{n}:=\sqrt{\frac{1}{n}\sum_{i=1}^{n}\sigma_{i}^{2}},\quad Z_{n}:=\frac{S_{n}}{\sqrt{n}B_{n}},\quad\text{and}\quad\lambda_{3,n}:=\frac{1}{n}\sum_{i=1}^{n}\frac{\EB[X_{i}^{3}]}{B_{n}^{3}}." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>S</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>n</mi></msub><mo rspace="0.111em">:=</mo><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><msub><mrow></mrow><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><msup><mrow></mrow><mi>n</mi></msup><mi>X</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>i</mi></msub><mo rspace="1.167em">,</mo><mi>B</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>n</mi></msub><mo>:=</mo><msqrt><mrow><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mi>n</mi></mfrac><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>n</mi></munderover><msubsup><mi>σ</mi><mi>i</mi><mn>2</mn></msubsup></mrow></mrow></msqrt><mo rspace="1.167em">,</mo><mi>Z</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>n</mi></msub><mo>:=</mo><mfrac><msub><mi>S</mi><mi>n</mi></msub><mrow><msqrt><mi>n</mi></msqrt><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>B</mi><mi>n</mi></msub></mrow></mfrac><mo rspace="1.167em">,</mo><mtext class="ltx_mathvariant_italic">and</mtext><mi>λ</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mrow><mn>3</mn><mo>,</mo><mi>n</mi></mrow></msub><mo>:=</mo><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mi>n</mi></mfrac><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><msub><mrow></mrow><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><msup><mrow></mrow><mi>n</mi></msup><mfrac><mrow><mi>𝔼</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><msubsup><mi>X</mi><mi>i</mi><mn>3</mn></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><msubsup><mi>B</mi><mi>n</mi><mn>3</mn></msubsup></mfrac><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">S_{n}:=\sum_{i=1}^{n}X_{i},\quad B_{n}:=\sqrt{\frac{1}{n}\sum_{i=1}^{n}\sigma_{i}^{2}},\quad Z_{n}:=\frac{S_{n}}{\sqrt{n}B_{n}},\quad\text{and}\quad\lambda_{3,n}:=\frac{1}{n}\sum_{i=1}^{n}\frac{\EB[X_{i}^{3}]}{B_{n}^{3}}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A1.Thmlem9.p1.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="A1.Thmlem9.p1.2.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">Suppose the following conditions hold:</span></p>
<ol id="A1.I3" class="ltx_enumerate">
<li id="A1.I3.i1" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">1.</span> 
<div id="A1.I3.i1.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A1.I3.i1.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><math id="A1.I3.i1.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\liminf\limits_{n\to\infty}B_{n}&gt;0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><munder><mo movablelimits="false">lim inf</mo><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">∞</mi></mrow></munder><msub><mi>B</mi><mi>n</mi></msub></mrow><mo>&gt;</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\liminf\limits_{n\to\infty}B_{n}&gt;0</annotation></semantics></math><span id="A1.I3.i1.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic"> and </span><math id="A1.I3.i1.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\limsup_{n\to\infty}\frac{1}{n}\EB[|X_{j}|^{3}]&lt;\infty" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mo>lim sup</mo><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">∞</mi></mrow></msub><mrow><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mi>n</mi></mfrac><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mi>𝔼</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><msub><mi>X</mi><mi>j</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow><mn>3</mn></msup><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>&lt;</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">∞</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\limsup_{n\to\infty}\frac{1}{n}\EB[|X_{j}|^{3}]&lt;\infty</annotation></semantics></math><span id="A1.I3.i1.p1.1.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">.</span></p>
</div></li>
<li id="A1.I3.i2" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">2.</span> 
<div id="A1.I3.i2.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A1.I3.i2.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A1.I3.i2.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">For some positive </span><math id="A1.I3.i2.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\tau&lt;1/2" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>τ</mi><mo>&lt;</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>/</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\tau&lt;1/2</annotation></semantics></math><span id="A1.I3.i2.p1.1.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">, </span><math id="A1.I3.i2.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\frac{1}{n}\sum_{j=1}^{n}\EB\left[|X_{j}|^{3}\mathbf{1}_{|X_{j}|&gt;n^{\tau}}\right]\to 0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mi>n</mi></mfrac><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><msubsup><mo>∑</mo><mrow><mi>j</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>n</mi></msubsup><mrow><mi>𝔼</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>[</mo><mrow><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><msub><mi>X</mi><mi>j</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow><mn>3</mn></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mn>𝟏</mn><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><msub><mi>X</mi><mi>j</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow><mo>&gt;</mo><msup><mi>n</mi><mi>τ</mi></msup></mrow></msub></mrow><mo>]</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\frac{1}{n}\sum_{j=1}^{n}\EB\left[|X_{j}|^{3}\mathbf{1}_{|X_{j}|&gt;n^{\tau}}\right]\to 0</annotation></semantics></math><span id="A1.I3.i2.p1.1.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic"> as </span><math id="A1.I3.i2.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="n\to\infty" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">∞</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">n\to\infty</annotation></semantics></math><span id="A1.I3.i2.p1.1.4" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">.</span></p>
</div></li>
<li id="A1.I3.i3" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">3.</span> 
<div id="A1.I3.i3.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A1.I3.i3.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A1.I3.i3.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold ltx_font_italic">(Cramér’s condition)</span><span id="A1.I3.i3.p1.1.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic"> For every fixed </span><math id="A1.I3.i3.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\varepsilon&gt;0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>ε</mi><mo>&gt;</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\varepsilon&gt;0</annotation></semantics></math><span id="A1.I3.i3.p1.1.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">, </span><math id="A1.I3.i3.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="{n}\int_{|t|&gt;\varepsilon}\prod_{j=1}^{n}|v_{j}(t)|dt\to 0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><msub><mo rspace="0em">∫</mo><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow><mo>&gt;</mo><mi>ε</mi></mrow></msub><mrow><msubsup><mo rspace="0em">∏</mo><mrow><mi>j</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>n</mi></msubsup><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><mrow><msub><mi>v</mi><mi>j</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo rspace="0em">𝑑</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{n}\int_{|t|&gt;\varepsilon}\prod_{j=1}^{n}|v_{j}(t)|dt\to 0</annotation></semantics></math><span id="A1.I3.i3.p1.1.4" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic"> as </span><math id="A1.I3.i3.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="n\to\infty" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">∞</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">n\to\infty</annotation></semantics></math><span id="A1.I3.i3.p1.1.5" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic"> where </span><math id="A1.I3.i3.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="v_{j}(t)=\EB[\exp(t{\textnormal{i}}X_{j})]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>v</mi><mi>j</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>𝔼</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><mi>exp</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mtext>i</mtext><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>X</mi><mi>j</mi></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">v_{j}(t)=\EB[\exp(t{\textnormal{i}}X_{j})]</annotation></semantics></math><span id="A1.I3.i3.p1.1.6" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic"> is the characteristic function of </span><math id="A1.I3.i3.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="X_{j}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>X</mi><mi>j</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">X_{j}</annotation></semantics></math><span id="A1.I3.i3.p1.1.7" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">.</span></p>
</div></li>
</ol>
<p id="A1.Thmlem9.p1.3" class="ltx_p"><span id="A1.Thmlem9.p1.3.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">Then, the Edgeworth expansion satisfies</span></p>
<table id="A1.Ex70" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A1.Ex70.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\sup_{x\in{\mathbb{R}}}\left|p_{Z_{n}}(x)-\left[\varphi(x)+\frac{\lambda_{3,n}}{6\sqrt{n}}(x^{3}-3x)\varphi(x)\right]\right|=o\left(\frac{1}{\sqrt{n}}\right)," display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><munder><mo movablelimits="false">sup</mo><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo>∈</mo><mi>ℝ</mi></mrow></munder><mrow><mo lspace="0em">|</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>p</mi><msub><mi>Z</mi><mi>n</mi></msub></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mo>[</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>φ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mfrac><msub><mi>λ</mi><mrow><mn>3</mn><mo>,</mo><mi>n</mi></mrow></msub><mrow><mn>6</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msqrt><mi>n</mi></msqrt></mrow></mfrac><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msup><mi>x</mi><mn>3</mn></msup><mo>−</mo><mrow><mn>3</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>x</mi></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>φ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>]</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>|</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>o</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mfrac><mn>1</mn><msqrt><mi>n</mi></msqrt></mfrac><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\sup_{x\in{\mathbb{R}}}\left|p_{Z_{n}}(x)-\left[\varphi(x)+\frac{\lambda_{3,n}}{6\sqrt{n}}(x^{3}-3x)\varphi(x)\right]\right|=o\left(\frac{1}{\sqrt{n}}\right),</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A1.Thmlem9.p1.4" class="ltx_p"><span id="A1.Thmlem9.p1.4.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">where <math id="A1.Thmlem9.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\varphi(x)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>φ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\varphi(x)</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="A1.Thmlem9.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="p_{Z_{n}}(x)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>p</mi><msub><mi>Z</mi><mi>n</mi></msub></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">p_{Z_{n}}(x)</annotation></semantics></math> are the PDFs of the standard normal distribution <math id="A1.Thmlem9.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="{\mathcal{N}}(0,1)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒩</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>1</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\mathcal{N}}(0,1)</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="A1.Thmlem9.p1.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="Z_{n}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>Z</mi><mi>n</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">Z_{n}</annotation></semantics></math>, respectively.</span></p>
</div>
</div>
<div id="A1.SS5.2.1" class="ltx_proof">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_font_italic ltx_title_proof">Proof of Lemma <a href="#A1.Thmlem9" title="Lemma A.9 (Classical Edgeworth expansion). ‣ Proof of Lemma . ‣ A.5 Proof of Lemma ‣ Appendix A Proof for the General Framework ‣ Optimal Detection for Language Watermarks with Pseudorandom Collision" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">A.9</span></a>.</h6>
<div id="A1.SS5.p2" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A1.SS5.p2.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A1.SS5.p2.1.1" class="ltx_text">The result follows directly from Theorem 7 in Chapter VI, §4 of <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_cite">[<a href="#bib.bib40" title="" class="ltx_ref">40</a>]</cite>. Its proof, which we omit, relies on the analysis of the class of random variables denoted by <math id="A1.SS5.p2.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="S(3,1,1)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>S</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>3</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>1</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">S(3,1,1)</annotation></semantics></math>, as defined in the same reference.
∎</span></p>
</div>
</div>
<div id="A1.SS5.p3" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A1.SS5.p3.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A1.SS5.p3.1.1" class="ltx_text">To apply Lemma <a href="#A1.Thmlem9" title="Lemma A.9 (Classical Edgeworth expansion). ‣ Proof of Lemma . ‣ A.5 Proof of Lemma ‣ Appendix A Proof for the General Framework ‣ Optimal Detection for Language Watermarks with Pseudorandom Collision" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">A.9</span></a>, we define the mean-zero, independent variables <math id="A1.SS5.p3.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\{\widetilde{X}_{{\mathcal{V}}}\}_{{\mathcal{V}}\in\Pi}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>X</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒱</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒱</mi><mo>∈</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">Π</mi></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\{\widetilde{X}_{{\mathcal{V}}}\}_{{\mathcal{V}}\in\Pi}</annotation></semantics></math> by centering the tilted variables:</span></p>
<table id="A1.Ex71" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A1.Ex71.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\widetilde{X}_{{\mathcal{V}}}=\bar{X}_{{\mathcal{V}}}-\EB_{1}[\bar{X}_{{\mathcal{V}}}]=\bar{X}_{{\mathcal{V}}}-m_{{\mathcal{V}}}(\theta)" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>X</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒱</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mrow><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>X</mi><mo>¯</mo></mover><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒱</mi></msub><mo>−</mo><mrow><msub><mi>𝔼</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>X</mi><mo>¯</mo></mover><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒱</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>X</mi><mo>¯</mo></mover><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒱</mi></msub><mo>−</mo><mrow><msub><mi>m</mi><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒱</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>θ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\widetilde{X}_{{\mathcal{V}}}=\bar{X}_{{\mathcal{V}}}-\EB_{1}[\bar{X}_{{\mathcal{V}}}]=\bar{X}_{{\mathcal{V}}}-m_{{\mathcal{V}}}(\theta)</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A1.SS5.p3.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="A1.SS5.p3.2.1" class="ltx_text">where <math id="A1.SS5.p3.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="m_{{\mathcal{V}}}(\theta)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>m</mi><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒱</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>θ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">m_{{\mathcal{V}}}(\theta)</annotation></semantics></math> is defined in (<a href="#A1.E43" title="In Step 1: Define tilted random variables. ‣ A.3 Proof of Lemma ‣ Appendix A Proof for the General Framework ‣ Optimal Detection for Language Watermarks with Pseudorandom Collision" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">43</span></a>). These variables remain independent because they preserve the dependence structure of the original variables <math id="A1.SS5.p3.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\{X_{{\mathcal{V}}}\}_{{\mathcal{V}}\in\Pi}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><msub><mi>X</mi><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒱</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒱</mi><mo>∈</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">Π</mi></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\{X_{{\mathcal{V}}}\}_{{\mathcal{V}}\in\Pi}</annotation></semantics></math>. The required regularity conditions for applying the Edgeworth expansion are ensured by Assumption <a href="#A1.Thmasmp1" title="Assumption A.1 (Regularity conditions for lower bound tightness). ‣ A.2 Asymptotic Tightness ‣ Appendix A Proof for the General Framework ‣ Optimal Detection for Language Watermarks with Pseudorandom Collision" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">A.1</span></a>, as we now formalize.</span></p>
</div>
<div id="A1.Thmfact1" class="ltx_theorem ltx_theorem_fact">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_title_theorem"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_theorem"><span id="A1.Thmfact1.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Fact A.1</span></span><span id="A1.Thmfact1.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold"> </span>(Facts about centered tilted distributions)<span id="A1.Thmfact1.4" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">.</span></h6>
<div id="A1.Thmfact1.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A1.Thmfact1.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A1.Thmfact1.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">Let <math id="A1.Thmfact1.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="[\underline{M},\overline{M}]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><munder accentunder="true"><mi>M</mi><mo stretchy="true">¯</mo></munder><mo>,</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>M</mi><mo stretchy="true">¯</mo></mover><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">[\underline{M},\overline{M}]</annotation></semantics></math> be the interval defined in Lemma <a href="#A1.Thmlem8" title="Lemma A.8 (Stability of roots for mixture equations). ‣ Step 4: Putting the pieces together. ‣ A.3 Proof of Lemma ‣ Appendix A Proof for the General Framework ‣ Optimal Detection for Language Watermarks with Pseudorandom Collision" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">A.8</span></a> and fix any <math id="A1.Thmfact1.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\theta\in[\underline{M},\overline{M}]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>θ</mi><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><munder accentunder="true"><mi>M</mi><mo stretchy="true">¯</mo></munder><mo>,</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>M</mi><mo stretchy="true">¯</mo></mover></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\theta\in[\underline{M},\overline{M}]</annotation></semantics></math>. Under Assumption <a href="#A1.Thmasmp1" title="Assumption A.1 (Regularity conditions for lower bound tightness). ‣ A.2 Asymptotic Tightness ‣ Appendix A Proof for the General Framework ‣ Optimal Detection for Language Watermarks with Pseudorandom Collision" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">A.1</span></a>, the centered tilted variables <math id="A1.Thmfact1.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\widetilde{X}_{{\mathcal{V}}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>X</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒱</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\widetilde{X}_{{\mathcal{V}}}</annotation></semantics></math> satisfy:</span></p>
<ol id="A1.I4" class="ltx_enumerate">
<li id="A1.I4.i1" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">1.</span> 
<div id="A1.I4.i1.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A1.I4.i1.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A1.I4.i1.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold ltx_font_italic">Uniformly bounded moments:</span><span id="A1.I4.i1.p1.1.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic"> There exists a constant </span><math id="A1.I4.i1.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="C_{\max}&gt;0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>C</mi><mi>max</mi></msub><mo>&gt;</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">C_{\max}&gt;0</annotation></semantics></math><span id="A1.I4.i1.p1.1.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic"> such that for all </span><math id="A1.I4.i1.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="{\mathcal{V}}\in\Pi" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒱</mi><mo>∈</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">Π</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\mathcal{V}}\in\Pi</annotation></semantics></math><span id="A1.I4.i1.p1.1.4" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic"> and all </span><math id="A1.I4.i1.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\theta\in[\underline{M},\overline{M}]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>θ</mi><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><munder accentunder="true"><mi>M</mi><mo stretchy="true">¯</mo></munder><mo>,</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>M</mi><mo stretchy="true">¯</mo></mover></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\theta\in[\underline{M},\overline{M}]</annotation></semantics></math><span id="A1.I4.i1.p1.1.5" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">,</span></p>
<table id="A1.Ex72" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A1.Ex72.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\EB_{1}[\widetilde{X}_{{\mathcal{V}}}^{4}]\leq C_{\max}." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>𝔼</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><msubsup><mover accent="true"><mi>X</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒱</mi><mn>4</mn></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>≤</mo><msub><mi>C</mi><mi>max</mi></msub></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\EB_{1}[\widetilde{X}_{{\mathcal{V}}}^{4}]\leq C_{\max}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A1.I4.i1.p1.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="A1.I4.i1.p1.2.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">In particular, this also implies uniform bounds on third moments, that is, </span><math id="A1.I4.i1.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\EB[|\widetilde{X}_{{\mathcal{V}}}|^{3}]\leq C^{\prime}_{\max}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>𝔼</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>X</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒱</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow><mn>3</mn></msup><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>≤</mo><msubsup><mi>C</mi><mi>max</mi><mo>′</mo></msubsup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\EB[|\widetilde{X}_{{\mathcal{V}}}|^{3}]\leq C^{\prime}_{\max}</annotation></semantics></math><span id="A1.I4.i1.p1.2.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">.</span></p>
</div></li>
<li id="A1.I4.i2" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">2.</span> 
<div id="A1.I4.i2.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A1.I4.i2.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A1.I4.i2.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold ltx_font_italic">(Uniform Non-degeneracy of Variance)</span><span id="A1.I4.i2.p1.1.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic"> </span><span id="A1.I4.i2.p1.1.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold ltx_font_italic">Uniformly bounded variance away from zero:</span><span id="A1.I4.i2.p1.1.4" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic"> There exists a constant </span><math id="A1.I4.i2.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\sigma_{\min}^{2}&gt;0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msubsup><mi>σ</mi><mi>min</mi><mn>2</mn></msubsup><mo>&gt;</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\sigma_{\min}^{2}&gt;0</annotation></semantics></math><span id="A1.I4.i2.p1.1.5" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic"> such that for all </span><math id="A1.I4.i2.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="{\mathcal{V}}\in\Pi" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒱</mi><mo>∈</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">Π</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\mathcal{V}}\in\Pi</annotation></semantics></math><span id="A1.I4.i2.p1.1.6" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic"> and all </span><math id="A1.I4.i2.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\theta\in[\underline{M},\overline{M}]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>θ</mi><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><munder accentunder="true"><mi>M</mi><mo stretchy="true">¯</mo></munder><mo>,</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>M</mi><mo stretchy="true">¯</mo></mover></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\theta\in[\underline{M},\overline{M}]</annotation></semantics></math><span id="A1.I4.i2.p1.1.7" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">,</span></p>
<table id="A1.Ex73" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A1.Ex73.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathrm{Var}(\bar{X}_{\mathcal{V}})=\EB[(\widetilde{X}_{\mathcal{V}})^{2}]=\sigma_{{\mathcal{V}}}^{2}(\theta)\geq\sigma^{2}_{\min}." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>Var</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>X</mi><mo>¯</mo></mover><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒱</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>𝔼</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>X</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒱</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>σ</mi><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒱</mi><mn>2</mn></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>θ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>≥</mo><msubsup><mi>σ</mi><mi>min</mi><mn>2</mn></msubsup></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathrm{Var}(\bar{X}_{\mathcal{V}})=\EB[(\widetilde{X}_{\mathcal{V}})^{2}]=\sigma_{{\mathcal{V}}}^{2}(\theta)\geq\sigma^{2}_{\min}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div></li>
</ol>
</div>
</div>
<div id="A1.SS5.p4" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A1.SS5.p4.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A1.SS5.p4.1.1" class="ltx_text">We now verify the conditions in Lemma <a href="#A1.Thmlem9" title="Lemma A.9 (Classical Edgeworth expansion). ‣ Proof of Lemma . ‣ A.5 Proof of Lemma ‣ Appendix A Proof for the General Framework ‣ Optimal Detection for Language Watermarks with Pseudorandom Collision" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">A.9</span></a> using the above properties:</span></p>
</div>
<div id="A1.SS5.p5" class="ltx_para">
<ul id="A1.I5" class="ltx_itemize">
<li id="A1.I5.i1" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">•</span> 
<div id="A1.I5.i1.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A1.I5.i1.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A1.I5.i1.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Condition (i):</span> The term</p>
<table id="A1.Ex74" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A1.Ex74.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\frac{1}{N_{n}}\sum_{{\mathcal{V}}\in\Pi}\EB[|\widetilde{X}_{{\mathcal{V}}}|^{3}]\leq C^{\prime}_{\max}&lt;\infty," display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mfrac><mn>1</mn><msub><mi>N</mi><mi>n</mi></msub></mfrac><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><munder><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒱</mi><mo>∈</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">Π</mi></mrow></munder><mrow><mi>𝔼</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>X</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒱</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow><mn>3</mn></msup><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>≤</mo><msubsup><mi>C</mi><mi>max</mi><mo>′</mo></msubsup><mo>&lt;</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">∞</mi></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\frac{1}{N_{n}}\sum_{{\mathcal{V}}\in\Pi}\EB[|\widetilde{X}_{{\mathcal{V}}}|^{3}]\leq C^{\prime}_{\max}&lt;\infty,</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A1.I5.i1.p1.2" class="ltx_p">is uniformly bounded. Moreover,</p>
<table id="A1.Ex75" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A1.Ex75.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\frac{1}{N_{n}}\sum_{{\mathcal{V}}\in\Pi}\EB[|\widetilde{X}_{{\mathcal{V}}}|^{2}]=\frac{1}{N_{n}}\sum_{{\mathcal{V}}\in\Pi}\sigma_{{\mathcal{V}}}^{2}(\theta)\geq\sigma_{\min}^{2}&gt;0." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mfrac><mn>1</mn><msub><mi>N</mi><mi>n</mi></msub></mfrac><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><munder><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒱</mi><mo>∈</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">Π</mi></mrow></munder><mrow><mi>𝔼</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>X</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒱</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mfrac><mn>1</mn><msub><mi>N</mi><mi>n</mi></msub></mfrac><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><munder><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒱</mi><mo>∈</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">Π</mi></mrow></munder><mrow><msubsup><mi>σ</mi><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒱</mi><mn>2</mn></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>θ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>≥</mo><msubsup><mi>σ</mi><mi>min</mi><mn>2</mn></msubsup><mo>&gt;</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\frac{1}{N_{n}}\sum_{{\mathcal{V}}\in\Pi}\EB[|\widetilde{X}_{{\mathcal{V}}}|^{2}]=\frac{1}{N_{n}}\sum_{{\mathcal{V}}\in\Pi}\sigma_{{\mathcal{V}}}^{2}(\theta)\geq\sigma_{\min}^{2}&gt;0.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div></li>
<li id="A1.I5.i2" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">•</span> 
<div id="A1.I5.i2.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A1.I5.i2.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A1.I5.i2.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Condition (ii):</span> Since we have uniform bounds on the fourth moments, for any <math id="A1.I5.i2.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\tau&lt;1/2" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>τ</mi><mo>&lt;</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>/</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\tau&lt;1/2</annotation></semantics></math>, when <math id="A1.I5.i2.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="n\to\infty" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">∞</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">n\to\infty</annotation></semantics></math>, we have</p>
<table id="A1.EGx35" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A1.E56"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.E56.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\frac{1}{N_{n}}\sum_{{\mathcal{V}}\in\Pi}\EB[|\widetilde{X}_{{\mathcal{V}}}|^{3}\mathbf{1}_{|\widetilde{X}_{{\mathcal{V}}}|&gt;N_{n}^{\tau}}]\leq\frac{1}{N_{n}^{1+\tau}}\sum_{{\mathcal{V}}\in\Pi}\EB[|\widetilde{X}_{{\mathcal{V}}}|^{4}\mathbf{1}_{|\widetilde{X}_{{\mathcal{V}}}|&gt;N_{n}^{\tau}}]\leq\frac{C_{\max}}{N_{n}^{\tau}}\to 0." display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mn>1</mn><msub><mi>N</mi><mi>n</mi></msub></mfrac></mstyle><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munder><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒱</mi><mo>∈</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">Π</mi></mrow></munder></mstyle><mrow><mi>𝔼</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>X</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒱</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow><mn>3</mn></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mn>𝟏</mn><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>X</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒱</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow><mo>&gt;</mo><msubsup><mi>N</mi><mi>n</mi><mi>τ</mi></msubsup></mrow></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>≤</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mn>1</mn><msubsup><mi>N</mi><mi>n</mi><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>+</mo><mi>τ</mi></mrow></msubsup></mfrac></mstyle><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munder><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒱</mi><mo>∈</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">Π</mi></mrow></munder></mstyle><mrow><mi>𝔼</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>X</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒱</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow><mn>4</mn></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mn>𝟏</mn><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>X</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒱</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow><mo>&gt;</mo><msubsup><mi>N</mi><mi>n</mi><mi>τ</mi></msubsup></mrow></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>≤</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><msub><mi>C</mi><mi>max</mi></msub><msubsup><mi>N</mi><mi>n</mi><mi>τ</mi></msubsup></mfrac></mstyle><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\frac{1}{N_{n}}\sum_{{\mathcal{V}}\in\Pi}\EB[|\widetilde{X}_{{\mathcal{V}}}|^{3}\mathbf{1}_{|\widetilde{X}_{{\mathcal{V}}}|&gt;N_{n}^{\tau}}]\leq\frac{1}{N_{n}^{1+\tau}}\sum_{{\mathcal{V}}\in\Pi}\EB[|\widetilde{X}_{{\mathcal{V}}}|^{4}\mathbf{1}_{|\widetilde{X}_{{\mathcal{V}}}|&gt;N_{n}^{\tau}}]\leq\frac{C_{\max}}{N_{n}^{\tau}}\to 0.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(56)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div></li>
<li id="A1.I5.i3" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">•</span> 
<div id="A1.I5.i3.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A1.I5.i3.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A1.I5.i3.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Condition (iii):</span> Cramér’s condition is satisfied as a consequence of the results presented in <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_cite">[<a href="#bib.bib40" title="" class="ltx_ref">40</a>]</cite> (Chapter VI, §4, Lemma 10 and the subsequent discussion), combined with our assumptions on score density regularity in Assumption <a href="#A1.Thmasmp1" title="Assumption A.1 (Regularity conditions for lower bound tightness). ‣ A.2 Asymptotic Tightness ‣ Appendix A Proof for the General Framework ‣ Optimal Detection for Language Watermarks with Pseudorandom Collision" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">A.1</span></a>.</p>
</div></li>
</ul>
<p id="A1.SS5.p5.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A1.SS5.p5.1.1" class="ltx_text">Therefore, all conditions in Lemma <a href="#A1.Thmlem9" title="Lemma A.9 (Classical Edgeworth expansion). ‣ Proof of Lemma . ‣ A.5 Proof of Lemma ‣ Appendix A Proof for the General Framework ‣ Optimal Detection for Language Watermarks with Pseudorandom Collision" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">A.9</span></a> are satisfied for the centered tilted variables <math id="A1.SS5.p5.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\{\widetilde{X}_{{\mathcal{V}}}\}_{{\mathcal{V}}\in\Pi}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>X</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒱</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒱</mi><mo>∈</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">Π</mi></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\{\widetilde{X}_{{\mathcal{V}}}\}_{{\mathcal{V}}\in\Pi}</annotation></semantics></math>. Applying the lemma yields</span></p>
<table id="A1.EGx36" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A1.E57"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.E57.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\frac{{\mathrm{d}}\bar{H}_{n}(x)}{{\mathrm{d}}x}=\varphi(x)+\frac{\lambda_{3,N_{n}}}{6\sqrt{N_{n}}}(x^{3}-3x)\varphi(x)+R_{N_{n}}(x)," display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>H</mi><mo>¯</mo></mover><mi>n</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>x</mi></mrow></mfrac></mstyle><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>φ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><msub><mi>λ</mi><mrow><mn>3</mn><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>N</mi><mi>n</mi></msub></mrow></msub><mrow><mn>6</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msqrt><msub><mi>N</mi><mi>n</mi></msub></msqrt></mrow></mfrac></mstyle><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msup><mi>x</mi><mn>3</mn></msup><mo>−</mo><mrow><mn>3</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>x</mi></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>φ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><msub><mi>R</mi><msub><mi>N</mi><mi>n</mi></msub></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\frac{{\mathrm{d}}\bar{H}_{n}(x)}{{\mathrm{d}}x}=\varphi(x)+\frac{\lambda_{3,N_{n}}}{6\sqrt{N_{n}}}(x^{3}-3x)\varphi(x)+R_{N_{n}}(x),</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(57)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A1.SS5.p5.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="A1.SS5.p5.2.1" class="ltx_text">where the remainder satisfies</span></p>
<table id="A1.EGx37" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A1.E58"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.E58.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\sup_{x\in{\mathbb{R}}}|R_{N_{n}}(x)|=o\left(\frac{1}{{\sqrt{N_{n}}}}\right)," display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><munder><mo movablelimits="false">sup</mo><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo>∈</mo><mi>ℝ</mi></mrow></munder><mrow><mo lspace="0em" stretchy="false">|</mo><mrow><msub><mi>R</mi><msub><mi>N</mi><mi>n</mi></msub></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>o</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mn>1</mn><msqrt><msub><mi>N</mi><mi>n</mi></msub></msqrt></mfrac></mstyle><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\sup_{x\in{\mathbb{R}}}|R_{N_{n}}(x)|=o\left(\frac{1}{{\sqrt{N_{n}}}}\right),</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(58)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A1.SS5.p5.3" class="ltx_p"><span id="A1.SS5.p5.3.1" class="ltx_text">concluding the proof.
∎</span></p>
</div>
</div>
</section>
<section id="A1.SS6" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection">A.6 </span>Proof of Lemma <a href="#A1.Thmlem7" title="Lemma A.7. ‣ Step 3: Decompose the tail integral via Edgeworth expansion. ‣ A.3 Proof of Lemma ‣ Appendix A Proof for the General Framework ‣ Optimal Detection for Language Watermarks with Pseudorandom Collision" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">A.7</span></a></h3>

<div id="A1.SS6.2" class="ltx_proof">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_font_italic ltx_title_proof">Proof of Lemma <a href="#A1.Thmlem7" title="Lemma A.7. ‣ Step 3: Decompose the tail integral via Edgeworth expansion. ‣ A.3 Proof of Lemma ‣ Appendix A Proof for the General Framework ‣ Optimal Detection for Language Watermarks with Pseudorandom Collision" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">A.7</span></a>.</h6>
<div id="A1.SS6.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A1.SS6.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A1.SS6.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text">We begin by defining the integral of interest:</span></p>
<table id="A1.EGx38" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A1.Ex76"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.Ex76.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle I:=\int_{0}^{\infty}{\mathrm{e}}^{-\theta\sqrt{N_{n}\sigma^{2}(\theta)}t}{\mathrm{d}}\bar{H}_{n}(t)." display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>I</mi><mo>:=</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><msubsup><mo>∫</mo><mn>0</mn><mi mathvariant="normal">∞</mi></msubsup></mstyle><mrow><msup><mi>e</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>θ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msqrt><mrow><msub><mi>N</mi><mi>n</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>σ</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>θ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></msqrt><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>d</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>H</mi><mo>¯</mo></mover><mi>n</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle I:=\int_{0}^{\infty}{\mathrm{e}}^{-\theta\sqrt{N_{n}\sigma^{2}(\theta)}t}{\mathrm{d}}\bar{H}_{n}(t).</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A1.SS6.p1.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="A1.SS6.p1.2.1" class="ltx_text">Applying the Edgeworth expansion from Lemma <a href="#A1.Thmlem6" title="Lemma A.6. ‣ Step 3: Decompose the tail integral via Edgeworth expansion. ‣ A.3 Proof of Lemma ‣ Appendix A Proof for the General Framework ‣ Optimal Detection for Language Watermarks with Pseudorandom Collision" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">A.6</span></a>, we have</span></p>
<table id="A1.Ex77" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A1.Ex77.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\frac{{\mathrm{d}}\bar{H}_{n}(t)}{{\mathrm{d}}t}=\varphi(t)+\frac{\lambda_{3,N_{n}}}{6\sqrt{N_{n}}}(t^{3}-3t)\varphi(t)+R_{N_{n}}(t)," display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mfrac><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>H</mi><mo>¯</mo></mover><mi>n</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow></mfrac><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>φ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mfrac><msub><mi>λ</mi><mrow><mn>3</mn><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>N</mi><mi>n</mi></msub></mrow></msub><mrow><mn>6</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msqrt><msub><mi>N</mi><mi>n</mi></msub></msqrt></mrow></mfrac><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msup><mi>t</mi><mn>3</mn></msup><mo>−</mo><mrow><mn>3</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>φ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><msub><mi>R</mi><msub><mi>N</mi><mi>n</mi></msub></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\frac{{\mathrm{d}}\bar{H}_{n}(t)}{{\mathrm{d}}t}=\varphi(t)+\frac{\lambda_{3,N_{n}}}{6\sqrt{N_{n}}}(t^{3}-3t)\varphi(t)+R_{N_{n}}(t),</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A1.SS6.p1.3" class="ltx_p"><span id="A1.SS6.p1.3.1" class="ltx_text">where <math id="A1.SS6.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\varphi(x)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>φ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\varphi(x)</annotation></semantics></math> is the PDF of the standard normal distribution.</span></p>
</div>
<div id="A1.SS6.p2" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A1.SS6.p2.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A1.SS6.p2.1.1" class="ltx_text">Substituting this expansion into the expression for <math id="A1.SS6.p2.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="I" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>I</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">I</annotation></semantics></math>, we obtain</span></p>
<table id="A1.EGx39" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A1.E59"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.E59.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle I" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>I</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle I</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.E59.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=\int_{0}^{\infty}{\mathrm{e}}^{-\theta\sqrt{N_{n}\sigma^{2}(\theta)}t}\varphi(t){\mathrm{d}}t+\frac{\lambda_{3,N_{n}}}{6\sqrt{N_{n}}}\int_{0}^{\infty}{\mathrm{e}}^{-\theta\sqrt{N_{n}\sigma^{2}(\theta)}t}(t^{3}-3t)\varphi(t){\mathrm{d}}t" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><msubsup><mo>∫</mo><mn>0</mn><mi mathvariant="normal">∞</mi></msubsup></mstyle><mrow><msup><mi>e</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>θ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msqrt><mrow><msub><mi>N</mi><mi>n</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>σ</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>θ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></msqrt><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>φ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo rspace="0em">𝑑</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><msub><mi>λ</mi><mrow><mn>3</mn><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>N</mi><mi>n</mi></msub></mrow></msub><mrow><mn>6</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msqrt><msub><mi>N</mi><mi>n</mi></msub></msqrt></mrow></mfrac></mstyle><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><msubsup><mo>∫</mo><mn>0</mn><mi mathvariant="normal">∞</mi></msubsup></mstyle><mrow><msup><mi>e</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>θ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msqrt><mrow><msub><mi>N</mi><mi>n</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>σ</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>θ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></msqrt><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msup><mi>t</mi><mn>3</mn></msup><mo>−</mo><mrow><mn>3</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>φ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo rspace="0em">𝑑</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=\int_{0}^{\infty}{\mathrm{e}}^{-\theta\sqrt{N_{n}\sigma^{2}(\theta)}t}\varphi(t){\mathrm{d}}t+\frac{\lambda_{3,N_{n}}}{6\sqrt{N_{n}}}\int_{0}^{\infty}{\mathrm{e}}^{-\theta\sqrt{N_{n}\sigma^{2}(\theta)}t}(t^{3}-3t)\varphi(t){\mathrm{d}}t</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(59)</span></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A1.E60"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.E60.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\displaystyle+\int_{0}^{\infty}{\mathrm{e}}^{-\theta\sqrt{N_{n}\sigma^{2}(\theta)}t}R_{N_{n}}(t){\mathrm{d}}t." display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo>+</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><msubsup><mo>∫</mo><mn>0</mn><mi mathvariant="normal">∞</mi></msubsup></mstyle><msup><mi>e</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>θ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msqrt><mrow><msub><mi>N</mi><mi>n</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>σ</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>θ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></msqrt><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow></mrow></msup><msub><mi>R</mi><msub><mi>N</mi><mi>n</mi></msub></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mi>d</mi><mi>t</mi><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle+\int_{0}^{\infty}{\mathrm{e}}^{-\theta\sqrt{N_{n}\sigma^{2}(\theta)}t}R_{N_{n}}(t){\mathrm{d}}t.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(60)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
<div id="A1.SS6.p3" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A1.SS6.p3.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A1.SS6.p3.1.1" class="ltx_text">We now analyze each term on the right-hand side:</span></p>
<ul id="A1.I6" class="ltx_itemize">
<li id="A1.I6.i1" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">•</span> 
<div id="A1.I6.i1.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A1.I6.i1.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A1.I6.i1.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">First term:</span> We compute the integral as follows:</p>
<table id="A1.EGx40" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A1.E61"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.E61.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\int_{0}^{\infty}{\mathrm{e}}^{-\theta\sqrt{N_{n}\sigma^{2}(\theta)}t}\varphi(t){\mathrm{d}}t" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><msubsup><mo>∫</mo><mn>0</mn><mi mathvariant="normal">∞</mi></msubsup></mstyle><mrow><msup><mi>e</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>θ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msqrt><mrow><msub><mi>N</mi><mi>n</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>σ</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>θ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></msqrt><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>φ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo rspace="0em">𝑑</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\int_{0}^{\infty}{\mathrm{e}}^{-\theta\sqrt{N_{n}\sigma^{2}(\theta)}t}\varphi(t){\mathrm{d}}t</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.E61.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=\int_{0}^{\infty}\frac{1}{\sqrt{2\pi}}e^{-\frac{1}{2}\left(t^{2}+2\theta\sqrt{N_{n}\sigma^{2}(\theta)}t\right)}{\mathrm{d}}t" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><msubsup><mo>∫</mo><mn>0</mn><mi mathvariant="normal">∞</mi></msubsup></mstyle><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mn>1</mn><msqrt><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>π</mi></mrow></msqrt></mfrac></mstyle><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>e</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mn>2</mn></mfrac><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><msup><mi>t</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>+</mo><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>θ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msqrt><mrow><msub><mi>N</mi><mi>n</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>σ</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>θ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></msqrt><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo rspace="0em">𝑑</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=\int_{0}^{\infty}\frac{1}{\sqrt{2\pi}}e^{-\frac{1}{2}\left(t^{2}+2\theta\sqrt{N_{n}\sigma^{2}(\theta)}t\right)}{\mathrm{d}}t</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(61)</span></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A1.E62"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.E62.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=\int_{0}^{\infty}\frac{1}{\sqrt{2\pi}}{\mathrm{e}}^{-\frac{1}{2}\left(t+\theta\sqrt{N_{n}\sigma^{2}(\theta)}\right)^{2}+\frac{\theta^{2}N_{n}\sigma^{2}(\theta)}{2}}{\mathrm{d}}t" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><msubsup><mo>∫</mo><mn>0</mn><mi mathvariant="normal">∞</mi></msubsup></mstyle><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mn>1</mn><msqrt><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>π</mi></mrow></msqrt></mfrac></mstyle><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>e</mi><mrow><mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mn>2</mn></mfrac><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>+</mo><mrow><mi>θ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msqrt><mrow><msub><mi>N</mi><mi>n</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>σ</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>θ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></msqrt></mrow></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mfrac><mrow><msup><mi>θ</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>N</mi><mi>n</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>σ</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>θ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mn>2</mn></mfrac></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo rspace="0em">𝑑</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=\int_{0}^{\infty}\frac{1}{\sqrt{2\pi}}{\mathrm{e}}^{-\frac{1}{2}\left(t+\theta\sqrt{N_{n}\sigma^{2}(\theta)}\right)^{2}+\frac{\theta^{2}N_{n}\sigma^{2}(\theta)}{2}}{\mathrm{d}}t</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(62)</span></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A1.E63"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.E63.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle={\mathrm{e}}^{\frac{\theta^{2}N_{n}\sigma^{2}(\theta)}{2}}\int_{\theta\sqrt{N_{n}\sigma^{2}(\theta)}}^{\infty}\frac{1}{\sqrt{2\pi}}{\mathrm{e}}^{-\frac{u^{2}}{2}}{\mathrm{d}}u" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><msup><mi>e</mi><mfrac><mrow><msup><mi>θ</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>N</mi><mi>n</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>σ</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>θ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mn>2</mn></mfrac></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><msubsup><mo>∫</mo><mrow><mi>θ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msqrt><mrow><msub><mi>N</mi><mi>n</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>σ</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>θ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></msqrt></mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">∞</mi></msubsup></mstyle><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mn>1</mn><msqrt><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>π</mi></mrow></msqrt></mfrac></mstyle><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>e</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mfrac><msup><mi>u</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mn>2</mn></mfrac></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo rspace="0em">𝑑</mo><mi>u</mi></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle={\mathrm{e}}^{\frac{\theta^{2}N_{n}\sigma^{2}(\theta)}{2}}\int_{\theta\sqrt{N_{n}\sigma^{2}(\theta)}}^{\infty}\frac{1}{\sqrt{2\pi}}{\mathrm{e}}^{-\frac{u^{2}}{2}}{\mathrm{d}}u</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(63)</span></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A1.E64"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.E64.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=\frac{1}{\sqrt{2\pi}}\cdot\frac{1-\Phi(\theta\sqrt{N_{n}\sigma^{2}(\theta)})}{\varphi(\theta\sqrt{N_{n}\sigma^{2}(\theta)})}." display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mn>1</mn><msqrt><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>π</mi></mrow></msqrt></mfrac></mstyle><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Φ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>θ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msqrt><mrow><msub><mi>N</mi><mi>n</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>σ</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>θ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></msqrt></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mrow><mi>φ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>θ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msqrt><mrow><msub><mi>N</mi><mi>n</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>σ</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>θ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></msqrt></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mfrac></mstyle></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=\frac{1}{\sqrt{2\pi}}\cdot\frac{1-\Phi(\theta\sqrt{N_{n}\sigma^{2}(\theta)})}{\varphi(\theta\sqrt{N_{n}\sigma^{2}(\theta)})}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(64)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
<div id="A1.Thmlem10" class="ltx_theorem ltx_theorem_lem">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_title_theorem"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_theorem"><span id="A1.Thmlem10.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Lemma A.10</span></span><span id="A1.Thmlem10.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold"> </span>(Mill’s ratio <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_cite">[<a href="#bib.bib13" title="" class="ltx_ref">13</a>]</cite>)<span id="A1.Thmlem10.4" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">.</span></h6>
<div id="A1.Thmlem10.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A1.Thmlem10.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A1.Thmlem10.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">Let <math id="A1.Thmlem10.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\Phi(x)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Φ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Phi(x)</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="A1.Thmlem10.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\varphi(x)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>φ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\varphi(x)</annotation></semantics></math> denote the CDF and PDF of the standard normal distribution <math id="A1.Thmlem10.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="{\mathcal{N}}(0,1)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒩</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>1</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\mathcal{N}}(0,1)</annotation></semantics></math>, respectively. Then for all <math id="A1.Thmlem10.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="x&gt;0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo>&gt;</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">x&gt;0</annotation></semantics></math>, it holds that</span></p>
<table id="A1.Ex78" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A1.Ex78.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\frac{x}{1+x^{2}}&lt;\frac{1-\Phi(x)}{\varphi(x)}&lt;\frac{1}{x}." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mfrac><mi>x</mi><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>+</mo><msup><mi>x</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow></mfrac><mo>&lt;</mo><mfrac><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Φ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mrow><mi>φ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mfrac><mo>&lt;</mo><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mi>x</mi></mfrac></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\frac{x}{1+x^{2}}&lt;\frac{1-\Phi(x)}{\varphi(x)}&lt;\frac{1}{x}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
</div>
<div id="A1.I6.i1.p2" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A1.I6.i1.p2.1" class="ltx_p">Using the classical Mill’s ratio bound in Lemma <a href="#A1.Thmlem10" title="Lemma A.10 (Mill’s ratio []). ‣ 1st item ‣ Proof of Lemma . ‣ A.6 Proof of Lemma ‣ Appendix A Proof for the General Framework ‣ Optimal Detection for Language Watermarks with Pseudorandom Collision" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">A.10</span></a>, we obtain</p>
<table id="A1.Ex79" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A1.Ex79.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\int_{0}^{\infty}{\mathrm{e}}^{-\theta\sqrt{N_{n}\sigma^{2}(\theta)}t}\varphi(t){\mathrm{d}}t=\Theta\left(\frac{1}{\theta\sqrt{N_{n}\sigma^{2}(\theta)}}\right)=\Theta\left(\frac{1}{\sqrt{N_{n}}}\right)." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><msubsup><mo>∫</mo><mn>0</mn><mi mathvariant="normal">∞</mi></msubsup><mrow><msup><mi>e</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>θ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msqrt><mrow><msub><mi>N</mi><mi>n</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>σ</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>θ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></msqrt><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>φ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo rspace="0em">𝑑</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Θ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mrow><mi>θ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msqrt><mrow><msub><mi>N</mi><mi>n</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>σ</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>θ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></msqrt></mrow></mfrac><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Θ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mfrac><mn>1</mn><msqrt><msub><mi>N</mi><mi>n</mi></msub></msqrt></mfrac><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\int_{0}^{\infty}{\mathrm{e}}^{-\theta\sqrt{N_{n}\sigma^{2}(\theta)}t}\varphi(t){\mathrm{d}}t=\Theta\left(\frac{1}{\theta\sqrt{N_{n}\sigma^{2}(\theta)}}\right)=\Theta\left(\frac{1}{\sqrt{N_{n}}}\right).</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div></li>
<li id="A1.I6.i2" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">•</span> 
<div id="A1.I6.i2.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A1.I6.i2.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A1.I6.i2.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Second term:</span> Since <math id="A1.I6.i2.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\lambda_{3,N_{n}}\leq C" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>λ</mi><mrow><mn>3</mn><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>N</mi><mi>n</mi></msub></mrow></msub><mo>≤</mo><mi>C</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\lambda_{3,N_{n}}\leq C</annotation></semantics></math> by assumption, we can bound this term as</p>
<table id="A1.EGx41" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A1.E65"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.E65.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\left|\frac{\lambda_{3,N_{n}}}{6\sqrt{2\pi N_{n}}}\int_{0}^{\infty}{\mathrm{e}}^{-\theta\sqrt{N_{n}\sigma^{2}(\theta)}t}(t^{3}-3t){\mathrm{e}}^{-\frac{t^{2}}{2}}{\mathrm{d}}t\right|" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo>|</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><msub><mi>λ</mi><mrow><mn>3</mn><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>N</mi><mi>n</mi></msub></mrow></msub><mrow><mn>6</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msqrt><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>π</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>N</mi><mi>n</mi></msub></mrow></msqrt></mrow></mfrac></mstyle><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><msubsup><mo>∫</mo><mn>0</mn><mi mathvariant="normal">∞</mi></msubsup></mstyle><mrow><msup><mi>e</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>θ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msqrt><mrow><msub><mi>N</mi><mi>n</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>σ</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>θ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></msqrt><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msup><mi>t</mi><mn>3</mn></msup><mo>−</mo><mrow><mn>3</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>e</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mfrac><msup><mi>t</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mn>2</mn></mfrac></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo rspace="0em">𝑑</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>|</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\left|\frac{\lambda_{3,N_{n}}}{6\sqrt{2\pi N_{n}}}\int_{0}^{\infty}{\mathrm{e}}^{-\theta\sqrt{N_{n}\sigma^{2}(\theta)}t}(t^{3}-3t){\mathrm{e}}^{-\frac{t^{2}}{2}}{\mathrm{d}}t\right|</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.E65.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\leq\frac{C}{\sqrt{N_{n}}}\int_{0}^{\infty}{\mathrm{e}}^{-\theta\sqrt{N_{n}\sigma^{2}(\theta)}t}(t^{3}+3t){\mathrm{e}}^{-\frac{t^{2}}{2}}{\mathrm{d}}t" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>≤</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mi>C</mi><msqrt><msub><mi>N</mi><mi>n</mi></msub></msqrt></mfrac></mstyle><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><msubsup><mo>∫</mo><mn>0</mn><mi mathvariant="normal">∞</mi></msubsup></mstyle><mrow><msup><mi>e</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>θ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msqrt><mrow><msub><mi>N</mi><mi>n</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>σ</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>θ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></msqrt><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msup><mi>t</mi><mn>3</mn></msup><mo>+</mo><mrow><mn>3</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>e</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mfrac><msup><mi>t</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mn>2</mn></mfrac></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo rspace="0em">𝑑</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\leq\frac{C}{\sqrt{N_{n}}}\int_{0}^{\infty}{\mathrm{e}}^{-\theta\sqrt{N_{n}\sigma^{2}(\theta)}t}(t^{3}+3t){\mathrm{e}}^{-\frac{t^{2}}{2}}{\mathrm{d}}t</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(65)</span></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A1.E66"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.E66.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\leq\frac{C}{\sqrt{N_{n}}}\left[O\left(\frac{1}{N_{n}^{2}}\right)+O\left(\frac{1}{N_{n}}\right)\right]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>≤</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mi>C</mi><msqrt><msub><mi>N</mi><mi>n</mi></msub></msqrt></mfrac></mstyle><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>[</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>O</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mn>1</mn><msubsup><mi>N</mi><mi>n</mi><mn>2</mn></msubsup></mfrac></mstyle><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mi>O</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mn>1</mn><msub><mi>N</mi><mi>n</mi></msub></mfrac></mstyle><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>]</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\leq\frac{C}{\sqrt{N_{n}}}\left[O\left(\frac{1}{N_{n}^{2}}\right)+O\left(\frac{1}{N_{n}}\right)\right]</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(66)</span></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A1.E67"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.E67.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=O\left(\frac{1}{N_{n}^{3/2}}\right)." display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>O</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mn>1</mn><msubsup><mi>N</mi><mi>n</mi><mrow><mn>3</mn><mo>/</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></msubsup></mfrac></mstyle><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=O\left(\frac{1}{N_{n}^{3/2}}\right).</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(67)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div></li>
<li id="A1.I6.i3" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">•</span> 
<div id="A1.I6.i3.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A1.I6.i3.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A1.I6.i3.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Third term:</span> Using the bound <math id="A1.I6.i3.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\sup_{x\in{\mathbb{R}}}|R_{N_{n}}(x)|=o(1/{\sqrt{N_{n}}})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mo>sup</mo><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo>∈</mo><mi>ℝ</mi></mrow></msub><mrow><mo lspace="0em" stretchy="false">|</mo><mrow><msub><mi>R</mi><msub><mi>N</mi><mi>n</mi></msub></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>o</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>/</mo><msqrt><msub><mi>N</mi><mi>n</mi></msub></msqrt></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\sup_{x\in{\mathbb{R}}}|R_{N_{n}}(x)|=o(1/{\sqrt{N_{n}}})</annotation></semantics></math> from Lemma <a href="#A1.Thmlem6" title="Lemma A.6. ‣ Step 3: Decompose the tail integral via Edgeworth expansion. ‣ A.3 Proof of Lemma ‣ Appendix A Proof for the General Framework ‣ Optimal Detection for Language Watermarks with Pseudorandom Collision" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">A.6</span></a>, we have</p>
<table id="A1.EGx42" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A1.E68"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.E68.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\int_{0}^{\infty}{\mathrm{e}}^{-\theta\sqrt{N_{n}\sigma^{2}(\theta)}t}R_{N_{n}}(t){\mathrm{d}}t=o\left(\frac{1}{{N_{n}}}\right)." display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><msubsup><mo>∫</mo><mn>0</mn><mi mathvariant="normal">∞</mi></msubsup></mstyle><mrow><msup><mi>e</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>θ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msqrt><mrow><msub><mi>N</mi><mi>n</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>σ</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>θ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></msqrt><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>R</mi><msub><mi>N</mi><mi>n</mi></msub></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo rspace="0em">𝑑</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>o</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mn>1</mn><msub><mi>N</mi><mi>n</mi></msub></mfrac></mstyle><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\int_{0}^{\infty}{\mathrm{e}}^{-\theta\sqrt{N_{n}\sigma^{2}(\theta)}t}R_{N_{n}}(t){\mathrm{d}}t=o\left(\frac{1}{{N_{n}}}\right).</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(68)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div></li>
</ul>
</div>
<div id="A1.SS6.p4" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A1.SS6.p4.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A1.SS6.p4.1.1" class="ltx_text">Putting all terms together, we conclude that</span></p>
<table id="A1.EGx43" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A1.E69"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.E69.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle I" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>I</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle I</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.E69.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=\Theta\left(\frac{1}{\sqrt{N_{n}}}\right)+O\left(\frac{1}{N_{n}^{3/2}}\right)+o\left(\frac{1}{{N_{n}}}\right)=\Theta\left(\frac{1}{\sqrt{N_{n}}}\right)." display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Θ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mn>1</mn><msqrt><msub><mi>N</mi><mi>n</mi></msub></msqrt></mfrac></mstyle><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mi>O</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mn>1</mn><msubsup><mi>N</mi><mi>n</mi><mrow><mn>3</mn><mo>/</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></msubsup></mfrac></mstyle><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mi>o</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mn>1</mn><msub><mi>N</mi><mi>n</mi></msub></mfrac></mstyle><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Θ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mn>1</mn><msqrt><msub><mi>N</mi><mi>n</mi></msub></msqrt></mfrac></mstyle><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=\Theta\left(\frac{1}{\sqrt{N_{n}}}\right)+O\left(\frac{1}{N_{n}^{3/2}}\right)+o\left(\frac{1}{{N_{n}}}\right)=\Theta\left(\frac{1}{\sqrt{N_{n}}}\right).</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(69)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
<div id="A1.SS6.p5" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A1.SS6.p5.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A1.SS6.p5.1.1" class="ltx_text">∎</span></p>
</div>
</div>
</section>
<section id="A1.SS7" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection">A.7 </span>Proof of Lemma <a href="#A1.Thmlem8" title="Lemma A.8 (Stability of roots for mixture equations). ‣ Step 4: Putting the pieces together. ‣ A.3 Proof of Lemma ‣ Appendix A Proof for the General Framework ‣ Optimal Detection for Language Watermarks with Pseudorandom Collision" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">A.8</span></a></h3>

<div id="A1.SS7.2" class="ltx_proof">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_font_italic ltx_title_proof">Proof of Lemma <a href="#A1.Thmlem8" title="Lemma A.8 (Stability of roots for mixture equations). ‣ Step 4: Putting the pieces together. ‣ A.3 Proof of Lemma ‣ Appendix A Proof for the General Framework ‣ Optimal Detection for Language Watermarks with Pseudorandom Collision" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">A.8</span></a>.</h6>
<div id="A1.SS7.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A1.SS7.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A1.SS7.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text">Recall that the empirical mean and variance functions are defined by</span></p>
<table id="A1.Ex80" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A1.Ex80.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="m(\theta):=\frac{1}{N_{n}}\sum_{{\mathcal{V}}\in\Pi}m_{{\mathcal{V}}}(\theta),\qquad\sigma^{2}(\theta):=\frac{1}{N_{n}}\sum_{{\mathcal{V}}\in\Pi}\sigma^{2}_{{\mathcal{V}}}(\theta)." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>m</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>θ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>:=</mo><mrow><mfrac><mn>1</mn><msub><mi>N</mi><mi>n</mi></msub></mfrac><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><munder><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒱</mi><mo>∈</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">Π</mi></mrow></munder><mrow><msub><mi>m</mi><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒱</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>θ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="2.167em">,</mo><mrow><mrow><msup><mi>σ</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>θ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>:=</mo><mrow><mfrac><mn>1</mn><msub><mi>N</mi><mi>n</mi></msub></mfrac><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><munder><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒱</mi><mo>∈</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">Π</mi></mrow></munder><mrow><msubsup><mi>σ</mi><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒱</mi><mn>2</mn></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>θ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">m(\theta):=\frac{1}{N_{n}}\sum_{{\mathcal{V}}\in\Pi}m_{{\mathcal{V}}}(\theta),\qquad\sigma^{2}(\theta):=\frac{1}{N_{n}}\sum_{{\mathcal{V}}\in\Pi}\sigma^{2}_{{\mathcal{V}}}(\theta).</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A1.SS7.p1.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="A1.SS7.p1.2.1" class="ltx_text">We claim that there exists a unique non-negative solution to the equation <math id="A1.SS7.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="m(\theta)=-\frac{\gamma_{n,\alpha}}{N_{n}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>m</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>θ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo>−</mo><mfrac><msub><mi>γ</mi><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>α</mi></mrow></msub><msub><mi>N</mi><mi>n</mi></msub></mfrac></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">m(\theta)=-\frac{\gamma_{n,\alpha}}{N_{n}}</annotation></semantics></math>. This follows from the following facts:</span></p>
<ul id="A1.I7" class="ltx_itemize">
<li id="A1.I7.i1" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">•</span> 
<div id="A1.I7.i1.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A1.I7.i1.p1.1" class="ltx_p">The function <math id="A1.I7.i1.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="m" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>m</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">m</annotation></semantics></math> is strictly increasing for sufficiently large <math id="A1.I7.i1.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="N_{n}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>N</mi><mi>n</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">N_{n}</annotation></semantics></math>, since <math id="A1.I7.i1.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="m^{\prime}=\sigma^{2}&gt;0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msup><mi>m</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo>=</mo><msup><mi>σ</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>&gt;</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">m^{\prime}=\sigma^{2}&gt;0</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>
</div></li>
<li id="A1.I7.i2" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">•</span> 
<div id="A1.I7.i2.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A1.I7.i2.p1.1" class="ltx_p">We have <math id="A1.I7.i2.p1.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="m(0)=-\frac{1}{N_{n}}\sum_{{\mathcal{V}}\in\Pi}\cdot\EB_{1,\bm{Q}_{i,{\mathcal{V}}}}[h_{{\mathcal{V}}}]&lt;-\frac{1}{N_{n}}\sum_{{\mathcal{V}}\in\Pi}\EB_{0}[h_{{\mathcal{V}}}]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>m</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>0</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo rspace="0em">=</mo><mo lspace="0em">−</mo><mfrac><mn>1</mn><msub><mi>N</mi><mi>n</mi></msub></mfrac><msub><mo rspace="0em">∑</mo><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒱</mi><mo>∈</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">Π</mi></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><msub><mi>𝔼</mi><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>𝐐</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>,</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒱</mi></mrow></msub></mrow></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><msub><mi>h</mi><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒱</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow><mo rspace="0em">&lt;</mo><mo lspace="0em">−</mo><mfrac><mn>1</mn><msub><mi>N</mi><mi>n</mi></msub></mfrac><msub><mo>∑</mo><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒱</mi><mo>∈</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">Π</mi></mrow></msub><msub><mi>𝔼</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><msub><mi>h</mi><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒱</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">m(0)=-\frac{1}{N_{n}}\sum_{{\mathcal{V}}\in\Pi}\cdot\EB_{1,\bm{Q}_{i,{\mathcal{V}}}}[h_{{\mathcal{V}}}]&lt;-\frac{1}{N_{n}}\sum_{{\mathcal{V}}\in\Pi}\EB_{0}[h_{{\mathcal{V}}}]</annotation></semantics></math> due to informativeness.</p>
</div></li>
<li id="A1.I7.i3" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">•</span> 
<div id="A1.I7.i3.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A1.I7.i3.p1.1" class="ltx_p">Lemma <a href="#A1.Thmlem11" title="Lemma A.11 (Asymptotic behavior of the tilted mean). ‣ 3rd item ‣ Proof of Lemma . ‣ A.7 Proof of Lemma ‣ Appendix A Proof for the General Framework ‣ Optimal Detection for Language Watermarks with Pseudorandom Collision" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">A.11</span></a> implies that</p>
<table id="A1.Ex81" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A1.Ex81.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\lim_{\theta\to\infty}m(\theta)=\frac{1}{N_{n}}\sum_{{\mathcal{V}}\in\Pi}\mathrm{esssup}(-h_{{\mathcal{V}}})=-\frac{1}{N_{n}}\sum_{{\mathcal{V}}\in\Pi}\mathrm{essinf}(h_{{\mathcal{V}}})&gt;-\frac{1}{N_{n}}\sum_{{\mathcal{V}}\in\Pi}\EB_{0}[h_{{\mathcal{V}}}]." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><munder><mo movablelimits="false">lim</mo><mrow><mi>θ</mi><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">∞</mi></mrow></munder><mi>m</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>θ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mn>1</mn><msub><mi>N</mi><mi>n</mi></msub></mfrac><munder><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒱</mi><mo>∈</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">Π</mi></mrow></munder><mi>esssup</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mo lspace="0em">−</mo><msub><mi>h</mi><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒱</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo rspace="0em">=</mo><mo lspace="0em">−</mo><mfrac><mn>1</mn><msub><mi>N</mi><mi>n</mi></msub></mfrac><munder><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒱</mi><mo>∈</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">Π</mi></mrow></munder><mi>essinf</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>h</mi><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒱</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo rspace="0em">&gt;</mo><mo lspace="0em">−</mo><mfrac><mn>1</mn><msub><mi>N</mi><mi>n</mi></msub></mfrac><munder><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒱</mi><mo>∈</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">Π</mi></mrow></munder><msub><mi>𝔼</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><msub><mi>h</mi><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒱</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\lim_{\theta\to\infty}m(\theta)=\frac{1}{N_{n}}\sum_{{\mathcal{V}}\in\Pi}\mathrm{esssup}(-h_{{\mathcal{V}}})=-\frac{1}{N_{n}}\sum_{{\mathcal{V}}\in\Pi}\mathrm{essinf}(h_{{\mathcal{V}}})&gt;-\frac{1}{N_{n}}\sum_{{\mathcal{V}}\in\Pi}\EB_{0}[h_{{\mathcal{V}}}].</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
<div id="A1.Thmlem11" class="ltx_theorem ltx_theorem_lem">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_title_theorem"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_theorem"><span id="A1.Thmlem11.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Lemma A.11</span></span><span id="A1.Thmlem11.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold"> </span>(Asymptotic behavior of the tilted mean)<span id="A1.Thmlem11.4" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">.</span></h6>
<div id="A1.Thmlem11.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A1.Thmlem11.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A1.Thmlem11.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">Let <math id="A1.Thmlem11.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="X" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>X</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">X</annotation></semantics></math> be a real-valued random variable with CDF <math id="A1.Thmlem11.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="F" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>F</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">F</annotation></semantics></math>, and define its MGF by <math id="A1.Thmlem11.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\phi(\theta):=\EB[{\mathrm{e}}^{\theta X}]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>ϕ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>θ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>:=</mo><mrow><mi>𝔼</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><msup><mi mathvariant="normal">e</mi><mrow><mi>θ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">X</mi></mrow></msup><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\phi(\theta):=\EB[{\mathrm{e}}^{\theta X}]</annotation></semantics></math>. Assume that <math id="A1.Thmlem11.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\phi_{\tau}(\theta)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>ϕ</mi><mi>τ</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>θ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\phi_{\tau}(\theta)</annotation></semantics></math> is finite for all <math id="A1.Thmlem11.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\theta\in[0,\infty)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>θ</mi><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">∞</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\theta\in[0,\infty)</annotation></semantics></math>.
Let <math id="A1.Thmlem11.p1.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="m(\theta):=\frac{{\mathrm{d}}}{{\mathrm{d}}\theta}\log\phi(\theta)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>m</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>θ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>:=</mo><mrow><mfrac><mi mathvariant="normal">d</mi><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">d</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>θ</mi></mrow></mfrac><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><mi>ϕ</mi></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>θ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">m(\theta):=\frac{{\mathrm{d}}}{{\mathrm{d}}\theta}\log\phi(\theta)</annotation></semantics></math> denote the mean of the exponentially tilted distribution. Then,</span></p>
<table id="A1.EGx44" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_gather ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A1.Ex82"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A1.Ex82.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\lim_{\theta\to\infty}m(\theta)=\mathrm{esssup}(X):=\inf\{x\in{\mathbb{R}}:{\mathbb{P}}(X\leq x)=1\}." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><munder><mo movablelimits="false">lim</mo><mrow><mi>θ</mi><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">∞</mi></mrow></munder><mrow><mi>m</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>θ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>esssup</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>X</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.1389em">:=</mo><mrow><mo lspace="0.1389em" movablelimits="false" rspace="0em">inf</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo>∈</mo><mi>ℝ</mi></mrow><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>ℙ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>X</mi><mo>≤</mo><mi>x</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\lim_{\theta\to\infty}m(\theta)=\mathrm{esssup}(X):=\inf\{x\in{\mathbb{R}}:{\mathbb{P}}(X\leq x)=1\}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
</div>
<div id="A1.I7.i3.p2" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A1.I7.i3.p2.1" class="ltx_p">We defer the proof of this lemma at the end of this section.</p>
</div></li>
<li id="A1.I7.i4" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">•</span> 
<div id="A1.I7.i4.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A1.I7.i4.p1.1" class="ltx_p">When <math id="A1.I7.i4.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="N_{n}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>N</mi><mi>n</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">N_{n}</annotation></semantics></math> is sufficiently large, Lemma <a href="#A1.Thmlem1" title="Lemma A.1. ‣ Proof of Theorem . ‣ A.1 Proof of Theorem ‣ Appendix A Proof for the General Framework ‣ Optimal Detection for Language Watermarks with Pseudorandom Collision" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">A.1</span></a> implies that <math id="A1.I7.i4.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\frac{\gamma_{n,\alpha}}{N_{n}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mfrac><msub><mi>γ</mi><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>α</mi></mrow></msub><msub><mi>N</mi><mi>n</mi></msub></mfrac><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\frac{\gamma_{n,\alpha}}{N_{n}}</annotation></semantics></math> concentrates to <math id="A1.I7.i4.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\frac{1}{N_{n}}\sum_{{\mathcal{V}}\in\Pi}\EB_{0}[h_{{\mathcal{V}}}]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mfrac><mn>1</mn><msub><mi>N</mi><mi>n</mi></msub></mfrac><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><msub><mo>∑</mo><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒱</mi><mo>∈</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">Π</mi></mrow></msub><mrow><msub><mi>𝔼</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><msub><mi>h</mi><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒱</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\frac{1}{N_{n}}\sum_{{\mathcal{V}}\in\Pi}\EB_{0}[h_{{\mathcal{V}}}]</annotation></semantics></math>, so that <math id="A1.I7.i4.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="-\frac{\gamma_{n,\alpha}}{N_{n}}\in[m(0),\lim\limits_{\theta\to\infty}m(\theta))" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mo>−</mo><mfrac><msub><mi>γ</mi><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>α</mi></mrow></msub><msub><mi>N</mi><mi>n</mi></msub></mfrac></mrow><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><mi>m</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>0</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo><mrow><munder><mo lspace="0em" movablelimits="false" rspace="0.167em">lim</mo><mrow><mi>θ</mi><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">∞</mi></mrow></munder><mrow><mi>m</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>θ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">-\frac{\gamma_{n,\alpha}}{N_{n}}\in[m(0),\lim\limits_{\theta\to\infty}m(\theta))</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>
</div></li>
</ul>
</div>
<div id="A1.SS7.p2" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A1.SS7.p2.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A1.SS7.p2.1.1" class="ltx_text">We denote by <math id="A1.SS7.p2.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\theta^{\star}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi>θ</mi><mo>⋆</mo></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\theta^{\star}</annotation></semantics></math> the unique solution to the equation <math id="A1.SS7.p2.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="m(\theta)=-\frac{\gamma_{n,\alpha}}{N_{n}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>m</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>θ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo>−</mo><mfrac><msub><mi>γ</mi><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>α</mi></mrow></msub><msub><mi>N</mi><mi>n</mi></msub></mfrac></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">m(\theta)=-\frac{\gamma_{n,\alpha}}{N_{n}}</annotation></semantics></math>.
By Lemma <a href="#A1.Thmlem2" title="Lemma A.2. ‣ Proof of Theorem . ‣ A.1 Proof of Theorem ‣ Appendix A Proof for the General Framework ‣ Optimal Detection for Language Watermarks with Pseudorandom Collision" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">A.2</span></a>, we already know that <math id="A1.SS7.p2.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\theta^{\star}\leq\overline{M}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msup><mi>θ</mi><mo>⋆</mo></msup><mo>≤</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>M</mi><mo stretchy="true">¯</mo></mover></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\theta^{\star}\leq\overline{M}</annotation></semantics></math>.
It therefore suffices to establish a lower bound <math id="A1.SS7.p2.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\underline{M}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><munder accentunder="true"><mi>M</mi><mo stretchy="true">¯</mo></munder><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\underline{M}</annotation></semantics></math> such that <math id="A1.SS7.p2.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\theta^{\star}\geq\underline{M}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msup><mi>θ</mi><mo>⋆</mo></msup><mo>≥</mo><munder accentunder="true"><mi>M</mi><mo stretchy="true">¯</mo></munder></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\theta^{\star}\geq\underline{M}</annotation></semantics></math>.</span></p>
</div>
<div id="A1.SS7.p3" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A1.SS7.p3.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A1.SS7.p3.1.1" class="ltx_text">Fix the interval <math id="A1.SS7.p3.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="K:=[0,\overline{M}]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>K</mi><mo>:=</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>M</mi><mo stretchy="true">¯</mo></mover></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">K:=[0,\overline{M}]</annotation></semantics></math>.
By the CGF regularity in Assumption <a href="#A1.Thmasmp1" title="Assumption A.1 (Regularity conditions for lower bound tightness). ‣ A.2 Asymptotic Tightness ‣ Appendix A Proof for the General Framework ‣ Optimal Detection for Language Watermarks with Pseudorandom Collision" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">A.1</span></a>, for any <math id="A1.SS7.p3.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\theta\in K" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>θ</mi><mo>∈</mo><mi>K</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\theta\in K</annotation></semantics></math> we have</span></p>
<table id="A1.Ex83" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A1.Ex83.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="0&lt;\sigma^{2}_{\min}(K)\;\leq\;m^{\prime}(\theta)\;\leq\;C_{2}(K)." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mn>0</mn><mo>&lt;</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>σ</mi><mi>min</mi><mn>2</mn></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>K</mi><mo rspace="0.280em" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.558em">≤</mo><mrow><msup><mi>m</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>θ</mi><mo rspace="0.280em" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.558em">≤</mo><mrow><msub><mi>C</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>K</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">0&lt;\sigma^{2}_{\min}(K)\;\leq\;m^{\prime}(\theta)\;\leq\;C_{2}(K).</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A1.SS7.p3.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="A1.SS7.p3.2.1" class="ltx_text">Consequently,</span></p>
<table id="A1.Ex84" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A1.Ex84.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="m(0)+\sigma^{2}_{\min}(K)\cdot\theta^{\star}\;\leq\;m(\theta^{\star})=-\frac{\gamma_{n,\alpha}}{N_{n}}\;\leq\;m(0)+C_{2}(K)\cdot\theta^{\star}." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>m</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>0</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mrow><msubsup><mi>σ</mi><mi>min</mi><mn>2</mn></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>K</mi><mo rspace="0.055em" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><msup><mi>θ</mi><mo>⋆</mo></msup></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.558em">≤</mo><mrow><mi>m</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>θ</mi><mo>⋆</mo></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo>−</mo><mfrac><msub><mi>γ</mi><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>α</mi></mrow></msub><msub><mi>N</mi><mi>n</mi></msub></mfrac></mrow><mo lspace="0.558em" rspace="0.558em">≤</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>m</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>0</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>C</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>K</mi><mo rspace="0.055em" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><msup><mi>θ</mi><mo>⋆</mo></msup></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">m(0)+\sigma^{2}_{\min}(K)\cdot\theta^{\star}\;\leq\;m(\theta^{\star})=-\frac{\gamma_{n,\alpha}}{N_{n}}\;\leq\;m(0)+C_{2}(K)\cdot\theta^{\star}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A1.SS7.p3.3" class="ltx_p"><span id="A1.SS7.p3.3.1" class="ltx_text">By Lemma <a href="#A1.Thmlem1" title="Lemma A.1. ‣ Proof of Theorem . ‣ A.1 Proof of Theorem ‣ Appendix A Proof for the General Framework ‣ Optimal Detection for Language Watermarks with Pseudorandom Collision" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">A.1</span></a>, when <math id="A1.SS7.p3.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="N_{n}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>N</mi><mi>n</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">N_{n}</annotation></semantics></math> is sufficiently large, <math id="A1.SS7.p3.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\frac{\gamma_{n,\alpha}}{N_{n}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mfrac><msub><mi>γ</mi><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>α</mi></mrow></msub><msub><mi>N</mi><mi>n</mi></msub></mfrac><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\frac{\gamma_{n,\alpha}}{N_{n}}</annotation></semantics></math> concentrates around <math id="A1.SS7.p3.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\frac{1}{N_{n}}\sum_{{\mathcal{V}}\in\Pi}\EB_{1,{\mathcal{Q}}_{1,{\mathcal{V}}}}[h_{{\mathcal{V}}}]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mfrac><mn>1</mn><msub><mi>N</mi><mi>n</mi></msub></mfrac><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><msub><mo>∑</mo><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒱</mi><mo>∈</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">Π</mi></mrow></msub><mrow><msub><mi>𝔼</mi><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>,</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒬</mi><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>,</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒱</mi></mrow></msub></mrow></msub><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><msub><mi>h</mi><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒱</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\frac{1}{N_{n}}\sum_{{\mathcal{V}}\in\Pi}\EB_{1,{\mathcal{Q}}_{1,{\mathcal{V}}}}[h_{{\mathcal{V}}}]</annotation></semantics></math>.
Hence, for large <math id="A1.SS7.p3.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="N_{n}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>N</mi><mi>n</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">N_{n}</annotation></semantics></math>, it follows that</span></p>
<table id="A1.Ex85" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A1.Ex85.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\frac{\frac{1}{N_{n}}\sum_{{\mathcal{V}}\in\Pi}\bigl(\EB_{1,{\mathcal{Q}}_{1,{\mathcal{V}}}}[h_{{\mathcal{V}}}]-\EB_{0}[h_{{\mathcal{V}}}]\bigr)}{C_{2}(K)}\;\leq\;\theta^{\star}\;\leq\;\frac{\frac{1}{N_{n}}\sum_{{\mathcal{V}}\in\Pi}\bigl(\EB_{1,{\mathcal{Q}}_{1,{\mathcal{V}}}}[h_{{\mathcal{V}}}]-\EB_{0}[h_{{\mathcal{V}}}]\bigr)}{\sigma^{2}_{\min}(K)}." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mfrac><mrow><mfrac><mn>1</mn><msub><mi>N</mi><mi>n</mi></msub></mfrac><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><msub><mo rspace="0em">∑</mo><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒱</mi><mo>∈</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">Π</mi></mrow></msub><mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">(</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>𝔼</mi><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>,</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒬</mi><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>,</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒱</mi></mrow></msub></mrow></msub><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><msub><mi>h</mi><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒱</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><msub><mi>𝔼</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><msub><mi>h</mi><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒱</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mrow><msub><mi>C</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>K</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mfrac><mo lspace="0.558em" rspace="0.558em">≤</mo><msup><mi>θ</mi><mo>⋆</mo></msup><mo rspace="0.558em">≤</mo><mfrac><mrow><mfrac><mn>1</mn><msub><mi>N</mi><mi>n</mi></msub></mfrac><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><msub><mo rspace="0em">∑</mo><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒱</mi><mo>∈</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">Π</mi></mrow></msub><mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">(</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>𝔼</mi><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>,</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒬</mi><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>,</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒱</mi></mrow></msub></mrow></msub><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><msub><mi>h</mi><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒱</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><msub><mi>𝔼</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><msub><mi>h</mi><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒱</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mrow><msubsup><mi>σ</mi><mi>min</mi><mn>2</mn></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>K</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mfrac></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\frac{\frac{1}{N_{n}}\sum_{{\mathcal{V}}\in\Pi}\bigl(\EB_{1,{\mathcal{Q}}_{1,{\mathcal{V}}}}[h_{{\mathcal{V}}}]-\EB_{0}[h_{{\mathcal{V}}}]\bigr)}{C_{2}(K)}\;\leq\;\theta^{\star}\;\leq\;\frac{\frac{1}{N_{n}}\sum_{{\mathcal{V}}\in\Pi}\bigl(\EB_{1,{\mathcal{Q}}_{1,{\mathcal{V}}}}[h_{{\mathcal{V}}}]-\EB_{0}[h_{{\mathcal{V}}}]\bigr)}{\sigma^{2}_{\min}(K)}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A1.SS7.p3.4" class="ltx_p"><span id="A1.SS7.p3.4.1" class="ltx_text">We complete the proof by setting</span></p>
<table id="A1.Ex86" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A1.Ex86.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\underline{M}\;=\;\frac{1}{C_{2}([0,\overline{M}])}\inf_{{\mathcal{V}}\in\Pi}\;\inf_{\bm{P}_{{\mathcal{V}}}\subseteq{\mathcal{P}}_{{\mathcal{V}}}^{\star}}\Bigl[\EB_{1,\bm{P}_{{\mathcal{V}}}}[h_{{\mathcal{V}}}]-\EB_{0}[h_{{\mathcal{V}}}]\Bigr]," display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><munder accentunder="true"><mi>M</mi><mo stretchy="true">¯</mo></munder><mo lspace="0.558em" rspace="0.558em">=</mo><mrow><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mrow><msub><mi>C</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>M</mi><mo stretchy="true">¯</mo></mover></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mfrac><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><munder><mo movablelimits="false" rspace="0.0835em">inf</mo><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒱</mi><mo>∈</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">Π</mi></mrow></munder><mrow><munder><mo lspace="0.0835em" movablelimits="false" rspace="0em">inf</mo><mrow><msub><mi>𝑷</mi><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒱</mi></msub><mo>⊆</mo><msubsup><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒫</mi><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒱</mi><mo>⋆</mo></msubsup></mrow></munder><mrow><mo maxsize="1.600em" minsize="1.600em">[</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>𝔼</mi><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>𝐏</mi><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒱</mi></msub></mrow></msub><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><msub><mi>h</mi><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒱</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><msub><mi>𝔼</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><msub><mi>h</mi><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒱</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo maxsize="1.600em" minsize="1.600em">]</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\underline{M}\;=\;\frac{1}{C_{2}([0,\overline{M}])}\inf_{{\mathcal{V}}\in\Pi}\;\inf_{\bm{P}_{{\mathcal{V}}}\subseteq{\mathcal{P}}_{{\mathcal{V}}}^{\star}}\Bigl[\EB_{1,\bm{P}_{{\mathcal{V}}}}[h_{{\mathcal{V}}}]-\EB_{0}[h_{{\mathcal{V}}}]\Bigr],</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A1.SS7.p3.5" class="ltx_p"><span id="A1.SS7.p3.5.1" class="ltx_text">which is positive by the informativeness condition in Assumption <a href="#A1.Thmasmp1" title="Assumption A.1 (Regularity conditions for lower bound tightness). ‣ A.2 Asymptotic Tightness ‣ Appendix A Proof for the General Framework ‣ Optimal Detection for Language Watermarks with Pseudorandom Collision" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">A.1</span></a>.
∎</span></p>
</div>
</div>
<div id="A1.SS7.p4" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A1.SS7.p4.1" class="ltx_p">At the end, we provide the proof of Lemma <a href="#A1.Thmlem11" title="Lemma A.11 (Asymptotic behavior of the tilted mean). ‣ 3rd item ‣ Proof of Lemma . ‣ A.7 Proof of Lemma ‣ Appendix A Proof for the General Framework ‣ Optimal Detection for Language Watermarks with Pseudorandom Collision" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">A.11</span></a> below.</p>
</div>
<div id="A1.SS7.3" class="ltx_proof">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_font_italic ltx_title_proof">Proof of Lemma <a href="#A1.Thmlem11" title="Lemma A.11 (Asymptotic behavior of the tilted mean). ‣ 3rd item ‣ Proof of Lemma . ‣ A.7 Proof of Lemma ‣ Appendix A Proof for the General Framework ‣ Optimal Detection for Language Watermarks with Pseudorandom Collision" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">A.11</span></a>.</h6>
<div id="A1.SS7.p5" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A1.SS7.p5.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A1.SS7.p5.1.1" class="ltx_text">The function <math id="A1.SS7.p5.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="m(\theta)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>m</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>θ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">m(\theta)</annotation></semantics></math> is the expected value of <math id="A1.SS7.p5.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="X" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>X</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">X</annotation></semantics></math> under the exponentially tilted probability measure:</span></p>
<table id="A1.Ex87" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A1.Ex87.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="m(\theta)=\frac{\int_{-\infty}^{\infty}x{\mathrm{e}}^{\theta x}\,{\mathrm{d}}F(x)}{\int_{-\infty}^{\infty}{\mathrm{e}}^{\theta x}\,{\mathrm{d}}F(x)}." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>m</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>θ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mrow><msubsup><mo>∫</mo><mrow><mo>−</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">∞</mi></mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">∞</mi></msubsup><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>e</mi><mrow><mi>θ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>x</mi></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo rspace="0em">𝑑</mo><mi>F</mi></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mrow><msubsup><mo>∫</mo><mrow><mo>−</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">∞</mi></mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">∞</mi></msubsup><mrow><msup><mi>e</mi><mrow><mi>θ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>x</mi></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo rspace="0em">𝑑</mo><mi>F</mi></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mfrac></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">m(\theta)=\frac{\int_{-\infty}^{\infty}x{\mathrm{e}}^{\theta x}\,{\mathrm{d}}F(x)}{\int_{-\infty}^{\infty}{\mathrm{e}}^{\theta x}\,{\mathrm{d}}F(x)}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A1.SS7.p5.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="A1.SS7.p5.2.1" class="ltx_text">Let <math id="A1.SS7.p5.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="x^{\star}:=\mathrm{esssup}(X)=\inf\{x\in\mathbb{R}:{\mathbb{P}}(X\leq x)=1\}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msup><mi>x</mi><mo>⋆</mo></msup><mo>:=</mo><mrow><mi>esssup</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>X</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.1389em">=</mo><mrow><mo lspace="0.1389em" rspace="0em">inf</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo>∈</mo><mi>ℝ</mi></mrow><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>ℙ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>X</mi><mo>≤</mo><mi>x</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">x^{\star}:=\mathrm{esssup}(X)=\inf\{x\in\mathbb{R}:{\mathbb{P}}(X\leq x)=1\}</annotation></semantics></math>. We aim to show that <math id="A1.SS7.p5.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\lim_{\theta\to\infty}(\theta)=x^{\star}." display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><msub><mo>lim</mo><mrow><mi>θ</mi><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">∞</mi></mrow></msub><mrow><mo lspace="0em" stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>θ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><msup><mi>x</mi><mo>⋆</mo></msup></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\lim_{\theta\to\infty}(\theta)=x^{\star}.</annotation></semantics></math></span></p>
</div>
</div>
<section id="A1.SS7.SSS0.Px1" class="ltx_paragraph">
<h5 class="ltx_title ltx_title_paragraph">Step 1: Upper bound.</h5>

<div id="A1.SS7.SSS0.Px1.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A1.SS7.SSS0.Px1.p1.1" class="ltx_p">For any <math id="A1.SS7.SSS0.Px1.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\varepsilon&gt;0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>ε</mi><mo>&gt;</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\varepsilon&gt;0</annotation></semantics></math>, define <math id="A1.SS7.SSS0.Px1.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="B:=x^{\star}+\varepsilon" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>B</mi><mo>:=</mo><mrow><msup><mi>x</mi><mo>⋆</mo></msup><mo>+</mo><mi>ε</mi></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">B:=x^{\star}+\varepsilon</annotation></semantics></math>. Since <math id="A1.SS7.SSS0.Px1.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="{\mathbb{P}}(X&gt;B)=0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>ℙ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>X</mi><mo>&gt;</mo><mi>B</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\mathbb{P}}(X&gt;B)=0</annotation></semantics></math>, the tilted mean satisfies</p>
<table id="A1.Ex88" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A1.Ex88.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="m(\theta)\leq\frac{\int_{-\infty}^{B}x{\mathrm{e}}^{\theta x}\,{\mathrm{d}}F(x)}{\int_{-\infty}^{B}{\mathrm{e}}^{\theta x}\,{\mathrm{d}}F(x)}\leq B." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>m</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>θ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>≤</mo><mfrac><mrow><msubsup><mo>∫</mo><mrow><mo>−</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">∞</mi></mrow><mi>B</mi></msubsup><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>e</mi><mrow><mi>θ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>x</mi></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo rspace="0em">𝑑</mo><mi>F</mi></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mrow><msubsup><mo>∫</mo><mrow><mo>−</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">∞</mi></mrow><mi>B</mi></msubsup><mrow><msup><mi>e</mi><mrow><mi>θ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>x</mi></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo rspace="0em">𝑑</mo><mi>F</mi></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mfrac><mo>≤</mo><mi>B</mi></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">m(\theta)\leq\frac{\int_{-\infty}^{B}x{\mathrm{e}}^{\theta x}\,{\mathrm{d}}F(x)}{\int_{-\infty}^{B}{\mathrm{e}}^{\theta x}\,{\mathrm{d}}F(x)}\leq B.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A1.SS7.SSS0.Px1.p1.2" class="ltx_p">Therefore, for all <math id="A1.SS7.SSS0.Px1.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\theta" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>θ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\theta</annotation></semantics></math>, <math id="A1.SS7.SSS0.Px1.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="m(\theta)\leq x^{\star}+\varepsilon" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>m</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>θ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>≤</mo><mrow><msup><mi>x</mi><mo>⋆</mo></msup><mo>+</mo><mi>ε</mi></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">m(\theta)\leq x^{\star}+\varepsilon</annotation></semantics></math>. Taking <math id="A1.SS7.SSS0.Px1.p1.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\limsup" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mo>lim sup</mo><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\limsup</annotation></semantics></math> and then letting <math id="A1.SS7.SSS0.Px1.p1.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\varepsilon\to 0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>ε</mi><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\varepsilon\to 0</annotation></semantics></math> gives</p>
<table id="A1.Ex89" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A1.Ex89.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\limsup_{\theta\to\infty}m(\theta)\leq x^{\star}." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><munder><mo movablelimits="false">lim sup</mo><mrow><mi>θ</mi><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">∞</mi></mrow></munder><mrow><mi>m</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>θ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>≤</mo><msup><mi>x</mi><mo>⋆</mo></msup></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\limsup_{\theta\to\infty}m(\theta)\leq x^{\star}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
</section>
<section id="A1.SS7.SSS0.Px2" class="ltx_paragraph">
<h5 class="ltx_title ltx_title_paragraph">Step 2: Lower bound.</h5>

<div id="A1.SS7.SSS0.Px2.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A1.SS7.SSS0.Px2.p1.1" class="ltx_p">Fix <math id="A1.SS7.SSS0.Px2.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\delta&gt;0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>δ</mi><mo>&gt;</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\delta&gt;0</annotation></semantics></math> and let <math id="A1.SS7.SSS0.Px2.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="A:=x^{\star}-\delta" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>A</mi><mo>:=</mo><mrow><msup><mi>x</mi><mo>⋆</mo></msup><mo>−</mo><mi>δ</mi></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">A:=x^{\star}-\delta</annotation></semantics></math>. By the definition of <math id="A1.SS7.SSS0.Px2.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="x^{\star}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi>x</mi><mo>⋆</mo></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">x^{\star}</annotation></semantics></math>, we have <math id="A1.SS7.SSS0.Px2.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="{\mathbb{P}}(X\geq A)&gt;0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>ℙ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>X</mi><mo>≥</mo><mi>A</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>&gt;</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\mathbb{P}}(X\geq A)&gt;0</annotation></semantics></math>. Decompose <math id="A1.SS7.SSS0.Px2.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="m(\theta)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>m</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>θ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">m(\theta)</annotation></semantics></math> as</p>
<table id="A1.Ex90" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A1.Ex90.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="m(\theta)=\frac{\int_{x&lt;A}x{\mathrm{e}}^{\theta x}\,{\mathrm{d}}F(x)+\int_{x\geq A}x{\mathrm{e}}^{\theta x}\,{\mathrm{d}}F(x)}{\int_{x&lt;A}{\mathrm{e}}^{\theta x}\,{\mathrm{d}}F(x)+\int_{x\geq A}{\mathrm{e}}^{\theta x}\,{\mathrm{d}}F(x)}." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>m</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>θ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mrow><mrow><msub><mo>∫</mo><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo>&lt;</mo><mi>A</mi></mrow></msub><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>e</mi><mrow><mi>θ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>x</mi></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo rspace="0em">𝑑</mo><mi>F</mi></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.055em">+</mo><mrow><msub><mo>∫</mo><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo>≥</mo><mi>A</mi></mrow></msub><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>e</mi><mrow><mi>θ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>x</mi></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo rspace="0em">𝑑</mo><mi>F</mi></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mrow><mrow><msub><mo>∫</mo><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo>&lt;</mo><mi>A</mi></mrow></msub><mrow><msup><mi>e</mi><mrow><mi>θ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>x</mi></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo rspace="0em">𝑑</mo><mi>F</mi></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.055em">+</mo><mrow><msub><mo>∫</mo><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo>≥</mo><mi>A</mi></mrow></msub><mrow><msup><mi>e</mi><mrow><mi>θ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>x</mi></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo rspace="0em">𝑑</mo><mi>F</mi></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow></mfrac></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">m(\theta)=\frac{\int_{x&lt;A}x{\mathrm{e}}^{\theta x}\,{\mathrm{d}}F(x)+\int_{x\geq A}x{\mathrm{e}}^{\theta x}\,{\mathrm{d}}F(x)}{\int_{x&lt;A}{\mathrm{e}}^{\theta x}\,{\mathrm{d}}F(x)+\int_{x\geq A}{\mathrm{e}}^{\theta x}\,{\mathrm{d}}F(x)}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A1.SS7.SSS0.Px2.p1.2" class="ltx_p">Rewrite both numerator and denominator by factoring out <math id="A1.SS7.SSS0.Px2.p1.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="{\mathrm{e}}^{\theta A}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi>e</mi><mrow><mi>θ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>A</mi></mrow></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\mathrm{e}}^{\theta A}</annotation></semantics></math>:</p>
<table id="A1.Ex91" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A1.Ex91.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="m(\theta)=\frac{\int_{x&lt;A}x{\mathrm{e}}^{\theta(x-A)}\,{\mathrm{d}}F(x)+\int_{x\geq A}x{\mathrm{e}}^{\theta(x-A)}\,{\mathrm{d}}F(x)}{\int_{x&lt;A}{\mathrm{e}}^{\theta(x-A)}\,{\mathrm{d}}F(x)+\int_{x\geq A}{\mathrm{e}}^{\theta(x-A)}\,{\mathrm{d}}F(x)}." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>m</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>θ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mrow><mrow><msub><mo>∫</mo><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo>&lt;</mo><mi>A</mi></mrow></msub><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>e</mi><mrow><mi>θ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo>−</mo><mi>A</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo rspace="0em">𝑑</mo><mi>F</mi></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.055em">+</mo><mrow><msub><mo>∫</mo><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo>≥</mo><mi>A</mi></mrow></msub><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>e</mi><mrow><mi>θ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo>−</mo><mi>A</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo rspace="0em">𝑑</mo><mi>F</mi></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mrow><mrow><msub><mo>∫</mo><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo>&lt;</mo><mi>A</mi></mrow></msub><mrow><msup><mi>e</mi><mrow><mi>θ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo>−</mo><mi>A</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo rspace="0em">𝑑</mo><mi>F</mi></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.055em">+</mo><mrow><msub><mo>∫</mo><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo>≥</mo><mi>A</mi></mrow></msub><mrow><msup><mi>e</mi><mrow><mi>θ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo>−</mo><mi>A</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo rspace="0em">𝑑</mo><mi>F</mi></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow></mfrac></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">m(\theta)=\frac{\int_{x&lt;A}x{\mathrm{e}}^{\theta(x-A)}\,{\mathrm{d}}F(x)+\int_{x\geq A}x{\mathrm{e}}^{\theta(x-A)}\,{\mathrm{d}}F(x)}{\int_{x&lt;A}{\mathrm{e}}^{\theta(x-A)}\,{\mathrm{d}}F(x)+\int_{x\geq A}{\mathrm{e}}^{\theta(x-A)}\,{\mathrm{d}}F(x)}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A1.SS7.SSS0.Px2.p1.3" class="ltx_p">As <math id="A1.SS7.SSS0.Px2.p1.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\theta\to\infty" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>θ</mi><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">∞</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\theta\to\infty</annotation></semantics></math>, the integrals over <math id="A1.SS7.SSS0.Px2.p1.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="x&lt;A" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo>&lt;</mo><mi>A</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">x&lt;A</annotation></semantics></math> vanish by the dominated convergence theorem, since <math id="A1.SS7.SSS0.Px2.p1.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="x-A&lt;0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo>−</mo><mi>A</mi></mrow><mo>&lt;</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">x-A&lt;0</annotation></semantics></math> in this range and the MGF is finite. Thus,</p>
<table id="A1.Ex92" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A1.Ex92.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\lim_{\theta\to\infty}m(\theta)=\lim_{\theta\to\infty}\frac{\int_{x\geq A}x{\mathrm{e}}^{\theta(x-A)}\,{\mathrm{d}}F(x)}{\int_{x\geq A}{\mathrm{e}}^{\theta(x-A)}\,{\mathrm{d}}F(x)}." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><munder><mo movablelimits="false">lim</mo><mrow><mi>θ</mi><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">∞</mi></mrow></munder><mrow><mi>m</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>θ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.1389em">=</mo><mrow><munder><mo lspace="0.1389em" movablelimits="false" rspace="0.167em">lim</mo><mrow><mi>θ</mi><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">∞</mi></mrow></munder><mfrac><mrow><msub><mo>∫</mo><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo>≥</mo><mi>A</mi></mrow></msub><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>e</mi><mrow><mi>θ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo>−</mo><mi>A</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo rspace="0em">𝑑</mo><mi>F</mi></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mrow><msub><mo>∫</mo><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo>≥</mo><mi>A</mi></mrow></msub><mrow><msup><mi>e</mi><mrow><mi>θ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo>−</mo><mi>A</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo rspace="0em">𝑑</mo><mi>F</mi></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mfrac></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\lim_{\theta\to\infty}m(\theta)=\lim_{\theta\to\infty}\frac{\int_{x\geq A}x{\mathrm{e}}^{\theta(x-A)}\,{\mathrm{d}}F(x)}{\int_{x\geq A}{\mathrm{e}}^{\theta(x-A)}\,{\mathrm{d}}F(x)}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A1.SS7.SSS0.Px2.p1.4" class="ltx_p">Since <math id="A1.SS7.SSS0.Px2.p1.m10" class="ltx_Math" alttext="x\geq A" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo>≥</mo><mi>A</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">x\geq A</annotation></semantics></math> on the support of both integrals, we have the pointwise bound</p>
<table id="A1.Ex93" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A1.Ex93.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\frac{\int_{x\geq A}x{\mathrm{e}}^{\theta(x-A)}\,{\mathrm{d}}F(x)}{\int_{x\geq A}{\mathrm{e}}^{\theta(x-A)}\,{\mathrm{d}}F(x)}\geq A=x^{\star}-\delta." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mfrac><mrow><msub><mo>∫</mo><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo>≥</mo><mi>A</mi></mrow></msub><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>e</mi><mrow><mi>θ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo>−</mo><mi>A</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo rspace="0em">𝑑</mo><mi>F</mi></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mrow><msub><mo>∫</mo><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo>≥</mo><mi>A</mi></mrow></msub><mrow><msup><mi>e</mi><mrow><mi>θ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo>−</mo><mi>A</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo rspace="0em">𝑑</mo><mi>F</mi></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mfrac><mo>≥</mo><mi>A</mi><mo>=</mo><mrow><msup><mi>x</mi><mo>⋆</mo></msup><mo>−</mo><mi>δ</mi></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\frac{\int_{x\geq A}x{\mathrm{e}}^{\theta(x-A)}\,{\mathrm{d}}F(x)}{\int_{x\geq A}{\mathrm{e}}^{\theta(x-A)}\,{\mathrm{d}}F(x)}\geq A=x^{\star}-\delta.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A1.SS7.SSS0.Px2.p1.5" class="ltx_p">Therefore, <math id="A1.SS7.SSS0.Px2.p1.m11" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\liminf_{\theta\to\infty}m(\theta)\geq x^{\star}-\delta" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mo>lim inf</mo><mrow><mi>θ</mi><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">∞</mi></mrow></msub><mrow><mi>m</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>θ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>≥</mo><mrow><msup><mi>x</mi><mo>⋆</mo></msup><mo>−</mo><mi>δ</mi></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\liminf_{\theta\to\infty}m(\theta)\geq x^{\star}-\delta</annotation></semantics></math>. Since <math id="A1.SS7.SSS0.Px2.p1.m12" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\delta&gt;0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>δ</mi><mo>&gt;</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\delta&gt;0</annotation></semantics></math> is arbitrary, we conclude</p>
<table id="A1.Ex94" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A1.Ex94.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\liminf_{\theta\to\infty}m(\theta)\geq x^{\star}." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><munder><mo movablelimits="false">lim inf</mo><mrow><mi>θ</mi><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">∞</mi></mrow></munder><mrow><mi>m</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>θ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>≥</mo><msup><mi>x</mi><mo>⋆</mo></msup></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\liminf_{\theta\to\infty}m(\theta)\geq x^{\star}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A1.SS7.SSS0.Px2.p1.6" class="ltx_p">Combining both steps, we have <math id="A1.SS7.SSS0.Px2.p1.m13" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\liminf_{\theta\to\infty}m(\theta)\geq x^{\star}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mo>lim inf</mo><mrow><mi>θ</mi><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">∞</mi></mrow></msub><mrow><mi>m</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>θ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>≥</mo><msup><mi>x</mi><mo>⋆</mo></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\liminf_{\theta\to\infty}m(\theta)\geq x^{\star}</annotation></semantics></math> and complete the proof.
∎</p>
</div>
</section>
</section>
<section id="A1.SS8" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection">A.8 </span>Verification of Regularity Conditions for Considered Watermarks</h3>

<div id="A1.SS8.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A1.SS8.p1.1" class="ltx_p">In this section, we show that the required conditions are satisfied for the established optimal detection rules of the two watermarking schemes under study. The independence structure in Assumption <a href="#S3.Thmasmp3" title="Assumption 3.3. ‣ 3.3 Detection Efficiency and Optimal Scores ‣ 3 A Statistical Framework under Pseudorandomness Collision ‣ Optimal Detection for Language Watermarks with Pseudorandom Collision" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">3.3</span></a> is already justified by the sensitivity of hash functions and therefore does not require further verification. We thus focus on the remaining conditions.</p>
</div>
<section id="A1.SS8.SSS1" class="ltx_subsubsection">
<h4 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsubsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsubsection">A.8.1 </span>Inverse Transform Watermark</h4>

<div id="A1.SS8.SSS1.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A1.SS8.SSS1.p1.1" class="ltx_p">We begin with the inverse transform watermark, as its verification is more straightforward.
First, Assumption <a href="#S5.Thmasmp1" title="Assumption 5.1 (Asymptotic NTP conditions). ‣ 5.1 Asymptotic Distributions ‣ 5 Application to the Inverse Transform Watermark ‣ Optimal Detection for Language Watermarks with Pseudorandom Collision" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">5.1</span></a> cannot be verified in practice since it is introduced as a simplifying assumption for theoretical analysis. Thus, it suffices to check the remaining two conditions in Assumption <a href="#S3.Thmasmp3" title="Assumption 3.3. ‣ 3.3 Detection Efficiency and Optimal Scores ‣ 3 A Statistical Framework under Pseudorandomness Collision ‣ Optimal Detection for Language Watermarks with Pseudorandom Collision" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">3.3</span></a>.</p>
</div>
<div id="A1.SS8.SSS1.p2" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A1.SS8.SSS1.p2.1" class="ltx_p">On the one hand, the bounded variance condition in Assumption <a href="#S3.Thmasmp3" title="Assumption 3.3. ‣ 3.3 Detection Efficiency and Optimal Scores ‣ 3 A Statistical Framework under Pseudorandomness Collision ‣ Optimal Detection for Language Watermarks with Pseudorandom Collision" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">3.3</span></a><a href="#S3.I3.i2" title="item (ii) ‣ Assumption 3.3. ‣ 3.3 Detection Efficiency and Optimal Scores ‣ 3 A Statistical Framework under Pseudorandomness Collision ‣ Optimal Detection for Language Watermarks with Pseudorandom Collision" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">(ii)</span></a> holds immediately because <math id="A1.SS8.SSS1.p2.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="[h_{{\mathcal{V}}}^{\mathrm{inv}}]{[-M,M]}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><msubsup><mi>h</mi><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒱</mi><mi>inv</mi></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><mrow><mo>−</mo><mi>M</mi></mrow><mo>,</mo><mi>M</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">[h_{{\mathcal{V}}}^{\mathrm{inv}}]{[-M,M]}</annotation></semantics></math> is uniformly bounded by <math id="A1.SS8.SSS1.p2.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="M" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>M</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">M</annotation></semantics></math>.
On the other hand, the well-posedness condition in Assumption <a href="#S3.Thmasmp3" title="Assumption 3.3. ‣ 3.3 Detection Efficiency and Optimal Scores ‣ 3 A Statistical Framework under Pseudorandomness Collision ‣ Optimal Detection for Language Watermarks with Pseudorandom Collision" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">3.3</span></a> <a href="#S3.I3.i3" title="item (iii) ‣ Assumption 3.3. ‣ 3.3 Detection Efficiency and Optimal Scores ‣ 3 A Statistical Framework under Pseudorandomness Collision ‣ Optimal Detection for Language Watermarks with Pseudorandom Collision" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">(iii)</span></a> is automatically satisfied because in deriving (<a href="#S7.E30" title="In 7.2 Proof of Theorem ‣ 7 Proof of Main Results ‣ Optimal Detection for Language Watermarks with Pseudorandom Collision" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">30</span></a>) we essentially set the minimizer to <math id="A1.SS8.SSS1.p2.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\theta=1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>θ</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\theta=1</annotation></semantics></math>, which is uniformly bounded.
To make this intuition more rigorous, we can instead argue more directly: for the score functions <math id="A1.SS8.SSS1.p2.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="{\bm{h}}=\{h_{{\mathcal{V}}}\}_{{\mathcal{V}}\in\Pi}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>𝒉</mi><mo>=</mo><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><msub><mi>h</mi><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒱</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒱</mi><mo>∈</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">Π</mi></mrow></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\bm{h}}=\{h_{{\mathcal{V}}}\}_{{\mathcal{V}}\in\Pi}</annotation></semantics></math>, we have</p>
<table id="A1.EGx45" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A1.Ex95"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.Ex95.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\bar{R}_{n,\mathscr{P}}({\bm{h}})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>R</mi><mo>¯</mo></mover><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>,</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathscript">𝒫</mi></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝒉</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\bar{R}_{n,\mathscr{P}}({\bm{h}})</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.Ex95.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\overset{(a)}{\geq}\liminf_{|{{\mathcal{W}}}|\to\infty}D_{n,\mathscr{P}}({\bm{h}})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mover accent="true"><mo>≥</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="0.700em" minsize="0.700em">(</mo><mi mathsize="0.700em">a</mi><mo maxsize="0.700em" minsize="0.700em">)</mo></mrow></mover><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><munder><mo movablelimits="false" rspace="0.167em">lim inf</mo><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒲</mi><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">∞</mi></mrow></munder><mrow><msub><mi>D</mi><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>,</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathscript">𝒫</mi></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝒉</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\overset{(a)}{\geq}\liminf_{|{{\mathcal{W}}}|\to\infty}D_{n,\mathscr{P}}({\bm{h}})</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A1.Ex96"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.Ex96.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\overset{(b)}{\geq}-\limsup_{|{{\mathcal{W}}}|\to\infty}\left(\frac{\gamma_{n,\alpha}}{N_{n}}+\frac{1}{N_{n}}\sum_{{\mathcal{V}}\in\Pi}\sup_{\bm{P}_{{\mathcal{V}}}\subseteq\overline{{\mathcal{P}}}_{\Delta_{{\mathcal{V}}}}}\log\phi_{\bm{P}_{{\mathcal{V}}},h_{{\mathcal{V}}}}(1)\right)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mover accent="true"><mo>≥</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="0.700em" minsize="0.700em">(</mo><mi mathsize="0.700em">b</mi><mo maxsize="0.700em" minsize="0.700em">)</mo></mrow></mover><mo lspace="0em">−</mo><mrow><munder><mo lspace="0em" movablelimits="false" rspace="0em">lim sup</mo><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒲</mi><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">∞</mi></mrow></munder><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><msub><mi>γ</mi><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>α</mi></mrow></msub><msub><mi>N</mi><mi>n</mi></msub></mfrac></mstyle><mo>+</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mn>1</mn><msub><mi>N</mi><mi>n</mi></msub></mfrac></mstyle><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munder><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒱</mi><mo>∈</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">Π</mi></mrow></munder></mstyle><mrow><munder><mo lspace="0.167em" movablelimits="false" rspace="0.167em">sup</mo><mrow><msub><mi>𝑷</mi><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒱</mi></msub><mo>⊆</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒫</mi><mo stretchy="true">¯</mo></mover><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒱</mi></msub></msub></mrow></munder><mrow><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><msub><mi>ϕ</mi><mrow><msub><mi>𝑷</mi><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒱</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>h</mi><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒱</mi></msub></mrow></msub></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>1</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\overset{(b)}{\geq}-\limsup_{|{{\mathcal{W}}}|\to\infty}\left(\frac{\gamma_{n,\alpha}}{N_{n}}+\frac{1}{N_{n}}\sum_{{\mathcal{V}}\in\Pi}\sup_{\bm{P}_{{\mathcal{V}}}\subseteq\overline{{\mathcal{P}}}_{\Delta_{{\mathcal{V}}}}}\log\phi_{\bm{P}_{{\mathcal{V}}},h_{{\mathcal{V}}}}(1)\right)</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A1.Ex97"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.Ex97.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\overset{(c)}{\geq}-\limsup_{|{{\mathcal{W}}}|\to\infty}\frac{1}{N_{n}}\sum_{{\mathcal{V}}\in\Pi}\left(\EB_{0}[h_{{\mathcal{V}}}(Y_{{\mathcal{V}}})]+\sup_{\bm{P}_{{\mathcal{V}}}\subseteq\overline{{\mathcal{P}}}_{\Delta_{{\mathcal{V}}}}}\log\phi_{\bm{P}_{{\mathcal{V}}},h_{{\mathcal{V}}}}(1)\right)-\omega_{N_{n}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mover accent="true"><mo>≥</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="0.700em" minsize="0.700em">(</mo><mi mathsize="0.700em">c</mi><mo maxsize="0.700em" minsize="0.700em">)</mo></mrow></mover><mo lspace="0em">−</mo><mrow><munder><mo lspace="0em" movablelimits="false" rspace="0.167em">lim sup</mo><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒲</mi><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">∞</mi></mrow></munder><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mn>1</mn><msub><mi>N</mi><mi>n</mi></msub></mfrac></mstyle><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munder><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒱</mi><mo>∈</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">Π</mi></mrow></munder></mstyle><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>𝔼</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><msub><mi>h</mi><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒱</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>Y</mi><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒱</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><munder><mo lspace="0em" movablelimits="false" rspace="0.167em">sup</mo><mrow><msub><mi>𝐏</mi><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒱</mi></msub><mo>⊆</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒫</mi><mo stretchy="true">¯</mo></mover><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒱</mi></msub></msub></mrow></munder><mrow><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><msub><mi>ϕ</mi><mrow><msub><mi>𝐏</mi><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒱</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>h</mi><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒱</mi></msub></mrow></msub></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>1</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>ω</mi><msub><mi>N</mi><mi>n</mi></msub></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\overset{(c)}{\geq}-\limsup_{|{{\mathcal{W}}}|\to\infty}\frac{1}{N_{n}}\sum_{{\mathcal{V}}\in\Pi}\left(\EB_{0}[h_{{\mathcal{V}}}(Y_{{\mathcal{V}}})]+\sup_{\bm{P}_{{\mathcal{V}}}\subseteq\overline{{\mathcal{P}}}_{\Delta_{{\mathcal{V}}}}}\log\phi_{\bm{P}_{{\mathcal{V}}},h_{{\mathcal{V}}}}(1)\right)-\omega_{N_{n}}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A1.Ex98"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.Ex98.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\overset{}{=}-\frac{1}{N_{n}}\sum_{{\mathcal{V}}\in\Pi}\limsup_{|{{\mathcal{W}}}|\to\infty}\left(\EB_{0}[h_{{\mathcal{V}}}(Y_{{\mathcal{V}}})]+\sup_{\bm{P}_{{\mathcal{V}}}\subseteq\overline{{\mathcal{P}}}_{\Delta_{{\mathcal{V}}}}}\log\phi_{\bm{P}_{{\mathcal{V}}},h_{{\mathcal{V}}}}(1)\right)-\omega_{N_{n}}." display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mover accent="true"><mo>=</mo><mphantom></mphantom></mover><mo lspace="0em">−</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mn>1</mn><msub><mi>N</mi><mi>n</mi></msub></mfrac></mstyle><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munder><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒱</mi><mo>∈</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">Π</mi></mrow></munder></mstyle><mrow><munder><mo lspace="0.167em" movablelimits="false" rspace="0em">lim sup</mo><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒲</mi><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">∞</mi></mrow></munder><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>𝔼</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><msub><mi>h</mi><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒱</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>Y</mi><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒱</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><munder><mo lspace="0em" movablelimits="false" rspace="0.167em">sup</mo><mrow><msub><mi>𝐏</mi><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒱</mi></msub><mo>⊆</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒫</mi><mo stretchy="true">¯</mo></mover><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒱</mi></msub></msub></mrow></munder><mrow><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><msub><mi>ϕ</mi><mrow><msub><mi>𝐏</mi><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒱</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>h</mi><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒱</mi></msub></mrow></msub></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>1</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>ω</mi><msub><mi>N</mi><mi>n</mi></msub></msub></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\overset{}{=}-\frac{1}{N_{n}}\sum_{{\mathcal{V}}\in\Pi}\limsup_{|{{\mathcal{W}}}|\to\infty}\left(\EB_{0}[h_{{\mathcal{V}}}(Y_{{\mathcal{V}}})]+\sup_{\bm{P}_{{\mathcal{V}}}\subseteq\overline{{\mathcal{P}}}_{\Delta_{{\mathcal{V}}}}}\log\phi_{\bm{P}_{{\mathcal{V}}},h_{{\mathcal{V}}}}(1)\right)-\omega_{N_{n}}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(<a href="#S7.E30" title="In 7.2 Proof of Theorem ‣ 7 Proof of Main Results ‣ Optimal Detection for Language Watermarks with Pseudorandom Collision" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">30</span></a>)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A1.SS8.SSS1.p2.2" class="ltx_p">Here, <math id="A1.SS8.SSS1.p2.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(a)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>a</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(a)</annotation></semantics></math> follows from (<a href="#A1.Ex28" title="In Proof of Theorem . ‣ A.1 Proof of Theorem ‣ Appendix A Proof for the General Framework ‣ Optimal Detection for Language Watermarks with Pseudorandom Collision" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">31</span></a>), <math id="A1.SS8.SSS1.p2.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(b)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>b</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(b)</annotation></semantics></math> from setting <math id="A1.SS8.SSS1.p2.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\theta=1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>θ</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\theta=1</annotation></semantics></math> in the definition of <math id="A1.SS8.SSS1.p2.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="D_{n,\mathscr{P}}({\bm{h}})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>D</mi><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>,</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathscript">𝒫</mi></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝒉</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">D_{n,\mathscr{P}}({\bm{h}})</annotation></semantics></math> in (<a href="#A1.E32" title="In Proof of Theorem . ‣ A.1 Proof of Theorem ‣ Appendix A Proof for the General Framework ‣ Optimal Detection for Language Watermarks with Pseudorandom Collision" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">32</span></a>), and <math id="A1.SS8.SSS1.p2.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(c)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>c</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(c)</annotation></semantics></math> from Lemma <a href="#A1.Thmlem1" title="Lemma A.1. ‣ Proof of Theorem . ‣ A.1 Proof of Theorem ‣ Appendix A Proof for the General Framework ‣ Optimal Detection for Language Watermarks with Pseudorandom Collision" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">A.1</span></a>.
As a result, we still arrive at (<a href="#S7.E30" title="In 7.2 Proof of Theorem ‣ 7 Proof of Main Results ‣ Optimal Detection for Language Watermarks with Pseudorandom Collision" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">30</span></a>).</p>
</div>
</section>
<section id="A1.SS8.SSS2" class="ltx_subsubsection">
<h4 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsubsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsubsection">A.8.2 </span>Gumbel-max Watermark</h4>

<div id="A1.SS8.SSS2.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A1.SS8.SSS2.p1.1" class="ltx_p">The main effort is devoted to the Gumbel-max watermark, as we need to verify both conditions in Assumption <a href="#S3.Thmasmp3" title="Assumption 3.3. ‣ 3.3 Detection Efficiency and Optimal Scores ‣ 3 A Statistical Framework under Pseudorandomness Collision ‣ Optimal Detection for Language Watermarks with Pseudorandom Collision" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">3.3</span></a> as well as the additional Assumption <a href="#A1.Thmasmp1" title="Assumption A.1 (Regularity conditions for lower bound tightness). ‣ A.2 Asymptotic Tightness ‣ Appendix A Proof for the General Framework ‣ Optimal Detection for Language Watermarks with Pseudorandom Collision" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">A.1</span></a>, which is required for establishing the asymptotic tightness in Remark <a href="#S3.Thmrem3" title="Remark 3.3 (Asymptotic tightness). ‣ 3.3 Detection Efficiency and Optimal Scores ‣ 3 A Statistical Framework under Pseudorandomness Collision ‣ Optimal Detection for Language Watermarks with Pseudorandom Collision" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">3.3</span></a>.
For clarity, we fix a minimal unit <math id="A1.SS8.SSS2.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="{\mathcal{V}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒱</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\mathcal{V}}</annotation></semantics></math> and denote the two proposed score functions as</p>
<table id="A1.E70" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A1.E70.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="h_{{\bm{S}}_{\Delta}^{\star}}(y):=\frac{(|{\mathcal{V}}|\wedge|{{\mathcal{W}}}|)\,\Delta}{(|{\mathcal{V}}|\wedge|{{\mathcal{W}}}|-1)(1-\Delta)}\,\log y\quad\text{and}\quad h_{\bm{P}_{\Delta}^{\star}}(y):=\log\left(y^{\frac{\Delta}{1-\Delta}}+y^{\frac{1-\Delta}{\Delta}}\right)." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>h</mi><msubsup><mi>𝑺</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo>⋆</mo></msubsup></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>y</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>:=</mo><mrow><mfrac><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒱</mi><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow><mo>∧</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒲</mi><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0.170em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi></mrow><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒱</mi><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow><mo>∧</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒲</mi><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mfrac><mo lspace="0.337em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><mi>y</mi></mrow></mrow></mrow><mspace style="width:1em;" width="1em"></mspace><mtext>and</mtext><mspace style="width:1em;" width="1em"></mspace><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>h</mi><msubsup><mi>𝑷</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo>⋆</mo></msubsup></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>y</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>:=</mo><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><msup><mi>y</mi><mfrac><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi></mrow></mfrac></msup><mo>+</mo><msup><mi>y</mi><mfrac><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi></mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi></mfrac></msup></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">h_{{\bm{S}}_{\Delta}^{\star}}(y):=\frac{(|{\mathcal{V}}|\wedge|{{\mathcal{W}}}|)\,\Delta}{(|{\mathcal{V}}|\wedge|{{\mathcal{W}}}|-1)(1-\Delta)}\,\log y\quad\text{and}\quad h_{\bm{P}_{\Delta}^{\star}}(y):=\log\left(y^{\frac{\Delta}{1-\Delta}}+y^{\frac{1-\Delta}{\Delta}}\right).</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(70)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
<section id="A1.SS8.SSS2.Px1" class="ltx_paragraph">
<h5 class="ltx_title ltx_title_paragraph">Verification of Assumption <a href="#S3.Thmasmp3" title="Assumption 3.3. ‣ 3.3 Detection Efficiency and Optimal Scores ‣ 3 A Statistical Framework under Pseudorandomness Collision ‣ Optimal Detection for Language Watermarks with Pseudorandom Collision" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">3.3</span></a>.</h5>

<div id="A1.SS8.SSS2.Px1.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A1.SS8.SSS2.Px1.p1.1" class="ltx_p">Note that both optimal scores <math id="A1.SS8.SSS2.Px1.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="h_{{\bm{S}}_{\Delta}^{\star}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>h</mi><msubsup><mi>𝑺</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo>⋆</mo></msubsup></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">h_{{\bm{S}}_{\Delta}^{\star}}</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="A1.SS8.SSS2.Px1.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="h_{\bm{P}_{\Delta}^{\star}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>h</mi><msubsup><mi>𝑷</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo>⋆</mo></msubsup></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">h_{\bm{P}_{\Delta}^{\star}}</annotation></semantics></math> are log-likelihood ratio functions corresponding to the least-favorable distribution vectors <math id="A1.SS8.SSS2.Px1.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="{\bm{S}}_{\Delta}^{\star}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msubsup><mi>𝑺</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo>⋆</mo></msubsup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\bm{S}}_{\Delta}^{\star}</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="A1.SS8.SSS2.Px1.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\bm{P}_{\Delta}^{\star}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msubsup><mi>𝑷</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo>⋆</mo></msubsup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\bm{P}_{\Delta}^{\star}</annotation></semantics></math>, respectively. By direct computation, their moment generating functions are finite and their variances are uniformly bounded. Under these optimal scores, the minimization in <math id="A1.SS8.SSS2.Px1.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\theta" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>θ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\theta</annotation></semantics></math> is achieved at <math id="A1.SS8.SSS2.Px1.p1.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\theta=1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>θ</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\theta=1</annotation></semantics></math>, which is uniformly bounded. Hence, the well-posedness condition is satisfied.</p>
</div>
</section>
<section id="A1.SS8.SSS2.Px2" class="ltx_paragraph">
<h5 class="ltx_title ltx_title_paragraph">Verification of Assumption <a href="#A1.Thmasmp1" title="Assumption A.1 (Regularity conditions for lower bound tightness). ‣ A.2 Asymptotic Tightness ‣ Appendix A Proof for the General Framework ‣ Optimal Detection for Language Watermarks with Pseudorandom Collision" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">A.1</span></a>.</h5>

<div id="A1.SS8.SSS2.Px2.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A1.SS8.SSS2.Px2.p1.1" class="ltx_p">There are four conditions in Assumption <a href="#A1.Thmasmp1" title="Assumption A.1 (Regularity conditions for lower bound tightness). ‣ A.2 Asymptotic Tightness ‣ Appendix A Proof for the General Framework ‣ Optimal Detection for Language Watermarks with Pseudorandom Collision" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">A.1</span></a>, and we verify them one by one.</p>
<ol id="A1.I8" class="ltx_enumerate">
<li id="A1.I8.i1" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">1.</span> 
<div id="A1.I8.i1.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A1.I8.i1.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A1.I8.i1.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold ltx_font_italic">(Finite maximizers)</span>
This condition follows from Lemma <a href="#S7.Thmlem6" title="Lemma 7.6 (Maximum over polyhedron). ‣ 7.1 Proof of Theorem ‣ 7 Proof of Main Results ‣ Optimal Detection for Language Watermarks with Pseudorandom Collision" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">7.6</span></a>, together with the fact that both <math id="A1.I8.i1.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="h_{{\bm{S}}_{\Delta}^{\star}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>h</mi><msubsup><mi>𝑺</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo>⋆</mo></msubsup></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">h_{{\bm{S}}_{\Delta}^{\star}}</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="A1.I8.i1.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="h_{\bm{P}_{\Delta}^{\star}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>h</mi><msubsup><mi>𝑷</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo>⋆</mo></msubsup></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">h_{\bm{P}_{\Delta}^{\star}}</annotation></semantics></math> are increasing. Hence, only <math id="A1.I8.i1.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="{\bm{S}}_{\Delta}^{\star}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msubsup><mi>𝑺</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo>⋆</mo></msubsup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\bm{S}}_{\Delta}^{\star}</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="A1.I8.i1.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\bm{P}_{\Delta}^{\star}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msubsup><mi>𝑷</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo>⋆</mo></msubsup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\bm{P}_{\Delta}^{\star}</annotation></semantics></math> can serve as least-favorable distribution vectors.</p>
</div></li>
<li id="A1.I8.i2" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">2.</span> 
<div id="A1.I8.i2.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A1.I8.i2.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A1.I8.i2.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold ltx_font_italic">(Informative scores)</span>
By Lemma <a href="#S4.Thmlem1" title="Lemma 4.1. ‣ 4 Application to the Gumbel-max Watermark ‣ Optimal Detection for Language Watermarks with Pseudorandom Collision" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">4.1</span></a>, the null and alternative CDFs are given by <math id="A1.I8.i2.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="F_{0}(y)=y" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>F</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>y</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mi>y</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">F_{0}(y)=y</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="A1.I8.i2.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="F_{{\bm{S}}}(y)=(\sum_{w}S_{w})^{-1}\sum_{w}S_{w}y^{1/S_{w}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>F</mi><mi>𝑺</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>y</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mo lspace="0em">∑</mo><mi>w</mi></msub><msub><mi>S</mi><mi>w</mi></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><msub><mo>∑</mo><mi>w</mi></msub><mrow><msub><mi>S</mi><mi>w</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>y</mi><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>/</mo><msub><mi>S</mi><mi>w</mi></msub></mrow></msup></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">F_{{\bm{S}}}(y)=(\sum_{w}S_{w})^{-1}\sum_{w}S_{w}y^{1/S_{w}}</annotation></semantics></math> with <math id="A1.I8.i2.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="{\bm{S}}=(S_{1},\ldots,S_{|{{\mathcal{W}}}|})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>𝑺</mi><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>S</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>S</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒲</mi><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\bm{S}}=(S_{1},\ldots,S_{|{{\mathcal{W}}}|})</annotation></semantics></math>, respectively. From Lemma <a href="#S7.Thmlem2" title="Lemma 7.2 (Properties of the domain 𝒟_Δ). ‣ 7.1 Proof of Theorem ‣ 7 Proof of Main Results ‣ Optimal Detection for Language Watermarks with Pseudorandom Collision" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">7.2</span></a>, we know that <math id="A1.I8.i2.p1.m4" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="S_{w}\in[0,1-\Delta)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>S</mi><mi>w</mi></msub><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">S_{w}\in[0,1-\Delta)</annotation></semantics></math> for any <math id="A1.I8.i2.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="w" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>w</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">w</annotation></semantics></math>, so <math id="A1.I8.i2.p1.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="S_{w}&lt;1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>S</mi><mi>w</mi></msub><mo>&lt;</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">S_{w}&lt;1</annotation></semantics></math> and thus <math id="A1.I8.i2.p1.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="y^{1/S_{w}}&lt;y" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msup><mi>y</mi><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>/</mo><msub><mi>S</mi><mi>w</mi></msub></mrow></msup><mo>&lt;</mo><mi>y</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">y^{1/S_{w}}&lt;y</annotation></semantics></math> for any <math id="A1.I8.i2.p1.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="y\in(0,1)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>y</mi><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>1</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">y\in(0,1)</annotation></semantics></math>. Consequently,</p>
<table id="A1.EGx46" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A1.Ex99"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.Ex99.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle F_{{\bm{S}}}(y)=\frac{\sum_{w}S_{w}y^{1/S_{w}}}{\sum_{w}S_{w}}&lt;\frac{\sum_{w}S_{w}y}{\sum_{w}S_{w}}=y=F_{0}(y)." display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>F</mi><mi>𝑺</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>y</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><msub><mo>∑</mo><mi>w</mi></msub><mrow><msub><mi>S</mi><mi>w</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>y</mi><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>/</mo><msub><mi>S</mi><mi>w</mi></msub></mrow></msup></mrow></mrow><mrow><msub><mo>∑</mo><mi>w</mi></msub><msub><mi>S</mi><mi>w</mi></msub></mrow></mfrac></mstyle><mo>&lt;</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><msub><mo>∑</mo><mi>w</mi></msub><mrow><msub><mi>S</mi><mi>w</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>y</mi></mrow></mrow><mrow><msub><mo>∑</mo><mi>w</mi></msub><msub><mi>S</mi><mi>w</mi></msub></mrow></mfrac></mstyle><mo>=</mo><mi>y</mi><mo>=</mo><mrow><msub><mi>F</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>y</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle F_{{\bm{S}}}(y)=\frac{\sum_{w}S_{w}y^{1/S_{w}}}{\sum_{w}S_{w}}&lt;\frac{\sum_{w}S_{w}y}{\sum_{w}S_{w}}=y=F_{0}(y).</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A1.I8.i2.p1.2" class="ltx_p">Thus, the alternative distribution of <math id="A1.I8.i2.p1.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="Y" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>Y</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">Y</annotation></semantics></math> is stochastically dominated by the null distribution. Since both <math id="A1.I8.i2.p1.m10" class="ltx_Math" alttext="h_{{\bm{S}}_{\Delta}^{\star}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>h</mi><msubsup><mi>𝑺</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo>⋆</mo></msubsup></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">h_{{\bm{S}}_{\Delta}^{\star}}</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="A1.I8.i2.p1.m11" class="ltx_Math" alttext="h_{\bm{P}_{\Delta}^{\star}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>h</mi><msubsup><mi>𝑷</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo>⋆</mo></msubsup></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">h_{\bm{P}_{\Delta}^{\star}}</annotation></semantics></math> are strictly increasing, integration by parts shows that <math id="A1.I8.i2.p1.m12" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\EB_{1,\bm{P}_{\mathcal{V}}}[h(Y)]&gt;\EB_{0}[h(Y)]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>𝔼</mi><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>𝐏</mi><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒱</mi></msub></mrow></msub><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><mi>h</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>Y</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>&gt;</mo><mrow><msub><mi>𝔼</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><mi>h</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>Y</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\EB_{1,\bm{P}_{\mathcal{V}}}[h(Y)]&gt;\EB_{0}[h(Y)]</annotation></semantics></math> for <math id="A1.I8.i2.p1.m13" class="ltx_Math" alttext="h\in\{h_{{\bm{S}}_{\Delta}^{\star}},h_{\bm{P}_{\Delta}^{\star}}\}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>h</mi><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><msub><mi>h</mi><msubsup><mi>𝑺</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo>⋆</mo></msubsup></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>h</mi><msubsup><mi>𝑷</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo>⋆</mo></msubsup></msub><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">h\in\{h_{{\bm{S}}_{\Delta}^{\star}},h_{\bm{P}_{\Delta}^{\star}}\}</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>
</div></li>
<li id="A1.I8.i3" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">3.</span> 
<div id="A1.I8.i3.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A1.I8.i3.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A1.I8.i3.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold ltx_font_italic">(CGF regularity)</span>
Recall that the CGF is defined as the logarithm of the MGF. Formally, for a score function <math id="A1.I8.i3.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="h" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>h</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">h</annotation></semantics></math>, the MGF is <math id="A1.I8.i3.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\phi_{{\bm{S}}}(\theta)=\EB_{1,{\bm{S}}}[\exp(-\theta h(Y_{\mathcal{V}}))]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>ϕ</mi><mi>𝑺</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>θ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><msub><mi>𝔼</mi><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>,</mo><mi>𝐒</mi></mrow></msub><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><mi>exp</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>θ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>h</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>Y</mi><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒱</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\phi_{{\bm{S}}}(\theta)=\EB_{1,{\bm{S}}}[\exp(-\theta h(Y_{\mathcal{V}}))]</annotation></semantics></math> and the CGF is given by <math id="A1.I8.i3.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="K(\theta)=\log\phi_{{\bm{S}}}(\theta)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>K</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>θ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><msub><mi>ϕ</mi><mi>𝑺</mi></msub></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>θ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">K(\theta)=\log\phi_{{\bm{S}}}(\theta)</annotation></semantics></math>. For simplicity, we denote the alternative density by <math id="A1.I8.i3.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="f_{{\bm{S}}}(y)=F^{\prime}_{{\bm{S}}}(y)=(\sum{w^{\prime}}S_{w^{\prime}})^{-1}\sum_{w}y^{1/S_{w}-1}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>f</mi><mi>𝑺</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>y</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>F</mi><mi>𝑺</mi><mo>′</mo></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>y</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mo lspace="0em">∑</mo><mrow><msup><mi>w</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>S</mi><msup><mi>w</mi><mo>′</mo></msup></msub></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><msub><mo>∑</mo><mi>w</mi></msub><msup><mi>y</mi><mrow><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>/</mo><msub><mi>S</mi><mi>w</mi></msub></mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">f_{{\bm{S}}}(y)=F^{\prime}_{{\bm{S}}}(y)=(\sum{w^{\prime}}S_{w^{\prime}})^{-1}\sum_{w}y^{1/S_{w}-1}</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>
<ul id="A1.I8.i3.I1" class="ltx_itemize">
<li id="A1.I8.i3.I1.i1" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">•</span> 
<div id="A1.I8.i3.I1.i1.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A1.I8.i3.I1.i1.p1.1" class="ltx_p">For <math id="A1.I8.i3.I1.i1.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="h_{{\bm{S}}_{\Delta}^{\star}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>h</mi><msubsup><mi>𝑺</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo>⋆</mo></msubsup></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">h_{{\bm{S}}_{\Delta}^{\star}}</annotation></semantics></math>, the MGF takes the explicit form</p>
<table id="A1.Ex100" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A1.Ex100.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\phi_{{\bm{S}}}(\theta)=\int_{0}^{1}{\mathrm{e}}^{-\theta c\log y}f_{{\bm{S}}}(y){\mathrm{d}}y=\int_{0}^{1}y^{-\theta c}\frac{\sum_{w}y^{1/S_{w}-1}}{\sum_{w^{\prime}}S_{w^{\prime}}}{\mathrm{d}}y=\frac{1}{\sum_{w^{\prime}}S_{w^{\prime}}}\sum_{w}\frac{S_{w}}{1-\theta cS_{w}}." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>ϕ</mi><mi>𝑺</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>θ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.111em">=</mo><mrow><msubsup><mo>∫</mo><mn>0</mn><mn>1</mn></msubsup><mrow><msup><mi>e</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>θ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>c</mi><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><mi>y</mi></mrow></mrow></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>f</mi><mi>𝑺</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>y</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo rspace="0em">𝑑</mo><mi>y</mi></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.111em">=</mo><mrow><msubsup><mo>∫</mo><mn>0</mn><mn>1</mn></msubsup><mrow><msup><mi>y</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>θ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>c</mi></mrow></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mfrac><mrow><msub><mo>∑</mo><mi>w</mi></msub><msup><mi>y</mi><mrow><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>/</mo><msub><mi>S</mi><mi>w</mi></msub></mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup></mrow><mrow><msub><mo>∑</mo><msup><mi>w</mi><mo>′</mo></msup></msub><msub><mi>S</mi><msup><mi>w</mi><mo>′</mo></msup></msub></mrow></mfrac><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo rspace="0em">𝑑</mo><mi>y</mi></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mrow><msub><mo>∑</mo><msup><mi>w</mi><mo>′</mo></msup></msub><msub><mi>S</mi><msup><mi>w</mi><mo>′</mo></msup></msub></mrow></mfrac><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><munder><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mi>w</mi></munder><mfrac><msub><mi>S</mi><mi>w</mi></msub><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>θ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>c</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>S</mi><mi>w</mi></msub></mrow></mrow></mfrac></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\phi_{{\bm{S}}}(\theta)=\int_{0}^{1}{\mathrm{e}}^{-\theta c\log y}f_{{\bm{S}}}(y){\mathrm{d}}y=\int_{0}^{1}y^{-\theta c}\frac{\sum_{w}y^{1/S_{w}-1}}{\sum_{w^{\prime}}S_{w^{\prime}}}{\mathrm{d}}y=\frac{1}{\sum_{w^{\prime}}S_{w^{\prime}}}\sum_{w}\frac{S_{w}}{1-\theta cS_{w}}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div></li>
<li id="A1.I8.i3.I1.i2" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">•</span> 
<div id="A1.I8.i3.I1.i2.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A1.I8.i3.I1.i2.p1.1" class="ltx_p">For <math id="A1.I8.i3.I1.i2.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="h_{\bm{P}_{\Delta}^{\star}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>h</mi><msubsup><mi>𝑷</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo>⋆</mo></msubsup></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">h_{\bm{P}_{\Delta}^{\star}}</annotation></semantics></math>, the MGF is</p>
<table id="A1.Ex101" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A1.Ex101.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\phi_{{\bm{S}}}(\theta)=\int_{0}^{1}(y^{\frac{1-\Delta}{\Delta}}+y^{\frac{\Delta}{1-\Delta}})^{-\theta}f_{{\bm{S}}}(y)dy." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>ϕ</mi><mi>𝑺</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>θ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.111em">=</mo><mrow><msubsup><mo rspace="0em">∫</mo><mn>0</mn><mn>1</mn></msubsup><mrow><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msup><mi>y</mi><mfrac><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi></mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi></mfrac></msup><mo>+</mo><msup><mi>y</mi><mfrac><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi></mrow></mfrac></msup></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mrow><mo>−</mo><mi>θ</mi></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>f</mi><mi>𝑺</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>y</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo rspace="0em">𝑑</mo><mi>y</mi></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\phi_{{\bm{S}}}(\theta)=\int_{0}^{1}(y^{\frac{1-\Delta}{\Delta}}+y^{\frac{\Delta}{1-\Delta}})^{-\theta}f_{{\bm{S}}}(y)dy.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div></li>
</ul>
<p id="A1.I8.i3.p1.2" class="ltx_p">On any compact set <math id="A1.I8.i3.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="[0,\overline{M}]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>M</mi><mo stretchy="true">¯</mo></mover><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">[0,\overline{M}]</annotation></semantics></math>, the derivatives of <math id="A1.I8.i3.p1.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\log\phi_{{\bm{S}}}(\theta)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><msub><mi>ϕ</mi><mi>𝑺</mi></msub></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>θ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\log\phi_{{\bm{S}}}(\theta)</annotation></semantics></math> are smooth and bounded, which yields uniform upper bounds. For the lower bound, note that <math id="A1.I8.i3.p1.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="K^{\prime\prime}(\theta)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msup><mi>K</mi><mo>′′</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>θ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">K^{\prime\prime}(\theta)</annotation></semantics></math> equals the variance of <math id="A1.I8.i3.p1.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="-h(Y)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>h</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>Y</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">-h(Y)</annotation></semantics></math> under a tilted measure, which is strictly positive as long as <math id="A1.I8.i3.p1.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="h(Y)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>h</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>Y</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">h(Y)</annotation></semantics></math> is not constant. By continuity, <math id="A1.I8.i3.p1.m10" class="ltx_Math" alttext="K^{\prime\prime}(\theta)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msup><mi>K</mi><mo>′′</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>θ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">K^{\prime\prime}(\theta)</annotation></semantics></math> is uniformly bounded below on <math id="A1.I8.i3.p1.m11" class="ltx_Math" alttext="[0,\overline{M}]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>M</mi><mo stretchy="true">¯</mo></mover><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">[0,\overline{M}]</annotation></semantics></math> by some constant <math id="A1.I8.i3.p1.m12" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\sigma_{\min}^{2}(K)&gt;0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msubsup><mi>σ</mi><mi>min</mi><mn>2</mn></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>K</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>&gt;</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\sigma_{\min}^{2}(K)&gt;0</annotation></semantics></math>. These constants can be chosen independently of any specific <math id="A1.I8.i3.p1.m13" class="ltx_Math" alttext="{\bm{S}}\in\mathcal{D}_{\Delta}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>𝑺</mi><mo>∈</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒟</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\bm{S}}\in\mathcal{D}_{\Delta}</annotation></semantics></math>, thanks to compactness of <math id="A1.I8.i3.p1.m14" class="ltx_Math" alttext="[0,\overline{M}]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>M</mi><mo stretchy="true">¯</mo></mover><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">[0,\overline{M}]</annotation></semantics></math> and smoothness of the CGF.</p>
</div></li>
<li id="A1.I8.i4" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">4.</span> 
<div id="A1.I8.i4.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A1.I8.i4.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A1.I8.i4.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold ltx_font_italic">(Score density regularity)</span>
The last condition is verified directly by Lemma <a href="#A1.Thmlem12" title="Lemma A.12 (Bounded total variation). ‣ Verification of Assumption . ‣ A.8.2 Gumbel-max Watermark ‣ A.8 Verification of Regularity Conditions for Considered Watermarks ‣ Appendix A Proof for the General Framework ‣ Optimal Detection for Language Watermarks with Pseudorandom Collision" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">A.12</span></a>.</p>
</div></li>
</ol>
</div>
<div id="A1.Thmlem12" class="ltx_theorem ltx_theorem_lem">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_title_theorem"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_theorem"><span id="A1.Thmlem12.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Lemma A.12</span></span><span id="A1.Thmlem12.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold"> </span>(Bounded total variation)<span id="A1.Thmlem12.4" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">.</span></h6>
<div id="A1.Thmlem12.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A1.Thmlem12.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A1.Thmlem12.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">Let <math id="A1.Thmlem12.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathrm{TV}(\rho):=\int_{-\infty}^{\infty}|\rho^{\prime}(x)|{\mathrm{d}}x" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>TV</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>ρ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.111em">:=</mo><mrow><msubsup><mo rspace="0em">∫</mo><mrow><mo>−</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">∞</mi></mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">∞</mi></msubsup><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><mrow><msup><mi>ρ</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo rspace="0em">𝑑</mo><mi>x</mi></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathrm{TV}(\rho):=\int_{-\infty}^{\infty}|\rho^{\prime}(x)|{\mathrm{d}}x</annotation></semantics></math> denote the total variation of a PDF <math id="A1.Thmlem12.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\rho" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>ρ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\rho</annotation></semantics></math>.
When <math id="A1.Thmlem12.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="|{\mathcal{V}}|=1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒱</mi><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">|{\mathcal{V}}|=1</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="A1.Thmlem12.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\Delta\in(0,1/2)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>/</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Delta\in(0,1/2)</annotation></semantics></math>, with <math id="A1.Thmlem12.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="h_{{\bm{S}}_{\Delta}^{\star}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>h</mi><msubsup><mi>𝐒</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo>⋆</mo></msubsup></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">h_{{\bm{S}}_{\Delta}^{\star}}</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="A1.Thmlem12.p1.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="h_{\bm{P}_{\Delta}^{\star}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>h</mi><msubsup><mi>𝐏</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo>⋆</mo></msubsup></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">h_{\bm{P}_{\Delta}^{\star}}</annotation></semantics></math> defined in (<a href="#A1.E70" title="In A.8.2 Gumbel-max Watermark ‣ A.8 Verification of Regularity Conditions for Considered Watermarks ‣ Appendix A Proof for the General Framework ‣ Optimal Detection for Language Watermarks with Pseudorandom Collision" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">70</span></a>), we have a universal constant <math id="A1.Thmlem12.p1.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="C_{R}&gt;0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>C</mi><mi>R</mi></msub><mo>&gt;</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">C_{R}&gt;0</annotation></semantics></math> such that</span></p>
<table id="A1.Ex102" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A1.Ex102.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathrm{TV}(h_{{\bm{S}}_{\Delta}^{\star}})\leq|{{\mathcal{W}}}|\qquad\text{and}\qquad\mathrm{TV}(h_{\bm{P}_{\Delta}^{\star}})\leq|{{\mathcal{W}}}|+C_{R}." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>TV</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>h</mi><msubsup><mi>𝑺</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo>⋆</mo></msubsup></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>≤</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒲</mi><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow></mrow><mspace style="width:2em;" width="2em"></mspace><mtext class="ltx_mathvariant_italic">and</mtext><mspace style="width:2em;" width="2em"></mspace><mrow><mrow><mi>TV</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>h</mi><msubsup><mi>𝑷</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo>⋆</mo></msubsup></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>≤</mo><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒲</mi><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow><mo>+</mo><msub><mi>C</mi><mi>R</mi></msub></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathrm{TV}(h_{{\bm{S}}_{\Delta}^{\star}})\leq|{{\mathcal{W}}}|\qquad\text{and}\qquad\mathrm{TV}(h_{\bm{P}_{\Delta}^{\star}})\leq|{{\mathcal{W}}}|+C_{R}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
</div>
<div id="A1.SS8.SSS2.Px2.1" class="ltx_proof">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_font_italic ltx_title_proof">Proof of Lemma <a href="#A1.Thmlem12" title="Lemma A.12 (Bounded total variation). ‣ Verification of Assumption . ‣ A.8.2 Gumbel-max Watermark ‣ A.8 Verification of Regularity Conditions for Considered Watermarks ‣ Appendix A Proof for the General Framework ‣ Optimal Detection for Language Watermarks with Pseudorandom Collision" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">A.12</span></a>.</h6>
<div id="A1.SS8.SSS2.Px2.p2" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A1.SS8.SSS2.Px2.p2.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A1.SS8.SSS2.Px2.p2.1.1" class="ltx_text">Let <math id="A1.SS8.SSS2.Px2.p2.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="Z=h(Y)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>Z</mi><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>h</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>Y</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">Z=h(Y)</annotation></semantics></math> denote the score for a minimal unit <math id="A1.SS8.SSS2.Px2.p2.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{V}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒱</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{V}</annotation></semantics></math>.
When <math id="A1.SS8.SSS2.Px2.p2.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="|{\mathcal{V}}|=1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒱</mi><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">|{\mathcal{V}}|=1</annotation></semantics></math>, there is no repetition and each <math id="A1.SS8.SSS2.Px2.p2.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="{\bm{S}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>𝑺</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\bm{S}}</annotation></semantics></math> reduces to <math id="A1.SS8.SSS2.Px2.p2.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\bm{P}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>𝑷</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\bm{P}</annotation></semantics></math>.
By Lemma <a href="#S4.Thmlem1" title="Lemma 4.1. ‣ 4 Application to the Gumbel-max Watermark ‣ Optimal Detection for Language Watermarks with Pseudorandom Collision" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">4.1</span></a>, the alternative PDF of <math id="A1.SS8.SSS2.Px2.p2.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="Y" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>Y</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">Y</annotation></semantics></math> is</span></p>
<table id="A1.Ex103" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A1.Ex103.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="f_{\bm{P}}(y)=F^{\prime}_{\bm{P}}(y)=\sum_{w}y^{1/P_{w}-1}." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>f</mi><mi>𝑷</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>y</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>F</mi><mi>𝑷</mi><mo>′</mo></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>y</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.111em">=</mo><mrow><munder><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mi>w</mi></munder><msup><mi>y</mi><mrow><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>/</mo><msub><mi>P</mi><mi>w</mi></msub></mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">f_{\bm{P}}(y)=F^{\prime}_{\bm{P}}(y)=\sum_{w}y^{1/P_{w}-1}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A1.SS8.SSS2.Px2.p2.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="A1.SS8.SSS2.Px2.p2.2.1" class="ltx_text">By a change of variables, the PDF of <math id="A1.SS8.SSS2.Px2.p2.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="Z" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>Z</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">Z</annotation></semantics></math>, denoted by <math id="A1.SS8.SSS2.Px2.p2.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\rho_{\bm{P}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>ρ</mi><mi>𝑷</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\rho_{\bm{P}}</annotation></semantics></math>, is
<math id="A1.SS8.SSS2.Px2.p2.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\rho_{\bm{P}}(z)=f_{\bm{P}}(g(z))|g^{\prime}(z)|" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>ρ</mi><mi>𝑷</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>z</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><msub><mi>f</mi><mi>𝑷</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>g</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>z</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><mrow><msup><mi>g</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>z</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\rho_{\bm{P}}(z)=f_{\bm{P}}(g(z))|g^{\prime}(z)|</annotation></semantics></math>, where <math id="A1.SS8.SSS2.Px2.p2.m10" class="ltx_Math" alttext="y=g(z)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>y</mi><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>g</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>z</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">y=g(z)</annotation></semantics></math> is the inverse of <math id="A1.SS8.SSS2.Px2.p2.m11" class="ltx_Math" alttext="z=h(y)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>z</mi><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>h</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>y</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">z=h(y)</annotation></semantics></math>.</span></p>
</div>
</div>
</section>
<section id="A1.SS8.SSS2.Px3" class="ltx_paragraph">
<h5 class="ltx_title ltx_title_paragraph">Case 1: <math id="A1.SS8.SSS2.Px3.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="h_{{\bm{S}}_{\Delta}^{\star}}(y)=C\log y" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>h</mi><msubsup><mi>𝑺</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo>⋆</mo></msubsup></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>y</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>C</mi><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><mi>y</mi></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">h_{{\bm{S}}_{\Delta}^{\star}}(y)=C\log y</annotation></semantics></math>.</h5>

<div id="A1.SS8.SSS2.Px3.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A1.SS8.SSS2.Px3.p1.1" class="ltx_p">Here <math id="A1.SS8.SSS2.Px3.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="C=\frac{\Delta}{1-\Delta}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>C</mi><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi></mrow></mfrac></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">C=\frac{\Delta}{1-\Delta}</annotation></semantics></math>, and the inverse function is <math id="A1.SS8.SSS2.Px3.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="y=g(z)=e^{z/C}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>y</mi><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>g</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>z</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><msup><mi>e</mi><mrow><mi>z</mi><mo>/</mo><mi>C</mi></mrow></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">y=g(z)=e^{z/C}</annotation></semantics></math> for <math id="A1.SS8.SSS2.Px3.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="z\in(-\infty,0)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>z</mi><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mo>−</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">∞</mi></mrow><mo>,</mo><mn>0</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">z\in(-\infty,0)</annotation></semantics></math> with derivative <math id="A1.SS8.SSS2.Px3.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="g^{\prime}(z)=\tfrac{1}{C}e^{z/C}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msup><mi>g</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>z</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mi>C</mi></mfrac><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>e</mi><mrow><mi>z</mi><mo>/</mo><mi>C</mi></mrow></msup></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">g^{\prime}(z)=\tfrac{1}{C}e^{z/C}</annotation></semantics></math>. The density of <math id="A1.SS8.SSS2.Px3.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="Z" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>Z</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">Z</annotation></semantics></math> is</p>
<table id="A1.Ex104" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A1.Ex104.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\rho_{\bm{P}}(z)=f_{\bm{P}}(e^{z/C})\cdot\frac{1}{C}e^{z/C}=\frac{1}{C}\sum_{w}e^{z/(CP_{w})}." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>ρ</mi><mi>𝑷</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>z</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>f</mi><mi>𝑷</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>e</mi><mrow><mi>z</mi><mo>/</mo><mi>C</mi></mrow></msup><mo rspace="0.055em" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mi>C</mi></mfrac></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>e</mi><mrow><mi>z</mi><mo>/</mo><mi>C</mi></mrow></msup></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mi>C</mi></mfrac><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><munder><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mi>w</mi></munder><msup><mi>e</mi><mrow><mi>z</mi><mo>/</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>C</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>P</mi><mi>w</mi></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></msup></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\rho_{\bm{P}}(z)=f_{\bm{P}}(e^{z/C})\cdot\frac{1}{C}e^{z/C}=\frac{1}{C}\sum_{w}e^{z/(CP_{w})}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A1.SS8.SSS2.Px3.p1.2" class="ltx_p">Since <math id="A1.SS8.SSS2.Px3.p1.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\rho_{\bm{P}}^{\prime}(z)&gt;0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msubsup><mi>ρ</mi><mi>𝑷</mi><mo>′</mo></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>z</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>&gt;</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\rho_{\bm{P}}^{\prime}(z)&gt;0</annotation></semantics></math> for <math id="A1.SS8.SSS2.Px3.p1.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="z\in(-\infty,0)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>z</mi><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mo>−</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">∞</mi></mrow><mo>,</mo><mn>0</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">z\in(-\infty,0)</annotation></semantics></math>, it follows that</p>
<table id="A1.Ex105" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A1.Ex105.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathrm{TV}(\rho_{\bm{P}})=\int_{-\infty}^{0}\rho_{\bm{P}}^{\prime}(z)\,{\mathrm{d}}z=\rho_{\bm{P}}(0)-\lim_{z\to-\infty}\rho_{\bm{P}}(z)=\frac{|{{\mathcal{W}}}|}{C}\leq|{{\mathcal{W}}}|," display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>TV</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>ρ</mi><mi>𝑷</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.111em">=</mo><mrow><msubsup><mo>∫</mo><mrow><mo>−</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">∞</mi></mrow><mn>0</mn></msubsup><mrow><msubsup><mi>ρ</mi><mi>𝑷</mi><mo>′</mo></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>z</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0.170em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo rspace="0em">𝑑</mo><mi>z</mi></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>ρ</mi><mi>𝑷</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>0</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><munder><mo lspace="0em" movablelimits="false" rspace="0.167em">lim</mo><mrow><mi>z</mi><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><mrow><mo>−</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">∞</mi></mrow></mrow></munder><mrow><msub><mi>ρ</mi><mi>𝑷</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>z</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒲</mi><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow><mi>C</mi></mfrac><mo>≤</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒲</mi><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathrm{TV}(\rho_{\bm{P}})=\int_{-\infty}^{0}\rho_{\bm{P}}^{\prime}(z)\,{\mathrm{d}}z=\rho_{\bm{P}}(0)-\lim_{z\to-\infty}\rho_{\bm{P}}(z)=\frac{|{{\mathcal{W}}}|}{C}\leq|{{\mathcal{W}}}|,</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A1.SS8.SSS2.Px3.p1.3" class="ltx_p">where the last inequality holds because <math id="A1.SS8.SSS2.Px3.p1.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="C&gt;1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>C</mi><mo>&gt;</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">C&gt;1</annotation></semantics></math> when <math id="A1.SS8.SSS2.Px3.p1.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\Delta\in(0,1/2)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>/</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Delta\in(0,1/2)</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>
</div>
</section>
<section id="A1.SS8.SSS2.Px4" class="ltx_paragraph">
<h5 class="ltx_title ltx_title_paragraph">Case 2: <math id="A1.SS8.SSS2.Px4.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="h_{\bm{P}_{\Delta}^{\star}}(y)=\log(y^{C}+y^{1/C})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>h</mi><msubsup><mi>𝑷</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo>⋆</mo></msubsup></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>y</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msup><mi>y</mi><mi>C</mi></msup><mo>+</mo><msup><mi>y</mi><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>/</mo><mi>C</mi></mrow></msup></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">h_{\bm{P}_{\Delta}^{\star}}(y)=\log(y^{C}+y^{1/C})</annotation></semantics></math>.</h5>

<div id="A1.SS8.SSS2.Px4.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A1.SS8.SSS2.Px4.p1.1" class="ltx_p">Here <math id="A1.SS8.SSS2.Px4.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="C=\frac{\Delta}{1-\Delta}\in(0,1)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>C</mi><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi></mrow></mfrac><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>1</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">C=\frac{\Delta}{1-\Delta}\in(0,1)</annotation></semantics></math>. By definition,</p>
<table id="A1.Ex106" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A1.Ex106.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathrm{TV}(\rho_{\bm{P}})=\int|\rho_{\bm{P}}^{\prime}(z)|\,{\mathrm{d}}z=\int_{0}^{1}\left|\frac{d}{dy}\left(\frac{f_{\bm{P}}(y)}{h^{\prime}(y)}\right)\right|{\mathrm{d}}y\leq\underbrace{\int_{0}^{1}\left|\frac{f_{\bm{P}}^{\prime}(y)}{h^{\prime}(y)}\right|{\mathrm{d}}y}_{(I)}+\underbrace{\int_{0}^{1}f_{\bm{P}}(y)\left|\frac{h^{\prime\prime}(y)}{(h^{\prime}(y))^{2}}\right|{\mathrm{d}}y}_{(II)}." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>TV</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>ρ</mi><mi>𝑷</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.111em">=</mo><mrow><mo rspace="0em">∫</mo><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>ρ</mi><mi>𝑷</mi><mo>′</mo></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>z</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0.170em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo rspace="0em">𝑑</mo><mi>z</mi></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.111em">=</mo><mrow><msubsup><mo rspace="0em">∫</mo><mn>0</mn><mn>1</mn></msubsup><mrow><mrow><mo>|</mo><mrow><mfrac><mi>d</mi><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>y</mi></mrow></mfrac><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mfrac><mrow><msub><mi>f</mi><mi>𝑷</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>y</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mrow><msup><mi>h</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>y</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mfrac><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>|</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo rspace="0em">𝑑</mo><mi>y</mi></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.111em">≤</mo><mrow><munder><munder accentunder="true"><mrow><msubsup><mo rspace="0em">∫</mo><mn>0</mn><mn>1</mn></msubsup><mrow><mrow><mo>|</mo><mfrac><mrow><msubsup><mi>f</mi><mi>𝑷</mi><mo>′</mo></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>y</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mrow><msup><mi>h</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>y</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mfrac><mo>|</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo rspace="0em">d</mo><mi>y</mi></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="true">⏟</mo></munder><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>I</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></munder><mo rspace="0.055em">+</mo><munder><munder accentunder="true"><mrow><msubsup><mo>∫</mo><mn>0</mn><mn>1</mn></msubsup><mrow><msub><mi>f</mi><mi>𝑷</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>y</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>|</mo><mfrac><mrow><msup><mi>h</mi><mo>′′</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>y</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msup><mi>h</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>y</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup></mfrac><mo>|</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo rspace="0em">d</mo><mi>y</mi></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="true">⏟</mo></munder><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>I</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>I</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></munder></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathrm{TV}(\rho_{\bm{P}})=\int|\rho_{\bm{P}}^{\prime}(z)|\,{\mathrm{d}}z=\int_{0}^{1}\left|\frac{d}{dy}\left(\frac{f_{\bm{P}}(y)}{h^{\prime}(y)}\right)\right|{\mathrm{d}}y\leq\underbrace{\int_{0}^{1}\left|\frac{f_{\bm{P}}^{\prime}(y)}{h^{\prime}(y)}\right|{\mathrm{d}}y}_{(I)}+\underbrace{\int_{0}^{1}f_{\bm{P}}(y)\left|\frac{h^{\prime\prime}(y)}{(h^{\prime}(y))^{2}}\right|{\mathrm{d}}y}_{(II)}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
<div id="A1.SS8.SSS2.Px4.p2" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A1.SS8.SSS2.Px4.p2.1" class="ltx_p">We first analyze the term (II). For simplicity, we define <math id="A1.SS8.SSS2.Px4.p2.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="R(y):=\big|h^{\prime\prime}(y)/(h^{\prime}(y))^{2}\big|" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>R</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>y</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>:=</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em" stretchy="true">|</mo><mrow><mrow><msup><mi>h</mi><mo>′′</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>y</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>/</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msup><mi>h</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>y</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em" stretchy="true">|</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">R(y):=\big|h^{\prime\prime}(y)/(h^{\prime}(y))^{2}\big|</annotation></semantics></math>, which is independent of <math id="A1.SS8.SSS2.Px4.p2.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\bm{P}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>𝑷</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\bm{P}</annotation></semantics></math>.
As <math id="A1.SS8.SSS2.Px4.p2.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="y\to 1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>y</mi><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">y\to 1</annotation></semantics></math>, <math id="A1.SS8.SSS2.Px4.p2.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="h^{\prime}(1)=(C+1/C)/2\neq 0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msup><mi>h</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>1</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>C</mi><mo>+</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>/</mo><mi>C</mi></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>/</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow><mo>≠</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">h^{\prime}(1)=(C+1/C)/2\neq 0</annotation></semantics></math>, so <math id="A1.SS8.SSS2.Px4.p2.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="R(1)&lt;\infty" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>R</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>1</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>&lt;</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">∞</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">R(1)&lt;\infty</annotation></semantics></math>.
As <math id="A1.SS8.SSS2.Px4.p2.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="y\to 0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>y</mi><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">y\to 0</annotation></semantics></math>, <math id="A1.SS8.SSS2.Px4.p2.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="h^{\prime}(y)\sim C/y" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msup><mi>h</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>y</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>∼</mo><mrow><mi>C</mi><mo>/</mo><mi>y</mi></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">h^{\prime}(y)\sim C/y</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="A1.SS8.SSS2.Px4.p2.m8" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="h^{\prime\prime}(y)\sim-C/y^{2}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msup><mi>h</mi><mo>′′</mo></msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>y</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo rspace="0em">∼</mo><mo lspace="0em">−</mo><mi>C</mi><mo>/</mo><msup><mi>y</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">h^{\prime\prime}(y)\sim-C/y^{2}</annotation></semantics></math>, hence <math id="A1.SS8.SSS2.Px4.p2.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\lim_{y\to 0}R(y)=1/C" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mo>lim</mo><mrow><mi>y</mi><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow></msub><mrow><mi>R</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>y</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>/</mo><mi>C</mi></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\lim_{y\to 0}R(y)=1/C</annotation></semantics></math>.
Since <math id="A1.SS8.SSS2.Px4.p2.m10" class="ltx_Math" alttext="R(y)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>R</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>y</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">R(y)</annotation></semantics></math> is continuous on <math id="A1.SS8.SSS2.Px4.p2.m11" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(0,1]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>1</mn><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(0,1]</annotation></semantics></math> with finite boundary limits, it is uniformly bounded by some constant <math id="A1.SS8.SSS2.Px4.p2.m12" class="ltx_Math" alttext="C_{R}&lt;\infty" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>C</mi><mi>R</mi></msub><mo>&lt;</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">∞</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">C_{R}&lt;\infty</annotation></semantics></math>. Thus,</p>
<table id="A1.Ex107" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A1.Ex107.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(II)\leq C_{R}\int_{0}^{1}f_{\bm{P}}(y){\mathrm{d}}y=C_{R}." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>I</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>I</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>≤</mo><mrow><msub><mi>C</mi><mi>R</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><msubsup><mo>∫</mo><mn>0</mn><mn>1</mn></msubsup><mrow><msub><mi>f</mi><mi>𝑷</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>y</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo rspace="0em">𝑑</mo><mi>y</mi></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><msub><mi>C</mi><mi>R</mi></msub></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(II)\leq C_{R}\int_{0}^{1}f_{\bm{P}}(y){\mathrm{d}}y=C_{R}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
<div id="A1.SS8.SSS2.Px4.p3" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A1.SS8.SSS2.Px4.p3.1" class="ltx_p">Next, we analyze the term (I). Since <math id="A1.SS8.SSS2.Px4.p3.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="P_{w}&lt;1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>P</mi><mi>w</mi></msub><mo>&lt;</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">P_{w}&lt;1</annotation></semantics></math> for any <math id="A1.SS8.SSS2.Px4.p3.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\bm{P}\in\mathcal{P}_{\Delta}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>𝑷</mi><mo>∈</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒫</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\bm{P}\in\mathcal{P}_{\Delta}</annotation></semantics></math>, we have <math id="A1.SS8.SSS2.Px4.p3.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="f_{\bm{P}}^{\prime}(y)=\sum_{w}(1/P_{w}-1)y^{1/P_{w}-2}&gt;0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msubsup><mi>f</mi><mi>𝑷</mi><mo>′</mo></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>y</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.111em">=</mo><mrow><msub><mo rspace="0em">∑</mo><mi>w</mi></msub><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>/</mo><msub><mi>P</mi><mi>w</mi></msub></mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>y</mi><mrow><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>/</mo><msub><mi>P</mi><mi>w</mi></msub></mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></msup></mrow></mrow><mo>&gt;</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">f_{\bm{P}}^{\prime}(y)=\sum_{w}(1/P_{w}-1)y^{1/P_{w}-2}&gt;0</annotation></semantics></math>, so the absolute value can be removed. Integration by parts gives</p>
<table id="A1.Ex108" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A1.Ex108.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(I)=\int_{0}^{1}\frac{f_{\bm{P}}^{\prime}(y)}{h^{\prime}(y)}{\mathrm{d}}y=\left[\frac{f_{\bm{P}}(y)}{h^{\prime}(y)}\right]_{0}^{1}+\int_{0}^{1}f_{\bm{P}}(y)\frac{h^{\prime\prime}(y)}{(h^{\prime}(y))^{2}}dy." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>I</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo rspace="0.111em">=</mo><mrow><msubsup><mo>∫</mo><mn>0</mn><mn>1</mn></msubsup><mrow><mfrac><mrow><msubsup><mi>f</mi><mi>𝑷</mi><mo>′</mo></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>y</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mrow><msup><mi>h</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>y</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mfrac><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo rspace="0em">𝑑</mo><mi>y</mi></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><msubsup><mrow><mo>[</mo><mfrac><mrow><msub><mi>f</mi><mi>𝑷</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>y</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mrow><msup><mi>h</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>y</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mfrac><mo>]</mo></mrow><mn>0</mn><mn>1</mn></msubsup><mo rspace="0.055em">+</mo><mrow><msubsup><mo>∫</mo><mn>0</mn><mn>1</mn></msubsup><mrow><msub><mi>f</mi><mi>𝑷</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>y</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mfrac><mrow><msup><mi>h</mi><mo>′′</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>y</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msup><mi>h</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>y</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup></mfrac><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo rspace="0em">𝑑</mo><mi>y</mi></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(I)=\int_{0}^{1}\frac{f_{\bm{P}}^{\prime}(y)}{h^{\prime}(y)}{\mathrm{d}}y=\left[\frac{f_{\bm{P}}(y)}{h^{\prime}(y)}\right]_{0}^{1}+\int_{0}^{1}f_{\bm{P}}(y)\frac{h^{\prime\prime}(y)}{(h^{\prime}(y))^{2}}dy.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A1.SS8.SSS2.Px4.p3.2" class="ltx_p">At <math id="A1.SS8.SSS2.Px4.p3.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="y=1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>y</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">y=1</annotation></semantics></math>, <math id="A1.SS8.SSS2.Px4.p3.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="f_{\bm{P}}(1)=|{{\mathcal{W}}}|" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>f</mi><mi>𝑷</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>1</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒲</mi><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">f_{\bm{P}}(1)=|{{\mathcal{W}}}|</annotation></semantics></math>.
As <math id="A1.SS8.SSS2.Px4.p3.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="y\to 0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>y</mi><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">y\to 0</annotation></semantics></math>, using <math id="A1.SS8.SSS2.Px4.p3.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="h^{\prime}(y)\sim C/y" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msup><mi>h</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>y</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>∼</mo><mrow><mi>C</mi><mo>/</mo><mi>y</mi></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">h^{\prime}(y)\sim C/y</annotation></semantics></math>,</p>
<table id="A1.Ex109" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A1.Ex109.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\lim_{y\to 0}\frac{f_{\bm{P}}(y)}{h^{\prime}(y)}=\frac{1}{C}\lim_{y\to 0}\sum_{w}y^{1/P_{w}}=0." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><munder><mo movablelimits="false">lim</mo><mrow><mi>y</mi><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow></munder><mfrac><mrow><msub><mi>f</mi><mi>𝑷</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>y</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mrow><msup><mi>h</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>y</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mfrac></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mi>C</mi></mfrac><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><munder><mo movablelimits="false" rspace="0em">lim</mo><mrow><mi>y</mi><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow></munder><mrow><munder><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mi>w</mi></munder><msup><mi>y</mi><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>/</mo><msub><mi>P</mi><mi>w</mi></msub></mrow></msup></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\lim_{y\to 0}\frac{f_{\bm{P}}(y)}{h^{\prime}(y)}=\frac{1}{C}\lim_{y\to 0}\sum_{w}y^{1/P_{w}}=0.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A1.SS8.SSS2.Px4.p3.3" class="ltx_p">The integral term is bounded in magnitude by (II). Hence,</p>
<table id="A1.Ex110" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A1.Ex110.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(I)\leq\frac{|{{\mathcal{W}}}|}{h^{\prime}(1)}+C_{R}=\frac{2|{{\mathcal{W}}}|}{C+1/C}+C_{R}." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>I</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>≤</mo><mrow><mfrac><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒲</mi><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow><mrow><msup><mi>h</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>1</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mfrac><mo>+</mo><msub><mi>C</mi><mi>R</mi></msub></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mfrac><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒲</mi><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow></mrow><mrow><mi>C</mi><mo>+</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>/</mo><mi>C</mi></mrow></mrow></mfrac><mo>+</mo><msub><mi>C</mi><mi>R</mi></msub></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(I)\leq\frac{|{{\mathcal{W}}}|}{h^{\prime}(1)}+C_{R}=\frac{2|{{\mathcal{W}}}|}{C+1/C}+C_{R}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A1.SS8.SSS2.Px4.p3.4" class="ltx_p">Combining the bounds for (I) and (II) yields</p>
<table id="A1.Ex111" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A1.Ex111.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathrm{TV}(\rho_{\bm{P}})\leq\frac{2|{{\mathcal{W}}}|}{C+1/C}+2C_{R}\leq|{{\mathcal{W}}}|+2C_{R}" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>TV</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>ρ</mi><mi>𝑷</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>≤</mo><mrow><mfrac><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒲</mi><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow></mrow><mrow><mi>C</mi><mo>+</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>/</mo><mi>C</mi></mrow></mrow></mfrac><mo>+</mo><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>C</mi><mi>R</mi></msub></mrow></mrow><mo>≤</mo><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒲</mi><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>C</mi><mi>R</mi></msub></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathrm{TV}(\rho_{\bm{P}})\leq\frac{2|{{\mathcal{W}}}|}{C+1/C}+2C_{R}\leq|{{\mathcal{W}}}|+2C_{R}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A1.SS8.SSS2.Px4.p3.5" class="ltx_p">which is finite and uniform over <math id="A1.SS8.SSS2.Px4.p3.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\bm{P}\in\mathcal{P}_{\Delta}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>𝑷</mi><mo>∈</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒫</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\bm{P}\in\mathcal{P}_{\Delta}</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>
</div>
<div id="A1.SS8.SSS2.Px4.p4" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A1.SS8.SSS2.Px4.p4.1" class="ltx_p">In both cases, <math id="A1.SS8.SSS2.Px4.p4.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathrm{TV}(\rho_{\bm{P}})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>TV</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>ρ</mi><mi>𝑷</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathrm{TV}(\rho_{\bm{P}})</annotation></semantics></math> is finite and bounded by a multiple of <math id="A1.SS8.SSS2.Px4.p4.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="|{{\mathcal{W}}}|" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒲</mi><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">|{{\mathcal{W}}}|</annotation></semantics></math>, completing the proof.
∎</p>
</div>
</section>
</section>
</section>
</section>
<section id="A2" class="ltx_appendix">
<h2 class="ltx_title ltx_title_appendix"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_appendix">Appendix B </span>Proof for Gumbel-max Watermarks in Section <a href="#S4" title="4 Application to the Gumbel-max Watermark ‣ Optimal Detection for Language Watermarks with Pseudorandom Collision" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">4</span></a></h2>

<section id="A2.SS1" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection">B.1 </span>Proof of Lemma <a href="#S4.Thmlem1" title="Lemma 4.1. ‣ 4 Application to the Gumbel-max Watermark ‣ Optimal Detection for Language Watermarks with Pseudorandom Collision" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">4.1</span></a></h3>

<div id="A2.SS1.2" class="ltx_proof">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_font_italic ltx_title_proof">Proof of Lemma <a href="#S4.Thmlem1" title="Lemma 4.1. ‣ 4 Application to the Gumbel-max Watermark ‣ Optimal Detection for Language Watermarks with Pseudorandom Collision" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">4.1</span></a>.</h6>
<div id="A2.SS1.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A2.SS1.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A2.SS1.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text">We assert that <math id="A2.SS1.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="Y_{t_{1}}=\cdots=Y_{t_{k}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>Y</mi><msub><mi>t</mi><mn>1</mn></msub></msub><mo rspace="0.1389em">=</mo><mo lspace="0.1389em" rspace="0.1389em">⋯</mo><mo lspace="0.1389em">=</mo><msub><mi>Y</mi><msub><mi>t</mi><mi>k</mi></msub></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">Y_{t_{1}}=\cdots=Y_{t_{k}}</annotation></semantics></math> if and only if <math id="A2.SS1.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="w_{t_{1}}=\cdots=w_{t_{k}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>w</mi><msub><mi>t</mi><mn>1</mn></msub></msub><mo rspace="0.1389em">=</mo><mo lspace="0.1389em" rspace="0.1389em">⋯</mo><mo lspace="0.1389em">=</mo><msub><mi>w</mi><msub><mi>t</mi><mi>k</mi></msub></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">w_{t_{1}}=\cdots=w_{t_{k}}</annotation></semantics></math>. This follows from the fact that if <math id="A2.SS1.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="w_{t_{1}}\neq w_{t_{2}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>w</mi><msub><mi>t</mi><mn>1</mn></msub></msub><mo>≠</mo><msub><mi>w</mi><msub><mi>t</mi><mn>2</mn></msub></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">w_{t_{1}}\neq w_{t_{2}}</annotation></semantics></math>, then <math id="A2.SS1.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="Y_{t_{1}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>Y</mi><msub><mi>t</mi><mn>1</mn></msub></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">Y_{t_{1}}</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="A2.SS1.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="Y_{t_{2}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>Y</mi><msub><mi>t</mi><mn>2</mn></msub></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">Y_{t_{2}}</annotation></semantics></math> are independent by Assumption <a href="#S3.Thmasmp2" title="Assumption 3.2 (Independence across sub-blocks). ‣ Two-level partitions. ‣ 3.1 Structural Dependence and Distribution Factorization ‣ 3 A Statistical Framework under Pseudorandomness Collision ‣ Optimal Detection for Language Watermarks with Pseudorandom Collision" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">3.2</span></a>. Since each <math id="A2.SS1.p1.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="Y_{t}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>Y</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">Y_{t}</annotation></semantics></math> has a smooth CDF, the probability <math id="A2.SS1.p1.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="{\mathbb{P}}_{1}(Y_{t_{1}}=Y_{t_{2}}\mid w_{t_{1}}\neq w_{t_{2}})=0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>ℙ</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>Y</mi><msub><mi>t</mi><mn>1</mn></msub></msub><mo>=</mo><msub><mi>Y</mi><msub><mi>t</mi><mn>2</mn></msub></msub></mrow><mo fence="true" lspace="0em" rspace="0em">∣</mo><mrow><msub><mi>w</mi><msub><mi>t</mi><mn>1</mn></msub></msub><mo>≠</mo><msub><mi>w</mi><msub><mi>t</mi><mn>2</mn></msub></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\mathbb{P}}_{1}(Y_{t_{1}}=Y_{t_{2}}\mid w_{t_{1}}\neq w_{t_{2}})=0</annotation></semantics></math>, making such an event almost surely impossible.</span></p>
</div>
<div id="A2.SS1.p2" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A2.SS1.p2.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A2.SS1.p2.1.1" class="ltx_text">Recall that the NTP distribution for <math id="A2.SS1.p2.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="w_{t_{i}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>w</mi><msub><mi>t</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">w_{t_{i}}</annotation></semantics></math> is given by <math id="A2.SS1.p2.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\bm{P}_{t_{i}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>𝑷</mi><msub><mi>t</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\bm{P}_{t_{i}}</annotation></semantics></math>. Since the same pseudorandom variable is used to generate all <math id="A2.SS1.p2.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="w_{t_{i}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>w</mi><msub><mi>t</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">w_{t_{i}}</annotation></semantics></math> for <math id="A2.SS1.p2.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="t_{i}\in{\mathcal{V}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>t</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>∈</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒱</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">t_{i}\in{\mathcal{V}}</annotation></semantics></math>, we denote it by <math id="A2.SS1.p2.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\zeta=(U_{w})_{w\in{{\mathcal{W}}}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>ζ</mi><mo>=</mo><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>U</mi><mi>w</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mrow><mi>w</mi><mo>∈</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒲</mi></mrow></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\zeta=(U_{w})_{w\in{{\mathcal{W}}}}</annotation></semantics></math>. Consequently, each token satisfies <math id="A2.SS1.p2.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="w_{t_{i}}={\mathcal{S}}(\bm{P}_{t_{i}},\zeta)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>w</mi><msub><mi>t</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></msub><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒮</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>𝑷</mi><msub><mi>t</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></msub><mo>,</mo><mi>ζ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">w_{t_{i}}={\mathcal{S}}(\bm{P}_{t_{i}},\zeta)</annotation></semantics></math> for all <math id="A2.SS1.p2.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="t_{i}\in{\mathcal{V}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>t</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>∈</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒱</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">t_{i}\in{\mathcal{V}}</annotation></semantics></math>.
Under the event <math id="A2.SS1.p2.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="Y_{t_{1}}=\cdots=Y_{t_{k}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>Y</mi><msub><mi>t</mi><mn>1</mn></msub></msub><mo rspace="0.1389em">=</mo><mo lspace="0.1389em" rspace="0.1389em">⋯</mo><mo lspace="0.1389em">=</mo><msub><mi>Y</mi><msub><mi>t</mi><mi>k</mi></msub></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">Y_{t_{1}}=\cdots=Y_{t_{k}}</annotation></semantics></math>, we define <math id="A2.SS1.p2.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="w_{t_{1}}=\cdots=w_{t_{k}}=w" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>w</mi><msub><mi>t</mi><mn>1</mn></msub></msub><mo rspace="0.1389em">=</mo><mo lspace="0.1389em" rspace="0.1389em">⋯</mo><mo lspace="0.1389em">=</mo><msub><mi>w</mi><msub><mi>t</mi><mi>k</mi></msub></msub><mo>=</mo><mi>w</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">w_{t_{1}}=\cdots=w_{t_{k}}=w</annotation></semantics></math>. This implies that <math id="A2.SS1.p2.m10" class="ltx_Math" alttext="w={\mathcal{S}}(\bm{P}_{t},\zeta)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>w</mi><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒮</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>𝑷</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><mi>ζ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">w={\mathcal{S}}(\bm{P}_{t},\zeta)</annotation></semantics></math> for all <math id="A2.SS1.p2.m11" class="ltx_Math" alttext="t\in{\mathcal{V}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>∈</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒱</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">t\in{\mathcal{V}}</annotation></semantics></math>.
Therefore, it follows that</span></p>
<table id="A2.EGx47" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A2.Ex112"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A2.Ex112.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\displaystyle{\mathbb{P}}_{1}(Y_{t_{1}}\leq y~|~Y_{t_{1}}=\cdots=Y_{t_{k}},\bm{P}_{{\mathcal{V}}})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>ℙ</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>Y</mi><msub><mi>t</mi><mn>1</mn></msub></msub><mo>≤</mo><mi>y</mi><mo fence="false" lspace="0.330em" rspace="0.497em" stretchy="false">|</mo><msub><mi>Y</mi><msub><mi>t</mi><mn>1</mn></msub></msub><mo rspace="0.1389em">=</mo><mo lspace="0.1389em" rspace="0.1389em">⋯</mo><mo lspace="0.1389em">=</mo><msub><mi>Y</mi><msub><mi>t</mi><mi>k</mi></msub></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>𝑷</mi><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒱</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle{\mathbb{P}}_{1}(Y_{t_{1}}\leq y~|~Y_{t_{1}}=\cdots=Y_{t_{k}},\bm{P}_{{\mathcal{V}}})</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A2.Ex112.m2" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\displaystyle={\mathbb{P}}_{1}(Y_{t_{1}}\leq y,~w_{t_{1}}=\cdots=w_{t_{k}}|\,Y_{t_{1}}=\cdots=Y_{t_{k}},\bm{P}_{{\mathcal{V}}})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo>=</mo><msub><mi>ℙ</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>Y</mi><msub><mi>t</mi><mn>1</mn></msub></msub><mo>≤</mo><mi>y</mi><mo rspace="0.497em">,</mo><msub><mi>w</mi><msub><mi>t</mi><mn>1</mn></msub></msub><mo rspace="0.1389em">=</mo><mo lspace="0.1389em" rspace="0.1389em">⋯</mo><mo lspace="0.1389em">=</mo><msub><mi>w</mi><msub><mi>t</mi><mi>k</mi></msub></msub><mo fence="false" rspace="0.337em" stretchy="false">|</mo><msub><mi>Y</mi><msub><mi>t</mi><mn>1</mn></msub></msub><mo rspace="0.1389em">=</mo><mo lspace="0.1389em" rspace="0.1389em">⋯</mo><mo lspace="0.1389em">=</mo><msub><mi>Y</mi><msub><mi>t</mi><mi>k</mi></msub></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>𝑷</mi><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒱</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle={\mathbb{P}}_{1}(Y_{t_{1}}\leq y,~w_{t_{1}}=\cdots=w_{t_{k}}|\,Y_{t_{1}}=\cdots=Y_{t_{k}},\bm{P}_{{\mathcal{V}}})</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A2.Ex113"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A2.Ex113.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\displaystyle=\sum_{w\in{{\mathcal{W}}}}{\mathbb{P}}_{1}(Y_{t_{1}}\leq y,~w_{t_{1}}=\cdots=w_{t_{k}}=w|\,Y_{t_{1}}=\cdots=Y_{t_{k}},\bm{P}_{{\mathcal{V}}})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo>=</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munder><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>w</mi><mo>∈</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒲</mi></mrow></munder></mstyle><msub><mi>ℙ</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>Y</mi><msub><mi>t</mi><mn>1</mn></msub></msub><mo>≤</mo><mi>y</mi><mo rspace="0.497em">,</mo><msub><mi>w</mi><msub><mi>t</mi><mn>1</mn></msub></msub><mo rspace="0.1389em">=</mo><mo lspace="0.1389em" rspace="0.1389em">⋯</mo><mo lspace="0.1389em">=</mo><msub><mi>w</mi><msub><mi>t</mi><mi>k</mi></msub></msub><mo>=</mo><mi>w</mi><mo fence="false" rspace="0.337em" stretchy="false">|</mo><msub><mi>Y</mi><msub><mi>t</mi><mn>1</mn></msub></msub><mo rspace="0.1389em">=</mo><mo lspace="0.1389em" rspace="0.1389em">⋯</mo><mo lspace="0.1389em">=</mo><msub><mi>Y</mi><msub><mi>t</mi><mi>k</mi></msub></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>𝑷</mi><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒱</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=\sum_{w\in{{\mathcal{W}}}}{\mathbb{P}}_{1}(Y_{t_{1}}\leq y,~w_{t_{1}}=\cdots=w_{t_{k}}=w|\,Y_{t_{1}}=\cdots=Y_{t_{k}},\bm{P}_{{\mathcal{V}}})</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A2.Ex114"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A2.Ex114.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\displaystyle=\sum_{w\in{{\mathcal{W}}}}{\mathbb{P}}_{1}(Y(w,\zeta)\leq y~|~w={\mathcal{S}}(\bm{P}_{t},\zeta),~\forall t\in{\mathcal{V}})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo>=</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munder><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>w</mi><mo>∈</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒲</mi></mrow></munder></mstyle><msub><mi>ℙ</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>Y</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>w</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>ζ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>≤</mo><mi>y</mi><mo fence="false" lspace="0.330em" rspace="0.497em" stretchy="false">|</mo><mi>w</mi><mo>=</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒮</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>𝑷</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><mi>ζ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo rspace="0.497em">,</mo><mo rspace="0.167em">∀</mo><mi>t</mi><mo>∈</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒱</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=\sum_{w\in{{\mathcal{W}}}}{\mathbb{P}}_{1}(Y(w,\zeta)\leq y~|~w={\mathcal{S}}(\bm{P}_{t},\zeta),~\forall t\in{\mathcal{V}})</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A2.Ex115"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A2.Ex115.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\displaystyle=\sum_{w\in{{\mathcal{W}}}}{\mathbb{P}}_{1}\left(U_{w}\leq y~\Big|~U_{w^{\prime}}\leq U_{{w}}^{\max_{t\in{\mathcal{V}}}\left(\frac{P_{t,w^{\prime}}}{P_{t,w}}\right)},\forall w^{\prime}\neq{w}\right)." display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo>=</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munder><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>w</mi><mo>∈</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒲</mi></mrow></munder></mstyle><msub><mi>ℙ</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mrow><mo>(</mo><msub><mi>U</mi><mi>w</mi></msub><mo>≤</mo><mi>y</mi><mo fence="false" lspace="0.330em" maxsize="1.600em" minsize="1.600em" rspace="0.497em" stretchy="true">|</mo><msub><mi>U</mi><msup><mi>w</mi><mo>′</mo></msup></msub><mo>≤</mo><msubsup><mi>U</mi><mi>w</mi><mrow><msub><mi>max</mi><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>∈</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒱</mi></mrow></msub><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mfrac><msub><mi>P</mi><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>,</mo><msup><mi>w</mi><mo>′</mo></msup></mrow></msub><msub><mi>P</mi><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>w</mi></mrow></msub></mfrac><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow></msubsup><mo>,</mo><mo rspace="0.167em">∀</mo><msup><mi>w</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo>≠</mo><mi>w</mi><mo>)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=\sum_{w\in{{\mathcal{W}}}}{\mathbb{P}}_{1}\left(U_{w}\leq y~\Big|~U_{w^{\prime}}\leq U_{{w}}^{\max_{t\in{\mathcal{V}}}\left(\frac{P_{t,w^{\prime}}}{P_{t,w}}\right)},\forall w^{\prime}\neq{w}\right).</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A2.SS1.p2.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="A2.SS1.p2.2.1" class="ltx_text">Given that <math id="A2.SS1.p2.m12" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\{U_{w}\}_{w\in{{\mathcal{W}}}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><msub><mi>U</mi><mi>w</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow><mrow><mi>w</mi><mo>∈</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒲</mi></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\{U_{w}\}_{w\in{{\mathcal{W}}}}</annotation></semantics></math> are i.i.d. <math id="A2.SS1.p2.m13" class="ltx_Math" alttext="{U}(0,1)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>U</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>1</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{U}(0,1)</annotation></semantics></math>, direct calculation yields that</span></p>
<table id="A2.EGx48" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A2.Ex116"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A2.Ex116.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\displaystyle{\mathbb{P}}_{1}\left(U_{w}\leq y,U_{w^{\prime}}\leq U_{{w}}^{\max_{t\in{\mathcal{V}}}\left(\frac{P_{t,w^{\prime}}}{P_{t,w}}\right)},\forall w^{\prime}\neq{w}\right)=S_{w}y^{1/S_{w}}." display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>ℙ</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mrow><mo>(</mo><msub><mi>U</mi><mi>w</mi></msub><mo>≤</mo><mi>y</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>U</mi><msup><mi>w</mi><mo>′</mo></msup></msub><mo>≤</mo><msubsup><mi>U</mi><mi>w</mi><mrow><msub><mi>max</mi><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>∈</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒱</mi></mrow></msub><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mfrac><msub><mi>P</mi><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>,</mo><msup><mi>w</mi><mo>′</mo></msup></mrow></msub><msub><mi>P</mi><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>w</mi></mrow></msub></mfrac><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow></msubsup><mo>,</mo><mo rspace="0.167em">∀</mo><msup><mi>w</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo>≠</mo><mi>w</mi><mo>)</mo></mrow><mo>=</mo><msub><mi>S</mi><mi>w</mi></msub><msup><mi>y</mi><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>/</mo><msub><mi>S</mi><mi>w</mi></msub></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle{\mathbb{P}}_{1}\left(U_{w}\leq y,U_{w^{\prime}}\leq U_{{w}}^{\max_{t\in{\mathcal{V}}}\left(\frac{P_{t,w^{\prime}}}{P_{t,w}}\right)},\forall w^{\prime}\neq{w}\right)=S_{w}y^{1/S_{w}}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A2.SS1.p2.3" class="ltx_p"><span id="A2.SS1.p2.3.1" class="ltx_text">As a result, it follows from Bayes’ theorem that</span></p>
<table id="A2.Ex117" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A2.Ex117.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="{\mathbb{P}}_{1}\left(U_{w}\leq y~\Big|~U_{w^{\prime}}\leq U_{{w}}^{\max_{t\in{\mathcal{V}}}\left(\frac{P_{t,w^{\prime}}}{P_{t,w}}\right)},\forall w^{\prime}\neq{w}\right)=\frac{S_{w}y^{1/S_{w}}}{\sum_{w^{\prime}\in{{\mathcal{W}}}}S_{w^{\prime}}}." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>ℙ</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mrow><mo>(</mo><msub><mi>U</mi><mi>w</mi></msub><mo>≤</mo><mi>y</mi><mo fence="false" lspace="0.330em" maxsize="1.600em" minsize="1.600em" rspace="0.497em" stretchy="true">|</mo><msub><mi>U</mi><msup><mi>w</mi><mo>′</mo></msup></msub><mo>≤</mo><msubsup><mi>U</mi><mi>w</mi><mrow><msub><mi>max</mi><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>∈</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒱</mi></mrow></msub><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mfrac><msub><mi>P</mi><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>,</mo><msup><mi>w</mi><mo>′</mo></msup></mrow></msub><msub><mi>P</mi><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>w</mi></mrow></msub></mfrac><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow></msubsup><mo>,</mo><mo rspace="0.167em">∀</mo><msup><mi>w</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo>≠</mo><mi>w</mi><mo>)</mo></mrow><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mrow><msub><mi>S</mi><mi>w</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>y</mi><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>/</mo><msub><mi>S</mi><mi>w</mi></msub></mrow></msup></mrow><mrow><msub><mo>∑</mo><mrow><msup><mi>w</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo>∈</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒲</mi></mrow></msub><msub><mi>S</mi><msup><mi>w</mi><mo>′</mo></msup></msub></mrow></mfrac><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\mathbb{P}}_{1}\left(U_{w}\leq y~\Big|~U_{w^{\prime}}\leq U_{{w}}^{\max_{t\in{\mathcal{V}}}\left(\frac{P_{t,w^{\prime}}}{P_{t,w}}\right)},\forall w^{\prime}\neq{w}\right)=\frac{S_{w}y^{1/S_{w}}}{\sum_{w^{\prime}\in{{\mathcal{W}}}}S_{w^{\prime}}}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A2.SS1.p2.4" class="ltx_p"><span id="A2.SS1.p2.4.1" class="ltx_text">Summing the last probability over all <math id="A2.SS1.p2.m14" class="ltx_Math" alttext="w\in{{\mathcal{W}}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>w</mi><mo>∈</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒲</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">w\in{{\mathcal{W}}}</annotation></semantics></math> completes the proof.
∎</span></p>
</div>
</div>
</section>
<section id="A2.SS2" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection">B.2 </span>Proof of Lemma <a href="#S7.Thmlem1" title="Lemma 7.1 (Necessity of optimal score functions). ‣ 7.1 Proof of Theorem ‣ 7 Proof of Main Results ‣ Optimal Detection for Language Watermarks with Pseudorandom Collision" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">7.1</span></a></h3>

<div id="A2.SS2.2" class="ltx_proof">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_font_italic ltx_title_proof">Proof of Lemma <a href="#S7.Thmlem1" title="Lemma 7.1 (Necessity of optimal score functions). ‣ 7.1 Proof of Theorem ‣ 7 Proof of Main Results ‣ Optimal Detection for Language Watermarks with Pseudorandom Collision" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">7.1</span></a>.</h6>
<div id="A2.SS2.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A2.SS2.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A2.SS2.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Proof of the “if” direction.<span id="A2.SS2.p1.1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_medium">
If there exists a vector <math id="A2.SS2.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="{\bm{S}}^{\star}\in{\mathcal{D}}_{\Delta}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msup><mi>𝑺</mi><mo>⋆</mo></msup><mo>∈</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒟</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\bm{S}}^{\star}\in{\mathcal{D}}_{\Delta}</annotation></semantics></math> such that</span></span></p>
<table id="A2.Ex118" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A2.Ex118.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\max_{{\bm{S}}\in{\mathcal{D}}_{\Delta}}L(h_{{\bm{S}}^{\star}},{\bm{S}})=L(h_{{\bm{S}}^{\star}},{\bm{S}}^{\star})," display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><munder><mi>max</mi><mrow><mi>𝑺</mi><mo>∈</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒟</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi></msub></mrow></munder><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><mrow><mi>L</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>h</mi><msup><mi>𝑺</mi><mo>⋆</mo></msup></msub><mo>,</mo><mi>𝑺</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>L</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>h</mi><msup><mi>𝑺</mi><mo>⋆</mo></msup></msub><mo>,</mo><msup><mi>𝑺</mi><mo>⋆</mo></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\max_{{\bm{S}}\in{\mathcal{D}}_{\Delta}}L(h_{{\bm{S}}^{\star}},{\bm{S}})=L(h_{{\bm{S}}^{\star}},{\bm{S}}^{\star}),</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(<a href="#S7.E27" title="In Lemma 7.1 (Necessity of optimal score functions). ‣ 7.1 Proof of Theorem ‣ 7 Proof of Main Results ‣ Optimal Detection for Language Watermarks with Pseudorandom Collision" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">27</span></a>)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A2.SS2.p1.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="A2.SS2.p1.2.1" class="ltx_text">on the one hand, it follows from the Donsker–Varadhan representation that</span></p>
<table id="A2.Ex119" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A2.Ex119.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\min_{h}\max_{{\bm{S}}\in{\mathcal{D}}_{\Delta}}L(h,{\bm{S}})\geq\min_{h}L(h,{\bm{S}}^{\star})=-\mathrm{KL}(F_{0}\|F_{{\bm{S}}^{\star}})." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><munder><mi>min</mi><mi>h</mi></munder><munder><mi>max</mi><mrow><mi>𝑺</mi><mo>∈</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒟</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi></msub></mrow></munder><mi>L</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>h</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>𝑺</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>≥</mo><munder><mi>min</mi><mi>h</mi></munder><mi>L</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>h</mi><mo>,</mo><msup><mi>𝑺</mi><mo>⋆</mo></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo rspace="0em">=</mo><mo lspace="0em">−</mo><mi>KL</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>F</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.167em">∥</mo><msub><mi>F</mi><msup><mi>𝑺</mi><mo>⋆</mo></msup></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\min_{h}\max_{{\bm{S}}\in{\mathcal{D}}_{\Delta}}L(h,{\bm{S}})\geq\min_{h}L(h,{\bm{S}}^{\star})=-\mathrm{KL}(F_{0}\|F_{{\bm{S}}^{\star}}).</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A2.SS2.p1.3" class="ltx_p"><span id="A2.SS2.p1.3.1" class="ltx_text">On the other hand, by the condition (<a href="#S7.E27" title="In Lemma 7.1 (Necessity of optimal score functions). ‣ 7.1 Proof of Theorem ‣ 7 Proof of Main Results ‣ Optimal Detection for Language Watermarks with Pseudorandom Collision" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">27</span></a>), it follows that</span></p>
<table id="A2.EGx49" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A2.Ex120"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A2.Ex120.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\displaystyle\min_{h}\max_{{\bm{S}}\in{\mathcal{D}}_{\Delta}}L(h,{\bm{S}})\leq\max_{{\bm{S}}\in{\mathcal{D}}_{\Delta}}L(h_{{\bm{S}}^{\star}},{\bm{S}})=L(h_{{\bm{S}}^{\star}},{\bm{S}}^{\star})=-\mathrm{KL}(F_{0}\|F_{{\bm{S}}^{\star}})." display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><munder><mi>min</mi><mi>h</mi></munder><munder><mi>max</mi><mrow><mi>𝑺</mi><mo>∈</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒟</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi></msub></mrow></munder><mi>L</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>h</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>𝑺</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>≤</mo><munder><mi>max</mi><mrow><mi>𝑺</mi><mo>∈</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒟</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi></msub></mrow></munder><mi>L</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>h</mi><msup><mi>𝑺</mi><mo>⋆</mo></msup></msub><mo>,</mo><mi>𝑺</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>=</mo><mi>L</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>h</mi><msup><mi>𝑺</mi><mo>⋆</mo></msup></msub><mo>,</mo><msup><mi>𝑺</mi><mo>⋆</mo></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo rspace="0em">=</mo><mo lspace="0em">−</mo><mi>KL</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>F</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.167em">∥</mo><msub><mi>F</mi><msup><mi>𝑺</mi><mo>⋆</mo></msup></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\min_{h}\max_{{\bm{S}}\in{\mathcal{D}}_{\Delta}}L(h,{\bm{S}})\leq\max_{{\bm{S}}\in{\mathcal{D}}_{\Delta}}L(h_{{\bm{S}}^{\star}},{\bm{S}})=L(h_{{\bm{S}}^{\star}},{\bm{S}}^{\star})=-\mathrm{KL}(F_{0}\|F_{{\bm{S}}^{\star}}).</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A2.SS2.p1.4" class="ltx_p"><span id="A2.SS2.p1.4.1" class="ltx_text">Combining the above two directions, we know that <math id="A2.SS2.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(h_{{\bm{S}}^{\star}},{\bm{S}}^{\star})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>h</mi><msup><mi>𝑺</mi><mo>⋆</mo></msup></msub><mo>,</mo><msup><mi>𝑺</mi><mo>⋆</mo></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(h_{{\bm{S}}^{\star}},{\bm{S}}^{\star})</annotation></semantics></math> is a solution pair of the minimax problem (<a href="#S7.E26" title="In 7.1 Proof of Theorem ‣ 7 Proof of Main Results ‣ Optimal Detection for Language Watermarks with Pseudorandom Collision" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">26</span></a>).</span></p>
</div>
<div id="A2.SS2.p2" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A2.SS2.p2.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A2.SS2.p2.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Proof of the “only if” direction.<span id="A2.SS2.p2.1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_medium">
Suppose the pair <math id="A2.SS2.p2.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(h^{\star},{\bm{S}}^{\star})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>h</mi><mo>⋆</mo></msup><mo>,</mo><msup><mi>𝑺</mi><mo>⋆</mo></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(h^{\star},{\bm{S}}^{\star})</annotation></semantics></math> solves the minimax problem (<a href="#S7.E26" title="In 7.1 Proof of Theorem ‣ 7 Proof of Main Results ‣ Optimal Detection for Language Watermarks with Pseudorandom Collision" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">26</span></a>). By definition, we have</span></span></p>
<table id="A2.EGx50" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A2.Ex121"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A2.Ex121.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle L(h^{\star},{\bm{S}}^{\star})=\min_{h}\max_{{\bm{S}}\in{\mathcal{D}}_{\Delta}}L(h,{\bm{S}})=\max_{{\bm{S}}\in{\mathcal{D}}_{\Delta}}L(h^{\star},{\bm{S}})=\min_{h}L(h,{\bm{S}}^{\star})." display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>L</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>h</mi><mo>⋆</mo></msup><mo>,</mo><msup><mi>𝑺</mi><mo>⋆</mo></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><munder><mi>min</mi><mi>h</mi></munder><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><mrow><munder><mi>max</mi><mrow><mi>𝑺</mi><mo>∈</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒟</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi></msub></mrow></munder><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><mrow><mi>L</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>h</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>𝑺</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><munder><mi>max</mi><mrow><mi>𝑺</mi><mo>∈</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒟</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi></msub></mrow></munder><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><mrow><mi>L</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>h</mi><mo>⋆</mo></msup><mo>,</mo><mi>𝑺</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><munder><mi>min</mi><mi>h</mi></munder><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><mrow><mi>L</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>h</mi><mo>,</mo><msup><mi>𝑺</mi><mo>⋆</mo></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle L(h^{\star},{\bm{S}}^{\star})=\min_{h}\max_{{\bm{S}}\in{\mathcal{D}}_{\Delta}}L(h,{\bm{S}})=\max_{{\bm{S}}\in{\mathcal{D}}_{\Delta}}L(h^{\star},{\bm{S}})=\min_{h}L(h,{\bm{S}}^{\star}).</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A2.SS2.p2.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="A2.SS2.p2.2.1" class="ltx_text">The last equality holds if and only if <math id="A2.SS2.p2.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="h^{\star}=h_{{\bm{S}}^{\star}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msup><mi>h</mi><mo>⋆</mo></msup><mo>=</mo><msub><mi>h</mi><msup><mi>𝑺</mi><mo>⋆</mo></msup></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">h^{\star}=h_{{\bm{S}}^{\star}}</annotation></semantics></math> (up to a constant shift), by the Donsker–Varadhan representation. The second equality corresponds exactly to the optimality condition (<a href="#S7.E27" title="In Lemma 7.1 (Necessity of optimal score functions). ‣ 7.1 Proof of Theorem ‣ 7 Proof of Main Results ‣ Optimal Detection for Language Watermarks with Pseudorandom Collision" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">27</span></a>).</span></p>
</div>
<div id="A2.SS2.p3" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A2.SS2.p3.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A2.SS2.p3.1.1" class="ltx_text">∎</span></p>
</div>
</div>
</section>
<section id="A2.SS3" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection">B.3 </span>Proof of Lemma <a href="#S7.Thmlem2" title="Lemma 7.2 (Properties of the domain 𝒟_Δ). ‣ 7.1 Proof of Theorem ‣ 7 Proof of Main Results ‣ Optimal Detection for Language Watermarks with Pseudorandom Collision" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">7.2</span></a></h3>

<div id="A2.SS3.2" class="ltx_proof">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_font_italic ltx_title_proof">Proof of Lemma <a href="#S7.Thmlem2" title="Lemma 7.2 (Properties of the domain 𝒟_Δ). ‣ 7.1 Proof of Theorem ‣ 7 Proof of Main Results ‣ Optimal Detection for Language Watermarks with Pseudorandom Collision" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">7.2</span></a>.</h6>
<div id="A2.SS3.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A2.SS3.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A2.SS3.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text">Recall that for any <math id="A2.SS3.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="{\bm{S}}\in{\mathcal{D}}_{\Delta}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>𝑺</mi><mo>∈</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒟</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\bm{S}}\in{\mathcal{D}}_{\Delta}</annotation></semantics></math> there exists <math id="A2.SS3.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\bm{P}_{{\mathcal{V}}}\subseteq{\mathcal{P}}_{\Delta}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>𝑷</mi><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒱</mi></msub><mo>⊆</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒫</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\bm{P}_{{\mathcal{V}}}\subseteq{\mathcal{P}}_{\Delta}</annotation></semantics></math> such that for each <math id="A2.SS3.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="w\in{{\mathcal{W}}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>w</mi><mo>∈</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒲</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">w\in{{\mathcal{W}}}</annotation></semantics></math>,</span></p>
<table id="A2.E71" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A2.E71.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="S_{w}=\left(\sum_{w^{\prime}\in{{\mathcal{W}}}}\max_{t\in{\mathcal{V}}}\frac{P_{t,w^{\prime}}}{P_{t,w}}\right)^{-1}." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>S</mi><mi>w</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><msup><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><munder><mo lspace="0em" movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><msup><mi>w</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo>∈</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒲</mi></mrow></munder><mrow><munder><mi>max</mi><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>∈</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒱</mi></mrow></munder><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><mfrac><msub><mi>P</mi><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>,</mo><msup><mi>w</mi><mo>′</mo></msup></mrow></msub><msub><mi>P</mi><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>w</mi></mrow></msub></mfrac></mrow></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">S_{w}=\left(\sum_{w^{\prime}\in{{\mathcal{W}}}}\max_{t\in{\mathcal{V}}}\frac{P_{t,w^{\prime}}}{P_{t,w}}\right)^{-1}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(71)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A2.SS3.p1.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="A2.SS3.p1.2.1" class="ltx_text">According to this definition, the permutation invariance of <math id="A2.SS3.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="{\mathcal{D}}_{\Delta}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒟</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\mathcal{D}}_{\Delta}</annotation></semantics></math> follows directly by permuting the order of entries in each NTP distribution in <math id="A2.SS3.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\bm{P}_{{\mathcal{V}}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>𝑷</mi><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒱</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\bm{P}_{{\mathcal{V}}}</annotation></semantics></math>.
We now turn to prove the remaining part.
Using the fact that <math id="A2.SS3.p1.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\frac{P_{t,w^{\prime}}}{P_{t,w}}\leq\max_{t\in{\mathcal{V}}}\frac{P_{t,w^{\prime}}}{P_{t,w}}\leq\sum_{t\in{\mathcal{V}}}\frac{P_{t,w^{\prime}}}{P_{t,w}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mfrac><msub><mi>P</mi><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>,</mo><msup><mi>w</mi><mo>′</mo></msup></mrow></msub><msub><mi>P</mi><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>w</mi></mrow></msub></mfrac><mo>≤</mo><mrow><msub><mi>max</mi><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>∈</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒱</mi></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><mfrac><msub><mi>P</mi><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>,</mo><msup><mi>w</mi><mo>′</mo></msup></mrow></msub><msub><mi>P</mi><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>w</mi></mrow></msub></mfrac></mrow><mo rspace="0.111em">≤</mo><mrow><msub><mo>∑</mo><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>∈</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒱</mi></mrow></msub><mfrac><msub><mi>P</mi><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>,</mo><msup><mi>w</mi><mo>′</mo></msup></mrow></msub><msub><mi>P</mi><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>w</mi></mrow></msub></mfrac></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\frac{P_{t,w^{\prime}}}{P_{t,w}}\leq\max_{t\in{\mathcal{V}}}\frac{P_{t,w^{\prime}}}{P_{t,w}}\leq\sum_{t\in{\mathcal{V}}}\frac{P_{t,w^{\prime}}}{P_{t,w}}</annotation></semantics></math> for any <math id="A2.SS3.p1.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="t\in{\mathcal{V}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>∈</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒱</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">t\in{\mathcal{V}}</annotation></semantics></math>, we have that</span></p>
<table id="A2.E72" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A2.E72.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\left(\sum_{t\in{\mathcal{V}}}\frac{1}{P_{t,w}}-(|{\mathcal{V}}|-1)\right)^{-1}\leq S_{w}\leq\min_{t\in{\mathcal{V}}}P_{t,w}." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msup><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mrow><munder><mo lspace="0em" movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>∈</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒱</mi></mrow></munder><mfrac><mn>1</mn><msub><mi>P</mi><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>w</mi></mrow></msub></mfrac></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒱</mi><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup><mo>≤</mo><msub><mi>S</mi><mi>w</mi></msub><mo>≤</mo><mrow><munder><mi>min</mi><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>∈</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒱</mi></mrow></munder><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><msub><mi>P</mi><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>w</mi></mrow></msub></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\left(\sum_{t\in{\mathcal{V}}}\frac{1}{P_{t,w}}-(|{\mathcal{V}}|-1)\right)^{-1}\leq S_{w}\leq\min_{t\in{\mathcal{V}}}P_{t,w}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(72)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
<div id="A2.SS3.p2" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A2.SS3.p2.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A2.SS3.p2.1.1" class="ltx_text">With this result, we are now ready to prove the three bullet points.</span></p>
<ol id="A2.I1" class="ltx_enumerate">
<li id="A2.I1.ix1" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">(i)</span> 
<div id="A2.I1.ix1.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A2.I1.ix1.p1.1" class="ltx_p">By the definition in (<a href="#A2.E71" title="In Proof of Lemma . ‣ B.3 Proof of Lemma ‣ Appendix B Proof for Gumbel-max Watermarks in Section ‣ Optimal Detection for Language Watermarks with Pseudorandom Collision" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">71</span></a>), it is clear that <math id="A2.I1.ix1.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="0\leq S_{w}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mn>0</mn><mo>≤</mo><msub><mi>S</mi><mi>w</mi></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">0\leq S_{w}</annotation></semantics></math>. Using (<a href="#A2.E72" title="In Proof of Lemma . ‣ B.3 Proof of Lemma ‣ Appendix B Proof for Gumbel-max Watermarks in Section ‣ Optimal Detection for Language Watermarks with Pseudorandom Collision" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">72</span></a>), it follows that <math id="A2.I1.ix1.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="S_{w}\leq\min_{t\in{\mathcal{V}}}P_{t,w}\leq 1-\Delta" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>S</mi><mi>w</mi></msub><mo>≤</mo><mrow><msub><mi>min</mi><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>∈</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒱</mi></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><msub><mi>P</mi><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>w</mi></mrow></msub></mrow><mo>≤</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">S_{w}\leq\min_{t\in{\mathcal{V}}}P_{t,w}\leq 1-\Delta</annotation></semantics></math> due to <math id="A2.I1.ix1.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\bm{P}_{{\mathcal{V}}}\subseteq{\mathcal{P}}_{\Delta}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>𝑷</mi><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒱</mi></msub><mo>⊆</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒫</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\bm{P}_{{\mathcal{V}}}\subseteq{\mathcal{P}}_{\Delta}</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>
</div></li>
<li id="A2.I1.ix2" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">(ii)</span> 
<div id="A2.I1.ix2.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A2.I1.ix2.p1.1" class="ltx_p">By (<a href="#A2.E72" title="In Proof of Lemma . ‣ B.3 Proof of Lemma ‣ Appendix B Proof for Gumbel-max Watermarks in Section ‣ Optimal Detection for Language Watermarks with Pseudorandom Collision" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">72</span></a>), we have that <math id="A2.I1.ix2.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\sum_{w}S_{w}\leq\sum_{w}\min_{t\in{\mathcal{V}}}P_{t,w}\leq\sum_{w}P_{t,w}=1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mo>∑</mo><mi>w</mi></msub><msub><mi>S</mi><mi>w</mi></msub></mrow><mo rspace="0.111em">≤</mo><mrow><msub><mo>∑</mo><mi>w</mi></msub><mrow><msub><mi>min</mi><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>∈</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒱</mi></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><msub><mi>P</mi><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>w</mi></mrow></msub></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.111em">≤</mo><mrow><msub><mo>∑</mo><mi>w</mi></msub><msub><mi>P</mi><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>w</mi></mrow></msub></mrow><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\sum_{w}S_{w}\leq\sum_{w}\min_{t\in{\mathcal{V}}}P_{t,w}\leq\sum_{w}P_{t,w}=1</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>
</div></li>
<li id="A2.I1.ix3" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">(iii)</span> 
<div id="A2.I1.ix3.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A2.I1.ix3.p1.1" class="ltx_p">By some algebraic manipulation, the target inequality <math id="A2.I1.ix3.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\frac{\max_{w}S_{w}}{1-\Delta}\leq 1-\frac{1-\sum_{w}S_{w}}{|{\mathcal{V}}|\wedge|{{\mathcal{W}}}|}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mfrac><mrow><msub><mi>max</mi><mi>w</mi></msub><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><msub><mi>S</mi><mi>w</mi></msub></mrow><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi></mrow></mfrac><mo>≤</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mfrac><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="false"><msub><mo maxsize="0.700em" minsize="0.700em" stretchy="true">∑</mo><mi>w</mi></msub></mstyle><msub><mi>S</mi><mi>w</mi></msub></mrow></mrow><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒱</mi><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow><mo>∧</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒲</mi><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow></mrow></mfrac></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\frac{\max_{w}S_{w}}{1-\Delta}\leq 1-\frac{1-\sum_{w}S_{w}}{|{\mathcal{V}}|\wedge|{{\mathcal{W}}}|}</annotation></semantics></math> is equivalent to</p>
<table id="A2.E73" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A2.E73.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\left(1+\frac{\Delta}{|{\mathcal{V}}|\wedge|{{\mathcal{W}}}|-1}\right)S_{w}\leq(1-\Delta)\cdot\left(\frac{\sum_{w^{\prime}\neq w}S_{w^{\prime}}}{|{\mathcal{V}}|\wedge|{{\mathcal{W}}}|-1}+1\right),~\forall~w\in{{\mathcal{W}}}." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mrow><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>+</mo><mfrac><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mrow><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒱</mi><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow><mo>∧</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒲</mi><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mfrac></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>S</mi><mi>w</mi></msub></mrow><mo>≤</mo><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi></mrow><mo rspace="0.055em" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mfrac><mrow><msub><mo>∑</mo><mrow><msup><mi>w</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo>≠</mo><mi>w</mi></mrow></msub><msub><mi>S</mi><msup><mi>w</mi><mo>′</mo></msup></msub></mrow><mrow><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒱</mi><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow><mo>∧</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒲</mi><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mfrac><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.497em">,</mo><mrow><mrow><mo rspace="0.497em">∀</mo><mi>w</mi></mrow><mo>∈</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒲</mi></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\left(1+\frac{\Delta}{|{\mathcal{V}}|\wedge|{{\mathcal{W}}}|-1}\right)S_{w}\leq(1-\Delta)\cdot\left(\frac{\sum_{w^{\prime}\neq w}S_{w^{\prime}}}{|{\mathcal{V}}|\wedge|{{\mathcal{W}}}|-1}+1\right),~\forall~w\in{{\mathcal{W}}}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(73)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A2.I1.ix3.p1.2" class="ltx_p">We then turn to prove (<a href="#A2.E73" title="In item (iii) ‣ Proof of Lemma . ‣ B.3 Proof of Lemma ‣ Appendix B Proof for Gumbel-max Watermarks in Section ‣ Optimal Detection for Language Watermarks with Pseudorandom Collision" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">73</span></a>).
Fix any <math id="A2.I1.ix3.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="w\in{{\mathcal{W}}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>w</mi><mo>∈</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒲</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">w\in{{\mathcal{W}}}</annotation></semantics></math>.
If <math id="A2.I1.ix3.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="S_{w}=0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>S</mi><mi>w</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">S_{w}=0</annotation></semantics></math>, then (<a href="#A2.E73" title="In item (iii) ‣ Proof of Lemma . ‣ B.3 Proof of Lemma ‣ Appendix B Proof for Gumbel-max Watermarks in Section ‣ Optimal Detection for Language Watermarks with Pseudorandom Collision" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">73</span></a>) holds trivially. Otherwise, if <math id="A2.I1.ix3.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="S_{w}&gt;0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>S</mi><mi>w</mi></msub><mo>&gt;</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">S_{w}&gt;0</annotation></semantics></math>, then by the relation (<a href="#A2.E72" title="In Proof of Lemma . ‣ B.3 Proof of Lemma ‣ Appendix B Proof for Gumbel-max Watermarks in Section ‣ Optimal Detection for Language Watermarks with Pseudorandom Collision" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">72</span></a>), we have <math id="A2.I1.ix3.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="0&lt;S_{w}\leq\min_{t\in{\mathcal{V}}}P_{t,w}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mn>0</mn><mo>&lt;</mo><msub><mi>S</mi><mi>w</mi></msub><mo>≤</mo><mrow><msub><mi>min</mi><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>∈</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒱</mi></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><msub><mi>P</mi><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>w</mi></mrow></msub></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">0&lt;S_{w}\leq\min_{t\in{\mathcal{V}}}P_{t,w}</annotation></semantics></math>. This implies that <math id="A2.I1.ix3.p1.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="P_{t,w}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>P</mi><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>w</mi></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">P_{t,w}</annotation></semantics></math> is strictly positive for all indices <math id="A2.I1.ix3.p1.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="t\in{\mathcal{V}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>∈</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒱</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">t\in{\mathcal{V}}</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>
</div>
<div id="A2.I1.ix3.p2" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A2.I1.ix3.p2.1" class="ltx_p">In this case, on the one hand, it follows that</p>
<table id="A2.EGx51" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A2.E74"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A2.E74.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle S_{w}=\left(1+\sum_{w^{\prime}\neq w}\max_{t\in{\mathcal{V}}}\frac{P_{t,w^{\prime}}}{P_{t,w}}\right)^{-1}\leq\left(1+\frac{\sum_{w^{\prime}\neq w}\max_{t\in{\mathcal{V}}}P_{t,w^{\prime}}}{1-\Delta}\right)^{-1}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>S</mi><mi>w</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><msup><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>+</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munder><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><msup><mi>w</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo>≠</mo><mi>w</mi></mrow></munder></mstyle><mrow><munder><mi>max</mi><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>∈</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒱</mi></mrow></munder><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><msub><mi>P</mi><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>,</mo><msup><mi>w</mi><mo>′</mo></msup></mrow></msub><msub><mi>P</mi><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>w</mi></mrow></msub></mfrac></mstyle></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup><mo>≤</mo><msup><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>+</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><msub><mo>∑</mo><mrow><msup><mi>w</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo>≠</mo><mi>w</mi></mrow></msub><mrow><msub><mi>max</mi><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>∈</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒱</mi></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><msub><mi>P</mi><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>,</mo><msup><mi>w</mi><mo>′</mo></msup></mrow></msub></mrow></mrow><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi></mrow></mfrac></mstyle></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle S_{w}=\left(1+\sum_{w^{\prime}\neq w}\max_{t\in{\mathcal{V}}}\frac{P_{t,w^{\prime}}}{P_{t,w}}\right)^{-1}\leq\left(1+\frac{\sum_{w^{\prime}\neq w}\max_{t\in{\mathcal{V}}}P_{t,w^{\prime}}}{1-\Delta}\right)^{-1}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(74)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A2.I1.ix3.p2.2" class="ltx_p">where the inequality holds because <math id="A2.I1.ix3.p2.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="P_{t,w}\leq 1-\Delta" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>P</mi><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>w</mi></mrow></msub><mo>≤</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">P_{t,w}\leq 1-\Delta</annotation></semantics></math> for all <math id="A2.I1.ix3.p2.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="t" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>t</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">t</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="A2.I1.ix3.p2.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="w" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>w</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">w</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>
</div>
<div id="A2.I1.ix3.p3" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A2.I1.ix3.p3.1" class="ltx_p">On the other hand, we have that</p>
<table id="A2.EGx52" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A2.Ex122"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A2.Ex122.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\sum_{w^{\prime}\neq w}S_{w^{\prime}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munder><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><msup><mi>w</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo>≠</mo><mi>w</mi></mrow></munder></mstyle><msub><mi>S</mi><msup><mi>w</mi><mo>′</mo></msup></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\sum_{w^{\prime}\neq w}S_{w^{\prime}}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A2.Ex122.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=\sum_{w^{\prime}\neq w}\left(\sum_{j\in{{\mathcal{W}}}}\max_{t\in{\mathcal{V}}}\frac{P_{t,j}}{P_{t,w^{\prime}}}\right)^{-1}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munder><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><msup><mi>w</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo>≠</mo><mi>w</mi></mrow></munder></mstyle><msup><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munder><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>j</mi><mo>∈</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒲</mi></mrow></munder></mstyle><mrow><munder><mi>max</mi><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>∈</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒱</mi></mrow></munder><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><msub><mi>P</mi><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow></msub><msub><mi>P</mi><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>,</mo><msup><mi>w</mi><mo>′</mo></msup></mrow></msub></mfrac></mstyle></mrow></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=\sum_{w^{\prime}\neq w}\left(\sum_{j\in{{\mathcal{W}}}}\max_{t\in{\mathcal{V}}}\frac{P_{t,j}}{P_{t,w^{\prime}}}\right)^{-1}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A2.E75"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A2.E75.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\geq\sum_{w^{\prime}\neq w}\left(1+\sum_{j\neq w^{\prime}}\frac{\max_{t\in{\mathcal{V}}}P_{t,j}}{\min_{t\in{\mathcal{V}}}P_{t,w^{\prime}}}\right)^{-1}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>≥</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munder><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><msup><mi>w</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo>≠</mo><mi>w</mi></mrow></munder></mstyle><msup><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>+</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munder><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>j</mi><mo>≠</mo><msup><mi>w</mi><mo>′</mo></msup></mrow></munder></mstyle><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><msub><mi>max</mi><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>∈</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒱</mi></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><msub><mi>P</mi><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow></msub></mrow><mrow><msub><mi>min</mi><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>∈</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒱</mi></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><msub><mi>P</mi><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>,</mo><msup><mi>w</mi><mo>′</mo></msup></mrow></msub></mrow></mfrac></mstyle></mrow></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\geq\sum_{w^{\prime}\neq w}\left(1+\sum_{j\neq w^{\prime}}\frac{\max_{t\in{\mathcal{V}}}P_{t,j}}{\min_{t\in{\mathcal{V}}}P_{t,w^{\prime}}}\right)^{-1}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(75)</span></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A2.Ex123"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A2.Ex123.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=\sum_{w^{\prime}\neq w}\min_{t\in{\mathcal{V}}}P_{t,w^{\prime}}\cdot\left(\min_{t\in{\mathcal{V}}}P_{t,w^{\prime}}+\sum_{j\neq w^{\prime}}\max_{t\in{\mathcal{V}}}P_{t,j}\right)^{-1}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munder><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><msup><mi>w</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo>≠</mo><mi>w</mi></mrow></munder></mstyle><mrow><munder><mi>min</mi><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>∈</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒱</mi></mrow></munder><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><msub><mi>P</mi><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>,</mo><msup><mi>w</mi><mo>′</mo></msup></mrow></msub></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><msup><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mrow><munder><mi>min</mi><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>∈</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒱</mi></mrow></munder><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><msub><mi>P</mi><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>,</mo><msup><mi>w</mi><mo>′</mo></msup></mrow></msub></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munder><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>j</mi><mo>≠</mo><msup><mi>w</mi><mo>′</mo></msup></mrow></munder></mstyle><mrow><munder><mi>max</mi><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>∈</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒱</mi></mrow></munder><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><msub><mi>P</mi><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow></msub></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=\sum_{w^{\prime}\neq w}\min_{t\in{\mathcal{V}}}P_{t,w^{\prime}}\cdot\left(\min_{t\in{\mathcal{V}}}P_{t,w^{\prime}}+\sum_{j\neq w^{\prime}}\max_{t\in{\mathcal{V}}}P_{t,j}\right)^{-1}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A2.Ex124"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A2.Ex124.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\geq\frac{\sum_{w^{\prime}\neq w}\min_{t\in{\mathcal{V}}}P_{t,w^{\prime}}}{1-\Delta+\sum_{w^{\prime}\neq w}\max_{t\in{\mathcal{V}}}P_{t,w^{\prime}}}," display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>≥</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><msub><mo>∑</mo><mrow><msup><mi>w</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo>≠</mo><mi>w</mi></mrow></msub><mrow><msub><mi>min</mi><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>∈</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒱</mi></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><msub><mi>P</mi><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>,</mo><msup><mi>w</mi><mo>′</mo></msup></mrow></msub></mrow></mrow><mrow><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi></mrow><mo rspace="0.055em">+</mo><mrow><msub><mo>∑</mo><mrow><msup><mi>w</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo>≠</mo><mi>w</mi></mrow></msub><mrow><msub><mi>max</mi><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>∈</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒱</mi></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><msub><mi>P</mi><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>,</mo><msup><mi>w</mi><mo>′</mo></msup></mrow></msub></mrow></mrow></mrow></mfrac></mstyle></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\geq\frac{\sum_{w^{\prime}\neq w}\min_{t\in{\mathcal{V}}}P_{t,w^{\prime}}}{1-\Delta+\sum_{w^{\prime}\neq w}\max_{t\in{\mathcal{V}}}P_{t,w^{\prime}}},</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A2.I1.ix3.p3.2" class="ltx_p">where the last inequality follows from the fact that, for any <math id="A2.I1.ix3.p3.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="w^{\prime}\neq w" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msup><mi>w</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo>≠</mo><mi>w</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">w^{\prime}\neq w</annotation></semantics></math>,</p>
<table id="A2.EGx53" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A2.Ex125"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A2.Ex125.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\min_{t\in{\mathcal{V}}}P_{t,w^{\prime}}+\sum_{j\neq w^{\prime}}\max_{t\in{\mathcal{V}}}P_{t,j}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><munder><mi>min</mi><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>∈</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒱</mi></mrow></munder><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><msub><mi>P</mi><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>,</mo><msup><mi>w</mi><mo>′</mo></msup></mrow></msub></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munder><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>j</mi><mo>≠</mo><msup><mi>w</mi><mo>′</mo></msup></mrow></munder></mstyle><mrow><munder><mi>max</mi><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>∈</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒱</mi></mrow></munder><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><msub><mi>P</mi><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow></msub></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\min_{t\in{\mathcal{V}}}P_{t,w^{\prime}}+\sum_{j\neq w^{\prime}}\max_{t\in{\mathcal{V}}}P_{t,j}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A2.Ex125.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\leq\min_{t\in{\mathcal{V}}}P_{t,w^{\prime}}+\max_{t\in{\mathcal{V}}}P_{t,w}+\sum_{j\notin\{w,w^{\prime}\}}\max_{t\in{\mathcal{V}}}P_{t,j}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>≤</mo><mrow><mrow><munder><mi>min</mi><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>∈</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒱</mi></mrow></munder><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><msub><mi>P</mi><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>,</mo><msup><mi>w</mi><mo>′</mo></msup></mrow></msub></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><munder><mi>max</mi><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>∈</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒱</mi></mrow></munder><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><msub><mi>P</mi><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>w</mi></mrow></msub></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munder><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>j</mi><mo>∉</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mrow><mi>w</mi><mo>,</mo><msup><mi>w</mi><mo>′</mo></msup></mrow><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow></mrow></munder></mstyle><mrow><munder><mi>max</mi><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>∈</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒱</mi></mrow></munder><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><msub><mi>P</mi><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow></msub></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\leq\min_{t\in{\mathcal{V}}}P_{t,w^{\prime}}+\max_{t\in{\mathcal{V}}}P_{t,w}+\sum_{j\notin\{w,w^{\prime}\}}\max_{t\in{\mathcal{V}}}P_{t,j}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A2.Ex126"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A2.Ex126.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\leq\max_{t\in{\mathcal{V}}}P_{t,w^{\prime}}+(1-\Delta)+\sum_{j\notin\{w,w^{\prime}\}}\max_{t\in{\mathcal{V}}}P_{t,j}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>≤</mo><mrow><mrow><munder><mi>max</mi><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>∈</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒱</mi></mrow></munder><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><msub><mi>P</mi><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>,</mo><msup><mi>w</mi><mo>′</mo></msup></mrow></msub></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munder><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>j</mi><mo>∉</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mrow><mi>w</mi><mo>,</mo><msup><mi>w</mi><mo>′</mo></msup></mrow><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow></mrow></munder></mstyle><mrow><munder><mi>max</mi><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>∈</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒱</mi></mrow></munder><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><msub><mi>P</mi><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow></msub></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\leq\max_{t\in{\mathcal{V}}}P_{t,w^{\prime}}+(1-\Delta)+\sum_{j\notin\{w,w^{\prime}\}}\max_{t\in{\mathcal{V}}}P_{t,j}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A2.Ex127"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A2.Ex127.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\leq 1-\Delta+\sum_{w^{\prime}\neq w}\max_{t\in{\mathcal{V}}}P_{t,w^{\prime}}." display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>≤</mo><mrow><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munder><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><msup><mi>w</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo>≠</mo><mi>w</mi></mrow></munder></mstyle><mrow><munder><mi>max</mi><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>∈</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒱</mi></mrow></munder><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><msub><mi>P</mi><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>,</mo><msup><mi>w</mi><mo>′</mo></msup></mrow></msub></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\leq 1-\Delta+\sum_{w^{\prime}\neq w}\max_{t\in{\mathcal{V}}}P_{t,w^{\prime}}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
<div id="A2.I1.ix3.p4" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A2.I1.ix3.p4.1" class="ltx_p">We observe that (<a href="#A2.E74" title="In item (iii) ‣ Proof of Lemma . ‣ B.3 Proof of Lemma ‣ Appendix B Proof for Gumbel-max Watermarks in Section ‣ Optimal Detection for Language Watermarks with Pseudorandom Collision" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">74</span></a>) provides an upper bound for the left-hand side of (<a href="#A2.E73" title="In item (iii) ‣ Proof of Lemma . ‣ B.3 Proof of Lemma ‣ Appendix B Proof for Gumbel-max Watermarks in Section ‣ Optimal Detection for Language Watermarks with Pseudorandom Collision" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">73</span></a>) in terms of <math id="A2.I1.ix3.p4.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\sum_{w^{\prime}\neq w}\max_{t\in{\mathcal{V}}}P_{t,w^{\prime}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mo>∑</mo><mrow><msup><mi>w</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo>≠</mo><mi>w</mi></mrow></msub><mrow><msub><mi>max</mi><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>∈</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒱</mi></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><msub><mi>P</mi><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>,</mo><msup><mi>w</mi><mo>′</mo></msup></mrow></msub></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\sum_{w^{\prime}\neq w}\max_{t\in{\mathcal{V}}}P_{t,w^{\prime}}</annotation></semantics></math>, while (<a href="#A2.Ex122" title="In item (iii) ‣ Proof of Lemma . ‣ B.3 Proof of Lemma ‣ Appendix B Proof for Gumbel-max Watermarks in Section ‣ Optimal Detection for Language Watermarks with Pseudorandom Collision" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">75</span></a>) provides a lower bound for the right-hand side of (<a href="#A2.E73" title="In item (iii) ‣ Proof of Lemma . ‣ B.3 Proof of Lemma ‣ Appendix B Proof for Gumbel-max Watermarks in Section ‣ Optimal Detection for Language Watermarks with Pseudorandom Collision" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">73</span></a>) involving both <math id="A2.I1.ix3.p4.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\sum_{w^{\prime}\neq w}\max_{t\in{\mathcal{V}}}P_{t,w^{\prime}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mo>∑</mo><mrow><msup><mi>w</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo>≠</mo><mi>w</mi></mrow></msub><mrow><msub><mi>max</mi><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>∈</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒱</mi></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><msub><mi>P</mi><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>,</mo><msup><mi>w</mi><mo>′</mo></msup></mrow></msub></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\sum_{w^{\prime}\neq w}\max_{t\in{\mathcal{V}}}P_{t,w^{\prime}}</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="A2.I1.ix3.p4.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\sum_{w^{\prime}\neq w}\min_{t\in{\mathcal{V}}}P_{t,w^{\prime}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mo>∑</mo><mrow><msup><mi>w</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo>≠</mo><mi>w</mi></mrow></msub><mrow><msub><mi>min</mi><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>∈</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒱</mi></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><msub><mi>P</mi><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>,</mo><msup><mi>w</mi><mo>′</mo></msup></mrow></msub></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\sum_{w^{\prime}\neq w}\min_{t\in{\mathcal{V}}}P_{t,w^{\prime}}</annotation></semantics></math>.
To connect these bounds, we use the following fact that bridges both <math id="A2.I1.ix3.p4.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\sum_{w^{\prime}\neq w}\max_{t\in{\mathcal{V}}}P_{t,w^{\prime}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mo>∑</mo><mrow><msup><mi>w</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo>≠</mo><mi>w</mi></mrow></msub><mrow><msub><mi>max</mi><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>∈</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒱</mi></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><msub><mi>P</mi><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>,</mo><msup><mi>w</mi><mo>′</mo></msup></mrow></msub></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\sum_{w^{\prime}\neq w}\max_{t\in{\mathcal{V}}}P_{t,w^{\prime}}</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="A2.I1.ix3.p4.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\sum_{w^{\prime}\neq w}\min_{t\in{\mathcal{V}}}P_{t,w^{\prime}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mo>∑</mo><mrow><msup><mi>w</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo>≠</mo><mi>w</mi></mrow></msub><mrow><msub><mi>min</mi><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>∈</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒱</mi></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><msub><mi>P</mi><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>,</mo><msup><mi>w</mi><mo>′</mo></msup></mrow></msub></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\sum_{w^{\prime}\neq w}\min_{t\in{\mathcal{V}}}P_{t,w^{\prime}}</annotation></semantics></math>:</p>
<table id="A2.E76" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A2.E76.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\sum_{w^{\prime}\neq w}\min_{t\in{\mathcal{V}}}P_{t,w^{\prime}}+(|{\mathcal{V}}|\wedge|{{\mathcal{W}}}|-1)\cdot\sum_{w^{\prime}\neq w}\max_{t\in{\mathcal{V}}}P_{t,w^{\prime}}\geq(|{\mathcal{V}}|\wedge|{{\mathcal{W}}}|)\cdot\Delta," display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mrow><munder><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><msup><mi>w</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo>≠</mo><mi>w</mi></mrow></munder><mrow><munder><mi>min</mi><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>∈</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒱</mi></mrow></munder><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><msub><mi>P</mi><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>,</mo><msup><mi>w</mi><mo>′</mo></msup></mrow></msub></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒱</mi><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow><mo>∧</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒲</mi><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo rspace="0.055em" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo rspace="0.055em">⋅</mo><mrow><munder><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><msup><mi>w</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo>≠</mo><mi>w</mi></mrow></munder><mrow><munder><mi>max</mi><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>∈</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒱</mi></mrow></munder><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><msub><mi>P</mi><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>,</mo><msup><mi>w</mi><mo>′</mo></msup></mrow></msub></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>≥</mo><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒱</mi><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow><mo>∧</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒲</mi><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.055em" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\sum_{w^{\prime}\neq w}\min_{t\in{\mathcal{V}}}P_{t,w^{\prime}}+(|{\mathcal{V}}|\wedge|{{\mathcal{W}}}|-1)\cdot\sum_{w^{\prime}\neq w}\max_{t\in{\mathcal{V}}}P_{t,w^{\prime}}\geq(|{\mathcal{V}}|\wedge|{{\mathcal{W}}}|)\cdot\Delta,</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(76)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A2.I1.ix3.p4.2" class="ltx_p">which follows because <math id="A2.I1.ix3.p4.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\min_{t\in{\mathcal{V}}}P_{t,w^{\prime}}+\sum_{j\notin\{w,w^{\prime}\}}\max_{t\in{\mathcal{V}}}P_{t,j}\geq 1-\max_{t\in{\mathcal{V}}}P_{t,w}\geq\Delta" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>min</mi><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>∈</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒱</mi></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><msub><mi>P</mi><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>,</mo><msup><mi>w</mi><mo>′</mo></msup></mrow></msub></mrow><mo rspace="0.055em">+</mo><mrow><msub><mo>∑</mo><mrow><mi>j</mi><mo>∉</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mrow><mi>w</mi><mo>,</mo><msup><mi>w</mi><mo>′</mo></msup></mrow><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow></mrow></msub><mrow><msub><mi>max</mi><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>∈</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒱</mi></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><msub><mi>P</mi><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow></msub></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>≥</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mrow><msub><mi>max</mi><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>∈</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒱</mi></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><msub><mi>P</mi><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>w</mi></mrow></msub></mrow></mrow><mo>≥</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\min_{t\in{\mathcal{V}}}P_{t,w^{\prime}}+\sum_{j\notin\{w,w^{\prime}\}}\max_{t\in{\mathcal{V}}}P_{t,j}\geq 1-\max_{t\in{\mathcal{V}}}P_{t,w}\geq\Delta</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>
</div>
<div id="A2.I1.ix3.p5" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A2.I1.ix3.p5.1" class="ltx_p">Combining the inequalities (<a href="#A2.E74" title="In item (iii) ‣ Proof of Lemma . ‣ B.3 Proof of Lemma ‣ Appendix B Proof for Gumbel-max Watermarks in Section ‣ Optimal Detection for Language Watermarks with Pseudorandom Collision" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">74</span></a>), (<a href="#A2.Ex122" title="In item (iii) ‣ Proof of Lemma . ‣ B.3 Proof of Lemma ‣ Appendix B Proof for Gumbel-max Watermarks in Section ‣ Optimal Detection for Language Watermarks with Pseudorandom Collision" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">75</span></a>), and (<a href="#A2.E76" title="In item (iii) ‣ Proof of Lemma . ‣ B.3 Proof of Lemma ‣ Appendix B Proof for Gumbel-max Watermarks in Section ‣ Optimal Detection for Language Watermarks with Pseudorandom Collision" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">76</span></a>), we complete the proof of (<a href="#A2.E73" title="In item (iii) ‣ Proof of Lemma . ‣ B.3 Proof of Lemma ‣ Appendix B Proof for Gumbel-max Watermarks in Section ‣ Optimal Detection for Language Watermarks with Pseudorandom Collision" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">73</span></a>) for a fixed <math id="A2.I1.ix3.p5.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="w" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>w</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">w</annotation></semantics></math>. Since the same argument holds for all <math id="A2.I1.ix3.p5.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="w" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>w</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">w</annotation></semantics></math>, this establishes (<a href="#A2.E73" title="In item (iii) ‣ Proof of Lemma . ‣ B.3 Proof of Lemma ‣ Appendix B Proof for Gumbel-max Watermarks in Section ‣ Optimal Detection for Language Watermarks with Pseudorandom Collision" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">73</span></a>).</p>
</div></li>
<li id="A2.I1.ix4" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">(iv)</span> 
<div id="A2.I1.ix4.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A2.I1.ix4.p1.1" class="ltx_p">Finally, we show that <math id="A2.I1.ix4.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="{\bm{S}}_{\Delta}^{\star}:=\left(\frac{1-\Delta}{1+\frac{\Delta}{|{\mathcal{V}}|\wedge|{{\mathcal{W}}}|-1}},0,0,\ldots,0\right)\in{\mathcal{D}}_{\Delta}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msubsup><mi>𝑺</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo>⋆</mo></msubsup><mo>:=</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mfrac><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi></mrow><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>+</mo><mfrac><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mrow><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒱</mi><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow><mo>∧</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒲</mi><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mfrac></mrow></mfrac><mo>,</mo><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi><mo>,</mo><mn>0</mn><mo>)</mo></mrow><mo>∈</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒟</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\bm{S}}_{\Delta}^{\star}:=\left(\frac{1-\Delta}{1+\frac{\Delta}{|{\mathcal{V}}|\wedge|{{\mathcal{W}}}|-1}},0,0,\ldots,0\right)\in{\mathcal{D}}_{\Delta}</annotation></semantics></math> by explicit construction. We consider two cases based on the relative sizes of <math id="A2.I1.ix4.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="|{{\mathcal{W}}}|" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒲</mi><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">|{{\mathcal{W}}}|</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="A2.I1.ix4.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="|{\mathcal{V}}|" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒱</mi><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">|{\mathcal{V}}|</annotation></semantics></math>:</p>
</div>
<div id="A2.I1.ix4.p2" class="ltx_para">
<ul id="A2.I1.ix4.I1" class="ltx_itemize">
<li id="A2.I1.ix4.I1.i1" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">•</span> 
<div id="A2.I1.ix4.I1.i1.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A2.I1.ix4.I1.i1.p1.1" class="ltx_p">If <math id="A2.I1.ix4.I1.i1.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="|{{\mathcal{W}}}|\geq|{\mathcal{V}}|+1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒲</mi><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow><mo>≥</mo><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒱</mi><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">|{{\mathcal{W}}}|\geq|{\mathcal{V}}|+1</annotation></semantics></math>, we construct the first NTP distribution <math id="A2.I1.ix4.I1.i1.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\bm{P}_{t}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>𝑷</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\bm{P}_{t}</annotation></semantics></math> as follows:</p>
<table id="A2.E77" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A2.E77.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\bm{P}_{t}=\begin{pmatrix}1-\Delta,&amp;\frac{\Delta}{|{\mathcal{V}}|-1},&amp;\frac{\Delta}{|{\mathcal{V}}|-1},&amp;\cdots,&amp;\frac{\Delta}{|{\mathcal{V}}|-1},&amp;0,&amp;\cdots,&amp;0\end{pmatrix}." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>𝑷</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mtable columnspacing="5pt" displaystyle="true"><mtr><mtd><mrow><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow></mtd><mtd><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="false"><mfrac><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒱</mi><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mfrac></mstyle><mo>,</mo></mrow></mtd><mtd><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="false"><mfrac><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒱</mi><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mfrac></mstyle><mo>,</mo></mrow></mtd><mtd><mrow><mo rspace="0em">⋯</mo><mo>,</mo></mrow></mtd><mtd><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="false"><mfrac><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒱</mi><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mfrac></mstyle><mo>,</mo></mrow></mtd><mtd><mrow><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo></mrow></mtd><mtd><mrow><mo rspace="0em">⋯</mo><mo>,</mo></mrow></mtd><mtd><mn>0</mn></mtd></mtr></mtable><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\bm{P}_{t}=\begin{pmatrix}1-\Delta,&amp;\frac{\Delta}{|{\mathcal{V}}|-1},&amp;\frac{\Delta}{|{\mathcal{V}}|-1},&amp;\cdots,&amp;\frac{\Delta}{|{\mathcal{V}}|-1},&amp;0,&amp;\cdots,&amp;0\end{pmatrix}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(77)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A2.I1.ix4.I1.i1.p1.2" class="ltx_p">For <math id="A2.I1.ix4.I1.i1.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="i=2,\ldots,|{\mathcal{V}}|+1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi><mo>,</mo><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒱</mi><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">i=2,\ldots,|{\mathcal{V}}|+1</annotation></semantics></math>, we define the <math id="A2.I1.ix4.I1.i1.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="i" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>i</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">i</annotation></semantics></math>-th NTP distribution by setting the first entry to <math id="A2.I1.ix4.I1.i1.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="1-\Delta" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">1-\Delta</annotation></semantics></math>, the <math id="A2.I1.ix4.I1.i1.p1.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="i" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>i</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">i</annotation></semantics></math>-th entry to zero, and all other entries among the first <math id="A2.I1.ix4.I1.i1.p1.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="|{\mathcal{V}}|+1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒱</mi><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">|{\mathcal{V}}|+1</annotation></semantics></math> positions to <math id="A2.I1.ix4.I1.i1.p1.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\frac{\Delta}{|{\mathcal{V}}|-1}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mfrac><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒱</mi><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mfrac><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\frac{\Delta}{|{\mathcal{V}}|-1}</annotation></semantics></math>. A direct computation shows that all such distributions yield this very <math id="A2.I1.ix4.I1.i1.p1.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="{\bm{S}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>𝑺</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\bm{S}}</annotation></semantics></math>-vector:</p>
<table id="A2.Ex128" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A2.Ex128.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="{\bm{S}}_{\Delta}^{\star}=\begin{pmatrix}\frac{1-\Delta}{1+\frac{\Delta}{|{\mathcal{V}}|-1}},&amp;0,&amp;\cdots,&amp;0\end{pmatrix}." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msubsup><mi>𝑺</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo>⋆</mo></msubsup><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mtable columnspacing="5pt" displaystyle="true"><mtr><mtd><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="false"><mfrac><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi></mrow><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>+</mo><mfrac><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒱</mi><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mfrac></mrow></mfrac></mstyle><mo>,</mo></mrow></mtd><mtd><mrow><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo></mrow></mtd><mtd><mrow><mo rspace="0em">⋯</mo><mo>,</mo></mrow></mtd><mtd><mn>0</mn></mtd></mtr></mtable><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\bm{S}}_{\Delta}^{\star}=\begin{pmatrix}\frac{1-\Delta}{1+\frac{\Delta}{|{\mathcal{V}}|-1}},&amp;0,&amp;\cdots,&amp;0\end{pmatrix}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div></li>
<li id="A2.I1.ix4.I1.i2" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">•</span> 
<div id="A2.I1.ix4.I1.i2.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A2.I1.ix4.I1.i2.p1.1" class="ltx_p">If <math id="A2.I1.ix4.I1.i2.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="|{{\mathcal{W}}}|\leq|{\mathcal{V}}|" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒲</mi><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow><mo>≤</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒱</mi><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">|{{\mathcal{W}}}|\leq|{\mathcal{V}}|</annotation></semantics></math>, we instead construct the first NTP distribution as</p>
<table id="A2.Ex129" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A2.Ex129.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\bm{P}_{t}=\begin{pmatrix}1-\Delta,&amp;\frac{\Delta}{|{{\mathcal{W}}}|-1},&amp;\frac{\Delta}{|{{\mathcal{W}}}|-1},&amp;\cdots,&amp;\frac{\Delta}{|{{\mathcal{W}}}|-1},&amp;0,&amp;\cdots,&amp;0\end{pmatrix}," display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>𝑷</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mtable columnspacing="5pt" displaystyle="true"><mtr><mtd><mrow><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow></mtd><mtd><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="false"><mfrac><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒲</mi><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mfrac></mstyle><mo>,</mo></mrow></mtd><mtd><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="false"><mfrac><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒲</mi><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mfrac></mstyle><mo>,</mo></mrow></mtd><mtd><mrow><mo rspace="0em">⋯</mo><mo>,</mo></mrow></mtd><mtd><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="false"><mfrac><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒲</mi><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mfrac></mstyle><mo>,</mo></mrow></mtd><mtd><mrow><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo></mrow></mtd><mtd><mrow><mo rspace="0em">⋯</mo><mo>,</mo></mrow></mtd><mtd><mn>0</mn></mtd></mtr></mtable><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\bm{P}_{t}=\begin{pmatrix}1-\Delta,&amp;\frac{\Delta}{|{{\mathcal{W}}}|-1},&amp;\frac{\Delta}{|{{\mathcal{W}}}|-1},&amp;\cdots,&amp;\frac{\Delta}{|{{\mathcal{W}}}|-1},&amp;0,&amp;\cdots,&amp;0\end{pmatrix},</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A2.I1.ix4.I1.i2.p1.2" class="ltx_p">and define the remaining NTP distributions by cyclically shifting the zero entry among the first <math id="A2.I1.ix4.I1.i2.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="|{{\mathcal{W}}}|+1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒲</mi><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">|{{\mathcal{W}}}|+1</annotation></semantics></math> positions while keeping the first entry fixed at <math id="A2.I1.ix4.I1.i2.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="1-\Delta" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">1-\Delta</annotation></semantics></math>. The argument mirrors the previous case and is omitted for brevity.</p>
</div></li>
</ul>
</div></li>
</ol>
</div>
<div id="A2.SS3.p3" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A2.SS3.p3.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A2.SS3.p3.1.1" class="ltx_text">∎</span></p>
</div>
</div>
</section>
<section id="A2.SS4" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection">B.4 </span>Proof of Lemma <a href="#S7.Thmlem3" title="Lemma 7.3 (Schur-convexity). ‣ 7.1 Proof of Theorem ‣ 7 Proof of Main Results ‣ Optimal Detection for Language Watermarks with Pseudorandom Collision" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">7.3</span></a></h3>

<div id="A2.SS4.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A2.SS4.p1.1" class="ltx_p">We first introduce an ancillary lemma that establishes the Schur-convexity of CDF, that is the mapping <math id="A2.SS4.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="{\bm{S}}\mapsto F_{\bm{S}}(y)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>𝑺</mi><mo stretchy="false">↦</mo><mrow><msub><mi>F</mi><mi>𝑺</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>y</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\bm{S}}\mapsto F_{\bm{S}}(y)</annotation></semantics></math>, in Lemma <a href="#A2.Thmlem1" title="Lemma B.1 (Schur-convexity). ‣ B.4 Proof of Lemma ‣ Appendix B Proof for Gumbel-max Watermarks in Section ‣ Optimal Detection for Language Watermarks with Pseudorandom Collision" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">B.1</span></a>.</p>
</div>
<div id="A2.Thmlem1" class="ltx_theorem ltx_theorem_lem">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_title_theorem"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_theorem"><span id="A2.Thmlem1.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Lemma B.1</span></span><span id="A2.Thmlem1.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold"> </span>(Schur-convexity)<span id="A2.Thmlem1.4" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">.</span></h6>
<div id="A2.Thmlem1.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A2.Thmlem1.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A2.Thmlem1.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">For any <math id="A2.Thmlem1.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="y\in[0,1]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>y</mi><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">y\in[0,1]</annotation></semantics></math>, the map <math id="A2.Thmlem1.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="{\bm{S}}\mapsto F_{\bm{S}}({\mathrm{d}}y)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>𝐒</mi><mo stretchy="false">↦</mo><mrow><msub><mi>F</mi><mi>𝐒</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">d</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>y</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\bm{S}}\mapsto F_{\bm{S}}({\mathrm{d}}y)</annotation></semantics></math> is Schur-convex in <math id="A2.Thmlem1.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="{\bm{S}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>𝐒</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\bm{S}}</annotation></semantics></math>.</span></p>
</div>
</div>
<div id="A2.SS4.2" class="ltx_proof">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_font_italic ltx_title_proof">Proof of Lemma <a href="#A2.Thmlem1" title="Lemma B.1 (Schur-convexity). ‣ B.4 Proof of Lemma ‣ Appendix B Proof for Gumbel-max Watermarks in Section ‣ Optimal Detection for Language Watermarks with Pseudorandom Collision" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">B.1</span></a>.</h6>
<div id="A2.SS4.p2" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A2.SS4.p2.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A2.SS4.p2.1.1" class="ltx_text">For simplicity, we define <math id="A2.SS4.p2.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="G({\bm{S}})=F_{\bm{S}}(y)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>G</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝑺</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><msub><mi>F</mi><mi>𝑺</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>y</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">G({\bm{S}})=F_{\bm{S}}(y)</annotation></semantics></math> for any fixed <math id="A2.SS4.p2.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="y\in[0,1]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>y</mi><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">y\in[0,1]</annotation></semantics></math>. It is straightforward to verify that (i) <math id="A2.SS4.p2.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="G" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>G</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">G</annotation></semantics></math> is invariant under permutations of its coordinates, meaning that <math id="A2.SS4.p2.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="G({\bm{S}})=G(\pi({\bm{S}}))" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>G</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝑺</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>G</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>π</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝑺</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">G({\bm{S}})=G(\pi({\bm{S}}))</annotation></semantics></math> for any permutation <math id="A2.SS4.p2.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\pi\in\mathrm{Perm}({{\mathcal{W}}})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>π</mi><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mi>Perm</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒲</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\pi\in\mathrm{Perm}({{\mathcal{W}}})</annotation></semantics></math>, and (ii) all first partial derivatives of <math id="A2.SS4.p2.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="G" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>G</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">G</annotation></semantics></math> exist. By the Schur–Ostrowski criterion, <math id="A2.SS4.p2.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="G" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>G</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">G</annotation></semantics></math> is Schur-convex in <math id="A2.SS4.p2.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="{\bm{S}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>𝑺</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\bm{S}}</annotation></semantics></math> if and only if, for any <math id="A2.SS4.p2.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="{\bm{S}}\in{\mathbb{R}}^{d}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>𝑺</mi><mo>∈</mo><msup><mi>ℝ</mi><mi>d</mi></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\bm{S}}\in{\mathbb{R}}^{d}</annotation></semantics></math> and any <math id="A2.SS4.p2.m10" class="ltx_Math" alttext="w,w^{\prime}\in{{\mathcal{W}}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>w</mi><mo>,</mo><msup><mi>w</mi><mo>′</mo></msup></mrow><mo>∈</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒲</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">w,w^{\prime}\in{{\mathcal{W}}}</annotation></semantics></math>, the following condition holds:</span></p>
<table id="A2.Ex130" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A2.Ex130.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(S_{w}-S_{w^{\prime}})\left(\frac{\partial G}{\partial S_{w}}-\frac{\partial G}{\partial S_{w^{\prime}}}\right)\geq 0." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>S</mi><mi>w</mi></msub><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>S</mi><msup><mi>w</mi><mo>′</mo></msup></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mfrac><mrow><mo>∂</mo><mi>G</mi></mrow><mrow><mo>∂</mo><msub><mi>S</mi><mi>w</mi></msub></mrow></mfrac><mo>−</mo><mfrac><mrow><mo>∂</mo><mi>G</mi></mrow><mrow><mo>∂</mo><msub><mi>S</mi><msup><mi>w</mi><mo>′</mo></msup></msub></mrow></mfrac></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>≥</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(S_{w}-S_{w^{\prime}})\left(\frac{\partial G}{\partial S_{w}}-\frac{\partial G}{\partial S_{w^{\prime}}}\right)\geq 0.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A2.SS4.p2.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="A2.SS4.p2.2.1" class="ltx_text">Direct calculation shows that</span></p>
<table id="A2.Ex131" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A2.Ex131.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\frac{\partial(S_{w}y^{1/S_{w}})}{\partial S_{w}}=y^{1/S_{w}}\left(1+\frac{\ln\frac{1}{y}}{S_{w}}\right)\quad\text{and}\quad\frac{\partial^{2}(S_{w}y^{1/S_{w}})}{\partial^{2}S_{w}}=y^{1/S_{w}}\frac{\ln^{2}\frac{1}{y}}{S_{w}^{3}}." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mfrac><mrow><mo>∂</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>S</mi><mi>w</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>y</mi><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>/</mo><msub><mi>S</mi><mi>w</mi></msub></mrow></msup></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mrow><mo>∂</mo><msub><mi>S</mi><mi>w</mi></msub></mrow></mfrac><mo>=</mo><mrow><msup><mi>y</mi><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>/</mo><msub><mi>S</mi><mi>w</mi></msub></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>+</mo><mfrac><mrow><mi>ln</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mi>y</mi></mfrac></mrow><msub><mi>S</mi><mi>w</mi></msub></mfrac></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mspace style="width:1em;" width="1em"></mspace><mtext>and</mtext><mspace style="width:1em;" width="1em"></mspace><mrow><mfrac><mrow><msup><mo>∂</mo><mn>2</mn></msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>S</mi><mi>w</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>y</mi><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>/</mo><msub><mi>S</mi><mi>w</mi></msub></mrow></msup></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mrow><msup><mo>∂</mo><mn>2</mn></msup><msub><mi>S</mi><mi>w</mi></msub></mrow></mfrac><mo>=</mo><mrow><msup><mi>y</mi><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>/</mo><msub><mi>S</mi><mi>w</mi></msub></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mfrac><mrow><msup><mi>ln</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mi>y</mi></mfrac></mrow><msubsup><mi>S</mi><mi>w</mi><mn>3</mn></msubsup></mfrac></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\frac{\partial(S_{w}y^{1/S_{w}})}{\partial S_{w}}=y^{1/S_{w}}\left(1+\frac{\ln\frac{1}{y}}{S_{w}}\right)\quad\text{and}\quad\frac{\partial^{2}(S_{w}y^{1/S_{w}})}{\partial^{2}S_{w}}=y^{1/S_{w}}\frac{\ln^{2}\frac{1}{y}}{S_{w}^{3}}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A2.SS4.p2.3" class="ltx_p"><span id="A2.SS4.p2.3.1" class="ltx_text">As a result,</span></p>
<table id="A2.EGx54" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A2.Ex132"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A2.Ex132.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle(S_{w}-S_{w^{\prime}})\left(\frac{\partial G}{\partial S_{w}}-\frac{\partial G}{\partial S_{w^{\prime}}}\right)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>S</mi><mi>w</mi></msub><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>S</mi><msup><mi>w</mi><mo>′</mo></msup></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><mo>∂</mo><mi>G</mi></mrow><mrow><mo>∂</mo><msub><mi>S</mi><mi>w</mi></msub></mrow></mfrac></mstyle><mo>−</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><mo>∂</mo><mi>G</mi></mrow><mrow><mo>∂</mo><msub><mi>S</mi><msup><mi>w</mi><mo>′</mo></msup></msub></mrow></mfrac></mstyle></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle(S_{w}-S_{w^{\prime}})\left(\frac{\partial G}{\partial S_{w}}-\frac{\partial G}{\partial S_{w^{\prime}}}\right)</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A2.Ex132.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=\frac{(S_{w}-S_{w^{\prime}})}{\sum_{w}S_{w}}\left[y^{1/S_{w}}\left(1+\frac{\ln\frac{1}{y}}{S_{w}}\right)-y^{1/S_{w^{\prime}}}\left(1+\frac{\ln\frac{1}{y}}{S_{w^{\prime}}}\right)\right]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>S</mi><mi>w</mi></msub><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>S</mi><msup><mi>w</mi><mo>′</mo></msup></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mrow><msub><mo>∑</mo><mi>w</mi></msub><msub><mi>S</mi><mi>w</mi></msub></mrow></mfrac></mstyle><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>[</mo><mrow><mrow><msup><mi>y</mi><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>/</mo><msub><mi>S</mi><mi>w</mi></msub></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>+</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><mi>ln</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mi>y</mi></mfrac></mrow><msub><mi>S</mi><mi>w</mi></msub></mfrac></mstyle></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><msup><mi>y</mi><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>/</mo><msub><mi>S</mi><msup><mi>w</mi><mo>′</mo></msup></msub></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>+</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><mi>ln</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mi>y</mi></mfrac></mrow><msub><mi>S</mi><msup><mi>w</mi><mo>′</mo></msup></msub></mfrac></mstyle></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>]</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=\frac{(S_{w}-S_{w^{\prime}})}{\sum_{w}S_{w}}\left[y^{1/S_{w}}\left(1+\frac{\ln\frac{1}{y}}{S_{w}}\right)-y^{1/S_{w^{\prime}}}\left(1+\frac{\ln\frac{1}{y}}{S_{w^{\prime}}}\right)\right]</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A2.Ex133"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A2.Ex133.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=\frac{(S_{w}-S_{w^{\prime}})^{2}}{\sum_{w}S_{w}}\cdot y^{1/\widetilde{S}_{w}}\frac{\ln^{2}\frac{1}{y}}{\widetilde{S}_{w}^{3}}\geq 0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>S</mi><mi>w</mi></msub><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>S</mi><msup><mi>w</mi><mo>′</mo></msup></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup><mrow><msub><mo>∑</mo><mi>w</mi></msub><msub><mi>S</mi><mi>w</mi></msub></mrow></mfrac></mstyle><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><msup><mi>y</mi><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>/</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>S</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mi>w</mi></msub></mrow></msup></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><msup><mi>ln</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mi>y</mi></mfrac></mrow><msubsup><mover accent="true"><mi>S</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mi>w</mi><mn>3</mn></msubsup></mfrac></mstyle></mrow><mo>≥</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=\frac{(S_{w}-S_{w^{\prime}})^{2}}{\sum_{w}S_{w}}\cdot y^{1/\widetilde{S}_{w}}\frac{\ln^{2}\frac{1}{y}}{\widetilde{S}_{w}^{3}}\geq 0</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A2.SS4.p2.4" class="ltx_p"><span id="A2.SS4.p2.4.1" class="ltx_text">where the last equation uses the mean value theorem and <math id="A2.SS4.p2.m11" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\widetilde{S}_{w}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>S</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mi>w</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\widetilde{S}_{w}</annotation></semantics></math> lies between <math id="A2.SS4.p2.m12" class="ltx_Math" alttext="S_{w}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>S</mi><mi>w</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">S_{w}</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="A2.SS4.p2.m13" class="ltx_Math" alttext="S_{w^{\prime}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>S</mi><msup><mi>w</mi><mo>′</mo></msup></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">S_{w^{\prime}}</annotation></semantics></math>.
∎</span></p>
</div>
</div>
<div id="A2.SS4.p3" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A2.SS4.p3.1" class="ltx_p">Now, using Lemma <a href="#A2.Thmlem1" title="Lemma B.1 (Schur-convexity). ‣ B.4 Proof of Lemma ‣ Appendix B Proof for Gumbel-max Watermarks in Section ‣ Optimal Detection for Language Watermarks with Pseudorandom Collision" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">B.1</span></a>, we can proceed to prove Lemma <a href="#S7.Thmlem3" title="Lemma 7.3 (Schur-convexity). ‣ 7.1 Proof of Theorem ‣ 7 Proof of Main Results ‣ Optimal Detection for Language Watermarks with Pseudorandom Collision" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">7.3</span></a>.</p>
</div>
<div id="A2.SS4.3" class="ltx_proof">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_font_italic ltx_title_proof">Proof of Lemma <a href="#S7.Thmlem3" title="Lemma 7.3 (Schur-convexity). ‣ 7.1 Proof of Theorem ‣ 7 Proof of Main Results ‣ Optimal Detection for Language Watermarks with Pseudorandom Collision" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">7.3</span></a>.</h6>
<div id="A2.SS4.p4" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A2.SS4.p4.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A2.SS4.p4.1.1" class="ltx_text">For any non-decreasing score function <math id="A2.SS4.p4.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="h" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>h</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">h</annotation></semantics></math>, by integration by parts, we have that</span></p>
<table id="A2.E78" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A2.E78.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\EB_{F_{\bm{S}}}[{\mathrm{e}}^{-h(Y_{{\mathcal{V}}})}]=\int{\mathrm{e}}^{-h(y)}F_{\bm{S}}({\mathrm{d}}y)={\mathrm{e}}^{-h(1)}+\int_{0}^{1}F_{\bm{S}}(y){\mathrm{e}}^{-h(y)}h({\mathrm{d}}y)." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>𝔼</mi><msub><mi>F</mi><mi>𝐒</mi></msub></msub><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><msup><mi>e</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>h</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>Y</mi><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒱</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></msup><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.111em">=</mo><mrow><mo>∫</mo><mrow><msup><mi>e</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>h</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>y</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>F</mi><mi>𝐒</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>dy</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><msup><mi>e</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>h</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>1</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></msup><mo rspace="0.055em">+</mo><mrow><msubsup><mo>∫</mo><mn>0</mn><mn>1</mn></msubsup><mrow><msub><mi>F</mi><mi>𝐒</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>y</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>e</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>h</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>y</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>h</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>dy</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\EB_{F_{\bm{S}}}[{\mathrm{e}}^{-h(Y_{{\mathcal{V}}})}]=\int{\mathrm{e}}^{-h(y)}F_{\bm{S}}({\mathrm{d}}y)={\mathrm{e}}^{-h(1)}+\int_{0}^{1}F_{\bm{S}}(y){\mathrm{e}}^{-h(y)}h({\mathrm{d}}y).</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(78)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A2.SS4.p4.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="A2.SS4.p4.2.1" class="ltx_text">This implies that <math id="A2.SS4.p4.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\EB_{F_{\bm{S}}}[{\mathrm{e}}^{-h(Y_{{\mathcal{V}}})}]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>𝔼</mi><msub><mi>F</mi><mi>𝐒</mi></msub></msub><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><msup><mi>e</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>h</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>Y</mi><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒱</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></msup><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\EB_{F_{\bm{S}}}[{\mathrm{e}}^{-h(Y_{{\mathcal{V}}})}]</annotation></semantics></math> is a non-negative weighted sum of <math id="A2.SS4.p4.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="F_{\bm{S}}(y)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>F</mi><mi>𝑺</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>y</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">F_{\bm{S}}(y)</annotation></semantics></math> evaluated over all possible values of <math id="A2.SS4.p4.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="y" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>y</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">y</annotation></semantics></math>.
By Lemma <a href="#A2.Thmlem1" title="Lemma B.1 (Schur-convexity). ‣ B.4 Proof of Lemma ‣ Appendix B Proof for Gumbel-max Watermarks in Section ‣ Optimal Detection for Language Watermarks with Pseudorandom Collision" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">B.1</span></a>, we know that the mapping <math id="A2.SS4.p4.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="{\bm{S}}\mapsto F_{\bm{S}}(y)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>𝑺</mi><mo stretchy="false">↦</mo><mrow><msub><mi>F</mi><mi>𝑺</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>y</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\bm{S}}\mapsto F_{\bm{S}}(y)</annotation></semantics></math> is Schur-convex in <math id="A2.SS4.p4.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="{\bm{S}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>𝑺</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\bm{S}}</annotation></semantics></math> for any fixed <math id="A2.SS4.p4.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="y\in[0,1]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>y</mi><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">y\in[0,1]</annotation></semantics></math>. Using this result and applying Definition <a href="#S7.Thmdefn1" title="Definition 7.1 (Schur-convexity). ‣ 7.1 Proof of Theorem ‣ 7 Proof of Main Results ‣ Optimal Detection for Language Watermarks with Pseudorandom Collision" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">7.1</span></a>, we conclude that the function <math id="A2.SS4.p4.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="{\bm{S}}\mapsto\int e^{-h(y)}F_{\bm{S}}({\mathrm{d}}y)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>𝑺</mi><mo rspace="0.111em" stretchy="false">↦</mo><mrow><mo>∫</mo><mrow><msup><mi>e</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>h</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>y</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>F</mi><mi>𝑺</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">𝑑</mo><mi>y</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\bm{S}}\mapsto\int e^{-h(y)}F_{\bm{S}}({\mathrm{d}}y)</annotation></semantics></math> is isotonic, order-preserving, and therefore Schur-convex in <math id="A2.SS4.p4.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="{\bm{S}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>𝑺</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\bm{S}}</annotation></semantics></math>.</span></p>
</div>
<div id="A2.SS4.p5" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A2.SS4.p5.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A2.SS4.p5.1.1" class="ltx_text">∎</span></p>
</div>
</div>
</section>
<section id="A2.SS5" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection">B.5 </span>Proof of Lemma <a href="#S7.Thmlem4" title="Lemma 7.4 (Reduced domain). ‣ 7.1 Proof of Theorem ‣ 7 Proof of Main Results ‣ Optimal Detection for Language Watermarks with Pseudorandom Collision" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">7.4</span></a></h3>

<div id="A2.SS5.2" class="ltx_proof">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_font_italic ltx_title_proof">Proof of Lemma <a href="#S7.Thmlem4" title="Lemma 7.4 (Reduced domain). ‣ 7.1 Proof of Theorem ‣ 7 Proof of Main Results ‣ Optimal Detection for Language Watermarks with Pseudorandom Collision" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">7.4</span></a>.</h6>
<div id="A2.SS5.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A2.SS5.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A2.SS5.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text">The integration by parts implies that</span></p>
<table id="A2.Ex134" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A2.Ex134.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\int{\mathrm{e}}^{-h(y)}F_{\bm{S}}({\mathrm{d}}y)={\mathrm{e}}^{-h(1)}+\int F_{\bm{S}}(y){\mathrm{e}}^{-h(y)}h({\mathrm{d}}y)." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mo>∫</mo><mrow><msup><mi>e</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>h</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>y</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>F</mi><mi>𝑺</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">𝑑</mo><mi>y</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><msup><mi>e</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>h</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>1</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></msup><mo rspace="0.055em">+</mo><mrow><mo>∫</mo><mrow><msub><mi>F</mi><mi>𝑺</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>y</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>e</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>h</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>y</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>h</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">𝑑</mo><mi>y</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\int{\mathrm{e}}^{-h(y)}F_{\bm{S}}({\mathrm{d}}y)={\mathrm{e}}^{-h(1)}+\int F_{\bm{S}}(y){\mathrm{e}}^{-h(y)}h({\mathrm{d}}y).</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(<a href="#A2.E78" title="In Proof of Lemma . ‣ B.4 Proof of Lemma ‣ Appendix B Proof for Gumbel-max Watermarks in Section ‣ Optimal Detection for Language Watermarks with Pseudorandom Collision" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">78</span></a>)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A2.SS5.p1.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="A2.SS5.p1.2.1" class="ltx_text">It suffices to prove that</span></p>
<table id="A2.Ex135" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A2.Ex135.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\max_{{\bm{S}}\in{\mathcal{D}}_{\Delta}}\int F_{\bm{S}}(y){\mathrm{e}}^{-h(y)}h({\mathrm{d}}y)\leq\max_{{\bm{S}}\in{\mathcal{D}}_{\Delta}\cap{\mathcal{H}}_{\Delta}}\int F_{\bm{S}}(y){\mathrm{e}}^{-h(y)}h({\mathrm{d}}y)." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>max</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mrow><mmultiscripts><mo>∫</mo><mprescripts></mprescripts><mrow><mi>𝑺</mi><mo>∈</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒟</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi></msub></mrow><mrow></mrow></mmultiscripts><mo>⁡</mo><msub><mi>F</mi><mi>𝑺</mi></msub></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>y</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>e</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>h</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>y</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>h</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">𝑑</mo><mi>y</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>≤</mo><mrow><mi>max</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mrow><mmultiscripts><mo>∫</mo><mprescripts></mprescripts><mrow><mi>𝑺</mi><mo>∈</mo><mrow><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒟</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi></msub><mo>∩</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℋ</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi></msub></mrow></mrow><mrow></mrow></mmultiscripts><mo>⁡</mo><msub><mi>F</mi><mi>𝑺</mi></msub></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>y</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>e</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>h</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>y</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>h</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">𝑑</mo><mi>y</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\max_{{\bm{S}}\in{\mathcal{D}}_{\Delta}}\int F_{\bm{S}}(y){\mathrm{e}}^{-h(y)}h({\mathrm{d}}y)\leq\max_{{\bm{S}}\in{\mathcal{D}}_{\Delta}\cap{\mathcal{H}}_{\Delta}}\int F_{\bm{S}}(y){\mathrm{e}}^{-h(y)}h({\mathrm{d}}y).</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A2.SS5.p1.3" class="ltx_p"><span id="A2.SS5.p1.3.1" class="ltx_text">To achieve this, it suffices to prove that</span></p>
<table id="A2.E79" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A2.E79.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\max_{{\bm{S}}\in{\mathcal{D}}_{\Delta}\setminus{\mathcal{H}}_{\Delta}}\int F_{\bm{S}}(y){\mathrm{e}}^{-h(y)}h({\mathrm{d}}y)\leq\int F_{{\bm{S}}_{\Delta}^{\star}}(y){\mathrm{e}}^{-h(y)}h({\mathrm{d}}y)." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>max</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mrow><mmultiscripts><mo>∫</mo><mprescripts></mprescripts><mrow><mi>𝑺</mi><mo>∈</mo><mrow><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒟</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi></msub><mo>∖</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℋ</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi></msub></mrow></mrow><mrow></mrow></mmultiscripts><mo>⁡</mo><msub><mi>F</mi><mi>𝑺</mi></msub></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>y</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>e</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>h</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>y</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>h</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">𝑑</mo><mi>y</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.111em">≤</mo><mrow><mo>∫</mo><mrow><msub><mi>F</mi><msubsup><mi>𝑺</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo>⋆</mo></msubsup></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>y</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>e</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>h</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>y</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>h</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">𝑑</mo><mi>y</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\max_{{\bm{S}}\in{\mathcal{D}}_{\Delta}\setminus{\mathcal{H}}_{\Delta}}\int F_{\bm{S}}(y){\mathrm{e}}^{-h(y)}h({\mathrm{d}}y)\leq\int F_{{\bm{S}}_{\Delta}^{\star}}(y){\mathrm{e}}^{-h(y)}h({\mathrm{d}}y).</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(79)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A2.SS5.p1.4" class="ltx_p"><span id="A2.SS5.p1.4.1" class="ltx_text">where <math id="A2.SS5.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="{\bm{S}}_{\Delta}^{\star}:=\left(\frac{1-\Delta}{1+\frac{\Delta}{|{\mathcal{V}}|\wedge|{{\mathcal{W}}}|-1}},0,0,\ldots,0\right)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msubsup><mi>𝑺</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo>⋆</mo></msubsup><mo>:=</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mfrac><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi></mrow><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>+</mo><mfrac><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mrow><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒱</mi><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow><mo>∧</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒲</mi><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mfrac></mrow></mfrac><mo>,</mo><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi><mo>,</mo><mn>0</mn><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\bm{S}}_{\Delta}^{\star}:=\left(\frac{1-\Delta}{1+\frac{\Delta}{|{\mathcal{V}}|\wedge|{{\mathcal{W}}}|-1}},0,0,\ldots,0\right)</annotation></semantics></math>.</span></p>
</div>
<div id="A2.SS5.p2" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A2.SS5.p2.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A2.SS5.p2.1.1" class="ltx_text">From Lemma <a href="#S7.Thmlem2" title="Lemma 7.2 (Properties of the domain 𝒟_Δ). ‣ 7.1 Proof of Theorem ‣ 7 Proof of Main Results ‣ Optimal Detection for Language Watermarks with Pseudorandom Collision" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">7.2</span></a>, it follows that <math id="A2.SS5.p2.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="{\bm{S}}_{\Delta}^{\star}\in{\mathcal{D}}_{\Delta}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msubsup><mi>𝑺</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo>⋆</mo></msubsup><mo>∈</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒟</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\bm{S}}_{\Delta}^{\star}\in{\mathcal{D}}_{\Delta}</annotation></semantics></math>.
By the definition of <math id="A2.SS5.p2.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="{\mathcal{H}}_{\Delta}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℋ</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\mathcal{H}}_{\Delta}</annotation></semantics></math>, it is clear that <math id="A2.SS5.p2.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="{\bm{S}}_{\Delta}^{\star}\in{\mathcal{H}}_{\Delta}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msubsup><mi>𝑺</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo>⋆</mo></msubsup><mo>∈</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℋ</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\bm{S}}_{\Delta}^{\star}\in{\mathcal{H}}_{\Delta}</annotation></semantics></math>.
Consequently, <math id="A2.SS5.p2.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="{\bm{S}}_{\Delta}^{\star}\in{\mathcal{D}}_{\Delta}\cap{\mathcal{H}}_{\Delta}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msubsup><mi>𝑺</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo>⋆</mo></msubsup><mo>∈</mo><mrow><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒟</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi></msub><mo>∩</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℋ</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi></msub></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\bm{S}}_{\Delta}^{\star}\in{\mathcal{D}}_{\Delta}\cap{\mathcal{H}}_{\Delta}</annotation></semantics></math>.
With this result, once (<a href="#A2.E79" title="In Proof of Lemma . ‣ B.5 Proof of Lemma ‣ Appendix B Proof for Gumbel-max Watermarks in Section ‣ Optimal Detection for Language Watermarks with Pseudorandom Collision" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">79</span></a>) is established, it follows that</span></p>
<table id="A2.Ex136" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A2.Ex136.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\max_{{\bm{S}}\in{\mathcal{D}}_{\Delta}\setminus{\mathcal{H}}_{\Delta}}\int F_{\bm{S}}(y){\mathrm{e}}^{-h(y)}h({\mathrm{d}}y)\leq\int F_{{\bm{S}}_{\Delta}^{\star}}(y){\mathrm{e}}^{-h(y)}h({\mathrm{d}}y)\leq\max_{{\bm{S}}\in{\mathcal{D}}_{\Delta}\cap{\mathcal{H}}_{\Delta}}\int F_{\bm{S}}(y){\mathrm{e}}^{-h(y)}h({\mathrm{d}}y)," display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>max</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mrow><mmultiscripts><mo>∫</mo><mprescripts></mprescripts><mrow><mi>𝑺</mi><mo>∈</mo><mrow><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒟</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi></msub><mo>∖</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℋ</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi></msub></mrow></mrow><mrow></mrow></mmultiscripts><mo>⁡</mo><msub><mi>F</mi><mi>𝑺</mi></msub></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>y</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>e</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>h</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>y</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>h</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">𝑑</mo><mi>y</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.111em">≤</mo><mrow><mo>∫</mo><mrow><msub><mi>F</mi><msubsup><mi>𝑺</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo>⋆</mo></msubsup></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>y</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>e</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>h</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>y</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>h</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">𝑑</mo><mi>y</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>≤</mo><mrow><mi>max</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mrow><mmultiscripts><mo>∫</mo><mprescripts></mprescripts><mrow><mi>𝑺</mi><mo>∈</mo><mrow><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒟</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi></msub><mo>∩</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℋ</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi></msub></mrow></mrow><mrow></mrow></mmultiscripts><mo>⁡</mo><msub><mi>F</mi><mi>𝑺</mi></msub></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>y</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>e</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>h</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>y</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>h</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">𝑑</mo><mi>y</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\max_{{\bm{S}}\in{\mathcal{D}}_{\Delta}\setminus{\mathcal{H}}_{\Delta}}\int F_{\bm{S}}(y){\mathrm{e}}^{-h(y)}h({\mathrm{d}}y)\leq\int F_{{\bm{S}}_{\Delta}^{\star}}(y){\mathrm{e}}^{-h(y)}h({\mathrm{d}}y)\leq\max_{{\bm{S}}\in{\mathcal{D}}_{\Delta}\cap{\mathcal{H}}_{\Delta}}\int F_{\bm{S}}(y){\mathrm{e}}^{-h(y)}h({\mathrm{d}}y),</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A2.SS5.p2.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="A2.SS5.p2.2.1" class="ltx_text">which completes the proof.</span></p>
</div>
<div id="A2.SS5.p3" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A2.SS5.p3.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A2.SS5.p3.1.1" class="ltx_text">In the following, we will prove (<a href="#A2.E79" title="In Proof of Lemma . ‣ B.5 Proof of Lemma ‣ Appendix B Proof for Gumbel-max Watermarks in Section ‣ Optimal Detection for Language Watermarks with Pseudorandom Collision" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">79</span></a>).
For any <math id="A2.SS5.p3.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="{\bm{S}}\in{\mathcal{D}}_{\Delta}\setminus{\mathcal{H}}_{\Delta}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>𝑺</mi><mo>∈</mo><mrow><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒟</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi></msub><mo>∖</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℋ</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi></msub></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\bm{S}}\in{\mathcal{D}}_{\Delta}\setminus{\mathcal{H}}_{\Delta}</annotation></semantics></math>, by Eqn. (<a href="#A2.E78" title="In Proof of Lemma . ‣ B.4 Proof of Lemma ‣ Appendix B Proof for Gumbel-max Watermarks in Section ‣ Optimal Detection for Language Watermarks with Pseudorandom Collision" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">78</span></a>), Lemma <a href="#S7.Thmlem3" title="Lemma 7.3 (Schur-convexity). ‣ 7.1 Proof of Theorem ‣ 7 Proof of Main Results ‣ Optimal Detection for Language Watermarks with Pseudorandom Collision" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">7.3</span></a>, and the definition of Schur-convexity, it follows that</span></p>
<table id="A2.Ex137" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A2.Ex137.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\int F_{\bm{S}}(y){\mathrm{e}}^{-h(y)}h({\mathrm{d}}y)\leq\int F_{{\bm{S}}_{1}}(y){\mathrm{e}}^{-h(y)}h({\mathrm{d}}y)," display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mo>∫</mo><mrow><msub><mi>F</mi><mi>𝑺</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>y</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>e</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>h</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>y</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>h</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">𝑑</mo><mi>y</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.111em">≤</mo><mrow><mo>∫</mo><mrow><msub><mi>F</mi><msub><mi>𝑺</mi><mn>1</mn></msub></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>y</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>e</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>h</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>y</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>h</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">𝑑</mo><mi>y</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\int F_{\bm{S}}(y){\mathrm{e}}^{-h(y)}h({\mathrm{d}}y)\leq\int F_{{\bm{S}}_{1}}(y){\mathrm{e}}^{-h(y)}h({\mathrm{d}}y),</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A2.SS5.p3.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="A2.SS5.p3.2.1" class="ltx_text">where <math id="A2.SS5.p3.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="{\bm{S}}_{1}:=\left(\sum_{w}S_{w},0,\ldots,0\right)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>𝑺</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>:=</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><msub><mo lspace="0em">∑</mo><mi>w</mi></msub><msub><mi>S</mi><mi>w</mi></msub></mrow><mo>,</mo><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi><mo>,</mo><mn>0</mn><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\bm{S}}_{1}:=\left(\sum_{w}S_{w},0,\ldots,0\right)</annotation></semantics></math> majorizes the given <math id="A2.SS5.p3.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="{\bm{S}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>𝑺</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\bm{S}}</annotation></semantics></math>.
Next, note that <math id="A2.SS5.p3.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="{\bm{S}}\in{\mathcal{D}}_{\Delta}\setminus{\mathcal{H}}_{\Delta}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>𝑺</mi><mo>∈</mo><mrow><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒟</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi></msub><mo>∖</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℋ</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi></msub></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\bm{S}}\in{\mathcal{D}}_{\Delta}\setminus{\mathcal{H}}_{\Delta}</annotation></semantics></math> implies <math id="A2.SS5.p3.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\sum_{w}S_{w}\leq\frac{1-\Delta}{1+\frac{\Delta}{|{\mathcal{V}}|\wedge|{{\mathcal{W}}}|-1}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mo>∑</mo><mi>w</mi></msub><msub><mi>S</mi><mi>w</mi></msub></mrow><mo>≤</mo><mfrac><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi></mrow><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>+</mo><mfrac><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mrow><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒱</mi><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow><mo>∧</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒲</mi><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mfrac></mrow></mfrac></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\sum_{w}S_{w}\leq\frac{1-\Delta}{1+\frac{\Delta}{|{\mathcal{V}}|\wedge|{{\mathcal{W}}}|-1}}</annotation></semantics></math>. Since <math id="A2.SS5.p3.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="F_{\bm{P}}(y)=y^{1/S_{1}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>F</mi><mi>𝑷</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>y</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><msup><mi>y</mi><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>/</mo><msub><mi>S</mi><mn>1</mn></msub></mrow></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">F_{\bm{P}}(y)=y^{1/S_{1}}</annotation></semantics></math> is increasing in <math id="A2.SS5.p3.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="S_{1}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>S</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">S_{1}</annotation></semantics></math> when <math id="A2.SS5.p3.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="{\bm{S}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>𝑺</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\bm{S}}</annotation></semantics></math> has only one non-zero entry (that is, <math id="A2.SS5.p3.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="{\bm{S}}=(S_{1},0,\ldots,0)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>𝑺</mi><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>S</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi><mo>,</mo><mn>0</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\bm{S}}=(S_{1},0,\ldots,0)</annotation></semantics></math>), we deduce that <math id="A2.SS5.p3.m10" class="ltx_Math" alttext="F_{{\bm{S}}_{1}}(y)\leq F_{{\bm{S}}_{\Delta}^{\star}}(y)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>F</mi><msub><mi>𝑺</mi><mn>1</mn></msub></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>y</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>≤</mo><mrow><msub><mi>F</mi><msubsup><mi>𝑺</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo>⋆</mo></msubsup></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>y</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">F_{{\bm{S}}_{1}}(y)\leq F_{{\bm{S}}_{\Delta}^{\star}}(y)</annotation></semantics></math> for any <math id="A2.SS5.p3.m11" class="ltx_Math" alttext="y\in[0,1]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>y</mi><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">y\in[0,1]</annotation></semantics></math>.
As a result, the last inequality holds, which completes the proof.
∎</span></p>
</div>
</div>
</section>
<section id="A2.SS6" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection">B.6 </span>Proof of Lemma <a href="#S7.Thmlem5" title="Lemma 7.5 (Convex envelope of 𝒟_Δ∩ℋ_Δ). ‣ 7.1 Proof of Theorem ‣ 7 Proof of Main Results ‣ Optimal Detection for Language Watermarks with Pseudorandom Collision" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">7.5</span></a></h3>

<div id="A2.SS6.2" class="ltx_proof">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_font_italic ltx_title_proof">Proof of Lemma <a href="#S7.Thmlem5" title="Lemma 7.5 (Convex envelope of 𝒟_Δ∩ℋ_Δ). ‣ 7.1 Proof of Theorem ‣ 7 Proof of Main Results ‣ Optimal Detection for Language Watermarks with Pseudorandom Collision" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">7.5</span></a>.</h6>
<div id="A2.SS6.p1" class="ltx_para">
<ol id="A2.I2" class="ltx_enumerate">
<li id="A2.I2.i1" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">1.</span> 
<div id="A2.I2.i1.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A2.I2.i1.p1.1" class="ltx_p">Since <math id="A2.I2.i1.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="{\mathcal{K}}_{\Delta}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒦</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\mathcal{K}}_{\Delta}</annotation></semantics></math> is the intersection of several half-spaces, it forms a convex polyhedron. We now prove that the extreme points of <math id="A2.I2.i1.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="{\mathcal{K}}_{\Delta}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒦</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\mathcal{K}}_{\Delta}</annotation></semantics></math> are precisely the elements of <math id="A2.I2.i1.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="{\mathcal{E}}_{\Delta}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℰ</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\mathcal{E}}_{\Delta}</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>
</div>
<div id="A2.I2.i1.p2" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A2.I2.i1.p2.1" class="ltx_p">First, observe that both <math id="A2.I2.i1.p2.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\bm{P}_{\Delta}^{\star}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msubsup><mi>𝑷</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo>⋆</mo></msubsup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\bm{P}_{\Delta}^{\star}</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="A2.I2.i1.p2.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="{\bm{S}}_{\Delta}^{\star}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msubsup><mi>𝑺</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo>⋆</mo></msubsup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\bm{S}}_{\Delta}^{\star}</annotation></semantics></math> belong to <math id="A2.I2.i1.p2.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="{\mathcal{K}}_{\Delta}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒦</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\mathcal{K}}_{\Delta}</annotation></semantics></math>, and by the permutation invariance of <math id="A2.I2.i1.p2.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="{\mathcal{K}}_{\Delta}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒦</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\mathcal{K}}_{\Delta}</annotation></semantics></math>, we have <math id="A2.I2.i1.p2.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="{\mathcal{E}}_{\Delta}\subseteq{\mathcal{K}}_{\Delta}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℰ</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi></msub><mo>⊆</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒦</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\mathcal{E}}_{\Delta}\subseteq{\mathcal{K}}_{\Delta}</annotation></semantics></math>. This implies <math id="A2.I2.i1.p2.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathrm{conv}({\mathcal{E}}_{\Delta})\subseteq{\mathcal{K}}_{\Delta}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>conv</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℰ</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>⊆</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒦</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathrm{conv}({\mathcal{E}}_{\Delta})\subseteq{\mathcal{K}}_{\Delta}</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>
</div>
<div id="A2.I2.i1.p3" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A2.I2.i1.p3.1" class="ltx_p">To prove the reverse inclusion, it suffices to show that any point in <math id="A2.I2.i1.p3.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="{\mathcal{K}}_{\Delta}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒦</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\mathcal{K}}_{\Delta}</annotation></semantics></math> can be expressed as a convex combination of points in <math id="A2.I2.i1.p3.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="{\mathcal{E}}_{\Delta}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℰ</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\mathcal{E}}_{\Delta}</annotation></semantics></math>. Consider an arbitrary <math id="A2.I2.i1.p3.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="{\bm{S}}\in{\mathcal{K}}_{\Delta}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>𝑺</mi><mo>∈</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒦</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\bm{S}}\in{\mathcal{K}}_{\Delta}</annotation></semantics></math>, and define <math id="A2.I2.i1.p3.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="C=\sum_{w}S_{w}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>C</mi><mo rspace="0.111em">=</mo><mrow><msub><mo>∑</mo><mi>w</mi></msub><msub><mi>S</mi><mi>w</mi></msub></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">C=\sum_{w}S_{w}</annotation></semantics></math> as the sum of its coordinates. By the definition of <math id="A2.I2.i1.p3.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="{\mathcal{K}}_{\Delta}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒦</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\mathcal{K}}_{\Delta}</annotation></semantics></math>, the largest coordinate of <math id="A2.I2.i1.p3.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="{\bm{S}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>𝑺</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\bm{S}}</annotation></semantics></math> satisfies</p>
<table id="A2.Ex138" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A2.Ex138.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\max_{w}S_{w}\leq(1-\Delta)\left(1-\frac{1-C}{|{\mathcal{V}}|\wedge|{{\mathcal{W}}}|}\right)." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><munder><mi>max</mi><mi>w</mi></munder><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><msub><mi>S</mi><mi>w</mi></msub></mrow><mo>≤</mo><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mfrac><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mi>C</mi></mrow><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒱</mi><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow><mo>∧</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒲</mi><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow></mrow></mfrac></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\max_{w}S_{w}\leq(1-\Delta)\left(1-\frac{1-C}{|{\mathcal{V}}|\wedge|{{\mathcal{W}}}|}\right).</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A2.I2.i1.p3.2" class="ltx_p">We assert that <math id="A2.I2.i1.p3.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="{\bm{S}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>𝑺</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\bm{S}}</annotation></semantics></math> is majorized by the following vector</p>
<table id="A2.Ex139" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A2.Ex139.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\bm{S}_{\mathrm{new}}=\left((1-\Delta)(1-\frac{1-C}{|{\mathcal{V}}|\wedge|{{\mathcal{W}}}|}),C-(1-\Delta)(1-\frac{1-C}{|{\mathcal{V}}|\wedge|{{\mathcal{W}}}|}),0,\dots\right)," display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>𝑺</mi><mi>new</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mfrac><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mi>C</mi></mrow><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒱</mi><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow><mo>∧</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒲</mi><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow></mrow></mfrac></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo><mrow><mi>C</mi><mo>−</mo><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mfrac><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mi>C</mi></mrow><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒱</mi><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow><mo>∧</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒲</mi><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow></mrow></mfrac></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\bm{S}_{\mathrm{new}}=\left((1-\Delta)(1-\frac{1-C}{|{\mathcal{V}}|\wedge|{{\mathcal{W}}}|}),C-(1-\Delta)(1-\frac{1-C}{|{\mathcal{V}}|\wedge|{{\mathcal{W}}}|}),0,\dots\right),</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A2.I2.i1.p3.3" class="ltx_p">which, by definition, belongs to <math id="A2.I2.i1.p3.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="{\mathcal{K}}_{\Delta}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒦</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\mathcal{K}}_{\Delta}</annotation></semantics></math>.
By Lemma <a href="#A2.Thmlem2" title="Lemma B.2 ([]). ‣ item 1 ‣ Proof of Lemma . ‣ B.6 Proof of Lemma ‣ Appendix B Proof for Gumbel-max Watermarks in Section ‣ Optimal Detection for Language Watermarks with Pseudorandom Collision" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">B.2</span></a>, <math id="A2.I2.i1.p3.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="{\bm{S}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>𝑺</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\bm{S}}</annotation></semantics></math> can thus be expressed as a convex combination of permutations of <math id="A2.I2.i1.p3.m10" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\bm{S}_{\mathrm{new}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>𝑺</mi><mi>new</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\bm{S}_{\mathrm{new}}</annotation></semantics></math>. Since <math id="A2.I2.i1.p3.m11" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\bm{S}_{\mathrm{new}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>𝑺</mi><mi>new</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\bm{S}_{\mathrm{new}}</annotation></semantics></math> itself is a convex combination of <math id="A2.I2.i1.p3.m12" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\bm{P}_{\Delta}^{\star}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msubsup><mi>𝑷</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo>⋆</mo></msubsup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\bm{P}_{\Delta}^{\star}</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="A2.I2.i1.p3.m13" class="ltx_Math" alttext="{\bm{S}}_{\Delta}^{\star}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msubsup><mi>𝑺</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo>⋆</mo></msubsup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\bm{S}}_{\Delta}^{\star}</annotation></semantics></math>, it follows that <math id="A2.I2.i1.p3.m14" class="ltx_Math" alttext="{\bm{S}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>𝑺</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\bm{S}}</annotation></semantics></math> is a convex combination of points in <math id="A2.I2.i1.p3.m15" class="ltx_Math" alttext="{\mathcal{E}}_{\Delta}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℰ</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\mathcal{E}}_{\Delta}</annotation></semantics></math>. This completes the proof.</p>
</div>
<div id="A2.Thmlem2" class="ltx_theorem ltx_theorem_lem">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_title_theorem"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_theorem"><span id="A2.Thmlem2.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Lemma B.2</span></span><span id="A2.Thmlem2.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold"> </span>(<cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_cite">[<a href="#bib.bib30" title="" class="ltx_ref">30</a>]</cite>)<span id="A2.Thmlem2.4" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">.</span></h6>
<div id="A2.Thmlem2.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A2.Thmlem2.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A2.Thmlem2.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">Given two vectors <math id="A2.Thmlem2.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="{\bm{x}},{\bm{y}}\in{\mathbb{R}}^{d}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>𝐱</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>𝐲</mi></mrow><mo>∈</mo><msup><mi>ℝ</mi><mi>d</mi></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\bm{x}},{\bm{y}}\in{\mathbb{R}}^{d}</annotation></semantics></math>, if <math id="A2.Thmlem2.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="{\bm{x}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>𝐱</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\bm{x}}</annotation></semantics></math> majorizes <math id="A2.Thmlem2.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="{\bm{y}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>𝐲</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\bm{y}}</annotation></semantics></math>, then <math id="A2.Thmlem2.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="{\bm{y}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>𝐲</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\bm{y}}</annotation></semantics></math> is a convex combination of <math id="A2.Thmlem2.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="{\bm{x}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>𝐱</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\bm{x}}</annotation></semantics></math> and its permutations.</span></p>
</div>
</div></li>
<li id="A2.I2.i2" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">2.</span> 
<div id="A2.I2.i2.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A2.I2.i2.p1.1" class="ltx_p">By Lemma <a href="#S7.Thmlem2" title="Lemma 7.2 (Properties of the domain 𝒟_Δ). ‣ 7.1 Proof of Theorem ‣ 7 Proof of Main Results ‣ Optimal Detection for Language Watermarks with Pseudorandom Collision" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">7.2</span></a>, we know that <math id="A2.I2.i2.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="{\bm{S}}_{\Delta}^{\star}\in{\mathcal{D}}_{\Delta}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msubsup><mi>𝑺</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo>⋆</mo></msubsup><mo>∈</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒟</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\bm{S}}_{\Delta}^{\star}\in{\mathcal{D}}_{\Delta}</annotation></semantics></math>. Additionally, we have <math id="A2.I2.i2.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\bm{P}_{\Delta}^{\star}\in{\mathcal{D}}_{\Delta}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msubsup><mi>𝑷</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo>⋆</mo></msubsup><mo>∈</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒟</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\bm{P}_{\Delta}^{\star}\in{\mathcal{D}}_{\Delta}</annotation></semantics></math> because setting <math id="A2.I2.i2.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\bm{P}_{t_{1}}=\cdots=\bm{P}_{t_{k}}=\bm{P}_{\Delta}^{\star}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>𝑷</mi><msub><mi>t</mi><mn>1</mn></msub></msub><mo rspace="0.1389em">=</mo><mo lspace="0.1389em" rspace="0.1389em">⋯</mo><mo lspace="0.1389em">=</mo><msub><mi>𝑷</mi><msub><mi>t</mi><mi>k</mi></msub></msub><mo>=</mo><msubsup><mi>𝑷</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo>⋆</mo></msubsup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\bm{P}_{t_{1}}=\cdots=\bm{P}_{t_{k}}=\bm{P}_{\Delta}^{\star}</annotation></semantics></math> results in a corresponding <math id="A2.I2.i2.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="{\bm{S}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>𝑺</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\bm{S}}</annotation></semantics></math>-vector equal to <math id="A2.I2.i2.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\bm{P}_{\Delta}^{\star}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msubsup><mi>𝑷</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo>⋆</mo></msubsup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\bm{P}_{\Delta}^{\star}</annotation></semantics></math>, which, by definition, belongs to <math id="A2.I2.i2.p1.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="{\mathcal{D}}_{\Delta}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒟</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\mathcal{D}}_{\Delta}</annotation></semantics></math>. Combining these observations with the permutation invariance of <math id="A2.I2.i2.p1.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="{\mathcal{D}}_{\Delta}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒟</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\mathcal{D}}_{\Delta}</annotation></semantics></math>, we conclude that <math id="A2.I2.i2.p1.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="{\mathcal{E}}_{\Delta}\subseteq{\mathcal{D}}_{\Delta}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℰ</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi></msub><mo>⊆</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒟</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\mathcal{E}}_{\Delta}\subseteq{\mathcal{D}}_{\Delta}</annotation></semantics></math>.
On the other hand, by definition, we also have <math id="A2.I2.i2.p1.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="{\mathcal{E}}_{\Delta}\subseteq{\mathcal{K}}_{\Delta}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℰ</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi></msub><mo>⊆</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒦</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\mathcal{E}}_{\Delta}\subseteq{\mathcal{K}}_{\Delta}</annotation></semantics></math>. The conclusion then follows.</p>
</div></li>
<li id="A2.I2.i3" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">3.</span> 
<div id="A2.I2.i3.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A2.I2.i3.p1.1" class="ltx_p">It suffices to prove that <math id="A2.I2.i3.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="{\mathcal{D}}_{\Delta}\cap{\mathcal{H}}_{\Delta}\subseteq{\mathcal{K}}_{\Delta}\subseteq\mathrm{conv}({\mathcal{D}}_{\Delta}\cap{\mathcal{H}}_{\Delta})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒟</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi></msub><mo>∩</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℋ</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi></msub></mrow><mo>⊆</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒦</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi></msub><mo>⊆</mo><mrow><mi>conv</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒟</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi></msub><mo>∩</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℋ</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\mathcal{D}}_{\Delta}\cap{\mathcal{H}}_{\Delta}\subseteq{\mathcal{K}}_{\Delta}\subseteq\mathrm{conv}({\mathcal{D}}_{\Delta}\cap{\mathcal{H}}_{\Delta})</annotation></semantics></math> since <math id="A2.I2.i3.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="{\mathcal{K}}_{\Delta}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒦</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\mathcal{K}}_{\Delta}</annotation></semantics></math> is convex.
By Lemma <a href="#S7.Thmlem2" title="Lemma 7.2 (Properties of the domain 𝒟_Δ). ‣ 7.1 Proof of Theorem ‣ 7 Proof of Main Results ‣ Optimal Detection for Language Watermarks with Pseudorandom Collision" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">7.2</span></a>, we know that <math id="A2.I2.i3.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="{\mathcal{D}}_{\Delta}\cap{\mathcal{H}}_{\Delta}\subseteq{\mathcal{K}}_{\Delta}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒟</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi></msub><mo>∩</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℋ</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi></msub></mrow><mo>⊆</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒦</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\mathcal{D}}_{\Delta}\cap{\mathcal{H}}_{\Delta}\subseteq{\mathcal{K}}_{\Delta}</annotation></semantics></math>. We now turn to the opposite direction.
By the first point, we have <math id="A2.I2.i3.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="{\mathcal{K}}_{\Delta}=\mathrm{conv}({\mathcal{E}}_{\Delta})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒦</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>conv</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℰ</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\mathcal{K}}_{\Delta}=\mathrm{conv}({\mathcal{E}}_{\Delta})</annotation></semantics></math>. We have that <math id="A2.I2.i3.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="{\mathcal{E}}_{\Delta}\subseteq{\mathcal{D}}_{\Delta}\cap{\mathcal{H}}_{\Delta}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℰ</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi></msub><mo>⊆</mo><mrow><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒟</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi></msub><mo>∩</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℋ</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi></msub></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\mathcal{E}}_{\Delta}\subseteq{\mathcal{D}}_{\Delta}\cap{\mathcal{H}}_{\Delta}</annotation></semantics></math> from the second point. Consequently, it follows that <math id="A2.I2.i3.p1.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="{\mathcal{K}}_{\Delta}\subseteq\mathrm{conv}({\mathcal{D}}_{\Delta}\cap{\mathcal{H}}_{\Delta})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒦</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi></msub><mo>⊆</mo><mrow><mi>conv</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒟</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi></msub><mo>∩</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℋ</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\mathcal{K}}_{\Delta}\subseteq\mathrm{conv}({\mathcal{D}}_{\Delta}\cap{\mathcal{H}}_{\Delta})</annotation></semantics></math>, which completes the proof.</p>
</div></li>
</ol>
<p id="A2.SS6.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A2.SS6.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text">∎</span></p>
</div>
</div>
</section>
<section id="A2.SS7" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection">B.7 </span>Proof of Lemma <a href="#S7.Thmlem6" title="Lemma 7.6 (Maximum over polyhedron). ‣ 7.1 Proof of Theorem ‣ 7 Proof of Main Results ‣ Optimal Detection for Language Watermarks with Pseudorandom Collision" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">7.6</span></a></h3>

<div id="A2.SS7.2" class="ltx_proof">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_font_italic ltx_title_proof">Proof of Lemma <a href="#S7.Thmlem6" title="Lemma 7.6 (Maximum over polyhedron). ‣ 7.1 Proof of Theorem ‣ 7 Proof of Main Results ‣ Optimal Detection for Language Watermarks with Pseudorandom Collision" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">7.6</span></a>.</h6>
<div id="A2.SS7.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A2.SS7.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A2.SS7.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text">We note that</span></p>
<table id="A2.Ex140" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A2.Ex140.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\sup_{{\bm{S}}\in{\mathcal{K}}_{\Delta}}\int F_{\bm{S}}(y){\mathrm{e}}^{-h(y)}h({\mathrm{d}}y)=\sup_{C\in[\frac{1-\Delta}{1+\frac{\Delta}{|{\mathcal{V}}|\wedge|{{\mathcal{W}}}|-1}},1]}\sup_{{\bm{S}}\in{\mathcal{K}}_{\Delta}:\sum_{w}S_{w}=C}\int F_{\bm{S}}(y){\mathrm{e}}^{-h(y)}h({\mathrm{d}}y)." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><munder><mo movablelimits="false">sup</mo><mrow><mi>𝑺</mi><mo>∈</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒦</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi></msub></mrow></munder><mo lspace="0.167em">∫</mo><msub><mi>F</mi><mi>𝑺</mi></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>y</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><msup><mi>e</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>h</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>y</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></msup><mi>h</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>d</mi><mi>y</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo rspace="0.1389em">=</mo><munder><mo lspace="0.1389em" movablelimits="false" rspace="0.0835em">sup</mo><mrow><mi>C</mi><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><mfrac><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi></mrow><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>+</mo><mfrac><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mrow><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒱</mi><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow><mo>∧</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒲</mi><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mfrac></mrow></mfrac><mo>,</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow></munder><munder><mo lspace="0.0835em" movablelimits="false" rspace="0em">sup</mo><mrow><mi>𝑺</mi><mo>∈</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒦</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi></msub><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mrow><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="false"><msub><mo maxsize="0.700em" minsize="0.700em" stretchy="true">∑</mo><mi>w</mi></msub></mstyle><msub><mi>S</mi><mi>w</mi></msub></mrow><mo>=</mo><mi>C</mi></mrow></mrow></munder><mo>∫</mo><msub><mi>F</mi><mi>𝑺</mi></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>y</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><msup><mi>e</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>h</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>y</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></msup><mi>h</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>d</mi><mi>y</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\sup_{{\bm{S}}\in{\mathcal{K}}_{\Delta}}\int F_{\bm{S}}(y){\mathrm{e}}^{-h(y)}h({\mathrm{d}}y)=\sup_{C\in[\frac{1-\Delta}{1+\frac{\Delta}{|{\mathcal{V}}|\wedge|{{\mathcal{W}}}|-1}},1]}\sup_{{\bm{S}}\in{\mathcal{K}}_{\Delta}:\sum_{w}S_{w}=C}\int F_{\bm{S}}(y){\mathrm{e}}^{-h(y)}h({\mathrm{d}}y).</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A2.SS7.p1.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="A2.SS7.p1.2.1" class="ltx_text">On the intersection of the plane <math id="A2.SS7.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\sum_{w}S_{w}=C" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mo>∑</mo><mi>w</mi></msub><msub><mi>S</mi><mi>w</mi></msub></mrow><mo>=</mo><mi>C</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\sum_{w}S_{w}=C</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="A2.SS7.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="{\mathcal{K}}_{\Delta}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒦</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\mathcal{K}}_{\Delta}</annotation></semantics></math>, we assert that <math id="A2.SS7.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\lambda{\bm{S}}_{\Delta}^{\star}+(1-\lambda)\bm{P}_{\Delta}^{\star}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>λ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>𝑺</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo>⋆</mo></msubsup></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mi>λ</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>𝑷</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo>⋆</mo></msubsup></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\lambda{\bm{S}}_{\Delta}^{\star}+(1-\lambda)\bm{P}_{\Delta}^{\star}</annotation></semantics></math> majorizes any other points because it has the largest possible first entry.
The calculation shows that here</span></p>
<table id="A2.Ex141" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A2.Ex141.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\lambda=\frac{(1-C)\cdot(|{\mathcal{V}}|\wedge|{{\mathcal{W}}}|-1+\Delta)}{\Delta\cdot|{\mathcal{V}}|\wedge|{{\mathcal{W}}}|}\in[0,1]." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>λ</mi><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mi>C</mi></mrow><mo rspace="0.055em" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mrow><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒱</mi><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow><mo>∧</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒲</mi><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo>+</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mrow><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒱</mi><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>∧</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒲</mi><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow></mrow></mfrac><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\lambda=\frac{(1-C)\cdot(|{\mathcal{V}}|\wedge|{{\mathcal{W}}}|-1+\Delta)}{\Delta\cdot|{\mathcal{V}}|\wedge|{{\mathcal{W}}}|}\in[0,1].</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A2.SS7.p1.3" class="ltx_p"><span id="A2.SS7.p1.3.1" class="ltx_text">By the definition of Schur-convexity, we have</span></p>
<table id="A2.Ex142" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A2.Ex142.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\sup_{{\bm{S}}\in{\mathcal{K}}_{\Delta}:\sum_{w}S_{w}=C}\int F_{\bm{S}}(y){\mathrm{e}}^{-h(y)}h({\mathrm{d}}y)=\int F_{\lambda{\bm{S}}_{\Delta}^{\star}+(1-\lambda)\bm{P}_{\Delta}^{\star}}(y){\mathrm{e}}^{-h(y)}h({\mathrm{d}}y)=:G(C)." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><munder><mo movablelimits="false">sup</mo><mrow><mi>𝑺</mi><mo>∈</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒦</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi></msub><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mrow><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="false"><msub><mo maxsize="0.700em" minsize="0.700em" stretchy="true">∑</mo><mi>w</mi></msub></mstyle><msub><mi>S</mi><mi>w</mi></msub></mrow><mo>=</mo><mi>C</mi></mrow></mrow></munder><mo lspace="0.167em">∫</mo><msub><mi>F</mi><mi>𝑺</mi></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>y</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><msup><mi>e</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>h</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>y</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></msup><mi>h</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>d</mi><mi>y</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo rspace="0.111em">=</mo><mo>∫</mo><msub><mi>F</mi><mrow><mrow><mi>λ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>𝑺</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo>⋆</mo></msubsup></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mi>λ</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>𝑷</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo>⋆</mo></msubsup></mrow></mrow></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>y</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><msup><mi>e</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>h</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>y</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></msup><mi>h</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>d</mi><mi>y</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo rspace="0em">=</mo><mo rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mi>G</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>C</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\sup_{{\bm{S}}\in{\mathcal{K}}_{\Delta}:\sum_{w}S_{w}=C}\int F_{\bm{S}}(y){\mathrm{e}}^{-h(y)}h({\mathrm{d}}y)=\int F_{\lambda{\bm{S}}_{\Delta}^{\star}+(1-\lambda)\bm{P}_{\Delta}^{\star}}(y){\mathrm{e}}^{-h(y)}h({\mathrm{d}}y)=:G(C).</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A2.SS7.p1.4" class="ltx_p"><span id="A2.SS7.p1.4.1" class="ltx_text">We denote the largest and the second largest entries in <math id="A2.SS7.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\lambda{\bm{S}}_{\Delta}^{\star}+(1-\lambda)\bm{P}_{\Delta}^{\star}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>λ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>𝑺</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo>⋆</mo></msubsup></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mi>λ</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>𝑷</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo>⋆</mo></msubsup></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\lambda{\bm{S}}_{\Delta}^{\star}+(1-\lambda)\bm{P}_{\Delta}^{\star}</annotation></semantics></math> by <math id="A2.SS7.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="S_{1}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>S</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">S_{1}</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="A2.SS7.p1.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="S_{2}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>S</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">S_{2}</annotation></semantics></math>.
One can see that</span></p>
<table id="A2.E80" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A2.E80.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="S_{1}=\lambda\frac{1-\Delta}{1+\frac{\Delta}{|{\mathcal{V}}|\wedge|{{\mathcal{W}}}|-1}}+(1-\lambda)(1-\Delta)\quad\text{and}\quad S_{2}=(1-\lambda)\Delta." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>S</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>λ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mfrac><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi></mrow><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>+</mo><mfrac><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mrow><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒱</mi><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow><mo>∧</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒲</mi><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mfrac></mrow></mfrac></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mi>λ</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mspace style="width:1em;" width="1em"></mspace><mtext>and</mtext><mspace style="width:1em;" width="1em"></mspace><mrow><msub><mi>S</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mi>λ</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">S_{1}=\lambda\frac{1-\Delta}{1+\frac{\Delta}{|{\mathcal{V}}|\wedge|{{\mathcal{W}}}|-1}}+(1-\lambda)(1-\Delta)\quad\text{and}\quad S_{2}=(1-\lambda)\Delta.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(80)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A2.SS7.p1.5" class="ltx_p"><span id="A2.SS7.p1.5.1" class="ltx_text">It then follows that</span></p>
<table id="A2.EGx55" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A2.Ex143"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A2.Ex143.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle F_{\lambda{\bm{S}}_{\Delta}^{\star}+(1-\lambda)\bm{P}_{\Delta}^{\star}}(y)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>F</mi><mrow><mrow><mi>λ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>𝑺</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo>⋆</mo></msubsup></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mi>λ</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>𝑷</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo>⋆</mo></msubsup></mrow></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>y</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle F_{\lambda{\bm{S}}_{\Delta}^{\star}+(1-\lambda)\bm{P}_{\Delta}^{\star}}(y)</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A2.Ex143.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=\frac{S_{1}y^{1/S_{1}}+S_{2}y^{1/S_{2}}}{S_{1}+S_{2}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>S</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>y</mi><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>/</mo><msub><mi>S</mi><mn>1</mn></msub></mrow></msup></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><msub><mi>S</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>y</mi><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>/</mo><msub><mi>S</mi><mn>2</mn></msub></mrow></msup></mrow></mrow><mrow><msub><mi>S</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>+</mo><msub><mi>S</mi><mn>2</mn></msub></mrow></mfrac></mstyle></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=\frac{S_{1}y^{1/S_{1}}+S_{2}y^{1/S_{2}}}{S_{1}+S_{2}}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A2.Ex144"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A2.Ex144.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\overset{(a)}{\leq}\frac{\lambda\frac{1-\Delta}{1+\frac{\Delta}{|{\mathcal{V}}|\wedge|{{\mathcal{W}}}|-1}}y^{\frac{1+\frac{\Delta}{|{\mathcal{V}}|\wedge|{{\mathcal{W}}}|-1}}{1-\Delta}}+(1-\lambda)(1-\Delta)y^{\frac{1}{1-\Delta}}+S_{2}y^{1/S_{2}}}{\lambda\frac{1-\Delta}{1+\frac{\Delta}{|{\mathcal{V}}|\wedge|{{\mathcal{W}}}|-1}}+(1-\lambda)(1-\Delta)+S_{2}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mover accent="true"><mo>≤</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="0.700em" minsize="0.700em">(</mo><mi mathsize="0.700em">a</mi><mo maxsize="0.700em" minsize="0.700em">)</mo></mrow></mover><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><mrow><mi>λ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mfrac><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi></mrow><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>+</mo><mfrac><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mrow><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒱</mi><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow><mo>∧</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒲</mi><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mfrac></mrow></mfrac><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>y</mi><mfrac><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>+</mo><mfrac><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mrow><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒱</mi><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow><mo>∧</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒲</mi><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mfrac></mrow><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi></mrow></mfrac></msup></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mi>λ</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>y</mi><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi></mrow></mfrac></msup></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><msub><mi>S</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>y</mi><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>/</mo><msub><mi>S</mi><mn>2</mn></msub></mrow></msup></mrow></mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>λ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mfrac><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi></mrow><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>+</mo><mfrac><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mrow><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒱</mi><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow><mo>∧</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒲</mi><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mfrac></mrow></mfrac></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mi>λ</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><msub><mi>S</mi><mn>2</mn></msub></mrow></mfrac></mstyle></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\overset{(a)}{\leq}\frac{\lambda\frac{1-\Delta}{1+\frac{\Delta}{|{\mathcal{V}}|\wedge|{{\mathcal{W}}}|-1}}y^{\frac{1+\frac{\Delta}{|{\mathcal{V}}|\wedge|{{\mathcal{W}}}|-1}}{1-\Delta}}+(1-\lambda)(1-\Delta)y^{\frac{1}{1-\Delta}}+S_{2}y^{1/S_{2}}}{\lambda\frac{1-\Delta}{1+\frac{\Delta}{|{\mathcal{V}}|\wedge|{{\mathcal{W}}}|-1}}+(1-\lambda)(1-\Delta)+S_{2}}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A2.Ex145"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A2.Ex145.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\overset{(b)}{\leq}\frac{\lambda\frac{1-\Delta}{1+\frac{\Delta}{|{\mathcal{V}}|\wedge|{{\mathcal{W}}}|-1}}y^{\frac{1+\frac{\Delta}{|{\mathcal{V}}|\wedge|{{\mathcal{W}}}|-1}}{1-\Delta}}+(1-\lambda)(1-\Delta)y^{\frac{1}{1-\Delta}}+(1-\lambda)\Delta y^{\frac{1}{\Delta}}}{\lambda\frac{1-\Delta}{1+\frac{\Delta}{|{\mathcal{V}}|\wedge|{{\mathcal{W}}}|-1}}+(1-\lambda)(1-\Delta)+(1-\lambda)\Delta}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mover accent="true"><mo>≤</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="0.700em" minsize="0.700em">(</mo><mi mathsize="0.700em">b</mi><mo maxsize="0.700em" minsize="0.700em">)</mo></mrow></mover><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><mrow><mi>λ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mfrac><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi></mrow><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>+</mo><mfrac><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mrow><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒱</mi><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow><mo>∧</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒲</mi><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mfrac></mrow></mfrac><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>y</mi><mfrac><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>+</mo><mfrac><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mrow><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒱</mi><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow><mo>∧</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒲</mi><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mfrac></mrow><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi></mrow></mfrac></msup></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mi>λ</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>y</mi><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi></mrow></mfrac></msup></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mi>λ</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>y</mi><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi></mfrac></msup></mrow></mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>λ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mfrac><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi></mrow><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>+</mo><mfrac><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mrow><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒱</mi><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow><mo>∧</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒲</mi><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mfrac></mrow></mfrac></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mi>λ</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mi>λ</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi></mrow></mrow></mfrac></mstyle></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\overset{(b)}{\leq}\frac{\lambda\frac{1-\Delta}{1+\frac{\Delta}{|{\mathcal{V}}|\wedge|{{\mathcal{W}}}|-1}}y^{\frac{1+\frac{\Delta}{|{\mathcal{V}}|\wedge|{{\mathcal{W}}}|-1}}{1-\Delta}}+(1-\lambda)(1-\Delta)y^{\frac{1}{1-\Delta}}+(1-\lambda)\Delta y^{\frac{1}{\Delta}}}{\lambda\frac{1-\Delta}{1+\frac{\Delta}{|{\mathcal{V}}|\wedge|{{\mathcal{W}}}|-1}}+(1-\lambda)(1-\Delta)+(1-\lambda)\Delta}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A2.Ex146"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A2.Ex146.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\overset{(c)}{=}\frac{\lambda\frac{1-\Delta}{1+\frac{\Delta}{|{\mathcal{V}}|\wedge|{{\mathcal{W}}}|-1}}F_{{\bm{S}}_{\Delta}^{\star}}(y)+(1-\lambda)F_{\bm{P}_{\Delta}^{\star}}(y)}{\lambda\frac{1-\Delta}{1+\frac{\Delta}{|{\mathcal{V}}|\wedge|{{\mathcal{W}}}|-1}}+(1-\lambda)}," display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mover accent="true"><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="0.700em" minsize="0.700em">(</mo><mi mathsize="0.700em">c</mi><mo maxsize="0.700em" minsize="0.700em">)</mo></mrow></mover><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><mrow><mi>λ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mfrac><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi></mrow><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>+</mo><mfrac><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mrow><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒱</mi><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow><mo>∧</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒲</mi><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mfrac></mrow></mfrac><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>F</mi><msubsup><mi>𝑺</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo>⋆</mo></msubsup></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>y</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mi>λ</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>F</mi><msubsup><mi>𝑷</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo>⋆</mo></msubsup></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>y</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>λ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mfrac><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi></mrow><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>+</mo><mfrac><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mrow><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒱</mi><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow><mo>∧</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒲</mi><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mfrac></mrow></mfrac></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mi>λ</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mfrac></mstyle></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\overset{(c)}{=}\frac{\lambda\frac{1-\Delta}{1+\frac{\Delta}{|{\mathcal{V}}|\wedge|{{\mathcal{W}}}|-1}}F_{{\bm{S}}_{\Delta}^{\star}}(y)+(1-\lambda)F_{\bm{P}_{\Delta}^{\star}}(y)}{\lambda\frac{1-\Delta}{1+\frac{\Delta}{|{\mathcal{V}}|\wedge|{{\mathcal{W}}}|-1}}+(1-\lambda)},</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A2.SS7.p1.6" class="ltx_p"><span id="A2.SS7.p1.6.1" class="ltx_text">where <math id="A2.SS7.p1.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(a)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>a</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(a)</annotation></semantics></math> uses the fact that the map <math id="A2.SS7.p1.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="S\mapsto Sy^{1/S}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>S</mi><mo stretchy="false">↦</mo><mrow><mi>S</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>y</mi><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>/</mo><mi>S</mi></mrow></msup></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">S\mapsto Sy^{1/S}</annotation></semantics></math> is convex in <math id="A2.SS7.p1.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="S" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>S</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">S</annotation></semantics></math>, <math id="A2.SS7.p1.m10" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(b)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>b</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(b)</annotation></semantics></math> uses the fact that <math id="A2.SS7.p1.m11" class="ltx_Math" alttext="y^{1/S_{2}}\leq y^{\frac{1}{\Delta}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msup><mi>y</mi><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>/</mo><msub><mi>S</mi><mn>2</mn></msub></mrow></msup><mo>≤</mo><msup><mi>y</mi><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi></mfrac></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">y^{1/S_{2}}\leq y^{\frac{1}{\Delta}}</annotation></semantics></math> due to <math id="A2.SS7.p1.m12" class="ltx_Math" alttext="y\in[0,1]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>y</mi><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">y\in[0,1]</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="A2.SS7.p1.m13" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\lambda\in[0,1]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>λ</mi><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\lambda\in[0,1]</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="A2.SS7.p1.m14" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(c)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>c</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(c)</annotation></semantics></math> follows from arrangement.</span></p>
</div>
<div id="A2.SS7.p2" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A2.SS7.p2.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A2.SS7.p2.1.1" class="ltx_text">Therefore, for any <math id="A2.SS7.p2.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="C\in[\frac{1-\Delta}{1+\frac{\Delta}{|{\mathcal{V}}|\wedge|{{\mathcal{W}}}|-1}},1]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>C</mi><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><mfrac><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi></mrow><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>+</mo><mfrac><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mrow><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒱</mi><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow><mo>∧</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒲</mi><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mfrac></mrow></mfrac><mo>,</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">C\in[\frac{1-\Delta}{1+\frac{\Delta}{|{\mathcal{V}}|\wedge|{{\mathcal{W}}}|-1}},1]</annotation></semantics></math>, it follows that</span></p>
<table id="A2.EGx56" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A2.Ex147"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A2.Ex147.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle G(C)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>G</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>C</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle G(C)</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A2.Ex147.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=\int F_{\lambda{\bm{S}}_{\Delta}^{\star}+(1-\lambda)\bm{P}_{\Delta}^{\star}}(y){\mathrm{e}}^{-h(y)}h({\mathrm{d}}y)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mrow><mo>∫</mo><mrow><msub><mi>F</mi><mrow><mrow><mi>λ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>𝑺</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo>⋆</mo></msubsup></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mi>λ</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>𝑷</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo>⋆</mo></msubsup></mrow></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>y</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>e</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>h</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>y</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>h</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">𝑑</mo><mi>y</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mstyle></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=\int F_{\lambda{\bm{S}}_{\Delta}^{\star}+(1-\lambda)\bm{P}_{\Delta}^{\star}}(y){\mathrm{e}}^{-h(y)}h({\mathrm{d}}y)</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A2.Ex148"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A2.Ex148.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\leq\int\frac{\lambda\frac{1-\Delta}{1+\frac{\Delta}{|{\mathcal{V}}|\wedge|{{\mathcal{W}}}|-1}}F_{{\bm{S}}_{\Delta}^{\star}}(y)+(1-\lambda)F_{\bm{P}_{\Delta}^{\star}}(y)}{\lambda\frac{1-\Delta}{1+\frac{\Delta}{|{\mathcal{V}}|\wedge|{{\mathcal{W}}}|-1}}+(1-\lambda)}{\mathrm{e}}^{-h(y)}h({\mathrm{d}}y)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>≤</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mrow><mo>∫</mo><mrow><mfrac><mrow><mrow><mi>λ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mfrac><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi></mrow><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>+</mo><mfrac><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mrow><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒱</mi><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow><mo>∧</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒲</mi><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mfrac></mrow></mfrac><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>F</mi><msubsup><mi>𝑺</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo>⋆</mo></msubsup></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>y</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mi>λ</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>F</mi><msubsup><mi>𝑷</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo>⋆</mo></msubsup></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>y</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>λ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mfrac><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi></mrow><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>+</mo><mfrac><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mrow><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒱</mi><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow><mo>∧</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒲</mi><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mfrac></mrow></mfrac></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mi>λ</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mfrac><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>e</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>h</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>y</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>h</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">𝑑</mo><mi>y</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mstyle></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\leq\int\frac{\lambda\frac{1-\Delta}{1+\frac{\Delta}{|{\mathcal{V}}|\wedge|{{\mathcal{W}}}|-1}}F_{{\bm{S}}_{\Delta}^{\star}}(y)+(1-\lambda)F_{\bm{P}_{\Delta}^{\star}}(y)}{\lambda\frac{1-\Delta}{1+\frac{\Delta}{|{\mathcal{V}}|\wedge|{{\mathcal{W}}}|-1}}+(1-\lambda)}{\mathrm{e}}^{-h(y)}h({\mathrm{d}}y)</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A2.Ex149"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A2.Ex149.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\leq\max\left\{\int F_{{\bm{S}}_{\Delta}^{\star}}{\mathrm{e}}^{-h(y)}h({\mathrm{d}}y),\int F_{\bm{P}_{\Delta}^{\star}}{\mathrm{e}}^{-h(y)}h({\mathrm{d}}y)\right\}," display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>≤</mo><mrow><mi>max</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>{</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mrow><mo>∫</mo><mrow><msub><mi>F</mi><msubsup><mi>𝑺</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo>⋆</mo></msubsup></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>e</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>h</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>y</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>h</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">𝑑</mo><mi>y</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mstyle><mo>,</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mrow><mo>∫</mo><mrow><msub><mi>F</mi><msubsup><mi>𝑷</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo>⋆</mo></msubsup></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>e</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>h</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>y</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>h</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">𝑑</mo><mi>y</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mstyle><mo>}</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\leq\max\left\{\int F_{{\bm{S}}_{\Delta}^{\star}}{\mathrm{e}}^{-h(y)}h({\mathrm{d}}y),\int F_{\bm{P}_{\Delta}^{\star}}{\mathrm{e}}^{-h(y)}h({\mathrm{d}}y)\right\},</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A2.SS7.p2.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="A2.SS7.p2.2.1" class="ltx_text">where the last inequality uses the fact that the maximum value of a linear function on a line segment is attained at the endpoints.</span></p>
</div>
<div id="A2.SS7.p3" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A2.SS7.p3.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A2.SS7.p3.1.1" class="ltx_text">∎</span></p>
</div>
</div>
</section>
<section id="A2.SS8" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection">B.8 </span>Optimal Score in the Intermediate Regime</h3>

<div id="A2.SS8.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A2.SS8.p1.1" class="ltx_p">In this subsection, we detail the discussion in Remark <a href="#S4.Thmrem1" title="Remark 4.1 (Beyond saddle point solutions). ‣ 4 Application to the Gumbel-max Watermark ‣ Optimal Detection for Language Watermarks with Pseudorandom Collision" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">4.1</span></a>.
Specifically, if we do not require the optimal score function to be part of a saddle point solution, that is, the optimal score function solves the following minimization problem</p>
<table id="A2.E81" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A2.E81.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\min_{h}J(h)~~\text{where}~~J(h):=\max_{{\bm{S}}\in{\mathcal{D}}_{\Delta}}L(h,{\bm{S}})~~\text{and}~~L(h,{\bm{S}}):=\EB_{0}[h(Y)]+\log\EB_{F_{\bm{S}}}[{\mathrm{e}}^{-h(Y)}]," display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><munder><mi>min</mi><mi>h</mi></munder><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>J</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>h</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0.660em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mtext>where</mtext><mo lspace="0.660em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>J</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>h</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>:=</mo><mrow><munder><mi>max</mi><mrow><mi>𝑺</mi><mo>∈</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒟</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi></msub></mrow></munder><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>L</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>h</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>𝑺</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0.660em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mtext>and</mtext><mo lspace="0.660em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>L</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>h</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>𝑺</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>:=</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>𝔼</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><mi>h</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>Y</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><msub><mi>𝔼</mi><msub><mi>F</mi><mi>𝐒</mi></msub></msub></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><msup><mi>e</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>h</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>Y</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></msup><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\min_{h}J(h)~~\text{where}~~J(h):=\max_{{\bm{S}}\in{\mathcal{D}}_{\Delta}}L(h,{\bm{S}})~~\text{and}~~L(h,{\bm{S}}):=\EB_{0}[h(Y)]+\log\EB_{F_{\bm{S}}}[{\mathrm{e}}^{-h(Y)}],</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(81)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A2.SS8.p1.2" class="ltx_p">then the optimal score function always exists in the intermediate regime.
However, it doesn’t have a closed form. In the following, we formally state this result.</p>
</div>
<div id="A2.Thmlem3" class="ltx_theorem ltx_theorem_lem">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_title_theorem"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_theorem"><span id="A2.Thmlem3.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Lemma B.3</span></span><span id="A2.Thmlem3.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">.</span></h6>
<div id="A2.Thmlem3.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A2.Thmlem3.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A2.Thmlem3.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">Any score function that minimizes <math id="A2.Thmlem3.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="J" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>J</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">J</annotation></semantics></math> in (<a href="#A2.E81" title="In B.8 Optimal Score in the Intermediate Regime ‣ Appendix B Proof for Gumbel-max Watermarks in Section ‣ Optimal Detection for Language Watermarks with Pseudorandom Collision" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">81</span></a>) is non-decreasing.</span></p>
</div>
</div>
<div id="A2.SS8.2" class="ltx_proof">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_font_italic ltx_title_proof">Proof of Lemma <a href="#A2.Thmlem3" title="Lemma B.3. ‣ B.8 Optimal Score in the Intermediate Regime ‣ Appendix B Proof for Gumbel-max Watermarks in Section ‣ Optimal Detection for Language Watermarks with Pseudorandom Collision" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">B.3</span></a>.</h6>
<div id="A2.SS8.p2" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A2.SS8.p2.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A2.SS8.p2.1.1" class="ltx_text">For any score function <math id="A2.SS8.p2.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="h" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>h</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">h</annotation></semantics></math>, we can construct a non-decreasing transformation <math id="A2.SS8.p2.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="h^{\uparrow}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi>h</mi><mo stretchy="false">↑</mo></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">h^{\uparrow}</annotation></semantics></math> such that <math id="A2.SS8.p2.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="L(h^{\uparrow},{\bm{S}})\leq L(h,{\bm{S}})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>L</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>h</mi><mo stretchy="false">↑</mo></msup><mo>,</mo><mi>𝑺</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>≤</mo><mrow><mi>L</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>h</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>𝑺</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">L(h^{\uparrow},{\bm{S}})\leq L(h,{\bm{S}})</annotation></semantics></math> for all <math id="A2.SS8.p2.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="{\bm{S}}\in{\mathcal{D}}_{\Delta}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>𝑺</mi><mo>∈</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒟</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\bm{S}}\in{\mathcal{D}}_{\Delta}</annotation></semantics></math>.
Specifically, let <math id="A2.SS8.p2.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="G_{h}(z)={\mathbb{P}}_{0}(h(Y)\leq z)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>G</mi><mi>h</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>z</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><msub><mi>ℙ</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>h</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>Y</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>≤</mo><mi>z</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">G_{h}(z)={\mathbb{P}}_{0}(h(Y)\leq z)</annotation></semantics></math> with <math id="A2.SS8.p2.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="Y\sim\mathrm{Unif}(0,1)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>Y</mi><mo>∼</mo><mrow><mi>Unif</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>1</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">Y\sim\mathrm{Unif}(0,1)</annotation></semantics></math> under <math id="A2.SS8.p2.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="H_{0}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>H</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">H_{0}</annotation></semantics></math>, and define <math id="A2.SS8.p2.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="h^{\uparrow}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi>h</mi><mo stretchy="false">↑</mo></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">h^{\uparrow}</annotation></semantics></math> as the generalized inverse of <math id="A2.SS8.p2.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="G_{h}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>G</mi><mi>h</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">G_{h}</annotation></semantics></math>:</span></p>
<table id="A2.Ex150" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A2.Ex150.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="h^{\uparrow}(y)=G_{h}^{-1}(y):=\inf\{z\in{\mathbb{R}}:G_{h}(z)\geq y\}." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><msup><mi>h</mi><mo stretchy="false">↑</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>y</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>G</mi><mi>h</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>y</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.1389em">:=</mo><mrow><mo lspace="0.1389em" movablelimits="false" rspace="0em">inf</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mrow><mi>z</mi><mo>∈</mo><mi>ℝ</mi></mrow><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>G</mi><mi>h</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>z</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>≥</mo><mi>y</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">h^{\uparrow}(y)=G_{h}^{-1}(y):=\inf\{z\in{\mathbb{R}}:G_{h}(z)\geq y\}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A2.SS8.p2.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="A2.SS8.p2.2.1" class="ltx_text">By construction, <math id="A2.SS8.p2.m10" class="ltx_Math" alttext="h^{\uparrow}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi>h</mi><mo stretchy="false">↑</mo></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">h^{\uparrow}</annotation></semantics></math> is non-decreasing. Moreover, for any <math id="A2.SS8.p2.m11" class="ltx_Math" alttext="z\in{\mathbb{R}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>z</mi><mo>∈</mo><mi>ℝ</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">z\in{\mathbb{R}}</annotation></semantics></math>,</span></p>
<table id="A2.Ex151" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A2.Ex151.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="{\mathbb{P}}_{0}(h^{\uparrow}(Y)\leq z)={\mathbb{P}}_{0}(G_{h}^{-1}(Y)\leq z)={\mathbb{P}}_{0}(Y\leq G_{h}(z))=G_{h}(z)={\mathbb{P}}_{0}(h(Y)\leq z)," display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>ℙ</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mrow><msup><mi>h</mi><mo stretchy="false">↑</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>Y</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>≤</mo><mi>z</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><msub><mi>ℙ</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mrow><msubsup><mi>G</mi><mi>h</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>Y</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>≤</mo><mi>z</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><msub><mi>ℙ</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>Y</mi><mo>≤</mo><mrow><msub><mi>G</mi><mi>h</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>z</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><msub><mi>G</mi><mi>h</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>z</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><msub><mi>ℙ</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>h</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>Y</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>≤</mo><mi>z</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\mathbb{P}}_{0}(h^{\uparrow}(Y)\leq z)={\mathbb{P}}_{0}(G_{h}^{-1}(Y)\leq z)={\mathbb{P}}_{0}(Y\leq G_{h}(z))=G_{h}(z)={\mathbb{P}}_{0}(h(Y)\leq z),</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A2.SS8.p2.3" class="ltx_p"><span id="A2.SS8.p2.3.1" class="ltx_text">so <math id="A2.SS8.p2.m12" class="ltx_Math" alttext="h^{\uparrow}(Y)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msup><mi>h</mi><mo stretchy="false">↑</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>Y</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">h^{\uparrow}(Y)</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="A2.SS8.p2.m13" class="ltx_Math" alttext="h(Y)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>h</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>Y</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">h(Y)</annotation></semantics></math> have the same distribution under <math id="A2.SS8.p2.m14" class="ltx_Math" alttext="H_{0}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>H</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">H_{0}</annotation></semantics></math>.</span></p>
</div>
<div id="A2.SS8.p3" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A2.SS8.p3.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A2.SS8.p3.1.1" class="ltx_text">We now examine the two terms in <math id="A2.SS8.p3.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="L(h,{\bm{S}})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>L</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>h</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>𝑺</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">L(h,{\bm{S}})</annotation></semantics></math>.
For the first term, <math id="A2.SS8.p3.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\EB_{0}[h(Y)]=\EB_{0}[h^{\uparrow}(Y)]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>𝔼</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><mi>h</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>Y</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><msub><mi>𝔼</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><msup><mi>h</mi><mo stretchy="false">↑</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>Y</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\EB_{0}[h(Y)]=\EB_{0}[h^{\uparrow}(Y)]</annotation></semantics></math> since the distributions coincide.
Let <math id="A2.SS8.p3.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="f_{\bm{S}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>f</mi><mi>𝑺</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">f_{\bm{S}}</annotation></semantics></math> denote the alternative PDF, which is non-decreasing in <math id="A2.SS8.p3.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="y" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>y</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">y</annotation></semantics></math>.
Consider the second term <math id="A2.SS8.p3.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\int_{0}^{1}{\mathrm{e}}^{-h(y)}f_{\bm{S}}(y){\mathrm{d}}y" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msubsup><mo>∫</mo><mn>0</mn><mn>1</mn></msubsup><mrow><msup><mi>e</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>h</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>y</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>f</mi><mi>𝑺</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>y</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo rspace="0em">𝑑</mo><mi>y</mi></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\int_{0}^{1}{\mathrm{e}}^{-h(y)}f_{\bm{S}}(y){\mathrm{d}}y</annotation></semantics></math>.
The Hardy–Littlewood inequality <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_cite">[<a href="#bib.bib4" title="" class="ltx_ref">4</a>, Chapter 2]</cite> implies that the integral of the product of two functions is minimized when the functions are ordered in opposite monotonicity.
Since <math id="A2.SS8.p3.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="f_{\bm{S}}(y)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>f</mi><mi>𝑺</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>y</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">f_{\bm{S}}(y)</annotation></semantics></math> is non-decreasing, this integral is minimized when <math id="A2.SS8.p3.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="{\mathrm{e}}^{-h(y)}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi>e</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>h</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>y</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\mathrm{e}}^{-h(y)}</annotation></semantics></math> is non-increasing, which is equivalent to <math id="A2.SS8.p3.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="h(y)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>h</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>y</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">h(y)</annotation></semantics></math> being non-decreasing.
Hence, <math id="A2.SS8.p3.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="L(h^{\uparrow},{\bm{S}})\leq L(h,{\bm{S}})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>L</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>h</mi><mo stretchy="false">↑</mo></msup><mo>,</mo><mi>𝑺</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>≤</mo><mrow><mi>L</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>h</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>𝑺</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">L(h^{\uparrow},{\bm{S}})\leq L(h,{\bm{S}})</annotation></semantics></math> for all <math id="A2.SS8.p3.m10" class="ltx_Math" alttext="{\bm{S}}\in{\mathcal{D}}_{\Delta}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>𝑺</mi><mo>∈</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒟</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\bm{S}}\in{\mathcal{D}}_{\Delta}</annotation></semantics></math>.
∎</span></p>
</div>
</div>
<div id="A2.SS8.p4" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A2.SS8.p4.1" class="ltx_p">By Lemma <a href="#A2.Thmlem3" title="Lemma B.3. ‣ B.8 Optimal Score in the Intermediate Regime ‣ Appendix B Proof for Gumbel-max Watermarks in Section ‣ Optimal Detection for Language Watermarks with Pseudorandom Collision" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">B.3</span></a> and Lemmas <a href="#S7.Thmlem4" title="Lemma 7.4 (Reduced domain). ‣ 7.1 Proof of Theorem ‣ 7 Proof of Main Results ‣ Optimal Detection for Language Watermarks with Pseudorandom Collision" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">7.4</span></a>, <a href="#S7.Thmlem5" title="Lemma 7.5 (Convex envelope of 𝒟_Δ∩ℋ_Δ). ‣ 7.1 Proof of Theorem ‣ 7 Proof of Main Results ‣ Optimal Detection for Language Watermarks with Pseudorandom Collision" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">7.5</span></a>, and <a href="#S7.Thmlem6" title="Lemma 7.6 (Maximum over polyhedron). ‣ 7.1 Proof of Theorem ‣ 7 Proof of Main Results ‣ Optimal Detection for Language Watermarks with Pseudorandom Collision" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">7.6</span></a>, for any non-decreasing function <math id="A2.SS8.p4.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="h" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>h</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">h</annotation></semantics></math>,</p>
<table id="A2.E82" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A2.E82.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="J(h)=\max\{L(h,\bm{P}_{\Delta}^{\star}),\,L(h,{\bm{S}}_{\Delta}^{\star})\}," display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>J</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>h</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>max</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mrow><mi>L</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>h</mi><mo>,</mo><msubsup><mi>𝑷</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo>⋆</mo></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.337em">,</mo><mrow><mi>L</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>h</mi><mo>,</mo><msubsup><mi>𝑺</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo>⋆</mo></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">J(h)=\max\{L(h,\bm{P}_{\Delta}^{\star}),\,L(h,{\bm{S}}_{\Delta}^{\star})\},</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(82)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A2.SS8.p4.2" class="ltx_p">where <math id="A2.SS8.p4.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\bm{P}_{\Delta}^{\star}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msubsup><mi>𝑷</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo>⋆</mo></msubsup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\bm{P}_{\Delta}^{\star}</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="A2.SS8.p4.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="{\bm{S}}_{\Delta}^{\star}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msubsup><mi>𝑺</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo>⋆</mo></msubsup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\bm{S}}_{\Delta}^{\star}</annotation></semantics></math> are the two distribution vectors defined in Lemma <a href="#S7.Thmlem5" title="Lemma 7.5 (Convex envelope of 𝒟_Δ∩ℋ_Δ). ‣ 7.1 Proof of Theorem ‣ 7 Proof of Main Results ‣ Optimal Detection for Language Watermarks with Pseudorandom Collision" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">7.5</span></a>.
Since <math id="A2.SS8.p4.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="L(h,{\bm{S}})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>L</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>h</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>𝑺</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">L(h,{\bm{S}})</annotation></semantics></math> is strictly convex in <math id="A2.SS8.p4.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="h" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>h</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">h</annotation></semantics></math> for any fixed <math id="A2.SS8.p4.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="{\bm{S}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>𝑺</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\bm{S}}</annotation></semantics></math>, the above objective, being the pointwise maximum of two strictly convex functions, is also strictly convex.
This ensures the existence and uniqueness of the minimizer of <math id="A2.SS8.p4.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="J" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>J</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">J</annotation></semantics></math>, which is characterized in the following lemma.</p>
</div>
<div id="A2.Thmlem4" class="ltx_theorem ltx_theorem_lem">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_title_theorem"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_theorem"><span id="A2.Thmlem4.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Lemma B.4</span></span><span id="A2.Thmlem4.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold"> </span>(Optimal score function)<span id="A2.Thmlem4.4" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">.</span></h6>
<div id="A2.Thmlem4.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A2.Thmlem4.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A2.Thmlem4.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">When <math id="A2.Thmlem4.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\Delta\in(\Delta_{1}^{\star},\Delta_{2}^{\star})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msubsup><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mn>1</mn><mo>⋆</mo></msubsup><mo>,</mo><msubsup><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mn>2</mn><mo>⋆</mo></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Delta\in(\Delta_{1}^{\star},\Delta_{2}^{\star})</annotation></semantics></math>, that is, we have <math id="A2.Thmlem4.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="L(h_{\bm{P}_{\Delta}^{\star}},\bm{P}_{\Delta}^{\star})&lt;L(h_{\bm{P}_{\Delta}^{\star}},{\bm{S}}_{\Delta}^{\star})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>L</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>h</mi><msubsup><mi>𝐏</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo>⋆</mo></msubsup></msub><mo>,</mo><msubsup><mi>𝐏</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo>⋆</mo></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>&lt;</mo><mrow><mi>L</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>h</mi><msubsup><mi>𝐏</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo>⋆</mo></msubsup></msub><mo>,</mo><msubsup><mi>𝐒</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo>⋆</mo></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">L(h_{\bm{P}_{\Delta}^{\star}},\bm{P}_{\Delta}^{\star})&lt;L(h_{\bm{P}_{\Delta}^{\star}},{\bm{S}}_{\Delta}^{\star})</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="A2.Thmlem4.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="L(h_{{\bm{S}}_{\Delta}^{\star}},{\bm{S}}_{\Delta}^{\star})&lt;L(h_{{\bm{S}}_{\Delta}^{\star}},\bm{P}_{\Delta}^{\star})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>L</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>h</mi><msubsup><mi>𝐒</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo>⋆</mo></msubsup></msub><mo>,</mo><msubsup><mi>𝐒</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo>⋆</mo></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>&lt;</mo><mrow><mi>L</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>h</mi><msubsup><mi>𝐒</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo>⋆</mo></msubsup></msub><mo>,</mo><msubsup><mi>𝐏</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo>⋆</mo></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">L(h_{{\bm{S}}_{\Delta}^{\star}},{\bm{S}}_{\Delta}^{\star})&lt;L(h_{{\bm{S}}_{\Delta}^{\star}},\bm{P}_{\Delta}^{\star})</annotation></semantics></math>, the optimal score that minimizes <math id="A2.Thmlem4.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="J" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>J</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">J</annotation></semantics></math> defined in (<a href="#A2.E81" title="In B.8 Optimal Score in the Intermediate Regime ‣ Appendix B Proof for Gumbel-max Watermarks in Section ‣ Optimal Detection for Language Watermarks with Pseudorandom Collision" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">81</span></a>) is</span></p>
<table id="A2.Ex152" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A2.Ex152.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="h_{\lambda^{\star}}^{\mathrm{gum}}(y)=\log(\lambda^{\star}\cdot y^{\frac{(|{\mathcal{V}}|\wedge|{{\mathcal{W}}}|)\,\Delta}{(|{\mathcal{V}}|\wedge|{{\mathcal{W}}}|-1)(1-\Delta)}}+(1-\lambda^{\star})\cdot(y^{\frac{\Delta}{1-\Delta}}+y^{\frac{1-\Delta}{\Delta}}))" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msubsup><mi>h</mi><msup><mi>λ</mi><mo>⋆</mo></msup><mi>gum</mi></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>y</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mrow><msup><mi>λ</mi><mo>⋆</mo></msup><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><msup><mi>y</mi><mfrac><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒱</mi><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow><mo>∧</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒲</mi><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0.170em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi></mrow><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒱</mi><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow><mo>∧</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒲</mi><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mfrac></msup></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><msup><mi>λ</mi><mo>⋆</mo></msup></mrow><mo rspace="0.055em" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msup><mi>y</mi><mfrac><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi></mrow></mfrac></msup><mo>+</mo><msup><mi>y</mi><mfrac><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi></mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi></mfrac></msup></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">h_{\lambda^{\star}}^{\mathrm{gum}}(y)=\log(\lambda^{\star}\cdot y^{\frac{(|{\mathcal{V}}|\wedge|{{\mathcal{W}}}|)\,\Delta}{(|{\mathcal{V}}|\wedge|{{\mathcal{W}}}|-1)(1-\Delta)}}+(1-\lambda^{\star})\cdot(y^{\frac{\Delta}{1-\Delta}}+y^{\frac{1-\Delta}{\Delta}}))</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A2.Thmlem4.p1.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="A2.Thmlem4.p1.2.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">where <math id="A2.Thmlem4.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\lambda^{\star}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi>λ</mi><mo>⋆</mo></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\lambda^{\star}</annotation></semantics></math> is the solution to this equation <math id="A2.Thmlem4.p1.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="L(h_{\lambda}^{\mathrm{gum}},\bm{P}_{\Delta}^{\star})=L(h_{\lambda}^{\mathrm{gum}},{\bm{S}}_{\Delta}^{\star})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>L</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msubsup><mi>h</mi><mi>λ</mi><mi>gum</mi></msubsup><mo>,</mo><msubsup><mi>𝐏</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo>⋆</mo></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>L</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msubsup><mi>h</mi><mi>λ</mi><mi>gum</mi></msubsup><mo>,</mo><msubsup><mi>𝐒</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo>⋆</mo></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">L(h_{\lambda}^{\mathrm{gum}},\bm{P}_{\Delta}^{\star})=L(h_{\lambda}^{\mathrm{gum}},{\bm{S}}_{\Delta}^{\star})</annotation></semantics></math>.</span></p>
</div>
</div>
<div id="A2.SS8.p5" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A2.SS8.p5.1" class="ltx_p">As shown in Lemma <a href="#A2.Thmlem4" title="Lemma B.4 (Optimal score function). ‣ B.8 Optimal Score in the Intermediate Regime ‣ Appendix B Proof for Gumbel-max Watermarks in Section ‣ Optimal Detection for Language Watermarks with Pseudorandom Collision" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">B.4</span></a>, the optimal score <math id="A2.SS8.p5.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="h_{\lambda^{\star}}^{\mathrm{gum}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msubsup><mi>h</mi><msup><mi>λ</mi><mo>⋆</mo></msup><mi>gum</mi></msubsup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">h_{\lambda^{\star}}^{\mathrm{gum}}</annotation></semantics></math> takes the form of a log-likelihood ratio score associated with a mixture alternative distribution, where the mixing parameter <math id="A2.SS8.p5.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\lambda^{\star}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi>λ</mi><mo>⋆</mo></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\lambda^{\star}</annotation></semantics></math> has no closed-form expression.
For this reason, we do not pursue it further in the main text.</p>
</div>
<div id="A2.SS8.3" class="ltx_proof">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_font_italic ltx_title_proof">Proof of Lemma <a href="#A2.Thmlem4" title="Lemma B.4 (Optimal score function). ‣ B.8 Optimal Score in the Intermediate Regime ‣ Appendix B Proof for Gumbel-max Watermarks in Section ‣ Optimal Detection for Language Watermarks with Pseudorandom Collision" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">B.4</span></a>.</h6>
<div id="A2.SS8.p6" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A2.SS8.p6.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A2.SS8.p6.1.1" class="ltx_text">For simplicity, let <math id="A2.SS8.p6.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="h^{\star}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi>h</mi><mo>⋆</mo></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">h^{\star}</annotation></semantics></math> denote the optimal score function.
We first claim that the unique minimizer <math id="A2.SS8.p6.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="h^{\star}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi>h</mi><mo>⋆</mo></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">h^{\star}</annotation></semantics></math> must satisfy the equalization condition:</span></p>
<table id="A2.E83" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A2.E83.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="L(h^{\star},\bm{P}_{\Delta}^{\star})=L(h^{\star},{\bm{S}}_{\Delta}^{\star})." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>L</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>h</mi><mo>⋆</mo></msup><mo>,</mo><msubsup><mi>𝑷</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo>⋆</mo></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>L</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>h</mi><mo>⋆</mo></msup><mo>,</mo><msubsup><mi>𝑺</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo>⋆</mo></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">L(h^{\star},\bm{P}_{\Delta}^{\star})=L(h^{\star},{\bm{S}}_{\Delta}^{\star}).</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(83)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A2.SS8.p6.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="A2.SS8.p6.2.1" class="ltx_text">Suppose, for contradiction, that <math id="A2.SS8.p6.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="L(h^{\star},\bm{P}_{\Delta}^{\star})&gt;L(h^{\star},{\bm{S}}_{\Delta}^{\star})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>L</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>h</mi><mo>⋆</mo></msup><mo>,</mo><msubsup><mi>𝑷</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo>⋆</mo></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>&gt;</mo><mrow><mi>L</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>h</mi><mo>⋆</mo></msup><mo>,</mo><msubsup><mi>𝑺</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo>⋆</mo></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">L(h^{\star},\bm{P}_{\Delta}^{\star})&gt;L(h^{\star},{\bm{S}}_{\Delta}^{\star})</annotation></semantics></math>.
Then we have <math id="A2.SS8.p6.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="J(h^{\star})=L(h^{\star},\bm{P}_{\Delta}^{\star})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>J</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>h</mi><mo>⋆</mo></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>L</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>h</mi><mo>⋆</mo></msup><mo>,</mo><msubsup><mi>𝑷</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo>⋆</mo></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">J(h^{\star})=L(h^{\star},\bm{P}_{\Delta}^{\star})</annotation></semantics></math> from (<a href="#A2.E82" title="In B.8 Optimal Score in the Intermediate Regime ‣ Appendix B Proof for Gumbel-max Watermarks in Section ‣ Optimal Detection for Language Watermarks with Pseudorandom Collision" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">82</span></a>), so <math id="A2.SS8.p6.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="h^{\star}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi>h</mi><mo>⋆</mo></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">h^{\star}</annotation></semantics></math> is also a local minimizer of <math id="A2.SS8.p6.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="L(h,\bm{P}_{\Delta}^{\star})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>L</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>h</mi><mo>,</mo><msubsup><mi>𝑷</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo>⋆</mo></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">L(h,\bm{P}_{\Delta}^{\star})</annotation></semantics></math>.
By strict convexity, this forces <math id="A2.SS8.p6.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="h^{\star}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi>h</mi><mo>⋆</mo></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">h^{\star}</annotation></semantics></math> to equal the unique global minimizer <math id="A2.SS8.p6.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="h_{\bm{P}_{\Delta}^{\star}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>h</mi><msubsup><mi>𝑷</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo>⋆</mo></msubsup></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">h_{\bm{P}_{\Delta}^{\star}}</annotation></semantics></math>.
But substituting back yields <math id="A2.SS8.p6.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="L(h_{\bm{P}_{\Delta}^{\star}},\bm{P}_{\Delta}^{\star})&gt;L(h_{\bm{P}_{\Delta}^{\star}},{\bm{S}}_{\Delta}^{\star})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>L</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>h</mi><msubsup><mi>𝑷</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo>⋆</mo></msubsup></msub><mo>,</mo><msubsup><mi>𝑷</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo>⋆</mo></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>&gt;</mo><mrow><mi>L</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>h</mi><msubsup><mi>𝑷</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo>⋆</mo></msubsup></msub><mo>,</mo><msubsup><mi>𝑺</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo>⋆</mo></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">L(h_{\bm{P}_{\Delta}^{\star}},\bm{P}_{\Delta}^{\star})&gt;L(h_{\bm{P}_{\Delta}^{\star}},{\bm{S}}_{\Delta}^{\star})</annotation></semantics></math>, which contradicts the condition that <math id="A2.SS8.p6.m10" class="ltx_Math" alttext="L(h_{\bm{P}_{\Delta}^{\star}},\bm{P}_{\Delta}^{\star})&lt;L(h_{\bm{P}_{\Delta}^{\star}},{\bm{S}}_{\Delta}^{\star})." display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>L</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>h</mi><msubsup><mi>𝑷</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo>⋆</mo></msubsup></msub><mo>,</mo><msubsup><mi>𝑷</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo>⋆</mo></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>&lt;</mo><mrow><mi>L</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>h</mi><msubsup><mi>𝑷</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo>⋆</mo></msubsup></msub><mo>,</mo><msubsup><mi>𝑺</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo>⋆</mo></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">L(h_{\bm{P}_{\Delta}^{\star}},\bm{P}_{\Delta}^{\star})&lt;L(h_{\bm{P}_{\Delta}^{\star}},{\bm{S}}_{\Delta}^{\star}).</annotation></semantics></math>
A similar argument rules out the case <math id="A2.SS8.p6.m11" class="ltx_Math" alttext="L(h^{\star},{\bm{S}}_{\Delta}^{\star})&gt;L(h^{\star},\bm{P}_{\Delta}^{\star})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>L</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>h</mi><mo>⋆</mo></msup><mo>,</mo><msubsup><mi>𝑺</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo>⋆</mo></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>&gt;</mo><mrow><mi>L</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>h</mi><mo>⋆</mo></msup><mo>,</mo><msubsup><mi>𝑷</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo>⋆</mo></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">L(h^{\star},{\bm{S}}_{\Delta}^{\star})&gt;L(h^{\star},\bm{P}_{\Delta}^{\star})</annotation></semantics></math>.
Thus, the equalization condition (<a href="#A2.E83" title="In Proof of Lemma . ‣ B.8 Optimal Score in the Intermediate Regime ‣ Appendix B Proof for Gumbel-max Watermarks in Section ‣ Optimal Detection for Language Watermarks with Pseudorandom Collision" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">83</span></a>) must hold. This means that at the optimal point <math id="A2.SS8.p6.m12" class="ltx_Math" alttext="h^{\star}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi>h</mi><mo>⋆</mo></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">h^{\star}</annotation></semantics></math>, both component functions are active and attain the same value.</span></p>
</div>
<div id="A2.SS8.p7" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A2.SS8.p7.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A2.SS8.p7.1.1" class="ltx_text">From the first-order stationary condition, the zero function belongs to the subdifferential set at <math id="A2.SS8.p7.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="h^{\star}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi>h</mi><mo>⋆</mo></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">h^{\star}</annotation></semantics></math>, that is, <math id="A2.SS8.p7.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="0\in\partial J(h^{\star})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mn>0</mn><mo rspace="0.111em">∈</mo><mrow><mo>∂</mo><mrow><mi>J</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>h</mi><mo>⋆</mo></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">0\in\partial J(h^{\star})</annotation></semantics></math>. By standard convex analysis, the subdifferential of the maximum of functions is the convex hull of the gradients of the active functions, namely <math id="A2.SS8.p7.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\partial J(h^{\star})=\mathrm{conv}\{\nabla_{h}L(h^{\star},\bm{P}_{\Delta}^{\star}),\nabla_{h}L(h^{\star},{\bm{S}}_{\Delta}^{\star})\}." display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mo>∂</mo><mphantom></mphantom><mrow><mrow><mi>J</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>h</mi><mo>⋆</mo></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>conv</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mo rspace="0.167em">∇</mo><mi>h</mi></msub><mi>L</mi></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>h</mi><mo>⋆</mo></msup><mo>,</mo><msubsup><mi>𝑷</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo>⋆</mo></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mo rspace="0.167em">∇</mo><mi>h</mi></msub><mi>L</mi></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>h</mi><mo>⋆</mo></msup><mo>,</mo><msubsup><mi>𝑺</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo>⋆</mo></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\partial J(h^{\star})=\mathrm{conv}\{\nabla_{h}L(h^{\star},\bm{P}_{\Delta}^{\star}),\nabla_{h}L(h^{\star},{\bm{S}}_{\Delta}^{\star})\}.</annotation></semantics></math>
This implies the existence of a mixing parameter <math id="A2.SS8.p7.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\lambda^{\star}\in(0,1)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msup><mi>λ</mi><mo>⋆</mo></msup><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>1</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\lambda^{\star}\in(0,1)</annotation></semantics></math> such that</span></p>
<table id="A2.E84" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A2.E84.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\lambda^{\star}\nabla_{h}L(h^{\star},\bm{P}_{\Delta}^{\star})+(1-\lambda^{\star})\nabla_{h}L(h^{\star},{\bm{S}}_{\Delta}^{\star})=0." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mrow><msup><mi>λ</mi><mo>⋆</mo></msup><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><msub><mo rspace="0.167em">∇</mo><mi>h</mi></msub><mi>L</mi></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>h</mi><mo>⋆</mo></msup><mo>,</mo><msubsup><mi>𝑷</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo>⋆</mo></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><msup><mi>λ</mi><mo>⋆</mo></msup></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><msub><mo rspace="0.167em">∇</mo><mi>h</mi></msub><mi>L</mi></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>h</mi><mo>⋆</mo></msup><mo>,</mo><msubsup><mi>𝑺</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo>⋆</mo></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\lambda^{\star}\nabla_{h}L(h^{\star},\bm{P}_{\Delta}^{\star})+(1-\lambda^{\star})\nabla_{h}L(h^{\star},{\bm{S}}_{\Delta}^{\star})=0.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(84)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A2.SS8.p7.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="A2.SS8.p7.2.1" class="ltx_text">We remark that we must have <math id="A2.SS8.p7.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\lambda^{\star}\in(0,1)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msup><mi>λ</mi><mo>⋆</mo></msup><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>1</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\lambda^{\star}\in(0,1)</annotation></semantics></math>; otherwise <math id="A2.SS8.p7.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="h^{\star}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi>h</mi><mo>⋆</mo></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">h^{\star}</annotation></semantics></math> would equal <math id="A2.SS8.p7.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="h_{\bm{P}_{\Delta}^{\star}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>h</mi><msubsup><mi>𝑷</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo>⋆</mo></msubsup></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">h_{\bm{P}_{\Delta}^{\star}}</annotation></semantics></math> or <math id="A2.SS8.p7.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="h_{{\bm{S}}_{\Delta}^{\star}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>h</mi><msubsup><mi>𝑺</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo>⋆</mo></msubsup></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">h_{{\bm{S}}_{\Delta}^{\star}}</annotation></semantics></math>, which contradicts <math id="A2.SS8.p7.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\Delta\in(\Delta_{1}^{\star},\Delta_{2}^{\star})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msubsup><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mn>1</mn><mo>⋆</mo></msubsup><mo>,</mo><msubsup><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mn>2</mn><mo>⋆</mo></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Delta\in(\Delta_{1}^{\star},\Delta_{2}^{\star})</annotation></semantics></math>.</span></p>
</div>
<div id="A2.SS8.p8" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A2.SS8.p8.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A2.SS8.p8.1.1" class="ltx_text">We now derive the explicit form of <math id="A2.SS8.p8.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="h^{\star}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi>h</mi><mo>⋆</mo></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">h^{\star}</annotation></semantics></math>.
Let <math id="A2.SS8.p8.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="f_{\bm{P}_{\Delta}^{\star}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>f</mi><msubsup><mi>𝑷</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo>⋆</mo></msubsup></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">f_{\bm{P}_{\Delta}^{\star}}</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="A2.SS8.p8.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="f_{{\bm{S}}_{\Delta}^{\star}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>f</mi><msubsup><mi>𝑺</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo>⋆</mo></msubsup></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">f_{{\bm{S}}_{\Delta}^{\star}}</annotation></semantics></math> denote the alternative PDFs associated with <math id="A2.SS8.p8.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="F_{\bm{P}_{\Delta}^{\star}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>F</mi><msubsup><mi>𝑷</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo>⋆</mo></msubsup></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">F_{\bm{P}_{\Delta}^{\star}}</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="A2.SS8.p8.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="F_{{\bm{S}}_{\Delta}^{\star}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>F</mi><msubsup><mi>𝑺</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo>⋆</mo></msubsup></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">F_{{\bm{S}}_{\Delta}^{\star}}</annotation></semantics></math>, respectively, and let <math id="A2.SS8.p8.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="f_{0}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>f</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">f_{0}</annotation></semantics></math> be the null PDF. The functional gradient of <math id="A2.SS8.p8.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="L(h,{\bm{S}})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>L</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>h</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>𝑺</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">L(h,{\bm{S}})</annotation></semantics></math> with respect to <math id="A2.SS8.p8.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="h" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>h</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">h</annotation></semantics></math> at a point <math id="A2.SS8.p8.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="y" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>y</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">y</annotation></semantics></math> is</span></p>
<table id="A2.Ex153" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A2.Ex153.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\nabla_{h}L(h,{\bm{S}})(y)=f_{0}(y)-\frac{{\mathrm{e}}^{-h(y)}f_{{\bm{S}}_{\Delta}^{\star}}(y)}{\EB_{F_{{\bm{S}}}}[{\mathrm{e}}^{-h}]}." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mrow><msub><mo>∇</mo><mi>h</mi></msub><mi>L</mi></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>h</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>𝑺</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>y</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>f</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>y</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mfrac><mrow><msup><mi>e</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>h</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>y</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>f</mi><msubsup><mi>𝑺</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo>⋆</mo></msubsup></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>y</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mrow><msub><mi>𝔼</mi><msub><mi>F</mi><mi>𝐒</mi></msub></msub><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><msup><mi>e</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mi>h</mi></mrow></msup><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow></mfrac></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\nabla_{h}L(h,{\bm{S}})(y)=f_{0}(y)-\frac{{\mathrm{e}}^{-h(y)}f_{{\bm{S}}_{\Delta}^{\star}}(y)}{\EB_{F_{{\bm{S}}}}[{\mathrm{e}}^{-h}]}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A2.SS8.p8.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="A2.SS8.p8.2.1" class="ltx_text">By the equalization condition (<a href="#A2.E83" title="In Proof of Lemma . ‣ B.8 Optimal Score in the Intermediate Regime ‣ Appendix B Proof for Gumbel-max Watermarks in Section ‣ Optimal Detection for Language Watermarks with Pseudorandom Collision" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">83</span></a>), the denominators are equal: <math id="A2.SS8.p8.m10" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\EB_{F_{\bm{P}_{\Delta}^{\star}}}[{\mathrm{e}}^{-h^{\star}}]=\EB_{F_{{\bm{S}}_{\Delta}^{\star}}}[{\mathrm{e}}^{-h^{\star}}]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>𝔼</mi><msub><mi>F</mi><msubsup><mi>𝐏</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo>⋆</mo></msubsup></msub></msub><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><msup><mi>e</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><msup><mi>h</mi><mo>⋆</mo></msup></mrow></msup><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><msub><mi>𝔼</mi><msub><mi>F</mi><msubsup><mi>𝐒</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo>⋆</mo></msubsup></msub></msub><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><msup><mi>e</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><msup><mi>h</mi><mo>⋆</mo></msup></mrow></msup><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\EB_{F_{\bm{P}_{\Delta}^{\star}}}[{\mathrm{e}}^{-h^{\star}}]=\EB_{F_{{\bm{S}}_{\Delta}^{\star}}}[{\mathrm{e}}^{-h^{\star}}]</annotation></semantics></math>. Let this common value be <math id="A2.SS8.p8.m11" class="ltx_Math" alttext="C^{\star}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi>C</mi><mo>⋆</mo></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">C^{\star}</annotation></semantics></math>. Substituting the gradients into the optimality condition (<a href="#A2.E84" title="In Proof of Lemma . ‣ B.8 Optimal Score in the Intermediate Regime ‣ Appendix B Proof for Gumbel-max Watermarks in Section ‣ Optimal Detection for Language Watermarks with Pseudorandom Collision" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">84</span></a>) gives</span></p>
<table id="A2.Ex154" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A2.Ex154.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="f_{0}(y)-\frac{{\mathrm{e}}^{-h^{\star}(y)}}{C^{*}}\left(\lambda^{\star}f_{\bm{P}_{\Delta}^{\star}}(y)+(1-\lambda^{\star})f_{{\bm{S}}_{\Delta}^{\star}}(y)\right)=0." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>f</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>y</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mfrac><msup><mi>e</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><msup><mi>h</mi><mo>⋆</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>y</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></msup><msup><mi>C</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup></mfrac><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mrow><msup><mi>λ</mi><mo>⋆</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>f</mi><msubsup><mi>𝑷</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo>⋆</mo></msubsup></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>y</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><msup><mi>λ</mi><mo>⋆</mo></msup></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>f</mi><msubsup><mi>𝑺</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo>⋆</mo></msubsup></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>y</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">f_{0}(y)-\frac{{\mathrm{e}}^{-h^{\star}(y)}}{C^{*}}\left(\lambda^{\star}f_{\bm{P}_{\Delta}^{\star}}(y)+(1-\lambda^{\star})f_{{\bm{S}}_{\Delta}^{\star}}(y)\right)=0.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A2.SS8.p8.3" class="ltx_p"><span id="A2.SS8.p8.3.1" class="ltx_text">Solving for <math id="A2.SS8.p8.m12" class="ltx_Math" alttext="h^{\star}(y)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msup><mi>h</mi><mo>⋆</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>y</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">h^{\star}(y)</annotation></semantics></math> and noting that the additive constant <math id="A2.SS8.p8.m13" class="ltx_Math" alttext="-\log C^{\star}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo rspace="0.167em">−</mo><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><msup><mi>C</mi><mo>⋆</mo></msup></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">-\log C^{\star}</annotation></semantics></math> does not affect detection performance, we obtain the explicit form of the optimal score function:</span></p>
<table id="A2.Ex155" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A2.Ex155.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="h^{\star}(y)=\log\left(\frac{\lambda^{\star}f_{\bm{P}_{\Delta}^{\star}}(y)+(1-\lambda^{\star})f_{{\bm{S}}_{\Delta}^{\star}}(y)}{f_{0}(y)}\right)." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><msup><mi>h</mi><mo>⋆</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>y</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mfrac><mrow><mrow><msup><mi>λ</mi><mo>⋆</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>f</mi><msubsup><mi>𝑷</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo>⋆</mo></msubsup></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>y</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><msup><mi>λ</mi><mo>⋆</mo></msup></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>f</mi><msubsup><mi>𝑺</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo>⋆</mo></msubsup></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>y</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mrow><msub><mi>f</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>y</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mfrac><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">h^{\star}(y)=\log\left(\frac{\lambda^{\star}f_{\bm{P}_{\Delta}^{\star}}(y)+(1-\lambda^{\star})f_{{\bm{S}}_{\Delta}^{\star}}(y)}{f_{0}(y)}\right).</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A2.SS8.p8.4" class="ltx_p"><span id="A2.SS8.p8.4.1" class="ltx_text">Thus, the optimal score function is precisely the log-likelihood ratio between the null distribution <math id="A2.SS8.p8.m14" class="ltx_Math" alttext="f_{0}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>f</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">f_{0}</annotation></semantics></math> and a mixture of the two extremal alternative distributions.</span></p>
</div>
<div id="A2.SS8.p9" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A2.SS8.p9.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A2.SS8.p9.1.1" class="ltx_text">∎</span></p>
</div>
</div>
</section>
</section>
<section id="A3" class="ltx_appendix">
<h2 class="ltx_title ltx_title_appendix"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_appendix">Appendix C </span>Proof for Inverse Transform Watermarks in Section <a href="#S5" title="5 Application to the Inverse Transform Watermark ‣ Optimal Detection for Language Watermarks with Pseudorandom Collision" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">5</span></a></h2>

<div id="A3.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A3.p1.1" class="ltx_p">We begin by introducing the notation and terminology used throughout this section, as the analysis of the inverse transform watermark involves several technical components.</p>
</div>
<section id="A3.SS0.SSS0.Px1" class="ltx_paragraph">
<h5 class="ltx_title ltx_title_paragraph">General notation.</h5>

<div id="A3.SS0.SSS0.Px1.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A3.SS0.SSS0.Px1.p1.1" class="ltx_p">Throughout the proof, we use <math id="A3.SS0.SSS0.Px1.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(\cdot)_{+}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">⋅</mo><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>+</mo></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(\cdot)_{+}</annotation></semantics></math> to denote the positive part function, that is, <math id="A3.SS0.SSS0.Px1.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(x)_{+}=\max\{x,0\}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>+</mo></msub><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>max</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>,</mo><mn>0</mn><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(x)_{+}=\max\{x,0\}</annotation></semantics></math>. For a function <math id="A3.SS0.SSS0.Px1.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="f:A\to\mathbb{R}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>f</mi><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mrow><mi>A</mi><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><mi>ℝ</mi></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">f:A\to\mathbb{R}</annotation></semantics></math> and a constant <math id="A3.SS0.SSS0.Px1.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="M&gt;0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>M</mi><mo>&gt;</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">M&gt;0</annotation></semantics></math>, we define the <em id="A3.SS0.SSS0.Px1.p1.1.1" class="ltx_emph ltx_font_italic">clipped extension</em> <math id="A3.SS0.SSS0.Px1.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="[f]_{[-M,M]}:\mathbb{R}\to\mathbb{R}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mi>f</mi><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><mrow><mo>−</mo><mi>M</mi></mrow><mo>,</mo><mi>M</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mrow><mi>ℝ</mi><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><mi>ℝ</mi></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">[f]_{[-M,M]}:\mathbb{R}\to\mathbb{R}</annotation></semantics></math> as a continuous function satisfying:</p>
<table id="A3.E85" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A3.E85.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="[f]_{[-M,M]}(x)=\begin{cases}f(x),&amp;\text{if }x\in A\text{ and }f(x)\in[-M,M],\\
M,&amp;\text{if }x\in A\text{ and }f(x)&gt;M,\\
-M,&amp;\text{if }x\in A\text{ and }f(x)&lt;-M,\\
\text{a continuous value in }[-M,M],&amp;\text{if }x\notin A.\end{cases}" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mi>f</mi><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><mrow><mo>−</mo><mi>M</mi></mrow><mo>,</mo><mi>M</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo>{</mo><mtable columnspacing="5pt" displaystyle="true" rowspacing="0pt"><mtr><mtd class="ltx_align_left" columnalign="left"><mrow><mrow><mi>f</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow></mtd><mtd class="ltx_align_left" columnalign="left"><mrow><mrow><mrow><mtext>if </mtext><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>x</mi></mrow><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mi>A</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mtext> and </mtext><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>f</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><mrow><mo>−</mo><mi>M</mi></mrow><mo>,</mo><mi>M</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow></mtd></mtr><mtr><mtd class="ltx_align_left" columnalign="left"><mrow><mi>M</mi><mo>,</mo></mrow></mtd><mtd class="ltx_align_left" columnalign="left"><mrow><mrow><mrow><mtext>if </mtext><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>x</mi></mrow><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mi>A</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mtext> and </mtext><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>f</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>&gt;</mo><mi>M</mi></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow></mtd></mtr><mtr><mtd class="ltx_align_left" columnalign="left"><mrow><mrow><mo>−</mo><mi>M</mi></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow></mtd><mtd class="ltx_align_left" columnalign="left"><mrow><mrow><mrow><mtext>if </mtext><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>x</mi></mrow><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mi>A</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mtext> and </mtext><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>f</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>&lt;</mo><mrow><mo>−</mo><mi>M</mi></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow></mtd></mtr><mtr><mtd class="ltx_align_left" columnalign="left"><mrow><mrow><mtext>a continuous value in </mtext><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><mrow><mo>−</mo><mi>M</mi></mrow><mo>,</mo><mi>M</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow></mtd><mtd class="ltx_align_left" columnalign="left"><mrow><mrow><mrow><mtext>if </mtext><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>x</mi></mrow><mo>∉</mo><mi>A</mi></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow></mtd></mtr></mtable></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">[f]_{[-M,M]}(x)=\begin{cases}f(x),&amp;\text{if }x\in A\text{ and }f(x)\in[-M,M],\\
M,&amp;\text{if }x\in A\text{ and }f(x)&gt;M,\\
-M,&amp;\text{if }x\in A\text{ and }f(x)&lt;-M,\\
\text{a continuous value in }[-M,M],&amp;\text{if }x\notin A.\end{cases}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(85)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A3.SS0.SSS0.Px1.p1.2" class="ltx_p">We denote the permutation group over <math id="A3.SS0.SSS0.Px1.p1.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="{{\mathcal{W}}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒲</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{{\mathcal{W}}}</annotation></semantics></math> by <math id="A3.SS0.SSS0.Px1.p1.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathrm{Perm}({{\mathcal{W}}})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>Perm</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒲</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathrm{Perm}({{\mathcal{W}}})</annotation></semantics></math>, and use <math id="A3.SS0.SSS0.Px1.p1.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\pi\in\mathrm{Perm}({{\mathcal{W}}})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>π</mi><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mi>Perm</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒲</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\pi\in\mathrm{Perm}({{\mathcal{W}}})</annotation></semantics></math> to represent a permutation of the vocabulary. The permutation <math id="A3.SS0.SSS0.Px1.p1.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\pi" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>π</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\pi</annotation></semantics></math> acts on token indices, so that <math id="A3.SS0.SSS0.Px1.p1.m10" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\pi(w)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>π</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>w</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\pi(w)</annotation></semantics></math> denotes the token to which <math id="A3.SS0.SSS0.Px1.p1.m11" class="ltx_Math" alttext="w" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>w</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">w</annotation></semantics></math> is mapped. For brevity, we denote the set <math id="A3.SS0.SSS0.Px1.p1.m12" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\{1,2,\ldots,m\}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>2</mn><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>m</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\{1,2,\ldots,m\}</annotation></semantics></math> by <math id="A3.SS0.SSS0.Px1.p1.m13" class="ltx_Math" alttext="[m]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mi>m</mi><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">[m]</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>
</div>
</section>
<section id="A3.SS0.SSS0.Px2" class="ltx_paragraph">
<h5 class="ltx_title ltx_title_paragraph">Belief classes.</h5>

<div id="A3.SS0.SSS0.Px2.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A3.SS0.SSS0.Px2.p1.1" class="ltx_p">We formally reformulate the conditions from Assumption <a href="#S5.Thmasmp1" title="Assumption 5.1 (Asymptotic NTP conditions). ‣ 5.1 Asymptotic Distributions ‣ 5 Application to the Inverse Transform Watermark ‣ Optimal Detection for Language Watermarks with Pseudorandom Collision" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">5.1</span></a> and collect all NTP distributions within a minimal unit <math id="A3.SS0.SSS0.Px2.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{V}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒱</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{V}</annotation></semantics></math> of type <math id="A3.SS0.SSS0.Px2.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\tau" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>τ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\tau</annotation></semantics></math> that satisfy Assumption <a href="#S5.Thmasmp1" title="Assumption 5.1 (Asymptotic NTP conditions). ‣ 5.1 Asymptotic Distributions ‣ 5 Application to the Inverse Transform Watermark ‣ Optimal Detection for Language Watermarks with Pseudorandom Collision" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">5.1</span></a> into the class <math id="A3.SS0.SSS0.Px2.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="{\mathcal{Q}}_{\tau,\bm{\Delta}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒬</mi><mrow><mi>τ</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>𝚫</mi></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\mathcal{Q}}_{\tau,\bm{\Delta}}</annotation></semantics></math>.
As defined, <math id="A3.SS0.SSS0.Px2.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="{\mathcal{Q}}_{\tau,\bm{\Delta}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒬</mi><mrow><mi>τ</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>𝚫</mi></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\mathcal{Q}}_{\tau,\bm{\Delta}}</annotation></semantics></math> depends only on the type <math id="A3.SS0.SSS0.Px2.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\tau" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>τ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\tau</annotation></semantics></math> and the regularity levels <math id="A3.SS0.SSS0.Px2.p1.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\bm{\Delta}=(\Delta_{t})_{t\in\mathcal{V}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>𝚫</mi><mo>=</mo><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>∈</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒱</mi></mrow></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\bm{\Delta}=(\Delta_{t})_{t\in\mathcal{V}}</annotation></semantics></math>, as this information is sufficient to determine all valid NTP distributions in the asymptotic regime we consider.</p>
</div>
<div id="A3.Thmdefn1" class="ltx_theorem ltx_theorem_defn">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_title_theorem"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_theorem"><span id="A3.Thmdefn1.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Definition C.1</span></span><span id="A3.Thmdefn1.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold"> </span>(Fixed-parameter belief class)<span id="A3.Thmdefn1.4" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">.</span></h6>
<div id="A3.Thmdefn1.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A3.Thmdefn1.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A3.Thmdefn1.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">For a minimal unit <math id="A3.Thmdefn1.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{V}={\mathcal{I}}^{\zeta}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒱</mi><mo>=</mo><msup><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℐ</mi><mi>ζ</mi></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{V}={\mathcal{I}}^{\zeta}</annotation></semantics></math> of type <math id="A3.Thmdefn1.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\tau" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>τ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\tau</annotation></semantics></math> and a sequence of regularity levels <math id="A3.Thmdefn1.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\bm{\Delta}=(\Delta_{t})_{t\in\mathcal{V}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>𝚫</mi><mo>=</mo><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>∈</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒱</mi></mrow></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\bm{\Delta}=(\Delta_{t})_{t\in\mathcal{V}}</annotation></semantics></math> with each <math id="A3.Thmdefn1.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\Delta_{t}\in[\Delta,1-\delta]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo>,</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mi>δ</mi></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Delta_{t}\in[\Delta,1-\delta]</annotation></semantics></math> as in Assumption <a href="#S5.Thmasmp1" title="Assumption 5.1 (Asymptotic NTP conditions). ‣ 5.1 Asymptotic Distributions ‣ 5 Application to the Inverse Transform Watermark ‣ Optimal Detection for Language Watermarks with Pseudorandom Collision" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">5.1</span></a>, we define the class <math id="A3.Thmdefn1.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="{\mathcal{Q}}_{\tau,\bm{\Delta}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒬</mi><mrow><mi>τ</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>𝚫</mi></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\mathcal{Q}}_{\tau,\bm{\Delta}}</annotation></semantics></math> as the set of all joint NTP distributions <math id="A3.Thmdefn1.p1.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\bm{P}_{\mathcal{V}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>𝐏</mi><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒱</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\bm{P}_{\mathcal{V}}</annotation></semantics></math> over the tokens in <math id="A3.Thmdefn1.p1.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{V}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒱</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{V}</annotation></semantics></math> that satisfy Assumption <a href="#S5.Thmasmp1" title="Assumption 5.1 (Asymptotic NTP conditions). ‣ 5.1 Asymptotic Distributions ‣ 5 Application to the Inverse Transform Watermark ‣ Optimal Detection for Language Watermarks with Pseudorandom Collision" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">5.1</span></a>:</span></p>
<table id="A3.E86" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A3.E86.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="{\mathcal{Q}}_{\tau,\bm{\Delta}}=\left\{\bm{P}_{{\mathcal{V}}}:\ \forall t\in{\mathcal{I}}^{\zeta},\ P_{t,w_{t}}=P_{t,(1)}=1-\Delta_{t}\ \text{and}\ \log|{{\mathcal{W}}}|\cdot P_{t,(2)}\leq{\varepsilon}_{|{{\mathcal{W}}}|}\right\}," display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒬</mi><mrow><mi>τ</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>𝚫</mi></mrow></msub><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo>{</mo><msub><mi>𝑷</mi><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒱</mi></msub><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.778em">:</mo><mo rspace="0.167em">∀</mo><mi>t</mi><mo>∈</mo><msup><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℐ</mi><mi>ζ</mi></msup><mo rspace="0.667em">,</mo><msub><mi>P</mi><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>w</mi><mi>t</mi></msub></mrow></msub><mo>=</mo><msub><mi>P</mi><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>,</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>1</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></msub><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mtext class="ltx_mathvariant_italic">and</mtext><mi>log</mi><mo fence="false" rspace="0.167em" stretchy="false">|</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒲</mi><mo fence="false" stretchy="false">|</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><msub><mi>P</mi><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>,</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>2</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></msub><mo>≤</mo><msub><mi>ε</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒲</mi><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow></msub><mo>}</mo></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\mathcal{Q}}_{\tau,\bm{\Delta}}=\left\{\bm{P}_{{\mathcal{V}}}:\ \forall t\in{\mathcal{I}}^{\zeta},\ P_{t,w_{t}}=P_{t,(1)}=1-\Delta_{t}\ \text{and}\ \log|{{\mathcal{W}}}|\cdot P_{t,(2)}\leq{\varepsilon}_{|{{\mathcal{W}}}|}\right\},</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(86)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A3.Thmdefn1.p1.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="A3.Thmdefn1.p1.2.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">where <math id="A3.Thmdefn1.p1.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\bm{P}_{{\mathcal{V}}}:=(\bm{P}_{t})_{t\in{\mathcal{V}}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>𝐏</mi><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒱</mi></msub><mo>:=</mo><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>𝐏</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>∈</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒱</mi></mrow></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\bm{P}_{{\mathcal{V}}}:=(\bm{P}_{t})_{t\in{\mathcal{V}}}</annotation></semantics></math> is the collection of marginal distributions of tokens in <math id="A3.Thmdefn1.p1.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="{\mathcal{V}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒱</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\mathcal{V}}</annotation></semantics></math>, and <math id="A3.Thmdefn1.p1.m10" class="ltx_Math" alttext="P_{t,(1)},P_{t,(2)}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>P</mi><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>,</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>1</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>P</mi><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>,</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>2</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">P_{t,(1)},P_{t,(2)}</annotation></semantics></math> denote the largest and second-largest probabilities in the NTP distribution <math id="A3.Thmdefn1.p1.m11" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\bm{P}_{t}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>𝐏</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\bm{P}_{t}</annotation></semantics></math>.</span></p>
</div>
</div>
</section>
<section id="A3.SS1" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection">C.1 </span>Proof of Lemma <a href="#S5.Thmlem1" title="Lemma 5.1 (Asymptotic joint distribution of pseudorandomness and tokens). ‣ 5.1 Asymptotic Distributions ‣ 5 Application to the Inverse Transform Watermark ‣ Optimal Detection for Language Watermarks with Pseudorandom Collision" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">5.1</span></a></h3>

<div id="A3.SS1.2" class="ltx_proof">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_font_italic ltx_title_proof">Proof of Lemma <a href="#S5.Thmlem1" title="Lemma 5.1 (Asymptotic joint distribution of pseudorandomness and tokens). ‣ 5.1 Asymptotic Distributions ‣ 5 Application to the Inverse Transform Watermark ‣ Optimal Detection for Language Watermarks with Pseudorandom Collision" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">5.1</span></a>.</h6>
<div id="A3.SS1.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A3.SS1.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A3.SS1.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text">To establish the asymptotic distribution of the pseudorandom numbers and tokens, we first characterize their exact joint distribution in Lemma <a href="#A3.Thmlem1" title="Lemma C.1 (Exact joint distribution). ‣ Proof of Lemma . ‣ C.1 Proof of Lemma ‣ Appendix C Proof for Inverse Transform Watermarks in Section ‣ Optimal Detection for Language Watermarks with Pseudorandom Collision" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">C.1</span></a>. Since our analysis focuses on a fixed minimal unit <math id="A3.SS1.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="{\mathcal{I}}_{k}^{\zeta}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msubsup><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℐ</mi><mi>k</mi><mi>ζ</mi></msubsup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\mathcal{I}}_{k}^{\zeta}</annotation></semantics></math>, we omit the subscript <math id="A3.SS1.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="k" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>k</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">k</annotation></semantics></math> for simplicity and denote it by <math id="A3.SS1.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="{\mathcal{V}}={\mathcal{I}}_{k}^{\zeta}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒱</mi><mo>=</mo><msubsup><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℐ</mi><mi>k</mi><mi>ζ</mi></msubsup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\mathcal{V}}={\mathcal{I}}_{k}^{\zeta}</annotation></semantics></math>, which contains <math id="A3.SS1.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="m" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>m</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">m</annotation></semantics></math> sub-blocks. We adopt this notational convention throughout the proof of Theorem <a href="#S5.Thmtheorem1" title="Theorem 5.1 (Asymptotic joint distribution of pivotal statistics). ‣ 5.1 Asymptotic Distributions ‣ 5 Application to the Inverse Transform Watermark ‣ Optimal Detection for Language Watermarks with Pseudorandom Collision" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">5.1</span></a> as well.</span></p>
</div>
<div id="A3.Thmlem1" class="ltx_theorem ltx_theorem_lem">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_title_theorem"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_theorem"><span id="A3.Thmlem1.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Lemma C.1</span></span><span id="A3.Thmlem1.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold"> </span>(Exact joint distribution)<span id="A3.Thmlem1.4" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">.</span></h6>
<div id="A3.Thmlem1.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A3.Thmlem1.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A3.Thmlem1.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">Fix a minimal unit (or block) <math id="A3.Thmlem1.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="{\mathcal{I}}^{\zeta}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℐ</mi><mi>ζ</mi></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\mathcal{I}}^{\zeta}</annotation></semantics></math> consisting of <math id="A3.Thmlem1.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="m" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>m</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">m</annotation></semantics></math> sub-blocks, denoted by <math id="A3.Thmlem1.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="{\mathcal{I}}_{\ell}^{Y}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msubsup><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℐ</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mi>Y</mi></msubsup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\mathcal{I}}_{\ell}^{Y}</annotation></semantics></math> for <math id="A3.Thmlem1.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\ell\in[m]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mi>m</mi><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\ell\in[m]</annotation></semantics></math>, such that <math id="A3.Thmlem1.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\bigcup_{\ell=1}^{m}{\mathcal{I}}_{\ell}^{Y}={\mathcal{I}}^{\zeta}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msubsup><mo>⋃</mo><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>m</mi></msubsup><msubsup><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℐ</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mi>Y</mi></msubsup></mrow><mo>=</mo><msup><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℐ</mi><mi>ζ</mi></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\bigcup_{\ell=1}^{m}{\mathcal{I}}_{\ell}^{Y}={\mathcal{I}}^{\zeta}</annotation></semantics></math>.
Let Assumption <a href="#S3.Thmasmp1" title="Assumption 3.1 (Independence across blocks). ‣ Two-level partitions. ‣ 3.1 Structural Dependence and Distribution Factorization ‣ 3 A Statistical Framework under Pseudorandomness Collision ‣ Optimal Detection for Language Watermarks with Pseudorandom Collision" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">3.1</span></a> hold.
Assume the shared pseudorandom variables for this block are <math id="A3.Thmlem1.p1.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(U,\pi)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>U</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>π</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(U,\pi)</annotation></semantics></math>, where <math id="A3.Thmlem1.p1.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="U\in[0,1]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>U</mi><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">U\in[0,1]</annotation></semantics></math> is uniform and <math id="A3.Thmlem1.p1.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\pi\in\mathrm{Perm}({{\mathcal{W}}})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>π</mi><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mi>Perm</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒲</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\pi\in\mathrm{Perm}({{\mathcal{W}}})</annotation></semantics></math> is a permutation of the vocabulary.
Denote the token associated with each sub-block <math id="A3.Thmlem1.p1.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="{\mathcal{I}}_{\ell}^{Y}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msubsup><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℐ</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mi>Y</mi></msubsup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\mathcal{I}}_{\ell}^{Y}</annotation></semantics></math> by <math id="A3.Thmlem1.p1.m10" class="ltx_Math" alttext="w_{\ell}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>w</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">w_{\ell}</annotation></semantics></math> for <math id="A3.Thmlem1.p1.m11" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\ell\in[m]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mi>m</mi><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\ell\in[m]</annotation></semantics></math>.</span></p>
</div>
<div id="A3.Thmlem1.p2" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A3.Thmlem1.p2.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A3.Thmlem1.p2.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">Then the joint distribution of <math id="A3.Thmlem1.p2.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(U,\pi(w_{1}),\ldots,\pi(w_{m}))" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>U</mi><mo>,</mo><mrow><mi>π</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>w</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi><mo>,</mo><mrow><mi>π</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>w</mi><mi>m</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(U,\pi(w_{1}),\ldots,\pi(w_{m}))</annotation></semantics></math> conditioned on the fixed block <math id="A3.Thmlem1.p2.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="{\mathcal{I}}^{\zeta}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℐ</mi><mi>ζ</mi></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\mathcal{I}}^{\zeta}</annotation></semantics></math> is given by</span></p>
<table id="A3.EGx57" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A3.E87"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A3.E87.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\displaystyle{\mathbb{P}}_{1}\left(U\leq r,\;\pi(w_{i}^{\prime})=w_{i}\text{ for }i=1,\dots,m\;\middle|\;{\mathcal{I}}^{\zeta}\right)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>ℙ</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mrow><mo>(</mo><mi>U</mi><mo>≤</mo><mi>r</mi><mo rspace="0.447em">,</mo><mi>π</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msubsup><mi>w</mi><mi>i</mi><mo>′</mo></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>=</mo><msub><mi>w</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mtext class="ltx_mathvariant_italic"> for </mtext><mi>i</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>m</mi><mo stretchy="true">|</mo><msup><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℐ</mi><mi>ζ</mi></msup><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle{\mathbb{P}}_{1}\left(U\leq r,\;\pi(w_{i}^{\prime})=w_{i}\text{ for }i=1,\dots,m\;\middle|\;{\mathcal{I}}^{\zeta}\right)</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(87)</span></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A3.E88"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A3.E88.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=\," display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mo>=</mo><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=\,</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A3.E88.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\frac{\frac{1}{|{{\mathcal{W}}}|!}\sum\limits_{\begin{subarray}{c}\pi\in\mathrm{Perm}({{\mathcal{W}}})\\
\pi(w_{\ell}^{\prime})=w_{\ell},\;\ell\in[m]\end{subarray}}{\mathbb{P}}\left(U\in\bigcap_{\ell=1}^{m}\bigcap_{t\in{\mathcal{I}}^{Y}_{\ell}}\left(a_{\pi,w_{\ell}^{\prime}-1}^{(t)},\;a_{\pi,w_{\ell}^{\prime}}^{(t)}\right)\cap[0,r]\right)}{\frac{1}{|{{\mathcal{W}}}|!}\sum\limits_{\begin{subarray}{c}w_{1}^{\prime},\ldots,w_{m}^{\prime}\\
\mathrm{distinct}\end{subarray}}\sum\limits_{\begin{subarray}{c}\pi\in\mathrm{Perm}({{\mathcal{W}}})\\
\pi(w_{\ell}^{\prime})=w_{\ell},\;\ell\in[m]\end{subarray}}{\mathbb{P}}\left(U\in\bigcap_{\ell=1}^{m}\bigcap_{t\in{\mathcal{I}}^{Y}_{\ell}}\left(a_{\pi,w_{\ell}^{\prime}-1}^{(t)},\;a_{\pi,w_{\ell}^{\prime}}^{(t)}\right)\right)}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒲</mi><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow><mo>!</mo></mrow></mfrac><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><munder><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mtable rowspacing="0pt"><mtr><mtd><mrow><mi>π</mi><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mi>Perm</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒲</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mtd></mtr><mtr><mtd><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>π</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msubsup><mi>w</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mo>′</mo></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><msub><mi>w</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi></msub></mrow><mo rspace="0.447em">,</mo><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mi>m</mi><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mtd></mtr></mtable></munder><mrow><mi>ℙ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mi>U</mi><mo rspace="0.111em">∈</mo><mrow><mrow><msubsup><mo rspace="0em">⋂</mo><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>m</mi></msubsup><mrow><msub><mo rspace="0em">⋂</mo><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>∈</mo><msubsup><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℐ</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mi>Y</mi></msubsup></mrow></msub><mrow><mo>(</mo><msubsup><mi>a</mi><mrow><mi>π</mi><mo>,</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>w</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mo>′</mo></msubsup><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup><mo rspace="0.447em">,</mo><msubsup><mi>a</mi><mrow><mi>π</mi><mo>,</mo><msubsup><mi>w</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mo>′</mo></msubsup></mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>∩</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mi>r</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mrow><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒲</mi><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow><mo>!</mo></mrow></mfrac><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><munder><mo movablelimits="false" rspace="0em">∑</mo><mtable rowspacing="0pt"><mtr><mtd><mrow><msubsup><mi>w</mi><mn>1</mn><mo>′</mo></msubsup><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi><mo>,</mo><msubsup><mi>w</mi><mi>m</mi><mo>′</mo></msubsup></mrow></mtd></mtr><mtr><mtd><mi>distinct</mi></mtd></mtr></mtable></munder><mrow><munder><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mtable rowspacing="0pt"><mtr><mtd><mrow><mi>π</mi><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mi>Perm</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒲</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mtd></mtr><mtr><mtd><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>π</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msubsup><mi>w</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mo>′</mo></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><msub><mi>w</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi></msub></mrow><mo rspace="0.447em">,</mo><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mi>m</mi><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mtd></mtr></mtable></munder><mrow><mi>ℙ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mi>U</mi><mo rspace="0.111em">∈</mo><mrow><msubsup><mo rspace="0em">⋂</mo><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>m</mi></msubsup><mrow><msub><mo rspace="0em">⋂</mo><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>∈</mo><msubsup><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℐ</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mi>Y</mi></msubsup></mrow></msub><mrow><mo>(</mo><msubsup><mi>a</mi><mrow><mi>π</mi><mo>,</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>w</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mo>′</mo></msubsup><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup><mo rspace="0.447em">,</mo><msubsup><mi>a</mi><mrow><mi>π</mi><mo>,</mo><msubsup><mi>w</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mo>′</mo></msubsup></mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow></mfrac></mstyle><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\frac{\frac{1}{|{{\mathcal{W}}}|!}\sum\limits_{\begin{subarray}{c}\pi\in\mathrm{Perm}({{\mathcal{W}}})\\
\pi(w_{\ell}^{\prime})=w_{\ell},\;\ell\in[m]\end{subarray}}{\mathbb{P}}\left(U\in\bigcap_{\ell=1}^{m}\bigcap_{t\in{\mathcal{I}}^{Y}_{\ell}}\left(a_{\pi,w_{\ell}^{\prime}-1}^{(t)},\;a_{\pi,w_{\ell}^{\prime}}^{(t)}\right)\cap[0,r]\right)}{\frac{1}{|{{\mathcal{W}}}|!}\sum\limits_{\begin{subarray}{c}w_{1}^{\prime},\ldots,w_{m}^{\prime}\\
\mathrm{distinct}\end{subarray}}\sum\limits_{\begin{subarray}{c}\pi\in\mathrm{Perm}({{\mathcal{W}}})\\
\pi(w_{\ell}^{\prime})=w_{\ell},\;\ell\in[m]\end{subarray}}{\mathbb{P}}\left(U\in\bigcap_{\ell=1}^{m}\bigcap_{t\in{\mathcal{I}}^{Y}_{\ell}}\left(a_{\pi,w_{\ell}^{\prime}-1}^{(t)},\;a_{\pi,w_{\ell}^{\prime}}^{(t)}\right)\right)}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(88)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A3.Thmlem1.p2.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="A3.Thmlem1.p2.2.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">where the endpoint <math id="A3.Thmlem1.p2.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="a_{\pi,w_{\ell}}^{(t)}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msubsup><mi>a</mi><mrow><mi>π</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>w</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi></msub></mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">a_{\pi,w_{\ell}}^{(t)}</annotation></semantics></math> is defined by</span></p>
<table id="A3.Ex156" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A3.Ex156.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="a_{\pi,w_{l}}^{(t)}=\sum_{j=1}^{w_{l}}P_{t,\pi(j)},\quad\forall t\in{\mathcal{I}}^{Y}_{\ell},\quad\forall\ell\in[m]." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><msubsup><mi>a</mi><mrow><mi>π</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>w</mi><mi>l</mi></msub></mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup><mo rspace="0.111em">=</mo><mrow><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>j</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><msub><mi>w</mi><mi>l</mi></msub></munderover><msub><mi>P</mi><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>,</mo><mrow><mi>π</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>j</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></msub></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="1.167em">,</mo><mrow><mrow><mo rspace="0.167em">∀</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow><mo>∈</mo><msubsup><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℐ</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mi>Y</mi></msubsup></mrow><mo rspace="1.167em">,</mo><mrow><mrow><mo rspace="0.167em">∀</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi></mrow><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mi>m</mi><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">a_{\pi,w_{l}}^{(t)}=\sum_{j=1}^{w_{l}}P_{t,\pi(j)},\quad\forall t\in{\mathcal{I}}^{Y}_{\ell},\quad\forall\ell\in[m].</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
</div>
<div id="A3.SS1.p2" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A3.SS1.p2.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A3.SS1.p2.1.1" class="ltx_text">The proof of Lemma <a href="#A3.Thmlem1" title="Lemma C.1 (Exact joint distribution). ‣ Proof of Lemma . ‣ C.1 Proof of Lemma ‣ Appendix C Proof for Inverse Transform Watermarks in Section ‣ Optimal Detection for Language Watermarks with Pseudorandom Collision" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">C.1</span></a> is provided in Section <a href="#A3.SS4" title="C.4 Proof of Lemma ‣ Appendix C Proof for Inverse Transform Watermarks in Section ‣ Optimal Detection for Language Watermarks with Pseudorandom Collision" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">C.4</span></a>. Following the convention in <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_cite">[<a href="#bib.bib27" title="" class="ltx_ref">27</a>]</cite>, we analyze the expectation of an arbitrary test function <math id="A3.SS1.p2.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="J" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>J</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">J</annotation></semantics></math> of <math id="A3.SS1.p2.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(U,\pi(w_{1}),\ldots,\pi(w_{m}))" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>U</mi><mo>,</mo><mrow><mi>π</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>w</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi><mo>,</mo><mrow><mi>π</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>w</mi><mi>m</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(U,\pi(w_{1}),\ldots,\pi(w_{m}))</annotation></semantics></math>, as it characterizes the joint distribution as well, is equivalent to studying the CDF, and facilitates the analysis of the asymptotic behavior.</span></p>
</div>
<div id="A3.Thmcor1" class="ltx_theorem ltx_theorem_cor">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_title_theorem"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_theorem"><span id="A3.Thmcor1.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Corollary C.1</span></span><span id="A3.Thmcor1.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">.</span></h6>
<div id="A3.Thmcor1.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A3.Thmcor1.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A3.Thmcor1.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">Under the same notation and assumption as in Lemma <a href="#A3.Thmlem1" title="Lemma C.1 (Exact joint distribution). ‣ Proof of Lemma . ‣ C.1 Proof of Lemma ‣ Appendix C Proof for Inverse Transform Watermarks in Section ‣ Optimal Detection for Language Watermarks with Pseudorandom Collision" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">C.1</span></a>, for any measurable test function <math id="A3.Thmcor1.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="J\colon[0,1]^{m+1}\to[0,\infty)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>J</mi><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mrow><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow><mrow><mi>m</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">∞</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">J\colon[0,1]^{m+1}\to[0,\infty)</annotation></semantics></math>, we have:</span></p>
<table id="A3.EGx58" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A3.Ex157"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A3.Ex157.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\EB_{1,\bm{P}_{{\mathcal{I}}^{\zeta}}}\left[J(U,\eta(\pi(w_{1})),\ldots,\eta(\pi(w_{m})))\right]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>𝔼</mi><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>𝐏</mi><msup><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℐ</mi><mi>ζ</mi></msup></msub></mrow></msub><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>[</mo><mrow><mi>J</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>U</mi><mo>,</mo><mrow><mi>η</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>π</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>w</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi><mo>,</mo><mrow><mi>η</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>π</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>w</mi><mi>m</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>]</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\EB_{1,\bm{P}_{{\mathcal{I}}^{\zeta}}}\left[J(U,\eta(\pi(w_{1})),\ldots,\eta(\pi(w_{m})))\right]</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A3.E89"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A3.E89.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=\frac{\sum_{\begin{subarray}{c}w^{\prime}_{1},\ldots,w^{\prime}_{m}\\
\mathrm{distinct}\end{subarray}}\sum_{\begin{subarray}{c}\pi\in\mathrm{Perm}({{\mathcal{W}}})\\
\pi(w_{\ell}^{\prime})=w_{\ell},\forall\ell\in[m]\end{subarray}}\left(\int_{\max\limits_{\ell,t}a_{\pi,w^{\prime}_{\ell}-1}^{(t)}}^{\min\limits_{\ell,t}a_{\pi,w^{\prime}_{\ell}}^{(t)}}J(u,\eta(w^{\prime}_{1}),\ldots,\eta(w^{\prime}_{m}))\,{\mathrm{d}}u\right){\bf 1}_{\min\limits_{\ell,t}a_{\pi,w^{\prime}_{\ell}}^{(t)}\geq\max\limits_{\ell,t}a_{\pi,w^{\prime}_{\ell}-1}^{(t)}}}{\sum_{\begin{subarray}{c}w^{\prime}_{1},\ldots,w^{\prime}_{m}\\
\mathrm{distinct}\end{subarray}}\sum_{\begin{subarray}{c}\pi\in\mathrm{Perm}({{\mathcal{W}}})\\
\pi(w_{\ell}^{\prime})=w_{\ell},\forall\ell\in[m]\end{subarray}}{\mathbb{P}}\left(U\in\bigcap_{\ell=1}^{m}\bigcap_{t\in{\mathcal{I}}^{Y}_{\ell}}\left(a_{\pi,w^{\prime}_{\ell}-1}^{(t)},a_{\pi,w^{\prime}_{\ell}}^{(t)}\right)\right)}." display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><msub><mo>∑</mo><mtable rowspacing="0pt"><mtr><mtd><mrow><msubsup><mi>w</mi><mn>1</mn><mo>′</mo></msubsup><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi><mo>,</mo><msubsup><mi>w</mi><mi>m</mi><mo>′</mo></msubsup></mrow></mtd></mtr><mtr><mtd><mi>distinct</mi></mtd></mtr></mtable></msub><mrow><msub><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">∑</mo><mtable rowspacing="0pt"><mtr><mtd><mrow><mi>π</mi><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mi>Perm</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒲</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mtd></mtr><mtr><mtd><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>π</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msubsup><mi>w</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mo>′</mo></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><msub><mi>w</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi></msub></mrow><mo>,</mo><mrow><mrow><mo rspace="0.167em">∀</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi></mrow><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mi>m</mi><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mtd></mtr></mtable></msub><mrow><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><msubsup><mo lspace="0em">∫</mo><mrow><munder><mi>max</mi><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow></munder><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><msubsup><mi>a</mi><mrow><mi>π</mi><mo>,</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>w</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mo>′</mo></msubsup><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup></mrow><mrow><munder><mi>min</mi><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow></munder><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><msubsup><mi>a</mi><mrow><mi>π</mi><mo>,</mo><msubsup><mi>w</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mo>′</mo></msubsup></mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup></mrow></msubsup><mrow><mrow><mi>J</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>u</mi><mo>,</mo><mrow><mi>η</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msubsup><mi>w</mi><mn>1</mn><mo>′</mo></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi><mo>,</mo><mrow><mi>η</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msubsup><mi>w</mi><mi>m</mi><mo>′</mo></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0.170em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo rspace="0em">𝑑</mo><mi>u</mi></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mn>𝟏</mn><mrow><mrow><munder><mi>min</mi><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow></munder><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><msubsup><mi>a</mi><mrow><mi>π</mi><mo>,</mo><msubsup><mi>w</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mo>′</mo></msubsup></mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup></mrow><mo>≥</mo><mrow><munder><mi>max</mi><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow></munder><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><msubsup><mi>a</mi><mrow><mi>π</mi><mo>,</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>w</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mo>′</mo></msubsup><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup></mrow></mrow></msub></mrow></mrow></mrow><mrow><msub><mo>∑</mo><mtable rowspacing="0pt"><mtr><mtd><mrow><msubsup><mi>w</mi><mn>1</mn><mo>′</mo></msubsup><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi><mo>,</mo><msubsup><mi>w</mi><mi>m</mi><mo>′</mo></msubsup></mrow></mtd></mtr><mtr><mtd><mi>distinct</mi></mtd></mtr></mtable></msub><mrow><msub><mo lspace="0.167em">∑</mo><mtable rowspacing="0pt"><mtr><mtd><mrow><mi>π</mi><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mi>Perm</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒲</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mtd></mtr><mtr><mtd><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>π</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msubsup><mi>w</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mo>′</mo></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><msub><mi>w</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi></msub></mrow><mo>,</mo><mrow><mrow><mo rspace="0.167em">∀</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi></mrow><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mi>m</mi><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mtd></mtr></mtable></msub><mrow><mi>ℙ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mi>U</mi><mo rspace="0.111em">∈</mo><mrow><msubsup><mo rspace="0em">⋂</mo><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>m</mi></msubsup><mrow><msub><mo rspace="0em">⋂</mo><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>∈</mo><msubsup><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℐ</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mi>Y</mi></msubsup></mrow></msub><mrow><mo>(</mo><msubsup><mi>a</mi><mrow><mi>π</mi><mo>,</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>w</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mo>′</mo></msubsup><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup><mo>,</mo><msubsup><mi>a</mi><mrow><mi>π</mi><mo>,</mo><msubsup><mi>w</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mo>′</mo></msubsup></mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow></mfrac></mstyle></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=\frac{\sum_{\begin{subarray}{c}w^{\prime}_{1},\ldots,w^{\prime}_{m}\\
\mathrm{distinct}\end{subarray}}\sum_{\begin{subarray}{c}\pi\in\mathrm{Perm}({{\mathcal{W}}})\\
\pi(w_{\ell}^{\prime})=w_{\ell},\forall\ell\in[m]\end{subarray}}\left(\int_{\max\limits_{\ell,t}a_{\pi,w^{\prime}_{\ell}-1}^{(t)}}^{\min\limits_{\ell,t}a_{\pi,w^{\prime}_{\ell}}^{(t)}}J(u,\eta(w^{\prime}_{1}),\ldots,\eta(w^{\prime}_{m}))\,{\mathrm{d}}u\right){\bf 1}_{\min\limits_{\ell,t}a_{\pi,w^{\prime}_{\ell}}^{(t)}\geq\max\limits_{\ell,t}a_{\pi,w^{\prime}_{\ell}-1}^{(t)}}}{\sum_{\begin{subarray}{c}w^{\prime}_{1},\ldots,w^{\prime}_{m}\\
\mathrm{distinct}\end{subarray}}\sum_{\begin{subarray}{c}\pi\in\mathrm{Perm}({{\mathcal{W}}})\\
\pi(w_{\ell}^{\prime})=w_{\ell},\forall\ell\in[m]\end{subarray}}{\mathbb{P}}\left(U\in\bigcap_{\ell=1}^{m}\bigcap_{t\in{\mathcal{I}}^{Y}_{\ell}}\left(a_{\pi,w^{\prime}_{\ell}-1}^{(t)},a_{\pi,w^{\prime}_{\ell}}^{(t)}\right)\right)}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(89)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A3.Thmcor1.p1.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="A3.Thmcor1.p1.2.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">where the <math id="A3.Thmcor1.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\min\limits_{\ell,t}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><munder><mi>min</mi><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow></munder><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\min\limits_{\ell,t}</annotation></semantics></math> or <math id="A3.Thmcor1.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\max\limits_{\ell,t}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><munder><mi>max</mi><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow></munder><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\max\limits_{\ell,t}</annotation></semantics></math> are taken over all sub-blocks <math id="A3.Thmcor1.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\ell\in[m]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mi>m</mi><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\ell\in[m]</annotation></semantics></math> and all token indices <math id="A3.Thmcor1.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="t\in{\mathcal{I}}^{Y}_{\ell}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>∈</mo><msubsup><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℐ</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mi>Y</mi></msubsup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">t\in{\mathcal{I}}^{Y}_{\ell}</annotation></semantics></math>.</span></p>
</div>
</div>
<div id="A3.SS1.p3" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A3.SS1.p3.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A3.SS1.p3.1.1" class="ltx_text">With Lemma <a href="#A3.Thmlem1" title="Lemma C.1 (Exact joint distribution). ‣ Proof of Lemma . ‣ C.1 Proof of Lemma ‣ Appendix C Proof for Inverse Transform Watermarks in Section ‣ Optimal Detection for Language Watermarks with Pseudorandom Collision" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">C.1</span></a> in place, we then derive the asymptotic joint distribution of <math id="A3.SS1.p3.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(U,\pi(w_{1}),\ldots,\pi(w_{m}))" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>U</mi><mo>,</mo><mrow><mi>π</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>w</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi><mo>,</mo><mrow><mi>π</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>w</mi><mi>m</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(U,\pi(w_{1}),\ldots,\pi(w_{m}))</annotation></semantics></math> when <math id="A3.SS1.p3.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="|{{\mathcal{W}}}|\to\infty" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒲</mi><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">∞</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">|{{\mathcal{W}}}|\to\infty</annotation></semantics></math>.
To do so, we examine the limiting expectation <math id="A3.SS1.p3.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\EB\left[J(U,\eta(\pi(w_{1})),\ldots,\eta(\pi(w_{m})))\right]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>𝔼</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>[</mo><mrow><mi>J</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>U</mi><mo>,</mo><mrow><mi>η</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>π</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>w</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi><mo>,</mo><mrow><mi>η</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>π</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>w</mi><mi>m</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>]</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\EB\left[J(U,\eta(\pi(w_{1})),\ldots,\eta(\pi(w_{m})))\right]</annotation></semantics></math> for any arbitrary test function <math id="A3.SS1.p3.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="J" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>J</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">J</annotation></semantics></math>.</span></p>
</div>
<div id="A3.Thmtheorem1" class="ltx_theorem ltx_theorem_theorem">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_title_theorem"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_theorem"><span id="A3.Thmtheorem1.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Theorem C.1</span></span><span id="A3.Thmtheorem1.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold"> </span>(Asymptotic distribution under <math id="A3.Thmtheorem1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="H_{1}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>H</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">H_{1}</annotation></semantics></math>)<span id="A3.Thmtheorem1.4" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">.</span></h6>
<div id="A3.Thmtheorem1.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A3.Thmtheorem1.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A3.Thmtheorem1.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">Let <math id="A3.Thmtheorem1.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="{\mathcal{I}}^{\zeta}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℐ</mi><mi>ζ</mi></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\mathcal{I}}^{\zeta}</annotation></semantics></math> be a minimal unit consisting of <math id="A3.Thmtheorem1.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="m" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>m</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">m</annotation></semantics></math> sub-blocks <math id="A3.Thmtheorem1.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\{{\mathcal{I}}^{Y}_{\ell}\}_{\ell=1}^{m}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msubsup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><msubsup><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℐ</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mi>Y</mi></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>m</mi></msubsup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\{{\mathcal{I}}^{Y}_{\ell}\}_{\ell=1}^{m}</annotation></semantics></math>, and let <math id="A3.Thmtheorem1.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\{w_{\ell}\}_{\ell=1}^{m}\subseteq{{\mathcal{W}}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msubsup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><msub><mi>w</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>m</mi></msubsup><mo>⊆</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒲</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\{w_{\ell}\}_{\ell=1}^{m}\subseteq{{\mathcal{W}}}</annotation></semantics></math> denote the distinct tokens representing these sub-blocks.
Let Assumptions <a href="#S3.Thmasmp1" title="Assumption 3.1 (Independence across blocks). ‣ Two-level partitions. ‣ 3.1 Structural Dependence and Distribution Factorization ‣ 3 A Statistical Framework under Pseudorandomness Collision ‣ Optimal Detection for Language Watermarks with Pseudorandom Collision" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">3.1</span></a> and <a href="#S5.Thmasmp1" title="Assumption 5.1 (Asymptotic NTP conditions). ‣ 5.1 Asymptotic Distributions ‣ 5 Application to the Inverse Transform Watermark ‣ Optimal Detection for Language Watermarks with Pseudorandom Collision" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">5.1</span></a> hold.
Let <math id="A3.Thmtheorem1.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(\Delta_{t})_{t\in{\mathcal{I}}^{\zeta}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>∈</mo><msup><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℐ</mi><mi>ζ</mi></msup></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(\Delta_{t})_{t\in{\mathcal{I}}^{\zeta}}</annotation></semantics></math> be the per-time regularity levels, where each <math id="A3.Thmtheorem1.p1.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\Delta_{t}\in[\Delta,1-\delta]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo>,</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mi>δ</mi></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Delta_{t}\in[\Delta,1-\delta]</annotation></semantics></math>, and define the sub-block regularity vector <math id="A3.Thmtheorem1.p1.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="({\bar{\Delta}}_{1},\ldots,{\bar{\Delta}}_{m})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo>¯</mo></mover><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo>¯</mo></mover><mi>m</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">({\bar{\Delta}}_{1},\ldots,{\bar{\Delta}}_{m})</annotation></semantics></math> by <math id="A3.Thmtheorem1.p1.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="{\bar{\Delta}}_{\ell}:=\max_{t\in{\mathcal{I}}^{Y}_{\ell}}\Delta_{t}." display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mover accent="true"><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo>¯</mo></mover><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi></msub><mo>:=</mo><mrow><msub><mi>max</mi><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>∈</mo><msubsup><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℐ</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mi>Y</mi></msubsup></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mi>t</mi></msub></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\bar{\Delta}}_{\ell}:=\max_{t\in{\mathcal{I}}^{Y}_{\ell}}\Delta_{t}.</annotation></semantics></math></span></p>
</div>
<div id="A3.Thmtheorem1.p2" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A3.Thmtheorem1.p2.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A3.Thmtheorem1.p2.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">Then for any measurable function <math id="A3.Thmtheorem1.p2.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="J\colon[0,1]^{m+1}\to[0,\infty)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>J</mi><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mrow><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow><mrow><mi>m</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">∞</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">J\colon[0,1]^{m+1}\to[0,\infty)</annotation></semantics></math>, the expectation in Corollary <a href="#A3.Thmcor1" title="Corollary C.1. ‣ Proof of Lemma . ‣ C.1 Proof of Lemma ‣ Appendix C Proof for Inverse Transform Watermarks in Section ‣ Optimal Detection for Language Watermarks with Pseudorandom Collision" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">C.1</span></a> converges as <math id="A3.Thmtheorem1.p2.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="|{{\mathcal{W}}}|\to\infty" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒲</mi><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">∞</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">|{{\mathcal{W}}}|\to\infty</annotation></semantics></math> to</span></p>
<table id="A3.EGx59" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A3.Ex158"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A3.Ex158.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\lim_{|{{\mathcal{W}}}|\to\infty}\EB_{1,\bm{P}_{{\mathcal{I}}^{\zeta}}}\bigl[J(U,\eta(\pi(w_{1})),\dots,\eta(\pi(w_{m})))\bigr]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><munder><mo movablelimits="false">lim</mo><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒲</mi><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">∞</mi></mrow></munder><mrow><msub><mi>𝔼</mi><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>𝐏</mi><msup><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℐ</mi><mi>ζ</mi></msup></msub></mrow></msub><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">[</mo><mrow><mi>J</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>U</mi><mo>,</mo><mrow><mi>η</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>π</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>w</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi><mo>,</mo><mrow><mi>η</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>π</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>w</mi><mi>m</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">]</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\lim_{|{{\mathcal{W}}}|\to\infty}\EB_{1,\bm{P}_{{\mathcal{I}}^{\zeta}}}\bigl[J(U,\eta(\pi(w_{1})),\dots,\eta(\pi(w_{m})))\bigr]</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A3.E90"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A3.E90.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\displaystyle\quad=\frac{1}{I_{m}(\bar{\bm{\Delta}})}\int_{[0,1]^{m}}\int_{\max\limits_{\ell\in[m]}{\bar{\Delta}}_{\ell}x_{\ell}}^{\min\limits_{\ell\in[m]}(1-{\bar{\Delta}}_{\ell}+{\bar{\Delta}}_{\ell}x_{\ell})}J(u,x_{1},\dots,x_{m}){\bf 1}_{\left\{\min\limits_{\ell\in[m]}(1-{\bar{\Delta}}_{\ell}+{\bar{\Delta}}_{\ell}x_{\ell})\geq\max\limits_{\ell\in[m]}{\bar{\Delta}}_{\ell}x_{\ell}\right\}}\,{\mathrm{d}}u{\mathrm{d}}x_{1}\cdots{\mathrm{d}}x_{m}," display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo>=</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mrow><msub><mi>I</mi><mi>m</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>𝚫</mi><mo>¯</mo></mover><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mfrac></mstyle><mstyle displaystyle="true"><msub><mo>∫</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow><mi>m</mi></msup></msub></mstyle><mstyle displaystyle="true"><msubsup><mo>∫</mo><mrow><mrow><munder><mi>max</mi><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mi>m</mi><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow></munder><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo>¯</mo></mover><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi></msub></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi></msub></mrow><mrow><munder><mi>min</mi><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mi>m</mi><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow></munder><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo>¯</mo></mover><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi></msub></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><msub><mover accent="true"><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo>¯</mo></mover><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi></msub></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></msubsup></mstyle><mi>J</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>u</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>m</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><msub><mn>𝟏</mn><mrow><mo>{</mo><mi>min</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mi>m</mi><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mover accent="true"><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo>¯</mo></mover><msub><mrow></mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi></msub><mo>+</mo><mover accent="true"><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo>¯</mo></mover><msub><mrow></mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi></msub><mi>x</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo><mo>≥</mo><mi>max</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mi>m</mi><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow></msub><mover accent="true"><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo>¯</mo></mover><msub><mrow></mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi></msub><mi>x</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi></msub><mo>}</mo></mrow></msub><mi>d</mi><mi>u</mi><mi>d</mi><msub><mi>x</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">⋯</mo><mi>d</mi><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>m</mi></msub><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\quad=\frac{1}{I_{m}(\bar{\bm{\Delta}})}\int_{[0,1]^{m}}\int_{\max\limits_{\ell\in[m]}{\bar{\Delta}}_{\ell}x_{\ell}}^{\min\limits_{\ell\in[m]}(1-{\bar{\Delta}}_{\ell}+{\bar{\Delta}}_{\ell}x_{\ell})}J(u,x_{1},\dots,x_{m}){\bf 1}_{\left\{\min\limits_{\ell\in[m]}(1-{\bar{\Delta}}_{\ell}+{\bar{\Delta}}_{\ell}x_{\ell})\geq\max\limits_{\ell\in[m]}{\bar{\Delta}}_{\ell}x_{\ell}\right\}}\,{\mathrm{d}}u{\mathrm{d}}x_{1}\cdots{\mathrm{d}}x_{m},</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(90)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A3.Thmtheorem1.p2.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="A3.Thmtheorem1.p2.2.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">where the normalization constant <math id="A3.Thmtheorem1.p2.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="I_{m}(\bar{\bm{\Delta}})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>I</mi><mi>m</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>𝚫</mi><mo>¯</mo></mover><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">I_{m}(\bar{\bm{\Delta}})</annotation></semantics></math> is the volume of the integration region:</span></p>
<table id="A3.Ex159" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A3.Ex159.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="I_{m}(\bar{\bm{\Delta}}):=\int_{[0,1]^{m}}\left(\min\limits_{\ell\in[m]}(1-{\bar{\Delta}}_{\ell}+{\bar{\Delta}}_{\ell}x_{\ell})-\max\limits_{\ell\in[m]}{\bar{\Delta}}_{\ell}x_{\ell}\right)_{+}\,{\mathrm{d}}x_{1}\cdots{\mathrm{d}}x_{m}." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>I</mi><mi>m</mi></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>𝚫</mi><mo>¯</mo></mover><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo rspace="0.111em">:=</mo><msub><mo rspace="0em">∫</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow><mi>m</mi></msup></msub><msub><mrow><mo>(</mo><munder><mi>min</mi><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mi>m</mi><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow></munder><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo>¯</mo></mover><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi></msub><mo>+</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo>¯</mo></mover><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi></msub><msub><mi>x</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>−</mo><munder><mi>max</mi><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mi>m</mi><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow></munder><msub><mover accent="true"><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo>¯</mo></mover><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi></msub><msub><mi>x</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi></msub><mo>)</mo></mrow><mo>+</mo></msub><mi>d</mi><msub><mi>x</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">⋯</mo><mi>d</mi><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>m</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">I_{m}(\bar{\bm{\Delta}}):=\int_{[0,1]^{m}}\left(\min\limits_{\ell\in[m]}(1-{\bar{\Delta}}_{\ell}+{\bar{\Delta}}_{\ell}x_{\ell})-\max\limits_{\ell\in[m]}{\bar{\Delta}}_{\ell}x_{\ell}\right)_{+}\,{\mathrm{d}}x_{1}\cdots{\mathrm{d}}x_{m}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A3.Thmtheorem1.p2.3" class="ltx_p"><span id="A3.Thmtheorem1.p2.3.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">Moreover, the convergence holds uniformly over any 1-Lipschitz test functions <math id="A3.Thmtheorem1.p2.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="J" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>J</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">J</annotation></semantics></math>, any NTP distributions <math id="A3.Thmtheorem1.p2.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\bm{P}_{{\mathcal{I}}^{\zeta}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>𝐏</mi><msup><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℐ</mi><mi>ζ</mi></msup></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\bm{P}_{{\mathcal{I}}^{\zeta}}</annotation></semantics></math> within the class <math id="A3.Thmtheorem1.p2.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="{\mathcal{Q}}_{\tau,\bm{\Delta}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒬</mi><mrow><mi>τ</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>𝚫</mi></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\mathcal{Q}}_{\tau,\bm{\Delta}}</annotation></semantics></math>, and any regularity vectors <math id="A3.Thmtheorem1.p2.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\bar{{\Delta}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mover accent="true"><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo>¯</mo></mover><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\bar{{\Delta}}</annotation></semantics></math>.</span></p>
</div>
</div>
<div id="A3.SS1.p4" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A3.SS1.p4.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A3.SS1.p4.1.1" class="ltx_text">The proof of Theorem <a href="#A3.Thmtheorem1" title="Theorem C.1 (Asymptotic distribution under 𝐻_1). ‣ Proof of Lemma . ‣ C.1 Proof of Lemma ‣ Appendix C Proof for Inverse Transform Watermarks in Section ‣ Optimal Detection for Language Watermarks with Pseudorandom Collision" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">C.1</span></a> can be found in Section <a href="#A3.SS5" title="C.5 Proof of Theorem ‣ Appendix C Proof for Inverse Transform Watermarks in Section ‣ Optimal Detection for Language Watermarks with Pseudorandom Collision" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">C.5</span></a>.
The arbitrariness of the test function <math id="A3.SS1.p4.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="J" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>J</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">J</annotation></semantics></math> in Theorem <a href="#A3.Thmtheorem1" title="Theorem C.1 (Asymptotic distribution under 𝐻_1). ‣ Proof of Lemma . ‣ C.1 Proof of Lemma ‣ Appendix C Proof for Inverse Transform Watermarks in Section ‣ Optimal Detection for Language Watermarks with Pseudorandom Collision" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">C.1</span></a> directly implies the following weak convergence.</span></p>
</div>
<div id="A3.Thmcor2" class="ltx_theorem ltx_theorem_cor">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_title_theorem"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_theorem"><span id="A3.Thmcor2.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Corollary C.2</span></span><span id="A3.Thmcor2.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold"> </span>(Asymptotic distribution under <math id="A3.Thmcor2.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="H_{1}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>H</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">H_{1}</annotation></semantics></math>)<span id="A3.Thmcor2.4" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">.</span></h6>
<div id="A3.Thmcor2.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A3.Thmcor2.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A3.Thmcor2.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">Under the same notation and assumptions as in Theorem <a href="#A3.Thmtheorem1" title="Theorem C.1 (Asymptotic distribution under 𝐻_1). ‣ Proof of Lemma . ‣ C.1 Proof of Lemma ‣ Appendix C Proof for Inverse Transform Watermarks in Section ‣ Optimal Detection for Language Watermarks with Pseudorandom Collision" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">C.1</span></a>, the joint vector</span></p>
<table id="A3.Ex160" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A3.Ex160.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(U,\eta(\pi(w_{1})),\ldots,\eta(\pi(w_{m})))" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>U</mi><mo>,</mo><mrow><mi>η</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>π</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>w</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi><mo>,</mo><mrow><mi>η</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>π</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>w</mi><mi>m</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(U,\eta(\pi(w_{1})),\ldots,\eta(\pi(w_{m})))</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A3.Thmcor2.p1.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="A3.Thmcor2.p1.2.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">converges in distribution to a random vector <math id="A3.Thmcor2.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(U,X_{1},\ldots,X_{m})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>U</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>X</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>X</mi><mi>m</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(U,X_{1},\ldots,X_{m})</annotation></semantics></math>, where <math id="A3.Thmcor2.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="X_{1},\ldots,X_{m}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>X</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>X</mi><mi>m</mi></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">X_{1},\ldots,X_{m}</annotation></semantics></math> are i.i.d. <math id="A3.Thmcor2.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathrm{Unif}(0,1)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>Unif</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>1</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathrm{Unif}(0,1)</annotation></semantics></math> random variables, and <math id="A3.Thmcor2.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="U" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>U</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">U</annotation></semantics></math> is independently drawn from the interval</span></p>
<table id="A3.Ex161" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A3.Ex161.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\left[\max\limits_{\ell\in[m]}\{{\bar{\Delta}}_{\ell}X_{\ell}\},\ \min\limits_{\ell\in[m]}\{1-{\bar{\Delta}}_{\ell}+{\bar{\Delta}}_{\ell}X_{\ell}\}\right]" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo>[</mo><mrow><munder><mi>max</mi><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mi>m</mi><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow></munder><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mrow><msub><mover accent="true"><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo>¯</mo></mover><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>X</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.667em">,</mo><mrow><munder><mi>min</mi><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mi>m</mi><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow></munder><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mrow><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo>¯</mo></mover><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi></msub></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><msub><mover accent="true"><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo>¯</mo></mover><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>X</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi></msub></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>]</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\left[\max\limits_{\ell\in[m]}\{{\bar{\Delta}}_{\ell}X_{\ell}\},\ \min\limits_{\ell\in[m]}\{1-{\bar{\Delta}}_{\ell}+{\bar{\Delta}}_{\ell}X_{\ell}\}\right]</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A3.Thmcor2.p1.3" class="ltx_p"><span id="A3.Thmcor2.p1.3.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">conditioned on the event that this interval is non-empty, that is, <math id="A3.Thmcor2.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\max\limits_{\ell\in[m]}\{{\bar{\Delta}}_{\ell}X_{\ell}\}\leq\min\limits_{\ell\in[m]}\{1-{\bar{\Delta}}_{\ell}+{\bar{\Delta}}_{\ell}X_{\ell}\}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><munder><mi>max</mi><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mi>m</mi><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow></munder><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mrow><msub><mover accent="true"><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo>¯</mo></mover><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>X</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>≤</mo><mrow><munder><mi>min</mi><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mi>m</mi><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow></munder><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mrow><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo>¯</mo></mover><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi></msub></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><msub><mover accent="true"><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo>¯</mo></mover><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>X</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi></msub></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\max\limits_{\ell\in[m]}\{{\bar{\Delta}}_{\ell}X_{\ell}\}\leq\min\limits_{\ell\in[m]}\{1-{\bar{\Delta}}_{\ell}+{\bar{\Delta}}_{\ell}X_{\ell}\}</annotation></semantics></math>.</span></p>
</div>
</div>
<div id="A3.SS1.2.1" class="ltx_proof">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_font_italic ltx_title_proof">Proof of Lemma <a href="#A3.Thmcor2" title="Corollary C.2 (Asymptotic distribution under 𝐻_1). ‣ Proof of Lemma . ‣ C.1 Proof of Lemma ‣ Appendix C Proof for Inverse Transform Watermarks in Section ‣ Optimal Detection for Language Watermarks with Pseudorandom Collision" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">C.2</span></a>.</h6>
<div id="A3.SS1.p5" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A3.SS1.p5.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A3.SS1.p5.1.1" class="ltx_text">This follows directly from Theorem <a href="#A3.Thmtheorem1" title="Theorem C.1 (Asymptotic distribution under 𝐻_1). ‣ Proof of Lemma . ‣ C.1 Proof of Lemma ‣ Appendix C Proof for Inverse Transform Watermarks in Section ‣ Optimal Detection for Language Watermarks with Pseudorandom Collision" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">C.1</span></a>, together with the Portmanteau theorem (Theorem 13.16 in <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_cite">[<a href="#bib.bib23" title="" class="ltx_ref">23</a>]</cite>) and Lemma <a href="#A3.Thmlem9" title="Lemma C.9. ‣ C.10 Auxiliary Lemmas ‣ Appendix C Proof for Inverse Transform Watermarks in Section ‣ Optimal Detection for Language Watermarks with Pseudorandom Collision" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">C.9</span></a>, which together allow us to translate convergence in expectation into weak convergence.
∎</span></p>
</div>
</div>
<div id="A3.SS1.p6" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A3.SS1.p6.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A3.SS1.p6.1.1" class="ltx_text">By an argument similar to that of Theorem <a href="#A3.Thmtheorem1" title="Theorem C.1 (Asymptotic distribution under 𝐻_1). ‣ Proof of Lemma . ‣ C.1 Proof of Lemma ‣ Appendix C Proof for Inverse Transform Watermarks in Section ‣ Optimal Detection for Language Watermarks with Pseudorandom Collision" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">C.1</span></a>, we can show that</span></p>
</div>
<div id="A3.Thmlem2" class="ltx_theorem ltx_theorem_lem">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_title_theorem"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_theorem"><span id="A3.Thmlem2.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Lemma C.2</span></span><span id="A3.Thmlem2.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold"> </span>(Asymptotic distribution under <math id="A3.Thmlem2.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="H_{0}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>H</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">H_{0}</annotation></semantics></math>)<span id="A3.Thmlem2.4" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">.</span></h6>
<div id="A3.Thmlem2.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A3.Thmlem2.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A3.Thmlem2.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">Under the null hypothesis <math id="A3.Thmlem2.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="H_{0}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>H</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">H_{0}</annotation></semantics></math>, the joint distribution of <math id="A3.Thmlem2.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(U,\eta(\pi(w_{1})),\ldots,\eta(\pi(w_{m})))" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>U</mi><mo>,</mo><mrow><mi>η</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>π</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>w</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi><mo>,</mo><mrow><mi>η</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>π</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>w</mi><mi>m</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(U,\eta(\pi(w_{1})),\ldots,\eta(\pi(w_{m})))</annotation></semantics></math> converges weakly to that of <math id="A3.Thmlem2.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(U,X_{1},\ldots,X_{m})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>U</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>X</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>X</mi><mi>m</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(U,X_{1},\ldots,X_{m})</annotation></semantics></math>, where <math id="A3.Thmlem2.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="U,X_{1},\ldots,X_{m}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>U</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>X</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>X</mi><mi>m</mi></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">U,X_{1},\ldots,X_{m}</annotation></semantics></math> are i.i.d. <math id="A3.Thmlem2.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathrm{Unif}(0,1)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>Unif</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>1</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathrm{Unif}(0,1)</annotation></semantics></math>.</span></p>
</div>
</div>
<div id="A3.SS1.p7" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A3.SS1.p7.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A3.SS1.p7.1.1" class="ltx_text">∎</span></p>
</div>
</div>
</section>
<section id="A3.SS2" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection">C.2 </span>Proof of Theorem <a href="#S5.Thmtheorem1" title="Theorem 5.1 (Asymptotic joint distribution of pivotal statistics). ‣ 5.1 Asymptotic Distributions ‣ 5 Application to the Inverse Transform Watermark ‣ Optimal Detection for Language Watermarks with Pseudorandom Collision" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">5.1</span></a></h3>

<div id="A3.SS2.2" class="ltx_proof">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_font_italic ltx_title_proof">Proof of Theorem <a href="#S5.Thmtheorem1" title="Theorem 5.1 (Asymptotic joint distribution of pivotal statistics). ‣ 5.1 Asymptotic Distributions ‣ 5 Application to the Inverse Transform Watermark ‣ Optimal Detection for Language Watermarks with Pseudorandom Collision" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">5.1</span></a>.</h6>
<div id="A3.SS2.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A3.SS2.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A3.SS2.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text">This theorem establishes the asymptotic joint distribution of the pivotal statistics within a minimal unit. To achieve this, we will make use of the results in Lemma <a href="#S5.Thmlem1" title="Lemma 5.1 (Asymptotic joint distribution of pseudorandomness and tokens). ‣ 5.1 Asymptotic Distributions ‣ 5 Application to the Inverse Transform Watermark ‣ Optimal Detection for Language Watermarks with Pseudorandom Collision" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">5.1</span></a>.</span></p>
</div>
</div>
<section id="A3.SS2.SSS0.Px1" class="ltx_paragraph">
<h5 class="ltx_title ltx_title_paragraph">Null joint distribution of pivotal statistics.</h5>

<div id="A3.SS2.SSS0.Px1.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A3.SS2.SSS0.Px1.p1.1" class="ltx_p">We first derive the joint distribution under <math id="A3.SS2.SSS0.Px1.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="H_{0}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>H</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">H_{0}</annotation></semantics></math> for the pivotal statistics <math id="A3.SS2.SSS0.Px1.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(Y_{t})_{t\in{\mathcal{I}}^{\zeta}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>Y</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>∈</mo><msup><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℐ</mi><mi>ζ</mi></msup></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(Y_{t})_{t\in{\mathcal{I}}^{\zeta}}</annotation></semantics></math> within a minimal unit.
By Lemma <a href="#S5.Thmlem1" title="Lemma 5.1 (Asymptotic joint distribution of pseudorandomness and tokens). ‣ 5.1 Asymptotic Distributions ‣ 5 Application to the Inverse Transform Watermark ‣ Optimal Detection for Language Watermarks with Pseudorandom Collision" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">5.1</span></a>, as <math id="A3.SS2.SSS0.Px1.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="|{{\mathcal{W}}}|\to\infty" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒲</mi><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">∞</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">|{{\mathcal{W}}}|\to\infty</annotation></semantics></math>, each <math id="A3.SS2.SSS0.Px1.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="Y_{\ell}=|U-\eta(\pi(w_{\ell}))|" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>Y</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><mrow><mi>U</mi><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>η</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>π</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>w</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">Y_{\ell}=|U-\eta(\pi(w_{\ell}))|</annotation></semantics></math> converges weakly to <math id="A3.SS2.SSS0.Px1.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="|U-X_{\ell}|" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><mrow><mi>U</mi><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>X</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">|U-X_{\ell}|</annotation></semantics></math> under <math id="A3.SS2.SSS0.Px1.p1.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="H_{0}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>H</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">H_{0}</annotation></semantics></math>, where <math id="A3.SS2.SSS0.Px1.p1.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="U,X_{1},\ldots,X_{m}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>U</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>X</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>X</mi><mi>m</mi></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">U,X_{1},\ldots,X_{m}</annotation></semantics></math> are i.i.d. random variables uniformly distributed on <math id="A3.SS2.SSS0.Px1.p1.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="[0,1]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>1</mn><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">[0,1]</annotation></semantics></math>.
With a slight abuse of notation, we relabel <math id="A3.SS2.SSS0.Px1.p1.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="Y_{\ell}:=|U-X_{\ell}|" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>Y</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi></msub><mo>:=</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><mrow><mi>U</mi><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>X</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">Y_{\ell}:=|U-X_{\ell}|</annotation></semantics></math> for <math id="A3.SS2.SSS0.Px1.p1.m10" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\ell\in[m]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mi>m</mi><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\ell\in[m]</annotation></semantics></math> to simplify notation.</p>
</div>
<div id="A3.SS2.SSS0.Px1.p2" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A3.SS2.SSS0.Px1.p2.1" class="ltx_p">We begin by analyzing the conditional CDF of <math id="A3.SS2.SSS0.Px1.p2.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="Y_{\ell}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>Y</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">Y_{\ell}</annotation></semantics></math> given <math id="A3.SS2.SSS0.Px1.p2.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="U=u" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>U</mi><mo>=</mo><mi>u</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">U=u</annotation></semantics></math>.
Fix <math id="A3.SS2.SSS0.Px1.p2.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="u\in[0,1]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>u</mi><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">u\in[0,1]</annotation></semantics></math> and take any <math id="A3.SS2.SSS0.Px1.p2.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="y\in[0,1]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>y</mi><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">y\in[0,1]</annotation></semantics></math>. The conditional CDF of <math id="A3.SS2.SSS0.Px1.p2.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="Y_{\ell}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>Y</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">Y_{\ell}</annotation></semantics></math> is:</p>
<table id="A3.EGx60" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A3.E91"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A3.E91.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle{\mathbb{P}}(Y_{\ell}\leq y\mid U=u)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>ℙ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>Y</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi></msub><mo>≤</mo><mi>y</mi></mrow><mo fence="true" lspace="0em" rspace="0em">∣</mo><mrow><mi>U</mi><mo>=</mo><mi>u</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle{\mathbb{P}}(Y_{\ell}\leq y\mid U=u)</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A3.E91.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle={\mathbb{P}}(|U-X_{\ell}|\leq y\mid U=u)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>ℙ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><mrow><mi>U</mi><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>X</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow><mo>≤</mo><mi>y</mi></mrow><mo fence="true" lspace="0em" rspace="0em">∣</mo><mrow><mi>U</mi><mo>=</mo><mi>u</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle={\mathbb{P}}(|U-X_{\ell}|\leq y\mid U=u)</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(91)</span></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A3.E92"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A3.E92.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle={\mathbb{P}}(u-y\leq X_{\ell}\leq u+y\mid U=u)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>ℙ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>u</mi><mo>−</mo><mi>y</mi></mrow><mo>≤</mo><msub><mi>X</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi></msub><mo>≤</mo><mrow><mi>u</mi><mo>+</mo><mi>y</mi></mrow></mrow><mo fence="true" lspace="0em" rspace="0em">∣</mo><mrow><mi>U</mi><mo>=</mo><mi>u</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle={\mathbb{P}}(u-y\leq X_{\ell}\leq u+y\mid U=u)</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(92)</span></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A3.E93"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A3.E93.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=[(u+y)\wedge 1]-[(u-y)\vee 0]." display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>u</mi><mo>+</mo><mi>y</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>∧</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>u</mi><mo>−</mo><mi>y</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>∨</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=[(u+y)\wedge 1]-[(u-y)\vee 0].</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(93)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A3.SS2.SSS0.Px1.p2.2" class="ltx_p">The corresponding conditional PDF is then</p>
<table id="A3.EGx61" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A3.E94"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A3.E94.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle f_{Y_{\ell}\mid U}(y\mid u)=\begin{cases}2,&amp;\text{if }0&lt;y&lt;\min(u,1-u),\\
1,&amp;\text{if }\min(u,1-u)&lt;y&lt;\max(u,1-u),\\
0,&amp;\text{otherwise}.\end{cases}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>f</mi><mrow><msub><mi>Y</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi></msub><mo fence="false">|</mo><mi>U</mi></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>y</mi><mo fence="true" lspace="0em" rspace="0em">∣</mo><mi>u</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo>{</mo><mtable columnspacing="5pt" rowspacing="0pt"><mtr><mtd class="ltx_align_left" columnalign="left"><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo>,</mo></mrow></mtd><mtd class="ltx_align_left" columnalign="left"><mrow><mrow><mrow><mtext>if </mtext><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><mo>&lt;</mo><mi>y</mi><mo>&lt;</mo><mrow><mi>min</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>u</mi><mo>,</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mi>u</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow></mtd></mtr><mtr><mtd class="ltx_align_left" columnalign="left"><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>,</mo></mrow></mtd><mtd class="ltx_align_left" columnalign="left"><mrow><mrow><mrow><mtext>if </mtext><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mi>min</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>u</mi><mo>,</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mi>u</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>&lt;</mo><mi>y</mi><mo>&lt;</mo><mrow><mi>max</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>u</mi><mo>,</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mi>u</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow></mtd></mtr><mtr><mtd class="ltx_align_left" columnalign="left"><mrow><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo></mrow></mtd><mtd class="ltx_align_left" columnalign="left"><mrow><mtext>otherwise</mtext><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow></mtd></mtr></mtable></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle f_{Y_{\ell}\mid U}(y\mid u)=\begin{cases}2,&amp;\text{if }0&lt;y&lt;\min(u,1-u),\\
1,&amp;\text{if }\min(u,1-u)&lt;y&lt;\max(u,1-u),\\
0,&amp;\text{otherwise}.\end{cases}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(94)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A3.SS2.SSS0.Px1.p2.3" class="ltx_p">Consequently, under <math id="A3.SS2.SSS0.Px1.p2.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="H_{0}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>H</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">H_{0}</annotation></semantics></math>, the joint PDF of <math id="A3.SS2.SSS0.Px1.p2.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\bm{Y}=(Y_{1},\ldots,Y_{m})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>𝒀</mi><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>Y</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>Y</mi><mi>m</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\bm{Y}=(Y_{1},\ldots,Y_{m})</annotation></semantics></math> given <math id="A3.SS2.SSS0.Px1.p2.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="U=u" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>U</mi><mo>=</mo><mi>u</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">U=u</annotation></semantics></math> is:</p>
<table id="A3.EGx62" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A3.E95"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A3.E95.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle f_{\bm{Y}}(y_{1},\ldots,y_{m})=\int_{0}^{1}f_{Y_{1},\ldots,Y_{m}\mid U}(y_{1},\ldots,y_{m}\mid u)\,{\mathrm{d}}u=\int_{0}^{1}\prod_{\ell=1}^{m}f_{Y_{\ell}\mid U}(y_{\ell}\mid u)\,{\mathrm{d}}u." display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>f</mi><mi>𝒀</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>y</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>y</mi><mi>m</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><msubsup><mo>∫</mo><mn>0</mn><mn>1</mn></msubsup></mstyle><mrow><msub><mi>f</mi><mrow><msub><mi>Y</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi><mo>,</mo><mrow><msub><mi>Y</mi><mi>m</mi></msub><mo fence="false">|</mo><mi>U</mi></mrow></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>y</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>y</mi><mi>m</mi></msub></mrow><mo fence="true" lspace="0em" rspace="0em">∣</mo><mi>u</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0.170em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo rspace="0em">𝑑</mo><mi>u</mi></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><msubsup><mo>∫</mo><mn>0</mn><mn>1</mn></msubsup></mstyle><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∏</mo><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>m</mi></munderover></mstyle><mrow><msub><mi>f</mi><mrow><msub><mi>Y</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi></msub><mo fence="false">|</mo><mi>U</mi></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>y</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi></msub><mo fence="true" lspace="0em" rspace="0em">∣</mo><mi>u</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0.170em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo rspace="0em">𝑑</mo><mi>u</mi></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle f_{\bm{Y}}(y_{1},\ldots,y_{m})=\int_{0}^{1}f_{Y_{1},\ldots,Y_{m}\mid U}(y_{1},\ldots,y_{m}\mid u)\,{\mathrm{d}}u=\int_{0}^{1}\prod_{\ell=1}^{m}f_{Y_{\ell}\mid U}(y_{\ell}\mid u)\,{\mathrm{d}}u.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(95)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A3.SS2.SSS0.Px1.p2.4" class="ltx_p">To simplify this expression, define two index sets depending on <math id="A3.SS2.SSS0.Px1.p2.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="u" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>u</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">u</annotation></semantics></math>:</p>
<table id="A3.EGx63" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A3.E96"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A3.E96.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle I_{1}(u)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>I</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>u</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle I_{1}(u)</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A3.E96.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=\{\ell:0&lt;y_{\ell}&lt;\min(u,1-u)\}," display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mrow><mn>0</mn><mo>&lt;</mo><msub><mi>y</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi></msub><mo>&lt;</mo><mrow><mi>min</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>u</mi><mo>,</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mi>u</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=\{\ell:0&lt;y_{\ell}&lt;\min(u,1-u)\},</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(96)</span></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A3.E97"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A3.E97.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle I_{2}(u)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>I</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>u</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle I_{2}(u)</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A3.E97.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=\{\ell:y_{\ell}\geq\max(u,1-u)\}." display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mrow><msub><mi>y</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi></msub><mo>≥</mo><mrow><mi>max</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>u</mi><mo>,</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mi>u</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=\{\ell:y_{\ell}\geq\max(u,1-u)\}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(97)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A3.SS2.SSS0.Px1.p2.5" class="ltx_p">Then the joint density becomes:</p>
<table id="A3.EGx64" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A3.E98"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A3.E98.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle f_{0}(y_{1},\ldots,y_{m}):=f_{\bm{Y}}(y_{1},\ldots,y_{m})=\int_{0}^{1}2^{|I_{1}(u)|}{\bf 1}_{I_{2}(u)=\emptyset}\,{\mathrm{d}}u." display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>f</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>y</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>y</mi><mi>m</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>:=</mo><mrow><msub><mi>f</mi><mi>𝒀</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>y</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>y</mi><mi>m</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><msubsup><mo>∫</mo><mn>0</mn><mn>1</mn></msubsup></mstyle><mrow><msup><mn>2</mn><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><mrow><msub><mi>I</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>u</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mn>𝟏</mn><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>I</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>u</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">∅</mi></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo rspace="0em">𝑑</mo><mi>u</mi></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle f_{0}(y_{1},\ldots,y_{m}):=f_{\bm{Y}}(y_{1},\ldots,y_{m})=\int_{0}^{1}2^{|I_{1}(u)|}{\bf 1}_{I_{2}(u)=\emptyset}\,{\mathrm{d}}u.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(98)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A3.SS2.SSS0.Px1.p2.6" class="ltx_p">We will later provide an alternative representation of this density that is more convenient for theoretical analysis but more complex in form. For numerical computations, however, the integral expression in (<a href="#A3.E98" title="In Null joint distribution of pivotal statistics. ‣ C.2 Proof of Theorem ‣ Appendix C Proof for Inverse Transform Watermarks in Section ‣ Optimal Detection for Language Watermarks with Pseudorandom Collision" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">98</span></a>) is preferable.</p>
</div>
</section>
<section id="A3.SS2.SSS0.Px2" class="ltx_paragraph">
<h5 class="ltx_title ltx_title_paragraph">Alternative joint distribution of pivotal statistics.</h5>

<div id="A3.SS2.SSS0.Px2.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A3.SS2.SSS0.Px2.p1.1" class="ltx_p">We now derive the joint distribution under <math id="A3.SS2.SSS0.Px2.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="H_{1}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>H</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">H_{1}</annotation></semantics></math> for the pivotal statistics <math id="A3.SS2.SSS0.Px2.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(Y_{t})_{t\in{\mathcal{I}}^{\zeta}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>Y</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>∈</mo><msup><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℐ</mi><mi>ζ</mi></msup></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(Y_{t})_{t\in{\mathcal{I}}^{\zeta}}</annotation></semantics></math> within a minimal unit. According to Lemma <a href="#S5.Thmlem1" title="Lemma 5.1 (Asymptotic joint distribution of pseudorandomness and tokens). ‣ 5.1 Asymptotic Distributions ‣ 5 Application to the Inverse Transform Watermark ‣ Optimal Detection for Language Watermarks with Pseudorandom Collision" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">5.1</span></a>, under <math id="A3.SS2.SSS0.Px2.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="H_{1}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>H</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">H_{1}</annotation></semantics></math>, the tuple <math id="A3.SS2.SSS0.Px2.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(U,\eta(\pi(w_{1})),\ldots,\eta(\pi(w_{m})))" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>U</mi><mo>,</mo><mrow><mi>η</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>π</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>w</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi><mo>,</mo><mrow><mi>η</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>π</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>w</mi><mi>m</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(U,\eta(\pi(w_{1})),\ldots,\eta(\pi(w_{m})))</annotation></semantics></math> converges in distribution to <math id="A3.SS2.SSS0.Px2.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(U,X_{1},\ldots,X_{m})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>U</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>X</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>X</mi><mi>m</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(U,X_{1},\ldots,X_{m})</annotation></semantics></math>, where <math id="A3.SS2.SSS0.Px2.p1.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="X_{1},\ldots,X_{m}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>X</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>X</mi><mi>m</mi></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">X_{1},\ldots,X_{m}</annotation></semantics></math> are i.i.d. <math id="A3.SS2.SSS0.Px2.p1.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathrm{Unif}(0,1)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>Unif</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>1</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathrm{Unif}(0,1)</annotation></semantics></math> random variables, and <math id="A3.SS2.SSS0.Px2.p1.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="U" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>U</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">U</annotation></semantics></math> is drawn independently and uniformly from the interval</p>
<table id="A3.Ex162" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A3.Ex162.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\left[\max\limits_{\ell\in[m]}\{{\bar{\Delta}}_{\ell}X_{\ell}\},\ \min\limits_{\ell\in[m]}\{1-{\bar{\Delta}}_{\ell}+{\bar{\Delta}}_{\ell}X_{\ell}\}\right]," display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mo>[</mo><mrow><munder><mi>max</mi><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mi>m</mi><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow></munder><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mrow><msub><mover accent="true"><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo>¯</mo></mover><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>X</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.667em">,</mo><mrow><munder><mi>min</mi><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mi>m</mi><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow></munder><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mrow><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo>¯</mo></mover><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi></msub></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><msub><mover accent="true"><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo>¯</mo></mover><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>X</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi></msub></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>]</mo></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\left[\max\limits_{\ell\in[m]}\{{\bar{\Delta}}_{\ell}X_{\ell}\},\ \min\limits_{\ell\in[m]}\{1-{\bar{\Delta}}_{\ell}+{\bar{\Delta}}_{\ell}X_{\ell}\}\right],</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A3.SS2.SSS0.Px2.p1.2" class="ltx_p">conditioned on the interval being non-empty. For convenience, we denote <math id="A3.SS2.SSS0.Px2.p1.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="Y_{\ell}:=|U-X_{\ell}|" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>Y</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi></msub><mo>:=</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><mrow><mi>U</mi><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>X</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">Y_{\ell}:=|U-X_{\ell}|</annotation></semantics></math> for <math id="A3.SS2.SSS0.Px2.p1.m10" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\ell\in[m]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mi>m</mi><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\ell\in[m]</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>
</div>
<div id="A3.SS2.SSS0.Px2.p2" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A3.SS2.SSS0.Px2.p2.1" class="ltx_p">To obtain the joint density of <math id="A3.SS2.SSS0.Px2.p2.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(Y_{1},\ldots,Y_{m})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>Y</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>Y</mi><mi>m</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(Y_{1},\ldots,Y_{m})</annotation></semantics></math>, we consider the transformation</p>
<table id="A3.Ex163" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A3.Ex163.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\Phi:(U,X_{1},\ldots,X_{m})\mapsto(U,Y_{1},\ldots,Y_{m})=(U,|U-X_{1}|,\ldots,|U-X_{m}|)." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Φ</mi><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>U</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>X</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>X</mi><mi>m</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo stretchy="false">↦</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>U</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>Y</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>Y</mi><mi>m</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>U</mi><mo>,</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><mrow><mi>U</mi><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>X</mi><mn>1</mn></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi><mo>,</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><mrow><mi>U</mi><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>X</mi><mi>m</mi></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Phi:(U,X_{1},\ldots,X_{m})\mapsto(U,Y_{1},\ldots,Y_{m})=(U,|U-X_{1}|,\ldots,|U-X_{m}|).</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A3.SS2.SSS0.Px2.p2.2" class="ltx_p">Since <math id="A3.SS2.SSS0.Px2.p2.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\Phi" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi mathvariant="normal">Φ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Phi</annotation></semantics></math> is continuous and the joint law of <math id="A3.SS2.SSS0.Px2.p2.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(U,X_{1},\ldots,X_{m})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>U</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>X</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>X</mi><mi>m</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(U,X_{1},\ldots,X_{m})</annotation></semantics></math> is absolutely continuous, we may ignore boundary events (e.g., <math id="A3.SS2.SSS0.Px2.p2.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="Y_{\ell}=0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>Y</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">Y_{\ell}=0</annotation></semantics></math> for some <math id="A3.SS2.SSS0.Px2.p2.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\ell" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\ell</annotation></semantics></math>) which have zero measure.</p>
</div>
<div id="A3.SS2.SSS0.Px2.p3" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A3.SS2.SSS0.Px2.p3.1" class="ltx_p">However, <math id="A3.SS2.SSS0.Px2.p3.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\Phi" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi mathvariant="normal">Φ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Phi</annotation></semantics></math> is not injective due to the absolute values. To apply the change-of-variable formula, we partition the domain into disjoint regions where <math id="A3.SS2.SSS0.Px2.p3.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\Phi" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi mathvariant="normal">Φ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Phi</annotation></semantics></math> becomes bijective. For each sign vector <math id="A3.SS2.SSS0.Px2.p3.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\bm{\sigma}=(\sigma_{1},\ldots,\sigma_{m})\in\{-1,1\}^{m}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>𝝈</mi><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>σ</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>σ</mi><mi>m</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>∈</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mrow><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo>,</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow><mi>m</mi></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\bm{\sigma}=(\sigma_{1},\ldots,\sigma_{m})\in\{-1,1\}^{m}</annotation></semantics></math>, define the region</p>
<table id="A3.EGx65" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A3.E99"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A3.E99.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\mathcal{R}_{\bm{\sigma}}:=\left\{(u,x_{1},\ldots,x_{m})\in[0,1]^{m+1}:\sign(x_{\ell}-u)=\sigma_{\ell}\text{ for all }\ell\right\}." display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℛ</mi><mi>𝝈</mi></msub><mo>:=</mo><mrow><mo>{</mo><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>u</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>m</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>∈</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo rspace="0.278em" stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow><mrow><mi>m</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup></mrow><mo rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>sign</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>x</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi></msub><mo>−</mo><mi>u</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><msub><mi>σ</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mtext> for all </mtext><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi></mrow></mrow><mo>}</mo></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\mathcal{R}_{\bm{\sigma}}:=\left\{(u,x_{1},\ldots,x_{m})\in[0,1]^{m+1}:\sign(x_{\ell}-u)=\sigma_{\ell}\text{ for all }\ell\right\}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(99)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A3.SS2.SSS0.Px2.p3.2" class="ltx_p">Within <math id="A3.SS2.SSS0.Px2.p3.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{R}_{\bm{\sigma}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℛ</mi><mi>𝝈</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{R}_{\bm{\sigma}}</annotation></semantics></math>, we have <math id="A3.SS2.SSS0.Px2.p3.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="x_{\ell}=u+\sigma_{\ell}y_{\ell}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>x</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>u</mi><mo>+</mo><mrow><msub><mi>σ</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>y</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi></msub></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">x_{\ell}=u+\sigma_{\ell}y_{\ell}</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="A3.SS2.SSS0.Px2.p3.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\Phi" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi mathvariant="normal">Φ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Phi</annotation></semantics></math> is bijective with Jacobian determinant of absolute value 1. Thus, the joint density of <math id="A3.SS2.SSS0.Px2.p3.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(U,Y_{1},\ldots,Y_{m})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>U</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>Y</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>Y</mi><mi>m</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(U,Y_{1},\ldots,Y_{m})</annotation></semantics></math> on this region is directly given by the density of <math id="A3.SS2.SSS0.Px2.p3.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(U,X_{1},\ldots,X_{m})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>U</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>X</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>X</mi><mi>m</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(U,X_{1},\ldots,X_{m})</annotation></semantics></math> evaluated at <math id="A3.SS2.SSS0.Px2.p3.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(u,x_{1},\ldots,x_{m})=(u,u+\sigma_{1}y_{1},\ldots,u+\sigma_{m}y_{m})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>u</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>m</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>u</mi><mo>,</mo><mrow><mi>u</mi><mo>+</mo><mrow><msub><mi>σ</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>y</mi><mn>1</mn></msub></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi><mo>,</mo><mrow><mi>u</mi><mo>+</mo><mrow><msub><mi>σ</mi><mi>m</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>y</mi><mi>m</mi></msub></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(u,x_{1},\ldots,x_{m})=(u,u+\sigma_{1}y_{1},\ldots,u+\sigma_{m}y_{m})</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>
</div>
<div id="A3.SS2.SSS0.Px2.p4" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A3.SS2.SSS0.Px2.p4.1" class="ltx_p">To integrate out the nuisance parameter <math id="A3.SS2.SSS0.Px2.p4.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="U" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>U</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">U</annotation></semantics></math>, we first characterize the feasible values of <math id="A3.SS2.SSS0.Px2.p4.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="u" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>u</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">u</annotation></semantics></math> given <math id="A3.SS2.SSS0.Px2.p4.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\bm{y}=(y_{1},\ldots,y_{m})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>𝒚</mi><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>y</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>y</mi><mi>m</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\bm{y}=(y_{1},\ldots,y_{m})</annotation></semantics></math> and a fixed sign vector <math id="A3.SS2.SSS0.Px2.p4.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\bm{\sigma}=(\sigma_{1},\ldots,\sigma_{m})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>𝝈</mi><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>σ</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>σ</mi><mi>m</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\bm{\sigma}=(\sigma_{1},\ldots,\sigma_{m})</annotation></semantics></math>. The first requirement is that each reconstructed <math id="A3.SS2.SSS0.Px2.p4.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="x_{\ell}=u+\sigma_{\ell}y_{\ell}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>x</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>u</mi><mo>+</mo><mrow><msub><mi>σ</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>y</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi></msub></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">x_{\ell}=u+\sigma_{\ell}y_{\ell}</annotation></semantics></math> must lie within the unit interval <math id="A3.SS2.SSS0.Px2.p4.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="[0,1]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>1</mn><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">[0,1]</annotation></semantics></math>, which leads to the constraint:</p>
<table id="A3.EGx66" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A3.Ex164"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A3.Ex164.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle L_{\bm{\sigma}}(\bm{y}):=\max_{\ell}(-\sigma_{\ell}y_{\ell})\leq u\leq\min_{\ell}(1-\sigma_{\ell}y_{\ell})=:U_{\bm{\sigma}}(\bm{y})." display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>L</mi><mi>𝝈</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝒚</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>:=</mo><mrow><munder><mi>max</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi></munder><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><msub><mi>σ</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>y</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi></msub></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>≤</mo><mi>u</mi><mo>≤</mo><mrow><munder><mi>min</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi></munder><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mrow><msub><mi>σ</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>y</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi></msub></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mphantom></mphantom><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mrow><msub><mi>U</mi><mi>𝝈</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝒚</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle L_{\bm{\sigma}}(\bm{y}):=\max_{\ell}(-\sigma_{\ell}y_{\ell})\leq u\leq\min_{\ell}(1-\sigma_{\ell}y_{\ell})=:U_{\bm{\sigma}}(\bm{y}).</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A3.SS2.SSS0.Px2.p4.2" class="ltx_p">Second, we enforce the conditional event to hold from Corollary <a href="#A3.Thmtheorem1" title="Theorem C.1 (Asymptotic distribution under 𝐻_1). ‣ Proof of Lemma . ‣ C.1 Proof of Lemma ‣ Appendix C Proof for Inverse Transform Watermarks in Section ‣ Optimal Detection for Language Watermarks with Pseudorandom Collision" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">C.1</span></a>, which requires</p>
<table id="A3.Ex165" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A3.Ex165.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="{\bar{\Delta}}_{\ell}x_{\ell}\leq u\leq 1-{\bar{\Delta}}_{\ell}+{\bar{\Delta}}_{\ell}x_{\ell}\quad\text{for all }\ell." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mrow><msub><mover accent="true"><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo>¯</mo></mover><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi></msub></mrow><mo>≤</mo><mi>u</mi><mo>≤</mo><mrow><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo>¯</mo></mover><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi></msub></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><msub><mover accent="true"><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo>¯</mo></mover><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi></msub></mrow></mrow></mrow><mspace style="width:1em;" width="1em"></mspace><mrow><mtext>for all </mtext><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\bar{\Delta}}_{\ell}x_{\ell}\leq u\leq 1-{\bar{\Delta}}_{\ell}+{\bar{\Delta}}_{\ell}x_{\ell}\quad\text{for all }\ell.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A3.SS2.SSS0.Px2.p4.3" class="ltx_p">Substituting <math id="A3.SS2.SSS0.Px2.p4.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="x_{\ell}=u+\sigma_{\ell}y_{\ell}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>x</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>u</mi><mo>+</mo><mrow><msub><mi>σ</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>y</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi></msub></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">x_{\ell}=u+\sigma_{\ell}y_{\ell}</annotation></semantics></math> and solving for <math id="A3.SS2.SSS0.Px2.p4.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="u" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>u</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">u</annotation></semantics></math> leads to</p>
<table id="A3.Ex166" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A3.Ex166.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\frac{{\bar{\Delta}}_{\ell}\sigma_{\ell}y_{\ell}}{1-{\bar{\Delta}}_{\ell}}\leq u\leq 1+\frac{{\bar{\Delta}}_{\ell}\sigma_{\ell}y_{\ell}}{1-{\bar{\Delta}}_{\ell}}." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mfrac><mrow><msub><mover accent="true"><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo>¯</mo></mover><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>σ</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>y</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi></msub></mrow><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo>¯</mo></mover><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi></msub></mrow></mfrac><mo>≤</mo><mi>u</mi><mo>≤</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>+</mo><mfrac><mrow><msub><mover accent="true"><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo>¯</mo></mover><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>σ</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>y</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi></msub></mrow><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo>¯</mo></mover><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi></msub></mrow></mfrac></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\frac{{\bar{\Delta}}_{\ell}\sigma_{\ell}y_{\ell}}{1-{\bar{\Delta}}_{\ell}}\leq u\leq 1+\frac{{\bar{\Delta}}_{\ell}\sigma_{\ell}y_{\ell}}{1-{\bar{\Delta}}_{\ell}}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A3.SS2.SSS0.Px2.p4.4" class="ltx_p">Taking the maximum lower bound and minimum upper bound across <math id="A3.SS2.SSS0.Px2.p4.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\ell" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\ell</annotation></semantics></math>, we define</p>
<table id="A3.EGx67" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A3.Ex167"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A3.Ex167.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle Y_{\bm{\sigma}}^{+}(\bm{y})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msubsup><mi>Y</mi><mi>𝝈</mi><mo>+</mo></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝒚</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle Y_{\bm{\sigma}}^{+}(\bm{y})</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A3.Ex167.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle:=\max\left(\left\{\frac{{\bar{\Delta}}_{\ell}y_{\ell}}{1-{\bar{\Delta}}_{\ell}}:\sigma_{\ell}=+1\right\}\cup\{0\}\right)," display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>max</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mrow><mo>{</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><msub><mover accent="true"><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo>¯</mo></mover><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>y</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi></msub></mrow><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo>¯</mo></mover><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi></msub></mrow></mfrac></mstyle><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mrow><msub><mi>σ</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mrow><mo>}</mo></mrow><mo>∪</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mn>0</mn><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle:=\max\left(\left\{\frac{{\bar{\Delta}}_{\ell}y_{\ell}}{1-{\bar{\Delta}}_{\ell}}:\sigma_{\ell}=+1\right\}\cup\{0\}\right),</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A3.Ex168"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A3.Ex168.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle Y_{\bm{\sigma}}^{-}(\bm{y})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msubsup><mi>Y</mi><mi>𝝈</mi><mo>−</mo></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝒚</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle Y_{\bm{\sigma}}^{-}(\bm{y})</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A3.Ex168.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle:=\max\left(\left\{\frac{{\bar{\Delta}}_{\ell}y_{\ell}}{1-{\bar{\Delta}}_{\ell}}:\sigma_{\ell}=-1\right\}\cup\{0\}\right)," display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>max</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mrow><mo>{</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><msub><mover accent="true"><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo>¯</mo></mover><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>y</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi></msub></mrow><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo>¯</mo></mover><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi></msub></mrow></mfrac></mstyle><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mrow><msub><mi>σ</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mrow><mo>}</mo></mrow><mo>∪</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mn>0</mn><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle:=\max\left(\left\{\frac{{\bar{\Delta}}_{\ell}y_{\ell}}{1-{\bar{\Delta}}_{\ell}}:\sigma_{\ell}=-1\right\}\cup\{0\}\right),</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A3.SS2.SSS0.Px2.p4.5" class="ltx_p">which yield the additional constraint:</p>
<table id="A3.Ex169" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A3.Ex169.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="Y_{\bm{\sigma}}^{+}(\bm{y})\leq u\leq 1-Y_{\bm{\sigma}}^{-}(\bm{y})." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><msubsup><mi>Y</mi><mi>𝝈</mi><mo>+</mo></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝒚</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>≤</mo><mi>u</mi><mo>≤</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>Y</mi><mi>𝝈</mi><mo>−</mo></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝒚</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">Y_{\bm{\sigma}}^{+}(\bm{y})\leq u\leq 1-Y_{\bm{\sigma}}^{-}(\bm{y}).</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
<div id="A3.SS2.SSS0.Px2.p5" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A3.SS2.SSS0.Px2.p5.1" class="ltx_p">Combining both sets of constraints, the overall feasible range for <math id="A3.SS2.SSS0.Px2.p5.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="u" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>u</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">u</annotation></semantics></math> is the interval</p>
<table id="A3.Ex170" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A3.Ex170.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\left[A_{\bm{\sigma}}^{\bar{\bm{\Delta}}}(\bm{y}),B_{\bm{\sigma}}^{\bar{\bm{\Delta}}}(\bm{y})\right],\quad\text{where}\quad\begin{cases}A_{\bm{\sigma}}^{\bar{\bm{\Delta}}}(\bm{y}):=\max\{L_{\bm{\sigma}}(\bm{y}),Y_{\bm{\sigma}}^{+}(\bm{y})\},\\
B_{\bm{\sigma}}^{\bar{\bm{\Delta}}}(\bm{y}):=\min\{U_{\bm{\sigma}}(\bm{y}),1-Y_{\bm{\sigma}}^{-}(\bm{y})\}.\end{cases}" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mo>[</mo><msubsup><mi>A</mi><mi>𝝈</mi><mover accent="true"><mi>𝚫</mi><mo>¯</mo></mover></msubsup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝒚</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>,</mo><msubsup><mi>B</mi><mi>𝝈</mi><mover accent="true"><mi>𝚫</mi><mo>¯</mo></mover></msubsup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝒚</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>]</mo></mrow><mo rspace="1.167em">,</mo><mtext>where</mtext><mrow><mo>{</mo><mtable columnspacing="5pt" displaystyle="true" rowspacing="0pt"><mtr><mtd class="ltx_align_left" columnalign="left"><mrow><mrow><mrow><msubsup><mi>A</mi><mi>𝝈</mi><mover accent="true"><mi>𝚫</mi><mo>¯</mo></mover></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝒚</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>:=</mo><mrow><mi>max</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mrow><msub><mi>L</mi><mi>𝝈</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝒚</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>Y</mi><mi>𝝈</mi><mo>+</mo></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝒚</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow></mtd><mtd></mtd></mtr><mtr><mtd class="ltx_align_left" columnalign="left"><mrow><mrow><mrow><msubsup><mi>B</mi><mi>𝝈</mi><mover accent="true"><mi>𝚫</mi><mo>¯</mo></mover></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝒚</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>:=</mo><mrow><mi>min</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>U</mi><mi>𝝈</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝒚</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>Y</mi><mi>𝝈</mi><mo>−</mo></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝒚</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow></mtd><mtd></mtd></mtr></mtable></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\left[A_{\bm{\sigma}}^{\bar{\bm{\Delta}}}(\bm{y}),B_{\bm{\sigma}}^{\bar{\bm{\Delta}}}(\bm{y})\right],\quad\text{where}\quad\begin{cases}A_{\bm{\sigma}}^{\bar{\bm{\Delta}}}(\bm{y}):=\max\{L_{\bm{\sigma}}(\bm{y}),Y_{\bm{\sigma}}^{+}(\bm{y})\},\\
B_{\bm{\sigma}}^{\bar{\bm{\Delta}}}(\bm{y}):=\min\{U_{\bm{\sigma}}(\bm{y}),1-Y_{\bm{\sigma}}^{-}(\bm{y})\}.\end{cases}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A3.SS2.SSS0.Px2.p5.2" class="ltx_p">Since the density of <math id="A3.SS2.SSS0.Px2.p5.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(U,X_{1},\ldots,X_{m})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>U</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>X</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>X</mi><mi>m</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(U,X_{1},\ldots,X_{m})</annotation></semantics></math> is constant and equals <math id="A3.SS2.SSS0.Px2.p5.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="1/I_{m}(\bar{\bm{\Delta}})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>/</mo><msub><mi>I</mi><mi>m</mi></msub></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>𝚫</mi><mo>¯</mo></mover><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">1/I_{m}(\bar{\bm{\Delta}})</annotation></semantics></math> over its support, the contribution from each region is proportional to the length of this feasible interval:</p>
<table id="A3.Ex171" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A3.Ex171.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\ell_{\bm{\sigma}}^{\bar{\bm{\Delta}}}(\bm{y}):=\left(B_{\bm{\sigma}}^{\bar{\bm{\Delta}}}(\bm{y})-A_{\bm{\sigma}}^{\bar{\bm{\Delta}}}(\bm{y})\right)_{+}." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><msubsup><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mi>𝝈</mi><mover accent="true"><mi>𝚫</mi><mo>¯</mo></mover></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝒚</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>:=</mo><msub><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mrow><msubsup><mi>B</mi><mi>𝝈</mi><mover accent="true"><mi>𝚫</mi><mo>¯</mo></mover></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝒚</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>A</mi><mi>𝝈</mi><mover accent="true"><mi>𝚫</mi><mo>¯</mo></mover></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝒚</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow><mo>+</mo></msub></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\ell_{\bm{\sigma}}^{\bar{\bm{\Delta}}}(\bm{y}):=\left(B_{\bm{\sigma}}^{\bar{\bm{\Delta}}}(\bm{y})-A_{\bm{\sigma}}^{\bar{\bm{\Delta}}}(\bm{y})\right)_{+}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A3.SS2.SSS0.Px2.p5.3" class="ltx_p">Summing over all <math id="A3.SS2.SSS0.Px2.p5.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="2^{m}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mn>2</mn><mi>m</mi></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">2^{m}</annotation></semantics></math> sign vectors, the joint density of <math id="A3.SS2.SSS0.Px2.p5.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\bm{Y}=(Y_{1},\ldots,Y_{m})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>𝒀</mi><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>Y</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>Y</mi><mi>m</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\bm{Y}=(Y_{1},\ldots,Y_{m})</annotation></semantics></math> is</p>
<table id="A3.Ex172" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A3.Ex172.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="f_{\bar{\bm{\Delta}}}(\bm{y}):=f_{\bm{Y}}^{\bar{\bm{\Delta}}}(\bm{y})=\frac{1}{I_{m}(\bar{\bm{\Delta}})}\sum_{\bm{\sigma}\in\{-1,1\}^{m}}\ell_{\bm{\sigma}}^{\bar{\bm{\Delta}}}(\bm{y})." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>f</mi><mover accent="true"><mi>𝚫</mi><mo>¯</mo></mover></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝒚</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>:=</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>f</mi><mi>𝒀</mi><mover accent="true"><mi>𝚫</mi><mo>¯</mo></mover></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝒚</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mrow><msub><mi>I</mi><mi>m</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>𝚫</mi><mo>¯</mo></mover><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mfrac><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><munder><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>𝝈</mi><mo>∈</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mrow><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo>,</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow><mi>m</mi></msup></mrow></munder><mrow><msubsup><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mi>𝝈</mi><mover accent="true"><mi>𝚫</mi><mo>¯</mo></mover></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝒚</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">f_{\bar{\bm{\Delta}}}(\bm{y}):=f_{\bm{Y}}^{\bar{\bm{\Delta}}}(\bm{y})=\frac{1}{I_{m}(\bar{\bm{\Delta}})}\sum_{\bm{\sigma}\in\{-1,1\}^{m}}\ell_{\bm{\sigma}}^{\bar{\bm{\Delta}}}(\bm{y}).</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
<div id="A3.Thmrem1" class="ltx_theorem ltx_theorem_rem">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_title_theorem"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_theorem"><span id="A3.Thmrem1.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">Remark C.1</span></span><span id="A3.Thmrem1.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">.</span></h6>
<div id="A3.Thmrem1.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A3.Thmrem1.p1.1" class="ltx_p">As a sanity check, when <math id="A3.Thmrem1.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\bar{\bm{\Delta}}={\bf 0}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mover accent="true"><mi>𝚫</mi><mo>¯</mo></mover><mo>=</mo><mn>𝟎</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\bar{\bm{\Delta}}={\bf 0}</annotation></semantics></math>, we recover the null case. In that case, <math id="A3.Thmrem1.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="Y_{\bm{\sigma}}^{+}=Y_{\bm{\sigma}}^{-}=0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msubsup><mi>Y</mi><mi>𝝈</mi><mo>+</mo></msubsup><mo>=</mo><msubsup><mi>Y</mi><mi>𝝈</mi><mo>−</mo></msubsup><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">Y_{\bm{\sigma}}^{+}=Y_{\bm{\sigma}}^{-}=0</annotation></semantics></math>, and the constraint reduces to <math id="A3.Thmrem1.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="L_{\bm{\sigma}}(\bm{y})\leq u\leq U_{\bm{\sigma}}(\bm{y})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>L</mi><mi>𝝈</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝒚</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>≤</mo><mi>u</mi><mo>≤</mo><mrow><msub><mi>U</mi><mi>𝝈</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝒚</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">L_{\bm{\sigma}}(\bm{y})\leq u\leq U_{\bm{\sigma}}(\bm{y})</annotation></semantics></math>, matching the joint density under <math id="A3.Thmrem1.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="H_{0}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>H</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">H_{0}</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>
</div>
</div>
<div id="A3.SS2.SSS0.Px2.p6" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A3.SS2.SSS0.Px2.p6.1" class="ltx_p">∎</p>
</div>
</section>
</section>
<section id="A3.SS3" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection">C.3 </span>Proof of Corollary <a href="#S5.Thmcor1" title="Corollary 5.1 (Case 𝑚_𝑘=1). ‣ 5.1 Asymptotic Distributions ‣ 5 Application to the Inverse Transform Watermark ‣ Optimal Detection for Language Watermarks with Pseudorandom Collision" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">5.1</span></a></h3>

<div id="A3.SS3.2" class="ltx_proof">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_font_italic ltx_title_proof">Proof of Corollary <a href="#S5.Thmcor1" title="Corollary 5.1 (Case 𝑚_𝑘=1). ‣ 5.1 Asymptotic Distributions ‣ 5 Application to the Inverse Transform Watermark ‣ Optimal Detection for Language Watermarks with Pseudorandom Collision" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">5.1</span></a>.</h6>
<div id="A3.SS3.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A3.SS3.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A3.SS3.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text">This corollary follows by simplifying the expressions in Theorem <a href="#S5.Thmtheorem1" title="Theorem 5.1 (Asymptotic joint distribution of pivotal statistics). ‣ 5.1 Asymptotic Distributions ‣ 5 Application to the Inverse Transform Watermark ‣ Optimal Detection for Language Watermarks with Pseudorandom Collision" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">5.1</span></a>.</span></p>
</div>
<div id="A3.SS3.p2" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A3.SS3.p2.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A3.SS3.p2.1.1" class="ltx_text">We begin by analyzing the alternative distribution.
When <math id="A3.SS3.p2.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="m=1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>m</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">m=1</annotation></semantics></math>, the general density formula simplifies to:</span></p>
<table id="A3.Ex173" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A3.Ex173.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="f_{Y_{1}}^{\Delta_{1}}(y_{1})=\frac{1}{1-\Delta_{1}}\sum_{\sigma\in\{-1,1\}}\left(B_{\sigma}^{\Delta_{1}}(y_{1})-A_{\sigma}^{\Delta_{1}}(y_{1})\right)\vee 0." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><msubsup><mi>f</mi><msub><mi>Y</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mn>1</mn></msub></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>y</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mn>1</mn></msub></mrow></mfrac><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><munder><mo movablelimits="false" rspace="0em">∑</mo><mrow><mi>σ</mi><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mrow><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo>,</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow></mrow></munder><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mrow><msubsup><mi>B</mi><mi>σ</mi><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mn>1</mn></msub></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>y</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>A</mi><mi>σ</mi><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mn>1</mn></msub></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>y</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>∨</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">f_{Y_{1}}^{\Delta_{1}}(y_{1})=\frac{1}{1-\Delta_{1}}\sum_{\sigma\in\{-1,1\}}\left(B_{\sigma}^{\Delta_{1}}(y_{1})-A_{\sigma}^{\Delta_{1}}(y_{1})\right)\vee 0.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
</div>
<section id="A3.SS3.SSS0.Px1" class="ltx_paragraph">
<h5 class="ltx_title ltx_title_paragraph">Case <math id="A3.SS3.SSS0.Px1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\sigma=+1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>σ</mi><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\sigma=+1</annotation></semantics></math>.</h5>

<div id="A3.SS3.SSS0.Px1.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A3.SS3.SSS0.Px1.p1.1" class="ltx_p">Using the definitions from the theorem, we compute:</p>
<table id="A3.EGx68" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A3.Ex174"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A3.Ex174.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle A_{+1}^{\Delta_{1}}(y_{1})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msubsup><mi>A</mi><mrow><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mn>1</mn></msub></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>y</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle A_{+1}^{\Delta_{1}}(y_{1})</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A3.Ex174.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=\max\left\{-y_{1},\frac{\Delta_{1}y_{1}}{1-\Delta_{1}}\right\}=\frac{\Delta_{1}y_{1}}{1-\Delta_{1}}," display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>max</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>{</mo><mrow><mrow><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>y</mi><mn>1</mn></msub></mrow><mo>,</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>y</mi><mn>1</mn></msub></mrow><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mn>1</mn></msub></mrow></mfrac></mstyle></mrow><mo>}</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>y</mi><mn>1</mn></msub></mrow><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mn>1</mn></msub></mrow></mfrac></mstyle></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=\max\left\{-y_{1},\frac{\Delta_{1}y_{1}}{1-\Delta_{1}}\right\}=\frac{\Delta_{1}y_{1}}{1-\Delta_{1}},</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A3.Ex175"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A3.Ex175.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle B_{+1}^{\Delta_{1}}(y_{1})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msubsup><mi>B</mi><mrow><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mn>1</mn></msub></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>y</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle B_{+1}^{\Delta_{1}}(y_{1})</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A3.Ex175.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=\min\left\{1-y_{1},1\right\}=1-y_{1}." display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>min</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>{</mo><mrow><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>y</mi><mn>1</mn></msub></mrow><mo>,</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo>}</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>y</mi><mn>1</mn></msub></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=\min\left\{1-y_{1},1\right\}=1-y_{1}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A3.SS3.SSS0.Px1.p1.2" class="ltx_p">The corresponding contribution is:</p>
<table id="A3.Ex176" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A3.Ex176.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\left(1-y_{1}-\frac{\Delta_{1}y_{1}}{1-\Delta_{1}}\right)\vee 0=\left(1-\frac{y_{1}}{1-\Delta_{1}}\right)\vee 0." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>y</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>−</mo><mfrac><mrow><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>y</mi><mn>1</mn></msub></mrow><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mn>1</mn></msub></mrow></mfrac></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow><mo>∨</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mfrac><msub><mi>y</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mn>1</mn></msub></mrow></mfrac></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow><mo>∨</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\left(1-y_{1}-\frac{\Delta_{1}y_{1}}{1-\Delta_{1}}\right)\vee 0=\left(1-\frac{y_{1}}{1-\Delta_{1}}\right)\vee 0.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
</section>
<section id="A3.SS3.SSS0.Px2" class="ltx_paragraph">
<h5 class="ltx_title ltx_title_paragraph">Case <math id="A3.SS3.SSS0.Px2.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\sigma=-1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>σ</mi><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\sigma=-1</annotation></semantics></math>.</h5>

<div id="A3.SS3.SSS0.Px2.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A3.SS3.SSS0.Px2.p1.1" class="ltx_p">We have:</p>
<table id="A3.EGx69" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A3.Ex177"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A3.Ex177.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle A_{-1}^{\Delta_{1}}(y_{1})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msubsup><mi>A</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mn>1</mn></msub></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>y</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle A_{-1}^{\Delta_{1}}(y_{1})</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A3.Ex177.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=\max\left\{y_{1},0\right\}=y_{1}," display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>max</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>{</mo><msub><mi>y</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><mn>0</mn><mo>}</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><msub><mi>y</mi><mn>1</mn></msub></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=\max\left\{y_{1},0\right\}=y_{1},</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A3.Ex178"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A3.Ex178.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle B_{-1}^{\Delta_{1}}(y_{1})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msubsup><mi>B</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mn>1</mn></msub></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>y</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle B_{-1}^{\Delta_{1}}(y_{1})</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A3.Ex178.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=\min\left\{1+y_{1},1-\frac{\Delta_{1}y_{1}}{1-\Delta_{1}}\right\}=1-\frac{\Delta_{1}y_{1}}{1-\Delta_{1}}." display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>min</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>{</mo><mrow><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>+</mo><msub><mi>y</mi><mn>1</mn></msub></mrow><mo>,</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>y</mi><mn>1</mn></msub></mrow><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mn>1</mn></msub></mrow></mfrac></mstyle></mrow></mrow><mo>}</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>y</mi><mn>1</mn></msub></mrow><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mn>1</mn></msub></mrow></mfrac></mstyle></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=\min\left\{1+y_{1},1-\frac{\Delta_{1}y_{1}}{1-\Delta_{1}}\right\}=1-\frac{\Delta_{1}y_{1}}{1-\Delta_{1}}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A3.SS3.SSS0.Px2.p1.2" class="ltx_p">The resulting contribution is:</p>
<table id="A3.Ex179" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A3.Ex179.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\left(1-\frac{\Delta_{1}y_{1}}{1-\Delta_{1}}-y_{1}\right)\vee 0=\left(1-\frac{y_{1}}{1-\Delta_{1}}\right)\vee 0." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mfrac><mrow><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>y</mi><mn>1</mn></msub></mrow><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mn>1</mn></msub></mrow></mfrac><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>y</mi><mn>1</mn></msub></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow><mo>∨</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mfrac><msub><mi>y</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mn>1</mn></msub></mrow></mfrac></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow><mo>∨</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\left(1-\frac{\Delta_{1}y_{1}}{1-\Delta_{1}}-y_{1}\right)\vee 0=\left(1-\frac{y_{1}}{1-\Delta_{1}}\right)\vee 0.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
<div id="A3.SS3.SSS0.Px2.p2" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A3.SS3.SSS0.Px2.p2.1" class="ltx_p">Since both sign cases yield the same value, we obtain the final density by summing and applying the normalization:</p>
<table id="A3.Ex180" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A3.Ex180.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="f_{Y_{1}}^{\Delta_{1}}(y_{1})=\frac{2}{1-\Delta_{1}}\left(1-\frac{y_{1}}{1-\Delta_{1}}\right)," display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><msubsup><mi>f</mi><msub><mi>Y</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mn>1</mn></msub></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>y</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mfrac><mn>2</mn><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mn>1</mn></msub></mrow></mfrac><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mfrac><msub><mi>y</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mn>1</mn></msub></mrow></mfrac></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">f_{Y_{1}}^{\Delta_{1}}(y_{1})=\frac{2}{1-\Delta_{1}}\left(1-\frac{y_{1}}{1-\Delta_{1}}\right),</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A3.SS3.SSS0.Px2.p2.2" class="ltx_p">which expands to the triangular form in (<a href="#S5.E21" title="In 2nd item ‣ Corollary 5.1 (Case 𝑚_𝑘=1). ‣ 5.1 Asymptotic Distributions ‣ 5 Application to the Inverse Transform Watermark ‣ Optimal Detection for Language Watermarks with Pseudorandom Collision" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">21</span></a>).</p>
</div>
<div id="A3.SS3.SSS0.Px2.p3" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A3.SS3.SSS0.Px2.p3.1" class="ltx_p">Next, we consider the null distribution. When <math id="A3.SS3.SSS0.Px2.p3.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="m=1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>m</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">m=1</annotation></semantics></math>, the formula from Theorem <a href="#S5.Thmtheorem1" title="Theorem 5.1 (Asymptotic joint distribution of pivotal statistics). ‣ 5.1 Asymptotic Distributions ‣ 5 Application to the Inverse Transform Watermark ‣ Optimal Detection for Language Watermarks with Pseudorandom Collision" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">5.1</span></a> becomes:</p>
<table id="A3.Ex181" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A3.Ex181.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="f_{Y_{1}}(y_{1})=\int_{u:y_{1}&lt;\max(u,1-u)}2^{{\bf 1}(y_{1}&lt;\min(u,1-u))}\,{\mathrm{d}}u." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>f</mi><msub><mi>Y</mi><mn>1</mn></msub></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>y</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo rspace="0.111em">=</mo><msub><mo>∫</mo><mrow><mi>u</mi><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mrow><msub><mi>y</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>&lt;</mo><mrow><mi>max</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>u</mi><mo>,</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mi>u</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow></msub><msup><mn>2</mn><mrow><mn>𝟏</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>y</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>&lt;</mo><mrow><mi>min</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>u</mi><mo>,</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mi>u</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></msup><mi>d</mi><mi>u</mi><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">f_{Y_{1}}(y_{1})=\int_{u:y_{1}&lt;\max(u,1-u)}2^{{\bf 1}(y_{1}&lt;\min(u,1-u))}\,{\mathrm{d}}u.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
</section>
<section id="A3.SS3.SSS0.Px3" class="ltx_paragraph">
<h5 class="ltx_title ltx_title_paragraph">Case <math id="A3.SS3.SSS0.Px3.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="0&lt;y_{1}\leq 1/2" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mn>0</mn><mo>&lt;</mo><msub><mi>y</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>≤</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>/</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">0&lt;y_{1}\leq 1/2</annotation></semantics></math>.</h5>

<div id="A3.SS3.SSS0.Px3.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A3.SS3.SSS0.Px3.p1.1" class="ltx_p">In this case, <math id="A3.SS3.SSS0.Px3.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="y_{1}&lt;\min(u,1-u)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>y</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>&lt;</mo><mrow><mi>min</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>u</mi><mo>,</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mi>u</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">y_{1}&lt;\min(u,1-u)</annotation></semantics></math> if and only if <math id="A3.SS3.SSS0.Px3.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="u\in(y_{1},1-y_{1})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>u</mi><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>y</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>y</mi><mn>1</mn></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">u\in(y_{1},1-y_{1})</annotation></semantics></math>, and <math id="A3.SS3.SSS0.Px3.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="y_{1}&lt;\max(u,1-u)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>y</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>&lt;</mo><mrow><mi>max</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>u</mi><mo>,</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mi>u</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">y_{1}&lt;\max(u,1-u)</annotation></semantics></math> for all <math id="A3.SS3.SSS0.Px3.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="u\in(0,1)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>u</mi><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>1</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">u\in(0,1)</annotation></semantics></math>. Therefore, the density is:</p>
<table id="A3.Ex182" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A3.Ex182.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="f_{Y_{1}}(y_{1})=\int_{y_{1}}^{1-y_{1}}2\,{\mathrm{d}}u+\int_{0}^{y_{1}}{\mathrm{d}}u+\int_{1-y_{1}}^{1}{\mathrm{d}}u=2(1-2y_{1})+y_{1}+y_{1}=2(1-y_{1})." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>f</mi><msub><mi>Y</mi><mn>1</mn></msub></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>y</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.111em">=</mo><mrow><mrow><msubsup><mo>∫</mo><msub><mi>y</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>y</mi><mn>1</mn></msub></mrow></msubsup><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0.170em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo rspace="0em">𝑑</mo><mi>u</mi></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.055em">+</mo><mrow><msubsup><mo>∫</mo><mn>0</mn><msub><mi>y</mi><mn>1</mn></msub></msubsup><mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">𝑑</mo><mi>u</mi></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.055em">+</mo><mrow><msubsup><mo>∫</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>y</mi><mn>1</mn></msub></mrow><mn>1</mn></msubsup><mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">𝑑</mo><mi>u</mi></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>y</mi><mn>1</mn></msub></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><msub><mi>y</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>+</mo><msub><mi>y</mi><mn>1</mn></msub></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>y</mi><mn>1</mn></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">f_{Y_{1}}(y_{1})=\int_{y_{1}}^{1-y_{1}}2\,{\mathrm{d}}u+\int_{0}^{y_{1}}{\mathrm{d}}u+\int_{1-y_{1}}^{1}{\mathrm{d}}u=2(1-2y_{1})+y_{1}+y_{1}=2(1-y_{1}).</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
</section>
<section id="A3.SS3.SSS0.Px4" class="ltx_paragraph">
<h5 class="ltx_title ltx_title_paragraph">Case <math id="A3.SS3.SSS0.Px4.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="1/2&lt;y_{1}&lt;1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>/</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow><mo>&lt;</mo><msub><mi>y</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>&lt;</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">1/2&lt;y_{1}&lt;1</annotation></semantics></math>.</h5>

<div id="A3.SS3.SSS0.Px4.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A3.SS3.SSS0.Px4.p1.1" class="ltx_p">Here, <math id="A3.SS3.SSS0.Px4.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="y_{1}\geq\min(u,1-u)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>y</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>≥</mo><mrow><mi>min</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>u</mi><mo>,</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mi>u</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">y_{1}\geq\min(u,1-u)</annotation></semantics></math>, so the integrand is always 1. The condition <math id="A3.SS3.SSS0.Px4.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="y_{1}&lt;\max(u,1-u)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>y</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>&lt;</mo><mrow><mi>max</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>u</mi><mo>,</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mi>u</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">y_{1}&lt;\max(u,1-u)</annotation></semantics></math> is satisfied when <math id="A3.SS3.SSS0.Px4.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="u\in(0,1-y_{1})\cup(y_{1},1)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>u</mi><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>y</mi><mn>1</mn></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>∪</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>y</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><mn>1</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">u\in(0,1-y_{1})\cup(y_{1},1)</annotation></semantics></math>, yielding:</p>
<table id="A3.Ex183" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A3.Ex183.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="f_{Y_{1}}(y_{1})=\int_{0}^{1-y_{1}}{\mathrm{d}}u+\int_{y_{1}}^{1}{\mathrm{d}}u=(1-y_{1})+(1-y_{1})=2(1-y_{1})." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>f</mi><msub><mi>Y</mi><mn>1</mn></msub></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>y</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.111em">=</mo><mrow><mrow><msubsup><mo>∫</mo><mn>0</mn><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>y</mi><mn>1</mn></msub></mrow></msubsup><mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">𝑑</mo><mi>u</mi></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.055em">+</mo><mrow><msubsup><mo>∫</mo><msub><mi>y</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mn>1</mn></msubsup><mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">𝑑</mo><mi>u</mi></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>y</mi><mn>1</mn></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>y</mi><mn>1</mn></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>y</mi><mn>1</mn></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">f_{Y_{1}}(y_{1})=\int_{0}^{1-y_{1}}{\mathrm{d}}u+\int_{y_{1}}^{1}{\mathrm{d}}u=(1-y_{1})+(1-y_{1})=2(1-y_{1}).</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
<div id="A3.SS3.SSS0.Px4.p2" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A3.SS3.SSS0.Px4.p2.1" class="ltx_p">In both cases, we conclude that <math id="A3.SS3.SSS0.Px4.p2.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="f_{Y_{1}}(y_{1})=2(1-y_{1})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>f</mi><msub><mi>Y</mi><mn>1</mn></msub></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>y</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>y</mi><mn>1</mn></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">f_{Y_{1}}(y_{1})=2(1-y_{1})</annotation></semantics></math> for all <math id="A3.SS3.SSS0.Px4.p2.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="y_{1}\in(0,1)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>y</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>1</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">y_{1}\in(0,1)</annotation></semantics></math>, completing the proof.</p>
</div>
<div id="A3.SS3.SSS0.Px4.p3" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A3.SS3.SSS0.Px4.p3.1" class="ltx_p">∎</p>
</div>
</section>
</section>
<section id="A3.SS4" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection">C.4 </span>Proof of Lemma <a href="#A3.Thmlem1" title="Lemma C.1 (Exact joint distribution). ‣ Proof of Lemma . ‣ C.1 Proof of Lemma ‣ Appendix C Proof for Inverse Transform Watermarks in Section ‣ Optimal Detection for Language Watermarks with Pseudorandom Collision" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">C.1</span></a></h3>

<div id="A3.SS4.2" class="ltx_proof">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_font_italic ltx_title_proof">Proof of Lemma <a href="#A3.Thmlem1" title="Lemma C.1 (Exact joint distribution). ‣ Proof of Lemma . ‣ C.1 Proof of Lemma ‣ Appendix C Proof for Inverse Transform Watermarks in Section ‣ Optimal Detection for Language Watermarks with Pseudorandom Collision" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">C.1</span></a>.</h6>
<div id="A3.SS4.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A3.SS4.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A3.SS4.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text">The randomness in this setting arises from the pseudorandom variables <math id="A3.SS4.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="U" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>U</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">U</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="A3.SS4.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\pi" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>π</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\pi</annotation></semantics></math>. Given the fixed minimal unit <math id="A3.SS4.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="{\mathcal{I}}^{\zeta}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℐ</mi><mi>ζ</mi></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\mathcal{I}}^{\zeta}</annotation></semantics></math>, we aim to compute</span></p>
<table id="A3.E100" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A3.E100.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="{\mathbb{P}}_{1}\bigl(U\leq r,\,\pi(w_{\ell})=w_{\ell}^{\prime}\text{ for }\ell\in[m]~|~{\mathcal{I}}^{\zeta}\bigr)." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>ℙ</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">(</mo><mi>U</mi><mo>≤</mo><mi>r</mi><mo rspace="0.337em">,</mo><mi>π</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>w</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>=</mo><msubsup><mi>w</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mo>′</mo></msubsup><mtext> for </mtext><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mi>m</mi><mo rspace="0.330em" stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow><mo fence="false" rspace="0.497em" stretchy="false">|</mo><msup><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℐ</mi><mi>ζ</mi></msup><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\mathbb{P}}_{1}\bigl(U\leq r,\,\pi(w_{\ell})=w_{\ell}^{\prime}\text{ for }\ell\in[m]~|~{\mathcal{I}}^{\zeta}\bigr).</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(100)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
<div id="A3.SS4.p2" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A3.SS4.p2.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A3.SS4.p2.1.1" class="ltx_text">For each permutation <math id="A3.SS4.p2.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\pi" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>π</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\pi</annotation></semantics></math> of the vocabulary, we can evaluate the probability that <math id="A3.SS4.p2.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="U\in[0,r]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>U</mi><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mi>r</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">U\in[0,r]</annotation></semantics></math> under the constraint that <math id="A3.SS4.p2.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\pi(w_{\ell})=w_{\ell}^{\prime}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>π</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>w</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><msubsup><mi>w</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mo>′</mo></msubsup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\pi(w_{\ell})=w_{\ell}^{\prime}</annotation></semantics></math> for all <math id="A3.SS4.p2.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\ell\in[m]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mi>m</mi><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\ell\in[m]</annotation></semantics></math>. Recall the definition of the inverse transform decoder: for any token <math id="A3.SS4.p2.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="w" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>w</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">w</annotation></semantics></math>,</span></p>
<table id="A3.Ex184" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A3.Ex184.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\mathcal{S}^{\text{inv}}(\bm{P},\zeta)=w\quad\text{if and only if}\quad\sum_{w^{\prime}\in{{\mathcal{W}}}}P_{w^{\prime}}\cdot\mathbf{1}_{\{\pi(w^{\prime})&lt;\pi(w)\}}\leq U\leq\sum_{w^{\prime}\in{{\mathcal{W}}}}P_{w^{\prime}}\cdot\mathbf{1}_{\{\pi(w^{\prime})\leq\pi(w)\}}." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msup><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒮</mi><mtext>inv</mtext></msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝑷</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>ζ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>=</mo><mi>w</mi><mtext>if and only if</mtext><munder><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><msup><mi>w</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo>∈</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒲</mi></mrow></munder><msub><mi>P</mi><msup><mi>w</mi><mo>′</mo></msup></msub><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><msub><mn>𝟏</mn><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mi>π</mi><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>w</mi><msup><mrow></mrow><mo>′</mo></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo><mo>&lt;</mo><mi>π</mi><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>w</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow></msub><mo>≤</mo><mi>U</mi><mo rspace="0.111em">≤</mo><munder><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><msup><mi>w</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo>∈</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒲</mi></mrow></munder><msub><mi>P</mi><msup><mi>w</mi><mo>′</mo></msup></msub><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><msub><mn>𝟏</mn><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mi>π</mi><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>w</mi><msup><mrow></mrow><mo>′</mo></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo><mo>≤</mo><mi>π</mi><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>w</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{S}^{\text{inv}}(\bm{P},\zeta)=w\quad\text{if and only if}\quad\sum_{w^{\prime}\in{{\mathcal{W}}}}P_{w^{\prime}}\cdot\mathbf{1}_{\{\pi(w^{\prime})&lt;\pi(w)\}}\leq U\leq\sum_{w^{\prime}\in{{\mathcal{W}}}}P_{w^{\prime}}\cdot\mathbf{1}_{\{\pi(w^{\prime})\leq\pi(w)\}}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
<div id="A3.SS4.p3" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A3.SS4.p3.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A3.SS4.p3.1.1" class="ltx_text">In our setting, knowing that <math id="A3.SS4.p3.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\pi(w_{\ell})=w_{\ell}^{\prime}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>π</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>w</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><msubsup><mi>w</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mo>′</mo></msubsup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\pi(w_{\ell})=w_{\ell}^{\prime}</annotation></semantics></math> for all <math id="A3.SS4.p3.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\ell\in[m]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mi>m</mi><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\ell\in[m]</annotation></semantics></math> and using the definition that <math id="A3.SS4.p3.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="a_{\pi,\,w_{\ell}}^{(t)}=\sum_{j=1}^{w_{\ell}}P_{t,\pi(j)}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msubsup><mi>a</mi><mrow><mi>π</mi><mo rspace="0.337em">,</mo><msub><mi>w</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi></msub></mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup><mo rspace="0.111em">=</mo><mrow><msubsup><mo>∑</mo><mrow><mi>j</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><msub><mi>w</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi></msub></msubsup><msub><mi>P</mi><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>,</mo><mrow><mi>π</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>j</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></msub></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">a_{\pi,\,w_{\ell}}^{(t)}=\sum_{j=1}^{w_{\ell}}P_{t,\pi(j)}</annotation></semantics></math>, the above condition becomes, for each <math id="A3.SS4.p3.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="t\in{\mathcal{I}}^{Y}_{\ell}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>∈</mo><msubsup><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℐ</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mi>Y</mi></msubsup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">t\in{\mathcal{I}}^{Y}_{\ell}</annotation></semantics></math> (where <math id="A3.SS4.p3.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="w_{\ell}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>w</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">w_{\ell}</annotation></semantics></math> is the token associated with sub-block <math id="A3.SS4.p3.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="{\mathcal{I}}^{Y}_{\ell}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msubsup><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℐ</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mi>Y</mi></msubsup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\mathcal{I}}^{Y}_{\ell}</annotation></semantics></math>),</span></p>
<table id="A3.EGx70" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A3.E101"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A3.E101.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle a_{\pi^{-1},\,w_{\ell}^{\prime}-1}^{(t)}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msubsup><mi>a</mi><mrow><msup><mi>π</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup><mo rspace="0.337em">,</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>w</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mo>′</mo></msubsup><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle a_{\pi^{-1},\,w_{\ell}^{\prime}-1}^{(t)}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A3.E101.m2" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\displaystyle=\sum_{w^{\prime}\in{{\mathcal{W}}}}P_{t,w^{\prime}}\cdot\mathbf{1}_{\{\pi(w^{\prime})&lt;w_{\ell}^{\prime}\}}\leq U\leq\sum_{w^{\prime}\in{{\mathcal{W}}}}P_{t,w^{\prime}}\cdot\mathbf{1}_{\{\pi(w^{\prime})\leq w_{\ell}^{\prime}\}}=a_{\pi^{-1},\,w_{\ell}^{\prime}}^{(t)}." display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo>=</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo></mstyle><msub><mrow></mrow><mrow><msup><mi>w</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo>∈</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒲</mi></mrow></msub><mi>P</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>,</mo><msup><mi>w</mi><mo>′</mo></msup></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><mn>𝟏</mn><msub><mrow></mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mi>π</mi><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>w</mi><msup><mrow></mrow><mo>′</mo></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo><mo>&lt;</mo><mi>w</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi></msub><msup><mrow></mrow><mo>′</mo></msup><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow></msub><mo>≤</mo><mi>U</mi><mo>≤</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo></mstyle><msub><mrow></mrow><mrow><msup><mi>w</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo>∈</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒲</mi></mrow></msub><mi>P</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>,</mo><msup><mi>w</mi><mo>′</mo></msup></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><mn>𝟏</mn><msub><mrow></mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mi>π</mi><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>w</mi><msup><mrow></mrow><mo>′</mo></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo><mo>≤</mo><mi>w</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi></msub><msup><mrow></mrow><mo>′</mo></msup><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow></msub><mo>=</mo><mi>a</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mrow><msup><mi>π</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup><mo rspace="0.337em">,</mo><msubsup><mi>w</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mo>′</mo></msubsup></mrow></msub><msup><mrow></mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=\sum_{w^{\prime}\in{{\mathcal{W}}}}P_{t,w^{\prime}}\cdot\mathbf{1}_{\{\pi(w^{\prime})&lt;w_{\ell}^{\prime}\}}\leq U\leq\sum_{w^{\prime}\in{{\mathcal{W}}}}P_{t,w^{\prime}}\cdot\mathbf{1}_{\{\pi(w^{\prime})\leq w_{\ell}^{\prime}\}}=a_{\pi^{-1},\,w_{\ell}^{\prime}}^{(t)}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(101)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
<div id="A3.SS4.p4" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A3.SS4.p4.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A3.SS4.p4.1.1" class="ltx_text">The corresponding feasible region for <math id="A3.SS4.p4.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="U" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>U</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">U</annotation></semantics></math> is thus the intersection</span></p>
<table id="A3.EGx71" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A3.E102"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A3.E102.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\bigcap_{\ell=1}^{m}\bigcap_{t\in{\mathcal{I}}^{Y}_{\ell}}\left(a_{\pi^{-1},w_{\ell}^{\prime}-1}^{(t)},\,a_{\pi^{-1},w_{\ell}^{\prime}}^{(t)}\right)." display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">⋂</mo><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>m</mi></munderover></mstyle><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munder><mo movablelimits="false">⋂</mo><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>∈</mo><msubsup><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℐ</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mi>Y</mi></msubsup></mrow></munder></mstyle><mrow><mo>(</mo><msubsup><mi>a</mi><mrow><msup><mi>π</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup><mo>,</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>w</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mo>′</mo></msubsup><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup><mo rspace="0.337em">,</mo><msubsup><mi>a</mi><mrow><msup><mi>π</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup><mo>,</mo><msubsup><mi>w</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mo>′</mo></msubsup></mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\bigcap_{\ell=1}^{m}\bigcap_{t\in{\mathcal{I}}^{Y}_{\ell}}\left(a_{\pi^{-1},w_{\ell}^{\prime}-1}^{(t)},\,a_{\pi^{-1},w_{\ell}^{\prime}}^{(t)}\right).</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(102)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A3.SS4.p4.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="A3.SS4.p4.2.1" class="ltx_text">Summing over all permutations <math id="A3.SS4.p4.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\pi" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>π</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\pi</annotation></semantics></math> and all tuples of mutually distinct tokens <math id="A3.SS4.p4.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="w_{1}^{\prime},\ldots,w_{m}^{\prime}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msubsup><mi>w</mi><mn>1</mn><mo>′</mo></msubsup><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi><mo>,</mo><msubsup><mi>w</mi><mi>m</mi><mo>′</mo></msubsup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">w_{1}^{\prime},\ldots,w_{m}^{\prime}</annotation></semantics></math> (that is, <math id="A3.SS4.p4.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathrm{distinct}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>distinct</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathrm{distinct}</annotation></semantics></math>), we obtain:</span></p>
<table id="A3.EGx72" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A3.E103"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A3.E103.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\displaystyle{\mathbb{P}}_{1}\bigl(U\leq r,\,\pi(w_{\ell})=w_{\ell}^{\prime}\text{ for }\ell\in[m]~|~{\mathcal{I}}^{\zeta}\bigr)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>ℙ</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">(</mo><mi>U</mi><mo>≤</mo><mi>r</mi><mo rspace="0.337em">,</mo><mi>π</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>w</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>=</mo><msubsup><mi>w</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mo>′</mo></msubsup><mtext> for </mtext><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mi>m</mi><mo rspace="0.330em" stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow><mo fence="false" rspace="0.497em" stretchy="false">|</mo><msup><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℐ</mi><mi>ζ</mi></msup><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle{\mathbb{P}}_{1}\bigl(U\leq r,\,\pi(w_{\ell})=w_{\ell}^{\prime}\text{ for }\ell\in[m]~|~{\mathcal{I}}^{\zeta}\bigr)</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(103)</span></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A3.E104"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A3.E104.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=\;" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mo>=</mo><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=\;</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A3.E104.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\frac{1}{|{{\mathcal{W}}}|!}\sum_{\begin{subarray}{c}\pi\in\mathrm{Perm}({{\mathcal{W}}})\\
\pi(w_{\ell}^{\prime})=w_{\ell},\;\ell\in[m]\end{subarray}}{\mathbb{P}}\left(U\in\bigcap_{\ell=1}^{m}\bigcap_{t\in{\mathcal{I}}^{Y}_{\ell}}\left(a_{\pi,w_{\ell}^{\prime}-1}^{(t)},\,a_{\pi,w_{\ell}^{\prime}}^{(t)}\right)\cap[0,r]\right)." display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒲</mi><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow><mo>!</mo></mrow></mfrac></mstyle><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munder><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mtable rowspacing="0pt"><mtr><mtd><mrow><mi>π</mi><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mi>Perm</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒲</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mtd></mtr><mtr><mtd><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>π</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msubsup><mi>w</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mo>′</mo></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><msub><mi>w</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi></msub></mrow><mo rspace="0.447em">,</mo><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mi>m</mi><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mtd></mtr></mtable></munder></mstyle><mrow><mi>ℙ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mi>U</mi><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">⋂</mo><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>m</mi></munderover></mstyle><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munder><mo movablelimits="false">⋂</mo><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>∈</mo><msubsup><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℐ</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mi>Y</mi></msubsup></mrow></munder></mstyle><mrow><mo>(</mo><msubsup><mi>a</mi><mrow><mi>π</mi><mo>,</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>w</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mo>′</mo></msubsup><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup><mo rspace="0.337em">,</mo><msubsup><mi>a</mi><mrow><mi>π</mi><mo>,</mo><msubsup><mi>w</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mo>′</mo></msubsup></mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>∩</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mi>r</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\frac{1}{|{{\mathcal{W}}}|!}\sum_{\begin{subarray}{c}\pi\in\mathrm{Perm}({{\mathcal{W}}})\\
\pi(w_{\ell}^{\prime})=w_{\ell},\;\ell\in[m]\end{subarray}}{\mathbb{P}}\left(U\in\bigcap_{\ell=1}^{m}\bigcap_{t\in{\mathcal{I}}^{Y}_{\ell}}\left(a_{\pi,w_{\ell}^{\prime}-1}^{(t)},\,a_{\pi,w_{\ell}^{\prime}}^{(t)}\right)\cap[0,r]\right).</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(104)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A3.SS4.p4.3" class="ltx_p"><span id="A3.SS4.p4.3.1" class="ltx_text">Note that since we sum over all permutations <math id="A3.SS4.p4.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\pi" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>π</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\pi</annotation></semantics></math>, the roles of <math id="A3.SS4.p4.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\pi" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>π</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\pi</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="A3.SS4.p4.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\pi^{-1}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi>π</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\pi^{-1}</annotation></semantics></math> are interchangeable in the expression above. Hence, we replace <math id="A3.SS4.p4.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\pi" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>π</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\pi</annotation></semantics></math> with <math id="A3.SS4.p4.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\pi^{-1}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi>π</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\pi^{-1}</annotation></semantics></math> in the last equation for notational simplicity.</span></p>
</div>
<div id="A3.SS4.p5" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A3.SS4.p5.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A3.SS4.p5.1.1" class="ltx_text">To obtain the normalization constant (that is, the denominator of the conditional probability), we set <math id="A3.SS4.p5.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="r=1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>r</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">r=1</annotation></semantics></math> and sum over all distinct <math id="A3.SS4.p5.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="w_{1}^{\prime},\ldots,w_{m}^{\prime}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msubsup><mi>w</mi><mn>1</mn><mo>′</mo></msubsup><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi><mo>,</mo><msubsup><mi>w</mi><mi>m</mi><mo>′</mo></msubsup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">w_{1}^{\prime},\ldots,w_{m}^{\prime}</annotation></semantics></math>:</span></p>
<table id="A3.EGx73" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A3.E105"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A3.E105.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\displaystyle\sum_{\begin{subarray}{c}w_{1}^{\prime},\ldots,w_{m}^{\prime}\\
\mathrm{distinct}\end{subarray}}{\mathbb{P}}\bigl(U\leq 1,\,\pi(w_{\ell})=w_{\ell}^{\prime}\text{ for }\ell\in[m]~|~{\mathcal{I}}^{\zeta}\bigr)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munder><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mtable rowspacing="0pt"><mtr><mtd><mrow><msubsup><mi>w</mi><mn>1</mn><mo>′</mo></msubsup><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi><mo>,</mo><msubsup><mi>w</mi><mi>m</mi><mo>′</mo></msubsup></mrow></mtd></mtr><mtr><mtd><mi>distinct</mi></mtd></mtr></mtable></munder></mstyle><mi>ℙ</mi><mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">(</mo><mi>U</mi><mo>≤</mo><mn>1</mn><mo rspace="0.337em">,</mo><mi>π</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>w</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>=</mo><msubsup><mi>w</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mo>′</mo></msubsup><mtext> for </mtext><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mi>m</mi><mo rspace="0.330em" stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow><mo fence="false" rspace="0.497em" stretchy="false">|</mo><msup><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℐ</mi><mi>ζ</mi></msup><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\sum_{\begin{subarray}{c}w_{1}^{\prime},\ldots,w_{m}^{\prime}\\
\mathrm{distinct}\end{subarray}}{\mathbb{P}}\bigl(U\leq 1,\,\pi(w_{\ell})=w_{\ell}^{\prime}\text{ for }\ell\in[m]~|~{\mathcal{I}}^{\zeta}\bigr)</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(105)</span></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A3.E106"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A3.E106.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=\;" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mo>=</mo><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=\;</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A3.E106.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\frac{1}{|{{\mathcal{W}}}|!}\sum_{\begin{subarray}{c}w_{1}^{\prime},\ldots,w_{m}^{\prime}\\
\mathrm{distinct}\end{subarray}}\sum_{\begin{subarray}{c}\pi\in\mathrm{Perm}({{\mathcal{W}}})\\
\pi(w_{\ell}^{\prime})=w_{\ell},\;\ell\in[m]\end{subarray}}{\mathbb{P}}\left(U\in\bigcap_{\ell=1}^{m}\bigcap_{t\in{\mathcal{I}}^{Y}_{\ell}}\left(a_{\pi,w_{\ell}^{\prime}-1}^{(t)},\,a_{\pi,w_{\ell}^{\prime}}^{(t)}\right)\cap[0,1]\right)." display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒲</mi><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow><mo>!</mo></mrow></mfrac></mstyle><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munder><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mtable rowspacing="0pt"><mtr><mtd><mrow><msubsup><mi>w</mi><mn>1</mn><mo>′</mo></msubsup><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi><mo>,</mo><msubsup><mi>w</mi><mi>m</mi><mo>′</mo></msubsup></mrow></mtd></mtr><mtr><mtd><mi>distinct</mi></mtd></mtr></mtable></munder></mstyle><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munder><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mtable rowspacing="0pt"><mtr><mtd><mrow><mi>π</mi><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mi>Perm</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒲</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mtd></mtr><mtr><mtd><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>π</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msubsup><mi>w</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mo>′</mo></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><msub><mi>w</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi></msub></mrow><mo rspace="0.447em">,</mo><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mi>m</mi><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mtd></mtr></mtable></munder></mstyle><mrow><mi>ℙ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mi>U</mi><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">⋂</mo><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>m</mi></munderover></mstyle><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munder><mo movablelimits="false">⋂</mo><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>∈</mo><msubsup><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℐ</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mi>Y</mi></msubsup></mrow></munder></mstyle><mrow><mo>(</mo><msubsup><mi>a</mi><mrow><mi>π</mi><mo>,</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>w</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mo>′</mo></msubsup><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup><mo rspace="0.337em">,</mo><msubsup><mi>a</mi><mrow><mi>π</mi><mo>,</mo><msubsup><mi>w</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mo>′</mo></msubsup></mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>∩</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\frac{1}{|{{\mathcal{W}}}|!}\sum_{\begin{subarray}{c}w_{1}^{\prime},\ldots,w_{m}^{\prime}\\
\mathrm{distinct}\end{subarray}}\sum_{\begin{subarray}{c}\pi\in\mathrm{Perm}({{\mathcal{W}}})\\
\pi(w_{\ell}^{\prime})=w_{\ell},\;\ell\in[m]\end{subarray}}{\mathbb{P}}\left(U\in\bigcap_{\ell=1}^{m}\bigcap_{t\in{\mathcal{I}}^{Y}_{\ell}}\left(a_{\pi,w_{\ell}^{\prime}-1}^{(t)},\,a_{\pi,w_{\ell}^{\prime}}^{(t)}\right)\cap[0,1]\right).</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(106)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
<div id="A3.SS4.p6" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A3.SS4.p6.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A3.SS4.p6.1.1" class="ltx_text">Thus, the conditional probability can be expressed as</span></p>
<table id="A3.EGx74" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A3.E107"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A3.E107.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\displaystyle{\mathbb{P}}\bigl(U\leq r,\,\pi(w_{\ell})=w_{\ell}^{\prime}\text{ for }\ell\in[m]\,\big|\,{\mathcal{I}}^{\zeta}\bigr)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>ℙ</mi><mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">(</mo><mi>U</mi><mo>≤</mo><mi>r</mi><mo rspace="0.337em">,</mo><mi>π</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>w</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>=</mo><msubsup><mi>w</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mo>′</mo></msubsup><mtext> for </mtext><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mi>m</mi><mo rspace="0.170em" stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow><mo fence="false" maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em" rspace="0.337em" stretchy="true">|</mo><msup><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℐ</mi><mi>ζ</mi></msup><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle{\mathbb{P}}\bigl(U\leq r,\,\pi(w_{\ell})=w_{\ell}^{\prime}\text{ for }\ell\in[m]\,\big|\,{\mathcal{I}}^{\zeta}\bigr)</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(107)</span></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A3.E108"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A3.E108.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=\;" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mo>=</mo><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=\;</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A3.E108.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\frac{\frac{1}{|{{\mathcal{W}}}|!}\sum_{\begin{subarray}{c}\pi\in\mathrm{Perm}({{\mathcal{W}}})\\
\pi(w_{\ell}^{\prime})=w_{\ell},\;\ell\in[m]\end{subarray}}{\mathbb{P}}\left(U\in\bigcap_{\ell=1}^{m}\bigcap_{t\in{\mathcal{I}}^{Y}_{\ell}}\left(a_{\pi,w_{\ell}^{\prime}-1}^{(t)},\,a_{\pi,w_{\ell}^{\prime}}^{(t)}\right)\cap[0,r]\right)}{\frac{1}{|{{\mathcal{W}}}|!}\sum_{\begin{subarray}{c}w_{1}^{\prime},\ldots,w_{m}^{\prime}\\
\mathrm{distinct}\end{subarray}}\sum_{\begin{subarray}{c}\pi\in\mathrm{Perm}({{\mathcal{W}}})\\
\pi(w_{\ell}^{\prime})=w_{\ell},\;\ell\in[m]\end{subarray}}{\mathbb{P}}\left(U\in\bigcap_{\ell=1}^{m}\bigcap_{t\in{\mathcal{I}}^{Y}_{\ell}}\left(a_{\pi,w_{\ell}^{\prime}-1}^{(t)},\,a_{\pi,w_{\ell}^{\prime}}^{(t)}\right)\right)}." display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒲</mi><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow><mo>!</mo></mrow></mfrac><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><msub><mo>∑</mo><mtable rowspacing="0pt"><mtr><mtd><mrow><mi>π</mi><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mi>Perm</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒲</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mtd></mtr><mtr><mtd><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>π</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msubsup><mi>w</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mo>′</mo></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><msub><mi>w</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi></msub></mrow><mo rspace="0.447em">,</mo><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mi>m</mi><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mtd></mtr></mtable></msub><mrow><mi>ℙ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mi>U</mi><mo rspace="0.111em">∈</mo><mrow><mrow><msubsup><mo rspace="0em">⋂</mo><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>m</mi></msubsup><mrow><msub><mo rspace="0em">⋂</mo><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>∈</mo><msubsup><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℐ</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mi>Y</mi></msubsup></mrow></msub><mrow><mo>(</mo><msubsup><mi>a</mi><mrow><mi>π</mi><mo>,</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>w</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mo>′</mo></msubsup><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup><mo rspace="0.337em">,</mo><msubsup><mi>a</mi><mrow><mi>π</mi><mo>,</mo><msubsup><mi>w</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mo>′</mo></msubsup></mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>∩</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mi>r</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mrow><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒲</mi><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow><mo>!</mo></mrow></mfrac><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><msub><mo rspace="0em">∑</mo><mtable rowspacing="0pt"><mtr><mtd><mrow><msubsup><mi>w</mi><mn>1</mn><mo>′</mo></msubsup><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi><mo>,</mo><msubsup><mi>w</mi><mi>m</mi><mo>′</mo></msubsup></mrow></mtd></mtr><mtr><mtd><mi>distinct</mi></mtd></mtr></mtable></msub><mrow><msub><mo>∑</mo><mtable rowspacing="0pt"><mtr><mtd><mrow><mi>π</mi><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mi>Perm</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒲</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mtd></mtr><mtr><mtd><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>π</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msubsup><mi>w</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mo>′</mo></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><msub><mi>w</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi></msub></mrow><mo rspace="0.447em">,</mo><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mi>m</mi><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mtd></mtr></mtable></msub><mrow><mi>ℙ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mi>U</mi><mo rspace="0.111em">∈</mo><mrow><msubsup><mo rspace="0em">⋂</mo><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>m</mi></msubsup><mrow><msub><mo rspace="0em">⋂</mo><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>∈</mo><msubsup><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℐ</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mi>Y</mi></msubsup></mrow></msub><mrow><mo>(</mo><msubsup><mi>a</mi><mrow><mi>π</mi><mo>,</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>w</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mo>′</mo></msubsup><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup><mo rspace="0.337em">,</mo><msubsup><mi>a</mi><mrow><mi>π</mi><mo>,</mo><msubsup><mi>w</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mo>′</mo></msubsup></mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow></mfrac></mstyle><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\frac{\frac{1}{|{{\mathcal{W}}}|!}\sum_{\begin{subarray}{c}\pi\in\mathrm{Perm}({{\mathcal{W}}})\\
\pi(w_{\ell}^{\prime})=w_{\ell},\;\ell\in[m]\end{subarray}}{\mathbb{P}}\left(U\in\bigcap_{\ell=1}^{m}\bigcap_{t\in{\mathcal{I}}^{Y}_{\ell}}\left(a_{\pi,w_{\ell}^{\prime}-1}^{(t)},\,a_{\pi,w_{\ell}^{\prime}}^{(t)}\right)\cap[0,r]\right)}{\frac{1}{|{{\mathcal{W}}}|!}\sum_{\begin{subarray}{c}w_{1}^{\prime},\ldots,w_{m}^{\prime}\\
\mathrm{distinct}\end{subarray}}\sum_{\begin{subarray}{c}\pi\in\mathrm{Perm}({{\mathcal{W}}})\\
\pi(w_{\ell}^{\prime})=w_{\ell},\;\ell\in[m]\end{subarray}}{\mathbb{P}}\left(U\in\bigcap_{\ell=1}^{m}\bigcap_{t\in{\mathcal{I}}^{Y}_{\ell}}\left(a_{\pi,w_{\ell}^{\prime}-1}^{(t)},\,a_{\pi,w_{\ell}^{\prime}}^{(t)}\right)\right)}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(108)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A3.SS4.p6.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="A3.SS4.p6.2.1" class="ltx_text">∎</span></p>
</div>
</div>
</section>
<section id="A3.SS5" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection">C.5 </span>Proof of Theorem <a href="#A3.Thmtheorem1" title="Theorem C.1 (Asymptotic distribution under 𝐻_1). ‣ Proof of Lemma . ‣ C.1 Proof of Lemma ‣ Appendix C Proof for Inverse Transform Watermarks in Section ‣ Optimal Detection for Language Watermarks with Pseudorandom Collision" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">C.1</span></a></h3>

<div id="A3.SS5.2" class="ltx_proof">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_font_italic ltx_title_proof">Proof of Theorem <a href="#A3.Thmtheorem1" title="Theorem C.1 (Asymptotic distribution under 𝐻_1). ‣ Proof of Lemma . ‣ C.1 Proof of Lemma ‣ Appendix C Proof for Inverse Transform Watermarks in Section ‣ Optimal Detection for Language Watermarks with Pseudorandom Collision" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">C.1</span></a>.</h6>
<div id="A3.SS5.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A3.SS5.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A3.SS5.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text">In this proof, we aim to show that the absolute error</span></p>
<table id="A3.EGx75" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A3.E109"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A3.E109.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\left|\EB_{1,\bm{P}_{{\mathcal{I}}^{\zeta}}}\left[J(U,\eta(\pi(w_{1})),\ldots,\eta(\pi(w_{m})))\right]-\frac{1}{I_{m}(\bar{\bm{\Delta}})}\int_{[0,1]^{m}}\left(\int_{{\mathcal{I}}(\bm{x},\bar{\bm{\Delta}})}J(u,\bm{x})\,{\mathrm{d}}u\right){\bf 1}_{{\mathcal{I}}(\bm{x},\bar{\bm{\Delta}})\neq\emptyset}{\mathrm{d}}\bm{x}\right|" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo>|</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>𝔼</mi><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>𝐏</mi><msup><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℐ</mi><mi>ζ</mi></msup></msub></mrow></msub><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>[</mo><mrow><mi>J</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>U</mi><mo>,</mo><mrow><mi>η</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>π</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>w</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi><mo>,</mo><mrow><mi>η</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>π</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>w</mi><mi>m</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>]</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mrow><msub><mi>I</mi><mi>m</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>𝚫</mi><mo>¯</mo></mover><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mfrac></mstyle><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><msub><mo>∫</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow><mi>m</mi></msup></msub></mstyle><mrow><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><msub><mo>∫</mo><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℐ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝐱</mi><mo>,</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>𝚫</mi><mo>¯</mo></mover><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></msub></mstyle><mrow><mrow><mi>J</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>u</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>𝐱</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0.170em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>du</mi></mrow></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mn>𝟏</mn><mrow><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℐ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝐱</mi><mo>,</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>𝚫</mi><mo>¯</mo></mover><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>≠</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">∅</mi></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo rspace="0em">𝑑</mo><mi>𝐱</mi></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>|</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\left|\EB_{1,\bm{P}_{{\mathcal{I}}^{\zeta}}}\left[J(U,\eta(\pi(w_{1})),\ldots,\eta(\pi(w_{m})))\right]-\frac{1}{I_{m}(\bar{\bm{\Delta}})}\int_{[0,1]^{m}}\left(\int_{{\mathcal{I}}(\bm{x},\bar{\bm{\Delta}})}J(u,\bm{x})\,{\mathrm{d}}u\right){\bf 1}_{{\mathcal{I}}(\bm{x},\bar{\bm{\Delta}})\neq\emptyset}{\mathrm{d}}\bm{x}\right|</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(109)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A3.SS5.p1.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="A3.SS5.p1.2.1" class="ltx_text">converges to zero as the vocabulary size <math id="A3.SS5.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="|{{\mathcal{W}}}|" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒲</mi><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">|{{\mathcal{W}}}|</annotation></semantics></math> tends to infinity, provided that the underlying NTP distributions <math id="A3.SS5.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\bm{P}_{{\mathcal{I}}^{\zeta}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>𝑷</mi><msup><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℐ</mi><mi>ζ</mi></msup></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\bm{P}_{{\mathcal{I}}^{\zeta}}</annotation></semantics></math> satisfy Assumption <a href="#S5.Thmasmp1" title="Assumption 5.1 (Asymptotic NTP conditions). ‣ 5.1 Asymptotic Distributions ‣ 5 Application to the Inverse Transform Watermark ‣ Optimal Detection for Language Watermarks with Pseudorandom Collision" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">5.1</span></a>.
In the expression (<a href="#A3.E109" title="In Proof of Theorem . ‣ C.5 Proof of Theorem ‣ Appendix C Proof for Inverse Transform Watermarks in Section ‣ Optimal Detection for Language Watermarks with Pseudorandom Collision" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">109</span></a>), we simplify the original target integral by letting <math id="A3.SS5.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\bm{x}=(x_{1},\ldots,x_{m})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>𝒙</mi><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>m</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\bm{x}=(x_{1},\ldots,x_{m})</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="A3.SS5.p1.m4" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="{\mathrm{d}}\bm{x}={\mathrm{d}}x_{1}\cdots{\mathrm{d}}x_{m}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>d</mi><mi>𝒙</mi><mo>=</mo><mi>d</mi><mi>x</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mn>1</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">⋯</mo><mi>d</mi><mi>x</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>m</mi></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\mathrm{d}}\bm{x}={\mathrm{d}}x_{1}\cdots{\mathrm{d}}x_{m}</annotation></semantics></math>, and by rewriting the normalization constant via</span></p>
<table id="A3.E110" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A3.E110.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="{\mathcal{I}}(\bm{x},\bar{\bm{\Delta}})=\left[\max\limits_{\ell\in[m]}\{{\bar{\Delta}}_{\ell}x_{\ell}\},\;\min\limits_{\ell\in[m]}\{1-{\bar{\Delta}}_{\ell}+{\bar{\Delta}}_{\ell}x_{\ell}\}\right]," display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℐ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝒙</mi><mo>,</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>𝚫</mi><mo>¯</mo></mover><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo>[</mo><mrow><mrow><munder><mi>max</mi><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mi>m</mi><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow></munder><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mrow><msub><mover accent="true"><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo>¯</mo></mover><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.447em">,</mo><mrow><munder><mi>min</mi><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mi>m</mi><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow></munder><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mrow><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo>¯</mo></mover><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi></msub></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><msub><mover accent="true"><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo>¯</mo></mover><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi></msub></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>]</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\mathcal{I}}(\bm{x},\bar{\bm{\Delta}})=\left[\max\limits_{\ell\in[m]}\{{\bar{\Delta}}_{\ell}x_{\ell}\},\;\min\limits_{\ell\in[m]}\{1-{\bar{\Delta}}_{\ell}+{\bar{\Delta}}_{\ell}x_{\ell}\}\right],</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(110)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A3.SS5.p1.3" class="ltx_p"><span id="A3.SS5.p1.3.1" class="ltx_text">where we define <math id="A3.SS5.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="{\bar{\Delta}}_{\ell}:=\max_{t\in{\mathcal{I}}^{Y}_{\ell}}\Delta_{t}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mover accent="true"><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo>¯</mo></mover><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi></msub><mo>:=</mo><mrow><msub><mi>max</mi><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>∈</mo><msubsup><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℐ</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mi>Y</mi></msubsup></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mi>t</mi></msub></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\bar{\Delta}}_{\ell}:=\max_{t\in{\mathcal{I}}^{Y}_{\ell}}\Delta_{t}</annotation></semantics></math>.
As specified in Definition <a href="#A3.Thmdefn1" title="Definition C.1 (Fixed-parameter belief class). ‣ Belief classes. ‣ Appendix C Proof for Inverse Transform Watermarks in Section ‣ Optimal Detection for Language Watermarks with Pseudorandom Collision" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">C.1</span></a>, the NTP distributions <math id="A3.SS5.p1.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\bm{P}_{{\mathcal{I}}^{\zeta}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>𝑷</mi><msup><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℐ</mi><mi>ζ</mi></msup></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\bm{P}_{{\mathcal{I}}^{\zeta}}</annotation></semantics></math> are assumed to belong to the class <math id="A3.SS5.p1.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="{\mathcal{Q}}_{\mathrm{type}(\bm{P}_{{\mathcal{I}}^{\zeta}}),\bm{\Delta}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒬</mi><mrow><mrow><mi>type</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>𝑷</mi><msup><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℐ</mi><mi>ζ</mi></msup></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo><mi>𝚫</mi></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\mathcal{Q}}_{\mathrm{type}(\bm{P}_{{\mathcal{I}}^{\zeta}}),\bm{\Delta}}</annotation></semantics></math> from Assumption <a href="#S5.Thmasmp1" title="Assumption 5.1 (Asymptotic NTP conditions). ‣ 5.1 Asymptotic Distributions ‣ 5 Application to the Inverse Transform Watermark ‣ Optimal Detection for Language Watermarks with Pseudorandom Collision" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">5.1</span></a>.</span></p>
</div>
<div id="A3.SS5.p2" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A3.SS5.p2.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A3.SS5.p2.1.1" class="ltx_text">Let <math id="A3.SS5.p2.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="J\colon[0,1]^{m+1}\to[0,\infty)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>J</mi><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mrow><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow><mrow><mi>m</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">∞</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">J\colon[0,1]^{m+1}\to[0,\infty)</annotation></semantics></math> be a 1-Lipschitz function.
Without loss of generality, we assume <math id="A3.SS5.p2.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="J(0,0,\ldots,0)=0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>J</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi><mo>,</mo><mn>0</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">J(0,0,\ldots,0)=0</annotation></semantics></math>. This is justified because replacing <math id="A3.SS5.p2.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="J" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>J</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">J</annotation></semantics></math> with <math id="A3.SS5.p2.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="J-C" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>J</mi><mo>−</mo><mi>C</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">J-C</annotation></semantics></math> for any constant <math id="A3.SS5.p2.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="C" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>C</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">C</annotation></semantics></math> does not affect the absolute error term in (<a href="#A3.E109" title="In Proof of Theorem . ‣ C.5 Proof of Theorem ‣ Appendix C Proof for Inverse Transform Watermarks in Section ‣ Optimal Detection for Language Watermarks with Pseudorandom Collision" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">109</span></a>) by using the fact that <math id="A3.SS5.p2.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="I_{m}(\bar{\bm{\Delta}})=\int_{[0,1]^{m}}|{\mathcal{I}}(\bm{x},\bar{\bm{\Delta}})|\cdot{\bf 1}_{{\mathcal{I}}(\bm{x},\bar{\bm{\Delta}})\neq\emptyset}\,{\mathrm{d}}\bm{x}." display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>I</mi><mi>m</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>𝚫</mi><mo>¯</mo></mover><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.111em">=</mo><mrow><mrow><mrow><msub><mo rspace="0em">∫</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow><mi>m</mi></msup></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℐ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝒙</mi><mo>,</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>𝚫</mi><mo>¯</mo></mover><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.055em" stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><msub><mn>𝟏</mn><mrow><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℐ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝒙</mi><mo>,</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>𝚫</mi><mo>¯</mo></mover><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>≠</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">∅</mi></mrow></msub></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo rspace="0em">𝑑</mo><mi>𝒙</mi></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">I_{m}(\bar{\bm{\Delta}})=\int_{[0,1]^{m}}|{\mathcal{I}}(\bm{x},\bar{\bm{\Delta}})|\cdot{\bf 1}_{{\mathcal{I}}(\bm{x},\bar{\bm{\Delta}})\neq\emptyset}\,{\mathrm{d}}\bm{x}.</annotation></semantics></math></span></p>
</div>
<div id="A3.SS5.p3" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A3.SS5.p3.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A3.SS5.p3.1.1" class="ltx_text">We are now ready to analyze the asymptotic behavior of <math id="A3.SS5.p3.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\EB_{1,\bm{P}_{{\mathcal{I}}^{\zeta}}}\left[J(U,\eta(\pi(w_{1})),\ldots,\eta(\pi(w_{m})))\right]." display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>𝔼</mi><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>𝐏</mi><msup><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℐ</mi><mi>ζ</mi></msup></msub></mrow></msub><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>[</mo><mrow><mi>J</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>U</mi><mo>,</mo><mrow><mi>η</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>π</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>w</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi><mo>,</mo><mrow><mi>η</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>π</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>w</mi><mi>m</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>]</mo></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\EB_{1,\bm{P}_{{\mathcal{I}}^{\zeta}}}\left[J(U,\eta(\pi(w_{1})),\ldots,\eta(\pi(w_{m})))\right].</annotation></semantics></math>
An exact formulation is provided by Corollary <a href="#A3.Thmcor1" title="Corollary C.1. ‣ Proof of Lemma . ‣ C.1 Proof of Lemma ‣ Appendix C Proof for Inverse Transform Watermarks in Section ‣ Optimal Detection for Language Watermarks with Pseudorandom Collision" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">C.1</span></a>:</span></p>
<table id="A3.EGx76" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A3.Ex185"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A3.Ex185.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\EB_{1,\bm{P}_{{\mathcal{I}}^{\zeta}}}\left[J(U,\eta(\pi(w_{1})),\ldots,\eta(\pi(w_{m})))\right]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>𝔼</mi><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>𝐏</mi><msup><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℐ</mi><mi>ζ</mi></msup></msub></mrow></msub><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>[</mo><mrow><mi>J</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>U</mi><mo>,</mo><mrow><mi>η</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>π</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>w</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi><mo>,</mo><mrow><mi>η</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>π</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>w</mi><mi>m</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>]</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\EB_{1,\bm{P}_{{\mathcal{I}}^{\zeta}}}\left[J(U,\eta(\pi(w_{1})),\ldots,\eta(\pi(w_{m})))\right]</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A3.E111"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A3.E111.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=\frac{\sum_{\begin{subarray}{c}w^{\prime}_{1},\ldots,w^{\prime}_{m}\\
\mathrm{distinct}\end{subarray}}\sum_{\begin{subarray}{c}\pi\in\mathrm{Perm}({{\mathcal{W}}})\\
\pi(w_{\ell}^{\prime})=w_{\ell},\forall\ell\in[m]\end{subarray}}\int_{\max\limits_{\ell,t}a_{\pi,w^{\prime}_{\ell}-1}^{(t)}}^{\min\limits_{\ell,t}a_{\pi,w^{\prime}_{\ell}}^{(t)}}J(u,\eta(w^{\prime}_{1}),\ldots,\eta(w^{\prime}_{m}))\,{\mathrm{d}}u{\bf 1}_{\min\limits_{\ell,t}a_{\pi,w^{\prime}_{\ell}}^{(t)}\geq\max\limits_{\ell,t}a_{\pi,w^{\prime}_{\ell}-1}^{(t)}}}{\sum_{\begin{subarray}{c}w^{\prime}_{1},\ldots,w^{\prime}_{m}\\
\mathrm{distinct}\end{subarray}}\sum_{\begin{subarray}{c}\pi\in\mathrm{Perm}({{\mathcal{W}}})\\
\pi(w_{\ell}^{\prime})=w_{\ell},\forall\ell\in[m]\end{subarray}}{\mathbb{P}}\left(U\in\bigcap_{\ell=1}^{m}\bigcap_{t\in{\mathcal{I}}^{Y}_{\ell}}\left(a_{\pi,w^{\prime}_{\ell}-1}^{(t)},a_{\pi,w^{\prime}_{\ell}}^{(t)}\right)\right)}," display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><msub><mo>∑</mo><mtable rowspacing="0pt"><mtr><mtd><mrow><msubsup><mi>w</mi><mn>1</mn><mo>′</mo></msubsup><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi><mo>,</mo><msubsup><mi>w</mi><mi>m</mi><mo>′</mo></msubsup></mrow></mtd></mtr><mtr><mtd><mi>distinct</mi></mtd></mtr></mtable></msub><mrow><msub><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">∑</mo><mtable rowspacing="0pt"><mtr><mtd><mrow><mi>π</mi><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mi>Perm</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒲</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mtd></mtr><mtr><mtd><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>π</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msubsup><mi>w</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mo>′</mo></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><msub><mi>w</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi></msub></mrow><mo>,</mo><mrow><mrow><mo rspace="0.167em">∀</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi></mrow><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mi>m</mi><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mtd></mtr></mtable></msub><mrow><msubsup><mo>∫</mo><mrow><munder><mi>max</mi><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow></munder><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><msubsup><mi>a</mi><mrow><mi>π</mi><mo>,</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>w</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mo>′</mo></msubsup><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup></mrow><mrow><munder><mi>min</mi><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow></munder><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><msubsup><mi>a</mi><mrow><mi>π</mi><mo>,</mo><msubsup><mi>w</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mo>′</mo></msubsup></mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup></mrow></msubsup><mrow><mrow><mi>J</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>u</mi><mo>,</mo><mrow><mi>η</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msubsup><mi>w</mi><mn>1</mn><mo>′</mo></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi><mo>,</mo><mrow><mi>η</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msubsup><mi>w</mi><mi>m</mi><mo>′</mo></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0.170em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo rspace="0em">𝑑</mo><mi>u</mi></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mn>𝟏</mn><mrow><mrow><munder><mi>min</mi><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow></munder><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><msubsup><mi>a</mi><mrow><mi>π</mi><mo>,</mo><msubsup><mi>w</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mo>′</mo></msubsup></mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup></mrow><mo>≥</mo><mrow><munder><mi>max</mi><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow></munder><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><msubsup><mi>a</mi><mrow><mi>π</mi><mo>,</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>w</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mo>′</mo></msubsup><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup></mrow></mrow></msub></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mrow><msub><mo>∑</mo><mtable rowspacing="0pt"><mtr><mtd><mrow><msubsup><mi>w</mi><mn>1</mn><mo>′</mo></msubsup><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi><mo>,</mo><msubsup><mi>w</mi><mi>m</mi><mo>′</mo></msubsup></mrow></mtd></mtr><mtr><mtd><mi>distinct</mi></mtd></mtr></mtable></msub><mrow><msub><mo lspace="0.167em">∑</mo><mtable rowspacing="0pt"><mtr><mtd><mrow><mi>π</mi><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mi>Perm</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒲</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mtd></mtr><mtr><mtd><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>π</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msubsup><mi>w</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mo>′</mo></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><msub><mi>w</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi></msub></mrow><mo>,</mo><mrow><mrow><mo rspace="0.167em">∀</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi></mrow><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mi>m</mi><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mtd></mtr></mtable></msub><mrow><mi>ℙ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mi>U</mi><mo rspace="0.111em">∈</mo><mrow><msubsup><mo rspace="0em">⋂</mo><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>m</mi></msubsup><mrow><msub><mo rspace="0em">⋂</mo><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>∈</mo><msubsup><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℐ</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mi>Y</mi></msubsup></mrow></msub><mrow><mo>(</mo><msubsup><mi>a</mi><mrow><mi>π</mi><mo>,</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>w</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mo>′</mo></msubsup><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup><mo>,</mo><msubsup><mi>a</mi><mrow><mi>π</mi><mo>,</mo><msubsup><mi>w</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mo>′</mo></msubsup></mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow></mfrac></mstyle></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=\frac{\sum_{\begin{subarray}{c}w^{\prime}_{1},\ldots,w^{\prime}_{m}\\
\mathrm{distinct}\end{subarray}}\sum_{\begin{subarray}{c}\pi\in\mathrm{Perm}({{\mathcal{W}}})\\
\pi(w_{\ell}^{\prime})=w_{\ell},\forall\ell\in[m]\end{subarray}}\int_{\max\limits_{\ell,t}a_{\pi,w^{\prime}_{\ell}-1}^{(t)}}^{\min\limits_{\ell,t}a_{\pi,w^{\prime}_{\ell}}^{(t)}}J(u,\eta(w^{\prime}_{1}),\ldots,\eta(w^{\prime}_{m}))\,{\mathrm{d}}u{\bf 1}_{\min\limits_{\ell,t}a_{\pi,w^{\prime}_{\ell}}^{(t)}\geq\max\limits_{\ell,t}a_{\pi,w^{\prime}_{\ell}-1}^{(t)}}}{\sum_{\begin{subarray}{c}w^{\prime}_{1},\ldots,w^{\prime}_{m}\\
\mathrm{distinct}\end{subarray}}\sum_{\begin{subarray}{c}\pi\in\mathrm{Perm}({{\mathcal{W}}})\\
\pi(w_{\ell}^{\prime})=w_{\ell},\forall\ell\in[m]\end{subarray}}{\mathbb{P}}\left(U\in\bigcap_{\ell=1}^{m}\bigcap_{t\in{\mathcal{I}}^{Y}_{\ell}}\left(a_{\pi,w^{\prime}_{\ell}-1}^{(t)},a_{\pi,w^{\prime}_{\ell}}^{(t)}\right)\right)},</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(111)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A3.SS5.p3.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="A3.SS5.p3.2.1" class="ltx_text">where <math id="A3.SS5.p3.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\min\limits_{\ell,t}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><munder><mi>min</mi><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow></munder><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\min\limits_{\ell,t}</annotation></semantics></math> denotes <math id="A3.SS5.p3.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\min_{\ell}\min_{t\in{\mathcal{I}}^{Y}_{\ell}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>min</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi></msub><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><msub><mi>min</mi><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>∈</mo><msubsup><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℐ</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mi>Y</mi></msubsup></mrow></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\min_{\ell}\min_{t\in{\mathcal{I}}^{Y}_{\ell}}</annotation></semantics></math> and similarly <math id="A3.SS5.p3.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\max\limits_{\ell,t}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><munder><mi>max</mi><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow></munder><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\max\limits_{\ell,t}</annotation></semantics></math> denotes <math id="A3.SS5.p3.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\max_{\ell}\max_{t\in{\mathcal{I}}^{Y}_{\ell}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>max</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi></msub><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><msub><mi>max</mi><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>∈</mo><msubsup><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℐ</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mi>Y</mi></msubsup></mrow></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\max_{\ell}\max_{t\in{\mathcal{I}}^{Y}_{\ell}}</annotation></semantics></math> for simplicity.</span></p>
</div>
</div>
<section id="A3.SS5.SSS0.Px1" class="ltx_paragraph">
<h5 class="ltx_title ltx_title_paragraph">Numerator.</h5>

<div id="A3.SS5.SSS0.Px1.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A3.SS5.SSS0.Px1.p1.1" class="ltx_p">We begin by analyzing the numerator of (<a href="#A3.E111" title="In Proof of Theorem . ‣ C.5 Proof of Theorem ‣ Appendix C Proof for Inverse Transform Watermarks in Section ‣ Optimal Detection for Language Watermarks with Pseudorandom Collision" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">111</span></a>):</p>
<table id="A3.EGx77" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A3.E112"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A3.E112.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\frac{1}{|{{\mathcal{W}}}|!}\sum_{\begin{subarray}{c}w^{\prime}_{1},\ldots,w^{\prime}_{m}\\
\mathrm{distinct}\end{subarray}}\sum_{\begin{subarray}{c}\pi\in\mathrm{Perm}({{\mathcal{W}}})\\
\pi(w_{\ell}^{\prime})=w_{\ell},\forall\ell\in[m]\end{subarray}}\left(\int_{\max\limits_{\ell,t}a_{\pi,w^{\prime}_{\ell}-1}^{(t)}}^{\min\limits_{\ell,t}a_{\pi,w^{\prime}_{\ell}}^{(t)}}J(u,\eta(w^{\prime}_{1}),\ldots,\eta(w^{\prime}_{m}))\,{\mathrm{d}}u\right){\bf 1}_{\min\limits_{\ell,t}a_{\pi,w^{\prime}_{\ell}}^{(t)}\geq\max\limits_{\ell,t}a_{\pi,w^{\prime}_{\ell}-1}^{(t)}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒲</mi><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow><mo>!</mo></mrow></mfrac></mstyle><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munder><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mtable rowspacing="0pt"><mtr><mtd><mrow><msubsup><mi>w</mi><mn>1</mn><mo>′</mo></msubsup><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi><mo>,</mo><msubsup><mi>w</mi><mi>m</mi><mo>′</mo></msubsup></mrow></mtd></mtr><mtr><mtd><mi>distinct</mi></mtd></mtr></mtable></munder></mstyle><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munder><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mtable rowspacing="0pt"><mtr><mtd><mrow><mi>π</mi><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mi>Perm</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒲</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mtd></mtr><mtr><mtd><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>π</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msubsup><mi>w</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mo>′</mo></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><msub><mi>w</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi></msub></mrow><mo>,</mo><mrow><mrow><mo rspace="0.167em">∀</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi></mrow><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mi>m</mi><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mtd></mtr></mtable></munder></mstyle><mrow><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><msubsup><mo>∫</mo><mrow><munder><mi>max</mi><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow></munder><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><msubsup><mi>a</mi><mrow><mi>π</mi><mo>,</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>w</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mo>′</mo></msubsup><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup></mrow><mrow><munder><mi>min</mi><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow></munder><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><msubsup><mi>a</mi><mrow><mi>π</mi><mo>,</mo><msubsup><mi>w</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mo>′</mo></msubsup></mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup></mrow></msubsup></mstyle><mrow><mrow><mi>J</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>u</mi><mo>,</mo><mrow><mi>η</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msubsup><mi>w</mi><mn>1</mn><mo>′</mo></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi><mo>,</mo><mrow><mi>η</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msubsup><mi>w</mi><mi>m</mi><mo>′</mo></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0.170em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo rspace="0em">𝑑</mo><mi>u</mi></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mn>𝟏</mn><mrow><mrow><munder><mi>min</mi><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow></munder><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><msubsup><mi>a</mi><mrow><mi>π</mi><mo>,</mo><msubsup><mi>w</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mo>′</mo></msubsup></mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup></mrow><mo>≥</mo><mrow><munder><mi>max</mi><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow></munder><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><msubsup><mi>a</mi><mrow><mi>π</mi><mo>,</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>w</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mo>′</mo></msubsup><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup></mrow></mrow></msub></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\frac{1}{|{{\mathcal{W}}}|!}\sum_{\begin{subarray}{c}w^{\prime}_{1},\ldots,w^{\prime}_{m}\\
\mathrm{distinct}\end{subarray}}\sum_{\begin{subarray}{c}\pi\in\mathrm{Perm}({{\mathcal{W}}})\\
\pi(w_{\ell}^{\prime})=w_{\ell},\forall\ell\in[m]\end{subarray}}\left(\int_{\max\limits_{\ell,t}a_{\pi,w^{\prime}_{\ell}-1}^{(t)}}^{\min\limits_{\ell,t}a_{\pi,w^{\prime}_{\ell}}^{(t)}}J(u,\eta(w^{\prime}_{1}),\ldots,\eta(w^{\prime}_{m}))\,{\mathrm{d}}u\right){\bf 1}_{\min\limits_{\ell,t}a_{\pi,w^{\prime}_{\ell}}^{(t)}\geq\max\limits_{\ell,t}a_{\pi,w^{\prime}_{\ell}-1}^{(t)}}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(112)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
<div id="A3.SS5.SSS0.Px1.p2" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A3.SS5.SSS0.Px1.p2.1" class="ltx_p">Our first step is to rewrite this expression by introducing a random permutation <math id="A3.SS5.SSS0.Px1.p2.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\pi" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>π</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\pi</annotation></semantics></math>. The sum over permutations can then be expressed as an expectation:</p>
<table id="A3.EGx78" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A3.Ex186"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A3.Ex186.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\EB_{\pi}\left[\sum_{\begin{subarray}{c}w^{\prime}_{1},\ldots,w^{\prime}_{m}\\
\text{distinct}\end{subarray}}{\bf 1}_{\pi(w^{\prime}_{\ell})=w_{\ell},\forall\ell\in[m]}\int_{\max\limits_{\ell,t}a_{\pi,w^{\prime}_{\ell}-1}^{(t)}}^{\min\limits_{\ell,t}a_{\pi,w^{\prime}_{\ell}}^{(t)}}J(u,\eta(w^{\prime}_{1}),\ldots,\eta(w^{\prime}_{m}))\,{\mathrm{d}}u\cdot{\bf 1}_{\min\limits_{\ell,t}a_{\pi,w^{\prime}_{\ell}}^{(t)}\geq\max\limits_{\ell,t}a_{\pi,w^{\prime}_{\ell}-1}^{(t)}}\right]." display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>𝔼</mi><mi>π</mi></msub><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>[</mo><mrow><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munder><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mtable rowspacing="0pt"><mtr><mtd><mrow><msubsup><mi>w</mi><mn>1</mn><mo>′</mo></msubsup><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi><mo>,</mo><msubsup><mi>w</mi><mi>m</mi><mo>′</mo></msubsup></mrow></mtd></mtr><mtr><mtd><mtext>distinct</mtext></mtd></mtr></mtable></munder></mstyle><mrow><msub><mn>𝟏</mn><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>π</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msubsup><mi>w</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mo>′</mo></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><msub><mi>w</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi></msub></mrow><mo>,</mo><mrow><mrow><mo rspace="0.167em">∀</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi></mrow><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mi>m</mi><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><msubsup><mo>∫</mo><mrow><munder><mi>max</mi><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow></munder><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><msubsup><mi>a</mi><mrow><mi>π</mi><mo>,</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>w</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mo>′</mo></msubsup><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup></mrow><mrow><munder><mi>min</mi><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow></munder><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><msubsup><mi>a</mi><mrow><mi>π</mi><mo>,</mo><msubsup><mi>w</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mo>′</mo></msubsup></mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup></mrow></msubsup></mstyle><mrow><mrow><mi>J</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>u</mi><mo>,</mo><mrow><mi>η</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msubsup><mi>w</mi><mn>1</mn><mo>′</mo></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi><mo>,</mo><mrow><mi>η</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msubsup><mi>w</mi><mi>m</mi><mo>′</mo></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0.170em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>du</mi></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><msub><mn>𝟏</mn><mrow><mrow><munder><mi>min</mi><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow></munder><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><msubsup><mi>a</mi><mrow><mi>π</mi><mo>,</mo><msubsup><mi>w</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mo>′</mo></msubsup></mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup></mrow><mo>≥</mo><mrow><munder><mi>max</mi><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow></munder><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><msubsup><mi>a</mi><mrow><mi>π</mi><mo>,</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>w</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mo>′</mo></msubsup><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup></mrow></mrow></msub></mrow><mo>]</mo></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\EB_{\pi}\left[\sum_{\begin{subarray}{c}w^{\prime}_{1},\ldots,w^{\prime}_{m}\\
\text{distinct}\end{subarray}}{\bf 1}_{\pi(w^{\prime}_{\ell})=w_{\ell},\forall\ell\in[m]}\int_{\max\limits_{\ell,t}a_{\pi,w^{\prime}_{\ell}-1}^{(t)}}^{\min\limits_{\ell,t}a_{\pi,w^{\prime}_{\ell}}^{(t)}}J(u,\eta(w^{\prime}_{1}),\ldots,\eta(w^{\prime}_{m}))\,{\mathrm{d}}u\cdot{\bf 1}_{\min\limits_{\ell,t}a_{\pi,w^{\prime}_{\ell}}^{(t)}\geq\max\limits_{\ell,t}a_{\pi,w^{\prime}_{\ell}-1}^{(t)}}\right].</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A3.SS5.SSS0.Px1.p2.2" class="ltx_p">By linearity of expectation, we can exchange the expectation and the outer summation over the source tokens <math id="A3.SS5.SSS0.Px1.p2.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="w^{\prime}_{1},\ldots,w^{\prime}_{m}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msubsup><mi>w</mi><mn>1</mn><mo>′</mo></msubsup><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi><mo>,</mo><msubsup><mi>w</mi><mi>m</mi><mo>′</mo></msubsup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">w^{\prime}_{1},\ldots,w^{\prime}_{m}</annotation></semantics></math>:</p>
<table id="A3.EGx79" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A3.E113"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A3.E113.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\sum_{\begin{subarray}{c}w^{\prime}_{1},\ldots,w^{\prime}_{m}\\
\text{distinct}\end{subarray}}\EB_{\pi}\left[{\bf 1}_{\pi(w^{\prime}_{\ell})=w_{\ell},\forall\ell\in[m]}\int_{\max\limits_{\ell,t}a_{\pi,w^{\prime}_{\ell}-1}^{(t)}}^{\min\limits_{\ell,t}a_{\pi,w^{\prime}_{\ell}}^{(t)}}J(u,\eta(w^{\prime}_{1}),\ldots,\eta(w^{\prime}_{m}))\,{\mathrm{d}}u\cdot{\bf 1}_{\min\limits_{\ell,t}a_{\pi,w^{\prime}_{\ell}}^{(t)}\geq\max\limits_{\ell,t}a_{\pi,w^{\prime}_{\ell}-1}^{(t)}}\right]." display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munder><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mtable rowspacing="0pt"><mtr><mtd><mrow><msubsup><mi>w</mi><mn>1</mn><mo>′</mo></msubsup><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi><mo>,</mo><msubsup><mi>w</mi><mi>m</mi><mo>′</mo></msubsup></mrow></mtd></mtr><mtr><mtd><mtext>distinct</mtext></mtd></mtr></mtable></munder></mstyle><mrow><msub><mi>𝔼</mi><mi>π</mi></msub><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>[</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mn>𝟏</mn><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>π</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msubsup><mi>w</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mo>′</mo></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><msub><mi>w</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi></msub></mrow><mo>,</mo><mrow><mrow><mo rspace="0.167em">∀</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi></mrow><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mi>m</mi><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><msubsup><mo>∫</mo><mrow><munder><mi>max</mi><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow></munder><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><msubsup><mi>a</mi><mrow><mi>π</mi><mo>,</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>w</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mo>′</mo></msubsup><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup></mrow><mrow><munder><mi>min</mi><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow></munder><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><msubsup><mi>a</mi><mrow><mi>π</mi><mo>,</mo><msubsup><mi>w</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mo>′</mo></msubsup></mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup></mrow></msubsup></mstyle><mrow><mrow><mi>J</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>u</mi><mo>,</mo><mrow><mi>η</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msubsup><mi>w</mi><mn>1</mn><mo>′</mo></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi><mo>,</mo><mrow><mi>η</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msubsup><mi>w</mi><mi>m</mi><mo>′</mo></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0.170em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>du</mi></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><msub><mn>𝟏</mn><mrow><mrow><munder><mi>min</mi><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow></munder><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><msubsup><mi>a</mi><mrow><mi>π</mi><mo>,</mo><msubsup><mi>w</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mo>′</mo></msubsup></mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup></mrow><mo>≥</mo><mrow><munder><mi>max</mi><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow></munder><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><msubsup><mi>a</mi><mrow><mi>π</mi><mo>,</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>w</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mo>′</mo></msubsup><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup></mrow></mrow></msub></mrow><mo>]</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\sum_{\begin{subarray}{c}w^{\prime}_{1},\ldots,w^{\prime}_{m}\\
\text{distinct}\end{subarray}}\EB_{\pi}\left[{\bf 1}_{\pi(w^{\prime}_{\ell})=w_{\ell},\forall\ell\in[m]}\int_{\max\limits_{\ell,t}a_{\pi,w^{\prime}_{\ell}-1}^{(t)}}^{\min\limits_{\ell,t}a_{\pi,w^{\prime}_{\ell}}^{(t)}}J(u,\eta(w^{\prime}_{1}),\ldots,\eta(w^{\prime}_{m}))\,{\mathrm{d}}u\cdot{\bf 1}_{\min\limits_{\ell,t}a_{\pi,w^{\prime}_{\ell}}^{(t)}\geq\max\limits_{\ell,t}a_{\pi,w^{\prime}_{\ell}-1}^{(t)}}\right].</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(113)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A3.SS5.SSS0.Px1.p2.3" class="ltx_p">For any fixed set of distinct source tokens <math id="A3.SS5.SSS0.Px1.p2.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\{w^{\prime}_{\ell}\}_{\ell=1}^{m}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msubsup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><msubsup><mi>w</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mo>′</mo></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>m</mi></msubsup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\{w^{\prime}_{\ell}\}_{\ell=1}^{m}</annotation></semantics></math> and distinct target tokens <math id="A3.SS5.SSS0.Px1.p2.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\{w_{\ell}\}_{\ell=1}^{m}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msubsup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><msub><mi>w</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>m</mi></msubsup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\{w_{\ell}\}_{\ell=1}^{m}</annotation></semantics></math>, let</p>
<table id="A3.Ex187" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A3.Ex187.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="C=\{\pi(w^{\prime}_{\ell})=w_{\ell},\forall\ell\in[m]\}" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>C</mi><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mi>π</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msubsup><mi>w</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mo>′</mo></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>=</mo><msub><mi>w</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><mo rspace="0.167em">∀</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mi>m</mi><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">C=\{\pi(w^{\prime}_{\ell})=w_{\ell},\forall\ell\in[m]\}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A3.SS5.SSS0.Px1.p2.4" class="ltx_p">denote the event that <math id="A3.SS5.SSS0.Px1.p2.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\pi" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>π</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\pi</annotation></semantics></math> maps <math id="A3.SS5.SSS0.Px1.p2.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="w^{\prime}_{\ell}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msubsup><mi>w</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mo>′</mo></msubsup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">w^{\prime}_{\ell}</annotation></semantics></math> to <math id="A3.SS5.SSS0.Px1.p2.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="w_{\ell}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>w</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">w_{\ell}</annotation></semantics></math> for each <math id="A3.SS5.SSS0.Px1.p2.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\ell\in[m]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mi>m</mi><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\ell\in[m]</annotation></semantics></math>. This event corresponds to a specific set of permutations, and its total count is <math id="A3.SS5.SSS0.Px1.p2.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(|{{\mathcal{W}}}|-m)!" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒲</mi><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow><mo>−</mo><mi>m</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>!</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(|{{\mathcal{W}}}|-m)!</annotation></semantics></math>. By the law of total expectation, we can write</p>
<table id="A3.Ex188" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A3.Ex188.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\EB[X\cdot{\bf 1}_{C}]=\EB[X\mid C]\cdot{\mathbb{P}}(C),\quad\text{where}\quad{\mathbb{P}}(C)=\frac{(|{{\mathcal{W}}}|-m)!}{|{{\mathcal{W}}}|!}" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>𝔼</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><mi>X</mi><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><msub><mn>𝟏</mn><mi>C</mi></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>𝔼</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><mi>X</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.167em">∣</mo><mi>C</mi></mrow><mo rspace="0.055em" stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><mrow><mi>ℙ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>C</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="1.167em">,</mo><mtext>where</mtext><mspace style="width:1em;" width="1em"></mspace><mrow><mrow><mi>ℙ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>C</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒲</mi><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow><mo>−</mo><mi>m</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>!</mo></mrow><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒲</mi><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow><mo>!</mo></mrow></mfrac></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\EB[X\cdot{\bf 1}_{C}]=\EB[X\mid C]\cdot{\mathbb{P}}(C),\quad\text{where}\quad{\mathbb{P}}(C)=\frac{(|{{\mathcal{W}}}|-m)!}{|{{\mathcal{W}}}|!}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A3.SS5.SSS0.Px1.p2.5" class="ltx_p">for any random variable <math id="A3.SS5.SSS0.Px1.p2.m10" class="ltx_Math" alttext="X" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>X</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">X</annotation></semantics></math>.
Substituting this into (<a href="#A3.E113" title="In Numerator. ‣ C.5 Proof of Theorem ‣ Appendix C Proof for Inverse Transform Watermarks in Section ‣ Optimal Detection for Language Watermarks with Pseudorandom Collision" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">113</span></a>), we obtain the following simplified form:</p>
<table id="A3.E114" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A3.E114.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\begin{split}\frac{1}{\prod_{\ell=0}^{m-1}(|{{\mathcal{W}}}|-\ell)}&amp;\sum_{\begin{subarray}{c}w^{\prime}_{1},\ldots,w^{\prime}_{m}\\
\mathrm{distinct}\end{subarray}}\EB_{\pi}\Bigg[\left(\int_{\max\limits_{\ell,t}a^{(t)}_{\pi,w^{\prime}_{\ell}-1}\Delta_{t}}^{\min\limits_{\ell,t}a_{\pi,w^{\prime}_{\ell}}^{(t)}}J\left(u,\eta(w^{\prime}_{1}),\ldots,\eta(w^{\prime}_{m})\right)\,{\mathrm{d}}u\right)\\
&amp;\qquad\qquad\qquad\cdot{\bf 1}_{\min\limits_{\ell,t}a_{\pi,w^{\prime}_{\ell}}^{(t)}\geq\max\limits_{\ell,t}a^{(t)}_{\pi,w^{\prime}_{\ell}-1}}\,\Bigg|\,\forall\ell,\ \pi(w^{\prime}_{\ell})=w_{\ell}\Bigg].\end{split}" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mtable columnspacing="0pt" displaystyle="true" rowspacing="0pt"><mtr><mtd class="ltx_align_right" columnalign="right"><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mrow><msubsup><mo>∏</mo><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><mrow><mi>m</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msubsup><mrow><mo lspace="0em" stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒲</mi><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow><mo>−</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mfrac></mtd><mtd class="ltx_align_left" columnalign="left"><mrow><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><msub><mrow></mrow><mtable rowspacing="0pt"><mtr><mtd><mrow><msubsup><mi>w</mi><mn>1</mn><mo>′</mo></msubsup><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi><mo>,</mo><msubsup><mi>w</mi><mi>m</mi><mo>′</mo></msubsup></mrow></mtd></mtr><mtr><mtd><mi>distinct</mi></mtd></mtr></mtable></msub><mi>𝔼</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>π</mi></msub><mo maxsize="2.600em" minsize="2.600em">[</mo><mo>(</mo><mo lspace="0em">∫</mo><msub><mrow></mrow><mrow><mrow><munder><mi>max</mi><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow></munder><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><msubsup><mi>a</mi><mrow><mi>π</mi><mo>,</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>w</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mo>′</mo></msubsup><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mi>t</mi></msub></mrow></msub><msup><mrow></mrow><mrow><munder><mi>min</mi><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow></munder><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><msubsup><mi>a</mi><mrow><mi>π</mi><mo>,</mo><msubsup><mi>w</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mo>′</mo></msubsup></mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup></mrow></msup><mi>J</mi><mo>(</mo><mi>u</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>η</mi><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>w</mi><msup><mrow></mrow><mo>′</mo></msup><msub><mrow></mrow><mn>1</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>η</mi><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>w</mi><msup><mrow></mrow><mo>′</mo></msup><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>m</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo><mo rspace="0.340em">)</mo><mi>du</mi><mo>)</mo></mrow></mtd></mtr><mtr><mtd></mtd><mtd class="ltx_align_left" columnalign="left"><mrow><mo rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><mn>𝟏</mn><msub><mrow></mrow><mrow><mrow><munder><mi>min</mi><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow></munder><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><msubsup><mi>a</mi><mrow><mi>π</mi><mo>,</mo><msubsup><mi>w</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mo>′</mo></msubsup></mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup></mrow><mo>≥</mo><mrow><munder><mi>max</mi><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow></munder><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><msubsup><mi>a</mi><mrow><mi>π</mi><mo>,</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>w</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mo>′</mo></msubsup><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup></mrow></mrow></msub><mo fence="false" lspace="0.170em" maxsize="2.600em" minsize="2.600em" rspace="0.507em" stretchy="true">|</mo><mo rspace="0.167em">∀</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mo rspace="1.167em">,</mo><mi>π</mi><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>w</mi><msup><mrow></mrow><mo>′</mo></msup><msub><mrow></mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo><mo>=</mo><mi>w</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi></msub><mo maxsize="2.600em" minsize="2.600em">]</mo><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow></mtd></mtr></mtable><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\begin{split}\frac{1}{\prod_{\ell=0}^{m-1}(|{{\mathcal{W}}}|-\ell)}&amp;\sum_{\begin{subarray}{c}w^{\prime}_{1},\ldots,w^{\prime}_{m}\\
\mathrm{distinct}\end{subarray}}\EB_{\pi}\Bigg[\left(\int_{\max\limits_{\ell,t}a^{(t)}_{\pi,w^{\prime}_{\ell}-1}\Delta_{t}}^{\min\limits_{\ell,t}a_{\pi,w^{\prime}_{\ell}}^{(t)}}J\left(u,\eta(w^{\prime}_{1}),\ldots,\eta(w^{\prime}_{m})\right)\,{\mathrm{d}}u\right)\\
&amp;\qquad\qquad\qquad\cdot{\bf 1}_{\min\limits_{\ell,t}a_{\pi,w^{\prime}_{\ell}}^{(t)}\geq\max\limits_{\ell,t}a^{(t)}_{\pi,w^{\prime}_{\ell}-1}}\,\Bigg|\,\forall\ell,\ \pi(w^{\prime}_{\ell})=w_{\ell}\Bigg].\end{split}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(114)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
<div id="A3.SS5.SSS0.Px1.p3" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A3.SS5.SSS0.Px1.p3.1" class="ltx_p">Next, we simplify the integration limits, <math id="A3.SS5.SSS0.Px1.p3.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\max\limits_{\ell,t}a_{\pi,w^{\prime}\ell-1}^{(t)}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><munder><mi>max</mi><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow></munder><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><msubsup><mi>a</mi><mrow><mi>π</mi><mo>,</mo><mrow><mrow><msup><mi>w</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi></mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\max\limits_{\ell,t}a_{\pi,w^{\prime}\ell-1}^{(t)}</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="A3.SS5.SSS0.Px1.p3.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\min\limits_{\ell,t}a_{\pi,w^{\prime}\ell}^{(t)}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><munder><mi>min</mi><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow></munder><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><msubsup><mi>a</mi><mrow><mi>π</mi><mo>,</mo><mrow><msup><mi>w</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi></mrow></mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\min\limits_{\ell,t}a_{\pi,w^{\prime}\ell}^{(t)}</annotation></semantics></math>, by applying concentration inequalities under the conditional distribution <math id="A3.SS5.SSS0.Px1.p3.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\pi\mid C" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>π</mi><mo fence="false">|</mo><mi>C</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\pi\mid C</annotation></semantics></math>.
In particular, applying Lemma <a href="#A3.Thmlem8" title="Lemma C.8. ‣ C.10 Auxiliary Lemmas ‣ Appendix C Proof for Inverse Transform Watermarks in Section ‣ Optimal Detection for Language Watermarks with Pseudorandom Collision" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">C.8</span></a> to the maximum function, we obtain</p>
<table id="A3.EGx80" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A3.E115"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A3.E115.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\left|\max_{\begin{subarray}{c}\ell\in[m]\\
t\in{\mathcal{I}}^{Y}_{\ell}\end{subarray}}a_{\pi,w^{\prime}_{\ell}-1}^{(t)}-\max_{\begin{subarray}{c}\ell\in[m]\\
t\in{\mathcal{I}}^{Y}_{\ell}\end{subarray}}\frac{(w^{\prime}_{\ell}-1)\Delta_{t}}{|{{\mathcal{W}}}|-1}\right|\leq\max_{\begin{subarray}{c}\ell\in[m]\\
t\in{\mathcal{I}}^{Y}_{\ell}\end{subarray}}\left|a_{\pi,w^{\prime}_{\ell}-1}^{(t)}-\frac{(w^{\prime}_{\ell}-1)\Delta_{t}}{|{{\mathcal{W}}}|-1}\right|." display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mo>|</mo><mrow><mrow><munder><mi>max</mi><mtable rowspacing="0pt"><mtr><mtd><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mi>m</mi><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow></mtd></mtr><mtr><mtd><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>∈</mo><msubsup><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℐ</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mi>Y</mi></msubsup></mrow></mtd></mtr></mtable></munder><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><msubsup><mi>a</mi><mrow><mi>π</mi><mo>,</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>w</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mo>′</mo></msubsup><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><munder><mi>max</mi><mtable rowspacing="0pt"><mtr><mtd><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mi>m</mi><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow></mtd></mtr><mtr><mtd><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>∈</mo><msubsup><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℐ</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mi>Y</mi></msubsup></mrow></mtd></mtr></mtable></munder><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>w</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mo>′</mo></msubsup><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mi>t</mi></msub></mrow><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒲</mi><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mfrac></mstyle></mrow></mrow><mo>|</mo></mrow><mo>≤</mo><mrow><munder><mi>max</mi><mtable rowspacing="0pt"><mtr><mtd><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mi>m</mi><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow></mtd></mtr><mtr><mtd><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>∈</mo><msubsup><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℐ</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mi>Y</mi></msubsup></mrow></mtd></mtr></mtable></munder><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>|</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>a</mi><mrow><mi>π</mi><mo>,</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>w</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mo>′</mo></msubsup><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup><mo>−</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>w</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mo>′</mo></msubsup><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mi>t</mi></msub></mrow><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒲</mi><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mfrac></mstyle></mrow><mo>|</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\left|\max_{\begin{subarray}{c}\ell\in[m]\\
t\in{\mathcal{I}}^{Y}_{\ell}\end{subarray}}a_{\pi,w^{\prime}_{\ell}-1}^{(t)}-\max_{\begin{subarray}{c}\ell\in[m]\\
t\in{\mathcal{I}}^{Y}_{\ell}\end{subarray}}\frac{(w^{\prime}_{\ell}-1)\Delta_{t}}{|{{\mathcal{W}}}|-1}\right|\leq\max_{\begin{subarray}{c}\ell\in[m]\\
t\in{\mathcal{I}}^{Y}_{\ell}\end{subarray}}\left|a_{\pi,w^{\prime}_{\ell}-1}^{(t)}-\frac{(w^{\prime}_{\ell}-1)\Delta_{t}}{|{{\mathcal{W}}}|-1}\right|.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(115)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A3.SS5.SSS0.Px1.p3.2" class="ltx_p">Using Lemma <a href="#A3.Thmlem3" title="Lemma C.3 (Concentration of max_{ℓ,𝑡}{𝑎_{𝜋,𝑤^′_ℓ-1}^(𝑡)}). ‣ Numerator. ‣ C.5 Proof of Theorem ‣ Appendix C Proof for Inverse Transform Watermarks in Section ‣ Optimal Detection for Language Watermarks with Pseudorandom Collision" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">C.3</span></a> below, we bound the right-hand side of (<a href="#A3.E115" title="In Numerator. ‣ C.5 Proof of Theorem ‣ Appendix C Proof for Inverse Transform Watermarks in Section ‣ Optimal Detection for Language Watermarks with Pseudorandom Collision" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">115</span></a>) by <math id="A3.SS5.SSS0.Px1.p3.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="O\left(\frac{1}{|{{\mathcal{W}}}|}+\sqrt{{\varepsilon}_{|{{\mathcal{W}}}|}\log|{{\mathcal{W}}}|}\right)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>O</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒲</mi><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow></mfrac><mo>+</mo><msqrt><mrow><msub><mi>ε</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒲</mi><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒲</mi><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></msqrt></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">O\left(\frac{1}{|{{\mathcal{W}}}|}+\sqrt{{\varepsilon}_{|{{\mathcal{W}}}|}\log|{{\mathcal{W}}}|}\right)</annotation></semantics></math>, which vanishes as <math id="A3.SS5.SSS0.Px1.p3.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="|{{\mathcal{W}}}|\to\infty" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒲</mi><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">∞</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">|{{\mathcal{W}}}|\to\infty</annotation></semantics></math>. The proof of Lemma <a href="#A3.Thmlem3" title="Lemma C.3 (Concentration of max_{ℓ,𝑡}{𝑎_{𝜋,𝑤^′_ℓ-1}^(𝑡)}). ‣ Numerator. ‣ C.5 Proof of Theorem ‣ Appendix C Proof for Inverse Transform Watermarks in Section ‣ Optimal Detection for Language Watermarks with Pseudorandom Collision" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">C.3</span></a> can be found in Section <a href="#A3.SS6" title="C.6 Proof of Lemma ‣ Appendix C Proof for Inverse Transform Watermarks in Section ‣ Optimal Detection for Language Watermarks with Pseudorandom Collision" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">C.6</span></a>.</p>
</div>
<div id="A3.Thmlem3" class="ltx_theorem ltx_theorem_lem">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_title_theorem"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_theorem"><span id="A3.Thmlem3.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Lemma C.3</span></span><span id="A3.Thmlem3.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold"> </span>(Concentration of <math id="A3.Thmlem3.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\max\limits_{\ell,t}a_{\pi,w^{\prime}_{\ell}-1}^{(t)}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><munder><mi>max</mi><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow></munder><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><msubsup><mi>a</mi><mrow><mi>π</mi><mo>,</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>w</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mo>′</mo></msubsup><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\max\limits_{\ell,t}a_{\pi,w^{\prime}_{\ell}-1}^{(t)}</annotation></semantics></math>)<span id="A3.Thmlem3.4" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">.</span></h6>
<div id="A3.Thmlem3.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A3.Thmlem3.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A3.Thmlem3.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">Under Assumption <a href="#S5.Thmasmp1" title="Assumption 5.1 (Asymptotic NTP conditions). ‣ 5.1 Asymptotic Distributions ‣ 5 Application to the Inverse Transform Watermark ‣ Optimal Detection for Language Watermarks with Pseudorandom Collision" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">5.1</span></a>, let <math id="A3.Thmlem3.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\pi" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>π</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\pi</annotation></semantics></math> be a uniformly random permutation over <math id="A3.Thmlem3.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="{{\mathcal{W}}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒲</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{{\mathcal{W}}}</annotation></semantics></math>. Then, for any distinct source tokens <math id="A3.Thmlem3.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\{w^{\prime}_{\ell}\}_{\ell=1}^{m}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msubsup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><msubsup><mi>w</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mo>′</mo></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>m</mi></msubsup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\{w^{\prime}_{\ell}\}_{\ell=1}^{m}</annotation></semantics></math> and target tokens <math id="A3.Thmlem3.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\{w_{\ell}\}_{\ell=1}^{m}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msubsup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><msub><mi>w</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>m</mi></msubsup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\{w_{\ell}\}_{\ell=1}^{m}</annotation></semantics></math>, we have</span></p>
<table id="A3.EGx81" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A3.Ex189"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A3.Ex189.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\max_{\begin{subarray}{c}w^{\prime}_{1},\ldots,w^{\prime}_{m}\\
\mathrm{distinct}\end{subarray}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><munder><mi>max</mi><mtable rowspacing="0pt"><mtr><mtd><mrow><msubsup><mi>w</mi><mn>1</mn><mo>′</mo></msubsup><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi><mo>,</mo><msubsup><mi>w</mi><mi>m</mi><mo>′</mo></msubsup></mrow></mtd></mtr><mtr><mtd><mi>distinct</mi></mtd></mtr></mtable></munder><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\max_{\begin{subarray}{c}w^{\prime}_{1},\ldots,w^{\prime}_{m}\\
\mathrm{distinct}\end{subarray}}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A3.Ex189.m2" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\displaystyle\EB_{\pi}\left[\max_{\begin{subarray}{c}\ell\in[m]\\
t\in{\mathcal{I}}^{Y}_{\ell}\end{subarray}}\left|a_{\pi,w^{\prime}_{\ell}-1}^{(t)}-\frac{(w^{\prime}_{\ell}-1)\Delta_{t}}{|{{\mathcal{W}}}|-1}\right|\Bigg|\forall\ell\in[m],\pi(w^{\prime}_{\ell})=w_{\ell}\right]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>𝔼</mi><mi>π</mi></msub><mrow><mo>[</mo><munder><mi>max</mi><mtable rowspacing="0pt"><mtr><mtd><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mi>m</mi><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow></mtd></mtr><mtr><mtd><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>∈</mo><msubsup><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℐ</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mi>Y</mi></msubsup></mrow></mtd></mtr></mtable></munder><mo fence="false" rspace="0.167em">|</mo><msubsup><mi>a</mi><mrow><mi>π</mi><mo>,</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>w</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mo>′</mo></msubsup><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup><mo>−</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>w</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mo>′</mo></msubsup><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mi>t</mi></msub></mrow><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒲</mi><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mfrac></mstyle><mo fence="false" rspace="0.167em">|</mo><mo fence="false" maxsize="2.600em" minsize="2.600em" rspace="0.167em" stretchy="true">|</mo><mo rspace="0.167em">∀</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mi>m</mi><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow><mo>,</mo><mi>π</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msubsup><mi>w</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mo>′</mo></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>=</mo><msub><mi>w</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi></msub><mo>]</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\EB_{\pi}\left[\max_{\begin{subarray}{c}\ell\in[m]\\
t\in{\mathcal{I}}^{Y}_{\ell}\end{subarray}}\left|a_{\pi,w^{\prime}_{\ell}-1}^{(t)}-\frac{(w^{\prime}_{\ell}-1)\Delta_{t}}{|{{\mathcal{W}}}|-1}\right|\Bigg|\forall\ell\in[m],\pi(w^{\prime}_{\ell})=w_{\ell}\right]</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A3.E116"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A3.E116.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\leq O(m)\cdot\max_{\begin{subarray}{c}\ell\in[m]\\
t\in{\mathcal{I}}^{Y}_{\ell}\end{subarray}}\left(\frac{1}{|{{\mathcal{W}}}|}+\sqrt{P_{t,(2)}\log|{{\mathcal{W}}}|}+P_{t,(2)}\log|{{\mathcal{W}}}|\right)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>≤</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>O</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>m</mi><mo rspace="0.055em" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><mrow><munder><mi>max</mi><mtable rowspacing="0pt"><mtr><mtd><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mi>m</mi><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow></mtd></mtr><mtr><mtd><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>∈</mo><msubsup><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℐ</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mi>Y</mi></msubsup></mrow></mtd></mtr></mtable></munder><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒲</mi><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow></mfrac></mstyle><mo>+</mo><msqrt><mrow><msub><mi>P</mi><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>,</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>2</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒲</mi><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></msqrt><mo>+</mo><mrow><msub><mi>P</mi><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>,</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>2</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒲</mi><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\leq O(m)\cdot\max_{\begin{subarray}{c}\ell\in[m]\\
t\in{\mathcal{I}}^{Y}_{\ell}\end{subarray}}\left(\frac{1}{|{{\mathcal{W}}}|}+\sqrt{P_{t,(2)}\log|{{\mathcal{W}}}|}+P_{t,(2)}\log|{{\mathcal{W}}}|\right)</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(116)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A3.Thmlem3.p1.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="A3.Thmlem3.p1.2.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">where <math id="A3.Thmlem3.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\Delta_{t}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Delta_{t}</annotation></semantics></math> is the regularity level for <math id="A3.Thmlem3.p1.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\bm{P}_{t}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>𝐏</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\bm{P}_{t}</annotation></semantics></math>, and <math id="A3.Thmlem3.p1.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="O(\cdot)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>O</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">⋅</mo><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">O(\cdot)</annotation></semantics></math> hides universal constants.</span></p>
</div>
</div>
<div id="A3.SS5.SSS0.Px1.p4" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A3.SS5.SSS0.Px1.p4.1" class="ltx_p">Note that</p>
<table id="A3.Ex190" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A3.Ex190.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="a_{\pi,\,w_{\ell}^{\prime}}^{(t)}=\sum_{j=1}^{w_{\ell}^{\prime}}P_{t,\pi(j)}=1-\Delta_{t}+\sum_{j=1}^{w_{\ell}^{\prime}-1}P_{t,\pi(j)}=1-\Delta_{t}+a_{\pi,\,w_{\ell}^{\prime}-1}^{(t)}." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msubsup><mi>a</mi><mrow><mi>π</mi><mo rspace="0.337em">,</mo><msubsup><mi>w</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mo>′</mo></msubsup></mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup><mo rspace="0.111em">=</mo><mrow><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>j</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><msubsup><mi>w</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mo>′</mo></msubsup></munderover><msub><mi>P</mi><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>,</mo><mrow><mi>π</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>j</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></msub></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mi>t</mi></msub></mrow><mo rspace="0.055em">+</mo><mrow><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>j</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mrow><msubsup><mi>w</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mo>′</mo></msubsup><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></munderover><msub><mi>P</mi><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>,</mo><mrow><mi>π</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>j</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></msub></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mi>t</mi></msub></mrow><mo>+</mo><msubsup><mi>a</mi><mrow><mi>π</mi><mo rspace="0.337em">,</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>w</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mo>′</mo></msubsup><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">a_{\pi,\,w_{\ell}^{\prime}}^{(t)}=\sum_{j=1}^{w_{\ell}^{\prime}}P_{t,\pi(j)}=1-\Delta_{t}+\sum_{j=1}^{w_{\ell}^{\prime}-1}P_{t,\pi(j)}=1-\Delta_{t}+a_{\pi,\,w_{\ell}^{\prime}-1}^{(t)}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A3.SS5.SSS0.Px1.p4.2" class="ltx_p">Using this identity, we can approximate the lower integration limit <math id="A3.SS5.SSS0.Px1.p4.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\min\limits_{\ell,t}a_{\pi,w^{\prime}_{\ell}}^{(t)}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><munder><mi>min</mi><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow></munder><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><msubsup><mi>a</mi><mrow><mi>π</mi><mo>,</mo><msubsup><mi>w</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mo>′</mo></msubsup></mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\min\limits_{\ell,t}a_{\pi,w^{\prime}_{\ell}}^{(t)}</annotation></semantics></math> as follows:</p>
<table id="A3.EGx82" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A3.Ex191"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A3.Ex191.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\left|\min_{\begin{subarray}{c}\ell\in[m]\\
t\in{\mathcal{I}}^{Y}_{\ell}\end{subarray}}a_{\pi,w_{\ell}^{\prime}}^{(t)}-\min_{\begin{subarray}{c}\ell\in[m]\\
t\in{\mathcal{I}}^{Y}_{\ell}\end{subarray}}\left[1-\frac{(|{{\mathcal{W}}}|-w_{\ell}^{\prime})\Delta_{t}}{|{{\mathcal{W}}}|-1}\right]\right|" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo>|</mo><mrow><mrow><munder><mi>min</mi><mtable rowspacing="0pt"><mtr><mtd><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mi>m</mi><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow></mtd></mtr><mtr><mtd><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>∈</mo><msubsup><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℐ</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mi>Y</mi></msubsup></mrow></mtd></mtr></mtable></munder><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><msubsup><mi>a</mi><mrow><mi>π</mi><mo>,</mo><msubsup><mi>w</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mo>′</mo></msubsup></mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><munder><mi>min</mi><mtable rowspacing="0pt"><mtr><mtd><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mi>m</mi><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow></mtd></mtr><mtr><mtd><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>∈</mo><msubsup><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℐ</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mi>Y</mi></msubsup></mrow></mtd></mtr></mtable></munder><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>[</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒲</mi><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow><mo>−</mo><msubsup><mi>w</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mo>′</mo></msubsup></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mi>t</mi></msub></mrow><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒲</mi><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mfrac></mstyle></mrow><mo>]</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>|</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\left|\min_{\begin{subarray}{c}\ell\in[m]\\
t\in{\mathcal{I}}^{Y}_{\ell}\end{subarray}}a_{\pi,w_{\ell}^{\prime}}^{(t)}-\min_{\begin{subarray}{c}\ell\in[m]\\
t\in{\mathcal{I}}^{Y}_{\ell}\end{subarray}}\left[1-\frac{(|{{\mathcal{W}}}|-w_{\ell}^{\prime})\Delta_{t}}{|{{\mathcal{W}}}|-1}\right]\right|</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A3.Ex191.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\leq\max_{\begin{subarray}{c}\ell\in[m]\\
t\in{\mathcal{I}}^{Y}_{\ell}\end{subarray}}\left|a_{\pi,w_{\ell}^{\prime}}^{(t)}-\left(1-\frac{(|{{\mathcal{W}}}|-w_{\ell}^{\prime})\Delta_{t}}{|{{\mathcal{W}}}|-1}\right)\right|" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>≤</mo><mrow><munder><mi>max</mi><mtable rowspacing="0pt"><mtr><mtd><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mi>m</mi><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow></mtd></mtr><mtr><mtd><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>∈</mo><msubsup><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℐ</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mi>Y</mi></msubsup></mrow></mtd></mtr></mtable></munder><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>|</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>a</mi><mrow><mi>π</mi><mo>,</mo><msubsup><mi>w</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mo>′</mo></msubsup></mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup><mo>−</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒲</mi><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow><mo>−</mo><msubsup><mi>w</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mo>′</mo></msubsup></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mi>t</mi></msub></mrow><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒲</mi><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mfrac></mstyle></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>|</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\leq\max_{\begin{subarray}{c}\ell\in[m]\\
t\in{\mathcal{I}}^{Y}_{\ell}\end{subarray}}\left|a_{\pi,w_{\ell}^{\prime}}^{(t)}-\left(1-\frac{(|{{\mathcal{W}}}|-w_{\ell}^{\prime})\Delta_{t}}{|{{\mathcal{W}}}|-1}\right)\right|</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A3.E117"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A3.E117.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=\max_{\begin{subarray}{c}\ell\in[m]\\
t\in{\mathcal{I}}^{Y}_{\ell}\end{subarray}}\left|a_{\pi,w^{\prime}_{\ell}-1}^{(t)}-\frac{(w^{\prime}_{\ell}-1)\Delta_{t}}{|{{\mathcal{W}}}|-1}\right|." display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><munder><mi>max</mi><mtable rowspacing="0pt"><mtr><mtd><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mi>m</mi><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow></mtd></mtr><mtr><mtd><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>∈</mo><msubsup><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℐ</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mi>Y</mi></msubsup></mrow></mtd></mtr></mtable></munder><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>|</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>a</mi><mrow><mi>π</mi><mo>,</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>w</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mo>′</mo></msubsup><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup><mo>−</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>w</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mo>′</mo></msubsup><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mi>t</mi></msub></mrow><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒲</mi><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mfrac></mstyle></mrow><mo>|</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=\max_{\begin{subarray}{c}\ell\in[m]\\
t\in{\mathcal{I}}^{Y}_{\ell}\end{subarray}}\left|a_{\pi,w^{\prime}_{\ell}-1}^{(t)}-\frac{(w^{\prime}_{\ell}-1)\Delta_{t}}{|{{\mathcal{W}}}|-1}\right|.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(117)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
<div id="A3.SS5.SSS0.Px1.p5" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A3.SS5.SSS0.Px1.p5.1" class="ltx_p">By using this approximation to the upper and lower integral limits, we assert that quantity (<a href="#A3.E114" title="In Numerator. ‣ C.5 Proof of Theorem ‣ Appendix C Proof for Inverse Transform Watermarks in Section ‣ Optimal Detection for Language Watermarks with Pseudorandom Collision" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">114</span></a>) will be close to the following quantity:</p>
<table id="A3.E118" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A3.E118.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\begin{split}\frac{1}{\prod_{\ell=0}^{m-1}(|{{\mathcal{W}}}|-\ell)}&amp;\sum_{\begin{subarray}{c}w^{\prime}_{1},\ldots,w^{\prime}_{m}\\
\mathrm{distinct}\end{subarray}}\EB_{\pi}\Bigg[\left(\int_{\max\limits_{\ell,t}\frac{w^{\prime}_{\ell}-1}{|{{\mathcal{W}}}|-1}\Delta_{t}}^{\min\limits_{\ell,t}\left[1-\frac{|{{\mathcal{W}}}|-w^{\prime}_{\ell}}{|{{\mathcal{W}}}|-1}\Delta_{t}\right]}J\left(u,\eta(w^{\prime}_{1}),\ldots,\eta(w^{\prime}_{m})\right)\,{\mathrm{d}}u\right)\\
&amp;\qquad\qquad\qquad\cdot{\bf 1}_{\min\limits_{\ell,t}\left[1-\frac{(|{{\mathcal{W}}}|-w^{\prime}_{\ell})\Delta_{t}}{|{{\mathcal{W}}}|-1}\right]\geq\max\limits_{\ell,t}\frac{(w^{\prime}_{\ell}-1)\Delta_{t}}{|{{\mathcal{W}}}|-1}}\,\Bigg|\,\forall\ell,\ \pi(w^{\prime}_{\ell})=w_{\ell}\Bigg]\end{split}" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mtable columnspacing="0pt" displaystyle="true" rowspacing="0pt"><mtr><mtd class="ltx_align_right" columnalign="right"><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mrow><msubsup><mo>∏</mo><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><mrow><mi>m</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msubsup><mrow><mo lspace="0em" stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒲</mi><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow><mo>−</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mfrac></mtd><mtd class="ltx_align_left" columnalign="left"><mrow><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><msub><mrow></mrow><mtable rowspacing="0pt"><mtr><mtd><mrow><msubsup><mi>w</mi><mn>1</mn><mo>′</mo></msubsup><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi><mo>,</mo><msubsup><mi>w</mi><mi>m</mi><mo>′</mo></msubsup></mrow></mtd></mtr><mtr><mtd><mi>distinct</mi></mtd></mtr></mtable></msub><mi>𝔼</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>π</mi></msub><mo maxsize="2.600em" minsize="2.600em">[</mo><mo>(</mo><mo lspace="0em">∫</mo><msub><mrow></mrow><mrow><mrow><munder><mi>max</mi><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow></munder><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><mfrac><mrow><msubsup><mi>w</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mo>′</mo></msubsup><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒲</mi><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mfrac></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mi>t</mi></msub></mrow></msub><msup><mrow></mrow><mrow><munder><mi>min</mi><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow></munder><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>[</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mrow><mfrac><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒲</mi><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow><mo>−</mo><msubsup><mi>w</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mo>′</mo></msubsup></mrow><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒲</mi><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mfrac><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mi>t</mi></msub></mrow></mrow><mo>]</mo></mrow></mrow></msup><mi>J</mi><mo>(</mo><mi>u</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>η</mi><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>w</mi><msup><mrow></mrow><mo>′</mo></msup><msub><mrow></mrow><mn>1</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>η</mi><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>w</mi><msup><mrow></mrow><mo>′</mo></msup><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>m</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo><mo rspace="0.340em">)</mo><mi>du</mi><mo>)</mo></mrow></mtd></mtr><mtr><mtd></mtd><mtd class="ltx_align_left" columnalign="left"><mrow><mo rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><mn>𝟏</mn><msub><mrow></mrow><mrow><mrow><munder><mi>min</mi><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow></munder><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>[</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mfrac><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒲</mi><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow><mo>−</mo><msubsup><mi>w</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mo>′</mo></msubsup></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mi>t</mi></msub></mrow><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒲</mi><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mfrac></mrow><mo>]</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>≥</mo><mrow><munder><mi>max</mi><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow></munder><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><mfrac><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>w</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mo>′</mo></msubsup><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mi>t</mi></msub></mrow><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒲</mi><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mfrac></mrow></mrow></msub><mo fence="false" lspace="0.170em" maxsize="2.600em" minsize="2.600em" rspace="0.507em" stretchy="true">|</mo><mo rspace="0.167em">∀</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mo rspace="1.167em">,</mo><mi>π</mi><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>w</mi><msup><mrow></mrow><mo>′</mo></msup><msub><mrow></mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo><mo>=</mo><mi>w</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi></msub><mo maxsize="2.600em" minsize="2.600em">]</mo></mrow></mtd></mtr></mtable><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\begin{split}\frac{1}{\prod_{\ell=0}^{m-1}(|{{\mathcal{W}}}|-\ell)}&amp;\sum_{\begin{subarray}{c}w^{\prime}_{1},\ldots,w^{\prime}_{m}\\
\mathrm{distinct}\end{subarray}}\EB_{\pi}\Bigg[\left(\int_{\max\limits_{\ell,t}\frac{w^{\prime}_{\ell}-1}{|{{\mathcal{W}}}|-1}\Delta_{t}}^{\min\limits_{\ell,t}\left[1-\frac{|{{\mathcal{W}}}|-w^{\prime}_{\ell}}{|{{\mathcal{W}}}|-1}\Delta_{t}\right]}J\left(u,\eta(w^{\prime}_{1}),\ldots,\eta(w^{\prime}_{m})\right)\,{\mathrm{d}}u\right)\\
&amp;\qquad\qquad\qquad\cdot{\bf 1}_{\min\limits_{\ell,t}\left[1-\frac{(|{{\mathcal{W}}}|-w^{\prime}_{\ell})\Delta_{t}}{|{{\mathcal{W}}}|-1}\right]\geq\max\limits_{\ell,t}\frac{(w^{\prime}_{\ell}-1)\Delta_{t}}{|{{\mathcal{W}}}|-1}}\,\Bigg|\,\forall\ell,\ \pi(w^{\prime}_{\ell})=w_{\ell}\Bigg]\end{split}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(118)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A3.SS5.SSS0.Px1.p5.2" class="ltx_p">This is because</p>
<table id="A3.EGx83" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A3.Ex192"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A3.Ex192.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle|\eqref{eq:numerator-simplified-1}-\eqref{eq:numerator-simplified-1.1}|" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><mrow><mrow><mtext>(</mtext><mtext><a href="#A3.E114" title="In Numerator. ‣ C.5 Proof of Theorem ‣ Appendix C Proof for Inverse Transform Watermarks in Section ‣ Optimal Detection for Language Watermarks with Pseudorandom Collision" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">114</span></a></mtext><mtext>)</mtext></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mtext>(</mtext><mtext><a href="#A3.E118" title="In Numerator. ‣ C.5 Proof of Theorem ‣ Appendix C Proof for Inverse Transform Watermarks in Section ‣ Optimal Detection for Language Watermarks with Pseudorandom Collision" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">118</span></a></mtext><mtext>)</mtext></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle|\eqref{eq:numerator-simplified-1}-\eqref{eq:numerator-simplified-1.1}|</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A3.Ex192.m2" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\displaystyle\overset{(a)}{\leq}4\|J\|_{\infty}\cdot\max_{\begin{subarray}{c}w_{1}^{\prime},\ldots,w_{m}^{\prime}\\
\mathrm{distinct}\end{subarray}}\EB_{\pi}\left[\max_{\begin{subarray}{c}\ell\in[m]\\
t\in{\mathcal{I}}^{Y}_{\ell}\end{subarray}}\left|a_{\pi,w_{\ell}^{\prime}-1}^{(t)}-\frac{(w_{\ell}^{\prime}-1)\Delta_{t}}{|{{\mathcal{W}}}|-1}\right|\Bigg|\pi(w_{\ell}^{\prime})=w_{\ell},\forall\ell\right]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mover accent="true"><mo>≤</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="0.700em" minsize="0.700em">(</mo><mi mathsize="0.700em">a</mi><mo maxsize="0.700em" minsize="0.700em">)</mo></mrow></mover><mn>4</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.167em">∥</mo><mi>J</mi><msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">∥</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">∞</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><munder><mi>max</mi><mtable rowspacing="0pt"><mtr><mtd><mrow><msubsup><mi>w</mi><mn>1</mn><mo>′</mo></msubsup><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi><mo>,</mo><msubsup><mi>w</mi><mi>m</mi><mo>′</mo></msubsup></mrow></mtd></mtr><mtr><mtd><mi>distinct</mi></mtd></mtr></mtable></munder><msub><mi>𝔼</mi><mi>π</mi></msub><mrow><mo>[</mo><munder><mi>max</mi><mtable rowspacing="0pt"><mtr><mtd><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mi>m</mi><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow></mtd></mtr><mtr><mtd><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>∈</mo><msubsup><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℐ</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mi>Y</mi></msubsup></mrow></mtd></mtr></mtable></munder><mo fence="false" rspace="0.167em">|</mo><msubsup><mi>a</mi><mrow><mi>π</mi><mo>,</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>w</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mo>′</mo></msubsup><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup><mo>−</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>w</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mo>′</mo></msubsup><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mi>t</mi></msub></mrow><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒲</mi><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mfrac></mstyle><mo fence="false" rspace="0.167em">|</mo><mo fence="false" maxsize="2.600em" minsize="2.600em" rspace="0.167em" stretchy="true">|</mo><mi>π</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msubsup><mi>w</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mo>′</mo></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>=</mo><msub><mi>w</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><mo rspace="0.167em">∀</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mo>]</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\overset{(a)}{\leq}4\|J\|_{\infty}\cdot\max_{\begin{subarray}{c}w_{1}^{\prime},\ldots,w_{m}^{\prime}\\
\mathrm{distinct}\end{subarray}}\EB_{\pi}\left[\max_{\begin{subarray}{c}\ell\in[m]\\
t\in{\mathcal{I}}^{Y}_{\ell}\end{subarray}}\left|a_{\pi,w_{\ell}^{\prime}-1}^{(t)}-\frac{(w_{\ell}^{\prime}-1)\Delta_{t}}{|{{\mathcal{W}}}|-1}\right|\Bigg|\pi(w_{\ell}^{\prime})=w_{\ell},\forall\ell\right]</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A3.E119"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A3.E119.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\overset{(b)}{\leq}O(m)\cdot\|J\|_{\infty}\cdot\max_{\begin{subarray}{c}\ell\in[m]\\
t\in{\mathcal{I}}^{Y}_{\ell}\end{subarray}}\left(\frac{1}{|{{\mathcal{W}}}|}+\sqrt{P_{t,(2)}\log|{{\mathcal{W}}}|}+P_{t,(2)}\log|{{\mathcal{W}}}|\right)," display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mover accent="true"><mo>≤</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="0.700em" minsize="0.700em">(</mo><mi mathsize="0.700em">b</mi><mo maxsize="0.700em" minsize="0.700em">)</mo></mrow></mover><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>O</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>m</mi><mo rspace="0.055em" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mi>J</mi><mo rspace="0.055em" stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">∞</mi></msub><mo rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><mrow><munder><mi>max</mi><mtable rowspacing="0pt"><mtr><mtd><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mi>m</mi><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow></mtd></mtr><mtr><mtd><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>∈</mo><msubsup><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℐ</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mi>Y</mi></msubsup></mrow></mtd></mtr></mtable></munder><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒲</mi><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow></mfrac></mstyle><mo>+</mo><msqrt><mrow><msub><mi>P</mi><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>,</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>2</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒲</mi><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></msqrt><mo>+</mo><mrow><msub><mi>P</mi><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>,</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>2</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒲</mi><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\overset{(b)}{\leq}O(m)\cdot\|J\|_{\infty}\cdot\max_{\begin{subarray}{c}\ell\in[m]\\
t\in{\mathcal{I}}^{Y}_{\ell}\end{subarray}}\left(\frac{1}{|{{\mathcal{W}}}|}+\sqrt{P_{t,(2)}\log|{{\mathcal{W}}}|}+P_{t,(2)}\log|{{\mathcal{W}}}|\right),</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(119)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A3.SS5.SSS0.Px1.p5.3" class="ltx_p">where <math id="A3.SS5.SSS0.Px1.p5.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(a)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>a</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(a)</annotation></semantics></math> follows from Lemma <a href="#A3.Thmlem10" title="Lemma C.10 (Integral approximation error). ‣ C.10 Auxiliary Lemmas ‣ Appendix C Proof for Inverse Transform Watermarks in Section ‣ Optimal Detection for Language Watermarks with Pseudorandom Collision" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">C.10</span></a>, with <math id="A3.SS5.SSS0.Px1.p5.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\|J\|_{\infty}:=\sup_{\bm{x}\in[0,1]^{m+1}}|J(\bm{x})|" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mi>J</mi><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">∞</mi></msub><mo rspace="0.1389em">:=</mo><mrow><msub><mo lspace="0.1389em" rspace="0em">sup</mo><mrow><mi>𝒙</mi><mo>∈</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow><mrow><mi>m</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup></mrow></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><mrow><mi>J</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝒙</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\|J\|_{\infty}:=\sup_{\bm{x}\in[0,1]^{m+1}}|J(\bm{x})|</annotation></semantics></math> denoting the supremum norm of <math id="A3.SS5.SSS0.Px1.p5.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="J" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>J</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">J</annotation></semantics></math> over <math id="A3.SS5.SSS0.Px1.p5.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="[0,1]^{m+1}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow><mrow><mi>m</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">[0,1]^{m+1}</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="A3.SS5.SSS0.Px1.p5.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(b)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>b</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(b)</annotation></semantics></math> follows from Lemma <a href="#A3.Thmlem3" title="Lemma C.3 (Concentration of max_{ℓ,𝑡}{𝑎_{𝜋,𝑤^′_ℓ-1}^(𝑡)}). ‣ Numerator. ‣ C.5 Proof of Theorem ‣ Appendix C Proof for Inverse Transform Watermarks in Section ‣ Optimal Detection for Language Watermarks with Pseudorandom Collision" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">C.3</span></a>, where <math id="A3.SS5.SSS0.Px1.p5.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="O(1)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>O</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>1</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">O(1)</annotation></semantics></math> denotes a universal constant.</p>
</div>
<div id="A3.SS5.SSS0.Px1.p6" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A3.SS5.SSS0.Px1.p6.1" class="ltx_p">Therefore, it suffices to analyze the expression in (<a href="#A3.E118" title="In Numerator. ‣ C.5 Proof of Theorem ‣ Appendix C Proof for Inverse Transform Watermarks in Section ‣ Optimal Detection for Language Watermarks with Pseudorandom Collision" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">118</span></a>).
Once the upper and lower integration limits are approximated, the entire integrand becomes independent of <math id="A3.SS5.SSS0.Px1.p6.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\pi" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>π</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\pi</annotation></semantics></math>, allowing us to safely remove the expectation over <math id="A3.SS5.SSS0.Px1.p6.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\pi" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>π</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\pi</annotation></semantics></math>.
To study the resulting deterministic quantity, we define the function</p>
<table id="A3.EGx84" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A3.Ex193"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A3.Ex193.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\Phi(x_{1},\ldots,x_{m})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Φ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>m</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\Phi(x_{1},\ldots,x_{m})</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A3.Ex193.m2" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\displaystyle=\left(\int_{\max\limits_{\ell,t}\Delta_{t}x_{\ell}}^{\min\limits_{\ell,t}[1-\Delta_{t}+\Delta_{t}x_{\ell}]}J(u,x_{1},\ldots,x_{m}){\mathrm{d}}u\right){\bf 1}_{\left\{\min\limits_{\ell,t}\{1-\Delta_{t}+\Delta_{t}x_{\ell}\}\geq\max\limits_{\ell,t}\Delta_{t}x_{\ell}\right\}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><msubsup><mo>∫</mo><mrow><mrow><munder><mi>max</mi><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow></munder><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mi>t</mi></msub></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi></msub></mrow><mrow><munder><mi>min</mi><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow></munder><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mi>t</mi></msub></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi></msub></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow></msubsup></mstyle><mi>J</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>u</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>m</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mi>d</mi><mi>u</mi><mo>)</mo></mrow><msub><mn>𝟏</mn><mrow><mo>{</mo><mi>min</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>t</mi></msub><mo>+</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>t</mi></msub><mi>x</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">}</mo><mo>≥</mo><mi>max</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow></msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>t</mi></msub><mi>x</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi></msub><mo>}</mo></mrow></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=\left(\int_{\max\limits_{\ell,t}\Delta_{t}x_{\ell}}^{\min\limits_{\ell,t}[1-\Delta_{t}+\Delta_{t}x_{\ell}]}J(u,x_{1},\ldots,x_{m}){\mathrm{d}}u\right){\bf 1}_{\left\{\min\limits_{\ell,t}\{1-\Delta_{t}+\Delta_{t}x_{\ell}\}\geq\max\limits_{\ell,t}\Delta_{t}x_{\ell}\right\}}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A3.Ex194"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A3.Ex194.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\displaystyle=\left(\int_{\max\limits_{\ell\in[m]}{\bar{\Delta}}_{\ell}x_{\ell}}^{\min\limits_{\ell\in[m]}[1-{\bar{\Delta}}_{\ell}+{\bar{\Delta}}_{\ell}x_{\ell}]}J(u,x_{1},\ldots,x_{m}){\mathrm{d}}u\right){\bf 1}_{\left\{\min\limits_{\ell\in[m]}[1-{\bar{\Delta}}_{\ell}+{\bar{\Delta}}_{\ell}x_{\ell}]\geq\max\limits_{\ell\in[m]}{\bar{\Delta}}_{\ell}x_{\ell}\right\}}," display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><msubsup><mo>∫</mo><mrow><mrow><munder><mi>max</mi><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mi>m</mi><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow></munder><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo>¯</mo></mover><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi></msub></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi></msub></mrow><mrow><munder><mi>min</mi><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mi>m</mi><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow></munder><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo>¯</mo></mover><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi></msub></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><msub><mover accent="true"><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo>¯</mo></mover><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi></msub></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow></msubsup></mstyle><mi>J</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>u</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>m</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mi>d</mi><mi>u</mi><mo>)</mo></mrow><msub><mn>𝟏</mn><mrow><mo>{</mo><mi>min</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mi>m</mi><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mover accent="true"><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo>¯</mo></mover><msub><mrow></mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi></msub><mo>+</mo><mover accent="true"><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo>¯</mo></mover><msub><mrow></mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi></msub><mi>x</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">]</mo><mo>≥</mo><mi>max</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mi>m</mi><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow></msub><mover accent="true"><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo>¯</mo></mover><msub><mrow></mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi></msub><mi>x</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi></msub><mo>}</mo></mrow></msub><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=\left(\int_{\max\limits_{\ell\in[m]}{\bar{\Delta}}_{\ell}x_{\ell}}^{\min\limits_{\ell\in[m]}[1-{\bar{\Delta}}_{\ell}+{\bar{\Delta}}_{\ell}x_{\ell}]}J(u,x_{1},\ldots,x_{m}){\mathrm{d}}u\right){\bf 1}_{\left\{\min\limits_{\ell\in[m]}[1-{\bar{\Delta}}_{\ell}+{\bar{\Delta}}_{\ell}x_{\ell}]\geq\max\limits_{\ell\in[m]}{\bar{\Delta}}_{\ell}x_{\ell}\right\}},</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A3.SS5.SSS0.Px1.p6.2" class="ltx_p">where <math id="A3.SS5.SSS0.Px1.p6.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="{\bar{\Delta}}_{\ell}:=\max_{t\in{\mathcal{I}}^{Y}_{\ell}}\Delta_{t}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mover accent="true"><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo>¯</mo></mover><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi></msub><mo>:=</mo><mrow><msub><mi>max</mi><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>∈</mo><msubsup><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℐ</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mi>Y</mi></msubsup></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mi>t</mi></msub></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\bar{\Delta}}_{\ell}:=\max_{t\in{\mathcal{I}}^{Y}_{\ell}}\Delta_{t}</annotation></semantics></math> denotes the maximum regularity level associated with sub-block <math id="A3.SS5.SSS0.Px1.p6.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="{\mathcal{I}}^{Y}_{\ell}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msubsup><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℐ</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mi>Y</mi></msubsup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\mathcal{I}}^{Y}_{\ell}</annotation></semantics></math>.
It is straightforward to verify that <math id="A3.SS5.SSS0.Px1.p6.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\Phi" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi mathvariant="normal">Φ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Phi</annotation></semantics></math> is Lipschitz continuous with respect to the <math id="A3.SS5.SSS0.Px1.p6.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="L^{\infty}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi>L</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">∞</mi></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">L^{\infty}</annotation></semantics></math> norm on <math id="A3.SS5.SSS0.Px1.p6.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="[0,1]^{m}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow><mi>m</mi></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">[0,1]^{m}</annotation></semantics></math>, owing to the Lipschitz continuity of <math id="A3.SS5.SSS0.Px1.p6.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="J" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>J</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">J</annotation></semantics></math> and the boundedness of the variables <math id="A3.SS5.SSS0.Px1.p6.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\{{\bar{\Delta}}_{\ell},x_{\ell}\}_{\ell=1}^{m}\subseteq[0,1]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msubsup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo>¯</mo></mover><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>m</mi></msubsup><mo>⊆</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\{{\bar{\Delta}}_{\ell},x_{\ell}\}_{\ell=1}^{m}\subseteq[0,1]</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>
</div>
<div id="A3.SS5.SSS0.Px1.p7" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A3.SS5.SSS0.Px1.p7.1" class="ltx_p">With this definition, we can rewrite (<a href="#A3.E118" title="In Numerator. ‣ C.5 Proof of Theorem ‣ Appendix C Proof for Inverse Transform Watermarks in Section ‣ Optimal Detection for Language Watermarks with Pseudorandom Collision" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">118</span></a>) as</p>
<table id="A3.EGx85" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A3.Ex195"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><span id="A3.Ex195.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_markedasmath">(<a href="#A3.E118" title="In Numerator. ‣ C.5 Proof of Theorem ‣ Appendix C Proof for Inverse Transform Watermarks in Section ‣ Optimal Detection for Language Watermarks with Pseudorandom Collision" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">118</span></a>)</span></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A3.Ex195.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=\frac{1}{\prod_{i=0}^{m-1}(|{{\mathcal{W}}}|-i)}\sum_{\begin{subarray}{c}w_{1}^{\prime},\ldots,w_{m}^{\prime}\\
\mathrm{distinct}\end{subarray}}\Phi(\eta(w_{1}^{\prime}),\ldots,\eta(w_{m}^{\prime}))" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mrow><msubsup><mo>∏</mo><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><mrow><mi>m</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msubsup><mrow><mo lspace="0em" stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒲</mi><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow><mo>−</mo><mi>i</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mfrac></mstyle><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munder><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mtable rowspacing="0pt"><mtr><mtd><mrow><msubsup><mi>w</mi><mn>1</mn><mo>′</mo></msubsup><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi><mo>,</mo><msubsup><mi>w</mi><mi>m</mi><mo>′</mo></msubsup></mrow></mtd></mtr><mtr><mtd><mi>distinct</mi></mtd></mtr></mtable></munder></mstyle><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Φ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>η</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msubsup><mi>w</mi><mn>1</mn><mo>′</mo></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi><mo>,</mo><mrow><mi>η</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msubsup><mi>w</mi><mi>m</mi><mo>′</mo></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=\frac{1}{\prod_{i=0}^{m-1}(|{{\mathcal{W}}}|-i)}\sum_{\begin{subarray}{c}w_{1}^{\prime},\ldots,w_{m}^{\prime}\\
\mathrm{distinct}\end{subarray}}\Phi(\eta(w_{1}^{\prime}),\ldots,\eta(w_{m}^{\prime}))</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A3.Ex196"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A3.Ex196.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\overset{(a)}{=}\frac{1}{|{{\mathcal{W}}}|^{m}}\sum_{\begin{subarray}{c}w_{1}^{\prime},\ldots,w_{m}^{\prime}\end{subarray}}\Phi(\eta(w_{1}^{\prime}),\ldots,\eta(w_{m}^{\prime}))+O\left(\frac{\|J\|_{\infty}}{|{{\mathcal{W}}}|}\right)," display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mover accent="true"><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="0.700em" minsize="0.700em">(</mo><mi mathsize="0.700em">a</mi><mo maxsize="0.700em" minsize="0.700em">)</mo></mrow></mover><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mn>1</mn><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒲</mi><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow><mi>m</mi></msup></mfrac></mstyle><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munder><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mtable><mtr><mtd><mrow><msubsup><mi>w</mi><mn>1</mn><mo>′</mo></msubsup><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi><mo>,</mo><msubsup><mi>w</mi><mi>m</mi><mo>′</mo></msubsup></mrow></mtd></mtr></mtable></munder></mstyle><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Φ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>η</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msubsup><mi>w</mi><mn>1</mn><mo>′</mo></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi><mo>,</mo><mrow><mi>η</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msubsup><mi>w</mi><mi>m</mi><mo>′</mo></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mi>O</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mi>J</mi><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">∞</mi></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒲</mi><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow></mfrac></mstyle><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\overset{(a)}{=}\frac{1}{|{{\mathcal{W}}}|^{m}}\sum_{\begin{subarray}{c}w_{1}^{\prime},\ldots,w_{m}^{\prime}\end{subarray}}\Phi(\eta(w_{1}^{\prime}),\ldots,\eta(w_{m}^{\prime}))+O\left(\frac{\|J\|_{\infty}}{|{{\mathcal{W}}}|}\right),</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A3.E120"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A3.E120.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\displaystyle\overset{(b)}{=}\int_{[0,1]^{m}}\Phi(x_{1},\ldots,x_{m}){\mathrm{d}}x_{1}\cdots{\mathrm{d}}x_{m}+O\left(\frac{1}{|{{\mathcal{W}}}|}\right)+O\left(\frac{\|J\|_{\infty}}{|{{\mathcal{W}}}|}\right)," display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mover accent="true"><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="0.700em" minsize="0.700em">(</mo><mi mathsize="0.700em">b</mi><mo maxsize="0.700em" minsize="0.700em">)</mo></mrow></mover><mstyle displaystyle="true"><msub><mo>∫</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow><mi>m</mi></msup></msub></mstyle><mi mathvariant="normal">Φ</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>m</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mi>d</mi><msub><mi>x</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">⋯</mo><mi>d</mi><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>m</mi></msub><mo>+</mo><mi>O</mi><mrow><mo>(</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒲</mi><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow></mfrac></mstyle><mo>)</mo></mrow><mo>+</mo><mi>O</mi><mrow><mo>(</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mi>J</mi><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">∞</mi></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒲</mi><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow></mfrac></mstyle><mo>)</mo></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\overset{(b)}{=}\int_{[0,1]^{m}}\Phi(x_{1},\ldots,x_{m}){\mathrm{d}}x_{1}\cdots{\mathrm{d}}x_{m}+O\left(\frac{1}{|{{\mathcal{W}}}|}\right)+O\left(\frac{\|J\|_{\infty}}{|{{\mathcal{W}}}|}\right),</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(120)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A3.SS5.SSS0.Px1.p7.2" class="ltx_p">where</p>
<ul id="A3.I1" class="ltx_itemize">
<li id="A3.I1.ix1" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">(a)</span> 
<div id="A3.I1.ix1.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A3.I1.ix1.p1.1" class="ltx_p">follows from the expansion <math id="A3.I1.ix1.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\prod_{i=0}^{m-1}(|{{\mathcal{W}}}|-i)=|{{\mathcal{W}}}|^{m}\left[1+O\left(\frac{m^{2}}{|{{\mathcal{W}}}|}\right)\right]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msubsup><mo>∏</mo><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><mrow><mi>m</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msubsup><mrow><mo lspace="0em" stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒲</mi><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow><mo>−</mo><mi>i</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒲</mi><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow><mi>m</mi></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>[</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>+</mo><mrow><mi>O</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mfrac><msup><mi>m</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒲</mi><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow></mfrac><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>]</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\prod_{i=0}^{m-1}(|{{\mathcal{W}}}|-i)=|{{\mathcal{W}}}|^{m}\left[1+O\left(\frac{m^{2}}{|{{\mathcal{W}}}|}\right)\right]</annotation></semantics></math> and the observation that the number of non-fully-distinct <math id="A3.I1.ix1.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="m" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>m</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">m</annotation></semantics></math>-tuples <math id="A3.I1.ix1.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(\eta(w_{1}^{\prime}),\ldots,\eta(w_{m}^{\prime}))" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>η</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msubsup><mi>w</mi><mn>1</mn><mo>′</mo></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi><mo>,</mo><mrow><mi>η</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msubsup><mi>w</mi><mi>m</mi><mo>′</mo></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(\eta(w_{1}^{\prime}),\ldots,\eta(w_{m}^{\prime}))</annotation></semantics></math> is at most <math id="A3.I1.ix1.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="O(m^{2}|{{\mathcal{W}}}|^{m-1})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>O</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msup><mi>m</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒲</mi><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow><mrow><mi>m</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">O(m^{2}|{{\mathcal{W}}}|^{m-1})</annotation></semantics></math>, with each summand bounded in magnitude by <math id="A3.I1.ix1.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\|J\|_{\infty}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mi>J</mi><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">∞</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\|J\|_{\infty}</annotation></semantics></math>;</p>
</div></li>
<li id="A3.I1.ix2" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">(b)</span> 
<div id="A3.I1.ix2.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A3.I1.ix2.p1.1" class="ltx_p">follows from approximating the Riemann sum over the uniform grid <math id="A3.I1.ix2.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\{\eta(w^{\prime})=(w^{\prime}-1)/(|{{\mathcal{W}}}|-1):w^{\prime}\in{{\mathcal{W}}}\}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>η</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>w</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msup><mi>w</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>/</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒲</mi><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo rspace="0.278em" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mrow><msup><mi>w</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo>∈</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒲</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\{\eta(w^{\prime})=(w^{\prime}-1)/(|{{\mathcal{W}}}|-1):w^{\prime}\in{{\mathcal{W}}}\}</annotation></semantics></math> of mesh size <math id="A3.I1.ix2.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="1/(|{{\mathcal{W}}}|-1)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>/</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒲</mi><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">1/(|{{\mathcal{W}}}|-1)</annotation></semantics></math>, which discretizes <math id="A3.I1.ix2.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="[0,1]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>1</mn><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">[0,1]</annotation></semantics></math> evenly. Since <math id="A3.I1.ix2.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\Phi" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi mathvariant="normal">Φ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Phi</annotation></semantics></math> is Lipschitz, the resulting Riemann sum converges to the Lebesgue integral with error <math id="A3.I1.ix2.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="O(1/|{{\mathcal{W}}}|)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>O</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>/</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒲</mi><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">O(1/|{{\mathcal{W}}}|)</annotation></semantics></math> per coordinate, yielding a total approximation error of <math id="A3.I1.ix2.p1.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="O(1/|{{\mathcal{W}}}|)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>O</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>/</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒲</mi><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">O(1/|{{\mathcal{W}}}|)</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>
</div></li>
</ul>
</div>
<div id="A3.SS5.SSS0.Px1.p8" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A3.SS5.SSS0.Px1.p8.1" class="ltx_p">Combining the results above, we conclude that</p>
<table id="A3.EGx86" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A3.Ex197"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A3.Ex197.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\displaystyle\text{Numerator of}~\eqref{eq:target-expectation-0}=\eqref{eq:numerator-simplified-1}\overset{\eqref{eq:integral-approximation-error1}}{=}\eqref{eq:numerator-simplified-1.1}+o(1)\overset{\eqref{eq:integral-approximation-error2}}{=}\int_{[0,1]^{m}}\Phi(x_{1},\ldots,x_{m})\,{\mathrm{d}}x_{1}\cdots{\mathrm{d}}x_{m}+o(1)," display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mtext>Numerator of</mtext><mrow><mtext>(</mtext><mtext><a href="#A3.E111" title="In Proof of Theorem . ‣ C.5 Proof of Theorem ‣ Appendix C Proof for Inverse Transform Watermarks in Section ‣ Optimal Detection for Language Watermarks with Pseudorandom Collision" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">111</span></a></mtext><mtext>)</mtext></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mtext>(</mtext><mtext><a href="#A3.E114" title="In Numerator. ‣ C.5 Proof of Theorem ‣ Appendix C Proof for Inverse Transform Watermarks in Section ‣ Optimal Detection for Language Watermarks with Pseudorandom Collision" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">114</span></a></mtext><mtext>)</mtext></mrow><mover accent="true"><mo>=</mo><mrow><mtext mathsize="0.700em">(</mtext><mtext mathsize="0.700em"><a href="#A3.E119" title="In Numerator. ‣ C.5 Proof of Theorem ‣ Appendix C Proof for Inverse Transform Watermarks in Section ‣ Optimal Detection for Language Watermarks with Pseudorandom Collision" class="ltx_ref" style="font-size:70%;"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">119</span></a></mtext><mtext mathsize="0.700em">)</mtext></mrow></mover><mrow><mtext>(</mtext><mtext><a href="#A3.E118" title="In Numerator. ‣ C.5 Proof of Theorem ‣ Appendix C Proof for Inverse Transform Watermarks in Section ‣ Optimal Detection for Language Watermarks with Pseudorandom Collision" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">118</span></a></mtext><mtext>)</mtext></mrow><mo>+</mo><mi>o</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>1</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mover accent="true"><mo>=</mo><mrow><mtext mathsize="0.700em">(</mtext><mtext mathsize="0.700em"><a href="#A3.E120" title="In Numerator. ‣ C.5 Proof of Theorem ‣ Appendix C Proof for Inverse Transform Watermarks in Section ‣ Optimal Detection for Language Watermarks with Pseudorandom Collision" class="ltx_ref" style="font-size:70%;"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">120</span></a></mtext><mtext mathsize="0.700em">)</mtext></mrow></mover><mstyle displaystyle="true"><msub><mo>∫</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow><mi>m</mi></msup></msub></mstyle><mi mathvariant="normal">Φ</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>m</mi></msub><mo rspace="0.170em" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mi>d</mi><msub><mi>x</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">⋯</mo><mi>d</mi><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>m</mi></msub><mo>+</mo><mi>o</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>1</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\text{Numerator of}~\eqref{eq:target-expectation-0}=\eqref{eq:numerator-simplified-1}\overset{\eqref{eq:integral-approximation-error1}}{=}\eqref{eq:numerator-simplified-1.1}+o(1)\overset{\eqref{eq:integral-approximation-error2}}{=}\int_{[0,1]^{m}}\Phi(x_{1},\ldots,x_{m})\,{\mathrm{d}}x_{1}\cdots{\mathrm{d}}x_{m}+o(1),</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A3.Ex198"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A3.Ex198.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\displaystyle=\int_{[0,1]^{m}}\int_{\max\limits_{\ell\in[m]}{\bar{\Delta}}_{\ell}x_{\ell}}^{\min\limits_{\ell\in[m]}[1-{\bar{\Delta}}_{\ell}+{\bar{\Delta}}_{\ell}x_{\ell}]}J(u,x_{1},\ldots,x_{m}){\bf 1}_{\left\{\min\limits_{\ell\in[m]}[1-{\bar{\Delta}}_{\ell}+{\bar{\Delta}}_{\ell}x_{\ell}]\geq\max\limits_{\ell\in[m]}{\bar{\Delta}}_{\ell}x_{\ell}\right\}}{\mathrm{d}}u{\mathrm{d}}x_{1}\cdots{\mathrm{d}}x_{m}+o(1)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo>=</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><msub><mo>∫</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow><mi>m</mi></msup></msub></mstyle><mstyle displaystyle="true"><msubsup><mo>∫</mo><mrow><mrow><munder><mi>max</mi><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mi>m</mi><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow></munder><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo>¯</mo></mover><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi></msub></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi></msub></mrow><mrow><munder><mi>min</mi><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mi>m</mi><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow></munder><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo>¯</mo></mover><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi></msub></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><msub><mover accent="true"><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo>¯</mo></mover><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi></msub></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow></msubsup></mstyle><mi>J</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>u</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>m</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><msub><mn>𝟏</mn><mrow><mo>{</mo><mi>min</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mi>m</mi><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mover accent="true"><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo>¯</mo></mover><msub><mrow></mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi></msub><mo>+</mo><mover accent="true"><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo>¯</mo></mover><msub><mrow></mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi></msub><mi>x</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">]</mo><mo>≥</mo><mi>max</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mi>m</mi><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow></msub><mover accent="true"><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo>¯</mo></mover><msub><mrow></mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi></msub><mi>x</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi></msub><mo>}</mo></mrow></msub><mi>d</mi><mi>u</mi><mi>d</mi><msub><mi>x</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">⋯</mo><mi>d</mi><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>m</mi></msub><mo>+</mo><mi>o</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>1</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=\int_{[0,1]^{m}}\int_{\max\limits_{\ell\in[m]}{\bar{\Delta}}_{\ell}x_{\ell}}^{\min\limits_{\ell\in[m]}[1-{\bar{\Delta}}_{\ell}+{\bar{\Delta}}_{\ell}x_{\ell}]}J(u,x_{1},\ldots,x_{m}){\bf 1}_{\left\{\min\limits_{\ell\in[m]}[1-{\bar{\Delta}}_{\ell}+{\bar{\Delta}}_{\ell}x_{\ell}]\geq\max\limits_{\ell\in[m]}{\bar{\Delta}}_{\ell}x_{\ell}\right\}}{\mathrm{d}}u{\mathrm{d}}x_{1}\cdots{\mathrm{d}}x_{m}+o(1)</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A3.E121"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A3.E121.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=\int_{[0,1]^{m}}\left(\int_{{\mathcal{I}}(\bm{x},\bar{\bm{\Delta}})}J(u,\bm{x})\,{\mathrm{d}}u\right){\bf 1}_{{\mathcal{I}}(\bm{x},\bar{\bm{\Delta}})\neq\emptyset}{\mathrm{d}}\bm{x}+o(1)," display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><msub><mo>∫</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow><mi>m</mi></msup></msub></mstyle><mrow><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><msub><mo>∫</mo><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℐ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝒙</mi><mo>,</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>𝚫</mi><mo>¯</mo></mover><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></msub></mstyle><mrow><mrow><mi>J</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>u</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>𝒙</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0.170em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo rspace="0em">𝑑</mo><mi>u</mi></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mn>𝟏</mn><mrow><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℐ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝒙</mi><mo>,</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>𝚫</mi><mo>¯</mo></mover><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>≠</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">∅</mi></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo rspace="0em">𝑑</mo><mi>𝒙</mi></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mi>o</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>1</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=\int_{[0,1]^{m}}\left(\int_{{\mathcal{I}}(\bm{x},\bar{\bm{\Delta}})}J(u,\bm{x})\,{\mathrm{d}}u\right){\bf 1}_{{\mathcal{I}}(\bm{x},\bar{\bm{\Delta}})\neq\emptyset}{\mathrm{d}}\bm{x}+o(1),</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(121)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A3.SS5.SSS0.Px1.p8.2" class="ltx_p">where the <math id="A3.SS5.SSS0.Px1.p8.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="o(1)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>o</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>1</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">o(1)</annotation></semantics></math> term vanishes uniformly as <math id="A3.SS5.SSS0.Px1.p8.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="|{{\mathcal{W}}}|\to\infty" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒲</mi><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">∞</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">|{{\mathcal{W}}}|\to\infty</annotation></semantics></math>, over all 1-Lipschitz functions <math id="A3.SS5.SSS0.Px1.p8.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="J" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>J</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">J</annotation></semantics></math>, all <math id="A3.SS5.SSS0.Px1.p8.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\bm{{\bar{\Delta}}}\in[\Delta,1-\delta]^{m}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mover accent="true"><mi>𝚫</mi><mo>¯</mo></mover><mo>∈</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo>,</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mi>δ</mi></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow><mi>m</mi></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\bm{{\bar{\Delta}}}\in[\Delta,1-\delta]^{m}</annotation></semantics></math>, and all <math id="A3.SS5.SSS0.Px1.p8.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\bm{P}_{{\mathcal{I}}^{\zeta}}\in{\mathcal{Q}}_{\tau,\bm{\Delta}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>𝑷</mi><msup><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℐ</mi><mi>ζ</mi></msup></msub><mo>∈</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒬</mi><mrow><mi>τ</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>𝚫</mi></mrow></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\bm{P}_{{\mathcal{I}}^{\zeta}}\in{\mathcal{Q}}_{\tau,\bm{\Delta}}</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>
</div>
</section>
<section id="A3.SS5.SSS0.Px2" class="ltx_paragraph">
<h5 class="ltx_title ltx_title_paragraph">Denominator.</h5>

<div id="A3.SS5.SSS0.Px2.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A3.SS5.SSS0.Px2.p1.1" class="ltx_p">We now turn to the denominator of (<a href="#A3.E111" title="In Proof of Theorem . ‣ C.5 Proof of Theorem ‣ Appendix C Proof for Inverse Transform Watermarks in Section ‣ Optimal Detection for Language Watermarks with Pseudorandom Collision" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">111</span></a>). Since it corresponds to the numerator with the constant function <math id="A3.SS5.SSS0.Px2.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="J\equiv 1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>J</mi><mo>≡</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">J\equiv 1</annotation></semantics></math>, we set <math id="A3.SS5.SSS0.Px2.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="J(u,x_{1},\ldots,x_{m}):=1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>J</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>u</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>m</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>:=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">J(u,x_{1},\ldots,x_{m}):=1</annotation></semantics></math> and obtain</p>
<table id="A3.EGx87" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A3.Ex199"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><span id="A3.Ex199.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_markedasmath">Denominator of</span> <span id="A3.Ex199.1.2" class="ltx_text ltx_markedasmath">(<a href="#A3.E111" title="In Proof of Theorem . ‣ C.5 Proof of Theorem ‣ Appendix C Proof for Inverse Transform Watermarks in Section ‣ Optimal Detection for Language Watermarks with Pseudorandom Collision" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">111</span></a>)</span></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A3.Ex199.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=\frac{1}{|{{\mathcal{W}}}|!}\sum_{\begin{subarray}{c}w_{1}^{\prime},\ldots,w_{m}^{\prime}\\
\mathrm{distinct}\end{subarray}}\sum_{\begin{subarray}{c}\pi\in\mathrm{Perm}({{\mathcal{W}}})\\
\pi(w_{\ell}^{\prime})=w_{\ell}\;\forall\ell\in[m]\end{subarray}}{\mathbb{P}}\left(U\in\bigcap_{\ell\in[m]}\bigcap_{t\in{\mathcal{I}}^{Y}_{\ell}}(a_{\pi,w_{\ell}^{\prime}-1}^{(t)},a_{\pi,w_{\ell}^{\prime}}^{(t)})\right)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒲</mi><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow><mo>!</mo></mrow></mfrac></mstyle><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munder><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mtable rowspacing="0pt"><mtr><mtd><mrow><msubsup><mi>w</mi><mn>1</mn><mo>′</mo></msubsup><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi><mo>,</mo><msubsup><mi>w</mi><mi>m</mi><mo>′</mo></msubsup></mrow></mtd></mtr><mtr><mtd><mi>distinct</mi></mtd></mtr></mtable></munder></mstyle><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munder><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mtable rowspacing="0pt"><mtr><mtd><mrow><mi>π</mi><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mi>Perm</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒲</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mtd></mtr><mtr><mtd><mrow><mrow><mi>π</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msubsup><mi>w</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mo>′</mo></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><msub><mi>w</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi></msub><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo rspace="0.167em">∀</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi></mrow></mrow><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mi>m</mi><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow></mtd></mtr></mtable></munder></mstyle><mrow><mi>ℙ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mi>U</mi><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munder><mo movablelimits="false">⋂</mo><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mi>m</mi><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow></munder></mstyle><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munder><mo movablelimits="false">⋂</mo><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>∈</mo><msubsup><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℐ</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mi>Y</mi></msubsup></mrow></munder></mstyle><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msubsup><mi>a</mi><mrow><mi>π</mi><mo>,</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>w</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mo>′</mo></msubsup><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup><mo>,</mo><msubsup><mi>a</mi><mrow><mi>π</mi><mo>,</mo><msubsup><mi>w</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mo>′</mo></msubsup></mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=\frac{1}{|{{\mathcal{W}}}|!}\sum_{\begin{subarray}{c}w_{1}^{\prime},\ldots,w_{m}^{\prime}\\
\mathrm{distinct}\end{subarray}}\sum_{\begin{subarray}{c}\pi\in\mathrm{Perm}({{\mathcal{W}}})\\
\pi(w_{\ell}^{\prime})=w_{\ell}\;\forall\ell\in[m]\end{subarray}}{\mathbb{P}}\left(U\in\bigcap_{\ell\in[m]}\bigcap_{t\in{\mathcal{I}}^{Y}_{\ell}}(a_{\pi,w_{\ell}^{\prime}-1}^{(t)},a_{\pi,w_{\ell}^{\prime}}^{(t)})\right)</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A3.Ex200"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A3.Ex200.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=\int_{[0,1]^{m}}|{\mathcal{I}}(\bm{x},\bar{\bm{\Delta}})|\cdot{\bf 1}_{{\mathcal{I}}(\bm{x},\bar{\bm{\Delta}})\neq\emptyset}\,{\mathrm{d}}\bm{x}+o(1)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mrow><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><msub><mo>∫</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow><mi>m</mi></msup></msub></mstyle><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℐ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝒙</mi><mo>,</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>𝚫</mi><mo>¯</mo></mover><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.055em" stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><msub><mn>𝟏</mn><mrow><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℐ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝒙</mi><mo>,</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>𝚫</mi><mo>¯</mo></mover><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>≠</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">∅</mi></mrow></msub></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo rspace="0em">𝑑</mo><mi>𝒙</mi></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mi>o</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>1</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=\int_{[0,1]^{m}}|{\mathcal{I}}(\bm{x},\bar{\bm{\Delta}})|\cdot{\bf 1}_{{\mathcal{I}}(\bm{x},\bar{\bm{\Delta}})\neq\emptyset}\,{\mathrm{d}}\bm{x}+o(1)</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A3.E122"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A3.E122.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=I_{m}(\bar{\bm{\Delta}})+o(1)," display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>I</mi><mi>m</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>𝚫</mi><mo>¯</mo></mover><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mi>o</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>1</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=I_{m}(\bar{\bm{\Delta}})+o(1),</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(122)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A3.SS5.SSS0.Px2.p1.2" class="ltx_p">uniformly over all 1-Lipschitz functions <math id="A3.SS5.SSS0.Px2.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="J" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>J</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">J</annotation></semantics></math>, all parameter vectors <math id="A3.SS5.SSS0.Px2.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\bm{{\bar{\Delta}}}\in[\Delta,1-\delta]^{m}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mover accent="true"><mi>𝚫</mi><mo>¯</mo></mover><mo>∈</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo>,</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mi>δ</mi></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow><mi>m</mi></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\bm{{\bar{\Delta}}}\in[\Delta,1-\delta]^{m}</annotation></semantics></math>, and all distributions <math id="A3.SS5.SSS0.Px2.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\bm{P}_{{\mathcal{I}}^{\zeta}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>𝑷</mi><msup><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℐ</mi><mi>ζ</mi></msup></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\bm{P}_{{\mathcal{I}}^{\zeta}}</annotation></semantics></math> in the class <math id="A3.SS5.SSS0.Px2.p1.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="{\mathcal{Q}}_{\tau,\bm{\Delta}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒬</mi><mrow><mi>τ</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>𝚫</mi></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\mathcal{Q}}_{\tau,\bm{\Delta}}</annotation></semantics></math> defined in (<a href="#A3.E86" title="In Definition C.1 (Fixed-parameter belief class). ‣ Belief classes. ‣ Appendix C Proof for Inverse Transform Watermarks in Section ‣ Optimal Detection for Language Watermarks with Pseudorandom Collision" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">86</span></a>).</p>
</div>
<div id="A3.SS5.SSS0.Px2.p2" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A3.SS5.SSS0.Px2.p2.1" class="ltx_p">Finally, combining (<a href="#A3.E121" title="In Numerator. ‣ C.5 Proof of Theorem ‣ Appendix C Proof for Inverse Transform Watermarks in Section ‣ Optimal Detection for Language Watermarks with Pseudorandom Collision" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">121</span></a>) and (<a href="#A3.E122" title="In Denominator. ‣ C.5 Proof of Theorem ‣ Appendix C Proof for Inverse Transform Watermarks in Section ‣ Optimal Detection for Language Watermarks with Pseudorandom Collision" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">122</span></a>) yields the desired result.</p>
</div>
<div id="A3.SS5.SSS0.Px2.p3" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A3.SS5.SSS0.Px2.p3.1" class="ltx_p">∎</p>
</div>
</section>
</section>
<section id="A3.SS6" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection">C.6 </span>Proof of Lemma <a href="#A3.Thmlem3" title="Lemma C.3 (Concentration of max_{ℓ,𝑡}{𝑎_{𝜋,𝑤^′_ℓ-1}^(𝑡)}). ‣ Numerator. ‣ C.5 Proof of Theorem ‣ Appendix C Proof for Inverse Transform Watermarks in Section ‣ Optimal Detection for Language Watermarks with Pseudorandom Collision" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">C.3</span></a></h3>

<div id="A3.SS6.2" class="ltx_proof">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_font_italic ltx_title_proof">Proof of Lemma <a href="#A3.Thmlem3" title="Lemma C.3 (Concentration of max_{ℓ,𝑡}{𝑎_{𝜋,𝑤^′_ℓ-1}^(𝑡)}). ‣ Numerator. ‣ C.5 Proof of Theorem ‣ Appendix C Proof for Inverse Transform Watermarks in Section ‣ Optimal Detection for Language Watermarks with Pseudorandom Collision" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">C.3</span></a>.</h6>
<div id="A3.SS6.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A3.SS6.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A3.SS6.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text">The result follows from the concentration inequality in Lemma <a href="#A3.Thmlem7" title="Lemma C.7 ([], Theorem 2.1). ‣ C.10 Auxiliary Lemmas ‣ Appendix C Proof for Inverse Transform Watermarks in Section ‣ Optimal Detection for Language Watermarks with Pseudorandom Collision" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">C.7</span></a>, which applies to sums over randomly permuted arrays.
Let</span></p>
<table id="A3.Ex201" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A3.Ex201.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="C=\{\pi(w_{\ell}^{\prime})=w_{\ell},\forall\ell\in[m]\}" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>C</mi><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mi>π</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msubsup><mi>w</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mo>′</mo></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>=</mo><msub><mi>w</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><mo rspace="0.167em">∀</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mi>m</mi><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">C=\{\pi(w_{\ell}^{\prime})=w_{\ell},\forall\ell\in[m]\}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A3.SS6.p1.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="A3.SS6.p1.2.1" class="ltx_text">denote the event that the random permutation <math id="A3.SS6.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\pi" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>π</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\pi</annotation></semantics></math> maps each <math id="A3.SS6.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="w_{\ell}^{\prime}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msubsup><mi>w</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mo>′</mo></msubsup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">w_{\ell}^{\prime}</annotation></semantics></math> to <math id="A3.SS6.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="w_{\ell}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>w</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">w_{\ell}</annotation></semantics></math>.
To apply Lemma <a href="#A3.Thmlem7" title="Lemma C.7 ([], Theorem 2.1). ‣ C.10 Auxiliary Lemmas ‣ Appendix C Proof for Inverse Transform Watermarks in Section ‣ Optimal Detection for Language Watermarks with Pseudorandom Collision" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">C.7</span></a>, we fix an index <math id="A3.SS6.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\ell\in[m]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mi>m</mi><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\ell\in[m]</annotation></semantics></math> and define</span></p>
<table id="A3.Ex202" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A3.Ex202.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="b^{(t)}_{i,j}=P_{t,j}\cdot\mathbf{1}_{\{i\leq w_{\ell}^{\prime}\,,\;j\not\in\{w_{1},\ldots,w_{m}\}\}},\quad\text{for }i,j\in{{\mathcal{W}}}." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><msubsup><mi>b</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup><mo>=</mo><mrow><msub><mi>P</mi><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><msub><mn>𝟏</mn><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>≤</mo><msubsup><mi>w</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mo>′</mo></msubsup></mrow><mo rspace="0.447em">,</mo><mrow><mi>j</mi><mo>∉</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><msub><mi>w</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>w</mi><mi>m</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow></msub></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="1.167em">,</mo><mrow><mtext>for </mtext><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>i</mi></mrow><mo>,</mo><mrow><mi>j</mi><mo>∈</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒲</mi></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">b^{(t)}_{i,j}=P_{t,j}\cdot\mathbf{1}_{\{i\leq w_{\ell}^{\prime}\,,\;j\not\in\{w_{1},\ldots,w_{m}\}\}},\quad\text{for }i,j\in{{\mathcal{W}}}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A3.SS6.p1.3" class="ltx_p"><span id="A3.SS6.p1.3.1" class="ltx_text">Recall that <math id="A3.SS6.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="a_{\pi,\,w_{\ell}^{\prime}-1}^{(t)}=\sum_{j=1}^{w_{\ell}^{\prime}-1}P_{t,\pi(j)}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msubsup><mi>a</mi><mrow><mi>π</mi><mo rspace="0.337em">,</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>w</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mo>′</mo></msubsup><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup><mo rspace="0.111em">=</mo><mrow><msubsup><mo>∑</mo><mrow><mi>j</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mrow><msubsup><mi>w</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mo>′</mo></msubsup><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msubsup><msub><mi>P</mi><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>,</mo><mrow><mi>π</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>j</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></msub></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">a_{\pi,\,w_{\ell}^{\prime}-1}^{(t)}=\sum_{j=1}^{w_{\ell}^{\prime}-1}P_{t,\pi(j)}</annotation></semantics></math> and a direct calculation shows that for any <math id="A3.SS6.p1.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="t\in{\mathcal{I}}^{Y}_{\ell}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>∈</mo><msubsup><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℐ</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mi>Y</mi></msubsup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">t\in{\mathcal{I}}^{Y}_{\ell}</annotation></semantics></math>,</span></p>
<table id="A3.EGx88" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A3.E123"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A3.E123.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\left|\sum_{j\in{{\mathcal{W}}}}b^{(t)}_{j,\pi(j)}-a_{\pi,w_{\ell}^{\prime}-1}^{(t)}\right|\leq mP_{t,(2)}." display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mo>|</mo><mrow><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munder><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>j</mi><mo>∈</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒲</mi></mrow></munder></mstyle><msubsup><mi>b</mi><mrow><mi>j</mi><mo>,</mo><mrow><mi>π</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>j</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup></mrow><mo>−</mo><msubsup><mi>a</mi><mrow><mi>π</mi><mo>,</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>w</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mo>′</mo></msubsup><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup></mrow><mo>|</mo></mrow><mo>≤</mo><mrow><mi>m</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>P</mi><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>,</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>2</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></msub></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\left|\sum_{j\in{{\mathcal{W}}}}b^{(t)}_{j,\pi(j)}-a_{\pi,w_{\ell}^{\prime}-1}^{(t)}\right|\leq mP_{t,(2)}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(123)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A3.SS6.p1.4" class="ltx_p"><span id="A3.SS6.p1.4.1" class="ltx_text">Note that, conditioned on the event <math id="A3.SS6.p1.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="C" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>C</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">C</annotation></semantics></math>, the permutation <math id="A3.SS6.p1.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\pi" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>π</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\pi</annotation></semantics></math> is uniformly distributed as a bijection from <math id="A3.SS6.p1.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="{{\mathcal{W}}}\setminus\{w_{1}^{\prime},\ldots,w_{m}^{\prime}\}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒲</mi><mo>∖</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><msubsup><mi>w</mi><mn>1</mn><mo>′</mo></msubsup><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi><mo>,</mo><msubsup><mi>w</mi><mi>m</mi><mo>′</mo></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{{\mathcal{W}}}\setminus\{w_{1}^{\prime},\ldots,w_{m}^{\prime}\}</annotation></semantics></math> to <math id="A3.SS6.p1.m10" class="ltx_Math" alttext="{{\mathcal{W}}}\setminus\{w_{1},\ldots,w_{m}\}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒲</mi><mo>∖</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><msub><mi>w</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>w</mi><mi>m</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{{\mathcal{W}}}\setminus\{w_{1},\ldots,w_{m}\}</annotation></semantics></math>. Therefore,</span></p>
<table id="A3.EGx89" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A3.Ex203"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A3.Ex203.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\EB_{\pi}\left[\sum_{j\in{{\mathcal{W}}}}b^{(t)}_{j,\pi(j)}\bigg|C\right]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>𝔼</mi><mi>π</mi></msub><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>[</mo><mrow><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munder><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>j</mi><mo>∈</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒲</mi></mrow></munder></mstyle><msubsup><mi>b</mi><mrow><mi>j</mi><mo>,</mo><mrow><mi>π</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>j</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup></mrow><mo fence="false" maxsize="2.100em" minsize="2.100em" rspace="0.167em" stretchy="true">|</mo><mi>C</mi></mrow><mo>]</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\EB_{\pi}\left[\sum_{j\in{{\mathcal{W}}}}b^{(t)}_{j,\pi(j)}\bigg|C\right]</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A3.Ex203.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=\sum_{j\in{{\mathcal{W}}}\setminus\{w_{1}^{\prime},\ldots,w_{m}^{\prime}\}}\EB_{\pi}\left[P_{t,\pi(j)}{\bf 1}_{j\leq w_{\ell}^{\prime}}\,\middle|\,C\right]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munder><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>j</mi><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒲</mi><mo>∖</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><msubsup><mi>w</mi><mn>1</mn><mo>′</mo></msubsup><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi><mo>,</mo><msubsup><mi>w</mi><mi>m</mi><mo>′</mo></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></munder></mstyle><mrow><msub><mi>𝔼</mi><mi>π</mi></msub><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>[</mo><mrow><msub><mi>P</mi><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>,</mo><mrow><mi>π</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>j</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mn>𝟏</mn><mrow><mi>j</mi><mo>≤</mo><msubsup><mi>w</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mo>′</mo></msubsup></mrow></msub></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.170em" stretchy="true">|</mo><mi>C</mi><mo>]</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=\sum_{j\in{{\mathcal{W}}}\setminus\{w_{1}^{\prime},\ldots,w_{m}^{\prime}\}}\EB_{\pi}\left[P_{t,\pi(j)}{\bf 1}_{j\leq w_{\ell}^{\prime}}\,\middle|\,C\right]</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A3.Ex204"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A3.Ex204.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=\left|\left\{j\leq w_{\ell}^{\prime}:j\notin\{w_{1}^{\prime},\ldots,w_{m}^{\prime}\}\right\}\right|\cdot\frac{1}{|{{\mathcal{W}}}|-m}\cdot\sum_{j\in{{\mathcal{W}}}\setminus\{w_{1},\ldots,w_{m}\}}P_{t,j}." display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mo>|</mo><mrow><mo>{</mo><mrow><mi>j</mi><mo>≤</mo><msubsup><mi>w</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mo>′</mo></msubsup></mrow><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mrow><mi>j</mi><mo>∉</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><msubsup><mi>w</mi><mn>1</mn><mo>′</mo></msubsup><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi><mo>,</mo><msubsup><mi>w</mi><mi>m</mi><mo>′</mo></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>}</mo></mrow><mo rspace="0.055em">|</mo></mrow><mo rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒲</mi><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow><mo>−</mo><mi>m</mi></mrow></mfrac></mstyle><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munder><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>j</mi><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒲</mi><mo>∖</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><msub><mi>w</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>w</mi><mi>m</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></munder></mstyle><msub><mi>P</mi><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow></msub></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=\left|\left\{j\leq w_{\ell}^{\prime}:j\notin\{w_{1}^{\prime},\ldots,w_{m}^{\prime}\}\right\}\right|\cdot\frac{1}{|{{\mathcal{W}}}|-m}\cdot\sum_{j\in{{\mathcal{W}}}\setminus\{w_{1},\ldots,w_{m}\}}P_{t,j}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A3.SS6.p1.5" class="ltx_p"><span id="A3.SS6.p1.5.1" class="ltx_text">Observe that</span></p>
<table id="A3.Ex205" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A3.Ex205.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="w_{\ell}^{\prime}-m\leq\left|\left\{j\leq w_{\ell}^{\prime}:j\notin\{w_{1}^{\prime},\ldots,w_{m}^{\prime}\}\right\}\right|\leq w_{\ell}^{\prime}-1." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><msubsup><mi>w</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mo>′</mo></msubsup><mo>−</mo><mi>m</mi></mrow><mo>≤</mo><mrow><mo>|</mo><mrow><mo>{</mo><mrow><mi>j</mi><mo>≤</mo><msubsup><mi>w</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mo>′</mo></msubsup></mrow><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mrow><mi>j</mi><mo>∉</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><msubsup><mi>w</mi><mn>1</mn><mo>′</mo></msubsup><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi><mo>,</mo><msubsup><mi>w</mi><mi>m</mi><mo>′</mo></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>}</mo></mrow><mo>|</mo></mrow><mo>≤</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>w</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mo>′</mo></msubsup><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">w_{\ell}^{\prime}-m\leq\left|\left\{j\leq w_{\ell}^{\prime}:j\notin\{w_{1}^{\prime},\ldots,w_{m}^{\prime}\}\right\}\right|\leq w_{\ell}^{\prime}-1.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A3.SS6.p1.6" class="ltx_p"><span id="A3.SS6.p1.6.1" class="ltx_text">Using this, we obtain</span></p>
<table id="A3.EGx90" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A3.E124"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A3.E124.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\displaystyle\left|\frac{\left|\left\{j\leq w_{\ell}^{\prime}:j\notin\{w_{1}^{\prime},\ldots,w_{m}^{\prime}\}\right\}\right|}{|{{\mathcal{W}}}|-m}-\frac{w_{\ell}^{\prime}-1}{|{{\mathcal{W}}}|-1}\right|" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo fence="false" rspace="0.167em">|</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><mo>|</mo><mrow><mo>{</mo><mrow><mi>j</mi><mo>≤</mo><msubsup><mi>w</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mo>′</mo></msubsup></mrow><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mrow><mi>j</mi><mo>∉</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><msubsup><mi>w</mi><mn>1</mn><mo>′</mo></msubsup><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi><mo>,</mo><msubsup><mi>w</mi><mi>m</mi><mo>′</mo></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>}</mo></mrow><mo>|</mo></mrow><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒲</mi><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow><mo>−</mo><mi>m</mi></mrow></mfrac></mstyle><mo>−</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><msubsup><mi>w</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mo>′</mo></msubsup><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒲</mi><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mfrac></mstyle><mo fence="false">|</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\left|\frac{\left|\left\{j\leq w_{\ell}^{\prime}:j\notin\{w_{1}^{\prime},\ldots,w_{m}^{\prime}\}\right\}\right|}{|{{\mathcal{W}}}|-m}-\frac{w_{\ell}^{\prime}-1}{|{{\mathcal{W}}}|-1}\right|</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A3.E124.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\leq\frac{m-1}{|{{\mathcal{W}}}|-m}+\frac{(w_{\ell}^{\prime}-1)(m-1)}{(|{{\mathcal{W}}}|-m)(|{{\mathcal{W}}}|-1)}=O\!\left(\frac{m}{|{{\mathcal{W}}}|}\right)." display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>≤</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><mi>m</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒲</mi><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow><mo>−</mo><mi>m</mi></mrow></mfrac></mstyle><mo>+</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>w</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mo>′</mo></msubsup><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>m</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒲</mi><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow><mo>−</mo><mi>m</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒲</mi><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mfrac></mstyle></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mpadded style="width:0.621em;" width="0.621em"><mi>O</mi></mpadded><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mi>m</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒲</mi><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow></mfrac></mstyle><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\leq\frac{m-1}{|{{\mathcal{W}}}|-m}+\frac{(w_{\ell}^{\prime}-1)(m-1)}{(|{{\mathcal{W}}}|-m)(|{{\mathcal{W}}}|-1)}=O\!\left(\frac{m}{|{{\mathcal{W}}}|}\right).</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(124)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A3.SS6.p1.7" class="ltx_p"><span id="A3.SS6.p1.7.1" class="ltx_text">On the other hand, since <math id="A3.SS6.p1.m11" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\sum_{j\in{{\mathcal{W}}}\setminus\{w_{t}\}}P_{t,j}=\Delta_{t}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mo>∑</mo><mrow><mi>j</mi><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒲</mi><mo>∖</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><msub><mi>w</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></msub><msub><mi>P</mi><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow></msub></mrow><mo>=</mo><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mi>t</mi></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\sum_{j\in{{\mathcal{W}}}\setminus\{w_{t}\}}P_{t,j}=\Delta_{t}</annotation></semantics></math>, we also have</span></p>
<table id="A3.EGx91" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A3.E125"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A3.E125.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\left|\sum_{j\in{{\mathcal{W}}}\setminus\{w_{1},\ldots,w_{m}\}}P_{t,j}-\sum_{j\in{{\mathcal{W}}}\setminus\{w_{t}\}}P_{t,j}\right|\leq(m-1)P_{t,(2)}." display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mo>|</mo><mrow><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munder><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>j</mi><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒲</mi><mo>∖</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><msub><mi>w</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>w</mi><mi>m</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></munder></mstyle><msub><mi>P</mi><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow></msub></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munder><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>j</mi><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒲</mi><mo>∖</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><msub><mi>w</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></munder></mstyle><msub><mi>P</mi><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow></msub></mrow></mrow><mo>|</mo></mrow><mo>≤</mo><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>m</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>P</mi><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>,</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>2</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></msub></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\left|\sum_{j\in{{\mathcal{W}}}\setminus\{w_{1},\ldots,w_{m}\}}P_{t,j}-\sum_{j\in{{\mathcal{W}}}\setminus\{w_{t}\}}P_{t,j}\right|\leq(m-1)P_{t,(2)}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(125)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A3.SS6.p1.8" class="ltx_p"><span id="A3.SS6.p1.8.1" class="ltx_text">Putting the bounds together, we conclude that</span></p>
<table id="A3.EGx92" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A3.E126"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A3.E126.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\left|\EB_{\pi}\left[\sum_{j\in{{\mathcal{W}}}}b^{(t)}_{j,\pi(j)}\,\middle|\,C\right]-\frac{(w_{\ell}^{\prime}-1)\Delta_{t}}{|{{\mathcal{W}}}|-1}\right|\leq 2m\left(P_{t,(2)}+\frac{1}{|{{\mathcal{W}}}|}\right),\quad\forall t\in{\mathcal{I}}^{Y}_{\ell}." display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mrow><mo>|</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>𝔼</mi><mi>π</mi></msub><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>[</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munder><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>j</mi><mo>∈</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒲</mi></mrow></munder></mstyle><msubsup><mi>b</mi><mrow><mi>j</mi><mo>,</mo><mrow><mi>π</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>j</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.170em" stretchy="true">|</mo><mi>C</mi><mo>]</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>w</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mo>′</mo></msubsup><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mi>t</mi></msub></mrow><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒲</mi><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mfrac></mstyle></mrow><mo>|</mo></mrow><mo>≤</mo><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>m</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>P</mi><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>,</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>2</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></msub><mo>+</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒲</mi><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow></mfrac></mstyle></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="1.167em">,</mo><mrow><mrow><mo rspace="0.167em">∀</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow><mo>∈</mo><msubsup><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℐ</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mi>Y</mi></msubsup></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\left|\EB_{\pi}\left[\sum_{j\in{{\mathcal{W}}}}b^{(t)}_{j,\pi(j)}\,\middle|\,C\right]-\frac{(w_{\ell}^{\prime}-1)\Delta_{t}}{|{{\mathcal{W}}}|-1}\right|\leq 2m\left(P_{t,(2)}+\frac{1}{|{{\mathcal{W}}}|}\right),\quad\forall t\in{\mathcal{I}}^{Y}_{\ell}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(126)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
<div id="A3.SS6.p2" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A3.SS6.p2.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A3.SS6.p2.1.1" class="ltx_text">Thus, Lemma <a href="#A3.Thmlem7" title="Lemma C.7 ([], Theorem 2.1). ‣ C.10 Auxiliary Lemmas ‣ Appendix C Proof for Inverse Transform Watermarks in Section ‣ Optimal Detection for Language Watermarks with Pseudorandom Collision" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">C.7</span></a> applies to <math id="A3.SS6.p2.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\sum_{j\in{{\mathcal{W}}}}b^{(t)}_{j,\pi(j)}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mo>∑</mo><mrow><mi>j</mi><mo>∈</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒲</mi></mrow></msub><msubsup><mi>b</mi><mrow><mi>j</mi><mo>,</mo><mrow><mi>π</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>j</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\sum_{j\in{{\mathcal{W}}}}b^{(t)}_{j,\pi(j)}</annotation></semantics></math> for each <math id="A3.SS6.p2.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="t\in{\mathcal{I}}^{Y}_{\ell}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>∈</mo><msubsup><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℐ</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mi>Y</mi></msubsup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">t\in{\mathcal{I}}^{Y}_{\ell}</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="A3.SS6.p2.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\ell\in[m]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mi>m</mi><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\ell\in[m]</annotation></semantics></math>.
More specifically, combining (<a href="#A3.E123" title="In Proof of Lemma . ‣ C.6 Proof of Lemma ‣ Appendix C Proof for Inverse Transform Watermarks in Section ‣ Optimal Detection for Language Watermarks with Pseudorandom Collision" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">123</span></a>) and (<a href="#A3.E126" title="In Proof of Lemma . ‣ C.6 Proof of Lemma ‣ Appendix C Proof for Inverse Transform Watermarks in Section ‣ Optimal Detection for Language Watermarks with Pseudorandom Collision" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">126</span></a>), for any <math id="A3.SS6.p2.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\lambda&gt;0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>λ</mi><mo>&gt;</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\lambda&gt;0</annotation></semantics></math>, we have that with probability at least <math id="A3.SS6.p2.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="1-\lambda" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mi>λ</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">1-\lambda</annotation></semantics></math>,</span></p>
<table id="A3.EGx93" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A3.E127"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A3.E127.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\left|a_{\pi,w_{\ell}^{\prime}-1}^{(t)}-\frac{(w_{\ell}^{\prime}-1)\Delta_{t}}{|{{\mathcal{W}}}|-1}\right|\leq O(m)\cdot\left(\sqrt{\frac{w_{\ell}^{\prime}}{|{{\mathcal{W}}}|}\sum_{j=2}^{|{{\mathcal{W}}}|}P_{t,(j)}^{2}\log\frac{1}{\lambda}}+P_{t,(2)}\log\frac{1}{\lambda}+\frac{1}{|{{\mathcal{W}}}|}\right)," display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mo>|</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>a</mi><mrow><mi>π</mi><mo>,</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>w</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mo>′</mo></msubsup><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup><mo>−</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>w</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mo>′</mo></msubsup><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mi>t</mi></msub></mrow><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒲</mi><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mfrac></mstyle></mrow><mo>|</mo></mrow><mo>≤</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>O</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>m</mi><mo rspace="0.055em" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><msqrt><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><msubsup><mi>w</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mo>′</mo></msubsup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒲</mi><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow></mfrac></mstyle><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>j</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒲</mi><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow></munderover></mstyle><mrow><msubsup><mi>P</mi><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>,</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>j</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mn>2</mn></msubsup><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mi>λ</mi></mfrac></mstyle></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow></msqrt><mo>+</mo><mrow><msub><mi>P</mi><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>,</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>2</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mi>λ</mi></mfrac></mstyle></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒲</mi><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow></mfrac></mstyle></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\left|a_{\pi,w_{\ell}^{\prime}-1}^{(t)}-\frac{(w_{\ell}^{\prime}-1)\Delta_{t}}{|{{\mathcal{W}}}|-1}\right|\leq O(m)\cdot\left(\sqrt{\frac{w_{\ell}^{\prime}}{|{{\mathcal{W}}}|}\sum_{j=2}^{|{{\mathcal{W}}}|}P_{t,(j)}^{2}\log\frac{1}{\lambda}}+P_{t,(2)}\log\frac{1}{\lambda}+\frac{1}{|{{\mathcal{W}}}|}\right),</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(127)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A3.SS6.p2.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="A3.SS6.p2.2.1" class="ltx_text">where a universal constant hidden in <math id="A3.SS6.p2.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="O(1)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>O</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>1</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">O(1)</annotation></semantics></math>.
Finally, we apply a union bound over all choices of distinct tokens <math id="A3.SS6.p2.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="w_{1}^{\prime},\ldots,w_{m}^{\prime}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msubsup><mi>w</mi><mn>1</mn><mo>′</mo></msubsup><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi><mo>,</mo><msubsup><mi>w</mi><mi>m</mi><mo>′</mo></msubsup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">w_{1}^{\prime},\ldots,w_{m}^{\prime}</annotation></semantics></math> and all <math id="A3.SS6.p2.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="t\in{\mathcal{I}}^{Y}_{\ell}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>∈</mo><msubsup><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℐ</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mi>Y</mi></msubsup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">t\in{\mathcal{I}}^{Y}_{\ell}</annotation></semantics></math>, <math id="A3.SS6.p2.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\ell\in[m]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mi>m</mi><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\ell\in[m]</annotation></semantics></math>. Setting <math id="A3.SS6.p2.m10" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\lambda=\frac{1}{m\,|{{\mathcal{W}}}|^{m+1}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>λ</mi><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mrow><mi>m</mi><mo lspace="0.170em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒲</mi><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow><mrow><mi>m</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup></mrow></mfrac></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\lambda=\frac{1}{m\,|{{\mathcal{W}}}|^{m+1}}</annotation></semantics></math>, we obtain</span></p>
<table id="A3.EGx94" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A3.E128"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A3.E128.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\displaystyle\sup_{\begin{subarray}{c}w_{1}^{\prime},\ldots,w_{m}^{\prime}\\
\mathrm{distinct}\end{subarray}}\EB_{\pi}\left[\max_{\begin{subarray}{c}\ell\in[m]\\
t\in{\mathcal{I}}^{Y}_{\ell}\end{subarray}}\left|a_{\pi,w_{\ell}^{\prime}-1}^{(t)}-\frac{(w_{\ell}^{\prime}-1)\Delta_{t}}{|{{\mathcal{W}}}|-1}\right|\,\Bigg|\,\pi(w_{\ell}^{\prime})=w_{\ell},\forall\ell\right]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><munder><mo movablelimits="false">sup</mo><mtable rowspacing="0pt"><mtr><mtd><mrow><msubsup><mi>w</mi><mn>1</mn><mo>′</mo></msubsup><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi><mo>,</mo><msubsup><mi>w</mi><mi>m</mi><mo>′</mo></msubsup></mrow></mtd></mtr><mtr><mtd><mi>distinct</mi></mtd></mtr></mtable></munder><msub><mi>𝔼</mi><mi>π</mi></msub><mrow><mo>[</mo><munder><mi>max</mi><mtable rowspacing="0pt"><mtr><mtd><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mi>m</mi><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow></mtd></mtr><mtr><mtd><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>∈</mo><msubsup><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℐ</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mi>Y</mi></msubsup></mrow></mtd></mtr></mtable></munder><mo fence="false" rspace="0.167em">|</mo><msubsup><mi>a</mi><mrow><mi>π</mi><mo>,</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>w</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mo>′</mo></msubsup><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup><mo>−</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>w</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mo>′</mo></msubsup><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mi>t</mi></msub></mrow><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒲</mi><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mfrac></mstyle><mo fence="false" rspace="0.337em">|</mo><mo fence="false" maxsize="2.600em" minsize="2.600em" rspace="0.337em" stretchy="true">|</mo><mi>π</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msubsup><mi>w</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mo>′</mo></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>=</mo><msub><mi>w</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><mo rspace="0.167em">∀</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mo>]</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\sup_{\begin{subarray}{c}w_{1}^{\prime},\ldots,w_{m}^{\prime}\\
\mathrm{distinct}\end{subarray}}\EB_{\pi}\left[\max_{\begin{subarray}{c}\ell\in[m]\\
t\in{\mathcal{I}}^{Y}_{\ell}\end{subarray}}\left|a_{\pi,w_{\ell}^{\prime}-1}^{(t)}-\frac{(w_{\ell}^{\prime}-1)\Delta_{t}}{|{{\mathcal{W}}}|-1}\right|\,\Bigg|\,\pi(w_{\ell}^{\prime})=w_{\ell},\forall\ell\right]</annotation></semantics></math></td>
