<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(129)</span></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A3.E130"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A3.E130.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\leq O(m)\cdot\max_{\begin{subarray}{c}\ell\in[m]\\
t\in{\mathcal{I}}^{Y}_{\ell}\end{subarray}}\left(\frac{1}{|{{\mathcal{W}}}|}+\sqrt{P_{t,(2)}\log|{{\mathcal{W}}}|}+P_{t,(2)}\log|{{\mathcal{W}}}|\right)." display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>≤</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>O</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>m</mi><mo rspace="0.055em" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><mrow><munder><mi>max</mi><mtable rowspacing="0pt"><mtr><mtd><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mi>m</mi><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow></mtd></mtr><mtr><mtd><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>∈</mo><msubsup><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℐ</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mi>Y</mi></msubsup></mrow></mtd></mtr></mtable></munder><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒲</mi><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow></mfrac></mstyle><mo>+</mo><msqrt><mrow><msub><mi>P</mi><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>,</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>2</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒲</mi><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></msqrt><mo>+</mo><mrow><msub><mi>P</mi><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>,</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>2</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒲</mi><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\leq O(m)\cdot\max_{\begin{subarray}{c}\ell\in[m]\\
t\in{\mathcal{I}}^{Y}_{\ell}\end{subarray}}\left(\frac{1}{|{{\mathcal{W}}}|}+\sqrt{P_{t,(2)}\log|{{\mathcal{W}}}|}+P_{t,(2)}\log|{{\mathcal{W}}}|\right).</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(130)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A3.SS6.p2.3" class="ltx_p"><span id="A3.SS6.p2.3.1" class="ltx_text">∎</span></p>
</div>
</div>
</section>
<section id="A3.SS7" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection">C.7 </span>Proof of Lemma <a href="#S7.Thmlem7" title="Lemma 7.7 (Simplified limits). ‣ 7.2 Proof of Theorem ‣ 7 Proof of Main Results ‣ Optimal Detection for Language Watermarks with Pseudorandom Collision" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">7.7</span></a></h3>

<div id="A3.SS7.2" class="ltx_proof">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_font_italic ltx_title_proof">Proof of Lemma <a href="#S7.Thmlem7" title="Lemma 7.7 (Simplified limits). ‣ 7.2 Proof of Theorem ‣ 7 Proof of Main Results ‣ Optimal Detection for Language Watermarks with Pseudorandom Collision" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">7.7</span></a>.</h6>
<div id="A3.SS7.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A3.SS7.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A3.SS7.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text">As we focus on a single block, the sub-block index <math id="A3.SS7.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="k" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>k</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">k</annotation></semantics></math> is omitted, following the convention in the proof of Theorem <a href="#S5.Thmtheorem1" title="Theorem 5.1 (Asymptotic joint distribution of pivotal statistics). ‣ 5.1 Asymptotic Distributions ‣ 5 Application to the Inverse Transform Watermark ‣ Optimal Detection for Language Watermarks with Pseudorandom Collision" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">5.1</span></a>.
For simplicity, we also write <math id="A3.SS7.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\Delta" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Delta</annotation></semantics></math> instead of <math id="A3.SS7.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\Delta_{{\mathcal{V}}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒱</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Delta_{{\mathcal{V}}}</annotation></semantics></math>.
For a minimal unit <math id="A3.SS7.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="{\mathcal{V}}={\mathcal{I}}^{\zeta}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒱</mi><mo>=</mo><msup><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℐ</mi><mi>ζ</mi></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\mathcal{V}}={\mathcal{I}}^{\zeta}</annotation></semantics></math> containing <math id="A3.SS7.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="m" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>m</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">m</annotation></semantics></math> sub-blocks, we represent its associated pivotal statistics <math id="A3.SS7.p1.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="Y_{{\mathcal{V}}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>Y</mi><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒱</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">Y_{{\mathcal{V}}}</annotation></semantics></math> as the vector <math id="A3.SS7.p1.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\bm{Y}=(Y_{1},\ldots,Y_{m})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>𝒀</mi><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>Y</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>Y</mi><mi>m</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\bm{Y}=(Y_{1},\ldots,Y_{m})</annotation></semantics></math>, where each component corresponds to a distinct sub-block. Since</span></p>
</div>
<div id="A3.SS7.p2" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A3.SS7.p2.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A3.SS7.p2.1.1" class="ltx_text">Under Assumption <a href="#S5.Thmasmp1" title="Assumption 5.1 (Asymptotic NTP conditions). ‣ 5.1 Asymptotic Distributions ‣ 5 Application to the Inverse Transform Watermark ‣ Optimal Detection for Language Watermarks with Pseudorandom Collision" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">5.1</span></a>, the set of NTP distributions in <math id="A3.SS7.p2.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="{\mathcal{V}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒱</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\mathcal{V}}</annotation></semantics></math> can be rewritten using the notation <math id="A3.SS7.p2.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="{\mathcal{Q}}_{\tau,\bm{\Delta}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒬</mi><mrow><mi>τ</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>𝚫</mi></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\mathcal{Q}}_{\tau,\bm{\Delta}}</annotation></semantics></math> from (<a href="#A3.E86" title="In Definition C.1 (Fixed-parameter belief class). ‣ Belief classes. ‣ Appendix C Proof for Inverse Transform Watermarks in Section ‣ Optimal Detection for Language Watermarks with Pseudorandom Collision" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">86</span></a>) as</span></p>
<table id="A3.E131" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A3.E131.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\{\bm{P}_{{\mathcal{V}}}:\bm{P}_{{\mathcal{V}}}\subseteq{\overline{{\mathcal{P}}}_{\Delta}}\}=\bigcup_{\Delta\leq\bm{\Delta}\leq 1-\delta}{\mathcal{Q}}_{{\mathcal{V}},\bm{\Delta}}." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><msub><mi>𝑷</mi><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒱</mi></msub><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mrow><msub><mi>𝑷</mi><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒱</mi></msub><mo>⊆</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒫</mi><mo stretchy="true">¯</mo></mover><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow><mo rspace="0.111em">=</mo><mrow><munder><mo movablelimits="false">⋃</mo><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo>≤</mo><mi>𝚫</mi><mo>≤</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mi>δ</mi></mrow></mrow></munder><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒬</mi><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒱</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>𝚫</mi></mrow></msub></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\{\bm{P}_{{\mathcal{V}}}:\bm{P}_{{\mathcal{V}}}\subseteq{\overline{{\mathcal{P}}}_{\Delta}}\}=\bigcup_{\Delta\leq\bm{\Delta}\leq 1-\delta}{\mathcal{Q}}_{{\mathcal{V}},\bm{\Delta}}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(131)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A3.SS7.p2.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="A3.SS7.p2.2.1" class="ltx_text">We aim to show that</span></p>
<table id="A3.E132" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A3.E132.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\limsup_{|{{\mathcal{W}}}|\to\infty}\left[\EB_{0}[h(\bm{Y})]+\sup_{\bm{P}_{{\mathcal{V}}}\subseteq{\overline{{\mathcal{P}}}_{\Delta}}}\log\EB_{1,\bm{P}_{{\mathcal{V}}}}[\exp(-h(\bm{Y}))]\right]=\sup_{\Delta\leq\bm{{\bar{\Delta}}}}L^{\prime}(h,\bm{{\bar{\Delta}}})," display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><munder><mo movablelimits="false">lim sup</mo><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒲</mi><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">∞</mi></mrow></munder><mrow><mo lspace="0em">[</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>𝔼</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><mi>h</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝐘</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><munder><mo lspace="0em" movablelimits="false" rspace="0.167em">sup</mo><mrow><msub><mi>𝐏</mi><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒱</mi></msub><mo>⊆</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒫</mi><mo stretchy="true">¯</mo></mover><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi></msub></mrow></munder><mrow><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><msub><mi>𝔼</mi><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>𝐏</mi><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒱</mi></msub></mrow></msub></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><mi>exp</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>h</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝐘</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>]</mo></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.1389em">=</mo><mrow><munder><mo lspace="0.1389em" movablelimits="false" rspace="0.167em">sup</mo><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo>≤</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>𝚫</mi><mo>¯</mo></mover></mrow></munder><mrow><msup><mi>L</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>h</mi><mo>,</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>𝚫</mi><mo>¯</mo></mover><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\limsup_{|{{\mathcal{W}}}|\to\infty}\left[\EB_{0}[h(\bm{Y})]+\sup_{\bm{P}_{{\mathcal{V}}}\subseteq{\overline{{\mathcal{P}}}_{\Delta}}}\log\EB_{1,\bm{P}_{{\mathcal{V}}}}[\exp(-h(\bm{Y}))]\right]=\sup_{\Delta\leq\bm{{\bar{\Delta}}}}L^{\prime}(h,\bm{{\bar{\Delta}}}),</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(132)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A3.SS7.p2.3" class="ltx_p"><span id="A3.SS7.p2.3.1" class="ltx_text">where <math id="A3.SS7.p2.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\bm{{\bar{\Delta}}}=({\bar{\Delta}}_{1},\ldots,{\bar{\Delta}}_{m_{k}})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mover accent="true"><mi>𝚫</mi><mo>¯</mo></mover><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo>¯</mo></mover><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo>¯</mo></mover><msub><mi>m</mi><mi>k</mi></msub></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\bm{{\bar{\Delta}}}=({\bar{\Delta}}_{1},\ldots,{\bar{\Delta}}_{m_{k}})</annotation></semantics></math>, with each <math id="A3.SS7.p2.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="{\bar{\Delta}}_{\ell}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mover accent="true"><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo>¯</mo></mover><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\bar{\Delta}}_{\ell}</annotation></semantics></math> defined in (<a href="#S5.E17" title="In Lemma 5.1 (Asymptotic joint distribution of pseudorandomness and tokens). ‣ 5.1 Asymptotic Distributions ‣ 5 Application to the Inverse Transform Watermark ‣ Optimal Detection for Language Watermarks with Pseudorandom Collision" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">17</span></a>), and <math id="A3.SS7.p2.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="L^{\prime}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi>L</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">L^{\prime}</annotation></semantics></math> is
defined by (given in (<a href="#S5.E23" title="In 5.2 Optimal Score Function ‣ 5 Application to the Inverse Transform Watermark ‣ Optimal Detection for Language Watermarks with Pseudorandom Collision" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">23</span></a>))</span></p>
<table id="A3.Ex206" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A3.Ex206.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="L^{\prime}(h,\bm{{\bar{\Delta}}})=\EB_{f_{0}}[h(\bm{Y})]+\log\EB_{f_{\bm{{\bar{\Delta}}}}}[\exp(-h(\bm{Y}))]," display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><msup><mi>L</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>h</mi><mo>,</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>𝚫</mi><mo>¯</mo></mover><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>𝔼</mi><msub><mi>f</mi><mn>0</mn></msub></msub><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><mi>h</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝐘</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><msub><mi>𝔼</mi><msub><mi>f</mi><mover accent="true"><mi>𝚫</mi><mo>¯</mo></mover></msub></msub></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><mi>exp</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>h</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝐘</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">L^{\prime}(h,\bm{{\bar{\Delta}}})=\EB_{f_{0}}[h(\bm{Y})]+\log\EB_{f_{\bm{{\bar{\Delta}}}}}[\exp(-h(\bm{Y}))],</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(<a href="#S5.E23" title="In 5.2 Optimal Score Function ‣ 5 Application to the Inverse Transform Watermark ‣ Optimal Detection for Language Watermarks with Pseudorandom Collision" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">23</span></a>)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A3.SS7.p2.4" class="ltx_p"><span id="A3.SS7.p2.4.1" class="ltx_text">where <math id="A3.SS7.p2.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="f_{0}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>f</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">f_{0}</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="A3.SS7.p2.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="f_{\bm{{\bar{\Delta}}}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>f</mi><mover accent="true"><mi>𝚫</mi><mo>¯</mo></mover></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">f_{\bm{{\bar{\Delta}}}}</annotation></semantics></math> denote the asymptotic PDFs of <math id="A3.SS7.p2.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\bm{Y}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>𝒀</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\bm{Y}</annotation></semantics></math> under the null and alternative, given in Theorem <a href="#S5.Thmtheorem1" title="Theorem 5.1 (Asymptotic joint distribution of pivotal statistics). ‣ 5.1 Asymptotic Distributions ‣ 5 Application to the Inverse Transform Watermark ‣ Optimal Detection for Language Watermarks with Pseudorandom Collision" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">5.1</span></a> respectively.</span></p>
</div>
<div id="A3.SS7.p3" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A3.SS7.p3.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A3.SS7.p3.1.1" class="ltx_text">To prove (<a href="#A3.E132" title="In Proof of Lemma . ‣ C.7 Proof of Lemma ‣ Appendix C Proof for Inverse Transform Watermarks in Section ‣ Optimal Detection for Language Watermarks with Pseudorandom Collision" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">132</span></a>), it follows that</span></p>
<table id="A3.EGx95" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A3.Ex207"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A3.Ex207.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\limsup_{|{{\mathcal{W}}}|\to\infty}\left[\EB_{0}[h(\bm{Y})]+\sup_{\bm{P}_{{\mathcal{V}}}\subseteq{\overline{{\mathcal{P}}}_{\Delta}}}\log\EB_{1,\bm{P}_{{\mathcal{V}}}}[\exp(-h(\bm{Y}))]\right]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><munder><mo movablelimits="false">lim sup</mo><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒲</mi><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">∞</mi></mrow></munder><mrow><mo lspace="0em">[</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>𝔼</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><mi>h</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝐘</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><munder><mo lspace="0em" movablelimits="false" rspace="0.167em">sup</mo><mrow><msub><mi>𝐏</mi><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒱</mi></msub><mo>⊆</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒫</mi><mo stretchy="true">¯</mo></mover><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi></msub></mrow></munder><mrow><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><msub><mi>𝔼</mi><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>𝐏</mi><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒱</mi></msub></mrow></msub></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><mi>exp</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>h</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝐘</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>]</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\limsup_{|{{\mathcal{W}}}|\to\infty}\left[\EB_{0}[h(\bm{Y})]+\sup_{\bm{P}_{{\mathcal{V}}}\subseteq{\overline{{\mathcal{P}}}_{\Delta}}}\log\EB_{1,\bm{P}_{{\mathcal{V}}}}[\exp(-h(\bm{Y}))]\right]</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A3.Ex208"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A3.Ex208.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\overset{(a)}{=}\limsup_{|{{\mathcal{W}}}|\to\infty}\sup_{\Delta\leq\bm{\Delta}}\sup_{\bm{P}_{{\mathcal{V}}}\in{\mathcal{Q}}_{\tau,\bm{\Delta}}}\left[\EB_{0}[h(\bm{Y})]+\log\EB_{1,\bm{P}_{{\mathcal{V}}}}[\exp(-h(\bm{Y}))]\right]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mover accent="true"><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="0.700em" minsize="0.700em">(</mo><mi mathsize="0.700em">a</mi><mo maxsize="0.700em" minsize="0.700em">)</mo></mrow></mover><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><munder><mo movablelimits="false" rspace="0.0835em">lim sup</mo><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒲</mi><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">∞</mi></mrow></munder><mrow><munder><mo lspace="0.0835em" movablelimits="false" rspace="0.0835em">sup</mo><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo>≤</mo><mi>𝚫</mi></mrow></munder><mrow><munder><mo lspace="0.0835em" movablelimits="false" rspace="0em">sup</mo><mrow><msub><mi>𝑷</mi><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒱</mi></msub><mo>∈</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒬</mi><mrow><mi>τ</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>𝚫</mi></mrow></msub></mrow></munder><mrow><mo>[</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>𝔼</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><mi>h</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝐘</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><msub><mi>𝔼</mi><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>𝐏</mi><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒱</mi></msub></mrow></msub></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><mi>exp</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>h</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝐘</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>]</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\overset{(a)}{=}\limsup_{|{{\mathcal{W}}}|\to\infty}\sup_{\Delta\leq\bm{\Delta}}\sup_{\bm{P}_{{\mathcal{V}}}\in{\mathcal{Q}}_{\tau,\bm{\Delta}}}\left[\EB_{0}[h(\bm{Y})]+\log\EB_{1,\bm{P}_{{\mathcal{V}}}}[\exp(-h(\bm{Y}))]\right]</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A3.Ex209"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A3.Ex209.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\overset{(b)}{=}\sup_{\Delta\leq\bm{\Delta}\leq 1-\delta}\sup_{\bm{P}_{{\mathcal{V}}}\in{\mathcal{Q}}_{\tau,\bm{\Delta}}}\limsup_{|{{\mathcal{W}}}|\to\infty}\left[\EB_{0}[h(\bm{Y})]+\log\EB_{1,\bm{P}_{{\mathcal{V}}}}[\exp(-h(\bm{Y}))]\right]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mover accent="true"><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="0.700em" minsize="0.700em">(</mo><mi mathsize="0.700em">b</mi><mo maxsize="0.700em" minsize="0.700em">)</mo></mrow></mover><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><munder><mo movablelimits="false" rspace="0.0835em">sup</mo><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo>≤</mo><mi>𝚫</mi><mo>≤</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mi>δ</mi></mrow></mrow></munder><mrow><munder><mo lspace="0.0835em" movablelimits="false" rspace="0.0835em">sup</mo><mrow><msub><mi>𝑷</mi><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒱</mi></msub><mo>∈</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒬</mi><mrow><mi>τ</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>𝚫</mi></mrow></msub></mrow></munder><mrow><munder><mo lspace="0.0835em" movablelimits="false" rspace="0em">lim sup</mo><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒲</mi><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">∞</mi></mrow></munder><mrow><mo>[</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>𝔼</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><mi>h</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝐘</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><msub><mi>𝔼</mi><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>𝐏</mi><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒱</mi></msub></mrow></msub></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><mi>exp</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>h</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝐘</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>]</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\overset{(b)}{=}\sup_{\Delta\leq\bm{\Delta}\leq 1-\delta}\sup_{\bm{P}_{{\mathcal{V}}}\in{\mathcal{Q}}_{\tau,\bm{\Delta}}}\limsup_{|{{\mathcal{W}}}|\to\infty}\left[\EB_{0}[h(\bm{Y})]+\log\EB_{1,\bm{P}_{{\mathcal{V}}}}[\exp(-h(\bm{Y}))]\right]</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A3.E133"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A3.E133.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\overset{(c)}{=}\sup_{\Delta\leq\bm{\Delta}\leq 1-\delta}\sup_{\bm{P}_{{\mathcal{V}}}\in{\mathcal{Q}}_{\tau,\bm{\Delta}}}\left[\EB_{f_{0}}[h(\bm{Y})]+\log\EB_{f_{\bm{{\bar{\Delta}}}}}[\exp(-h(\bm{Y}))]\right]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mover accent="true"><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="0.700em" minsize="0.700em">(</mo><mi mathsize="0.700em">c</mi><mo maxsize="0.700em" minsize="0.700em">)</mo></mrow></mover><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><munder><mo movablelimits="false" rspace="0.0835em">sup</mo><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo>≤</mo><mi>𝚫</mi><mo>≤</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mi>δ</mi></mrow></mrow></munder><mrow><munder><mo lspace="0.0835em" movablelimits="false" rspace="0em">sup</mo><mrow><msub><mi>𝑷</mi><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒱</mi></msub><mo>∈</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒬</mi><mrow><mi>τ</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>𝚫</mi></mrow></msub></mrow></munder><mrow><mo>[</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>𝔼</mi><msub><mi>f</mi><mn>0</mn></msub></msub><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><mi>h</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝐘</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><msub><mi>𝔼</mi><msub><mi>f</mi><mover accent="true"><mi>𝚫</mi><mo>¯</mo></mover></msub></msub></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><mi>exp</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>h</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝐘</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>]</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\overset{(c)}{=}\sup_{\Delta\leq\bm{\Delta}\leq 1-\delta}\sup_{\bm{P}_{{\mathcal{V}}}\in{\mathcal{Q}}_{\tau,\bm{\Delta}}}\left[\EB_{f_{0}}[h(\bm{Y})]+\log\EB_{f_{\bm{{\bar{\Delta}}}}}[\exp(-h(\bm{Y}))]\right]</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(133)</span></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A3.Ex210"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A3.Ex210.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\overset{(d)}{=}\sup_{\Delta\leq\bm{{\bar{\Delta}}}\leq 1-\delta}\left[\EB_{f_{0}}[h(\bm{Y})]+\log\EB_{f_{\bm{{\bar{\Delta}}}}}[\exp(-h(\bm{Y}))]\right]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mover accent="true"><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="0.700em" minsize="0.700em">(</mo><mi mathsize="0.700em">d</mi><mo maxsize="0.700em" minsize="0.700em">)</mo></mrow></mover><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><munder><mo movablelimits="false" rspace="0em">sup</mo><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo>≤</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>𝚫</mi><mo>¯</mo></mover><mo>≤</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mi>δ</mi></mrow></mrow></munder><mrow><mo>[</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>𝔼</mi><msub><mi>f</mi><mn>0</mn></msub></msub><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><mi>h</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝐘</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><msub><mi>𝔼</mi><msub><mi>f</mi><mover accent="true"><mi>𝚫</mi><mo>¯</mo></mover></msub></msub></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><mi>exp</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>h</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝐘</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>]</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\overset{(d)}{=}\sup_{\Delta\leq\bm{{\bar{\Delta}}}\leq 1-\delta}\left[\EB_{f_{0}}[h(\bm{Y})]+\log\EB_{f_{\bm{{\bar{\Delta}}}}}[\exp(-h(\bm{Y}))]\right]</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A3.E134"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A3.E134.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=\sup_{\Delta\leq\bm{{\bar{\Delta}}}\leq 1-\delta}L^{\prime}(h,\bm{{\bar{\Delta}}})," display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo rspace="0.1389em">=</mo><mrow><munder><mo lspace="0.1389em" movablelimits="false" rspace="0.167em">sup</mo><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo>≤</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>𝚫</mi><mo>¯</mo></mover><mo>≤</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mi>δ</mi></mrow></mrow></munder><mrow><msup><mi>L</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>h</mi><mo>,</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>𝚫</mi><mo>¯</mo></mover><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=\sup_{\Delta\leq\bm{{\bar{\Delta}}}\leq 1-\delta}L^{\prime}(h,\bm{{\bar{\Delta}}}),</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(134)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A3.SS7.p3.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="A3.SS7.p3.2.1" class="ltx_text">where (a) uses the equivalence in (<a href="#A3.E131" title="In Proof of Lemma . ‣ C.7 Proof of Lemma ‣ Appendix C Proof for Inverse Transform Watermarks in Section ‣ Optimal Detection for Language Watermarks with Pseudorandom Collision" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">131</span></a>), (b) follows by exchanging the order of the <math id="A3.SS7.p3.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\limsup" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mo>lim sup</mo><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\limsup</annotation></semantics></math> and the suprema, which we will justify later, (c) follows from the weak convergence in Theorem <a href="#A3.Thmtheorem1" title="Theorem C.1 (Asymptotic distribution under 𝐻_1). ‣ Proof of Lemma . ‣ C.1 Proof of Lemma ‣ Appendix C Proof for Inverse Transform Watermarks in Section ‣ Optimal Detection for Language Watermarks with Pseudorandom Collision" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">C.1</span></a>, and (d) simplifies the expression by eliminating the dependence on a single <math id="A3.SS7.p3.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\bm{P}_{{\mathcal{V}}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>𝑷</mi><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒱</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\bm{P}_{{\mathcal{V}}}</annotation></semantics></math> and replacing <math id="A3.SS7.p3.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\bm{\Delta}=(\Delta_{t})_{t\in{\mathcal{V}}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>𝚫</mi><mo>=</mo><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>∈</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒱</mi></mrow></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\bm{\Delta}=(\Delta_{t})_{t\in{\mathcal{V}}}</annotation></semantics></math> with <math id="A3.SS7.p3.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\bm{{\bar{\Delta}}}=({\bar{\Delta}}_{\ell})_{\ell\in[m_{k}]}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mover accent="true"><mi>𝚫</mi><mo>¯</mo></mover><mo>=</mo><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo>¯</mo></mover><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><msub><mi>m</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\bm{{\bar{\Delta}}}=({\bar{\Delta}}_{\ell})_{\ell\in[m_{k}]}</annotation></semantics></math>, where <math id="A3.SS7.p3.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="{\bar{\Delta}}_{\ell}:=\max_{t\in{\mathcal{I}}^{Y}_{\ell}}\Delta_{t}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mover accent="true"><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo>¯</mo></mover><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi></msub><mo>:=</mo><mrow><msub><mi>max</mi><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>∈</mo><msubsup><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℐ</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mi>Y</mi></msubsup></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mi>t</mi></msub></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\bar{\Delta}}_{\ell}:=\max_{t\in{\mathcal{I}}^{Y}_{\ell}}\Delta_{t}</annotation></semantics></math> for each <math id="A3.SS7.p3.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\ell" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\ell</annotation></semantics></math>.
At this point, the proof is complete.</span></p>
</div>
<div id="A3.SS7.p4" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A3.SS7.p4.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A3.SS7.p4.1.1" class="ltx_text">In the remainder, we establish the validity of the order exchange in step (b) above.
To this end, let us introduce a test function <math id="A3.SS7.p4.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="J:[0,1]^{m+1}\to\mathbb{R}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>J</mi><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mrow><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow><mrow><mi>m</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><mi>ℝ</mi></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">J:[0,1]^{m+1}\to\mathbb{R}</annotation></semantics></math> defined by</span></p>
<table id="A3.EGx96" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A3.Ex211"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A3.Ex211.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle J(u,x_{1},\ldots,x_{m})=\exp\big(-h(|u-x_{1}|,\ldots,|u-x_{m}|)\big)." display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>J</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>u</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>m</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>exp</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">(</mo><mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>h</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><mrow><mi>u</mi><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mn>1</mn></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi><mo>,</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><mrow><mi>u</mi><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>m</mi></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle J(u,x_{1},\ldots,x_{m})=\exp\big(-h(|u-x_{1}|,\ldots,|u-x_{m}|)\big).</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A3.SS7.p4.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="A3.SS7.p4.2.1" class="ltx_text">Since <math id="A3.SS7.p4.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="h" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>h</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">h</annotation></semantics></math> is Lipschitz continuous and both the exponential and absolute value functions are locally Lipschitz on a bounded domain, their composition <math id="A3.SS7.p4.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="J" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>J</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">J</annotation></semantics></math> is also Lipschitz continuous.
Theorem <a href="#A3.Thmtheorem1" title="Theorem C.1 (Asymptotic distribution under 𝐻_1). ‣ Proof of Lemma . ‣ C.1 Proof of Lemma ‣ Appendix C Proof for Inverse Transform Watermarks in Section ‣ Optimal Detection for Language Watermarks with Pseudorandom Collision" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">C.1</span></a> ensures that the convergence of the expectation of such a function is uniform. Specifically, it guarantees that</span></p>
<table id="A3.EGx97" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A3.E135"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A3.E135.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\lim_{|{{\mathcal{W}}}|\to\infty}\sup_{\Delta\leq\bm{\Delta}\leq 1-\delta}\sup_{\bm{P}_{{\mathcal{V}}}\in{\mathcal{Q}}_{\tau,\bm{\Delta}}}\left|\EB_{1,\bm{P}_{{\mathcal{V}}}}\big[J(U,\eta(\pi(w_{1})),\ldots,\eta(\pi(w_{m})))\big]-\mathcal{L}_{\bar{\bm{\Delta}}}(J)\right|=0," display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><munder><mo movablelimits="false">lim</mo><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒲</mi><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">∞</mi></mrow></munder><mrow><munder><mo lspace="0.167em" movablelimits="false" rspace="0.0835em">sup</mo><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo>≤</mo><mi>𝚫</mi><mo>≤</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mi>δ</mi></mrow></mrow></munder><mrow><munder><mo lspace="0.0835em" movablelimits="false" rspace="0em">sup</mo><mrow><msub><mi>𝑷</mi><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒱</mi></msub><mo>∈</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒬</mi><mrow><mi>τ</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>𝚫</mi></mrow></msub></mrow></munder><mrow><mo>|</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>𝔼</mi><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>𝐏</mi><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒱</mi></msub></mrow></msub><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">[</mo><mrow><mi>J</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>U</mi><mo>,</mo><mrow><mi>η</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>π</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>w</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi><mo>,</mo><mrow><mi>η</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>π</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>w</mi><mi>m</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">]</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℒ</mi><mover accent="true"><mi>𝚫</mi><mo>¯</mo></mover></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>J</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>|</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\lim_{|{{\mathcal{W}}}|\to\infty}\sup_{\Delta\leq\bm{\Delta}\leq 1-\delta}\sup_{\bm{P}_{{\mathcal{V}}}\in{\mathcal{Q}}_{\tau,\bm{\Delta}}}\left|\EB_{1,\bm{P}_{{\mathcal{V}}}}\big[J(U,\eta(\pi(w_{1})),\ldots,\eta(\pi(w_{m})))\big]-\mathcal{L}_{\bar{\bm{\Delta}}}(J)\right|=0,</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(135)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A3.SS7.p4.3" class="ltx_p"><span id="A3.SS7.p4.3.1" class="ltx_text">where <math id="A3.SS7.p4.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{L}_{\bar{\bm{\Delta}}}(J)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℒ</mi><mover accent="true"><mi>𝚫</mi><mo>¯</mo></mover></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>J</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{L}_{\bar{\bm{\Delta}}}(J)</annotation></semantics></math> is the asymptotic integral form</span></p>
<table id="A3.Ex212" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A3.Ex212.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\mathcal{L}_{\bar{\bm{\Delta}}}(J):=\int_{[0,1]^{m}}\int_{\max_{\ell}\{\Delta_{\ell}x_{\ell}\}}^{\min_{\ell}\{1-\Delta_{\ell}+\Delta_{\ell}x_{\ell}\}}\frac{J(u,x_{1},\dots,x_{m})}{I_{m}(\bar{\bm{\Delta}})}\,{\mathrm{d}}u\,\mathbf{1}_{\{\min_{i}\{1-\Delta_{i}+\Delta_{i}x_{i}\}\geq\max_{i}\{\Delta_{i}x_{i}\}\}}\,{\mathrm{d}}x_{1}\cdots{\mathrm{d}}x_{m}," display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℒ</mi><mover accent="true"><mi>𝚫</mi><mo>¯</mo></mover></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>J</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo rspace="0.111em">:=</mo><msub><mo rspace="0em">∫</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow><mi>m</mi></msup></msub><msubsup><mo>∫</mo><mrow><msub><mi>max</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi></msub><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mrow><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow></mrow><mrow><msub><mi>min</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi></msub><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mrow><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi></msub></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi></msub></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow></mrow></msubsup><mfrac><mrow><mi>J</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>u</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>m</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mrow><msub><mi>I</mi><mi>m</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>𝚫</mi><mo>¯</mo></mover><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mfrac><mi>d</mi><mi>u</mi><msub><mn class="ltx_mathvariant_bold" mathvariant="bold"> 1</mn><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mi>min</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>i</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>+</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>i</mi></msub><mi>x</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>i</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">}</mo><mo>≥</mo><mi>max</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>i</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>i</mi></msub><mi>x</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>i</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">}</mo><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow></msub><mi>d</mi><msub><mi>x</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">⋯</mo><mi>d</mi><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>m</mi></msub><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{L}_{\bar{\bm{\Delta}}}(J):=\int_{[0,1]^{m}}\int_{\max_{\ell}\{\Delta_{\ell}x_{\ell}\}}^{\min_{\ell}\{1-\Delta_{\ell}+\Delta_{\ell}x_{\ell}\}}\frac{J(u,x_{1},\dots,x_{m})}{I_{m}(\bar{\bm{\Delta}})}\,{\mathrm{d}}u\,\mathbf{1}_{\{\min_{i}\{1-\Delta_{i}+\Delta_{i}x_{i}\}\geq\max_{i}\{\Delta_{i}x_{i}\}\}}\,{\mathrm{d}}x_{1}\cdots{\mathrm{d}}x_{m},</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A3.SS7.p4.4" class="ltx_p"><span id="A3.SS7.p4.4.1" class="ltx_text">and <math id="A3.SS7.p4.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\bar{\bm{\Delta}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mover accent="true"><mi>𝚫</mi><mo>¯</mo></mover><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\bar{\bm{\Delta}}</annotation></semantics></math> denotes the sub-block-level vector derived from <math id="A3.SS7.p4.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\bm{\Delta}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>𝚫</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\bm{\Delta}</annotation></semantics></math>.
By the definition of <math id="A3.SS7.p4.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="J" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>J</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">J</annotation></semantics></math>, the uniform convergence in (<a href="#A3.E135" title="In Proof of Lemma . ‣ C.7 Proof of Lemma ‣ Appendix C Proof for Inverse Transform Watermarks in Section ‣ Optimal Detection for Language Watermarks with Pseudorandom Collision" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">135</span></a>) is equivalent to the uniform convergence of the moment-generating function term:</span></p>
<table id="A3.EGx98" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A3.Ex213"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A3.Ex213.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\lim_{|{{\mathcal{W}}}|\to\infty}\sup_{\Delta\leq\bm{\Delta}\leq 1-\delta}\sup_{\bm{P}_{{\mathcal{V}}}\in{\mathcal{Q}}_{\tau,\bm{\Delta}}}\left|\EB_{1,\bm{P}_{{\mathcal{V}}}}\big[\exp(-h(\bm{Y}))\big]-\mathcal{L}_{\bar{\bm{\Delta}}}(\exp(-h))\right|=0," display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><munder><mo movablelimits="false">lim</mo><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒲</mi><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">∞</mi></mrow></munder><mrow><munder><mo lspace="0.167em" movablelimits="false" rspace="0.0835em">sup</mo><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo>≤</mo><mi>𝚫</mi><mo>≤</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mi>δ</mi></mrow></mrow></munder><mrow><munder><mo lspace="0.0835em" movablelimits="false" rspace="0em">sup</mo><mrow><msub><mi>𝑷</mi><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒱</mi></msub><mo>∈</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒬</mi><mrow><mi>τ</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>𝚫</mi></mrow></msub></mrow></munder><mrow><mo>|</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>𝔼</mi><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>𝐏</mi><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒱</mi></msub></mrow></msub><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">[</mo><mrow><mi>exp</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>h</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝐘</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">]</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℒ</mi><mover accent="true"><mi>𝚫</mi><mo>¯</mo></mover></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>exp</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mo>−</mo><mi>h</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>|</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\lim_{|{{\mathcal{W}}}|\to\infty}\sup_{\Delta\leq\bm{\Delta}\leq 1-\delta}\sup_{\bm{P}_{{\mathcal{V}}}\in{\mathcal{Q}}_{\tau,\bm{\Delta}}}\left|\EB_{1,\bm{P}_{{\mathcal{V}}}}\big[\exp(-h(\bm{Y}))\big]-\mathcal{L}_{\bar{\bm{\Delta}}}(\exp(-h))\right|=0,</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A3.SS7.p4.5" class="ltx_p"><span id="A3.SS7.p4.5.1" class="ltx_text">which is precisely (<a href="#A3.E135" title="In Proof of Lemma . ‣ C.7 Proof of Lemma ‣ Appendix C Proof for Inverse Transform Watermarks in Section ‣ Optimal Detection for Language Watermarks with Pseudorandom Collision" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">135</span></a>).
Since <math id="A3.SS7.p4.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{L}_{\bar{\bm{\Delta}}}(\exp(-h))=\EB_{f_{\bm{{\bar{\Delta}}}}}[\exp(-h(\bm{Y}))]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℒ</mi><mover accent="true"><mi>𝚫</mi><mo>¯</mo></mover></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>exp</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mo>−</mo><mi>h</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><msub><mi>𝔼</mi><msub><mi>f</mi><mover accent="true"><mi>𝚫</mi><mo>¯</mo></mover></msub></msub><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><mi>exp</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>h</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝐘</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{L}_{\bar{\bm{\Delta}}}(\exp(-h))=\EB_{f_{\bm{{\bar{\Delta}}}}}[\exp(-h(\bm{Y}))]</annotation></semantics></math> (by the equivalence in Corollary <a href="#A3.Thmcor2" title="Corollary C.2 (Asymptotic distribution under 𝐻_1). ‣ Proof of Lemma . ‣ C.1 Proof of Lemma ‣ Appendix C Proof for Inverse Transform Watermarks in Section ‣ Optimal Detection for Language Watermarks with Pseudorandom Collision" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">C.2</span></a>), and the supremum is a nonexpansive operator (see Lemma <a href="#A3.Thmlem8" title="Lemma C.8. ‣ C.10 Auxiliary Lemmas ‣ Appendix C Proof for Inverse Transform Watermarks in Section ‣ Optimal Detection for Language Watermarks with Pseudorandom Collision" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">C.8</span></a>), we prove step (b).
∎</span></p>
</div>
</div>
</section>
<section id="A3.SS8" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection">C.8 </span>Proof of Lemma <a href="#S7.Thmlem8" title="Lemma 7.8. ‣ 7.2 Proof of Theorem ‣ 7 Proof of Main Results ‣ Optimal Detection for Language Watermarks with Pseudorandom Collision" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">7.8</span></a></h3>

<div id="A3.SS8.2" class="ltx_proof">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_font_italic ltx_title_proof">Proof of Lemma <a href="#S7.Thmlem8" title="Lemma 7.8. ‣ 7.2 Proof of Theorem ‣ 7 Proof of Main Results ‣ Optimal Detection for Language Watermarks with Pseudorandom Collision" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">7.8</span></a>.</h6>
<div id="A3.SS8.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A3.SS8.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A3.SS8.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text">Since we focus on a single block <math id="A3.SS8.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="{\mathcal{V}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒱</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\mathcal{V}}</annotation></semantics></math>, we write <math id="A3.SS8.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\Delta" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Delta</annotation></semantics></math> instead of <math id="A3.SS8.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\Delta_{{\mathcal{V}}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒱</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Delta_{{\mathcal{V}}}</annotation></semantics></math> for simplicity. In this lemma, the alternative PDF is evaluated at the homogeneous regularity-level vector <math id="A3.SS8.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(\Delta,\ldots,\Delta)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(\Delta,\ldots,\Delta)</annotation></semantics></math> and therefore depends only on the single parameter <math id="A3.SS8.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\Delta" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Delta</annotation></semantics></math>.
For simplicity, we write</span></p>
<table id="A3.Ex214" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A3.Ex214.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="f_{1,\Delta}:=f_{(\Delta,\ldots,\Delta)}," display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>f</mi><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi></mrow></msub><mo>:=</mo><msub><mi>f</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msub></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">f_{1,\Delta}:=f_{(\Delta,\ldots,\Delta)},</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A3.SS8.p1.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="A3.SS8.p1.2.1" class="ltx_text">to emphasize its dependence on the single parameter <math id="A3.SS8.p1.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\Delta" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Delta</annotation></semantics></math>.
For brevity, we define the truncated log-likelihood ratio as</span></p>
<table id="A3.EGx99" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A3.E136"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A3.E136.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle h_{\mathrm{opt},M}(\bm{y}):=\Biggl[\log\frac{f_{1,\Delta}(\bm{y})}{f_{0}(\bm{y})}\Biggr]_{[-M,M]}," display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>h</mi><mrow><mi>opt</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>M</mi></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝒚</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>:=</mo><msub><mrow><mo maxsize="2.600em" minsize="2.600em">[</mo><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><msub><mi>f</mi><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝒚</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mrow><msub><mi>f</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝒚</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mfrac></mstyle></mrow><mo maxsize="2.600em" minsize="2.600em">]</mo></mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><mrow><mo>−</mo><mi>M</mi></mrow><mo>,</mo><mi>M</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></msub></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle h_{\mathrm{opt},M}(\bm{y}):=\Biggl[\log\frac{f_{1,\Delta}(\bm{y})}{f_{0}(\bm{y})}\Biggr]_{[-M,M]},</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(136)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A3.SS8.p1.3" class="ltx_p"><span id="A3.SS8.p1.3.1" class="ltx_text">where <math id="A3.SS8.p1.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="[\,\cdot\,]_{[-M,M]}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mo>⋅</mo><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><mrow><mo>−</mo><mi>M</mi></mrow><mo>,</mo><mi>M</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">[\,\cdot\,]_{[-M,M]}</annotation></semantics></math> denotes truncation to the interval <math id="A3.SS8.p1.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="[-M,M]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><mrow><mo>−</mo><mi>M</mi></mrow><mo>,</mo><mi>M</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">[-M,M]</annotation></semantics></math>.</span></p>
</div>
<div id="A3.Thmlem4" class="ltx_theorem ltx_theorem_lem">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_title_theorem"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_theorem"><span id="A3.Thmlem4.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Lemma C.4</span></span><span id="A3.Thmlem4.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold"> </span>(Properties of the alternative PDF)<span id="A3.Thmlem4.4" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">.</span></h6>
<div id="A3.Thmlem4.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A3.Thmlem4.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A3.Thmlem4.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">Let <math id="A3.Thmlem4.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="f_{\bm{{\bar{\Delta}}}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>f</mi><mover accent="true"><mi>𝚫</mi><mo>¯</mo></mover></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">f_{\bm{{\bar{\Delta}}}}</annotation></semantics></math> denote the joint alternative PDF of the pivotal statistic
vector <math id="A3.Thmlem4.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\bm{Y}=(Y_{1},\ldots,Y_{m})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>𝐘</mi><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>Y</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>Y</mi><mi>m</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\bm{Y}=(Y_{1},\ldots,Y_{m})</annotation></semantics></math> under <math id="A3.Thmlem4.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="H_{1}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>H</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">H_{1}</annotation></semantics></math>, where the regularity levels are
<math id="A3.Thmlem4.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\bm{{\bar{\Delta}}}=({\bar{\Delta}}_{1},\ldots,{\bar{\Delta}}_{m})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mover accent="true"><mi>𝚫</mi><mo>¯</mo></mover><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo>¯</mo></mover><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo>¯</mo></mover><mi>m</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\bm{{\bar{\Delta}}}=({\bar{\Delta}}_{1},\ldots,{\bar{\Delta}}_{m})</annotation></semantics></math>.
Its explicit form is given in Theorem <a href="#S5.Thmtheorem1" title="Theorem 5.1 (Asymptotic joint distribution of pivotal statistics). ‣ 5.1 Asymptotic Distributions ‣ 5 Application to the Inverse Transform Watermark ‣ Optimal Detection for Language Watermarks with Pseudorandom Collision" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">5.1</span></a>.
Then, under Assumption <a href="#S5.Thmasmp1" title="Assumption 5.1 (Asymptotic NTP conditions). ‣ 5.1 Asymptotic Distributions ‣ 5 Application to the Inverse Transform Watermark ‣ Optimal Detection for Language Watermarks with Pseudorandom Collision" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">5.1</span></a>,</span></p>
<ul id="A3.I2" class="ltx_itemize">
<li id="A3.I2.i1" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">•</span> 
<div id="A3.I2.i1.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A3.I2.i1.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><math id="A3.I2.i1.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="f_{\bm{{\bar{\Delta}}}}(\bm{y})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>f</mi><mover accent="true"><mi>𝚫</mi><mo>¯</mo></mover></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝒚</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">f_{\bm{{\bar{\Delta}}}}(\bm{y})</annotation></semantics></math><span id="A3.I2.i1.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic"> is strictly positive for </span><math id="A3.I2.i1.p1.m2" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\bm{y}\in\prod_{\ell=1}^{m}[0,1-{\bar{\Delta}}_{\ell})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>𝒚</mi><mo rspace="0.111em">∈</mo><msubsup><mo rspace="0em">∏</mo><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>m</mi></msubsup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo>¯</mo></mover><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\bm{y}\in\prod_{\ell=1}^{m}[0,1-{\bar{\Delta}}_{\ell})</annotation></semantics></math><span id="A3.I2.i1.p1.1.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">, and equals </span><math id="A3.I2.i1.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mn>0</mn><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">0</annotation></semantics></math><span id="A3.I2.i1.p1.1.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic"> on the complement set </span><math id="A3.I2.i1.p1.m4" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="[0,1]^{m}\setminus\prod_{\ell=1}^{m}[0,1-{\bar{\Delta}}_{\ell})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>1</mn><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow><mi>m</mi></msup><mo rspace="0.055em">∖</mo><msubsup><mo rspace="0em">∏</mo><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>m</mi></msubsup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo>¯</mo></mover><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">[0,1]^{m}\setminus\prod_{\ell=1}^{m}[0,1-{\bar{\Delta}}_{\ell})</annotation></semantics></math><span id="A3.I2.i1.p1.1.4" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">.</span></p>
</div></li>
<li id="A3.I2.i2" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">•</span> 
<div id="A3.I2.i2.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A3.I2.i2.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A3.I2.i2.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">The mapping </span><math id="A3.I2.i2.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(\bm{y},\bm{{\bar{\Delta}}})\mapsto f_{\bm{{\bar{\Delta}}}}(\bm{y})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝒚</mi><mo>,</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>𝚫</mi><mo>¯</mo></mover><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo stretchy="false">↦</mo><mrow><msub><mi>f</mi><mover accent="true"><mi>𝚫</mi><mo>¯</mo></mover></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝒚</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(\bm{y},\bm{{\bar{\Delta}}})\mapsto f_{\bm{{\bar{\Delta}}}}(\bm{y})</annotation></semantics></math><span id="A3.I2.i2.p1.1.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">
is Lipschitz continuous on its domain
</span><math id="A3.I2.i2.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="[0,1]^{m}\times[0,1-\delta]^{m}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow><mi>m</mi></msup><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">×</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mi>δ</mi></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow><mi>m</mi></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">[0,1]^{m}\times[0,1-\delta]^{m}</annotation></semantics></math><span id="A3.I2.i2.p1.1.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">.
That is, there exists a universal constant </span><math id="A3.I2.i2.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="C&gt;0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>C</mi><mo>&gt;</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">C&gt;0</annotation></semantics></math><span id="A3.I2.i2.p1.1.4" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic"> such that for any
</span><math id="A3.I2.i2.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(\bm{y},\bm{{\bar{\Delta}}}),(\bm{y}^{\prime},\bm{{\bar{\Delta}}}^{\prime})\in[0,1]^{m}\times[0,1-\delta]^{m}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝒚</mi><mo>,</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>𝚫</mi><mo>¯</mo></mover><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>,</mo><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>𝒚</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo>,</mo><msup><mover accent="true"><mi>𝚫</mi><mo>¯</mo></mover><mo>′</mo></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>∈</mo><mrow><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo rspace="0.055em" stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow><mi>m</mi></msup><mo rspace="0.222em">×</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mi>δ</mi></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow><mi>m</mi></msup></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(\bm{y},\bm{{\bar{\Delta}}}),(\bm{y}^{\prime},\bm{{\bar{\Delta}}}^{\prime})\in[0,1]^{m}\times[0,1-\delta]^{m}</annotation></semantics></math><span id="A3.I2.i2.p1.1.5" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">,</span></p>
<table id="A3.Ex215" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A3.Ex215.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\big|f_{\bm{{\bar{\Delta}}}}(\bm{y})-f_{\bm{{\bar{\Delta}}}^{\prime}}(\bm{y}^{\prime})\big|\;\leq\;C\cdot\Big(\|\bm{y}-\bm{y}^{\prime}\|_{\infty}+\|\bm{{\bar{\Delta}}}-\bm{{\bar{\Delta}}}^{\prime}\|_{\infty}\Big)." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em" stretchy="true">|</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>f</mi><mover accent="true"><mi>𝚫</mi><mo>¯</mo></mover></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝒚</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><msub><mi>f</mi><msup><mover accent="true"><mi>𝚫</mi><mo>¯</mo></mover><mo>′</mo></msup></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>𝒚</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em" rspace="0.280em" stretchy="true">|</mo></mrow><mo rspace="0.558em">≤</mo><mrow><mi>C</mi><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="1.600em" minsize="1.600em">(</mo><mrow><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mrow><mi>𝒚</mi><mo>−</mo><msup><mi>𝒚</mi><mo>′</mo></msup></mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">∞</mi></msub><mo>+</mo><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mrow><mover accent="true"><mi>𝚫</mi><mo>¯</mo></mover><mo>−</mo><msup><mover accent="true"><mi>𝚫</mi><mo>¯</mo></mover><mo>′</mo></msup></mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">∞</mi></msub></mrow><mo maxsize="1.600em" minsize="1.600em">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\big|f_{\bm{{\bar{\Delta}}}}(\bm{y})-f_{\bm{{\bar{\Delta}}}^{\prime}}(\bm{y}^{\prime})\big|\;\leq\;C\cdot\Big(\|\bm{y}-\bm{y}^{\prime}\|_{\infty}+\|\bm{{\bar{\Delta}}}-\bm{{\bar{\Delta}}}^{\prime}\|_{\infty}\Big).</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div></li>
</ul>
</div>
</div>
<div id="A3.SS8.p2" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A3.SS8.p2.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A3.SS8.p2.1.1" class="ltx_text">Before proceeding with the proof, we first establish some properties of the PDF <math id="A3.SS8.p2.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="f_{1,\Delta}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>f</mi><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">f_{1,\Delta}</annotation></semantics></math>. The proof of this lemma is provided in Section <a href="#A3.SS9" title="C.9 Proof of Lemma ‣ Appendix C Proof for Inverse Transform Watermarks in Section ‣ Optimal Detection for Language Watermarks with Pseudorandom Collision" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">C.9</span></a>.</span></p>
</div>
<div id="A3.SS8.p3" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A3.SS8.p3.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A3.SS8.p3.1.1" class="ltx_text">With <math id="A3.SS8.p3.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="L^{\prime}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi>L</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">L^{\prime}</annotation></semantics></math> defined in (<a href="#S5.E23" title="In 5.2 Optimal Score Function ‣ 5 Application to the Inverse Transform Watermark ‣ Optimal Detection for Language Watermarks with Pseudorandom Collision" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">23</span></a>), we can decompose</span></p>
<table id="A3.EGx100" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A3.E137"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A3.E137.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle L^{\prime}(h_{\text{opt},M},\bm{{\bar{\Delta}}}^{\prime})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msup><mi>L</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>h</mi><mrow><mtext>opt</mtext><mo>,</mo><mi>M</mi></mrow></msub><mo>,</mo><msup><mover accent="true"><mi>𝚫</mi><mo>¯</mo></mover><mo>′</mo></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle L^{\prime}(h_{\text{opt},M},\bm{{\bar{\Delta}}}^{\prime})</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A3.E137.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=\underset{\text{(I)}}{\underbrace{\EB_{f_{0}}[h_{\text{opt},M}(\bm{Y})]}}+\underset{\text{(II)}}{\underbrace{\log\EB_{f_{\bm{{\bar{\Delta}}}^{\prime}}}[\exp(-h_{\text{opt},M}(\bm{Y}))]}}." display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><munder accentunder="true"><munder accentunder="true"><mrow><msub><mi>𝔼</mi><msub><mi>f</mi><mn>0</mn></msub></msub><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><msub><mi>h</mi><mrow><mtext>opt</mtext><mo>,</mo><mi>M</mi></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝐘</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="true">⏟</mo></munder><mtext mathsize="0.700em">(I)</mtext></munder><mo>+</mo><munder accentunder="true"><munder accentunder="true"><mrow><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><msub><mi>𝔼</mi><msub><mi>f</mi><msup><mover accent="true"><mi>𝚫</mi><mo>¯</mo></mover><mo>′</mo></msup></msub></msub></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><mi>exp</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><msub><mi>h</mi><mrow><mtext>opt</mtext><mo>,</mo><mi>M</mi></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝐘</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="true">⏟</mo></munder><mtext mathsize="0.700em">(II)</mtext></munder></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=\underset{\text{(I)}}{\underbrace{\EB_{f_{0}}[h_{\text{opt},M}(\bm{Y})]}}+\underset{\text{(II)}}{\underbrace{\log\EB_{f_{\bm{{\bar{\Delta}}}^{\prime}}}[\exp(-h_{\text{opt},M}(\bm{Y}))]}}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(137)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A3.SS8.p3.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="A3.SS8.p3.2.1" class="ltx_text">We then bound terms (I) and (II) separately.</span></p>
</div>
</div>
<section id="A3.SS8.SSS0.Px1" class="ltx_paragraph">
<h5 class="ltx_title ltx_title_paragraph">Analysis of Term (I).</h5>

<div id="A3.SS8.SSS0.Px1.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A3.SS8.SSS0.Px1.p1.1" class="ltx_p">By Lemma <a href="#A3.Thmlem4" title="Lemma C.4 (Properties of the alternative PDF). ‣ Proof of Lemma . ‣ C.8 Proof of Lemma ‣ Appendix C Proof for Inverse Transform Watermarks in Section ‣ Optimal Detection for Language Watermarks with Pseudorandom Collision" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">C.4</span></a>, <math id="A3.SS8.SSS0.Px1.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="f_{1,\Delta}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>f</mi><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">f_{1,\Delta}</annotation></semantics></math> is supported on <math id="A3.SS8.SSS0.Px1.p1.m2" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="[0,1-\Delta)^{m}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mi>m</mi></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">[0,1-\Delta)^{m}</annotation></semantics></math> and is Lipschitz continuous in <math id="A3.SS8.SSS0.Px1.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(\bm{y},\Delta)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝒚</mi><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(\bm{y},\Delta)</annotation></semantics></math>. Since <math id="A3.SS8.SSS0.Px1.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="f_{0}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>f</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">f_{0}</annotation></semantics></math> coincides with <math id="A3.SS8.SSS0.Px1.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="f_{1,\Delta}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>f</mi><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">f_{1,\Delta}</annotation></semantics></math> when <math id="A3.SS8.SSS0.Px1.p1.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\Delta=0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Delta=0</annotation></semantics></math> (see Corollary <a href="#A3.Thmcor2" title="Corollary C.2 (Asymptotic distribution under 𝐻_1). ‣ Proof of Lemma . ‣ C.1 Proof of Lemma ‣ Appendix C Proof for Inverse Transform Watermarks in Section ‣ Optimal Detection for Language Watermarks with Pseudorandom Collision" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">C.2</span></a> and Lemma <a href="#A3.Thmlem2" title="Lemma C.2 (Asymptotic distribution under 𝐻_0). ‣ Proof of Lemma . ‣ C.1 Proof of Lemma ‣ Appendix C Proof for Inverse Transform Watermarks in Section ‣ Optimal Detection for Language Watermarks with Pseudorandom Collision" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">C.2</span></a>), the null density <math id="A3.SS8.SSS0.Px1.p1.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="f_{0}(\bm{y})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>f</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝒚</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">f_{0}(\bm{y})</annotation></semantics></math> is continuous and strictly positive on <math id="A3.SS8.SSS0.Px1.p1.m8" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="[0,1)^{m}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>1</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mi>m</mi></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">[0,1)^{m}</annotation></semantics></math>. This ensures the existence of a finite upper bound for the following likelihood ratio:</p>
<table id="A3.Ex216" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A3.Ex216.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="M^{\prime}:=\sup_{\Delta^{\prime}\in[0,1]}\frac{\sup_{\bm{y}\in[0,1]^{m}}f_{1,\Delta^{\prime}}(\bm{y})}{\inf_{\bm{y}\in[0,1-\Delta)^{m}}f_{0}(\bm{y})}&lt;\infty." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msup><mi>M</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo rspace="0.1389em">:=</mo><mrow><munder><mo lspace="0.1389em" movablelimits="false" rspace="0.167em">sup</mo><mrow><msup><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow></munder><mfrac><mrow><msub><mo>sup</mo><mrow><mi>𝒚</mi><mo>∈</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow><mi>m</mi></msup></mrow></msub><mrow><msub><mi>f</mi><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>,</mo><msup><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo>′</mo></msup></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝒚</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mrow><mo rspace="0.167em">inf</mo><msub><mrow></mrow><mrow><mi>𝒚</mi><mo>∈</mo><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo><msup><mrow></mrow><mi>m</mi></msup></mrow></msub><mi>f</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mn>0</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝒚</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mfrac></mrow><mo>&lt;</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">∞</mi></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">M^{\prime}:=\sup_{\Delta^{\prime}\in[0,1]}\frac{\sup_{\bm{y}\in[0,1]^{m}}f_{1,\Delta^{\prime}}(\bm{y})}{\inf_{\bm{y}\in[0,1-\Delta)^{m}}f_{0}(\bm{y})}&lt;\infty.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A3.SS8.SSS0.Px1.p1.2" class="ltx_p">Importantly, <math id="A3.SS8.SSS0.Px1.p1.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="M^{\prime}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi>M</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">M^{\prime}</annotation></semantics></math> is independent of the clipping threshold <math id="A3.SS8.SSS0.Px1.p1.m10" class="ltx_Math" alttext="M" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>M</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">M</annotation></semantics></math>. When <math id="A3.SS8.SSS0.Px1.p1.m11" class="ltx_Math" alttext="M\geq|\log M^{\prime}|" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>M</mi><mo>≥</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><msup><mi>M</mi><mo>′</mo></msup></mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">M\geq|\log M^{\prime}|</annotation></semantics></math>, the log-likelihood ratio <math id="A3.SS8.SSS0.Px1.p1.m12" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\log\tfrac{f_{1,\Delta}(\bm{Y})}{f_{0}(\bm{Y})}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><mfrac><mrow><msub><mi>f</mi><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝒀</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mrow><msub><mi>f</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝒀</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mfrac></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\log\tfrac{f_{1,\Delta}(\bm{Y})}{f_{0}(\bm{Y})}</annotation></semantics></math> never exceeds <math id="A3.SS8.SSS0.Px1.p1.m13" class="ltx_Math" alttext="M" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>M</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">M</annotation></semantics></math>, so the score function <math id="A3.SS8.SSS0.Px1.p1.m14" class="ltx_Math" alttext="h_{\text{opt},M}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>h</mi><mrow><mtext>opt</mtext><mo>,</mo><mi>M</mi></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">h_{\text{opt},M}</annotation></semantics></math> can only be clipped at <math id="A3.SS8.SSS0.Px1.p1.m15" class="ltx_Math" alttext="-M" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo>−</mo><mi>M</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">-M</annotation></semantics></math>, which occurs when <math id="A3.SS8.SSS0.Px1.p1.m16" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\bm{Y}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>𝒀</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\bm{Y}</annotation></semantics></math> lies outside the support of <math id="A3.SS8.SSS0.Px1.p1.m17" class="ltx_Math" alttext="f_{\bm{{\bar{\Delta}}}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>f</mi><mover accent="true"><mi>𝚫</mi><mo>¯</mo></mover></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">f_{\bm{{\bar{\Delta}}}}</annotation></semantics></math>, that is, outside <math id="A3.SS8.SSS0.Px1.p1.m18" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="[0,1-\Delta)^{m}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mi>m</mi></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">[0,1-\Delta)^{m}</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>
<table id="A3.EGx101" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A3.Ex217"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A3.Ex217.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\EB_{f_{0}}[h_{\text{opt},M}(\bm{Y})]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>𝔼</mi><msub><mi>f</mi><mn>0</mn></msub></msub><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><msub><mi>h</mi><mrow><mtext>opt</mtext><mo>,</mo><mi>M</mi></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝐘</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\EB_{f_{0}}[h_{\text{opt},M}(\bm{Y})]</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A3.Ex217.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=\EB_{f_{0}}\left[\log\frac{f_{1,\Delta}(\bm{Y})}{f_{0}(\bm{Y})}\right]_{[-M,M]}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><msub><mi>𝔼</mi><msub><mi>f</mi><mn>0</mn></msub></msub><mo>⁡</mo><msub><mrow><mo>[</mo><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><msub><mi>f</mi><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝐘</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mrow><msub><mi>f</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝐘</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mfrac></mstyle></mrow><mo>]</mo></mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><mrow><mo>−</mo><mi>M</mi></mrow><mo>,</mo><mi>M</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></msub></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=\EB_{f_{0}}\left[\log\frac{f_{1,\Delta}(\bm{Y})}{f_{0}(\bm{Y})}\right]_{[-M,M]}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A3.Ex218"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A3.Ex218.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\displaystyle=\int_{[0,1-\Delta)^{m}}\left[\log\frac{f_{1,\Delta}(\bm{y})}{f_{0}(\bm{y})}\right]_{[-M,M]}f_{0}(\bm{y})\,{\mathrm{d}}\bm{y}+\int_{[0,1]^{m}\setminus[0,1-\Delta)^{m}}(-M)f_{0}(\bm{y})\,{\mathrm{d}}\bm{y}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo>=</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><msub><mo>∫</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo><msup><mrow></mrow><mi>m</mi></msup></mrow></msub></mstyle><msub><mrow><mo>[</mo><mi>log</mi><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><msub><mi>f</mi><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝒚</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mrow><msub><mi>f</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝒚</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mfrac></mstyle><mo>]</mo></mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><mrow><mo>−</mo><mi>M</mi></mrow><mo>,</mo><mi>M</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></msub><msub><mi>f</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝒚</mi><mo rspace="0.170em" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mi>d</mi><mi>𝒚</mi><mo>+</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><msub><mo>∫</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>1</mn><mo stretchy="false">]</mo><msup><mrow></mrow><mi>m</mi></msup><mo>∖</mo><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo><msup><mrow></mrow><mi>m</mi></msup></mrow></msub></mstyle><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mo lspace="0em">−</mo><mi>M</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><msub><mi>f</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝒚</mi><mo rspace="0.170em" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mi>d</mi><mi>𝒚</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=\int_{[0,1-\Delta)^{m}}\left[\log\frac{f_{1,\Delta}(\bm{y})}{f_{0}(\bm{y})}\right]_{[-M,M]}f_{0}(\bm{y})\,{\mathrm{d}}\bm{y}+\int_{[0,1]^{m}\setminus[0,1-\Delta)^{m}}(-M)f_{0}(\bm{y})\,{\mathrm{d}}\bm{y}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A3.Ex219"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A3.Ex219.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\displaystyle\leq\int_{[0,1-\Delta)^{m}}(\log M^{\prime})\cdot f_{0}(\bm{y})\,{\mathrm{d}}\bm{y}-M\cdot{\mathbb{P}}_{f_{0}}(\bm{Y}\notin[0,1-\Delta)^{m})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo>≤</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><msub><mo>∫</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo><msup><mrow></mrow><mi>m</mi></msup></mrow></msub></mstyle><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>log</mi><msup><mi>M</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo rspace="0.055em" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><msub><mi>f</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝒚</mi><mo rspace="0.170em" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mi>d</mi><mi>𝒚</mi><mo>−</mo><mi>M</mi><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><msub><mi>ℙ</mi><msub><mi>f</mi><mn>0</mn></msub></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝒀</mi><mo>∉</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mi>m</mi></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\leq\int_{[0,1-\Delta)^{m}}(\log M^{\prime})\cdot f_{0}(\bm{y})\,{\mathrm{d}}\bm{y}-M\cdot{\mathbb{P}}_{f_{0}}(\bm{Y}\notin[0,1-\Delta)^{m})</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A3.E138"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A3.E138.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\displaystyle\leq(\log M^{\prime})\cdot{\mathbb{P}}_{f_{0}}(\bm{Y}\in[0,1-\Delta)^{m})-M\cdot\bigl(1-{\mathbb{P}}_{f_{0}}(\bm{Y}\in[0,1-\Delta)^{m})\bigr)." display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo>≤</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>log</mi><msup><mi>M</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo rspace="0.055em" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><msub><mi>ℙ</mi><msub><mi>f</mi><mn>0</mn></msub></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝒀</mi><mo>∈</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mi>m</mi></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>−</mo><mi>M</mi><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">(</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>ℙ</mi><msub><mi>f</mi><mn>0</mn></msub></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝒀</mi><mo>∈</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mi>m</mi></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\leq(\log M^{\prime})\cdot{\mathbb{P}}_{f_{0}}(\bm{Y}\in[0,1-\Delta)^{m})-M\cdot\bigl(1-{\mathbb{P}}_{f_{0}}(\bm{Y}\in[0,1-\Delta)^{m})\bigr).</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(138)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A3.SS8.SSS0.Px1.p1.3" class="ltx_p">Although the probability <math id="A3.SS8.SSS0.Px1.p1.m19" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="{\mathbb{P}}_{f_{0}}(\bm{Y}\in[0,1-\Delta)^{m})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>ℙ</mi><msub><mi>f</mi><mn>0</mn></msub></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝒀</mi><mo>∈</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mi>m</mi></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\mathbb{P}}_{f_{0}}(\bm{Y}\in[0,1-\Delta)^{m})</annotation></semantics></math> depends on the shape of <math id="A3.SS8.SSS0.Px1.p1.m20" class="ltx_Math" alttext="f_{0}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>f</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">f_{0}</annotation></semantics></math>, it is bounded away from both <math id="A3.SS8.SSS0.Px1.p1.m21" class="ltx_Math" alttext="0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mn>0</mn><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">0</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="A3.SS8.SSS0.Px1.p1.m22" class="ltx_Math" alttext="1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mn>1</mn><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">1</annotation></semantics></math> when <math id="A3.SS8.SSS0.Px1.p1.m23" class="ltx_Math" alttext="0&lt;\Delta&lt;1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mn>0</mn><mo>&lt;</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo>&lt;</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">0&lt;\Delta&lt;1</annotation></semantics></math>. Hence, there exist positive constants <math id="A3.SS8.SSS0.Px1.p1.m24" class="ltx_Math" alttext="c" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>c</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">c</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="A3.SS8.SSS0.Px1.p1.m25" class="ltx_Math" alttext="C" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>C</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">C</annotation></semantics></math> such that</p>
<table id="A3.EGx102" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A3.E139"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A3.E139.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\EB_{f_{0}}[h_{\text{opt},M}(\bm{Y})]\leq-Mc+C," display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>𝔼</mi><msub><mi>f</mi><mn>0</mn></msub></msub><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><msub><mi>h</mi><mrow><mtext>opt</mtext><mo>,</mo><mi>M</mi></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝐘</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>≤</mo><mrow><mrow><mo>−</mo><mi>Mc</mi></mrow><mo>+</mo><mi>C</mi></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\EB_{f_{0}}[h_{\text{opt},M}(\bm{Y})]\leq-Mc+C,</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(139)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A3.SS8.SSS0.Px1.p1.4" class="ltx_p">where <math id="A3.SS8.SSS0.Px1.p1.m26" class="ltx_Math" alttext="c" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>c</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">c</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="A3.SS8.SSS0.Px1.p1.m27" class="ltx_Math" alttext="C" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>C</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">C</annotation></semantics></math> depend only on the fixed <math id="A3.SS8.SSS0.Px1.p1.m28" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\Delta" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Delta</annotation></semantics></math> used to define the score function <math id="A3.SS8.SSS0.Px1.p1.m29" class="ltx_Math" alttext="h_{\text{opt},M}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>h</mi><mrow><mtext>opt</mtext><mo>,</mo><mi>M</mi></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">h_{\text{opt},M}</annotation></semantics></math>, but are independent of <math id="A3.SS8.SSS0.Px1.p1.m30" class="ltx_Math" alttext="M" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>M</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">M</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="A3.SS8.SSS0.Px1.p1.m31" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\bm{\Delta}^{\prime}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi>𝚫</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\bm{\Delta}^{\prime}</annotation></semantics></math>, the latter introduced in (II).</p>
</div>
</section>
<section id="A3.SS8.SSS0.Px2" class="ltx_paragraph">
<h5 class="ltx_title ltx_title_paragraph">Analysis of Term (II).</h5>

<div id="A3.SS8.SSS0.Px2.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A3.SS8.SSS0.Px2.p1.1" class="ltx_p">We now analyze term (II), which takes the form of an integral over <math id="A3.SS8.SSS0.Px2.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="[0,1]^{m}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow><mi>m</mi></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">[0,1]^{m}</annotation></semantics></math></p>
<table id="A3.EGx103" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A3.Ex220"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A3.Ex220.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\EB_{f_{\bar{\bm{\Delta}}^{\prime}}}[\exp(-h_{\text{opt},M}(\bm{Y}))]=\int_{[0,1]^{m}}\exp\left(-\left[\log\frac{f_{\bm{{\bar{\Delta}}}}(\bm{y})}{f_{0}(\bm{y})}\right]_{[-M,M]}\right)f_{\bar{\bm{\Delta}}^{\prime}}(\bm{y})\,{\mathrm{d}}\bm{y}," display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>𝔼</mi><msub><mi>f</mi><msup><mover accent="true"><mi>𝚫</mi><mo>¯</mo></mover><mo>′</mo></msup></msub></msub><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><mi>exp</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><msub><mi>h</mi><mrow><mtext>opt</mtext><mo>,</mo><mi>M</mi></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝐘</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><msub><mo>∫</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow><mi>m</mi></msup></msub></mstyle><mrow><mrow><mi>exp</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mo>−</mo><msub><mrow><mo>[</mo><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><msub><mi>f</mi><mover accent="true"><mi>𝚫</mi><mo>¯</mo></mover></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝐲</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mrow><msub><mi>f</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝐲</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mfrac></mstyle></mrow><mo>]</mo></mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><mrow><mo>−</mo><mi>M</mi></mrow><mo>,</mo><mi>M</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></msub></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>f</mi><msup><mover accent="true"><mi>𝚫</mi><mo>¯</mo></mover><mo>′</mo></msup></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝐲</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0.170em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo rspace="0em">𝑑</mo><mi>𝐲</mi></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\EB_{f_{\bar{\bm{\Delta}}^{\prime}}}[\exp(-h_{\text{opt},M}(\bm{Y}))]=\int_{[0,1]^{m}}\exp\left(-\left[\log\frac{f_{\bm{{\bar{\Delta}}}}(\bm{y})}{f_{0}(\bm{y})}\right]_{[-M,M]}\right)f_{\bar{\bm{\Delta}}^{\prime}}(\bm{y})\,{\mathrm{d}}\bm{y},</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A3.SS8.SSS0.Px2.p1.2" class="ltx_p">where <math id="A3.SS8.SSS0.Px2.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\bar{\bm{\Delta}}=(\Delta,\ldots,\Delta)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mover accent="true"><mi>𝚫</mi><mo>¯</mo></mover><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\bar{\bm{\Delta}}=(\Delta,\ldots,\Delta)</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="A3.SS8.SSS0.Px2.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\bar{\bm{\Delta}}^{\prime}=(\Delta_{1}^{\prime},\ldots,\Delta_{m}^{\prime})\in{\mathbb{R}}^{m}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msup><mover accent="true"><mi>𝚫</mi><mo>¯</mo></mover><mo>′</mo></msup><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msubsup><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mn>1</mn><mo>′</mo></msubsup><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi><mo>,</mo><msubsup><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mi>m</mi><mo>′</mo></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>∈</mo><msup><mi>ℝ</mi><mi>m</mi></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\bar{\bm{\Delta}}^{\prime}=(\Delta_{1}^{\prime},\ldots,\Delta_{m}^{\prime})\in{\mathbb{R}}^{m}</annotation></semantics></math>.
By Lemma <a href="#A3.Thmlem4" title="Lemma C.4 (Properties of the alternative PDF). ‣ Proof of Lemma . ‣ C.8 Proof of Lemma ‣ Appendix C Proof for Inverse Transform Watermarks in Section ‣ Optimal Detection for Language Watermarks with Pseudorandom Collision" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">C.4</span></a>, the PDF <math id="A3.SS8.SSS0.Px2.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="f_{\bar{\bm{\Delta}}^{\prime}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>f</mi><msup><mover accent="true"><mi>𝚫</mi><mo>¯</mo></mover><mo>′</mo></msup></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">f_{\bar{\bm{\Delta}}^{\prime}}</annotation></semantics></math> vanishes outside the set <math id="A3.SS8.SSS0.Px2.p1.m5" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\prod_{\ell=1}^{m}[0,1-\Delta_{\ell}^{\prime})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msubsup><mo>∏</mo><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>m</mi></msubsup><mrow><mo lspace="0em" stretchy="false">[</mo><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><msubsup><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mo>′</mo></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\prod_{\ell=1}^{m}[0,1-\Delta_{\ell}^{\prime})</annotation></semantics></math>. Hence, the domain of integration can be restricted to this support without altering the integral:</p>
<table id="A3.EGx104" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A3.Ex221"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A3.Ex221.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\displaystyle\EB_{f_{\bar{\bm{\Delta}}^{\prime}}}[\exp(-h_{\text{opt},M}(\bm{Y}))]=\int_{\prod_{\ell=1}^{m}[0,1-\Delta^{\prime}_{\ell})}\exp\left(-\left[\log\frac{f_{\bm{{\bar{\Delta}}}}(\bm{y})}{f_{0}(\bm{y})}\right]_{[-M,M]}\right)f_{\bar{\bm{\Delta}}^{\prime}}(\bm{y})\,{\mathrm{d}}\bm{y}." display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>𝔼</mi><msub><mi>f</mi><msup><mover accent="true"><mi>𝚫</mi><mo>¯</mo></mover><mo>′</mo></msup></msub></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mi>exp</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mo lspace="0em">−</mo><msub><mi>h</mi><mrow><mtext>opt</mtext><mo>,</mo><mi>M</mi></mrow></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝐘</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow><mo>=</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><msub><mo>∫</mo><mrow><mstyle scriptlevel="-1"><mo maxsize="0.700em" minsize="0.700em" stretchy="true">∏</mo></mstyle><msub><mrow></mrow><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><msup><mrow></mrow><mi>m</mi></msup><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><msup><mrow></mrow><mo>′</mo></msup><msub><mrow></mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msub></mstyle><mi>exp</mi><mrow><mo>(</mo><mo lspace="0em">−</mo><msub><mrow><mo>[</mo><mi>log</mi><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><msub><mi>f</mi><mover accent="true"><mi>𝚫</mi><mo>¯</mo></mover></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝐲</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mrow><msub><mi>f</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝐲</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mfrac></mstyle><mo>]</mo></mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><mrow><mo>−</mo><mi>M</mi></mrow><mo>,</mo><mi>M</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></msub><mo>)</mo></mrow><msub><mi>f</mi><msup><mover accent="true"><mi>𝚫</mi><mo>¯</mo></mover><mo>′</mo></msup></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝐲</mi><mo rspace="0.170em" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mi>d</mi><mi>𝐲</mi><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\EB_{f_{\bar{\bm{\Delta}}^{\prime}}}[\exp(-h_{\text{opt},M}(\bm{Y}))]=\int_{\prod_{\ell=1}^{m}[0,1-\Delta^{\prime}_{\ell})}\exp\left(-\left[\log\frac{f_{\bm{{\bar{\Delta}}}}(\bm{y})}{f_{0}(\bm{y})}\right]_{[-M,M]}\right)f_{\bar{\bm{\Delta}}^{\prime}}(\bm{y})\,{\mathrm{d}}\bm{y}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
<div id="A3.SS8.SSS0.Px2.p2" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A3.SS8.SSS0.Px2.p2.1" class="ltx_p">From the analysis of term (I), we know that <math id="A3.SS8.SSS0.Px2.p2.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\log\tfrac{f_{\bm{{\bar{\Delta}}}}(\bm{y})}{f_{0}(\bm{y})}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><mfrac><mrow><msub><mi>f</mi><mover accent="true"><mi>𝚫</mi><mo>¯</mo></mover></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝒚</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mrow><msub><mi>f</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝒚</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mfrac></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\log\tfrac{f_{\bm{{\bar{\Delta}}}}(\bm{y})}{f_{0}(\bm{y})}</annotation></semantics></math> never exceeds <math id="A3.SS8.SSS0.Px2.p2.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="M" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>M</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">M</annotation></semantics></math> once <math id="A3.SS8.SSS0.Px2.p2.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="M\geq|\log M^{\prime}|" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>M</mi><mo>≥</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><msup><mi>M</mi><mo>′</mo></msup></mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">M\geq|\log M^{\prime}|</annotation></semantics></math>. Therefore, the clipping interval <math id="A3.SS8.SSS0.Px2.p2.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="[-M,M]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><mrow><mo>−</mo><mi>M</mi></mrow><mo>,</mo><mi>M</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">[-M,M]</annotation></semantics></math> can safely be replaced by <math id="A3.SS8.SSS0.Px2.p2.m5" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="[-M,\infty)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mo lspace="0em">−</mo><mi>M</mi><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">∞</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">[-M,\infty)</annotation></semantics></math>. This yields</p>
<table id="A3.EGx105" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A3.Ex222"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A3.Ex222.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\EB_{f_{\bar{\bm{\Delta}}^{\prime}}}[\exp(-h_{\text{opt},M}(\bm{Y}))]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>𝔼</mi><msub><mi>f</mi><msup><mover accent="true"><mi>𝚫</mi><mo>¯</mo></mover><mo>′</mo></msup></msub></msub><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><mi>exp</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><msub><mi>h</mi><mrow><mtext>opt</mtext><mo>,</mo><mi>M</mi></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝐘</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\EB_{f_{\bar{\bm{\Delta}}^{\prime}}}[\exp(-h_{\text{opt},M}(\bm{Y}))]</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A3.Ex222.m2" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\displaystyle=\int_{\prod_{\ell=1}^{m}[0,1-\Delta^{\prime}_{\ell})}\exp\left(-\left[\log\frac{f_{\bm{{\bar{\Delta}}}}(\bm{y})}{f_{0}(\bm{y})}\right]_{[-M,\infty)}\right)f_{\bar{\bm{\Delta}}^{\prime}}(\bm{y})\,{\mathrm{d}}\bm{y}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo>=</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><msub><mo>∫</mo><mrow><mstyle scriptlevel="-1"><mo maxsize="0.700em" minsize="0.700em" stretchy="true">∏</mo></mstyle><msub><mrow></mrow><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><msup><mrow></mrow><mi>m</mi></msup><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><msup><mrow></mrow><mo>′</mo></msup><msub><mrow></mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msub></mstyle><mi>exp</mi><mrow><mo>(</mo><mo lspace="0em">−</mo><msub><mrow><mo>[</mo><mi>log</mi><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><msub><mi>f</mi><mover accent="true"><mi>𝚫</mi><mo>¯</mo></mover></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝒚</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mrow><msub><mi>f</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝒚</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mfrac></mstyle><mo>]</mo></mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mo lspace="0em">−</mo><mi>M</mi><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">∞</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msub><mo>)</mo></mrow><msub><mi>f</mi><msup><mover accent="true"><mi>𝚫</mi><mo>¯</mo></mover><mo>′</mo></msup></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝒚</mi><mo rspace="0.170em" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mi>d</mi><mi>𝒚</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=\int_{\prod_{\ell=1}^{m}[0,1-\Delta^{\prime}_{\ell})}\exp\left(-\left[\log\frac{f_{\bm{{\bar{\Delta}}}}(\bm{y})}{f_{0}(\bm{y})}\right]_{[-M,\infty)}\right)f_{\bar{\bm{\Delta}}^{\prime}}(\bm{y})\,{\mathrm{d}}\bm{y}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A3.Ex223"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A3.Ex223.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\displaystyle\overset{(a)}{\leq}\int_{\prod_{\ell=1}^{m}[0,1-\Delta^{\prime}_{\ell})}\exp\left(-\log\frac{f_{\bm{{\bar{\Delta}}}}(\bm{y})}{f_{0}(\bm{y})}\right)f_{\bar{\bm{\Delta}}^{\prime}}(\bm{y})\,{\mathrm{d}}\bm{y}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mover accent="true"><mo>≤</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="0.700em" minsize="0.700em">(</mo><mi mathsize="0.700em">a</mi><mo maxsize="0.700em" minsize="0.700em">)</mo></mrow></mover><mstyle displaystyle="true"><msub><mo>∫</mo><mrow><mstyle scriptlevel="-1"><mo maxsize="0.700em" minsize="0.700em" stretchy="true">∏</mo></mstyle><msub><mrow></mrow><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><msup><mrow></mrow><mi>m</mi></msup><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><msup><mrow></mrow><mo>′</mo></msup><msub><mrow></mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msub></mstyle><mi>exp</mi><mrow><mo>(</mo><mo lspace="0em">−</mo><mi>log</mi><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><msub><mi>f</mi><mover accent="true"><mi>𝚫</mi><mo>¯</mo></mover></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝒚</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mrow><msub><mi>f</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝒚</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mfrac></mstyle><mo>)</mo></mrow><msub><mi>f</mi><msup><mover accent="true"><mi>𝚫</mi><mo>¯</mo></mover><mo>′</mo></msup></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝒚</mi><mo rspace="0.170em" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mi>d</mi><mi>𝒚</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\overset{(a)}{\leq}\int_{\prod_{\ell=1}^{m}[0,1-\Delta^{\prime}_{\ell})}\exp\left(-\log\frac{f_{\bm{{\bar{\Delta}}}}(\bm{y})}{f_{0}(\bm{y})}\right)f_{\bar{\bm{\Delta}}^{\prime}}(\bm{y})\,{\mathrm{d}}\bm{y}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A3.Ex224"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A3.Ex224.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\displaystyle=\int_{\prod_{\ell=1}^{m}[0,1-\Delta^{\prime}_{\ell})}\frac{f_{\bar{\bm{\Delta}}^{\prime}}(\bm{y})}{f_{\bm{{\bar{\Delta}}}}(\bm{y})}f_{0}(\bm{y})\,{\mathrm{d}}\bm{y}," display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo>=</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><msub><mo>∫</mo><mrow><mstyle scriptlevel="-1"><mo maxsize="0.700em" minsize="0.700em" stretchy="true">∏</mo></mstyle><msub><mrow></mrow><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><msup><mrow></mrow><mi>m</mi></msup><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><msup><mrow></mrow><mo>′</mo></msup><msub><mrow></mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msub></mstyle><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><msub><mi>f</mi><msup><mover accent="true"><mi>𝚫</mi><mo>¯</mo></mover><mo>′</mo></msup></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝒚</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mrow><msub><mi>f</mi><mover accent="true"><mi>𝚫</mi><mo>¯</mo></mover></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝒚</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mfrac></mstyle><msub><mi>f</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝒚</mi><mo rspace="0.170em" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mi>d</mi><mi>𝒚</mi><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=\int_{\prod_{\ell=1}^{m}[0,1-\Delta^{\prime}_{\ell})}\frac{f_{\bar{\bm{\Delta}}^{\prime}}(\bm{y})}{f_{\bm{{\bar{\Delta}}}}(\bm{y})}f_{0}(\bm{y})\,{\mathrm{d}}\bm{y},</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A3.E140"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A3.E140.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\displaystyle\overset{(b)}{\leq}\int_{\prod_{\ell=1}^{m}[0,1-\Delta^{\prime}_{\ell})}f_{0}(\bm{y})\,{\mathrm{d}}\bm{y}\cdot R\leq R," display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mover accent="true"><mo>≤</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="0.700em" minsize="0.700em">(</mo><mi mathsize="0.700em">b</mi><mo maxsize="0.700em" minsize="0.700em">)</mo></mrow></mover><mstyle displaystyle="true"><msub><mo>∫</mo><mrow><mstyle scriptlevel="-1"><mo maxsize="0.700em" minsize="0.700em" stretchy="true">∏</mo></mstyle><msub><mrow></mrow><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><msup><mrow></mrow><mi>m</mi></msup><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><msup><mrow></mrow><mo>′</mo></msup><msub><mrow></mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msub></mstyle><msub><mi>f</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝒚</mi><mo rspace="0.170em" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mi>d</mi><mi>𝒚</mi><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><mi>R</mi><mo>≤</mo><mi>R</mi><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\overset{(b)}{\leq}\int_{\prod_{\ell=1}^{m}[0,1-\Delta^{\prime}_{\ell})}f_{0}(\bm{y})\,{\mathrm{d}}\bm{y}\cdot R\leq R,</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(140)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A3.SS8.SSS0.Px2.p2.2" class="ltx_p">where (a) holds because removing the lower clipping at <math id="A3.SS8.SSS0.Px2.p2.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="-M" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo>−</mo><mi>M</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">-M</annotation></semantics></math> can only increase the integral, and (b) follows from the uniform boundedness of <math id="A3.SS8.SSS0.Px2.p2.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\tfrac{f_{\bar{\bm{\Delta}}^{\prime}}(\bm{y})}{f_{\bm{{\bar{\Delta}}}}(\bm{y})}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mfrac><mrow><msub><mi>f</mi><msup><mover accent="true"><mi>𝚫</mi><mo>¯</mo></mover><mo>′</mo></msup></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝒚</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mrow><msub><mi>f</mi><mover accent="true"><mi>𝚫</mi><mo>¯</mo></mover></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝒚</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mfrac><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\tfrac{f_{\bar{\bm{\Delta}}^{\prime}}(\bm{y})}{f_{\bm{{\bar{\Delta}}}}(\bm{y})}</annotation></semantics></math> established in Lemma <a href="#A3.Thmlem5" title="Lemma C.5 (Uniformly bounded density ratio). ‣ Analysis of Term (II). ‣ C.8 Proof of Lemma ‣ Appendix C Proof for Inverse Transform Watermarks in Section ‣ Optimal Detection for Language Watermarks with Pseudorandom Collision" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">C.5</span></a>.</p>
</div>
<div id="A3.Thmlem5" class="ltx_theorem ltx_theorem_lem">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_title_theorem"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_theorem"><span id="A3.Thmlem5.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Lemma C.5</span></span><span id="A3.Thmlem5.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold"> </span>(Uniformly bounded density ratio)<span id="A3.Thmlem5.4" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">.</span></h6>
<div id="A3.Thmlem5.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A3.Thmlem5.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A3.Thmlem5.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">There exists a constant <math id="A3.Thmlem5.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="R&gt;0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>R</mi><mo>&gt;</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">R&gt;0</annotation></semantics></math>, independent of <math id="A3.Thmlem5.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="M" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>M</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">M</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="A3.Thmlem5.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\bm{{\bar{\Delta}}}^{\prime}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mover accent="true"><mi>𝚫</mi><mo>¯</mo></mover><mo>′</mo></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\bm{{\bar{\Delta}}}^{\prime}</annotation></semantics></math>, such that</span></p>
<table id="A3.Ex225" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A3.Ex225.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\sup_{\Delta\leq\bm{{\bar{\Delta}}}^{\prime}\leq 1-\delta}\;\sup_{\bm{y}\in\prod_{\ell=1}^{m}[0,1-\Delta^{\prime}_{\ell})}\left|\frac{f_{\bar{\bm{\Delta}}^{\prime}}(\bm{y})}{f_{\bm{{\bar{\Delta}}}}(\bm{y})}\right|\;\leq\;R." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo movablelimits="false" rspace="0.0835em">sup</mo><msub><mrow></mrow><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo>≤</mo><msup><mover accent="true"><mi>𝚫</mi><mo>¯</mo></mover><mo>′</mo></msup><mo>≤</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mi>δ</mi></mrow></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0.0835em" movablelimits="false" rspace="0em">sup</mo><msub><mrow></mrow><mrow><mi>𝒚</mi><mo>∈</mo><mstyle scriptlevel="-1"><mo maxsize="0.700em" minsize="0.700em" stretchy="true">∏</mo></mstyle><msub><mrow></mrow><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><msup><mrow></mrow><mi>m</mi></msup><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><msup><mrow></mrow><mo>′</mo></msup><msub><mrow></mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msub><mo fence="false" rspace="0.167em">|</mo><mfrac><mrow><msub><mi>f</mi><msup><mover accent="true"><mi>𝚫</mi><mo>¯</mo></mover><mo>′</mo></msup></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝒚</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mrow><msub><mi>f</mi><mover accent="true"><mi>𝚫</mi><mo>¯</mo></mover></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝒚</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mfrac><mo fence="false" rspace="0.169em">|</mo><mo rspace="0.558em">≤</mo><mi>R</mi><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\sup_{\Delta\leq\bm{{\bar{\Delta}}}^{\prime}\leq 1-\delta}\;\sup_{\bm{y}\in\prod_{\ell=1}^{m}[0,1-\Delta^{\prime}_{\ell})}\left|\frac{f_{\bar{\bm{\Delta}}^{\prime}}(\bm{y})}{f_{\bm{{\bar{\Delta}}}}(\bm{y})}\right|\;\leq\;R.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
</div>
<div id="A3.SS8.SSS0.Px2.p3" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A3.SS8.SSS0.Px2.p3.1" class="ltx_p">Combining (<a href="#A3.E137" title="In Proof of Lemma . ‣ C.8 Proof of Lemma ‣ Appendix C Proof for Inverse Transform Watermarks in Section ‣ Optimal Detection for Language Watermarks with Pseudorandom Collision" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">137</span></a>), (<a href="#A3.E139" title="In Analysis of Term (I). ‣ C.8 Proof of Lemma ‣ Appendix C Proof for Inverse Transform Watermarks in Section ‣ Optimal Detection for Language Watermarks with Pseudorandom Collision" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">139</span></a>), and (<a href="#A3.E140" title="In Analysis of Term (II). ‣ C.8 Proof of Lemma ‣ Appendix C Proof for Inverse Transform Watermarks in Section ‣ Optimal Detection for Language Watermarks with Pseudorandom Collision" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">140</span></a>), we conclude that there exist positive constants <math id="A3.SS8.SSS0.Px2.p3.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="c,C,R&gt;0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>c</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>C</mi><mo>,</mo><mrow><mi>R</mi><mo>&gt;</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">c,C,R&gt;0</annotation></semantics></math>, independent of <math id="A3.SS8.SSS0.Px2.p3.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\bm{{\bar{\Delta}}}^{\prime}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mover accent="true"><mi>𝚫</mi><mo>¯</mo></mover><mo>′</mo></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\bm{{\bar{\Delta}}}^{\prime}</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="A3.SS8.SSS0.Px2.p3.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="M" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>M</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">M</annotation></semantics></math>, such that</p>
<table id="A3.Ex226" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A3.Ex226.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="L^{\prime}(h_{\text{opt},M},\bm{{\bar{\Delta}}}^{\prime})\leq-Mc+(C+R)." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><msup><mi>L</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>h</mi><mrow><mtext>opt</mtext><mo>,</mo><mi>M</mi></mrow></msub><mo>,</mo><msup><mover accent="true"><mi>𝚫</mi><mo>¯</mo></mover><mo>′</mo></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>≤</mo><mrow><mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>M</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>c</mi></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>C</mi><mo>+</mo><mi>R</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">L^{\prime}(h_{\text{opt},M},\bm{{\bar{\Delta}}}^{\prime})\leq-Mc+(C+R).</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A3.SS8.SSS0.Px2.p3.2" class="ltx_p">Taking the supremum over <math id="A3.SS8.SSS0.Px2.p3.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\bm{{\bar{\Delta}}}^{\prime}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mover accent="true"><mi>𝚫</mi><mo>¯</mo></mover><mo>′</mo></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\bm{{\bar{\Delta}}}^{\prime}</annotation></semantics></math> and then letting <math id="A3.SS8.SSS0.Px2.p3.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="M\to\infty" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>M</mi><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">∞</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">M\to\infty</annotation></semantics></math> gives</p>
<table id="A3.Ex227" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A3.Ex227.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\liminf_{M\to\infty}\;\sup_{\Delta\leq\bm{{\bar{\Delta}}}^{\prime}\leq 1-\delta}L^{\prime}(h_{\text{opt},M},\bm{{\bar{\Delta}}}^{\prime})=-\infty." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><munder><mo movablelimits="false">lim inf</mo><mrow><mi>M</mi><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">∞</mi></mrow></munder><mrow><munder><mo lspace="0.447em" movablelimits="false" rspace="0.167em">sup</mo><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo>≤</mo><msup><mover accent="true"><mi>𝚫</mi><mo>¯</mo></mover><mo>′</mo></msup><mo>≤</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mi>δ</mi></mrow></mrow></munder><mrow><msup><mi>L</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>h</mi><mrow><mtext>opt</mtext><mo>,</mo><mi>M</mi></mrow></msub><mo>,</mo><msup><mover accent="true"><mi>𝚫</mi><mo>¯</mo></mover><mo>′</mo></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo>−</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">∞</mi></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\liminf_{M\to\infty}\;\sup_{\Delta\leq\bm{{\bar{\Delta}}}^{\prime}\leq 1-\delta}L^{\prime}(h_{\text{opt},M},\bm{{\bar{\Delta}}}^{\prime})=-\infty.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
<div id="A3.SS8.SSS0.Px2.p4" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A3.SS8.SSS0.Px2.p4.1" class="ltx_p">∎</p>
</div>
<div id="A3.SS8.SSS0.Px2.p5" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A3.SS8.SSS0.Px2.p5.1" class="ltx_p">Finally, we provide the proof of Lemma <a href="#A3.Thmlem5" title="Lemma C.5 (Uniformly bounded density ratio). ‣ Analysis of Term (II). ‣ C.8 Proof of Lemma ‣ Appendix C Proof for Inverse Transform Watermarks in Section ‣ Optimal Detection for Language Watermarks with Pseudorandom Collision" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">C.5</span></a> below.</p>
</div>
<div id="A3.SS8.SSS0.Px2.1" class="ltx_proof">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_font_italic ltx_title_proof">Proof of Lemma <a href="#A3.Thmlem5" title="Lemma C.5 (Uniformly bounded density ratio). ‣ Analysis of Term (II). ‣ C.8 Proof of Lemma ‣ Appendix C Proof for Inverse Transform Watermarks in Section ‣ Optimal Detection for Language Watermarks with Pseudorandom Collision" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">C.5</span></a>.</h6>
<div id="A3.SS8.SSS0.Px2.p6" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A3.SS8.SSS0.Px2.p6.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A3.SS8.SSS0.Px2.p6.1.1" class="ltx_text">Fix any <math id="A3.SS8.SSS0.Px2.p6.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\bm{y}=(y_{1},\ldots,y_{m})\in\prod_{\ell=1}^{m}[0,1-\Delta_{\ell}^{\prime})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>𝒚</mi><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>y</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>y</mi><mi>m</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo rspace="0.111em">∈</mo><msubsup><mo rspace="0em">∏</mo><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>m</mi></msubsup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><msubsup><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mo>′</mo></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\bm{y}=(y_{1},\ldots,y_{m})\in\prod_{\ell=1}^{m}[0,1-\Delta_{\ell}^{\prime})</annotation></semantics></math>.
Without loss of generality, assume <math id="A3.SS8.SSS0.Px2.p6.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="y_{1}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>y</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">y_{1}</annotation></semantics></math> is the largest coordinate of <math id="A3.SS8.SSS0.Px2.p6.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\bm{y}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>𝒚</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\bm{y}</annotation></semantics></math>.
By definition, we have <math id="A3.SS8.SSS0.Px2.p6.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="y_{1}&lt;1-\Delta_{1}^{\prime}\leq 1-\Delta" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>y</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>&lt;</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><msubsup><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mn>1</mn><mo>′</mo></msubsup></mrow><mo>≤</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">y_{1}&lt;1-\Delta_{1}^{\prime}\leq 1-\Delta</annotation></semantics></math>.
We then construct the auxiliary vector <math id="A3.SS8.SSS0.Px2.p6.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\bm{y}^{\prime}=(1-\Delta_{1}^{\prime},y_{2},\ldots,y_{m})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msup><mi>𝒚</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><msubsup><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mn>1</mn><mo>′</mo></msubsup></mrow><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>y</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>y</mi><mi>m</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\bm{y}^{\prime}=(1-\Delta_{1}^{\prime},y_{2},\ldots,y_{m})</annotation></semantics></math>, which differs from <math id="A3.SS8.SSS0.Px2.p6.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\bm{y}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>𝒚</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\bm{y}</annotation></semantics></math> only in its largest entry.
By the Lipschitz continuity in Lemma <a href="#A3.Thmlem4" title="Lemma C.4 (Properties of the alternative PDF). ‣ Proof of Lemma . ‣ C.8 Proof of Lemma ‣ Appendix C Proof for Inverse Transform Watermarks in Section ‣ Optimal Detection for Language Watermarks with Pseudorandom Collision" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">C.4</span></a>, we know <math id="A3.SS8.SSS0.Px2.p6.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="f_{\bar{\bm{\Delta}}^{\prime}}(\bm{y}^{\prime})=0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>f</mi><msup><mover accent="true"><mi>𝚫</mi><mo>¯</mo></mover><mo>′</mo></msup></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>𝒚</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">f_{\bar{\bm{\Delta}}^{\prime}}(\bm{y}^{\prime})=0</annotation></semantics></math>, and</span></p>
<table id="A3.E141" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A3.E141.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="|f_{\bar{\bm{\Delta}}^{\prime}}(\bm{y})|\leq|f_{\bar{\bm{\Delta}}^{\prime}}(\bm{y})-f_{\bar{\bm{\Delta}}^{\prime}}(\bm{y}^{\prime})|\leq C\cdot\|\bm{y}-\bm{y}^{\prime}\|\leq C\cdot\left(1-\Delta-\max_{\ell\in[m]}y_{\ell}\right)." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><mrow><msub><mi>f</mi><msup><mover accent="true"><mi>𝚫</mi><mo>¯</mo></mover><mo>′</mo></msup></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝒚</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow><mo>≤</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>f</mi><msup><mover accent="true"><mi>𝚫</mi><mo>¯</mo></mover><mo>′</mo></msup></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝒚</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><msub><mi>f</mi><msup><mover accent="true"><mi>𝚫</mi><mo>¯</mo></mover><mo>′</mo></msup></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>𝒚</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow><mo>≤</mo><mrow><mi>C</mi><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mrow><mi>𝒚</mi><mo>−</mo><msup><mi>𝒚</mi><mo>′</mo></msup></mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>≤</mo><mrow><mi>C</mi><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo>−</mo><mrow><munder><mi>max</mi><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mi>m</mi><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow></munder><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><msub><mi>y</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi></msub></mrow></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">|f_{\bar{\bm{\Delta}}^{\prime}}(\bm{y})|\leq|f_{\bar{\bm{\Delta}}^{\prime}}(\bm{y})-f_{\bar{\bm{\Delta}}^{\prime}}(\bm{y}^{\prime})|\leq C\cdot\|\bm{y}-\bm{y}^{\prime}\|\leq C\cdot\left(1-\Delta-\max_{\ell\in[m]}y_{\ell}\right).</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(141)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A3.SS8.SSS0.Px2.p6.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="A3.SS8.SSS0.Px2.p6.2.1" class="ltx_text">where the constant <math id="A3.SS8.SSS0.Px2.p6.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="C" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>C</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">C</annotation></semantics></math>, given in Lemma <a href="#A3.Thmlem4" title="Lemma C.4 (Properties of the alternative PDF). ‣ Proof of Lemma . ‣ C.8 Proof of Lemma ‣ Appendix C Proof for Inverse Transform Watermarks in Section ‣ Optimal Detection for Language Watermarks with Pseudorandom Collision" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">C.4</span></a>, is independent of <math id="A3.SS8.SSS0.Px2.p6.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="M" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>M</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">M</annotation></semantics></math> and of <math id="A3.SS8.SSS0.Px2.p6.m10" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\bm{{\bar{\Delta}}}^{\prime}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mover accent="true"><mi>𝚫</mi><mo>¯</mo></mover><mo>′</mo></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\bm{{\bar{\Delta}}}^{\prime}</annotation></semantics></math>.</span></p>
</div>
<div id="A3.SS8.SSS0.Px2.p7" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A3.SS8.SSS0.Px2.p7.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A3.SS8.SSS0.Px2.p7.1.1" class="ltx_text">On the other hand, Theorem <a href="#S5.Thmtheorem1" title="Theorem 5.1 (Asymptotic joint distribution of pivotal statistics). ‣ 5.1 Asymptotic Distributions ‣ 5 Application to the Inverse Transform Watermark ‣ Optimal Detection for Language Watermarks with Pseudorandom Collision" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">5.1</span></a> gives</span></p>
<table id="A3.EGx106" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A3.Ex228"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A3.Ex228.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle f_{\bm{{\bar{\Delta}}}}(\bm{y})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>f</mi><mover accent="true"><mi>𝚫</mi><mo>¯</mo></mover></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝒚</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle f_{\bm{{\bar{\Delta}}}}(\bm{y})</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A3.Ex228.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=I_{m}(\bm{{\bar{\Delta}}})^{-1}\sum_{\bm{\sigma}\in\{-1,1\}^{m}}\left(B_{\bm{\sigma}}^{\bm{{\bar{\Delta}}}}(\bm{y})-A_{\bm{\sigma}}^{\bm{{\bar{\Delta}}}}(\bm{y})\right)_{+}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><msub><mi>I</mi><mi>m</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>𝚫</mi><mo>¯</mo></mover><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munder><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>𝝈</mi><mo>∈</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mrow><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo>,</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow><mi>m</mi></msup></mrow></munder></mstyle><msub><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mrow><msubsup><mi>B</mi><mi>𝝈</mi><mover accent="true"><mi>𝚫</mi><mo>¯</mo></mover></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝒚</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>A</mi><mi>𝝈</mi><mover accent="true"><mi>𝚫</mi><mo>¯</mo></mover></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝒚</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow><mo>+</mo></msub></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=I_{m}(\bm{{\bar{\Delta}}})^{-1}\sum_{\bm{\sigma}\in\{-1,1\}^{m}}\left(B_{\bm{\sigma}}^{\bm{{\bar{\Delta}}}}(\bm{y})-A_{\bm{\sigma}}^{\bm{{\bar{\Delta}}}}(\bm{y})\right)_{+}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A3.E142"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A3.E142.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\overset{(a)}{\geq}\left(B_{\bm{\sigma}^{\prime}}^{\bm{{\bar{\Delta}}}^{\prime}}(\bm{y})-A_{\bm{\sigma}^{\prime}}^{\bm{{\bar{\Delta}}}}(\bm{y})\right)_{+}\overset{(b)}{=}1-\frac{\max_{\ell\in[m]}y_{\ell}}{1-\Delta}," display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mover accent="true"><mo>≥</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="0.700em" minsize="0.700em">(</mo><mi mathsize="0.700em">a</mi><mo maxsize="0.700em" minsize="0.700em">)</mo></mrow></mover><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mrow><msubsup><mi>B</mi><msup><mi>𝝈</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><msup><mover accent="true"><mi>𝚫</mi><mo>¯</mo></mover><mo>′</mo></msup></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝒚</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>A</mi><msup><mi>𝝈</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mover accent="true"><mi>𝚫</mi><mo>¯</mo></mover></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝒚</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow><mo>+</mo></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mover accent="true"><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="0.700em" minsize="0.700em">(</mo><mi mathsize="0.700em">b</mi><mo maxsize="0.700em" minsize="0.700em">)</mo></mrow></mover><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo>−</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><msub><mi>max</mi><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mi>m</mi><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><msub><mi>y</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi></msub></mrow><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi></mrow></mfrac></mstyle></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\overset{(a)}{\geq}\left(B_{\bm{\sigma}^{\prime}}^{\bm{{\bar{\Delta}}}^{\prime}}(\bm{y})-A_{\bm{\sigma}^{\prime}}^{\bm{{\bar{\Delta}}}}(\bm{y})\right)_{+}\overset{(b)}{=}1-\frac{\max_{\ell\in[m]}y_{\ell}}{1-\Delta},</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(142)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A3.SS8.SSS0.Px2.p7.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="A3.SS8.SSS0.Px2.p7.2.1" class="ltx_text">where (a) uses the fact that <math id="A3.SS8.SSS0.Px2.p7.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="I_{m}(\bm{{\bar{\Delta}}})\leq 1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>I</mi><mi>m</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>𝚫</mi><mo>¯</mo></mover><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>≤</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">I_{m}(\bm{{\bar{\Delta}}})\leq 1</annotation></semantics></math> (since it is a probability) and keeps only the term with <math id="A3.SS8.SSS0.Px2.p7.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\bm{\sigma}^{\prime}=(-1,\ldots,-1)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msup><mi>𝝈</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi><mo>,</mo><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\bm{\sigma}^{\prime}=(-1,\ldots,-1)</annotation></semantics></math>, while (b) follows directly from the definitions of <math id="A3.SS8.SSS0.Px2.p7.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="B_{\bm{\sigma}^{\prime}}^{\bm{{\bar{\Delta}}}}(\bm{y})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msubsup><mi>B</mi><msup><mi>𝝈</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mover accent="true"><mi>𝚫</mi><mo>¯</mo></mover></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝒚</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">B_{\bm{\sigma}^{\prime}}^{\bm{{\bar{\Delta}}}}(\bm{y})</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="A3.SS8.SSS0.Px2.p7.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="A_{\bm{\sigma}^{\prime}}^{\bm{{\bar{\Delta}}}}(\bm{y})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msubsup><mi>A</mi><msup><mi>𝝈</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mover accent="true"><mi>𝚫</mi><mo>¯</mo></mover></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝒚</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">A_{\bm{\sigma}^{\prime}}^{\bm{{\bar{\Delta}}}}(\bm{y})</annotation></semantics></math>.</span></p>
</div>
<div id="A3.SS8.SSS0.Px2.p8" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A3.SS8.SSS0.Px2.p8.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A3.SS8.SSS0.Px2.p8.1.1" class="ltx_text">Combining (<a href="#A3.E141" title="In Proof of Lemma . ‣ Analysis of Term (II). ‣ C.8 Proof of Lemma ‣ Appendix C Proof for Inverse Transform Watermarks in Section ‣ Optimal Detection for Language Watermarks with Pseudorandom Collision" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">141</span></a>) and (<a href="#A3.E142" title="In Proof of Lemma . ‣ Analysis of Term (II). ‣ C.8 Proof of Lemma ‣ Appendix C Proof for Inverse Transform Watermarks in Section ‣ Optimal Detection for Language Watermarks with Pseudorandom Collision" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">142</span></a>) completes the proof with <math id="A3.SS8.SSS0.Px2.p8.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="R=C" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>R</mi><mo>=</mo><mi>C</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">R=C</annotation></semantics></math>.
∎</span></p>
</div>
</div>
</section>
</section>
<section id="A3.SS9" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection">C.9 </span>Proof of Lemma <a href="#A3.Thmlem4" title="Lemma C.4 (Properties of the alternative PDF). ‣ Proof of Lemma . ‣ C.8 Proof of Lemma ‣ Appendix C Proof for Inverse Transform Watermarks in Section ‣ Optimal Detection for Language Watermarks with Pseudorandom Collision" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">C.4</span></a></h3>

<div id="A3.SS9.2" class="ltx_proof">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_font_italic ltx_title_proof">Proof of Lemma <a href="#A3.Thmlem4" title="Lemma C.4 (Properties of the alternative PDF). ‣ Proof of Lemma . ‣ C.8 Proof of Lemma ‣ Appendix C Proof for Inverse Transform Watermarks in Section ‣ Optimal Detection for Language Watermarks with Pseudorandom Collision" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">C.4</span></a>.</h6>
<div id="A3.SS9.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A3.SS9.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A3.SS9.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text">From Theorem <a href="#S5.Thmtheorem1" title="Theorem 5.1 (Asymptotic joint distribution of pivotal statistics). ‣ 5.1 Asymptotic Distributions ‣ 5 Application to the Inverse Transform Watermark ‣ Optimal Detection for Language Watermarks with Pseudorandom Collision" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">5.1</span></a>, we know that</span></p>
<table id="A3.EGx107" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A3.E143"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A3.E143.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle f_{\bm{{\bar{\Delta}}}}(\bm{y})=\frac{1}{I_{m}(\bm{{\bar{\Delta}}})}\sum_{\bm{\sigma}\in\{-1,1\}^{m}}\left(B_{\bm{\sigma}}^{\bm{{\bar{\Delta}}}}(\bm{y})-A_{\bm{\sigma}}^{\bm{{\bar{\Delta}}}}(\bm{y})\right)_{+}," display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>f</mi><mover accent="true"><mi>𝚫</mi><mo>¯</mo></mover></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝒚</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mrow><msub><mi>I</mi><mi>m</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>𝚫</mi><mo>¯</mo></mover><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mfrac></mstyle><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munder><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>𝝈</mi><mo>∈</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mrow><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo>,</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow><mi>m</mi></msup></mrow></munder></mstyle><msub><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mrow><msubsup><mi>B</mi><mi>𝝈</mi><mover accent="true"><mi>𝚫</mi><mo>¯</mo></mover></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝒚</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>A</mi><mi>𝝈</mi><mover accent="true"><mi>𝚫</mi><mo>¯</mo></mover></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝒚</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow><mo>+</mo></msub></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle f_{\bm{{\bar{\Delta}}}}(\bm{y})=\frac{1}{I_{m}(\bm{{\bar{\Delta}}})}\sum_{\bm{\sigma}\in\{-1,1\}^{m}}\left(B_{\bm{\sigma}}^{\bm{{\bar{\Delta}}}}(\bm{y})-A_{\bm{\sigma}}^{\bm{{\bar{\Delta}}}}(\bm{y})\right)_{+},</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(143)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A3.SS9.p1.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="A3.SS9.p1.2.1" class="ltx_text">where for each sign vector <math id="A3.SS9.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\bm{\sigma}=(\sigma_{1},\ldots,\sigma_{m_{k}})\in\{-1,1\}^{m_{k}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>𝝈</mi><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>σ</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>σ</mi><msub><mi>m</mi><mi>k</mi></msub></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>∈</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mrow><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo>,</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow><msub><mi>m</mi><mi>k</mi></msub></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\bm{\sigma}=(\sigma_{1},\ldots,\sigma_{m_{k}})\in\{-1,1\}^{m_{k}}</annotation></semantics></math> and input <math id="A3.SS9.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\bm{y}=(y_{1},\ldots,y_{m})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>𝒚</mi><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>y</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>y</mi><mi>m</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\bm{y}=(y_{1},\ldots,y_{m})</annotation></semantics></math>,</span></p>
<table id="A3.EGx108" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A3.Ex229"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A3.Ex229.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle L_{\bm{\sigma}}(\bm{y})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>L</mi><mi>𝝈</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝒚</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle L_{\bm{\sigma}}(\bm{y})</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A3.Ex229.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle:=\max_{\ell\in[m]}(-\sigma_{\ell}y_{\ell})," display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><munder><mi>max</mi><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mi>m</mi><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow></munder><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><msub><mi>σ</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>y</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi></msub></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle:=\max_{\ell\in[m]}(-\sigma_{\ell}y_{\ell}),</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A3.Ex229.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle U_{\bm{\sigma}}(\bm{y})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>U</mi><mi>𝝈</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝒚</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle U_{\bm{\sigma}}(\bm{y})</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A3.Ex229.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle:=\min_{\ell\in[m]}(1-\sigma_{\ell}y_{\ell})," display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><munder><mi>min</mi><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mi>m</mi><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow></munder><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mrow><msub><mi>σ</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>y</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi></msub></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle:=\min_{\ell\in[m]}(1-\sigma_{\ell}y_{\ell}),</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A3.Ex230"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A3.Ex230.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle Y^{+}_{\bm{\sigma}}(\bm{y})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msubsup><mi>Y</mi><mi>𝝈</mi><mo>+</mo></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝒚</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle Y^{+}_{\bm{\sigma}}(\bm{y})</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A3.Ex230.m2" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\displaystyle:=\left(\max_{\ell:\sigma_{\ell}=1}\frac{{\bar{\Delta}}_{\ell}}{1-{\bar{\Delta}}_{\ell}}\cdot y_{\ell}\right)_{+}," display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo rspace="0em">:</mo><mo lspace="0em">=</mo><msub><mrow><mo>(</mo><munder><mi>max</mi><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mrow><msub><mi>σ</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mrow></munder><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><msub><mover accent="true"><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo>¯</mo></mover><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi></msub><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo>¯</mo></mover><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi></msub></mrow></mfrac></mstyle><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><msub><mi>y</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi></msub><mo>)</mo></mrow><mo>+</mo></msub><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle:=\left(\max_{\ell:\sigma_{\ell}=1}\frac{{\bar{\Delta}}_{\ell}}{1-{\bar{\Delta}}_{\ell}}\cdot y_{\ell}\right)_{+},</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A3.Ex230.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle Y^{-}_{\bm{\sigma}}(\bm{y})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msubsup><mi>Y</mi><mi>𝝈</mi><mo>−</mo></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝒚</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle Y^{-}_{\bm{\sigma}}(\bm{y})</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A3.Ex230.m4" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\displaystyle:=\left(\max_{\ell:\sigma_{\ell}=-1}\frac{{\bar{\Delta}}_{\ell}}{1-{\bar{\Delta}}_{\ell}}\cdot y_{\ell}\right)_{+}," display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo rspace="0em">:</mo><mo lspace="0em">=</mo><msub><mrow><mo>(</mo><munder><mi>max</mi><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mrow><msub><mi>σ</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mrow></mrow></munder><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><msub><mover accent="true"><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo>¯</mo></mover><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi></msub><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo>¯</mo></mover><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi></msub></mrow></mfrac></mstyle><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><msub><mi>y</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi></msub><mo>)</mo></mrow><mo>+</mo></msub><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle:=\left(\max_{\ell:\sigma_{\ell}=-1}\frac{{\bar{\Delta}}_{\ell}}{1-{\bar{\Delta}}_{\ell}}\cdot y_{\ell}\right)_{+},</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A3.Ex231"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A3.Ex231.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle A_{\bm{\sigma}}^{\bm{{\bar{\Delta}}}}(\bm{y})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msubsup><mi>A</mi><mi>𝝈</mi><mover accent="true"><mi>𝚫</mi><mo>¯</mo></mover></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝒚</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle A_{\bm{\sigma}}^{\bm{{\bar{\Delta}}}}(\bm{y})</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A3.Ex231.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle:=\max\left\{L_{\bm{\sigma}}(\bm{y}),\ Y^{+}_{\bm{\sigma}}(\bm{y})\right\}," display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>max</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>{</mo><mrow><msub><mi>L</mi><mi>𝝈</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝒚</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.667em">,</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>Y</mi><mi>𝝈</mi><mo>+</mo></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝒚</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>}</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle:=\max\left\{L_{\bm{\sigma}}(\bm{y}),\ Y^{+}_{\bm{\sigma}}(\bm{y})\right\},</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A3.Ex231.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle B_{\bm{\sigma}}^{\bm{{\bar{\Delta}}}}(\bm{y})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msubsup><mi>B</mi><mi>𝝈</mi><mover accent="true"><mi>𝚫</mi><mo>¯</mo></mover></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝒚</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle B_{\bm{\sigma}}^{\bm{{\bar{\Delta}}}}(\bm{y})</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A3.Ex231.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle:=\min\left\{U_{\bm{\sigma}}(\bm{y}),\ 1-Y^{-}_{\bm{\sigma}}(\bm{y})\right\}," display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>min</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>{</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>U</mi><mi>𝝈</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝒚</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo><mrow><mn> 1</mn><mo>−</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>Y</mi><mi>𝝈</mi><mo>−</mo></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝒚</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>}</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle:=\min\left\{U_{\bm{\sigma}}(\bm{y}),\ 1-Y^{-}_{\bm{\sigma}}(\bm{y})\right\},</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A3.SS9.p1.3" class="ltx_p"><span id="A3.SS9.p1.3.1" class="ltx_text">with <math id="A3.SS9.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(x)_{+}:=\max(x,0)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>+</mo></msub><mo>:=</mo><mrow><mi>max</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>,</mo><mn>0</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(x)_{+}:=\max(x,0)</annotation></semantics></math>, and the normalization constant <math id="A3.SS9.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="I_{m}(\bm{{\bar{\Delta}}}_{k})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>I</mi><mi>m</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>𝚫</mi><mo>¯</mo></mover><mi>k</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">I_{m}(\bm{{\bar{\Delta}}}_{k})</annotation></semantics></math> is given by</span></p>
<table id="A3.Ex232" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A3.Ex232.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="I_{m}(\bm{{\bar{\Delta}}}):=\int_{[0,1]^{m}}\left(\min_{\ell\in[m]}\{1-{\bar{\Delta}}_{k,\ell}+{\bar{\Delta}}_{k,\ell}x_{\ell}\}-\max_{\ell\in[m]}\{{\bar{\Delta}}_{k,\ell}x_{\ell}\}\right)_{+}{\mathrm{d}}x_{1}\cdots{\mathrm{d}}x_{m}." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>I</mi><mi>m</mi></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>𝚫</mi><mo>¯</mo></mover><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo rspace="0.111em">:=</mo><msub><mo rspace="0em">∫</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow><mi>m</mi></msup></msub><msub><mrow><mo>(</mo><munder><mi>min</mi><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mi>m</mi><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow></munder><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo>¯</mo></mover><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi></mrow></msub><mo>+</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo>¯</mo></mover><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi></mrow></msub><msub><mi>x</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow><mo>−</mo><munder><mi>max</mi><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mi>m</mi><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow></munder><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo>¯</mo></mover><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi></mrow></msub><msub><mi>x</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow><mo>+</mo></msub><mi>d</mi><msub><mi>x</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">⋯</mo><mi>d</mi><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>m</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">I_{m}(\bm{{\bar{\Delta}}}):=\int_{[0,1]^{m}}\left(\min_{\ell\in[m]}\{1-{\bar{\Delta}}_{k,\ell}+{\bar{\Delta}}_{k,\ell}x_{\ell}\}-\max_{\ell\in[m]}\{{\bar{\Delta}}_{k,\ell}x_{\ell}\}\right)_{+}{\mathrm{d}}x_{1}\cdots{\mathrm{d}}x_{m}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
</div>
<section id="A3.SS9.SSS0.Px1" class="ltx_paragraph">
<h5 class="ltx_title ltx_title_paragraph">Part 1: Support of <math id="A3.SS9.SSS0.Px1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="f_{\bm{{\bar{\Delta}}}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>f</mi><mover accent="true"><mi>𝚫</mi><mo>¯</mo></mover></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">f_{\bm{{\bar{\Delta}}}}</annotation></semantics></math>.</h5>

<div id="A3.SS9.SSS0.Px1.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A3.SS9.SSS0.Px1.p1.1" class="ltx_p">We first show that <math id="A3.SS9.SSS0.Px1.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="f_{\bm{{\bar{\Delta}}}}(\bm{y})=0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>f</mi><mover accent="true"><mi>𝚫</mi><mo>¯</mo></mover></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝒚</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">f_{\bm{{\bar{\Delta}}}}(\bm{y})=0</annotation></semantics></math> whenever <math id="A3.SS9.SSS0.Px1.p1.m2" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\bm{y}\notin\prod_{\ell=1}^{m}[0,1-{\bar{\Delta}}_{\ell})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>𝒚</mi><mo rspace="0.111em">∉</mo><msubsup><mo rspace="0em">∏</mo><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>m</mi></msubsup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo>¯</mo></mover><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\bm{y}\notin\prod_{\ell=1}^{m}[0,1-{\bar{\Delta}}_{\ell})</annotation></semantics></math>.
Take any <math id="A3.SS9.SSS0.Px1.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\bm{y}\in[0,1]^{m}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>𝒚</mi><mo>∈</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow><mi>m</mi></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\bm{y}\in[0,1]^{m}</annotation></semantics></math> with <math id="A3.SS9.SSS0.Px1.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="y_{\ell}\geq 1-{\bar{\Delta}}_{\ell}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>y</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi></msub><mo>≥</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo>¯</mo></mover><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi></msub></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">y_{\ell}\geq 1-{\bar{\Delta}}_{\ell}</annotation></semantics></math> for some index <math id="A3.SS9.SSS0.Px1.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\ell" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\ell</annotation></semantics></math>. Consider two cases depending on <math id="A3.SS9.SSS0.Px1.p1.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\sigma_{\ell}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>σ</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\sigma_{\ell}</annotation></semantics></math>:</p>
<ol id="A3.I3" class="ltx_enumerate">
<li id="A3.I3.i1" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">1.</span> 
<div id="A3.I3.i1.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A3.I3.i1.p1.1" class="ltx_p">If <math id="A3.I3.i1.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\sigma_{\ell}=1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>σ</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\sigma_{\ell}=1</annotation></semantics></math>, then</p>
<table id="A3.Ex233" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A3.Ex233.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="Y^{+}_{\bm{\sigma}}(\bm{y})\;\geq\;\tfrac{{\bar{\Delta}}_{\ell}}{1-{\bar{\Delta}}_{\ell}}(1-{\bar{\Delta}}_{\ell})={\bar{\Delta}}_{\ell},\quad U_{\bm{\sigma}}(\bm{y})\;\leq\;1-(1-{\bar{\Delta}}_{\ell})={\bar{\Delta}}_{\ell}." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mrow><msubsup><mi>Y</mi><mi>𝝈</mi><mo>+</mo></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝒚</mi><mo rspace="0.280em" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.558em">≥</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="false"><mfrac><msub><mover accent="true"><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo>¯</mo></mover><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi></msub><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo>¯</mo></mover><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi></msub></mrow></mfrac></mstyle><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo>¯</mo></mover><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo>¯</mo></mover><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi></msub></mrow><mo rspace="1.167em">,</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>U</mi><mi>𝝈</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝒚</mi><mo rspace="0.280em" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>≤</mo><mrow><mn> 1</mn><mo>−</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo>¯</mo></mover><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo>¯</mo></mover><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi></msub></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">Y^{+}_{\bm{\sigma}}(\bm{y})\;\geq\;\tfrac{{\bar{\Delta}}_{\ell}}{1-{\bar{\Delta}}_{\ell}}(1-{\bar{\Delta}}_{\ell})={\bar{\Delta}}_{\ell},\quad U_{\bm{\sigma}}(\bm{y})\;\leq\;1-(1-{\bar{\Delta}}_{\ell})={\bar{\Delta}}_{\ell}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A3.I3.i1.p1.2" class="ltx_p">Hence, <math id="A3.I3.i1.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="A_{\bm{\sigma}}^{\bm{{\bar{\Delta}}}}(\bm{y})\geq{\bar{\Delta}}_{\ell}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msubsup><mi>A</mi><mi>𝝈</mi><mover accent="true"><mi>𝚫</mi><mo>¯</mo></mover></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝒚</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>≥</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo>¯</mo></mover><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">A_{\bm{\sigma}}^{\bm{{\bar{\Delta}}}}(\bm{y})\geq{\bar{\Delta}}_{\ell}</annotation></semantics></math> and
<math id="A3.I3.i1.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="B_{\bm{\sigma}}^{\bm{{\bar{\Delta}}}}(\bm{y})\leq{\bar{\Delta}}_{\ell}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msubsup><mi>B</mi><mi>𝝈</mi><mover accent="true"><mi>𝚫</mi><mo>¯</mo></mover></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝒚</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>≤</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo>¯</mo></mover><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">B_{\bm{\sigma}}^{\bm{{\bar{\Delta}}}}(\bm{y})\leq{\bar{\Delta}}_{\ell}</annotation></semantics></math>, so that
<math id="A3.I3.i1.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(B_{\bm{\sigma}}^{\bm{{\bar{\Delta}}}}-A_{\bm{\sigma}}^{\bm{{\bar{\Delta}}}})_{+}=0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>B</mi><mi>𝝈</mi><mover accent="true"><mi>𝚫</mi><mo>¯</mo></mover></msubsup><mo>−</mo><msubsup><mi>A</mi><mi>𝝈</mi><mover accent="true"><mi>𝚫</mi><mo>¯</mo></mover></msubsup></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>+</mo></msub><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(B_{\bm{\sigma}}^{\bm{{\bar{\Delta}}}}-A_{\bm{\sigma}}^{\bm{{\bar{\Delta}}}})_{+}=0</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>
</div></li>
<li id="A3.I3.i2" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">2.</span> 
<div id="A3.I3.i2.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A3.I3.i2.p1.1" class="ltx_p">If <math id="A3.I3.i2.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\sigma_{\ell}=-1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>σ</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\sigma_{\ell}=-1</annotation></semantics></math>, then</p>
<table id="A3.Ex234" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A3.Ex234.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="Y^{-}_{\bm{\sigma}}(\bm{y})\;\geq\;\tfrac{{\bar{\Delta}}_{\ell}}{1-{\bar{\Delta}}_{\ell}}(1-{\bar{\Delta}}_{\ell})={\bar{\Delta}}_{\ell},\quad L_{\bm{\sigma}}(\bm{y})\;\geq\;1-{\bar{\Delta}}_{\ell}." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mrow><msubsup><mi>Y</mi><mi>𝝈</mi><mo>−</mo></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝒚</mi><mo rspace="0.280em" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.558em">≥</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="false"><mfrac><msub><mover accent="true"><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo>¯</mo></mover><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi></msub><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo>¯</mo></mover><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi></msub></mrow></mfrac></mstyle><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo>¯</mo></mover><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo>¯</mo></mover><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi></msub></mrow><mo rspace="1.167em">,</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>L</mi><mi>𝝈</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝒚</mi><mo rspace="0.280em" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>≥</mo><mrow><mn> 1</mn><mo>−</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo>¯</mo></mover><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi></msub></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">Y^{-}_{\bm{\sigma}}(\bm{y})\;\geq\;\tfrac{{\bar{\Delta}}_{\ell}}{1-{\bar{\Delta}}_{\ell}}(1-{\bar{\Delta}}_{\ell})={\bar{\Delta}}_{\ell},\quad L_{\bm{\sigma}}(\bm{y})\;\geq\;1-{\bar{\Delta}}_{\ell}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A3.I3.i2.p1.2" class="ltx_p">Consequently, <math id="A3.I3.i2.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="A_{\bm{\sigma}}^{\bm{{\bar{\Delta}}}}(\bm{y})\geq 1-{\bar{\Delta}}_{\ell}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msubsup><mi>A</mi><mi>𝝈</mi><mover accent="true"><mi>𝚫</mi><mo>¯</mo></mover></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝒚</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>≥</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo>¯</mo></mover><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi></msub></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">A_{\bm{\sigma}}^{\bm{{\bar{\Delta}}}}(\bm{y})\geq 1-{\bar{\Delta}}_{\ell}</annotation></semantics></math> while
<math id="A3.I3.i2.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="B_{\bm{\sigma}}^{\bm{{\bar{\Delta}}}}(\bm{y})\leq 1-{\bar{\Delta}}_{\ell}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msubsup><mi>B</mi><mi>𝝈</mi><mover accent="true"><mi>𝚫</mi><mo>¯</mo></mover></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝒚</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>≤</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo>¯</mo></mover><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi></msub></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">B_{\bm{\sigma}}^{\bm{{\bar{\Delta}}}}(\bm{y})\leq 1-{\bar{\Delta}}_{\ell}</annotation></semantics></math>, so again
<math id="A3.I3.i2.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(B_{\bm{\sigma}}^{\bm{{\bar{\Delta}}}}-A_{\bm{\sigma}}^{\bm{{\bar{\Delta}}}})_{+}=0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>B</mi><mi>𝝈</mi><mover accent="true"><mi>𝚫</mi><mo>¯</mo></mover></msubsup><mo>−</mo><msubsup><mi>A</mi><mi>𝝈</mi><mover accent="true"><mi>𝚫</mi><mo>¯</mo></mover></msubsup></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>+</mo></msub><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(B_{\bm{\sigma}}^{\bm{{\bar{\Delta}}}}-A_{\bm{\sigma}}^{\bm{{\bar{\Delta}}}})_{+}=0</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>
</div></li>
</ol>
<p id="A3.SS9.SSS0.Px1.p1.2" class="ltx_p">Since this holds for every <math id="A3.SS9.SSS0.Px1.p1.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\bm{\sigma}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>𝝈</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\bm{\sigma}</annotation></semantics></math>, the entire sum vanishes and <math id="A3.SS9.SSS0.Px1.p1.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="f_{\bm{{\bar{\Delta}}}}(\bm{y})=0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>f</mi><mover accent="true"><mi>𝚫</mi><mo>¯</mo></mover></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝒚</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">f_{\bm{{\bar{\Delta}}}}(\bm{y})=0</annotation></semantics></math>.
Thus the support is contained in <math id="A3.SS9.SSS0.Px1.p1.m9" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\prod_{\ell=1}^{m}[0,1-{\bar{\Delta}}_{\ell})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msubsup><mo>∏</mo><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>m</mi></msubsup><mrow><mo lspace="0em" stretchy="false">[</mo><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo>¯</mo></mover><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\prod_{\ell=1}^{m}[0,1-{\bar{\Delta}}_{\ell})</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>
</div>
<div id="A3.SS9.SSS0.Px1.p2" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A3.SS9.SSS0.Px1.p2.1" class="ltx_p">Conversely, let <math id="A3.SS9.SSS0.Px1.p2.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\bm{y}\in\prod_{\ell=1}^{m}[0,1-{\bar{\Delta}}_{\ell}-{\varepsilon}]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>𝒚</mi><mo rspace="0.111em">∈</mo><mrow><msubsup><mo rspace="0em">∏</mo><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>m</mi></msubsup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo>¯</mo></mover><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi></msub><mo>−</mo><mi>ε</mi></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\bm{y}\in\prod_{\ell=1}^{m}[0,1-{\bar{\Delta}}_{\ell}-{\varepsilon}]</annotation></semantics></math> for any small <math id="A3.SS9.SSS0.Px1.p2.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="{\varepsilon}&gt;0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>ε</mi><mo>&gt;</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\varepsilon}&gt;0</annotation></semantics></math>.
Take <math id="A3.SS9.SSS0.Px1.p2.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\bm{\sigma}=(1,\ldots,1)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>𝝈</mi><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi><mo>,</mo><mn>1</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\bm{\sigma}=(1,\ldots,1)</annotation></semantics></math>. Then</p>
<table id="A3.Ex235" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A3.Ex235.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="L_{\bm{\sigma}}(\bm{y})\leq 0,\quad U_{\bm{\sigma}}(\bm{y})\geq{\bar{\Delta}}_{\ell}+{\varepsilon}\ \text{for all }\ell,\quad Y^{-}_{\bm{\sigma}}(\bm{y})=0," display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>L</mi><mi>𝝈</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝒚</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>≤</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><mo rspace="1.167em">,</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>U</mi><mi>𝝈</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝒚</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>≥</mo><mrow><msub><mover accent="true"><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo>¯</mo></mover><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi></msub><mo>+</mo><mrow><mi>ε</mi><mo lspace="0.500em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mtext>for all </mtext><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="1.167em">,</mo><mrow><mrow><msubsup><mi>Y</mi><mi>𝝈</mi><mo>−</mo></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝒚</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">L_{\bm{\sigma}}(\bm{y})\leq 0,\quad U_{\bm{\sigma}}(\bm{y})\geq{\bar{\Delta}}_{\ell}+{\varepsilon}\ \text{for all }\ell,\quad Y^{-}_{\bm{\sigma}}(\bm{y})=0,</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A3.SS9.SSS0.Px1.p2.2" class="ltx_p">and</p>
<table id="A3.Ex236" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A3.Ex236.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="Y^{+}_{\bm{\sigma}}(\bm{y})\leq\max_{\ell}\tfrac{{\bar{\Delta}}_{\ell}}{1-{\bar{\Delta}}_{\ell}}(1-{\bar{\Delta}}_{\ell}-{\varepsilon})\leq\max_{\ell}{\bar{\Delta}}_{\ell}-\min_{\ell}\tfrac{{\bar{\Delta}}_{\ell}}{1-{\bar{\Delta}}_{\ell}}{\varepsilon}." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><msubsup><mi>Y</mi><mi>𝝈</mi><mo>+</mo></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝒚</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>≤</mo><mrow><mrow><munder><mi>max</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi></munder><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><mstyle displaystyle="false"><mfrac><msub><mover accent="true"><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo>¯</mo></mover><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi></msub><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo>¯</mo></mover><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi></msub></mrow></mfrac></mstyle></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo>¯</mo></mover><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi></msub><mo>−</mo><mi>ε</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>≤</mo><mrow><mrow><munder><mi>max</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi></munder><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo>¯</mo></mover><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi></msub></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mrow><munder><mi>min</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi></munder><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><mstyle displaystyle="false"><mfrac><msub><mover accent="true"><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo>¯</mo></mover><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi></msub><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo>¯</mo></mover><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi></msub></mrow></mfrac></mstyle></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>ε</mi></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">Y^{+}_{\bm{\sigma}}(\bm{y})\leq\max_{\ell}\tfrac{{\bar{\Delta}}_{\ell}}{1-{\bar{\Delta}}_{\ell}}(1-{\bar{\Delta}}_{\ell}-{\varepsilon})\leq\max_{\ell}{\bar{\Delta}}_{\ell}-\min_{\ell}\tfrac{{\bar{\Delta}}_{\ell}}{1-{\bar{\Delta}}_{\ell}}{\varepsilon}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A3.SS9.SSS0.Px1.p2.3" class="ltx_p">Hence,</p>
<table id="A3.Ex237" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A3.Ex237.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="A_{\bm{\sigma}}^{\bm{{\bar{\Delta}}}}(\bm{y})=Y^{+}_{\bm{\sigma}}(\bm{y})\leq\max_{\ell}{\bar{\Delta}}_{\ell}-\min_{\ell}\tfrac{{\bar{\Delta}}_{\ell}}{1-{\bar{\Delta}}_{\ell}}{\varepsilon},\quad B_{\bm{\sigma}}^{\bm{{\bar{\Delta}}}}(\bm{y})=U_{\bm{\sigma}}(\bm{y})\geq\max_{\ell}{\bar{\Delta}}_{\ell}+{\varepsilon}." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mrow><msubsup><mi>A</mi><mi>𝝈</mi><mover accent="true"><mi>𝚫</mi><mo>¯</mo></mover></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝒚</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>Y</mi><mi>𝝈</mi><mo>+</mo></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝒚</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>≤</mo><mrow><mrow><munder><mi>max</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi></munder><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo>¯</mo></mover><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi></msub></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mrow><munder><mi>min</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi></munder><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><mstyle displaystyle="false"><mfrac><msub><mover accent="true"><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo>¯</mo></mover><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi></msub><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo>¯</mo></mover><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi></msub></mrow></mfrac></mstyle></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>ε</mi></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="1.167em">,</mo><mrow><mrow><msubsup><mi>B</mi><mi>𝝈</mi><mover accent="true"><mi>𝚫</mi><mo>¯</mo></mover></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝒚</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><msub><mi>U</mi><mi>𝝈</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝒚</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>≥</mo><mrow><mrow><munder><mi>max</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi></munder><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo>¯</mo></mover><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi></msub></mrow><mo>+</mo><mi>ε</mi></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">A_{\bm{\sigma}}^{\bm{{\bar{\Delta}}}}(\bm{y})=Y^{+}_{\bm{\sigma}}(\bm{y})\leq\max_{\ell}{\bar{\Delta}}_{\ell}-\min_{\ell}\tfrac{{\bar{\Delta}}_{\ell}}{1-{\bar{\Delta}}_{\ell}}{\varepsilon},\quad B_{\bm{\sigma}}^{\bm{{\bar{\Delta}}}}(\bm{y})=U_{\bm{\sigma}}(\bm{y})\geq\max_{\ell}{\bar{\Delta}}_{\ell}+{\varepsilon}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A3.SS9.SSS0.Px1.p2.4" class="ltx_p">By Assumption <a href="#S5.Thmasmp1" title="Assumption 5.1 (Asymptotic NTP conditions). ‣ 5.1 Asymptotic Distributions ‣ 5 Application to the Inverse Transform Watermark ‣ Optimal Detection for Language Watermarks with Pseudorandom Collision" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">5.1</span></a>, <math id="A3.SS9.SSS0.Px1.p2.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="0&lt;{\bar{\Delta}}_{\ell}&lt;1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mn>0</mn><mo>&lt;</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo>¯</mo></mover><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi></msub><mo>&lt;</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">0&lt;{\bar{\Delta}}_{\ell}&lt;1</annotation></semantics></math>, so the gap</p>
<table id="A3.Ex238" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A3.Ex238.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="B_{\bm{\sigma}}^{\bm{{\bar{\Delta}}}}(\bm{y})-A_{\bm{\sigma}}^{\bm{{\bar{\Delta}}}}(\bm{y})\;\geq\;\frac{{\varepsilon}}{1-\max_{\ell}{\bar{\Delta}}_{\ell}}&gt;0." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mrow><msubsup><mi>B</mi><mi>𝝈</mi><mover accent="true"><mi>𝚫</mi><mo>¯</mo></mover></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝒚</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>A</mi><mi>𝝈</mi><mover accent="true"><mi>𝚫</mi><mo>¯</mo></mover></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝒚</mi><mo rspace="0.280em" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.558em">≥</mo><mfrac><mi>ε</mi><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mrow><msub><mi>max</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi></msub><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo>¯</mo></mover><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi></msub></mrow></mrow></mfrac><mo>&gt;</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">B_{\bm{\sigma}}^{\bm{{\bar{\Delta}}}}(\bm{y})-A_{\bm{\sigma}}^{\bm{{\bar{\Delta}}}}(\bm{y})\;\geq\;\frac{{\varepsilon}}{1-\max_{\ell}{\bar{\Delta}}_{\ell}}&gt;0.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A3.SS9.SSS0.Px1.p2.5" class="ltx_p">Thus, at least one term in the summation is strictly positive, and
<math id="A3.SS9.SSS0.Px1.p2.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="f_{\bm{{\bar{\Delta}}}}(\bm{y})&gt;0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>f</mi><mover accent="true"><mi>𝚫</mi><mo>¯</mo></mover></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝒚</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>&gt;</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">f_{\bm{{\bar{\Delta}}}}(\bm{y})&gt;0</annotation></semantics></math>.
This proves that <math id="A3.SS9.SSS0.Px1.p2.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="f_{\bm{{\bar{\Delta}}}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>f</mi><mover accent="true"><mi>𝚫</mi><mo>¯</mo></mover></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">f_{\bm{{\bar{\Delta}}}}</annotation></semantics></math> is strictly positive on
<math id="A3.SS9.SSS0.Px1.p2.m7" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\prod_{\ell=1}^{m}[0,1-{\bar{\Delta}}_{\ell})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msubsup><mo>∏</mo><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>m</mi></msubsup><mrow><mo lspace="0em" stretchy="false">[</mo><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo>¯</mo></mover><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\prod_{\ell=1}^{m}[0,1-{\bar{\Delta}}_{\ell})</annotation></semantics></math> and zero elsewhere.</p>
</div>
</section>
<section id="A3.SS9.SSS0.Px2" class="ltx_paragraph">
<h5 class="ltx_title ltx_title_paragraph">Part 2: Lipschitz continuity.</h5>

<div id="A3.SS9.SSS0.Px2.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A3.SS9.SSS0.Px2.p1.1" class="ltx_p">The joint density <math id="A3.SS9.SSS0.Px2.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="f_{\bm{{\bar{\Delta}}}}(\bm{y})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>f</mi><mover accent="true"><mi>𝚫</mi><mo>¯</mo></mover></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝒚</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">f_{\bm{{\bar{\Delta}}}}(\bm{y})</annotation></semantics></math> is uniformly continuous in
<math id="A3.SS9.SSS0.Px2.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(\bm{y},\bm{{\bar{\Delta}}})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝒚</mi><mo>,</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>𝚫</mi><mo>¯</mo></mover><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(\bm{y},\bm{{\bar{\Delta}}})</annotation></semantics></math> on <math id="A3.SS9.SSS0.Px2.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="[0,1]^{m}\times[0,1-\delta]^{m}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow><mi>m</mi></msup><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">×</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mi>δ</mi></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow><mi>m</mi></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">[0,1]^{m}\times[0,1-\delta]^{m}</annotation></semantics></math>, since it is given by a finite sum of continuous functions on a compact domain. To strengthen this to Lipschitz continuity, recall from Theorem <a href="#S5.Thmtheorem1" title="Theorem 5.1 (Asymptotic joint distribution of pivotal statistics). ‣ 5.1 Asymptotic Distributions ‣ 5 Application to the Inverse Transform Watermark ‣ Optimal Detection for Language Watermarks with Pseudorandom Collision" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">5.1</span></a> that each summand in the representation of <math id="A3.SS9.SSS0.Px2.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="f_{\bm{{\bar{\Delta}}}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>f</mi><mover accent="true"><mi>𝚫</mi><mo>¯</mo></mover></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">f_{\bm{{\bar{\Delta}}}}</annotation></semantics></math> is constructed from a finite combination of linear functions, maxima, minima, and positive-part operators. Each of these building blocks is Lipschitz continuous with constants depending only on <math id="A3.SS9.SSS0.Px2.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(m,\delta)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>m</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>δ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(m,\delta)</annotation></semantics></math>, and finite maxima/minima of Lipschitz functions remain Lipschitz with constants given by the maximum of the individual constants.</p>
</div>
<div id="A3.SS9.SSS0.Px2.p2" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A3.SS9.SSS0.Px2.p2.1" class="ltx_p">Therefore, every summand is Lipschitz continuous with respect to <math id="A3.SS9.SSS0.Px2.p2.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(\bm{y},\bm{{\bar{\Delta}}})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝒚</mi><mo>,</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>𝚫</mi><mo>¯</mo></mover><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(\bm{y},\bm{{\bar{\Delta}}})</annotation></semantics></math>, uniformly on the domain <math id="A3.SS9.SSS0.Px2.p2.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="[0,1]^{m}\times[0,1-\delta]^{m}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow><mi>m</mi></msup><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">×</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mi>δ</mi></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow><mi>m</mi></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">[0,1]^{m}\times[0,1-\delta]^{m}</annotation></semantics></math>. Since <math id="A3.SS9.SSS0.Px2.p2.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="f_{\bm{{\bar{\Delta}}}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>f</mi><mover accent="true"><mi>𝚫</mi><mo>¯</mo></mover></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">f_{\bm{{\bar{\Delta}}}}</annotation></semantics></math> is a finite sum of such summands, it follows that <math id="A3.SS9.SSS0.Px2.p2.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="f_{\bm{{\bar{\Delta}}}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>f</mi><mover accent="true"><mi>𝚫</mi><mo>¯</mo></mover></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">f_{\bm{{\bar{\Delta}}}}</annotation></semantics></math> itself is Lipschitz continuous, with a constant depending only on <math id="A3.SS9.SSS0.Px2.p2.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(m,\delta)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>m</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>δ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(m,\delta)</annotation></semantics></math>, but independent of <math id="A3.SS9.SSS0.Px2.p2.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(\bm{y},\bm{{\bar{\Delta}}})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝒚</mi><mo>,</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>𝚫</mi><mo>¯</mo></mover><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(\bm{y},\bm{{\bar{\Delta}}})</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>
</div>
<div id="A3.SS9.SSS0.Px2.p3" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A3.SS9.SSS0.Px2.p3.1" class="ltx_p">∎</p>
</div>
</section>
</section>
<section id="A3.SS10" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection">C.10 </span>Auxiliary Lemmas</h3>

<div id="A3.Thmlem6" class="ltx_theorem ltx_theorem_lem">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_title_theorem"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_theorem"><span id="A3.Thmlem6.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Lemma C.6</span></span><span id="A3.Thmlem6.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">.</span></h6>
<div id="A3.Thmlem6.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A3.Thmlem6.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A3.Thmlem6.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">Let</span></p>
<table id="A3.Ex239" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A3.Ex239.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="I_{m}(\Delta)=\int_{[0,1]^{m}}\bigl(1-\Delta-\Delta\,D(x_{1},\ldots,x_{m})\bigr)_{+}\,{\mathrm{d}}x_{1}\cdots{\mathrm{d}}x_{m},\quad D(x_{1},\ldots,x_{m})=\max_{1\leq i\leq m}x_{i}-\min_{1\leq i\leq m}x_{i}." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>I</mi><mi>m</mi></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo rspace="0.111em">=</mo><msub><mo rspace="0em">∫</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow><mi>m</mi></msup></msub><msub><mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">(</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo>−</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mi>D</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>m</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">)</mo></mrow><mo>+</mo></msub><mi>d</mi><msub><mi>x</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">⋯</mo><mi>d</mi><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>m</mi></msub><mo rspace="1.167em">,</mo><mi>D</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>m</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>=</mo><munder><mi>max</mi><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>≤</mo><mi>i</mi><mo>≤</mo><mi>m</mi></mrow></munder><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>−</mo><munder><mi>min</mi><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>≤</mo><mi>i</mi><mo>≤</mo><mi>m</mi></mrow></munder><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">I_{m}(\Delta)=\int_{[0,1]^{m}}\bigl(1-\Delta-\Delta\,D(x_{1},\ldots,x_{m})\bigr)_{+}\,{\mathrm{d}}x_{1}\cdots{\mathrm{d}}x_{m},\quad D(x_{1},\ldots,x_{m})=\max_{1\leq i\leq m}x_{i}-\min_{1\leq i\leq m}x_{i}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A3.Thmlem6.p1.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="A3.Thmlem6.p1.2.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">Then for <math id="A3.Thmlem6.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="0\leq\Delta&lt;1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mn>0</mn><mo>≤</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo>&lt;</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">0\leq\Delta&lt;1</annotation></semantics></math>, we have the closed form</span></p>
<table id="A3.Ex240" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A3.Ex240.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="I_{m}(\Delta)=\begin{cases}1-\dfrac{2m}{m+1}\,\Delta,&amp;0\leq\Delta\leq\tfrac{1}{2},\\[10.00002pt]
\displaystyle\left(\frac{1-\Delta}{\Delta}\right)^{m}\left[\,1-\frac{2m(1-\Delta)}{m+1}\right],&amp;\tfrac{1}{2}&lt;\Delta&lt;1.\end{cases}" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>I</mi><mi>m</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo>{</mo><mtable columnspacing="5pt" displaystyle="true" rowspacing="0pt"><mtr><mtd class="ltx_align_left" columnalign="left"><mrow><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mrow><mfrac><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>m</mi></mrow><mrow><mi>m</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mfrac><mo lspace="0.170em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow></mtd><mtd class="ltx_align_left" columnalign="left"><mrow><mrow><mn>0</mn><mo>≤</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo>≤</mo><mstyle displaystyle="false"><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mn>2</mn></mfrac></mstyle></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow></mtd></mtr><mtr><mtd class="ltx_align_left" columnalign="left"><mrow><mrow><msup><mrow><mo>(</mo><mfrac><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi></mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi></mfrac><mo>)</mo></mrow><mi>m</mi></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>[</mo><mrow><mn> 1</mn><mo>−</mo><mfrac><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>m</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mrow><mi>m</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mfrac></mrow><mo>]</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow></mtd><mtd class="ltx_align_left" columnalign="left"><mrow><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="false"><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mn>2</mn></mfrac></mstyle><mo>&lt;</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo>&lt;</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow></mtd></mtr></mtable></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">I_{m}(\Delta)=\begin{cases}1-\dfrac{2m}{m+1}\,\Delta,&amp;0\leq\Delta\leq\tfrac{1}{2},\\[10.00002pt]
\displaystyle\left(\frac{1-\Delta}{\Delta}\right)^{m}\left[\,1-\frac{2m(1-\Delta)}{m+1}\right],&amp;\tfrac{1}{2}&lt;\Delta&lt;1.\end{cases}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A3.Thmlem6.p1.3" class="ltx_p"><span id="A3.Thmlem6.p1.3.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">Moreover, <math id="A3.Thmlem6.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="I_{m}(\Delta)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>I</mi><mi>m</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">I_{m}(\Delta)</annotation></semantics></math> is uniformly continuous on <math id="A3.Thmlem6.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="[0,1-\delta]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mi>δ</mi></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">[0,1-\delta]</annotation></semantics></math> for any given <math id="A3.Thmlem6.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\delta\in(0,1)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>δ</mi><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>1</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\delta\in(0,1)</annotation></semantics></math>.</span></p>
</div>
</div>
<div id="A3.SS10.2" class="ltx_proof">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_font_italic ltx_title_proof">Proof of Lemma <a href="#A3.Thmlem6" title="Lemma C.6. ‣ C.10 Auxiliary Lemmas ‣ Appendix C Proof for Inverse Transform Watermarks in Section ‣ Optimal Detection for Language Watermarks with Pseudorandom Collision" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">C.6</span></a>.</h6>
<div id="A3.SS10.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A3.SS10.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A3.SS10.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text">Let <math id="A3.SS10.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="X_{1},\ldots,X_{m}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>X</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>X</mi><mi>m</mi></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">X_{1},\ldots,X_{m}</annotation></semantics></math> be i.i.d. <math id="A3.SS10.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathrm{Unif}(0,1)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>Unif</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>1</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathrm{Unif}(0,1)</annotation></semantics></math>. Then the target quantity can be expressed as <math id="A3.SS10.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="I_{m}(\Delta)=\EB\left[\left(1-\Delta-\Delta\,D\right)_{+}\right]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>I</mi><mi>m</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>𝔼</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>[</mo><msub><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo lspace="0.170em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>D</mi></mrow></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow><mo>+</mo></msub><mo>]</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">I_{m}(\Delta)=\EB\left[\left(1-\Delta-\Delta\,D\right)_{+}\right]</annotation></semantics></math>, where <math id="A3.SS10.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="D=\max_{i}X_{i}-\min_{i}X_{i}\in[0,1]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>D</mi><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>max</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><msub><mi>X</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><msub><mi>min</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><msub><mi>X</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></mrow></mrow><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">D=\max_{i}X_{i}-\min_{i}X_{i}\in[0,1]</annotation></semantics></math>. The density of <math id="A3.SS10.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="D" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>D</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">D</annotation></semantics></math> is given by <math id="A3.SS10.p1.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="f_{D}(r)=m(m-1)\,r^{m-2}(1-r)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>f</mi><mi>D</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>r</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>m</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>m</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0.170em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>r</mi><mrow><mi>m</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mi>r</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">f_{D}(r)=m(m-1)\,r^{m-2}(1-r)</annotation></semantics></math> for <math id="A3.SS10.p1.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="r\in[0,1]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>r</mi><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">r\in[0,1]</annotation></semantics></math>, as stated in formula (2.5.15) of <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_cite">[<a href="#bib.bib35" title="" class="ltx_ref">35</a>]</cite>.
Hence,</span></p>
<table id="A3.Ex241" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A3.Ex241.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="I_{m}(\Delta)=\int_{0}^{1}\left(1-\Delta-\Delta r\right)_{+}f_{D}(r)\,{\mathrm{d}}r=\int_{0}^{r_{0}}(1-\Delta-\Delta r)\,m(m-1)\,r^{m-2}(1-r)\,{\mathrm{d}}r," display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>I</mi><mi>m</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.111em">=</mo><mrow><msubsup><mo rspace="0em">∫</mo><mn>0</mn><mn>1</mn></msubsup><mrow><msub><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>r</mi></mrow></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow><mo>+</mo></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>f</mi><mi>D</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>r</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0.170em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo rspace="0em">𝑑</mo><mi>r</mi></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.111em">=</mo><mrow><msubsup><mo rspace="0em">∫</mo><mn>0</mn><msub><mi>r</mi><mn>0</mn></msub></msubsup><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>r</mi></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0.170em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>m</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>m</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0.170em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>r</mi><mrow><mi>m</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mi>r</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0.170em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo rspace="0em">𝑑</mo><mi>r</mi></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">I_{m}(\Delta)=\int_{0}^{1}\left(1-\Delta-\Delta r\right)_{+}f_{D}(r)\,{\mathrm{d}}r=\int_{0}^{r_{0}}(1-\Delta-\Delta r)\,m(m-1)\,r^{m-2}(1-r)\,{\mathrm{d}}r,</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A3.SS10.p1.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="A3.SS10.p1.2.1" class="ltx_text">where <math id="A3.SS10.p1.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="r_{0}=(1-\Delta)/\Delta" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>r</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>/</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">r_{0}=(1-\Delta)/\Delta</annotation></semantics></math>, since the integrand becomes zero for <math id="A3.SS10.p1.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="r&gt;r_{0}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>r</mi><mo>&gt;</mo><msub><mi>r</mi><mn>0</mn></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">r&gt;r_{0}</annotation></semantics></math>.</span></p>
</div>
<div id="A3.SS10.p2" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A3.SS10.p2.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A3.SS10.p2.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Case 1: <math id="A3.SS10.p2.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\Delta\leq\tfrac{1}{2}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo>≤</mo><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mn>2</mn></mfrac></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Delta\leq\tfrac{1}{2}</annotation></semantics></math>.</span> Then <math id="A3.SS10.p2.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="r_{0}\geq 1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>r</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo>≥</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">r_{0}\geq 1</annotation></semantics></math>, so the <math id="A3.SS10.p2.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(\cdot)_{+}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">⋅</mo><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>+</mo></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(\cdot)_{+}</annotation></semantics></math> operator has no effect over <math id="A3.SS10.p2.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="r\in[0,1]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>r</mi><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">r\in[0,1]</annotation></semantics></math>. Therefore,</p>
<table id="A3.Ex242" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A3.Ex242.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="I_{m}(\Delta)=\int_{0}^{1}\left((1-\Delta)-\Delta r\right)\,m(m-1)\,r^{m-2}(1-r)\,dr." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>I</mi><mi>m</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.111em">=</mo><mrow><msubsup><mo rspace="0em">∫</mo><mn>0</mn><mn>1</mn></msubsup><mrow><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>r</mi></mrow></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0.170em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>m</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>m</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0.170em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>r</mi><mrow><mi>m</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mi>r</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0.170em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo rspace="0em">𝑑</mo><mi>r</mi></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">I_{m}(\Delta)=\int_{0}^{1}\left((1-\Delta)-\Delta r\right)\,m(m-1)\,r^{m-2}(1-r)\,dr.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A3.SS10.p2.2" class="ltx_p">This evaluates to</p>
<table id="A3.Ex243" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A3.Ex243.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="I_{m}(\Delta)=(1-\Delta)-\Delta\cdot\frac{m-1}{m+1}=1-\frac{2m}{m+1}\,\Delta." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>I</mi><mi>m</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><mfrac><mrow><mi>m</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mrow><mi>m</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mfrac></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mrow><mfrac><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>m</mi></mrow><mrow><mi>m</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mfrac><mo lspace="0.170em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">I_{m}(\Delta)=(1-\Delta)-\Delta\cdot\frac{m-1}{m+1}=1-\frac{2m}{m+1}\,\Delta.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
<div id="A3.SS10.p3" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A3.SS10.p3.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A3.SS10.p3.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Case 2: <math id="A3.SS10.p3.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\Delta&gt;\tfrac{1}{2}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo>&gt;</mo><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mn>2</mn></mfrac></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Delta&gt;\tfrac{1}{2}</annotation></semantics></math>.</span> Then <math id="A3.SS10.p3.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="r_{0}&lt;1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>r</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo>&lt;</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">r_{0}&lt;1</annotation></semantics></math>, and the integral becomes</p>
<table id="A3.Ex244" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A3.Ex244.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="I_{m}(\Delta)=m(m-1)\int_{0}^{r_{0}}(1-\Delta-\Delta r)\,r^{m-2}(1-r)\,dr." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>I</mi><mi>m</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>m</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>m</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><msubsup><mo rspace="0em">∫</mo><mn>0</mn><msub><mi>r</mi><mn>0</mn></msub></msubsup><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>r</mi></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0.170em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>r</mi><mrow><mi>m</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mi>r</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0.170em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo rspace="0em">𝑑</mo><mi>r</mi></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">I_{m}(\Delta)=m(m-1)\int_{0}^{r_{0}}(1-\Delta-\Delta r)\,r^{m-2}(1-r)\,dr.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A3.SS10.p3.2" class="ltx_p">Let</p>
<table id="A3.Ex245" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A3.Ex245.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="A=\int_{0}^{r_{0}}r^{m-2}(1-r)\,dr=\frac{r_{0}^{m-1}}{m-1}-\frac{r_{0}^{m}}{m},\quad B=\int_{0}^{r_{0}}r^{m-1}(1-r)\,dr=\frac{r_{0}^{m}}{m}-\frac{r_{0}^{m+1}}{m+1}." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>A</mi><mo rspace="0.111em">=</mo><mrow><msubsup><mo>∫</mo><mn>0</mn><msub><mi>r</mi><mn>0</mn></msub></msubsup><mrow><msup><mi>r</mi><mrow><mi>m</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mi>r</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0.170em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo rspace="0em">𝑑</mo><mi>r</mi></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mfrac><msubsup><mi>r</mi><mn>0</mn><mrow><mi>m</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msubsup><mrow><mi>m</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mfrac><mo>−</mo><mfrac><msubsup><mi>r</mi><mn>0</mn><mi>m</mi></msubsup><mi>m</mi></mfrac></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="1.167em">,</mo><mrow><mi>B</mi><mo rspace="0.111em">=</mo><mrow><msubsup><mo>∫</mo><mn>0</mn><msub><mi>r</mi><mn>0</mn></msub></msubsup><mrow><msup><mi>r</mi><mrow><mi>m</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mi>r</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0.170em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo rspace="0em">𝑑</mo><mi>r</mi></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mfrac><msubsup><mi>r</mi><mn>0</mn><mi>m</mi></msubsup><mi>m</mi></mfrac><mo>−</mo><mfrac><msubsup><mi>r</mi><mn>0</mn><mrow><mi>m</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msubsup><mrow><mi>m</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mfrac></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">A=\int_{0}^{r_{0}}r^{m-2}(1-r)\,dr=\frac{r_{0}^{m-1}}{m-1}-\frac{r_{0}^{m}}{m},\quad B=\int_{0}^{r_{0}}r^{m-1}(1-r)\,dr=\frac{r_{0}^{m}}{m}-\frac{r_{0}^{m+1}}{m+1}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A3.SS10.p3.3" class="ltx_p">Then we have</p>
<table id="A3.Ex246" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A3.Ex246.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="I_{m}(\Delta)=m(m-1)\left[(1-\Delta)A-\Delta B\right]." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>I</mi><mi>m</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>m</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>m</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>[</mo><mrow><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>A</mi></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>B</mi></mrow></mrow><mo>]</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">I_{m}(\Delta)=m(m-1)\left[(1-\Delta)A-\Delta B\right].</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A3.SS10.p3.4" class="ltx_p">Substituting <math id="A3.SS10.p3.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="r_{0}=(1-\Delta)/\Delta" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>r</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>/</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">r_{0}=(1-\Delta)/\Delta</annotation></semantics></math> and simplifying gives</p>
<table id="A3.Ex247" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A3.Ex247.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="I_{m}(\Delta)=\left(\frac{1-\Delta}{\Delta}\right)^{m}\left[1-\frac{2m(1-\Delta)}{m+1}\right]." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>I</mi><mi>m</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><msup><mrow><mo>(</mo><mfrac><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi></mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi></mfrac><mo>)</mo></mrow><mi>m</mi></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>[</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mfrac><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>m</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mrow><mi>m</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mfrac></mrow><mo>]</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">I_{m}(\Delta)=\left(\frac{1-\Delta}{\Delta}\right)^{m}\left[1-\frac{2m(1-\Delta)}{m+1}\right].</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
<div id="A3.SS10.p4" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A3.SS10.p4.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A3.SS10.p4.1.1" class="ltx_text">The uniform continuity of <math id="A3.SS10.p4.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="I_{m}(\Delta)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>I</mi><mi>m</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">I_{m}(\Delta)</annotation></semantics></math> over <math id="A3.SS10.p4.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="[0,1-\delta]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mi>δ</mi></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">[0,1-\delta]</annotation></semantics></math> follows directly from the smoothness of the integrand and the compactness of the domain. This concludes the proof.
∎</span></p>
</div>
</div>
<div id="A3.Thmlem7" class="ltx_theorem ltx_theorem_lem">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_title_theorem"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_theorem"><span id="A3.Thmlem7.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Lemma C.7</span></span><span id="A3.Thmlem7.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold"> </span>(<cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_cite">[<a href="#bib.bib2" title="" class="ltx_ref">2</a>]</cite>, Theorem 2.1)<span id="A3.Thmlem7.4" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">.</span></h6>
<div id="A3.Thmlem7.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A3.Thmlem7.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A3.Thmlem7.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">Let <math id="A3.Thmlem7.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\{a_{i,j}\}_{1\leq i,j\leq|{{\mathcal{W}}}|}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><msub><mi>a</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow><mrow><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>≤</mo><mi>i</mi></mrow><mo>,</mo><mrow><mi>j</mi><mo>≤</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒲</mi><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\{a_{i,j}\}_{1\leq i,j\leq|{{\mathcal{W}}}|}</annotation></semantics></math> be a collection of real numbers, and let <math id="A3.Thmlem7.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\pi" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>π</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\pi</annotation></semantics></math> be a uniformly random permutation on <math id="A3.Thmlem7.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="{{\mathcal{W}}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒲</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{{\mathcal{W}}}</annotation></semantics></math>. Define</span></p>
<table id="A3.Ex248" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A3.Ex248.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="Z\;=\;\sum_{j=1}^{|{{\mathcal{W}}}|}a_{j,\pi(j)}." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>Z</mi><mo lspace="0.558em" rspace="0.391em">=</mo><mrow><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>j</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒲</mi><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow></munderover><msub><mi>a</mi><mrow><mi>j</mi><mo>,</mo><mrow><mi>π</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>j</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></msub></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">Z\;=\;\sum_{j=1}^{|{{\mathcal{W}}}|}a_{j,\pi(j)}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A3.Thmlem7.p1.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="A3.Thmlem7.p1.2.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">Then for all <math id="A3.Thmlem7.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="x&gt;0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo>&gt;</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">x&gt;0</annotation></semantics></math>,</span></p>
<table id="A3.Ex249" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A3.Ex249.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="{\mathbb{P}}\left(\bigl|Z-\EB[Z]\bigr|\;\geq\;2\sqrt{\,2\Bigl(\tfrac{1}{|{{\mathcal{W}}}|}\sum_{i,j=1}^{|{{\mathcal{W}}}|}a_{i,j}^{2}\Bigr)\,x\;+\;2\max_{1\leq i,j\leq|{{\mathcal{W}}}|}|a_{i,j}|\;x}\right)\;\leq\;16\,e^{1/16}\,\exp\Bigl(-\tfrac{x}{16}\Bigr)." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>ℙ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em" stretchy="true">|</mo><mrow><mi>Z</mi><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>𝔼</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mi>Z</mi><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em" rspace="0.280em" stretchy="true">|</mo></mrow><mo>≥</mo><mrow><mn> 2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msqrt><mrow><mrow><mn> 2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="1.600em" minsize="1.600em">(</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="false"><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒲</mi><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow></mfrac></mstyle><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒲</mi><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow></munderover><msubsup><mi>a</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow><mn>2</mn></msubsup></mrow></mrow><mo maxsize="1.600em" minsize="1.600em">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0.170em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>x</mi></mrow><mo lspace="0.502em">+</mo><mrow><mn> 2</mn><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><munder><mi>max</mi><mrow><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>≤</mo><mi>i</mi></mrow><mo>,</mo><mrow><mi>j</mi><mo>≤</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒲</mi><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></munder><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><msub><mi>a</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0.280em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>x</mi></mrow></mrow></msqrt></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.280em">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>≤</mo><mrow><mn> 16</mn><mo lspace="0.170em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>e</mi><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>/</mo><mn>16</mn></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mi>exp</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="1.600em" minsize="1.600em">(</mo><mrow><mo>−</mo><mstyle displaystyle="false"><mfrac><mi>x</mi><mn>16</mn></mfrac></mstyle></mrow><mo maxsize="1.600em" minsize="1.600em">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\mathbb{P}}\left(\bigl|Z-\EB[Z]\bigr|\;\geq\;2\sqrt{\,2\Bigl(\tfrac{1}{|{{\mathcal{W}}}|}\sum_{i,j=1}^{|{{\mathcal{W}}}|}a_{i,j}^{2}\Bigr)\,x\;+\;2\max_{1\leq i,j\leq|{{\mathcal{W}}}|}|a_{i,j}|\;x}\right)\;\leq\;16\,e^{1/16}\,\exp\Bigl(-\tfrac{x}{16}\Bigr).</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(15)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
</div>
<div id="A3.Thmlem8" class="ltx_theorem ltx_theorem_lem">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_title_theorem"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_theorem"><span id="A3.Thmlem8.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Lemma C.8</span></span><span id="A3.Thmlem8.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">.</span></h6>
<div id="A3.Thmlem8.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A3.Thmlem8.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A3.Thmlem8.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">The maximum function <math id="A3.Thmlem8.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\max:[0,1]^{m}\to[0,1]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>max</mi><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mrow><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow><mi>m</mi></msup><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\max:[0,1]^{m}\to[0,1]</annotation></semantics></math> is Lipschitz continuous with constant <math id="A3.Thmlem8.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mn>1</mn><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">1</annotation></semantics></math> with respect to the <math id="A3.Thmlem8.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="L^{\infty}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi>L</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">∞</mi></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">L^{\infty}</annotation></semantics></math> norm. That is, for any <math id="A3.Thmlem8.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="x,y\in[0,1]^{m}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>y</mi></mrow><mo>∈</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow><mi>m</mi></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">x,y\in[0,1]^{m}</annotation></semantics></math>, we have</span></p>
<table id="A3.E144" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A3.E144.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="|\max(x_{1},\ldots,x_{m})-\max(y_{1},\ldots,y_{m})|\leq\max_{i=1,\ldots,m}|x_{i}-y_{i}|." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>max</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>m</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>max</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>y</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>y</mi><mi>m</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow><mo>≤</mo><mrow><munder><mi>max</mi><mrow><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>m</mi></mrow></munder><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><mrow><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>y</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">|\max(x_{1},\ldots,x_{m})-\max(y_{1},\ldots,y_{m})|\leq\max_{i=1,\ldots,m}|x_{i}-y_{i}|.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(144)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A3.Thmlem8.p1.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="A3.Thmlem8.p1.2.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">Similarly, the minimum function <math id="A3.Thmlem8.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\min:[0,1]^{m}\to[0,1]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>min</mi><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mrow><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow><mi>m</mi></msup><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\min:[0,1]^{m}\to[0,1]</annotation></semantics></math> is also Lipschitz continuous with constant <math id="A3.Thmlem8.p1.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mn>1</mn><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">1</annotation></semantics></math> under the <math id="A3.Thmlem8.p1.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="L^{\infty}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi>L</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">∞</mi></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">L^{\infty}</annotation></semantics></math> norm:</span></p>
<table id="A3.E145" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A3.E145.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="|\min(x_{1},\ldots,x_{m})-\min(y_{1},\ldots,y_{m})|\leq\max_{i=1,\ldots,m}|x_{i}-y_{i}|." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>min</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>m</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>min</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>y</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>y</mi><mi>m</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow><mo>≤</mo><mrow><munder><mi>max</mi><mrow><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>m</mi></mrow></munder><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><mrow><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>y</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">|\min(x_{1},\ldots,x_{m})-\min(y_{1},\ldots,y_{m})|\leq\max_{i=1,\ldots,m}|x_{i}-y_{i}|.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(145)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
</div>
<div id="A3.SS10.3" class="ltx_proof">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_font_italic ltx_title_proof">Proof of Lemma <a href="#A3.Thmlem8" title="Lemma C.8. ‣ C.10 Auxiliary Lemmas ‣ Appendix C Proof for Inverse Transform Watermarks in Section ‣ Optimal Detection for Language Watermarks with Pseudorandom Collision" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">C.8</span></a>.</h6>
<div id="A3.SS10.p5" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A3.SS10.p5.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A3.SS10.p5.1.1" class="ltx_text">Without loss of generality, assume <math id="A3.SS10.p5.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\max(x_{1},\ldots,x_{m})=x_{i_{0}}\geq\max(y_{1},\ldots,y_{m})=y_{j_{0}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>max</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>m</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><msub><mi>i</mi><mn>0</mn></msub></msub><mo>≥</mo><mrow><mi>max</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>y</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>y</mi><mi>m</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><msub><mi>y</mi><msub><mi>j</mi><mn>0</mn></msub></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\max(x_{1},\ldots,x_{m})=x_{i_{0}}\geq\max(y_{1},\ldots,y_{m})=y_{j_{0}}</annotation></semantics></math> for some indices <math id="A3.SS10.p5.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="i_{0},j_{0}\in[m]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>i</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><mrow><msub><mi>j</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mi>m</mi><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">i_{0},j_{0}\in[m]</annotation></semantics></math>. Since <math id="A3.SS10.p5.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="y_{j_{0}}\geq y_{i_{0}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>y</mi><msub><mi>j</mi><mn>0</mn></msub></msub><mo>≥</mo><msub><mi>y</mi><msub><mi>i</mi><mn>0</mn></msub></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">y_{j_{0}}\geq y_{i_{0}}</annotation></semantics></math> (as <math id="A3.SS10.p5.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="y_{j_{0}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>y</mi><msub><mi>j</mi><mn>0</mn></msub></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">y_{j_{0}}</annotation></semantics></math> is the maximum of <math id="A3.SS10.p5.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="y" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>y</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">y</annotation></semantics></math>), we have</span></p>
<table id="A3.EGx109" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A3.E146"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A3.E146.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle|\max(x_{1},\ldots,x_{m})-\max(y_{1},\ldots,y_{m})|" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>max</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>m</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>max</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>y</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>y</mi><mi>m</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle|\max(x_{1},\ldots,x_{m})-\max(y_{1},\ldots,y_{m})|</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A3.E146.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=x_{i_{0}}-y_{j_{0}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><msub><mi>x</mi><msub><mi>i</mi><mn>0</mn></msub></msub><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>y</mi><msub><mi>j</mi><mn>0</mn></msub></msub></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=x_{i_{0}}-y_{j_{0}}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(146)</span></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A3.E147"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A3.E147.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\leq x_{i_{0}}-y_{i_{0}}\leq\max_{i=1,\ldots,m}|x_{i}-y_{i}|." display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>≤</mo><mrow><msub><mi>x</mi><msub><mi>i</mi><mn>0</mn></msub></msub><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>y</mi><msub><mi>i</mi><mn>0</mn></msub></msub></mrow><mo>≤</mo><mrow><munder><mi>max</mi><mrow><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>m</mi></mrow></munder><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><mrow><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>y</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\leq x_{i_{0}}-y_{i_{0}}\leq\max_{i=1,\ldots,m}|x_{i}-y_{i}|.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(147)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A3.SS10.p5.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="A3.SS10.p5.2.1" class="ltx_text">This proves the Lipschitz continuity of the maximum function. The result for the minimum follows by noting that</span></p>
<table id="A3.Ex250" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A3.Ex250.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\min(x_{1},\ldots,x_{m})=-\max(-x_{1},\ldots,-x_{m})," display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>min</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>m</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo rspace="0.167em">−</mo><mrow><mi>max</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mn>1</mn></msub></mrow><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi><mo>,</mo><mrow><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>m</mi></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\min(x_{1},\ldots,x_{m})=-\max(-x_{1},\ldots,-x_{m}),</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A3.SS10.p5.3" class="ltx_p"><span id="A3.SS10.p5.3.1" class="ltx_text">and applying the same argument to <math id="A3.SS10.p5.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="-x" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo>−</mo><mi>x</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">-x</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="A3.SS10.p5.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="-y" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo>−</mo><mi>y</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">-y</annotation></semantics></math>.
∎</span></p>
</div>
</div>
<div id="A3.Thmlem9" class="ltx_theorem ltx_theorem_lem">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_title_theorem"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_theorem"><span id="A3.Thmlem9.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Lemma C.9</span></span><span id="A3.Thmlem9.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">.</span></h6>
<div id="A3.Thmlem9.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A3.Thmlem9.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A3.Thmlem9.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">Let <math id="A3.Thmlem9.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="X_{1},\dots,X_{m}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>X</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>X</mi><mi>m</mi></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">X_{1},\dots,X_{m}</annotation></semantics></math> be independent <math id="A3.Thmlem9.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathrm{Unif}(0,1)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>Unif</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>1</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathrm{Unif}(0,1)</annotation></semantics></math> random variables, and conditionally on <math id="A3.Thmlem9.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(X_{1},\dots,X_{m})=\bm{x}:=(x_{1},\ldots,x_{m})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>X</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>X</mi><mi>m</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>=</mo><mi>𝐱</mi><mo>:=</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>m</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(X_{1},\dots,X_{m})=\bm{x}:=(x_{1},\ldots,x_{m})</annotation></semantics></math>, let</span></p>
<table id="A3.Ex251" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A3.Ex251.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="U\sim\mathrm{Unif}\bigl[a(\bm{x}),\,b(\bm{x})\bigr]," display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>U</mi><mo>∼</mo><mrow><mi>Unif</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">[</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>a</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝒙</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.337em">,</mo><mrow><mi>b</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝒙</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">]</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">U\sim\mathrm{Unif}\bigl[a(\bm{x}),\,b(\bm{x})\bigr],</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A3.Thmlem9.p1.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="A3.Thmlem9.p1.2.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">where <math id="A3.Thmlem9.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="a(\bm{x})=\max_{1\leq\ell\leq m}\{\Delta_{\ell}x_{\ell}\}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>a</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝐱</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><msub><mi>max</mi><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>≤</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mo>≤</mo><mi>m</mi></mrow></msub><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mrow><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">a(\bm{x})=\max_{1\leq\ell\leq m}\{\Delta_{\ell}x_{\ell}\}</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="A3.Thmlem9.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="b(\bm{x})=\min_{1\leq\ell\leq m}\{\Delta_{\ell}x_{\ell}+1-\Delta_{\ell}\}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>b</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝐱</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><msub><mi>min</mi><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>≤</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mo>≤</mo><mi>m</mi></mrow></msub><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mrow><mrow><mrow><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi></msub></mrow><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo>−</mo><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">b(\bm{x})=\min_{1\leq\ell\leq m}\{\Delta_{\ell}x_{\ell}+1-\Delta_{\ell}\}</annotation></semantics></math> with the convention that <math id="A3.Thmlem9.p1.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="U" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>U</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">U</annotation></semantics></math> has no mass if <math id="A3.Thmlem9.p1.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="a(x)\geq b(x)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>a</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>≥</mo><mrow><mi>b</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">a(x)\geq b(x)</annotation></semantics></math>.
With <math id="A3.Thmlem9.p1.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\bar{\bm{\Delta}}=({\bar{\Delta}}_{1},\ldots,{\bar{\Delta}}_{m})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mover accent="true"><mi>𝚫</mi><mo>¯</mo></mover><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo>¯</mo></mover><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo>¯</mo></mover><mi>m</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\bar{\bm{\Delta}}=({\bar{\Delta}}_{1},\ldots,{\bar{\Delta}}_{m})</annotation></semantics></math>, define</span></p>
<table id="A3.Ex252" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A3.Ex252.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="I_{m}(\bar{\bm{\Delta}})=\int_{[0,1]^{m}}\bigl(b(x)-a(x)\bigr)_{+}\,{\mathrm{d}}x." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>I</mi><mi>m</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>𝚫</mi><mo>¯</mo></mover><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.111em">=</mo><mrow><msub><mo rspace="0em">∫</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow><mi>m</mi></msup></msub><mrow><msub><mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">(</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>b</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>a</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">)</mo></mrow><mo>+</mo></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo rspace="0em">𝑑</mo><mi>x</mi></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">I_{m}(\bar{\bm{\Delta}})=\int_{[0,1]^{m}}\bigl(b(x)-a(x)\bigr)_{+}\,{\mathrm{d}}x.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A3.Thmlem9.p1.3" class="ltx_p"><span id="A3.Thmlem9.p1.3.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">Then for any measurable function <math id="A3.Thmlem9.p1.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="J\colon[0,1]^{m+1}\to[0,\infty)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>J</mi><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mrow><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow><mrow><mi>m</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">∞</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">J\colon[0,1]^{m+1}\to[0,\infty)</annotation></semantics></math>, we have</span></p>
<table id="A3.EGx110" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A3.E148"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A3.E148.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\EB\bigl[J(U,X_{1},\dots,X_{m})\bigr]=\frac{1}{I_{m}(\bar{\bm{\Delta}})}\int_{[0,1]^{m}}\int_{a(x)}^{b(x)}J\bigl(u,x_{1},\dots,x_{m}\bigr){\mathrm{d}}u\,\cdot\mathbf{1}_{a(\bm{x})&lt;b(\bm{x})}\,{\mathrm{d}}\bm{x}," display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>𝔼</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">[</mo><mrow><mi>J</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>U</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>X</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>X</mi><mi>m</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">]</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mrow><msub><mi>I</mi><mi>m</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>𝚫</mi><mo>¯</mo></mover><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mfrac></mstyle><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><msub><mo>∫</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow><mi>m</mi></msup></msub></mstyle><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><msubsup><mo>∫</mo><mrow><mi>a</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mrow><mi>b</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></msubsup></mstyle><mrow><mrow><mi>J</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">(</mo><mi>u</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>m</mi></msub><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>du</mi></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0.392em" rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><msub><mn>𝟏</mn><mrow><mrow><mi>a</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝐱</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>&lt;</mo><mrow><mi>b</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝐱</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></msub></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo rspace="0em">𝑑</mo><mi>𝐱</mi></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\EB\bigl[J(U,X_{1},\dots,X_{m})\bigr]=\frac{1}{I_{m}(\bar{\bm{\Delta}})}\int_{[0,1]^{m}}\int_{a(x)}^{b(x)}J\bigl(u,x_{1},\dots,x_{m}\bigr){\mathrm{d}}u\,\cdot\mathbf{1}_{a(\bm{x})&lt;b(\bm{x})}\,{\mathrm{d}}\bm{x},</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(148)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A3.Thmlem9.p1.4" class="ltx_p"><span id="A3.Thmlem9.p1.4.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">and hence the right-hand side defines the joint law of <math id="A3.Thmlem9.p1.m10" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(U,X_{1},\dots,X_{m})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>U</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>X</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>X</mi><mi>m</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(U,X_{1},\dots,X_{m})</annotation></semantics></math>.</span></p>
</div>
</div>
<div id="A3.SS10.4" class="ltx_proof">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_font_italic ltx_title_proof">Proof of Lemma <a href="#A3.Thmlem9" title="Lemma C.9. ‣ C.10 Auxiliary Lemmas ‣ Appendix C Proof for Inverse Transform Watermarks in Section ‣ Optimal Detection for Language Watermarks with Pseudorandom Collision" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">C.9</span></a>.</h6>
<div id="A3.SS10.p6" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A3.SS10.p6.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A3.SS10.p6.1.1" class="ltx_text">This follows directly from the law of total expectation and the conditional definition of <math id="A3.SS10.p6.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="U" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>U</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">U</annotation></semantics></math>, so we omit the details.
∎</span></p>
</div>
</div>
<div id="A3.Thmlem10" class="ltx_theorem ltx_theorem_lem">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_title_theorem"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_theorem"><span id="A3.Thmlem10.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Lemma C.10</span></span><span id="A3.Thmlem10.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold"> </span>(Integral approximation error)<span id="A3.Thmlem10.4" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">.</span></h6>
<div id="A3.Thmlem10.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A3.Thmlem10.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A3.Thmlem10.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">Let <math id="A3.Thmlem10.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="J:[0,1]^{m+1}\to\mathbb{R}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>J</mi><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mrow><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow><mrow><mi>m</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><mi>ℝ</mi></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">J:[0,1]^{m+1}\to\mathbb{R}</annotation></semantics></math> be a 1-Lipschitz function.
Let <math id="A3.Thmlem10.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="a_{\pi}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>a</mi><mi>π</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">a_{\pi}</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="A3.Thmlem10.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="b_{\pi}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>b</mi><mi>π</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">b_{\pi}</annotation></semantics></math> be random variables depending on a random variable <math id="A3.Thmlem10.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\pi" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>π</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\pi</annotation></semantics></math>, and let <math id="A3.Thmlem10.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\bar{a},\bar{b}\in[0,1]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mover accent="true"><mi>a</mi><mo>¯</mo></mover><mo>,</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>b</mi><mo>¯</mo></mover></mrow><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\bar{a},\bar{b}\in[0,1]</annotation></semantics></math> be deterministic values.
Then, for any fixed fractions <math id="A3.Thmlem10.p1.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\{x_{\ell}\}_{\ell=1}^{m}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msubsup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>m</mi></msubsup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\{x_{\ell}\}_{\ell=1}^{m}</annotation></semantics></math>, the following bound holds:</span></p>
<table id="A3.EGx111" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A3.Ex253"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A3.Ex253.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\displaystyle\left|\EB_{\pi}\left[\int_{a_{\pi}}^{b_{\pi}}J(u,x_{1},\ldots,x_{m}){\bf 1}_{\{b_{\pi}\geq a_{\pi}\}}\,{\mathrm{d}}u\right]-\int_{\bar{a}}^{\bar{b}}J(u,x_{1},\ldots,x_{m}){\bf 1}_{\{\bar{b}\geq\bar{a}\}}\,{\mathrm{d}}u\right|" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo fence="false" rspace="0.167em">|</mo><msub><mi>𝔼</mi><mi>π</mi></msub><mrow><mo>[</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><msubsup><mo>∫</mo><msub><mi>a</mi><mi>π</mi></msub><msub><mi>b</mi><mi>π</mi></msub></msubsup></mstyle><mi>J</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>u</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>m</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><msub><mn>𝟏</mn><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mi>b</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>π</mi></msub><mo>≥</mo><mi>a</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>π</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow></msub><mi>du</mi><mo>]</mo></mrow><mo>−</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><msubsup><mo>∫</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>a</mi><mo>¯</mo></mover><mover accent="true"><mi>b</mi><mo>¯</mo></mover></msubsup></mstyle><mi>J</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>u</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>m</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><msub><mn>𝟏</mn><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>b</mi><mo>¯</mo></mover><mo>≥</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>a</mi><mo>¯</mo></mover><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow></msub><mi>du</mi><mo fence="false">|</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\left|\EB_{\pi}\left[\int_{a_{\pi}}^{b_{\pi}}J(u,x_{1},\ldots,x_{m}){\bf 1}_{\{b_{\pi}\geq a_{\pi}\}}\,{\mathrm{d}}u\right]-\int_{\bar{a}}^{\bar{b}}J(u,x_{1},\ldots,x_{m}){\bf 1}_{\{\bar{b}\geq\bar{a}\}}\,{\mathrm{d}}u\right|</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A3.E149"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A3.E149.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\leq 2\|J\|_{\infty}\cdot\EB_{\pi}\left[|a_{\pi}-\bar{a}|+|b_{\pi}-\bar{b}|\right]." display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>≤</mo><mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mi>J</mi><mo rspace="0.055em" stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">∞</mi></msub></mrow><mo rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><mrow><msub><mi>𝔼</mi><mi>π</mi></msub><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>[</mo><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><mrow><msub><mi>a</mi><mi>π</mi></msub><mo>−</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>a</mi><mo>¯</mo></mover></mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><mrow><msub><mi>b</mi><mi>π</mi></msub><mo>−</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>b</mi><mo>¯</mo></mover></mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>]</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\leq 2\|J\|_{\infty}\cdot\EB_{\pi}\left[|a_{\pi}-\bar{a}|+|b_{\pi}-\bar{b}|\right].</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(149)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A3.Thmlem10.p1.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="A3.Thmlem10.p1.2.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">where <math id="A3.Thmlem10.p1.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\|J\|_{\infty}:=\max\limits_{(u,x_{1},\ldots,x_{m})\in[0,1]^{m+1}}|J(u,x_{1},\ldots,x_{m})|" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mi>J</mi><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">∞</mi></msub><mo>:=</mo><mrow><munder><mi>max</mi><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>u</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>m</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>∈</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow><mrow><mi>m</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup></mrow></munder><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><mrow><mi>J</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>u</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>m</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\|J\|_{\infty}:=\max\limits_{(u,x_{1},\ldots,x_{m})\in[0,1]^{m+1}}|J(u,x_{1},\ldots,x_{m})|</annotation></semantics></math> denotes the bound on <math id="A3.Thmlem10.p1.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="J" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>J</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">J</annotation></semantics></math>.</span></p>
</div>
</div>
<div id="A3.SS10.5" class="ltx_proof">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_font_italic ltx_title_proof">Proof of Lemma <a href="#A3.Thmlem10" title="Lemma C.10 (Integral approximation error). ‣ C.10 Auxiliary Lemmas ‣ Appendix C Proof for Inverse Transform Watermarks in Section ‣ Optimal Detection for Language Watermarks with Pseudorandom Collision" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">C.10</span></a>.</h6>
<div id="A3.SS10.p7" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A3.SS10.p7.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A3.SS10.p7.1.1" class="ltx_text">Since the values <math id="A3.SS10.p7.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\{x_{\ell}\}_{\ell=1}^{m}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msubsup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>m</mi></msubsup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\{x_{\ell}\}_{\ell=1}^{m}</annotation></semantics></math> are fixed, define the simplified function <math id="A3.SS10.p7.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="J(u):=J(u,x_{1},\ldots,x_{m})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>J</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>u</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>:=</mo><mrow><mi>J</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>u</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>m</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">J(u):=J(u,x_{1},\ldots,x_{m})</annotation></semantics></math>.
We decompose <math id="A3.SS10.p7.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="J" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>J</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">J</annotation></semantics></math> into its positive and negative parts:</span></p>
<table id="A3.Ex254" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A3.Ex254.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="J=J_{+}-J_{-},\quad\text{where}\quad J_{+}(u):=\max\{J(u),0\},\quad J_{-}(u):=\max\{-J(u),0\}." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>J</mi><mo>=</mo><mrow><msub><mi>J</mi><mo>+</mo></msub><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>J</mi><mo>−</mo></msub></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="1.167em">,</mo><mtext>where</mtext><mspace style="width:1em;" width="1em"></mspace><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>J</mi><mo>+</mo></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>u</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>:=</mo><mrow><mi>max</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mrow><mi>J</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>u</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo><mn>0</mn><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="1.167em">,</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>J</mi><mo>−</mo></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>u</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>:=</mo><mrow><mi>max</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mrow><mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>J</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>u</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">J=J_{+}-J_{-},\quad\text{where}\quad J_{+}(u):=\max\{J(u),0\},\quad J_{-}(u):=\max\{-J(u),0\}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A3.SS10.p7.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="A3.SS10.p7.2.1" class="ltx_text">Both <math id="A3.SS10.p7.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="J_{+}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>J</mi><mo>+</mo></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">J_{+}</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="A3.SS10.p7.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="J_{-}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>J</mi><mo>−</mo></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">J_{-}</annotation></semantics></math> are non-negative and 1-Lipschitz, with <math id="A3.SS10.p7.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\|J_{+}\|_{\infty},\|J_{-}\|_{\infty}\leq\|J\|_{\infty}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><msub><mi>J</mi><mo>+</mo></msub><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">∞</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><mrow><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><msub><mi>J</mi><mo>−</mo></msub><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">∞</mi></msub><mo>≤</mo><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mi>J</mi><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">∞</mi></msub></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\|J_{+}\|_{\infty},\|J_{-}\|_{\infty}\leq\|J\|_{\infty}</annotation></semantics></math>.</span></p>
</div>
<div id="A3.SS10.p8" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A3.SS10.p8.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A3.SS10.p8.1.1" class="ltx_text">Note that for any non-negative function <math id="A3.SS10.p8.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="f" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>f</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">f</annotation></semantics></math>, we have:</span></p>
<table id="A3.Ex255" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A3.Ex255.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\left(\int_{a}^{b}f(u)\,{\mathrm{d}}u\right){\bf 1}_{\{b\geq a\}}=\left(\int_{a}^{b}f(u)\,{\mathrm{d}}u\right)_{+}." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mo>(</mo><msubsup><mo lspace="0em">∫</mo><mi>a</mi><mi>b</mi></msubsup><mi>f</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>u</mi><mo rspace="0.170em" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mi>d</mi><mi>u</mi><mo>)</mo></mrow><msub><mn>𝟏</mn><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mi>b</mi><mo>≥</mo><mi>a</mi><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow></msub><mo>=</mo><msub><mrow><mo>(</mo><msubsup><mo lspace="0em">∫</mo><mi>a</mi><mi>b</mi></msubsup><mi>f</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>u</mi><mo rspace="0.170em" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mi>d</mi><mi>u</mi><mo>)</mo></mrow><mo>+</mo></msub><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\left(\int_{a}^{b}f(u)\,{\mathrm{d}}u\right){\bf 1}_{\{b\geq a\}}=\left(\int_{a}^{b}f(u)\,{\mathrm{d}}u\right)_{+}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A3.SS10.p8.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="A3.SS10.p8.2.1" class="ltx_text">Applying this to <math id="A3.SS10.p8.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="J_{+}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>J</mi><mo>+</mo></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">J_{+}</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="A3.SS10.p8.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="J_{-}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>J</mi><mo>−</mo></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">J_{-}</annotation></semantics></math>, we write:</span></p>
<table id="A3.EGx112" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A3.Ex256"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A3.Ex256.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\displaystyle\int_{a_{\pi}}^{b_{\pi}}J(u)\,{\mathrm{d}}u\cdot{\bf 1}_{\{b_{\pi}\geq a_{\pi}\}}-\int_{\bar{a}}^{\bar{b}}J(u)\,{\mathrm{d}}u\cdot{\bf 1}_{\{\bar{b}\geq\bar{a}\}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><msubsup><mo>∫</mo><msub><mi>a</mi><mi>π</mi></msub><msub><mi>b</mi><mi>π</mi></msub></msubsup></mstyle><mi>J</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>u</mi><mo rspace="0.170em" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mi>d</mi><mi>u</mi><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><msub><mn>𝟏</mn><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mi>b</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>π</mi></msub><mo>≥</mo><mi>a</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>π</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow></msub><mo>−</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><msubsup><mo>∫</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>a</mi><mo>¯</mo></mover><mover accent="true"><mi>b</mi><mo>¯</mo></mover></msubsup></mstyle><mi>J</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>u</mi><mo rspace="0.170em" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mi>d</mi><mi>u</mi><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><msub><mn>𝟏</mn><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>b</mi><mo>¯</mo></mover><mo>≥</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>a</mi><mo>¯</mo></mover><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\int_{a_{\pi}}^{b_{\pi}}J(u)\,{\mathrm{d}}u\cdot{\bf 1}_{\{b_{\pi}\geq a_{\pi}\}}-\int_{\bar{a}}^{\bar{b}}J(u)\,{\mathrm{d}}u\cdot{\bf 1}_{\{\bar{b}\geq\bar{a}\}}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A3.Ex257"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A3.Ex257.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=\left(\int_{a_{\pi}}^{b_{\pi}}J_{+}(u)\,{\mathrm{d}}u\right)_{+}-\left(\int_{\bar{a}}^{\bar{b}}J_{+}(u)\,{\mathrm{d}}u\right)_{+}-\left[\left(\int_{a_{\pi}}^{b_{\pi}}J_{-}(u)\,{\mathrm{d}}u\right)_{+}-\left(\int_{\bar{a}}^{\bar{b}}J_{-}(u)\,{\mathrm{d}}u\right)_{+}\right]." display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><msub><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><msubsup><mo>∫</mo><msub><mi>a</mi><mi>π</mi></msub><msub><mi>b</mi><mi>π</mi></msub></msubsup></mstyle><mrow><msub><mi>J</mi><mo>+</mo></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>u</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0.170em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo rspace="0em">𝑑</mo><mi>u</mi></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow><mo>+</mo></msub><mo>−</mo><msub><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><msubsup><mo>∫</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>a</mi><mo>¯</mo></mover><mover accent="true"><mi>b</mi><mo>¯</mo></mover></msubsup></mstyle><mrow><msub><mi>J</mi><mo>+</mo></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>u</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0.170em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo rspace="0em">𝑑</mo><mi>u</mi></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow><mo>+</mo></msub><mo>−</mo><mrow><mo>[</mo><mrow><msub><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><msubsup><mo>∫</mo><msub><mi>a</mi><mi>π</mi></msub><msub><mi>b</mi><mi>π</mi></msub></msubsup></mstyle><mrow><msub><mi>J</mi><mo>−</mo></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>u</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0.170em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo rspace="0em">𝑑</mo><mi>u</mi></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow><mo>+</mo></msub><mo>−</mo><msub><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><msubsup><mo>∫</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>a</mi><mo>¯</mo></mover><mover accent="true"><mi>b</mi><mo>¯</mo></mover></msubsup></mstyle><mrow><msub><mi>J</mi><mo>−</mo></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>u</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0.170em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo rspace="0em">𝑑</mo><mi>u</mi></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow><mo>+</mo></msub></mrow><mo>]</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=\left(\int_{a_{\pi}}^{b_{\pi}}J_{+}(u)\,{\mathrm{d}}u\right)_{+}-\left(\int_{\bar{a}}^{\bar{b}}J_{+}(u)\,{\mathrm{d}}u\right)_{+}-\left[\left(\int_{a_{\pi}}^{b_{\pi}}J_{-}(u)\,{\mathrm{d}}u\right)_{+}-\left(\int_{\bar{a}}^{\bar{b}}J_{-}(u)\,{\mathrm{d}}u\right)_{+}\right].</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
<div id="A3.SS10.p9" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A3.SS10.p9.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A3.SS10.p9.1.1" class="ltx_text">Applying the triangle inequality and the fact that <math id="A3.SS10.p9.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(\cdot)_{+}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">⋅</mo><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>+</mo></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(\cdot)_{+}</annotation></semantics></math> is 1-Lipschitz, we obtain:</span></p>
<table id="A3.EGx113" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A3.Ex258"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A3.Ex258.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\displaystyle\left|\int_{a_{\pi}}^{b_{\pi}}J(u)\,{\mathrm{d}}u\cdot{\bf 1}_{\{b_{\pi}\geq a_{\pi}\}}-\int_{\bar{a}}^{\bar{b}}J(u)\,{\mathrm{d}}u\cdot{\bf 1}_{\{\bar{b}\geq\bar{a}\}}\right|" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo fence="false" rspace="0.167em">|</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><msubsup><mo>∫</mo><msub><mi>a</mi><mi>π</mi></msub><msub><mi>b</mi><mi>π</mi></msub></msubsup></mstyle><mi>J</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>u</mi><mo rspace="0.170em" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mi>d</mi><mi>u</mi><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><msub><mn>𝟏</mn><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mi>b</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>π</mi></msub><mo>≥</mo><mi>a</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>π</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow></msub><mo>−</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><msubsup><mo>∫</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>a</mi><mo>¯</mo></mover><mover accent="true"><mi>b</mi><mo>¯</mo></mover></msubsup></mstyle><mi>J</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>u</mi><mo rspace="0.170em" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mi>d</mi><mi>u</mi><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><msub><mn>𝟏</mn><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>b</mi><mo>¯</mo></mover><mo>≥</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>a</mi><mo>¯</mo></mover><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow></msub><mo fence="false">|</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\left|\int_{a_{\pi}}^{b_{\pi}}J(u)\,{\mathrm{d}}u\cdot{\bf 1}_{\{b_{\pi}\geq a_{\pi}\}}-\int_{\bar{a}}^{\bar{b}}J(u)\,{\mathrm{d}}u\cdot{\bf 1}_{\{\bar{b}\geq\bar{a}\}}\right|</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A3.Ex259"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A3.Ex259.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\leq\left|\left(\int_{a_{\pi}}^{b_{\pi}}J_{+}(u)\,{\mathrm{d}}u\right)-\left(\int_{\bar{a}}^{\bar{b}}J_{+}(u)\,{\mathrm{d}}u\right)\right|+\left|\left(\int_{a_{\pi}}^{b_{\pi}}J_{-}(u)\,{\mathrm{d}}u\right)-\left(\int_{\bar{a}}^{\bar{b}}J_{-}(u)\,{\mathrm{d}}u\right)\right|" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>≤</mo><mrow><mrow><mo>|</mo><mrow><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><msubsup><mo>∫</mo><msub><mi>a</mi><mi>π</mi></msub><msub><mi>b</mi><mi>π</mi></msub></msubsup></mstyle><mrow><msub><mi>J</mi><mo>+</mo></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>u</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0.170em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo rspace="0em">𝑑</mo><mi>u</mi></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><msubsup><mo>∫</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>a</mi><mo>¯</mo></mover><mover accent="true"><mi>b</mi><mo>¯</mo></mover></msubsup></mstyle><mrow><msub><mi>J</mi><mo>+</mo></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>u</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0.170em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo rspace="0em">𝑑</mo><mi>u</mi></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>|</mo></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mo>|</mo><mrow><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><msubsup><mo>∫</mo><msub><mi>a</mi><mi>π</mi></msub><msub><mi>b</mi><mi>π</mi></msub></msubsup></mstyle><mrow><msub><mi>J</mi><mo>−</mo></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>u</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0.170em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo rspace="0em">𝑑</mo><mi>u</mi></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><msubsup><mo>∫</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>a</mi><mo>¯</mo></mover><mover accent="true"><mi>b</mi><mo>¯</mo></mover></msubsup></mstyle><mrow><msub><mi>J</mi><mo>−</mo></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>u</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0.170em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo rspace="0em">𝑑</mo><mi>u</mi></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>|</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\leq\left|\left(\int_{a_{\pi}}^{b_{\pi}}J_{+}(u)\,{\mathrm{d}}u\right)-\left(\int_{\bar{a}}^{\bar{b}}J_{+}(u)\,{\mathrm{d}}u\right)\right|+\left|\left(\int_{a_{\pi}}^{b_{\pi}}J_{-}(u)\,{\mathrm{d}}u\right)-\left(\int_{\bar{a}}^{\bar{b}}J_{-}(u)\,{\mathrm{d}}u\right)\right|</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A3.Ex260"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A3.Ex260.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\leq 2\|J\|_{\infty}\cdot(|a_{\pi}-\bar{a}|+|b_{\pi}-\bar{b}|)." display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>≤</mo><mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mi>J</mi><mo rspace="0.055em" stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">∞</mi></msub></mrow><mo rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><mrow><msub><mi>a</mi><mi>π</mi></msub><mo>−</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>a</mi><mo>¯</mo></mover></mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><mrow><msub><mi>b</mi><mi>π</mi></msub><mo>−</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>b</mi><mo>¯</mo></mover></mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\leq 2\|J\|_{\infty}\cdot(|a_{\pi}-\bar{a}|+|b_{\pi}-\bar{b}|).</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A3.SS10.p9.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="A3.SS10.p9.2.1" class="ltx_text">Taking expectation over <math id="A3.SS10.p9.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\pi" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>π</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\pi</annotation></semantics></math> completes the proof.
∎</span></p>
</div>
</div>
</section>
</section>
<section id="A4" class="ltx_appendix">
<h2 class="ltx_title ltx_title_appendix"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_appendix">Appendix D </span>Details of Simulation Study</h2>

<section id="A4.SS0.SSS0.Px1" class="ltx_paragraph">
<h5 class="ltx_title ltx_title_paragraph">Choice of pseudorandom variable.</h5>

<div id="A4.SS0.SSS0.Px1.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A4.SS0.SSS0.Px1.p1.1" class="ltx_p">We use a context window of size <math id="A4.SS0.SSS0.Px1.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="m=7" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>m</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>7</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">m=7</annotation></semantics></math>, so the pseudorandom variable <math id="A4.SS0.SSS0.Px1.p1.m2" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\zeta_{t}={\mathcal{A}}(s_{(t-m):(t-1)},{\mathtt{Key}})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>ζ</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒜</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>s</mi><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>−</mo><mi>m</mi></mrow><mo rspace="0.278em" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></msub><mo>,</mo><mi>𝙺𝚎𝚢</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\zeta_{t}={\mathcal{A}}(s_{(t-m):(t-1)},{\mathtt{Key}})</annotation></semantics></math> depends on the preceding <math id="A4.SS0.SSS0.Px1.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="m" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>m</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">m</annotation></semantics></math> tokens. With such a relatively large <math id="A4.SS0.SSS0.Px1.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="m" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>m</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">m</annotation></semantics></math>, nearly all pseudorandom collisions stem from our generation mechanism. In practice, at each step <math id="A4.SS0.SSS0.Px1.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="t" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>t</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">t</annotation></semantics></math>, the hash function <math id="A4.SS0.SSS0.Px1.p1.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="{\mathcal{A}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒜</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\mathcal{A}}</annotation></semantics></math> takes as input the <math id="A4.SS0.SSS0.Px1.p1.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="m" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>m</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">m</annotation></semantics></math> most recent tokens concatenated with the key <math id="A4.SS0.SSS0.Px1.p1.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="{\mathtt{Key}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>𝙺𝚎𝚢</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\mathtt{Key}}</annotation></semantics></math>, producing a hash value that serves as a random seed. This seed is then passed to a pseudorandom number generator, for which we use the PCG-64 generator <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_cite">[<a href="#bib.bib38" title="" class="ltx_ref">38</a>]</cite>, the default in Python’s <span id="A4.SS0.SSS0.Px1.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_sansserif">NumPy</span> package <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_cite">[<a href="#bib.bib17" title="" class="ltx_ref">17</a>]</cite>.</p>
</div>
</section>
<section id="A4.SS0.SSS0.Px2" class="ltx_paragraph">
<h5 class="ltx_title ltx_title_paragraph">Computation of critical values.</h5>

<div id="A4.SS0.SSS0.Px2.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A4.SS0.SSS0.Px2.p1.1" class="ltx_p">For the Gumbel-max watermark under score functions <math id="A4.SS0.SSS0.Px2.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="h_{\mathrm{ars}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>h</mi><mi>ars</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">h_{\mathrm{ars}}</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="A4.SS0.SSS0.Px2.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="h_{\mathrm{log}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>h</mi><mi>log</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">h_{\mathrm{log}}</annotation></semantics></math>, the sum of score values follows a gamma distribution. In this case, the critical values can be obtained directly from the gamma <math id="A4.SS0.SSS0.Px2.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(1-\alpha)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mi>α</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(1-\alpha)</annotation></semantics></math> quantile. For other score functions, the exact distribution of the score sum is generally unavailable, so we rely on Monte Carlo simulation.
Concretely, for each <math id="A4.SS0.SSS0.Px2.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="n" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>n</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">n</annotation></semantics></math>, we generate <math id="A4.SS0.SSS0.Px2.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="n" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>n</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">n</annotation></semantics></math> i.i.d. samples of the corresponding pivotal statistic <math id="A4.SS0.SSS0.Px2.p1.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="Y" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>Y</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">Y</annotation></semantics></math> from <math id="A4.SS0.SSS0.Px2.p1.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mu_{0}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>μ</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mu_{0}</annotation></semantics></math> and compute <math id="A4.SS0.SSS0.Px2.p1.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\sum_{{\mathcal{V}}\in\Pi}h(Y_{{\mathcal{V}}})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mo>∑</mo><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒱</mi><mo>∈</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">Π</mi></mrow></msub><mrow><mi>h</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>Y</mi><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒱</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\sum_{{\mathcal{V}}\in\Pi}h(Y_{{\mathcal{V}}})</annotation></semantics></math> for the score function <math id="A4.SS0.SSS0.Px2.p1.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="h" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>h</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">h</annotation></semantics></math>. This procedure is repeated 4000 times, and the empirical <math id="A4.SS0.SSS0.Px2.p1.m10" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(1-\alpha)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mi>α</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(1-\alpha)</annotation></semantics></math> quantile of these values serves as an estimate.</p>
</div>
</section>
<section id="A4.SS0.SSS0.Px3" class="ltx_paragraph">
<h5 class="ltx_title ltx_title_paragraph">Additional results.</h5>

<div id="A4.SS0.SSS0.Px3.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A4.SS0.SSS0.Px3.p1.1" class="ltx_p">Figure <a href="#A4.F6" title="Figure 6 ‣ Additional results. ‣ Appendix D Details of Simulation Study ‣ Optimal Detection for Language Watermarks with Pseudorandom Collision" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">6</span></a> reports Type II errors for other values of <math id="A4.SS0.SSS0.Px3.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\Delta_{\max}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mi>max</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Delta_{\max}</annotation></semantics></math>, showing patterns consistent with those in Section <a href="#S6.SS1" title="6.1 Synthetic Studies ‣ 6 Experiments ‣ Optimal Detection for Language Watermarks with Pseudorandom Collision" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">6.1</span></a>.</p>
</div>
<figure id="A4.F6" class="ltx_figure"><object type="image/svg+xml" data="2510.22007v1/Appendix-K1000N2000c7key23333T700alpha0.01-all0.9.svg" id="A4.F6.g1" class="ltx_graphics ltx_centering ltx_img_square" style="aspect-ratio:476/417;" width="476" height="417"></object>
<figcaption class="ltx_caption ltx_centering"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_figure">Figure 6: </span>Type II errors on synthetic datasets for the Gumbel-max watermark (left) and the inverse-transform watermark (right), with results shown for <math id="A4.F6.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\Delta_{\max}\in\{0.1,0.3,0.5,0.7\}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mi>max</mi></msub><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mrow><mn>0.1</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>0.3</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>0.5</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>0.7</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Delta_{\max}\in\{0.1,0.3,0.5,0.7\}</annotation></semantics></math> from top to bottom.
</figcaption>
</figure>
</section>
</section>
<section id="A5" class="ltx_appendix">
<h2 class="ltx_title ltx_title_appendix"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_appendix">Appendix E </span>Details for Real-World Examples</h2>

<section id="A5.SS0.SSS0.Px1" class="ltx_paragraph">
<h5 class="ltx_title ltx_title_paragraph">Detailed experimental setup.</h5>

<div id="A5.SS0.SSS0.Px1.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A5.SS0.SSS0.Px1.p1.1" class="ltx_p">In our empirical analysis of the detection performance of different watermark detection methods, we focus on the OPT-1.3B model <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_cite">[<a href="#bib.bib52" title="" class="ltx_ref">52</a>]</cite>.
We evaluate Type I errors using 2000 human-written samples from the C4 news-like dataset <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_cite">[<a href="#bib.bib42" title="" class="ltx_ref">42</a>]</cite>.
Specifically, for each human-written document in the dataset, we select it if and only if it contains at least 520 tokens, and we take the last 500 tokens as the initial prompt.
For each selected sample, we apply a hash function <math id="A5.SS0.SSS0.Px1.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="{\mathcal{A}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒜</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\mathcal{A}}</annotation></semantics></math> to compute the corresponding sequence of pseudorandom variables.
This procedure is repeated until we collect 2000 sequences, each containing 500 pivotal statistics.</p>
</div>
<div id="A5.SS0.SSS0.Px1.p2" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A5.SS0.SSS0.Px1.p2.1" class="ltx_p">To assess Type II errors, we randomly sample prompts from the same dataset.
We enforce a minimum prompt length of 50 tokens in all experiments and skip any document shorter than this threshold.
Each 50-token prompt is then fed into the model, which generates an additional 800 tokens.
Since 800 tokens are sufficiently long, we retain the generated text only if it contains at least 300 unique minimal units; otherwise, the generation is discarded.
Following this procedure, we collect 200 generated sequences, each consisting of at least 300 minimal units.</p>
</div>
<div id="A5.SS0.SSS0.Px1.p3" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A5.SS0.SSS0.Px1.p3.1" class="ltx_p">The temperature parameter controls the randomness of LLM generation.
Let <math id="A5.SS0.SSS0.Px1.p3.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\bm{L}=(L_{1},\ldots,L_{|{{\mathcal{W}}}|})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>𝑳</mi><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>L</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>L</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒲</mi><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\bm{L}=(L_{1},\ldots,L_{|{{\mathcal{W}}}|})</annotation></semantics></math> denote the model’s logit vector over the vocabulary <math id="A5.SS0.SSS0.Px1.p3.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="{{\mathcal{W}}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒲</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{{\mathcal{W}}}</annotation></semantics></math>.
The temperature <math id="A5.SS0.SSS0.Px1.p3.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\beta" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>β</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\beta</annotation></semantics></math> rescales this vector to obtain the token distribution <math id="A5.SS0.SSS0.Px1.p3.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\bm{P}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>𝑷</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\bm{P}</annotation></semantics></math>,</p>
<table id="A5.Ex261" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A5.Ex261.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="P_{{w}}=\frac{\exp(L_{{w}}/\beta)}{\sum_{{w}^{\prime}\in{{\mathcal{W}}}}\exp(L_{{w}^{\prime}}/\beta)}." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>P</mi><mi>w</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mrow><mi>exp</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>L</mi><mi>w</mi></msub><mo>/</mo><mi>β</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mrow><msub><mo>∑</mo><mrow><msup><mi>w</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo>∈</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒲</mi></mrow></msub><mrow><mi>exp</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>L</mi><msup><mi>w</mi><mo>′</mo></msup></msub><mo>/</mo><mi>β</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mfrac></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">P_{{w}}=\frac{\exp(L_{{w}}/\beta)}{\sum_{{w}^{\prime}\in{{\mathcal{W}}}}\exp(L_{{w}^{\prime}}/\beta)}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A5.SS0.SSS0.Px1.p3.2" class="ltx_p">A smaller <math id="A5.SS0.SSS0.Px1.p3.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\beta" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>β</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\beta</annotation></semantics></math> yields a more deterministic distribution.
To ensure a clear comparison across methods, we adopt relatively low temperatures: <math id="A5.SS0.SSS0.Px1.p3.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\beta=0.3" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>β</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>0.3</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\beta=0.3</annotation></semantics></math> for the Gumbel-max watermark and <math id="A5.SS0.SSS0.Px1.p3.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\beta=0.5" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>β</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>0.5</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\beta=0.5</annotation></semantics></math> for the inverse-transform watermark.
At higher temperatures (that is, more random generations), all detection methods tend to achieve nearly indistinguishable power within short text lengths.</p>
</div>
</section>
<section id="A5.SS0.SSS0.Px2" class="ltx_paragraph">
<h5 class="ltx_title ltx_title_paragraph">Details of Figure <a href="#S1.F1" title="Figure 1 ‣ 1 Introduction ‣ Optimal Detection for Language Watermarks with Pseudorandom Collision" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">1</span></a>.</h5>

<div id="A5.SS0.SSS0.Px2.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A5.SS0.SSS0.Px2.p1.1" class="ltx_p">We describe the experimental setup used to produce Figure <a href="#S1.F1" title="Figure 1 ‣ 1 Introduction ‣ Optimal Detection for Language Watermarks with Pseudorandom Collision" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">1</span></a>.
The left panel quantifies the proportion of token repetitions in both human-written and watermarked texts.</p>
<ul id="A5.I1" class="ltx_itemize">
<li id="A5.I1.i1" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">•</span> 
<div id="A5.I1.i1.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A5.I1.i1.p1.1" class="ltx_p">For the human-written case, we extract sentences from the C4 news-like dataset <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_cite">[<a href="#bib.bib42" title="" class="ltx_ref">42</a>]</cite>. Each sentence is tokenized using the OPT-1.3B decoder, and we retain those with at least 200 tokens, collecting 1000 sequences in total. For a given text window size <math id="A5.I1.i1.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="m\in\{2,3,\ldots,10\}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>m</mi><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>3</mn><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi><mo>,</mo><mn>10</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">m\in\{2,3,\ldots,10\}</annotation></semantics></math>, we compute the proportion of repeated tokens within each sequence and report the average repetition rate across all sequences.</p>
</div></li>
<li id="A5.I1.i2" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">•</span> 
<div id="A5.I1.i2.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A5.I1.i2.p1.1" class="ltx_p">For the watermarked case, we sample 1000 prompts, each containing at least 50 tokens, and generate the following 200 tokens using the Gumbel-max watermark with temperature 1. When generating each text, we specify a window size <math id="A5.I1.i2.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="m" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>m</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">m</annotation></semantics></math>, which is used to compute the pseudorandom variables. We then measure the repetition rate for each generation and report the final value as the average across all 1000 samples.</p>
</div></li>
</ul>
</div>
<div id="A5.SS0.SSS0.Px2.p2" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A5.SS0.SSS0.Px2.p2.1" class="ltx_p">The right panel of Figure <a href="#S1.F1" title="Figure 1 ‣ 1 Introduction ‣ Optimal Detection for Language Watermarks with Pseudorandom Collision" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">1</span></a> demonstrates that classic detection methods fail to control Type I error. To verify this, we generate 1000 sequences of 1000 tokens each using the OPT-1.3B model with temperature 0.1, without applying any watermarking. We then apply existing detection methods to these sequences and evaluate their empirical Type I error rates.</p>
</div>
</section>
</section>
</article>
</div>
</div>
